{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent","id":1502169,"title":"Feel free to vent.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-04T17:04:37-08:00","id":1502169,"title":"Feel free to vent.","content":"Just a random bitch and moan thread. No politics please.<br /> <br /> I'll start by saying how much I dislike the service at the local cell phone carrier's physical store (Spectrum in my case). The sales rep lied about their return and service policies, ordered me the wrong phone and I couldn't return it to the store because he ordered it form their website like I could have done from the comfort of my home without taking a trip to the store. When I asked to lower the tier of my internet service to cut down my bill he signed me up for home phone service with a limited time promotional rate, the exact thing I told him not to do when changing my plan. I assume he did this for some kind of bonus pay. Spectrum also lowered the price of their regular monthly unlimited plan and I had to fight with one rep and a store manager before I could get someone on the phone to fix the issue and change my plan.<br /> <br /> Considering I was buying a $1200 flagship phone from them rather than directly from Samsung it was the least they could do. I wasn't asking for anything special, just what people are currently paying for a single line (this isn't a promotional rate I was asking for). I had to call into their customer service call center and the people there were much nicer and pleasant to deal with, they said they fixed the plan rate issue and are sending me the correct phone (the new S23 Ultra, yay!). Now I have to wait until the phone is actually released on the 17th and my next bill to make sure they really fixed everything. I think the last time I had a hassle-free phone upgrade was the last flip phone I bought. I kept telling the phone center people they were so much nicer and easier to deal with (I spoke to like 4 or 5 over 2 days getting this fixed) and they all said they've heard that from multiple callers. That should be a huge fucking red flag, but I guess it somehow isn't cost effective to address the issue. I've learned my lesson and will never try buying anything from one of their stores again. Unfortunately, my apartment complex only allows internet service through them, or I would have changed ISP and phone services ASAP. Anyway, rant done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T08:54:29-08:00","id":1502210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent#post1502169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .I've learned my lesson and will never try buying anything from one of their stores again. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of companies nowadays, are trying to get customers to use their online-services and not use their in-store locations; my bank, there's an hour-wait for a teller; they've got like a dozen coves for tellers, and only two working, on a Friday. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T13:48:51-08:00","id":1502235,"title":"","content":"The continual chronic exhaustion and week... 7 (?) of being sick is wearing thin on me. Making progress and things are getting closer to mentally healthy point, but it is a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T11:31:02-08:00","id":1502525,"title":"","content":"My vent is just is when management makes the same dumb choices that haven't worked before and hoping for a different result. In this case let's cut our shift's staff in half as they think we got to many people, but slowly increase the workload like before and don't worry the previous shift will clean up before you arrive. This has never happened in my entire time there and after 8-9 hours of working most people just want to leave and head home and leave whatever is left for the next shift. Then watch management complain that they are paying out to much overtime and still the orders are not up to par and wonder what went wrong and go back to what we had before that was working better.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T15:18:32-08:00","id":1502647,"title":"","content":"I am too tall for Japan.<br /> <br /> Which, admittedly, I was very aware of that when I took this job, but it starts to wear when I get back aches just from sitting in the chairs at the teachers offices for the schools I work in.<br /> <br /> Related, much as I love the cold, this is the first time I've lived in a place with long winters. Which I've found to be very detrimental to my overall health - between Raynaud's Syndrome, heavy snowdrifts keeping me from running except on a treadmill, and portions of my torso becoming dried out patches of pure iching, I'm very ready for winter to end.<br /> <br /> Also, why is earth would you build carports with flat roofs in a place where the normal level of snowfall will crush them?! And it's not like they didn't think of sloped roofs - my neighbor has one!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-09-2023, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T15:42:01-08:00","id":1502651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1502647#post1502647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am too tall for Japan.<br /> <br /> Which, admittedly, I was very aware of that when I took this job, but it starts to wear when I get back aches just from sitting in the chairs at the teachers offices for the schools I work in.<br /> <br /> Related, much as I love the cold, this is the first time I've lived in a place with long winters. Which I've found to be very detrimental to my overall health - between Raynaud's Syndrome, heavy snowdrifts keeping me from running except on a treadmill, and portions of my torso becoming dried out patches of pure iching, I'm very ready for winter to end.<br /> <br /> Also, why is earth would you build carports with flat roofs in a place where the normal level of snowfall will crush them?! And it's not like they didn't think of sloped roofs - my neighbor has one!</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing to keep in mind once I finish my TEFL certification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T15:48:31-08:00","id":1502652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1502651#post1502651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thing to keep in mind once I finish my TEFL certification.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that I'm 6-foot-2 / 188cm tall. If you're 3 inches or more shorter than that, Asia in general isn't too bad. Also the fact that I'm in a dying town in rural Hokkaido means stuff like standing desks really aren't a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T17:03:24-08:00","id":1502659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1502652#post1502652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should note that I'm 6-foot-2 / 188cm tall. If you're 3 inches or more shorter than that, Asia in general isn't too bad. Also the fact that I'm in a dying town in rural Hokkaido means stuff like standing desks really aren't a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a 6'3&quot; girl. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Didn't really have any trouble in Tokyo, but then again job searching in Japan is not the same as working in Japan, in terms of regular physical positions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T17:20:13-08:00","id":1502660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1502659#post1502659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a 6'3&quot; girl. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Didn't really have any trouble in Tokyo, but then again job searching in Japan is not the same as working in Japan, in terms of regular physical positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>My advice is to get used to ducking. While I won't say the teacher housing I currently reside in is universal, the fact that I have to keep my head at an angle to avoid hitting the frame when going between rooms speaks volumes.<br /> <br /> Also, cars are cramped","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T12:27:29-08:00","id":1503052,"title":"","content":"I feel sorry for Rowling,because I feel like I understand her. I dont agree with her of course,but I understand. Rowling grow up dirtu poor,i grow up almost as dirty poor.<br /> after analyzing her tweets and the wiki page on her Rowling's political views,I feel like she sees that trans folks are &quot;hogging&quot; all the welfare ,Rowling feels that trans people are getting all the help they need and the people who are dirty poor and are suffering in poverty are not getting help by virtue of being cis. That's her problem with trans people,it's not that they are teans is that in Rowling view everyone is so focused in helping trans people they are forgetting the victims of poverty and abuse like Rowling herself was. She's not right,of course,but it hard to blame her,she's been hurt a great deal before she lucked out by writing a few books people liked","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T12:34:05-08:00","id":1503054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503052#post1503052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel sorry for Rowling,because I feel like I understand her. I dont agree with her of course,but I understand. Rowling grow up dirtu poor,i grow up almost as dirty poor.<br /> after analyzing her tweets and the wiki page on her Rowling's political views,I feel like she sees that trans folks are &quot;hogging&quot; all the welfare ,Rowling feels that trans people are getting all the help they need and the people who are dirty poor and are suffering in poverty are not getting help by virtue of being cis. That's her problem with trans people,it's not that they are teans is that in Rowling view everyone is so focused in helping trans people they are forgetting the victims of poverty and abuse like Rowling herself was. She's not right,of course,but it hard to blame her,she's been hurt a great deal before she lucked out by writing a few books people liked</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry,I really am.<br /> but &quot;she has suffered abuse&quot; simply isn't a exculpatory condition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T13:30:53-08:00","id":1503062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503052#post1503052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel sorry for Rowling,because I feel like I understand her. I dont agree with her of course,but I understand. Rowling grow up dirtu poor,i grow up almost as dirty poor.<br /> after analyzing her tweets and the wiki page on her Rowling's political views,I feel like she sees that trans folks are &quot;hogging&quot; all the welfare ,Rowling feels that trans people are getting all the help they need and the people who are dirty poor and are suffering in poverty are not getting help by virtue of being cis. That's her problem with trans people,it's not that they are teans is that in Rowling view everyone is so focused in helping trans people they are forgetting the victims of poverty and abuse like Rowling herself was. She's not right,of course,but it hard to blame her,she's been hurt a great deal before she lucked out by writing a few books people liked</div> </div> </div> </div>Hate to burst your bubble, but she did not grow up dirt poor. She came from a middle class family and was a university educated professor receving childcare benefits. The cafe she mentions having written early Harry Potter at was owned by her family, and they were supportive of her during that time. Her own family has sheepishly admitted over the years that dearest JK embellished a lot of what she was going through during her early rise to wealth and fame.<br /> <br /> It was a <i>rough</i> time for her, to be sure, since a lot of it came out when she was between jobs and was having trouble getting into other positions-but she was hardly in poverty. It was <i>rough </i>for a middle class citizen, but her experience was almost a good day for the actually impoverished.<br /> <br /> This explanation about her relationship to transness also sort of ignores the fact she has explained her position on it-she has openly stated that her actual issues relate to both a fundamental view of sex dictating gender and her fears of the potential for sexual predacity on the part of the trans community-and both the direct factors that lead her to this position (JK has been the subject of sexual assault at the hands of men, and she considers herself proudly a second-wave feminist which directly preaches sex as a prison one can never escape) and the indirect factors that lead into it (she's something of a British-oriented United Kingdom Nationalist, with her having been very vocal against Socttish independence, and it's notable that it's Scotland's transgender equality acts that caused her most vocal outing of herself as a TERF, and as a general rule has been classist and bigotted against other peoples in a dismissive, stereotyping way, and the trans community tend to fall under those categorizations for too many socio-economic reasons to get into).<br /> <br /> Jk Rowling bought everything that came to her plate in the recent years. The only actually sad thing about her story is that, for all it's flaws, her greatest work to date was an anthem to many people for the power of love and community amongst diverse persons, and the importance of standing up together against forces that would diminish and punish others for arbitrary and superficial reasons, and yet when people who were inspired by her works invited her to grow from her mistakes and do the same as she exhorted them to do, she instead said &quot;Nah.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-14-2023, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T15:00:49-08:00","id":1503069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503062#post1503062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jk Rowling bought everything that came to her plate in the recent years. The only actually sad thing about her story is that, for all it's flaws, her greatest work to date was an anthem to many people for the power of love and community amongst diverse persons, and the importance of standing up together against forces that would diminish and punish others for arbitrary and superficial reasons, and yet when people who were inspired by her works invited her to grow from her mistakes and do the same as she exhorted them to do, she instead said &quot;Nah.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that not the saddest thing of all? To be so deep into an ideology that one can no longer see or care how much it harms others, even betraying one's original principles? To reject those who would forgive you even after you harmed them? I wonder, does she see the contradiction between her written words, and her actions? Does her pain blind her, or did she ever believe in those words? I wonder, will she have reconsidered her stance by the time she passes on? Will she regret her choices? Or will she go into the grave certain of the correctness of her life? I don't know. I suppose I can never know. I just hope that everyone can learn from her, to better themselves where she could not, to have empathy where she could not.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T15:10:33-08:00","id":1503071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503069#post1503069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that not the saddest thing of all? To be so deep into an ideology that one can no longer see or care how much it harms others, even betraying one's original principles? To reject those who would forgive you even after you harmed them? I wonder, does she see the contradiction between her written words, and her actions? Does her pain blind her, or did she ever believe in those words? I wonder, will she have reconsidered her stance by the time she passes on? Will she regret her choices? Or will she go into the grave certain of the correctness of her life? I don't know. I suppose I can never know. I just hope that everyone can learn from her, to better themselves where she could not, to have empathy where she could not.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold what was good, drop what was not, and move forward.<br /> <br /> and back They Came From Witchford Academy! when it goes to Kickstarter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T17:04:43-08:00","id":1503083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503069#post1503069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that not the saddest thing of all? To be so deep into an ideology that one can no longer see or care how much it harms others, even betraying one's original principles? To reject those who would forgive you even after you harmed them? I wonder, does she see the contradiction between her written words, and her actions? Does her pain blind her, or did she ever believe in those words? I wonder, will she have reconsidered her stance by the time she passes on? Will she regret her choices? Or will she go into the grave certain of the correctness of her life? I don't know. I suppose I can never know. I just hope that everyone can learn from her, to better themselves where she could not, to have empathy where she could not.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has impacted her creative output as well at this point. She has this crime novel series that she writes under the pseudonym Robert Galbraith and the last two novels are... certainly something. &quot;Troubled Blood&quot; was all about a male serial killer dressing up as a woman to lure in victims. Meanwhile, here latest &quot;Ink Black Heart&quot; was about a creator of a series who was being harrassed online (for being anitsemitic, racist, ableist etc.) - and then killed (and JK Rowling claims this character is not a stand-in for herself, of course... but I mean, come on...). Here where things get really weird, though, because, despite this novel just being a bogstandard whodunnit, it has 1024 pages. And the reason for that is the novel being really obsessed with Twitter. There are entire chapters just being this stylized depictions of arguments on Twitter, people making Twitter threads and then when that isn't happening people are discussing what's said in these Twitter posts. And to make matters more annoying: No character is using their real name for their Twitter account and a central element of the mystery is about who's in control of what Twitter account at what time and who is responsible for posting something. It's boring but it's also weirdly obsessive when it comes to Twitter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T17:36:44-08:00","id":1503088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503083#post1503083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it has impacted her creative output as well at this point. She has this crime novel series that she writes under the pseudonym Robert Galbraith and the last two novels are... certainly something. &quot;Troubled Blood&quot; was all about a male serial killer dressing up as a woman to lure in victims. Meanwhile, here latest &quot;Ink Black Heart&quot; was about a creator of a series who was being harrassed online (for being anitsemitic, racist, ableist etc.) - and then killed (and JK Rowling claims this character is not a stand-in for herself, of course... but I mean, come on...). Here where things get really weird, though, because, despite this novel just being a bogstandard whodunnit, it has 1024 pages. And the reason for that is the novel being really obsessed with Twitter. There are entire chapters just being this stylized depictions of arguments on Twitter, people making Twitter threads and then when that isn't happening people are discussing what's said in these Twitter posts. And to make matters more annoying: No character is using their real name for their Twitter account and a central element of the mystery is about who's in control of what Twitter account at what time and who is responsible for posting something. It's boring but it's also weirdly obsessive when it comes to Twitter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cormoran Strike series started off as thinly veiled commentary posing as a noir-leaning detective series and has slowly been destroying more and more of it's veil as it all goes along, and if you thought you could see dearest JK's bigotry in some of her more out there choices in Potter but aren't sure if it's too much or too far, rest assured you will understand that she hates poor people, fat people, and non-British people in short order by reading Strike.<br /> <br /> One of the hard things to wrap your head around as you get older and particularly as you get into the craft of writing and storytelling is that it's entirely possible to make something that is thoroughly enjoyable and impactful while still having that product be of bad quality, and dearest JK is a very vivid example of that. She's not really that good of a writer, though she grasps the essentials better than others, and she mostly makes up for it by moving a lot of things that make an impression on you, be it a bit of setting detail, a strong character portrait (not <i>quite</i> the same as a strong character, mind), a clever call back, and the like in a rather succinct order-calling it the narrative equivalent of jangling keys is a lttle too dismissive of her skills, but it draws up to it.<br /> <br /> The Cormoran Strike Series is revelatory for her skill because she can't fall back on her imagination for novelty in a story grounded in the real world, and those strong character portraits are realized as characatures because they don't have the benefit of the fantasy setting softening and whimsifying the stereotypes, and while her perchance for setting things up and paying them off remains, her brisk pace makes it a lot more apparent she's trying to skirt past how flimsy any given explanation can be, where by the time you get to the end the only way it works is if you just went with the flow and accepted it.<br /> <br /> And like a lot of people like her, the more she's got to grind in her gears, the more the gears are going to be ground in her books. This also happened with Potter, but again the genre allows for some divide from that, where Cormoran...well, grinding her gears is kind of really all she's got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-14-2023, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T18:05:45-08:00","id":1503092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503083#post1503083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it has impacted her creative output as well at this point. She has this crime novel series that she writes under the pseudonym Robert Galbraith and the last two novels are... certainly something. &quot;Troubled Blood&quot; was all about a male serial killer dressing up as a woman to lure in victims.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, She is really obsessed with crossdressers and conflating them with trans people. Makes me wonder if that's part of what happened to her. Something has definitely caused her to fixate firmly on the idea. In any case, I hope she's getting effective therapy.<br /> <br /> (I don't know the details of her assault. Sorry, if I got it wildly wrong.)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503083#post1503083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, here latest &quot;Ink Black Heart&quot; was about a creator of a series who was being harrassed online (for being anitsemitic, racist, ableist etc.) - and then killed (and JK Rowling claims this character is not a stand-in for herself, of course... but I mean, come on...). Here where things get really weird, though, because, despite this novel just being a bogstandard whodunnit, it has 1024 pages. And the reason for that is the novel being really obsessed with Twitter. There are entire chapters just being this stylized depictions of arguments on Twitter, people making Twitter threads and then when that isn't happening people are discussing what's said in these Twitter posts. And to make matters more annoying: No character is using their real name for their Twitter account and a central element of the mystery is about who's in control of what Twitter account at what time and who is responsible for posting something. It's boring but it's also weirdly obsessive when it comes to Twitter.</div> </div> </div> </div> To be fair, I'd expect as much from what happened between her and the wider internet. Almost everywhere I see her name pop up, it becomes a fight about how terrible she is. I imagine she holds the much same bitterness. Can't help but have that come out in your writing, after all, write what you know.<br /> <br /> As a side note...that actually doesn't sound like a bad premise for a book. It would be extremely niche, but it might appeal to people who regularly read, but do not participate in online conversations. and like murder mysteries. Internet murder mystery, what a world.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T09:22:00-08:00","id":1503146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503092#post1503092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, She is really obsessed with crossdressers and conflating them with trans people. Makes me wonder if that's part of what happened to her. Something has definitely caused her to fixate firmly on the idea. In any case, I hope she's getting effective therapy.<br /> <br /> (I don't know the details of her assault. Sorry, if I got it wildly wrong.)<br /> To be fair, I'd expect as much from what happened between her and the wider internet. Almost everywhere I see her name pop up, it becomes a fight about how terrible she is. I imagine she holds the much same bitterness. Can't help but have that come out in your writing, after all, write what you know.<br /> <br /> As a side note...that actually doesn't sound like a bad premise for a book. It would be extremely niche, but it might appeal to people who regularly read, but do not participate in online conversations. and like murder mysteries. Internet murder mystery, what a world.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that it's more &quot;Grinding her gears&quot; than &quot;interesting premise for a book turned into an interesting story.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T01:52:26-08:00","id":1503216,"title":"","content":"I mean I.thought the Harry Potter books sucked, the films wernt particularly enjoyable either once they stopped being cosy (?).<br /> <br /> <br /> Less severe but fly tipping enrages me and I'm becoming increasingly frustrated with the stagnant nature of pop culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T15:18:28-08:00","id":1503266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503216#post1503216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I.thought the Harry Potter books sucked, the films wernt particularly enjoyable either once they stopped being cosy (?).<br /> <br /> <br /> Less severe but fly tipping enrages me and I'm becoming increasingly frustrated with the stagnant nature of pop culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're definitely not as good as people's engagement with it might suggest-I by and large agree with Ursula K Le Guin's take on it-but there <i>are</i> things to take away from them, from a craft perspective, and they were a net positive in terms of their effect in raising interest in literacy on a global scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T15:30:17-08:00","id":1503267,"title":"","content":"It helped that they (mostly) aged up with the primary demographic. Which is fairly obvious at this point, but still an important factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T15:46:28-08:00","id":1503269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503267#post1503267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helped that they (mostly) aged up with the primary demographic. Which is fairly obvious at this point, but still an important factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, in terms of marketing, Harry Potter is basically a masterclass, particularly this point. They're just not well-written stories","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T16:05:42-08:00","id":1503272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503216#post1503216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less severe but fly tipping enrages me and I'm becoming increasingly frustrated with the stagnant nature of pop culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fly tipping? What\u2019s that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T16:27:01-08:00","id":1503275,"title":"","content":"Fly tipping is a phrase for illegally dumping garbage (that is, a sizeable step up from simple littering). IME it's usually used when people either pile trash next to a full container, or place trash that doesn't belong in the type of contain present next to it. Both lead to trash piling up, and someone needs to do a serious clean up as both normal use of bins/etc. is being blocked and the unsanitary nature of people just tossing more on the pile as there seems to be a point where people just treat the mess as permission to make it worse..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T02:46:41-08:00","id":1503310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503052#post1503052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel sorry for Rowling,because I feel like I understand her. I dont agree with her of course,but I understand. Rowling grow up dirtu poor,i grow up almost as dirty poor.<br /> after analyzing her tweets and the wiki page on her Rowling's political views,I feel like she sees that trans folks are &quot;hogging&quot; all the welfare ,Rowling feels that trans people are getting all the help they need and the people who are dirty poor and are suffering in poverty are not getting help by virtue of being cis. That's her problem with trans people,it's not that they are teans is that in Rowling view everyone is so focused in helping trans people they are forgetting the victims of poverty and abuse like Rowling herself was. She's not right,of course,but it hard to blame her,she's been hurt a great deal before she lucked out by writing a few books people liked</div> </div> </div> </div>She lost the last of my charitability the week Roe vs. Wade was overturned. It's clear what she cares the most about and it isn't a woman's right to bodily autonomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T06:11:39-08:00","id":1503313,"title":"","content":"Not that she needs defending (and she's shown to me in plenty of ways that she doesn't deserve a lick of pity or emotional charity), I'm pretty sure the viral tweet about the Dobbs decision was fake. Maybe you're thinking of something else, but pretty much ever major Internet factchecker worth looking at seem to agree that an account that wasn't her official account sent that out, while her main account was tweeting against the ruling.<br /> <br /> Not that it absolves her of all the other crap, but she has been fairly consistent in her second wave feminist views (for good and a lot of ill).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T08:28:02-08:00","id":1503317,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about the tweet, I'm not thinking of anyone else. I know she's opposed to Roe vs. Wade being overturned... but, how many tweets is that compared to platforming transphobes many of whom are openly anti-abortion conservatives? Like what would you say the ratio of it is?<br /> <br /> Hence no more charity. She'd be happy as a wife in Gilead as long as she got to punch down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-17-2023, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T14:07:30-08:00","id":1503340,"title":"","content":"I completely agree with your conclusion there, she lost any charity from me way befor that. It just seemed odd to single out that specific event (esp. when there was a viral fake post around, which I feel hurts the cause of pointing out how shitty of a person she is when her real actions are plenty).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T10:44:04-08:00","id":1503388,"title":"","content":"I tried to read Rowling's Cormaran Strike series and found it quite poorly written and the main characters weren't all that likeable and it sounds like it wasn't just me on this board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T12:49:37-08:00","id":1503396,"title":"","content":"Since there's been a lot of razzing, I do want to say...not a good thing about it, but still get out a disappointment: There's a lot that's frustrating about The Strike Series, but perhaps the most frustrating is that the theory for them being good is there. Dearest JK is a little too forward with her foreshadowing to be as strong as she can be with the mystery genre, but her solid sense of pacing and commitment to setup and payoff(for the most part) is a good cornerstone for the genre, and while she's not so great at hiding the conclusion, she's at least good enough to get people to consider the alternate possibilities. All of that is more than can be said about a fair number of writers in the genre today, and if she could just keep focus on the story as a story to tell, she could be....not one of the greats, but reliably a staple writer for the genre, the sort of person where if you don't know what to listen to on a road trip, you could get one of her books and have a reliably entertaining enough ride.<br /> <br /> And, like, so many writers wish they could be reliably just-above mediocrity in a genre like that. And she is instead blowing it on this instead.<br /> <br /> Honestly, what she needs to do, asides from stop being TERF, a classist, and a nationalist, is to write the YA actual detective version of Harry Dresden. And yes, I realize I said she just need to write Harry Potter Again, but without the chosen one narrative this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T15:58:13-08:00","id":1503405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503092#post1503092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, She is really obsessed with crossdressers and conflating them with trans people. \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>She's not conflating them, she's looking for ways to disguise her transphobia. Nothing the creator in Ink Black Heart gets harassed for has anything to do with transphobia... there is an issue with ableism in connection with a <i>hermaphroditic </i>character, though.<br /> <br /> Of course, you have to look at these things in the light of a stringent transphobe writing the book and trying to hide her very personal stances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503092#post1503092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note...that actually doesn't sound like a bad premise for a book. It would be extremely niche, but it might appeal to people who regularly read, but do not participate in online conversations. and like murder mysteries. Internet murder mystery, what a world.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically, yes. But the mystery is bogstandard, it's busywork that wins the day... and the book sadly hurts you to get that message. A thousand pages for a crime this banal and petty is a new crime in itself. There's nothing extraordinary or interesting about the crime... And yet readers have to suffer through all those tweets in order to realize... &quot;Oh, it's just another one of those.&quot;There's no surprise or revelation waiting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T23:53:26-08:00","id":1503430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503317#post1503317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about the tweet, I'm not thinking of anyone else. I know she's opposed to Roe vs. Wade being overturned... but, how many tweets is that compared to platforming transphobes many of whom are openly anti-abortion conservatives? Like what would you say the ratio of it is?<br /> <br /> Hence no more charity. She'd be happy as a wife in Gilead as long as she got to punch down.</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion is terfs discredited themselves with roe vs wade when it should have been all hands in deck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:29:43-08:00","id":1503479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503430#post1503430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My opinion is terfs discredited themselves with roe vs wade when it should have been all hands in deck.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird... By feverishly denouncing transwomen their positions drift into some very conservative positions regarding women. Like, in order to oppose transwomen they make arguments like &quot;the most sacred duty of women is to be a mother&quot;. And even when they don't say it openly, Terfs are more than happy to ally themselves with groups that are deeply conservative and misogynistic.<br /> <br /> From a <a href=\"https://www.vox.com/identities/2019/9/5/20840101/terfs-radical-feminists-gender-critical\" target=\"_blank\">Vox-article about Terfs</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anti-trans alliances with conservative groups are by no means new for gender-critical feminists. During the Irish referendum on abortion rights in 2018, some British gender-critical feminists withheld support for campaigners who supported abortion rights, citing the trans supportive attitudes of Irish feminism, going so far as to schedule an anti-trans meeting in Dublin at the height of the campaign season. Irish feminists responded with a scathing open letter denouncing the event and reaffirming their support for the womanhood of trans women. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:55:35-08:00","id":1503481,"title":"","content":"That was kinda what I was trying to say. If apparently quite poorly. The TERFs/GCs have been showing themselves as putting being anti-trans over being actual feminists for a long time now.<br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> On a completely separate note: I really hope this week can settle on a temperature. Last week having three 15+ degree temp shifts is completely destroying my brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T13:18:24-08:00","id":1503483,"title":"","content":"if i may change the subject a little,i wish the idea that the &quot; jobs of a country should be primaliry for those born on that country &quot; would go away,a job should go to the most qualified. The plumbing job goes for the best plumber,the engineeering job goes for the best engineers and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T14:25:57-08:00","id":1503490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503483#post1503483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if i may change the subject a little,i wish the idea that the &quot; jobs of a country should be primaliry for those born on that country &quot; would go away,a job should go to the most qualified. The plumbing job goes for the best plumber,the engineeering job goes for the best engineers and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, the people who are making that argument aren't thinking of the jobs where it pays to have someone with specialized knowledge or skill where qualification matters a whole lot and more towards the low end jobs they think non-national citizens are getting as opposed to the average national joes. Of course, since they're often thinking in nationalistic terms (and often racist and religious discriminatory terms) and not accounting for the nature of the jobs that they often get shoved into (both the jobs that no one wants to do and &quot;the jobs no one wants to do&quot;) or the exploitative reasons they getting hired (cheaper wages because they're not obliged to by the law to pay them like a citizen, better control over them and greater ability to force compliance due to holding the deport card over them for increased exploitation of labor), those people can go fuck themselves.<br /> <br /> But, uh, yeah, the people who are saying that aren't exactly thinking of people coming in on a work visa.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Unrelated, god fucking damnit, these cases at work can move, I need my people to stop arbitrarily stopping them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-19-2023, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T21:43:02-08:00","id":1503513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503479#post1503479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's weird... By feverishly denouncing transwomen their positions drift into some very conservative positions regarding women. Like, in order to oppose transwomen they make arguments like &quot;the most sacred duty of women is to be a mother&quot;. And even when they don't say it openly, Terfs are more than happy to ally themselves with groups that are deeply conservative and misogynistic.<br /> <br /> From a <a href=\"https://www.vox.com/identities/2019/9/5/20840101/terfs-radical-feminists-gender-critical\" target=\"_blank\">Vox-article about Terfs</a>:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine undermining your own rights and long terms interests because you hate a tiny demographic just that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T09:08:34-08:00","id":1503526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503430#post1503430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My opinion is terfs discredited themselves with roe vs wade when it should have been all hands in deck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I at least know a few people IRL who'd previously fallen for some of their talking points who finally woke up because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T10:43:26-08:00","id":1503534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503513#post1503513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine undermining your own rights and long terms interests because you hate a tiny demographic just that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transphobia is insane, especially when it transitions to becoming a moral panic of some sort. It's all based on nightmarish scenarios of what-ifs and wild speculation.<br /> <br /> And then it also doesn't help when media buys into the &quot;hype&quot; of this moral panic. The New York Times just recently went through it. Early this year Tom Scocca <a href=\"https://popula.com/2023/01/29/the-worst-thing-we-read-this-week-why-is-the-new-york-times-so-obsessed-with-trans-kids/\" target=\"_blank\">wrote about the NYT's strange obsession with trans people</a>. And then people writing for the paper signed an <a href=\"https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2023/02/new-york-times-trans-coverage\" target=\"_blank\">open letter</a> recently with concerns about the coverage. And only a couple of days after that the New York Times published a <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2023/02/16/opinion/jk-rowling-transphobia.html\" target=\"_blank\">column</a> by Pamela Paul called &quot;In Defense Of JK Rowling&quot;...<br /> <br /> (The Onion also had a great parody of the NYT's dismissal of the open letter with its article called <a href=\"https://www.theonion.com/it-is-journalism-s-sacred-duty-to-endanger-the-lives-of-1850126997\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;It Is Journalism\u2019s Sacred Duty To Endanger The Lives Of As Many Trans People As Possible&quot;</a>.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T12:16:24-08:00","id":1503543,"title":"","content":"Why are car exhaust filters so expensive? And why would anyone build a machine without easy access to a part that regularly needs maintenance?<br /> <br /> Also, I really really don\u2019t care for the argument I\u2019ve recently experienced that trans people are apparently tricking people by being themselves. I don\u2019t get that mindset at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T12:22:37-08:00","id":1503544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503543#post1503543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are car exhaust filters so expensive? And why would anyone build a machine without easy access to a part that regularly needs maintenance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cynically? So that maintenance is more difficult and likely to be neglected, ultimately forcing you to buy a new car more frequently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T12:26:34-08:00","id":1503545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503544#post1503544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cynically? So that maintenance is more difficult and likely to be neglected, ultimately forcing you to buy a new car more frequently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda like how phones always seem to have major issues right before the next wave of phones are released? Yeah, I can see it. Unfortunately, I had to get this car used, so I\u2019m dealing with all the problems the previous owner didn\u2019t want to deal with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T12:27:48-08:00","id":1503547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503543#post1503543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are car exhaust filters so expensive? And why would anyone build a machine without easy access to a part that regularly needs maintenance?<br /> <br /> Also, I really really don\u2019t care for the argument I\u2019ve recently experienced that trans people are apparently tricking people by being themselves. I don\u2019t get that mindset at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of it is, in refusing to accept trans people as their gender, certain people getting mad about aesthetic or sexual attraction only to discover the person in question doesn't fit their preconceived notions of what's suppsoed to make them feel that, and the overall misconception that making something previously binary and simple complex and nuanced isn't for the purposes of accruately being and presenting one's self, but can only be for the purpose of trying to confuse and bamboozle them, often as part of some kind of scam.<br /> <br /> No idea about the car exhaust filters, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T12:34:11-08:00","id":1503548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503544#post1503544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cynically? So that maintenance is more difficult and likely to be neglected, ultimately forcing you to buy a new car more frequently.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other option is that your diligent about maintenance, but they force you to bring your car to their dealership, buy their parts, and so on, locking you into a monopolistic ecosystem where they can charge you far more than if third party repair shops had a fair shot. Most dealership repair shops get a fair larger share of the money you spend on repairs/parts than buying a whole new car.<br /> <br /> Manufactures win either way when they can do this. Once it becomes industry standard (like cellphones are as noted) your choice in buying has a hidden aspect of not just which product you want, but which company's ecosystem you want to be locked into for the duration of your ownership of the product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T12:48:16-08:00","id":1503551,"title":"","content":"'S a pity biking is so infeasible in most of the US.<br /> <br /> Edit: it IS worth noting though that we seem to be cramming more and more tech -both engine and electronics- into the same amount of space. So the less cynical-and not necessarily mutually exclusive- take is that there just isn't enough space without sweeping innovation or compromising the frame","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-20-2023, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T13:05:23-08:00","id":1503553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503551#post1503551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'S a pity biking is so infeasible in most of the US.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between my time as a Mormon missionary and my time in Japan, I have these deep and abiding want of a city where anything I want to reach can be done by public transport, walking, or biking. I originally planned on getting a commuter bike with plenty of space for storage after my mission, only to realize just how badly cities are built for independent car ownership. I just wanna bike to and from my grocery store, damnit!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-20-2023, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T13:13:08-08:00","id":1503556,"title":"","content":"Nah you can keep being plenty cynical about it.<br /> <br /> There are a few exceptions: changing standards in road vehicles has lead to oil filters being a lot hard to get to than they used to be if you don't have a pneumatic lift. But any third party lube/oil change place is completely unaffected by that. It just makes it harder on DIY folks. But for the most part there's more space in your car than ever. The electronics continue to get smaller, and continue to replace bulkier mechanical systems.<br /> <br /> What the advances in tech do, is just make it harder to amass the knowledge needed to fix anything yourself. What you used to be able to do with a simple jack and some basic hand tools, now requires specialized tools, understanding electronics, and being an IT pro all at the same time so you don't short out a wire and ruin a part by wiping some bit of code. If you need $10K worth of equipment to save yourself $1K in repair bills a year that might not all remain useful when you get your next car anyway, people are just going to give up on doing it themselves. Companies could absolutely make this easier; but they have no reason to on their own.<br /> <br /> There's a reason it was a huge legal win for farmers for &quot;right to repair&quot; laws to get passed to limit the ability of major agriculture machines to force customers into ridiculous costs to keep their gear running. That's really the only kind of way to fix this (baring a major change in global economics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T13:32:26-08:00","id":1503562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503553#post1503553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Between my time as a Mormon missionary and my time in Japan, I have these deep and abiding want of a city where anything I want to reach can be done by public transport, walking, or biking. I originally planned on getting a commuter bike with plenty of space for storage after my mission, only to realize just how badly cities are built for independent car ownership. I just wanna bike to and from my grocery store, damnit!</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly miss living in Singapore sometimes. Nice city, and the public transit is fantastic. Or it was when I was there a good decade and a half ago, things may have changed since then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T10:17:46-08:00","id":1503902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503481#post1503481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was kinda what I was trying to say. If apparently quite poorly. The TERFs/GCs have been showing themselves as putting being anti-trans over being actual feminists for a long time now.<br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> On a completely separate note: I really hope this week can settle on a temperature. Last week having three 15+ degree temp shifts is completely destroying my brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to have + 15 degree temp right now, but alas spring and summer are still a ways off and I think we are due for one more cold snap like we had this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T10:41:07-08:00","id":1503904,"title":"","content":"A positive jump up 15 degrees one day, and then dropping by 10 the next day, really isn't the same as it going up 5 degrees consistently. I don't mind slightly colder parts of the year personally, but it looks like in February around here,we'll have had five days of ridiculously high temps for winter, immediately followed by freezing temps in the following two or three days. Which is hell for my personal health issues,and also really hard on the environment as it can really mess up plants if too many of them think spring is starting and then freeze badly when it was a false heat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T19:28:54-08:00","id":1503922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503904#post1503904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A positive jump up 15 degrees one day, and then dropping by 10 the next day, really isn't the same as it going up 5 degrees consistently. I don't mind slightly colder parts of the year personally, but it looks like in February around here,we'll have had five days of ridiculously high temps for winter, immediately followed by freezing temps in the following two or three days. Which is hell for my personal health issues,and also really hard on the environment as it can really mess up plants if too many of them think spring is starting and then freeze badly when it was a false heat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just got finished recovering from a 3-day sinus infection caused by exactly this sort of scenario. It keeps jumping up to 63-65 and then falling down to 36-38, making my sinuses miserable and wrecking havoc on my allergies. And people STILL wanna think climate change isn't a problem!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T15:35:23-08:00","id":1503998,"title":"","content":"All this talk of cities and public transportation; Buenos Aires, by far, has the best public-transportation system; second, was SLC, except when it broke down. As for a vent: <i>Los porte</i>\u00f1<i>os son boludos y te robar\u00e1n su camisa de su espalda.</i><br /> <br /> In Bs. As., the buses show up every ten minutes and their three of them; and it costs like $0.27USD to ride them. The UTA in SLC, Ut., has the honor-system where you tap on and tap off, but I always forgot to tap-off so wouldn't tap-on. The Transit-Police, will inspect the trains on occasions. Then, you'll see a bunch of homeless-people up and run out the door because they could get arrested for not having a pass. With the card, they don't care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T17:59:28-08:00","id":1504010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1503998#post1503998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All this talk of cities and public transportation; Buenos Aires, by far, has the best public-transportation system; second, was SLC, except when it broke down. As for a vent: <i>Los porte</i>\u00f1<i>os son boludos y te robar\u00e1n su camisa de su espalda.</i><br /> <br /> In Bs. As., the buses show up every ten minutes and their three of them; and it costs like $0.27USD to ride them. The UTA in SLC, Ut., has the honor-system where you tap on and tap off, but I always forgot to tap-off so wouldn't tap-on. The Transit-Police, will inspect the trains on occasions. Then, you'll see a bunch of homeless-people up and run out the door because they could get arrested for not having a pass. With the card, they don't care.</div> </div> </div> </div>SLC directly I can't account for, but public transport in Happy Valley in general was abysmal. There are whole areas that your only hope of getting to was Uber and other such things, which on a secrutiy guard's pay was eating up every scrap of cash I made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T15:20:00-08:00","id":1504077,"title":"","content":"Two utterly petty things - <br /> <br /> First, I've got a pretty deep widow's peak, so I prefer to just shave my head. Unfortunately, my head hair also grows so slowly that I can't get a nice, clean shave unless I wait three or four days. So I get a day or two of smooth, and another two days looking like I'm fesh out of boot camp. I'm almost tempted to look into Nair or some other defoliator.<br /> <br /> Second, I tried re-installing a mobile game I used to play for nostalgia. It's effing massive though, so only my tablet had enough storage space for it. I don't know if it was just never meant to run on a tablet or if my tablet is just a potato/damaged, but MAN does the game not run well. It takes several minutes for it to load the login screen, and it sure as heck isn't stable once I'm in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T17:26:06-08:00","id":1504086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1504077#post1504077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two utterly petty things -<br /> <br /> First, I've got a pretty deep widow's peak, so I prefer to just shave my head. Unfortunately, my head hair also grows so slowly that I can't get a nice, clean shave unless I wait three or four days. So I get a day or two of smooth, and another two days looking like I'm fesh out of boot camp. I'm almost tempted to look into Nair or some other defoliator.<br /> <br /> Second, I tried re-installing a mobile game I used to play for nostalgia. It's effing massive though, so only my tablet had enough storage space for it. I don't know if it was just never meant to run on a tablet or if my tablet is just a potato/damaged, but MAN does the game not run well. It takes several minutes for it to load the login screen, and it sure as heck isn't stable once I'm in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna hazard a guess of it being Honkai Impact 3rd.<br /> <br /> And yeah, they make Nair for the hed, and I'd wager it's worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"ra