aker crap; so, you're constantly throwing other people under the bus and when you get thrown under, you cry like a little b*tch. I bet you got an early release for all your snitching. <br /> <br /> And thank you for texting me; you reminded me I have to talk to some attorneys over your BS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T00:46:53-08:00","id":1504247,"title":"","content":"Less an angry-vent and more something I find sad is how Japan's default response to their <i>rapidly</i> dropping population and looming social crisis is to ponder how to boost birth rates. Immigration apparently isnt even worth considering. Like... I legit think they're willing to let themselves go &quot;extinct&quot; as it were, rather than give up that isolationism.<br /> <br /> I was born here, and I'm glad I got to see the country as an adult, but the steadily dying town I'm working for is a bleak microcosm of some fairly depressing xenophobia issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T21:37:56-08:00","id":1504534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1504247#post1504247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less an angry-vent and more something I find sad is how Japan's default response to their <i>rapidly</i> dropping population and looming social crisis is to ponder how to boost birth rates. Immigration apparently isnt even worth considering. Like... I legit think they're willing to let themselves go &quot;extinct&quot; as it were, rather than give up that isolationism.<br /> <br /> I was born here, and I'm glad I got to see the country as an adult, but the steadily dying town I'm working for is a bleak microcosm of some fairly depressing xenophobia issues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> isn't japan's population decline due to economic factors so immigration would be a stop gap at best?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-06-2023, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T22:21:54-08:00","id":1504538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1504534#post1504534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> isn't japan's population decline due to economic factors so immigration would be a stop gap at best?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yyyyyes and no. Part of their economic situation is how weak the Yen is, which is a combination of several factors. But more pressing for them is the fact that the way their social security system is set up relies very heavily on there being a young population to support the old. Like most first-world countries, their elderly population is growing and the proportional population of youth is dropping, but they don't have <i>any </i>of the triage or mitigation like most other countries derive from immigrants. <br /> <br /> As to why the population is on the decline purely in terms of births... yeah. A good chunk of it is the same as other places -the malaise and sense of hopelessness- but there's also the cost of living in cities where space is at such a premium, and the work culture is so all-consuming. They might be able to stretch things further if they were to invest more in remote/teleworking, but the traditionalist bent of the country means its going to be even harder to make that wide spread. Hell, I can't even access an ATM after buisness hours because old folks are worried about not being able to talk to a real person - that one line in Mage Core on Tokyo was frustratingly accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T23:32:37-08:00","id":1504543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1504538#post1504538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yyyyyes and no. Part of their economic situation is how weak the Yen is, which is a combination of several factors. But more pressing for them is the fact that the way their social security system is set up relies very heavily on there being a young population to support the old. Like most first-world countries, their elderly population is growing and the proportional population of youth is dropping, but they don't have <i>any </i>of the triage or mitigation like most other countries derive from immigrants.<br /> <br /> As to why the population is on the decline purely in terms of births... yeah. A good chunk of it is the same as other places -the malaise and sense of hopelessness- but there's also the cost of living in cities where space is at such a premium, and the work culture is so all-consuming. They might be able to stretch things further if they were to invest more in remote/teleworking, but the traditionalist bent of the country means its going to be even harder to make that wide spread. Hell, I can't even access an ATM after buisness hours because old folks are worried about not being able to talk to a real person - that one line in Mage Core on Tokyo was frustratingly accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds even more like bringing in immigrants would be a stop gap solution and puts a bit grimer angle on my own countries historically more open policies. It sounds more like the country needs major internal economic reforms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T01:08:44-08:00","id":1504553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1504543#post1504543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds 