do errands because even the few things close enough not to drive to include multiple sections with no good bike and/or pedestrian paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T23:48:31-07:00","id":1507378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1507366#post1507366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangential vent:<br /> <br /> I really hate living in an area with shit non-car travel options. I grew up with access to good public transit, and I miss being able use commute time on things besides not getting into accidents. I can't even cycle to do errands because even the few things close enough not to drive to include multiple sections with no good bike and/or pedestrian paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the absolute worst, right? Cauthon and I had this rant a few pages back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T00:10:03-07:00","id":1507379,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://images.app.goo.gl/qxgAXmwFCrk298zA9\" target=\"_blank\">This infographic</a> always best expresses my frustrations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T02:13:44-07:00","id":1507380,"title":"","content":"My frustrations are slightly different, but only because I live in a very rural area in the US. A lot more of our problems are funding related than urban planning related. For example, all of our buses only go from small towns to the one thing we call a city around here (and it's not that big by city standards). There's no ring routes that connect the outlying towns. Despite the fact that we actually have roads a bus could easily handle, there's no buses that string together a bunch of towns in a row. You can drive, or you can take the bus to the city, and then take a second bus back out to the next town over (if you're lucky that will only take an hour, and they stop real early).<br /> <br /> We have miles of train tracks that basically only get used once a week that services agriculture. It's in use, so it's not like it needs to be fixed up or anything. It can handle a 50 car train full of corn, it can handle some light rail cars between towns.<br /> <br /> And of course, everyone complains about parking (these are small towns, there's no big parking lots or parking garages, street parking is competing with residential parking) and how there's no way to really build more parking because that would require demolishing people's homes. But suggest the idea that we increase transit that doesn't need parking and people act like you're asking them to fund the entire US military budget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T02:20:24-07:00","id":1507383,"title":"","content":"How's the population looking around where you live? On the rise, stagnant, or on the decline?<br /> <br /> The small towns around where my grandparents live are very much on the decline, which makes it really hard to justify the costs for maintaining public transit.<br /> <br /> Granted, that's rural North Dakota, where public transit is... ah... hard to justify in general. But something similar is happening here in rural Hokkaido, in that the increasingly elderly populations mean that the costs for maintaining the transit systems are slowly becoming untenable and unjustifiable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T05:36:38-07:00","id":1507396,"title":"","content":"Our county is technically growing, but marginally so (about +0.5% last year). It's relatively inexpensive on basic living expenses, and has good access to both local and interstate highways. So as we're losing small farms and other rural staples to megafarms, we're replacing with commuter communities that want quaint small town life that's not too far from major cities. We do have some mass transit, it just doesn't extend well beyond the only &quot;big city&quot; in the county. We also have an Amtrak station that has remarkably good prices to get to Philadelphia (which means depending your budget and schedule, gives you a lot of options as a major transit hub).<br /> <br /> My town is shrinking (rural very conservative, very poor retention rates of the 18-36 cohorts between jobs and social environment, and the only retirement communities/homes nearby are technically in other municipalities so we're losing on that end even faster too) though there's a serious mismanagement issue since the towns to the east, south, and west of us are all growing (and attracting young families in droves compared to us) despite no drastic economic/etc. differences. A lot of it comes down to our town being convinced to not invest in itself, while the towns around us all are, turning it into a self-fulfilling prophesy. For example, we used to be the only town in our little cluster that had an actual public swimming pool (and it was really nice with lots of space and different swim areas, surrounding by a park with cheap pavilion rentals for events, and it's across the street from the high school). But it hasn't been updated in 20 years because the people in charge of thing don't see it as a reason to get people to move here (and the tax revenue they'd bring with them to offset some red in the ledger for the pool) Less upkeep, less use, less use, less cash flow, less cash, less upkeep, etc. On top of that, in the meantime, the town to the east of us did a public-private partnership rec-center, and a full private rec-center opened in an unincorporated area between the towns to the south and west of us. So we went from drawing in all our neighbors to a nice local public pool (and all the economic impact for local businesses that meant), to everyone paying 3 to 5 times as much, but for equally better facilities that are way more than a pool.<br /> <br /> Those three neighboring towns are also building pretty good local tourism attractions. They loosened laws so there's actually night life stuff. You can spend a weekend, or even a week, in them and actually having something do to if you're just visiting. If we get better transit here, it's because we'd be leaching off of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-04-2023, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T10:53:12-07:00","id":1507417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1507366#post1507366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangential vent:<br /> <br /> I really hate living in an area with shit non-car travel options. I grew up with access to good public transit, and I miss being able use commute time on things besides not getting into accidents. I can't even cycle to do errands because even the few things close enough not to drive to include multiple sections with no good bike and/or pedestrian paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the weather is good. I'd just use my pedal bike or walk to my favorite places. Of course it helped that everything was pretty close by and we have good biking and walking trials near my home.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T03:32:20-07:00","id":1507469,"title":"","content":"That is sort of the problem though. While it's &quot;only&quot; two miles for me to go to most of the places I'd need to get to, that's two miles on an extremely busy road that has no bike lanes, frequently doesn't have sidewalks, and if there is any curb space, it's used for on-street parking. If I just want to cycle to a friend's house or something, and I don't mind some exertion on the way? It's no big deal. But if I want to take a bike that can carry a few grocery bags? It's a huge safety risk. If I want to get in my basic errands on safe roads, I'd be added 2.5 extra miles one way, and have to go up and back down a significant hill on top of it (not so bad with an empty bike... but again, doing errands and having a bunch of groceries or some stuff from the hardware store...). But that's also swapping a modern well maintained but heavily trafficked road for a bunch of rural roads with blind corners, and people going insanely fast because we don't have a police force that could possibly hope to patrol the size of the area to keep that down (and the number of crosses on the sides of the road at certain intersections is depressing in how little it seems to deter some people of overdoing it).<br /> <br /> It's just... so close to actually being more bike friendly because it's a small rural town, but everyone drives for work/etc. that they made things that could be non-car friendly into non-car unfriendly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T09:36:03-07:00","id":1507488,"title":"","content":"I hear you on that point Heavy Arms, I don't like biking on busy city streets where I live and I see way to many drivers on there phones and not paying attention. So I stick to the biking and hiking trails when I can and I lucked out on location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T07:49:41-07:00","id":1507767,"title":"","content":"<br /> I just read the <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/08/us/court-decision-invalidating-approval-of-mifepristone.html\" target=\"_blank\">Texas' judge's opinion</a>, in which he declared that the FDA could not allow the sale of Mifepristone, and I see where he's going. It's not going to be pretty.<br /> <br /> Judge Kacsmaryk repeatedly mentions the Comstock Act throughout his opinion, and notes that the FDA repeatedly violated the Comstock Act, and that this is the primary reason for his ruling. In other words, the Comstock Act is the cornerstone on which his decision rests. Now, the Comstock Act was ruled unconstitutional by the Supreme Court back in 1965 in Griswald v. Connecticut.<br /> <br /> If you remember last year when the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, Justice Thomas specifically called out several other Supreme Court rulings that he believed were &quot;wrongly decided&quot; based on the &quot;erroneous&quot; idea that Americans have a constitutional right to privacy. Among those rulings he listed Griswald.<br /> <br /> By basing his entire decision around the Comstock Act, this judge is basically setting the Supreme Court up to overrule Griswald. In sports terms, it's like in volleyball where one player gently tosses the ball so his partner can spike it. That's basically what Judge Kacsmaryk is doing with his legal decision. I fully expect that by next year, the Supreme Court will overrule Griswald.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T17:12:38-07:00","id":1507800,"title":"","content":"I mean, everyone paying attention saw this coming. They shopped specifically for Kacsmaryk because he cares more about legislating away rights from the bench than being a judge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T20:13:43-07:00","id":1507824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1507767#post1507767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By basing his entire decision around the Comstock Act, this judge is basically setting the Supreme Court up to overrule Griswald. In sports terms, it's like in volleyball where one player gently tosses the ball so his partner can spike it. That's basically what Judge Kacsmaryk is doing with his legal decision. I fully expect that by next year, the Supreme Court will overrule Griswald.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me even more concerned about Florida apparently trying to set up their own Brown Shirts. Even if I'm never planning to ever go there, that's a <i>bad</i> precedent to be getting as much serious consideration as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T20:17:01-07:00","id":1507826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1507824#post1507824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes me even more concerned about Florida apparently trying to set up their own Brown Shirts. Even if I'm never planning to ever go there, that's a <i>bad</i> precedent to be getting as much serious consideration as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what\u2019s been going on with Florida? I\u2019ve seen references to it everywhere on the internet, but nobody seems to go into details and the news on the internet hasn\u2019t been helpful either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T20:26:00-07:00","id":1507828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1507826#post1507826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what\u2019s been going on with Florida? I\u2019ve seen references to it everywhere on the internet, but nobody seems to go into details and the news on the internet hasn\u2019t been helpful either.</div> </div> </div> </div>DeSantis is proposing a civilian military force in Florida that answers only to him. No Federal oversight, just the &quot;Florida State Guard&quot;. Which, given that he already nominally has the National Guard for Florida answering to him, just shows that the only reason he'd want this thing would be for... well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T20:32:30-07:00","id":1507829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1507828#post1507828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> DeSantis is proposing a civilian military force in Florida that answers only to him. No Federal oversight, just the &quot;Florida State Guard&quo