":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T00:52:33-07:00","id":1508859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1508848#post1508848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buying a game on Steam and only then seeing there's $570 worth of DLC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. Get to it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T10:30:20-07:00","id":1508906,"title":"","content":"i wish people didn't fight so much about movies and they'd just agree to disagree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T18:44:43-07:00","id":1508964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1508906#post1508906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i wish people didn't fight so much about movies and they'd just agree to disagree</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, depends on the film. If a person's favorite film is Triumph of the Will, there's a minimum of two grounds to punch them until they beg for mercy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T19:37:35-07:00","id":1508974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1508964#post1508964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, depends on the film. If a person's favorite film is Triumph of the Will, there's a minimum of two grounds to punch them until they beg for mercy.</div> </div> </div> </div>i'm talking about more about superhero and scifi films","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T20:01:34-07:00","id":1508976,"title":"","content":"The lack of good faith in some arguments that revolve around certain movies get into those genres plenty. Sci-fi and superhero films have a huge history of being allegories promoting social justice and the benefits of diversity. I would love to have in-depth discussions of the pros and cons of certain films on various artistic measures, I far too often see people getting upset over things that make me wonder why they like the genre or specific franchise in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T09:14:06-07:00","id":1509044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1508976#post1508976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of good faith in some arguments that revolve around certain movies get into those genres plenty. Sci-fi and superhero films have a huge history of being allegories promoting social justice and the benefits of diversity. I would love to have in-depth discussions of the pros and cons of certain films on various artistic measures, I far too often see people getting upset over things that make me wonder why they like the genre or specific franchise in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I lots of times wonder the same thing or why certain writers or directors get gigs on genres they don't like or have no interest in learning more of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T10:43:37-07:00","id":1509066,"title":"","content":"How often do you really know what a director feels? I've seen plenty of accusations fly at various folks that never seem to really be based in much.<br /> <br /> Like I don't want to see Tim Burton touch any story that centers around Jewish source material, because he's explicitly stated that if he finds a story interesting, he feels it's better to retell the story without its roots to make the story &quot;for everyone.&quot; There's interviews of him responding to criticism about his tendency to perform Jewish erasure as a director (notably in The Corpse Bride and Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children), so I've seen what he's said knowing he's going to be asked about it, and I find it... unpleasant to say the least.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, I've seen dozens of online people claim that So-and-So doesn't like [genre/franchise/etc.] because of some out of context quote that really amounted to, &quot;I loved the original material, but I wanted to tell something new.&quot; A director is a creative position, so most directors want a chance to be creative, not just regurgitate what's been done in the past. The vast majority of times you can find a director seriously hated a film, is either (a) they had some sort of contract and got roped into a film they didn't really want to be doing or (b) they got fed up with executive notes until they started hating something they came in loving.<br /> <br /> There's also a weird debate going on about just how much of &quot;fans&quot; directors and other main creatives really should be; esp. when working on existing franchises/remakes/etc. Sometimes a bit of an outsider's perspective is good because most movies aren't made just for existing fans. I appreciate that Henry Cavill was frustrated by The Witcher higher ups deviating from the books, but The Witcher TV show is plenty popular, and there's a need to be flexible in adaptations. Meanwhile you have directors like Kenneth Branagh that's not really a comics or superhero kinda guy, but could draw on his love of classical theater and opera to bring out the grandiose nature of Thor to great acclaim, where Alan Taylor coming off of a lot of work on early Game of Thrones put out the least well received Thor movie so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T17:58:21-07:00","id":1509122,"title":"","content":"This might be a weird thing for a vent thread, but the DeSantis v. Disney fight and the Bud Light controversy (underlined with the internal conflict of the &quot;conservative&quot; movements of America wrestling with outraged-callers-to-and-of-action against the callers-for-dignity-and-building-reputation and the way that's actually kind of a fight now for them) is kind of fascinating to watch, even as I have to keep reminding myself it won't ultimately mean as much as it feels like right now and that whoever wins in this little scuffles, we all lose.<br /> <br /> Like, watching an angry man destroy cases of Busch Light in a Wal-Mart in Kansas doesn't bring me anything actually positive to feel, but there's something captivating about the surreality and false promise of it all. Conservatives aren't really going to have an internal civil war, which just makes all of the noisy bits that more interesting somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T18:53:27-07:00","id":1509126,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t get any of this. What does any of this actually do? What does smashing up beer actually accomplish, besides getting you arrested? And I don\u2019t get why DeSantis is going after Disney. That\u2019s not a fight he is going to win, and what does it accomplish if he does? Make everyone mad at him? I don\u2019t get politics.<br /> <br /> \u2026This is more friction to the various Conservative factions, yeah? Could lay the groundwork for the the next spark to catch light. Election is coming up right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T19:15:33-07:00","id":1509127,"title":"","content":"Reductive answer is that he's virtue-signaling to his supposed supporter base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T19:33:24-07:00","id":1509128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509126#post1509126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t get any of this. What does any of this actually do? What does smashing up beer actually accomplish, besides getting you arrested? And I don\u2019t get why DeSantis is going after Disney. That\u2019s not a fight he is going to win, and what does it accomplish if he does? Make everyone mad at him? I don\u2019t get politics.<br /> <br /> \u2026This is more friction to the various Conservative factions, yeah? Could lay the groundwork for the the next spark to catch light. Election is coming up right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No no, I get what that guy is getting out of that, and even if I didn't, I defend rioters and destruction-of-property-as-protest too much to rail against it, even if I stand against the politics behind it here. And I even get what DeSantis is thinking-it's fucking stupid, but it makes perfect sense from his perspective (and I'm not inclined to simply believe the Mouse will win it, even if the Mouse has been playing the game longer and more skillfully, because there's a lot of ways the two can and will change the rules of the game).<br /> <br /> And as I previously mentioned, I don't think it actually means anything, but all the same:<br /> <br /> There's a temptation to think that the &quot;conservative&quot; movements of America are facing a split between the free market, unregulated robber barony of capitalism inclined portion and the theocratically-flavored authoritarianism inclined portion, and that the instant that divide is finished cutting accross, we're likely to see an internal &quot;civil war&quot; whose victor would shape what &quot;conservatism&quot; in America would look like in the oncoming decades.<br /> <br /> TO a certain degree, you could argue it'd be inevitable-capitalism's infinite hunger is, at it's basest level, actually blind to what consumers are fed to it so long as it is <i>fed</i>, where as the &quot;theocrats&quot; care a whole damn lot what the patriot congregation looks like. Of course, all of that's superbly reductive and, in it's own way, optimistic in a useless way, and fails to neglect that it's made of a lot more ideas and forces than simply that and how even those two takes are intertwined in a way that is not simply cut, or indeed inclined to facilitate any such severence.<br /> <br /> But because none of this works that way, it makes it all the more fascinating is still shares that <i>look</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-20-2023, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T00:33:14-07:00","id":1509143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509066#post1509066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also a weird debate going on about just how much of &quot;fans&quot; directors and other main creatives really should be; esp. when working on existing franchises/remakes/etc. Sometimes a bit of an outsider's perspective is good because most movies aren't made just for existing fans. I appreciate that Henry Cavill was frustrated by The Witcher higher ups deviating from the books, but The Witcher TV show is plenty popular, and there's a need to be flexible in adaptations. Meanwhile you have directors like Kenneth Branagh that's not really a comics or superhero kinda guy, but could draw on his love of classical theater and opera to bring out the grandiose nature of Thor to great acclaim, where Alan Taylor coming off of a lot of work on early Game of Thrones put out the least well received Thor movie so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on this debate has always been that when deviating from the source-material is done well, nobody talks about it and when it's done badly it's the first thing that gets mentioned. Like with Witcher, I thought the first two season were good but that spin-off show Witcher Blood And Origin was terrible.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I get where this fan-outrage sometimes comes from. Like, that Halo TV show was terrible and there the showrunner openly talked about how he and the writers have never played a single second of a Halo game. I don't think you necessarily need to be a fan or be super-invested in the source-material but there needs to be some discernible reason for why it's getting adapted and it's these particular people doing it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T07:23:14-07:00","id":1509177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509126#post1509126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t get any of this. What does any of this actually do? What does smashing up beer actually accomplish, besides getting you arrested? And I don\u2019t get why DeSantis is going after Disney. That\u2019s not a fight he is going to win, and what does it accomplish if he does? Make everyone mad at him? I don\u2019t get politics.<br /> <br /> \u2026This is more friction to the various Conservative factions, yeah? Could lay the groundwork for the the next spark to catch light. Election is coming up right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Long story short, DeSantis doesn't really care if he &quot;wins&quot; or not when it comes to Disney. His goal is to become President. But before he can (realistically) run, he first needs to win the Republican Primary, which involves beating Donald Trump. During Obama's presidency, the Tea Party (extremist ideologues) started moving to the front of the Republican Party. When Trump won the nomination, many moderate Republicans left the party or were voted out. These days the more radical extremists are the ones in control of the party, and if you don't win their vote, you don't win at all.<br /> <br /> Then, keep in mind that the Republican Party doesn't really have a platform these days. In 2016 and 2020 the Republican platform was literally, &quot;We support anything Donald Trump does.&quot; So there's no firm, unifying position on a ton of issues. Having &quot;won&quot; the abortion debate with the overturning of Roe v Wade, and other than the Gun Rights argument, the only thing the Republican Party really has left is its culture war issues and its attack on gay/trans/minorities and the so-called &quot;woke&quot; issues. DeSantis is going to have a hard time standing up to Trump on nearly any issue, so what he's doing is, he's decided he wants to be the spearpoint of the Republican Party in attacking the LGBTQ+ community and other groups. His hope is that he will convince Republican voters that if elected, he will hurt those people more than Trump will, and that they will end up being willing to support him over Trump.<br /> <br /> Basically, this is the one area where DeSantis has an advantage over Trump and will be able to point towards things and say, &quot;See, I can hurt these people more than Trump ever did.&quot; That's why he's going all in on &quot;Don't Say Gay&quot;, kidnapping transgender children, etc. And ultimately it doesn't matter to him whether he &quot;beats&quot; Disney or not. Just by going after them, he generates press and shows he's willing to stand up to businesses that support gay and transgender Americans. He believes that that will help him on his path to the Oval Office, regardless of how effective (or ineffective) his attempts against Disney end up being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T09:31:36-07:00","id":1509199,"title":"","content":"I don't believe in a toxic fanbase but we do have a passionate one that are emotionally invested in certain genres or properties and we do have some that take it to far. IE I'm worried on how they will depict my favorite Star Wars character in an upcoming series which is Grand Admiral Thrawn and I hope that they will do it the style of how Timothy Zahn has written him. Unfornately it seems that Disney or others will use the one or two posters that take it to far and use it to paint legit concerns in the same camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T12:15:45-07:00","id":1509224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509199#post1509199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm worried on how they will depict my favorite Star Wars character in an upcoming series which is Grand Admiral Thrawn and I hope that they will do it the style of how Timothy Zahn has written him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the new Thrawn-trilogy by Timothy Zahn which is a prequel to his appearance in the later seasons of the Star Wars Rebels cartoon show? I liked the trilogy (the best bits were all Thrawn-centered, of course). There's also another Thrawn-trilogy (also by Timothy Zahn) about a young Thrawn rising in the ranks in the Chiss Ascendancy but I never picked up the second book after reading the first one. Honestly, I just didn't care enough about the Chiss Ascendancy.<br /> <br /> And I think the actor for the Ahsoka-show who's playing Thrawn was also the voice-actor for Thrawn in the Star Wars Rebels show. I'm wondering in general how well that Ahsoka-show will land if you haven't watched Clone Wars and/or Rebels.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T09:15:32-07:00","id":1509287,"title":"","content":"I have read nearly every Grand Admiral Thrawn book by Timothy Zahn and I even read his two books focusing on a young Mara Jade, but like you I haven't read his most recent one that focused on Thrawn's days at the Chiss military academy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T09:38:52-07:00","id":1509293,"title":"","content":"I'm not holding my breath with Disney version of Thrawn when you saw how the First Order didn't come across as scary and more sad ten anything else as the &quot;leaders&quot; came across inept clowns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T17:35:28-07:00","id":1509330,"title":"","content":"The movie with Thrawn is being directed by Filoni, who did all of the Admiral Thrawn related material with Rebels where Thrawn was treated decently (or so I hear, I haven't seen it myself). I expect that if anyone can do a decent movie with Thrawn it'll be Filoni, but I still don't have super high hopes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T17:25:45-07:00","id":1509422,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s pretty bad now that we don\u2019t have high hopes for Star Wars, Star Trek, Marvel and DC films and tv shows anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T17:35:43-07:00","id":1509423,"title":"","content":"It's not surprising, though. A TV series can easily jump the shark (my rule of thumb is about 3 seasons in most cases, but I'm enjoying Suits 5th season so far) and all the cinematic universes are is a long-form version of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-23-2023, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T19:42:44-07:00","id":1509431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509422#post1509422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s pretty bad now that we don\u2019t have high hopes for Star Wars, Star Trek, Marvel and DC films and tv shows anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Star Wars, the last thing I had high hopes for was The Old Republic MMO and that was not too good. The prequels were generally kinda bad, the sequels were even worse and just a hot mess all around, and the best stuff we've gotten for Star Wars in the last twenty years has largely been tertiary side material. With Star Trek, the last thing I enjoyed from the franchise was Deep Space Nine and that came out thirty (!) years ago. Marvel has had some incredible movies, but I feel like the formula is getting a bit long in the tooth and they need to switch things up somehow. Still, I'll look forward to a new Deadpool or Spiderman movie. As for DC, yeah... I'm not even going to talk about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T20:02:42-07:00","id":1509433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509431#post1509431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Star Trek, the last thing I enjoyed from the franchise was Deep Space Nine and that came out thirty (!) years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can recommend The Lower Decks, it's a decent show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T08:52:27-07:00","id":1509480,"title":"","content":"I think comic based movies have reached genre fatique right now and maybe a break is needed from the studios to let things recharge. But I'm not an executive at these companies who are pushing things off an assembly line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-28-2023, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T08:55:37-07:00","id":1509482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509423#post1509423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not surprising, though. A TV series can easily jump the shark (my rule of thumb is about 3 seasons in most cases, but I'm enjoying Suits 5th season so far) and all the cinematic universes are is a long-form version of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most great series peak around the 5th season and then afterwards we see a gradual decline in quality. Sure we get exceptions like NCIS, Law &amp; Order SVU and NCIS Los Angeles from time to time. But that seems to be the general rule of thumb when it comes to ongoing series.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T10:32:38-07:00","id":1509492,"title":"","content":"Even then, there are lots of reasons why decline happens. Game of Thrones largely fell apart due to them chatting up with the books and then having to wing it more in the last few seasons leading to all the horrible pacing and continuity issues (you know all the stuff GRRM hasn't finished yet).<br /> <br /> The Simpsons has lots of points people will say where when the show starting declining, but a big problem is that its premise can't support its need to stay relevant and time continues to make that basic issue worse and worse.<br /> <br /> Then you have things like Promised Neverland which completely shat the bed in its second season. For reasons nobody can really figure out, despite a wildly successful first season, they decided to cram at least two, if not three, seasons worth of material into one season and get to the end of the original story to extreme negative response. You can't cut and rush through that much plot and make it good.<br /> <br /> For me, if it's an original show, it should try to end on a high note instead of overstaying its welcome (though some formats can extend things like changing hosts), or for adaptations at least try to hit all the important beats of the original work<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Though I'd imagine we're also seeing the impact of how much Netflix hates scripted shows that last more than one or two seasons, because they focus so much on how many new users are coming in for new shows, and not even considering the loses of people that want to see shows last a season or two longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T13:29:59-07:00","id":1509516,"title":"","content":"Indeed the shows that I mentioned above were good examples of how cast changes from time to time can rejuvenate a series and see how the older cast interacts with the new ones. Usually though you need good writing to pull it off with any iota of smoothness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T13:37:41-07:00","id":1509517,"title":"","content":"So I'm picking up the feeling I've been the only one who's enjoyed the first two seasons of Picard and am looking forward to when we catch up with it after our catching up on Leverage Redemption? That accurate?<br /> <br /> As for the broader issue, yeah, there's a lot of brand fatique, and the exploitation of nostalgia is starting to lose returns. As Yahtzee Croshaw put it, you can't miss something if it never goes away, and with that I imagine we're all ready for a significant sea change in term of properties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T13:49:18-07:00","id":1509519,"title":"","content":"I think one important thing that needs to be considered here: One reason you would favor a multitude of one-or-two-season-shows is - money. The reason is that if you use unionized labor (both in terms of &quot;in front of the camera&quot; and &quot;behind the camera&quot;), depending on the union salaries <i>have to</i> go up in the second or the third season. So a third season is <i>really bad</i> if you want to save money.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is just the sort of greedy short-term-thinking you'd expect from corporations. Like, what do you think made more money: 10 whodunnit-shows from the early 00s that ran for one or two seasons that these days most people have never heard of or... Law &amp; Order? But the model Netflix is operating on is to bet on those 10 whodunnit-shows instead. And it's not going great of course...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T15:00:02-07:00","id":1509632,"title":"","content":"My current contract is up in August, so I've been working to secure a job for when I get back to the states. Which went well! Got a couple of offers, and accepted one. They all required joining the Reserve, which was fine, I was already in the IRR.<br /> <br /> Only this morning, I get a text telling me that the Army discharged me from the IRR and the Army as a whole a month ago. I'm so confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:52:09-07:00","id":1509729,"title":"","content":"I hate it when a new supervisor is hired and goes on a power trip and thinks he or she is so great and disrespects employees who been working at there jobs for a long time and get blow back from such behavior and act all shocked.<br /> <br /> I guess that the handbook that said that you should treat experienced employees with courtesy and respect was left out in the interview and HR wonders why they can't keep staff or why supervisors can't get there work done.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T19:53:24-07:00","id":1509822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509819#post1509819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think most people even know how much of what we know about Cleopatra comes from someone who was invested in minimalizing her.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is from the other thread, but this annoys me so much. I swear every time I think of Octavian, my blood starts boiling. Like, the dude is so frustrating. It's clear he was a master of manipulating the narrative to make himself look good since it worked, but like, come on. This is a guy who had enough ego to name a unit of Time after himself, why do people take his word on his political opponents seriously?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T19:56:26-07:00","id":1509824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509822#post1509822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is from the other thread, but this annoys me so much. I swear every time I think of Octavian, my blood starts boiling. Like, the dude is so frustrating. It's clear he was a master of manipulating the narrative to make himself look good since it worked, but like, come on. This is a guy who had enough ego to name a unit of Time after himself, why do people take his word on his political opponents seriously?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Because most people don't even know that, and a great many that do are incentivized to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T22:36:15-07:00","id":1509836,"title":"","content":"I hate that for the first time in my life, I'm ooting for Disney.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T15:14:32-07:00","id":1509901,"title":"","content":"I hate it when I have a good idea for a story then write myself into a corner and I can't find a solution for it and I'm left with no choice but to redo the whole mess and change things into a direction that I'm not keen on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T17:34:03-07:00","id":1509909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509901#post1509901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate it when I have a good idea for a story then write myself into a corner and I can't find a solution for it and I'm left with no choice but to redo the whole mess and change things into a direction that I'm not keen on.</div> </div> </div> </div>WHile it's a pain in the ass for stories, this is why I write backwards on the first draft-by setting up how it looks like how I want it to end, it's easy to make a checklist of what I have to setup and otherwise figure the pieces out.<br /> <br /> Of course, writing the story forwards in the second draft can still throw it off , so the pain is still very sadly real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T11:38:05-07:00","id":1509973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509909#post1509909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WHile it's a pain in the ass for stories, this is why I write backwards on the first draft-by setting up how it looks like how I want it to end, it's easy to make a checklist of what I have to setup and otherwise figure the pieces out.<br /> <br /> Of course, writing the story forwards in the second draft can still throw it off , so the pain is still very sadly real.</div> </div> </div> </div>out of curiosity kells,how do you feel about writing non chronologically as whole? what is the optimal way to do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T12:03:38-07:00","id":1509974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509973#post1509973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> out of curiosity kells,how do you feel about writing non chronologically as whole? what is the optimal way to do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with it at all and it worked quite well with Frank Miller's Sin City series as he didn't write his stuff in chronological order and you would see characters that died in previous story arcs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T12:12:40-07:00","id":1509979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509974#post1509974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no problem with it at all and it worked quite well with Frank Miller's Sin City series as he didn't write his stuff in chronological order and you would see characters that died in previous story arcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>i getcha <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T14:24:54-07:00","id":1509992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1509973#post1509973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> out of curiosity kells,how do you feel about writing non chronologically as whole? what is the optimal way to do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of depends on what you mean, but that just comes down to having good outlines mostly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T04:36:02-07:00","id":1510057,"title":"","content":"<br /> I'm sorry to hear about your negative experience with Spectrum's cell phone service. It's frustrating to deal with sales representatives who aren't upfront about policies and try to push products or services you didn't ask for. It's good that you were persistent in getting the issue resolved and that the customer service call center was able to help you out. It's unfortunate that their in-store service wasn't up to par, and it's a shame that you're limited to using Spectrum for internet service due to your apartment complex's restrictions. It's always a good idea to do research on a company's reputation and policies before making a purchase, but sometimes even that can't prevent bad experiences. Hopefully, your new phone and plan will work out smoothly and you won't have to deal with any more headaches from Spectrum.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27939-dazert1","name":"Dazert1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27939_1.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T00:27:08-07:00","id":1510170,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this is a bit political and self indulgant but transphobes online are an utter chore to deal with. The bigotry is one thing that's annoying but you anticipate that. The really annoying thing is how if a trans person is related or involved in some context they're guaranteed to shit up the conversation. I and some other guys on a forum where talking the writting of the new hellraiser film and some dim wit derails a perfectly good thread because the actress who plays pinhead is trans.<br /> <br /> the transphobia is appalling enough do you have to be a tedious bore on top of that? If I can talk lovecraft without mentioning he was a racist every 20 seconds do they really need to write diatribe every time a trans person is present?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-30-2023, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T10:47:25-07:00","id":1510215,"title":"","content":"People are quite willing to spout off isms to cover up there lack of arguments with people they disagree with. It\u2019s gotten to the point that the terms is meaninglessness. I mean the recent Blue Beatle flick had one the characters spouting off about Batman being a fascist and I wonder do they even know what the term even means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T12:50:21-07:00","id":1510237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510215#post1510215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are quite willing to spout off isms to cover up there lack of arguments with people they disagree with. It\u2019s gotten to the point that the terms is meaninglessness. I mean the recent Blue Beatle flick had one the characters spouting off about Batman being a fascist and I wonder do they even know what the term even means.</div> </div> </div> </div>In mild fairness, since it's still taking place in the DC cinematic universe set up by Zak &quot;I dedicated Sucker Punch to my mom&quot; Snyder, it is being applied to arguably the most openly fascistic depiction of Batman* in film. In fact, arguably something like that needs to be part of the marketing for DC going forward to strongly move the franchise away from the theming Snyder baked into the first couple of DC films for this run, particularly the ones he personally directed.<br /> <br /> I mean, it is still cringey, but I get the need for rebranding. That line is blunt and was unwieldy in presentation, but it's a solid signal for a lot of people put off by the DCCU that things are gonna change.<br /> <br /> (Of course, I have no skin in this game since I'm basically not gonna watch any of those films until there's a hard reboot.)<br /> <br /> *I stared at that line after posting and then remembered Nolan Batman's gross invasion of privacy. Love the Dark Knight, but I'm not going to deny it's theming gets fucky. That said, that movie has better sleight of hand than Snyder can ever manage, hence the clarification about &quot;openly&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-30-2023, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T13:15:54-07:00","id":1510244,"title":"","content":"I loved the Nolan take on the Batman, but I even admit that they are things like the Joker\u2019s bank robbery or Bane\u2019s hijacking of an aircraft in mid air that pushes suspension of disbelief to the max. Not to mention the cell phone tracking plan that even Lucius Fox was shocked by. At least at the end the Dark Knight disabled it because he felt that his friend was right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-30-2023, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T13:20:10-07:00","id":1510246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510244#post1510244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loved the Nolan take on the Batman, but I even admit that they are things like the Joker\u2019s bank robbery or Bane\u2019s hijacking of an aircraft in mid air that pushes suspension of disbelief to the max.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between having the elements of stylistic crime thriller and comic book movie (against Nolan's attempts to just tell his own story), I find it weird those are what inspires disbelief for you.<br /> <br /> Actual fucking ninjas in the first movie and the entire bit with the pit in the third were way more jarring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T13:26:42-07:00","id":1510247,"title":"","content":"There were others like Bruce Wayne in the pit and after getting his back reset and tried to get out and falls with a crunch and he isn\u201dt crippled again. Or Fox not turning on the trap for his kidnappers when he led him to that bomb.<br /> <br /> But I accept it as that balancing act between the charming absurdity of the premise that fans will love and making enjoyable for casual fans who don\u2019t follow it faithfully like I did when I was much younger before I aged out the genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-30-2023, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T13:52:03-07:00","id":1510251,"title":"","content":"I think the whole &quot;Batman is a fascist&quot;-discourse started with the idea of Bruce Wayne as a billionaire beating up villains and their henchmen and the economic inequality in that relationship in addition to the idea that the solution is said billionaire beating the shit out of them. &quot;Batman is a fascist&quot; is like the dumbest version of that because... it's just a character saying it. And nobody in that universe knows Batman is a billionaire anyway. But taking that bit of deconstruction and worrying about how rich Bruce Wayne is compared to the sorts of people he regularly beats up seems like a common trope to me for writing Batman these days. Of course, you can't just take that discourse and simply have a character say &quot;Batman is bad!&quot; or &quot;Batman is a fascist!&quot;. There has to be some sort of storytelling foundation for that.<br /> <br /> I liked the version in Sean Fletcher's White Knight comic where it turns out other rich people were exploiting the destructive results of Batman's exploits to gentrify neighborhoods, for example. Or that Mattson Tomlin limited series &quot;The Imposter&quot; where the existence of Batman is exploited by another person to do some extrajudicial killings. These versions aren't part of the main DC continuity, so there's room to explore some themes.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T14:52:45-07:00","id":1510265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510251#post1510251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the whole &quot;Batman is a fascist&quot;-discourse started with the idea of Bruce Wayne as a billionaire beating up villains and their henchmen and the economic inequality in that relationship in addition to the idea that the solution is said billionaire beating the shit out of them. &quot;Batman is a fascist&quot; is like the dumbest version of that because... it's just a character saying it. And nobody in that universe knows Batman is a billionaire anyway. But taking that bit of deconstruction and worrying about how rich Bruce Wayne is compared to the sorts of people he regularly beats up seems like a common trope to me for writing Batman these days. Of course, you can't just take that discourse and simply have a character say &quot;Batman is bad!&quot; or &quot;Batman is a fascist!&quot;. There has to be some sort of storytelling foundation for that.<br /> <br /> I liked the version in Sean Fletcher's White Knight comic where it turns out other rich people were exploiting the destructive results of Batman's exploits to gentrify neighborhoods, for example. Or that Mattson Tomlin limited series &quot;The Imposter&quot; where the existence of Batman is exploited by another person to do some extrajudicial killings. These versions aren't part of the main DC continuity, so there's room to explore some themes.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, no one knows he's a billionaire, but &quot;IdSPtmm&quot; Snyder DC Batman's clearly rolling around with military grade tech that he uses to bust up locales and directly assault peoples without authorization, and for a pretty long time has no problem with indirect murder. He's got a whole secret police thing going on that's easy to see as action for action sake, implies excessive violence as an appropriate response against criminal behavior as a treason against society, with that criminal society often being portrayed in the DC Snyderverse as ethnic minorities. His presence is more solidly supported by the middle class in those films, his entire presence creates the nominal notion that criminals are both too strong and too weak (conventional policing can't do anything about them, but Batman is an effective agent with his military grade equipment), there no compasion shown for the criminal populace, and is in fact strongly suggested that it never even crosses Batman's mind, he clearly values violence as an expression of strength and was at one time obsessed with getting a guy to bleed, and wrapping all of that in his signature icon makes it pretty easy to understand Batman as a death cultist. That may not be all of the points from Ur-Fascism, but that's a lot of them.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> <br /> Now that said, a lot of that can just be applied to superheroes in general (and is one of the many points Alan Moore made with Watchmen) that we kind of to shrug off and accept the metaphorical value of it in opposition to it (as I sarcastically put it, sometimes you need to have Jesus club the devil to death with a cross and then say that peace has won the day*), and I don't think that the film creators are interested in that being a deeply held take on Batman, considering that they apparently trust the Flash movie so little to stand on it's own that they had to lean into the fact they're using the Keaton Batman to prop it up.<br /> <br /> Again, for me, the line feels like a admittedly really bad attempt to signal that the DC Cinematic Universe is trying to cut off it's associations with Zak &quot;I dedicated Sucker Punch to my mom&quot; Snyder and his established themes and ideas in the early movies, which is kind of neccesary. Zak &quot;IdSPtmm&quot; Snyder is a fascist (and an idiot who clearly didn't understand Watchmen), and a lot of those early movies has him being very fascist with the characters, world, and overall ideology, and because of that, the franchise has cultivated one kind of audience and has alienated another, where the goal for most of these companies is to chew on as many people as possible. THe line is clumsy, but it's a calculated risk to start working towards getting more of an audience to be loyal to the brand and actually start seeing all the movies for the sake of seeing it-fun for fascists, antifascists, and everyone else in between makes more money.<br /> <br /> None of that actually saves how awkward that is in execution, but I can at least appreciate the logic behind it.<br /> <br /> *Why I say that with my current spicy meatball take on religion is admittedly a mystery to myself, but whatever, the point is that there's a certain level of allegory that most audiences engage with and must be acknowledged when critically thinking about these kinds of stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T15:01:54-07:00","id":1510270,"title":"","content":"An addendum:<br /> <br /> I feel I should probably mention that, while I am in the camp of people who feels like I see the rise of fascism across various nations as being a real problem modernly, I'm more interested in identifying movements and organizations as being fascist than I am individuals, because a) I don't want that word to lose it's value, and b) giving an inordinate number of people the benefit of the doubt, it's better to understand a lot of people who are manipulated by fascistic forces more than understanding them <i>as</i> fascists. Zak &quot;I dedicated Sucker Punch to my mom&quot; Snyder is one of the few individuals I will confidently assert as being a fascist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T15:03:07-07:00","id":1510271,"title":"","content":"I admit my knowledge of most DC superheroes is limited to the Justice League and Young Justice cartoons, but hasn't Gotham traditionally been a city with a <i>deeply</i> corrupt police force? Which only got worse once supervillains started to get involved? That would circumvent the &quot;infinitely strong infinitely weak&quot; problem for the most part, but if that angle is being left out then... well, that's just dumb then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T15:12:53-07:00","id":1510272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510271#post1510271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit my knowledge of most DC superheroes is limited to the Justice League and Young Justice cartoons, but hasn't Gotham traditionally been a city with a <i>deeply</i> corrupt police force? Which only got worse once supervillains started to get involved? That would circumvent the &quot;infinitely strong infinitely weak&quot; problem for the most part, but if that angle is being left out then... well, that's just dumb then.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, that portrayal of Gotham is still an authorial construct, and it's implementation can deliberately or accidentally convey certain kinds of messages. Over the course of Batman's publication, that has been used to support everything from socialistic takes to fascistic ones, and of course has also sometimes &quot;just been the setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, absolutely. As I mentioned, there's just as much risk in not engaging with the allegorical framing/context to superhero stories as there is in being uncritical about what the text of superhero narratives say by virtue of their setup. Hell, going back again to Alan Moore, for as much as he explored the text of superheroes as being inherently authoritarian and even fascistic in Watchmen, he wrote just as many superhero comics that gleefully used that framework for for it's ability to impart ideals for humanity. Both things can be true!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"htt