l of that in his signature icon makes it pretty easy to understand Batman as a death cultist. That may not be all of the points from Ur-Fascism, but that's a lot of them.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> <br /> Now that said, a lot of that can just be applied to superheroes in general (and is one of the many points Alan Moore made with Watchmen) that we kind of to shrug off and accept the metaphorical value of it in opposition to it (as I sarcastically put it, sometimes you need to have Jesus club the devil to death with a cross and then say that peace has won the day*), and I don't think that the film creators are interested in that being a deeply held take on Batman, considering that they apparently trust the Flash movie so little to stand on it's own that they had to lean into the fact they're using the Keaton Batman to prop it up.<br /> <br /> Again, for me, the line feels like a admittedly really bad attempt to signal that the DC Cinematic Universe is trying to cut off it's associations with Zak &quot;I dedicated Sucker Punch to my mom&quot; Snyder and his established themes and ideas in the early movies, which is kind of neccesary. Zak &quot;IdSPtmm&quot; Snyder is a fascist (and an idiot who clearly didn't understand Watchmen), and a lot of those early movies has him being very fascist with the characters, world, and overall ideology, and because of that, the franchise has cultivated one kind of audience and has alienated another, where the goal for most of these companies is to chew on as many people as possible. THe line is clumsy, but it's a calculated risk to start working towards getting more of an audience to be loyal to the brand and actually start seeing all the movies for the sake of seeing it-fun for fascists, antifascists, and everyone else in between makes more money.<br /> <br /> None of that actually saves how awkward that is in execution, but I can at least appreciate the logic behind it.<br /> <br /> *Why I say that with my current spicy meatball take on religion is admittedly a mystery to myself, but whatever, the point is that there's a certain level of allegory that most audiences engage with and must be acknowledged when critically thinking about these kinds of stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Zack Snyder is... As a filmmaker he's okay when he's able to really able to nail the bombast of an action-sequence. That's why I like his cut of the Justice League that came out later more than Joss Whedon's version (who is another strain of &quot;problematic&quot; altogether...).<br /> <br /> But ideologically, there are issues with Zack Snyder's movies but I think the person that should be talked about in that context isn't Zack Snyder but rather - Frank Miller. &quot;The Dark Knight Returns&quot; is a classic but there's some troublesome stuff in there and it only gets worse from there in the sequels. DC didn't even allow him to write his Batman-story about Batman joining the War on Terror where he's slaughtering Arabs (somebody else published it with &quot;not-Batman&quot; as the main-character called &quot;Holy Terror&quot;). But it got a part 3 called &quot;The Master Race&quot; (2015) and part 4 &quot;The Golden Child&quot; (2019).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T15:30:06-07:00","id":1510275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510273#post1510273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Zack Snyder is... As a filmmaker he's okay when he's able to really able to nail the bombast of an action-sequence. That's why I like his cut of the Justice League that came out later more than Joss Whedon's version (who is another strain of &quot;problematic&quot; altogether...).<br /> <br /> But ideologically, there are issues with Zack Snyder's movies but I think the person that should be talked about in that context isn't Zack Snyder but rather - Frank Miller. &quot;The Dark Knight Returns&quot; is a classic but there's some troublesome stuff in there and it only gets worse from there in the sequels. DC didn't even allow him to write his Batman-story about Batman joining the War on Terror where he's slaughtering Arabs (somebody else published it with &quot;not-Batman&quot; as the main-character called &quot;Holy Terror&quot;). But it got a part 3 called &quot;The Master Race&quot; (2015) and part 4 &quot;The Golden Child&quot; (2019).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, Frank Miller. It's like someone wanted to wrap up all of American Libertarianism's problematic elements up in one man.<br /> <br /> But, no,&quot;IdSPtmm&quot; Snyder's just as much a part of the problem as Miller. Arguably more so, since he's still unfortunately actively making media in a prolific way that Miller isn't.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I just found out that Zack Snyder considers himself left-leaning. I dunno what to do with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-30-2023, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T15:40:17-07:00","id":1510277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510275#post1510275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I just found out that Zack Snyder considers himself left-leaning. I dunno what to do with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say &quot;you can call yourself whatever you want, but it needs to be backed up with facts&quot;, but that swings dangerously close to &quot;No true Scotsman&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T15:44:48-07:00","id":1510278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510277#post1510277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to say &quot;you can call yourself whatever you want, but it needs to be backed up with facts&quot;, but that swings dangerously close to &quot;No true Scotsman&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly take it as a reminder that all of American politics skews so damn far right. And hey, taking him at his word, there's the clear concession that you don't need to be &quot;conservative&quot; to be a fascist.*<br /> <br /> Still, that <i>does</i> make some of his donations make more sense. I may have to do more research and run the risk of needing to give him more credit than just Guardians of Ga'hoole.<br /> <br /> Yes, I liked Guardians of Ga'hoole, yes I know how it's flawed.<br /> <br /> *because, yes, fascism can appear in a number of political stances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-30-2023, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T17:06:11-07:00","id":1510290,"title":"","content":"On the status of the Gotham City police: the problem is that they're always whatever the writer/plot says, leading to an incredibly inconsistent portrayal even by comic book standards.<br /> <br /> The example I usually use to demonstrate this: Why is the Joker alive?<br /> <br /> OK, Batman has his thing about not killing people, and the Joker is considered too insane to stand trial (or get the death penalty).<br /> <br /> But consider:<br /> <br /> Police that aren't even guilty of corruption in a technical sense have gunned strangers down on the excuse of mistaking a cellphone for a gun. The Joker is infamous for having lots of hidden lethal implements on his person at all times. No jumpy cop has ever shot Joker because the Joker was just going to fix his tie but the cop thought he was about to get sprayed with acid?<br /> <br /> The Joker is generally hated by the more traditional organized criminals of the city because he screws with them and their money too. No cop on the take has figure out how to off the Joker on behalf of who ever's paying them? Again, the Joker is a criminal that is a walking lethal threat. The self-defense argument is just too easy to make even if you gunned him down in front of hundreds of witnesses after he's handcuffed.<br /> <br /> What, exactly, is stopping such a corrupt police force from killing the Joker?<br /> <br /> The simple answer is that they're corrupt in an exceedingly unrealistic way. It's not just hypocrisy, but unexplainable beyond that they're fictional characters that serve authorial intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T17:18:49-07:00","id":1510291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510271#post1510271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit my knowledge of most DC superheroes is limited to the Justice League and Young Justice cartoons, but hasn't Gotham traditionally been a city with a <i>deeply</i> corrupt police force? Which only got worse once supervillains started to get involved? That would circumvent the &quot;infinitely strong infinitely weak&quot; problem for the most part, but if that angle is being left out then... well, that's just dumb then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes Gotham city has a notorious corrupt police force and it\u2019s amazing that they didn\u2019t clip guys like the Joker or Two Face when they started to upset the apple cart so to speak. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T17:26:10-07:00","id":1510293,"title":"","content":"Frank Miller is certainly is someone who seemly went over the deep end in the last 20+ years with dark and gritty stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T17:56:50-07:00","id":1510297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510293#post1510293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frank Miller is certainly is someone who seemly went over the deep end in the last 20+ years with dark and gritty stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably he started off over the deep end and has spent the rest of his career redefining what that means by showing how far a space there is beyond the deep end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T19:45:34-07:00","id":1510306,"title":"","content":"It's Miller time, and I hate beer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T19:49:08-07:00","id":1510307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510306#post1510306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Miller time, and I hate beer.</div> </div> </div> </div><img width=\"800\" height=\"450\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://th.bing.com/th/id/R.e34ffc19ffea355e8836433280726b3f?rik=I63qypU7b4Ds0w&amp;riu=http%3a%2f%2ftheelusivefish.com%2fwp-content%2fuploads%2f2015%2f03%2fCapAmIunderstoodthat.gif&amp;ehk=NdWl%2bzSZmE9wHcaSdZaaZHRlHo79jlRZmKf0NYrVRbM%3d&amp;risl=&amp;pid=ImgRaw&amp;r=0\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://th.bing.com/th/id/R.e34ffc19ffea355e8836433280726b3f?rik=I63qypU7b4Ds0w&amp;riu=http%3a%2f%2ftheelusivefish.com%2fwp-content%2fuploads%2f2015%2f03%2fCapAmIunderstoodthat.gif&amp;ehk=NdWl%2bzSZmE9wHcaSdZaaZHRlHo79jlRZmKf0NYrVRbM%3d&amp;risl=&amp;pid=ImgRaw&amp;r=0\" data-thumb-url=\"https://th.bing.com/th/id/R.e34ffc19ffea355e8836433280726b3f?rik=I63qypU7b4Ds0w&amp;riu=http%3a%2f%2ftheelusivefish.com%2fwp-content%2fuploads%2f2015%2f03%2fCapAmIunderstoodthat.gif&amp;ehk=NdWl%2bzSZmE9wHcaSdZaaZHRlHo79jlRZmKf0NYrVRbM%3d&amp;risl=&amp;pid=ImgRaw&amp;r=0\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> wordy wording","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-30-2023, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T20:48:35-07:00","id":1510309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510265#post1510265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah, no one knows he's a billionaire, but &quot;IdSPtmm&quot; Snyder DC Batman's clearly rolling around with military grade tech that he uses to bust up locales and directly assault peoples without authorization, and for a pretty long time has no problem with indirect murder. He's got a whole secret police thing going on that's easy to see as action for action sake, implies excessive violence as an appropriate response against criminal behavior as a treason against society, with that criminal society often being portrayed in the DC Snyderverse as ethnic minorities. His presence is more solidly supported by the middle class in those films, his entire presence creates the nominal notion that criminals are both too strong and too weak (conventional policing can't do anything about them, but Batman is an effective agent with his military grade equipment), there no compasion shown for the criminal populace, and is in fact strongly suggested that it never even crosses Batman's mind, he clearly values violence as an expression of strength and was at one time obsessed with getting a guy to bleed, and wrapping all of that in his signature icon makes it pretty easy to understand Batman as a death cultist. That may not be all of the points from Ur-Fascism, but that's a lot of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interestingly in the comics (at least some of them, there's obviously been a lot of different takes on Batman over the years) Bruce Wayne was very much a philanthropist who was noted to spend more than half his income every year funding charities, community food banks, homeless shelters, clinics for low-income individuals, etc. He fought the symptoms of crime as Batman, but as Bruce Wayne he attacked the root causes of crime, and on several occasions Alfred pointed out to him that that Bruce Wayne did more to help Gotham and stop crime than Batman ever could.<br /> <br /> It's not just Zack Snyder that ignores this aspect of Batman's character, you don't really ever see it get brought up in comic books, games, or movies by other directors. In the end, it's just not viewed as &quot;sexy&quot; or important enough, and entire character of Bruce Wayne largely gets glossed over and ignored because people want to see Batman going around punching bad guys in the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T21:12:37-07:00","id":1510313,"title":"","content":"Bruce way being a philanthropist (esp. for orphanages) does tend to get mentioned in a lot of incarnations of Batman.<br /> <br /> The problem is the message that all Batman media basically ends up having to make: Bruce Wayne, a person of ridiculous wealth, who can hire a hoard of consultants if he didn't want to do it himself, can't fix Gotham's problems with all that money. Like, you have to be epically bad with money... as a billionaire... to not have turned Gotham into a paradise with the kind of donations he supposedly throws around.<br /> <br /> To put this into some perspective. One group of experts estimated that getting every person in the US that's current unhoused or under-housed into a safe, secure, private domicile with fully functional facilities and utilities, would cost about 20 billion dollars. That's the whole damned country (also let us note the real world nonsense of our federal budget and how little it would cost us to not have a homeless problem)... Bruce can't manage it in one city?<br /> <br /> It might not be sexy, but there's a point where the &quot;not sexy&quot; argument falls apart because Batman can fight supervillains that aren't created by systemic issues and can't be stopped by traditional methods. There's always going to be outliers for him to fight. Superman manages. But the need to make Gotham a shithole of a city overrides that. It turns the idea that Bruce is a philanthropist of extreme generosity into a joke because there's no way money cannot of fixed all of Gotham's &quot;we don't have enough money for this,&quot; problems already.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm going to assume the edit spam bots struck again and I didn't make up a post about Bruce Wayne's philanthropic endeavors and responded to it in a delusional bit of oddity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T21:44:56-07:00","id":1510314,"title":"","content":"Isn't there one incarnation of Gotham where it's just always cursed to be a mess? Court of Owls, or something like that?<br /> <br /> edit: Google is telling me it's probably &quot;Dark Knight, Dark City&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T22:25:43-07:00","id":1510319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510314#post1510314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there one incarnation of Gotham where it's just always cursed to be a mess? Court of Owls, or something like that?<br /> <br /> edit: Google is telling me it's probably &quot;Dark Knight, Dark City&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>God, that sounds like an awful setting conceit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T23:37:24-07:00","id":1510325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510319#post1510319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God, that sounds like an awful setting conceit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it can be. As a self-contained or limited setting, it can give the city a distinct personality and make the city into its own character. Poorly done, or overused, it descends very quickly into &quot;too bleak, stopped caring&quot; territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T00:45:55-07:00","id":1510329,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1510313Edit: I'm going to assume the edit spam bots struck again and I didn't make up a post about Bruce Wayne's philanthropic endeavors and responded to it in a delusional bit of oddity.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Yeah, I noticed a typo and went back to fix it and my post got locked out as spam. <br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah, I think there's definitely a some thematic and plot conceits in regard to Batman that create a certain amount of logical inconsistency when you look at the setting. That's not really a surprise - many settings, and especially comic book settings, quickly begin falling apart under close scrutiny. Bruce Wayne is supposed to be doing a lot to lift Gotham up but if he fixed all the problems, Batman would no longer resemble itself. The main idea of Batman is that he's mostly in Gotham and is mostly a street level crime fighter and investigator. <br /> <br /> I think though that it's important to note that Bruce Wayne isn't holding back from helping Gotham so that he has an excuse to go around beating people up. It's just that, The Author basically says, &quot;Despite his best efforts, and he makes a lot of them, Batman and Bruce Wayne can't fix Gotham, even by extensively attacking the problem from both sides, which he does.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T00:49:25-07:00","id":1510330,"title":"","content":"Just to vent, with that recent shooting in Texas. Greg Abbot sent out a tweet claiming that the victims were illegal immigrants. In fact, they were actually legal permanent residents and that was just bullshit coming out of him. Like always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T09:18:46-07:00","id":1510368,"title":"","content":"Frank Miller was a good writer at one time and I did enjoy his work along with his Sin City stuff. But after 9/11 he literally became to dark &amp; depressing in his storytelling and his All-Star Batman &amp; Robin were awful in how he made Batman unlikeable to the exetreme and his sequels to Dark Knight Returns showed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T09:19:53-07:00","id":1510369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510319#post1510319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God, that sounds like an awful setting conceit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a bad idea that I destested when it first came out and I like it even less now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T09:24:08-07:00","id":1510371,"title":"","content":"We have an upcoming provincal election and neither candiate is appealing to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T13:15:22-07:00","id":1510396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510325#post1510325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, it can be. As a self-contained or limited setting, it can give the city a distinct personality and make the city into its own character. Poorly done, or overused, it descends very quickly into &quot;too bleak, stopped caring&quot; territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't have the time to elaborate on this point, so doing this now:<br /> <br /> What I mean by this is that it's one of those things that feels like it's there to justify the continual loop of Bruce Wayne's efforts in Gotham (again, nothing happens that a creator didn't decide on) which both arbitrarily maintains Bruce-y Boy's vigil, adds a bad underline to any power-based critical reading of Batman, and also unfortunately supports some enemies points<br /> <br /> In any story that deals with Batman in the larger context of the DC universe, Batman has allies who are some of the most potent sorcerers in the setting-Let John Constantine and Zatanna put their heads together and grab any number of other allies in the venture, they can probably unravel any curse that noxious. If they <i>can't</i>, then pretty much any villain arguing for the destruction of Gotham almost has the right idea, in that it would be better to engineer a disaster, arrange a city wide evacuation, wipe Gotham from the map, and beg forgiveness of those who couldn't-wouldn't-leave, because the alternative is to allow a cursed city to be a festering wound on all of it's citizens and it's larger regional and global neighbors. Neither of those things are done, though, because the entire point is to keep Batman doing his things. It's honestly easier, and less damning for the story, to just leave the buy-in for Batman unspoken.<br /> <br /> That idea has all the same problematic stink that the One More Day Spiderman story has-it's a problem that has legitimate solutions outside what it ends on, and in stipulating why those solutions aren't viable, it becomes all the more clear what the hand of the author is doing (in that case, taking a hammer to Peter's and Mary Jane's relationship because the author didn't like it and wanted to legitimately retcon it), which then goes on to cheapen and alienate the experience.<br /> <br /> Authors can run into the mistake of feeling the need to justify why their story happens outside of it's context. In this particular case, it can be viable to get realistic about Bruce Wayne's effect as a philanthropist, and what that does to him as he actually improves and makes the city better, possibly to a point where it's hard to justify being Batman (not because he needs to punch people, but just because it's been so much of a part of his trauma management method and his identity), or in really exploring an idea of how and why Bruce Wayne's efforts aren't enough, the ways in which he's rich, but not rich enough to actually make a change-but it can also be viable to accept the buy in that Batman just has an ongoing conflict where in he both needs to improve the city and take action against bad actors as Batman because the story is one consumers pick up with the understand that there will be value in watching the Bat go Biff, Wham, Pow and broodily solving the mysteries and that Bruce will have to reconcile with the city as a city and also what being Batman does to him as a person, with the limits of the problem just never being defined because we're here to see Batman play out his noir and Bruce Wayne be a human.<br /> <br /> The idea that Gotham is cursed is a solvable problem not being solved because it's a way to answer a question that doesn't always need to be answered to create substantial media just because they don't want to actually handle any particular marxist literary theory read in the story. And, like. I don't need that.*<br /> <br /> *Mind you, I say this like someone who seeks out Batman content, when I really don't.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510330#post1510330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to vent, with that recent shooting in Texas. Greg Abbot sent out a tweet claiming that the victims were illegal immigrants. In fact, they were actually legal permanent residents and that was just bullshit coming out of him. Like always.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus fucking christ, of course he did. Fucking Texas, man. I can't believe I used to be proud of my home state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-01-2023, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T13:38:04-07:00","id":1510399,"title":"","content":"I was mostly refering to the general idea of a city being cursed/doomed/fated to always be a hole, rather than Gotham specifically. There's interesting stories that can come from the sisyphean task of fight against a genus loci, be it a passive or active one. Granted, as you said, it's difficult to make that a <i>background element</i> and still have a good story and/or setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T13:40:44-07:00","id":1510400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510399#post1510399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was mostly refering to the general idea of a city being cursed/doomed/fated to always be a hole, rather than Gotham specifically. There's interesting stories that can come from the sisyphean task of fight against a genus loci, be it a passive or active one. Granted, as you said, it's difficult to make that a <i>background element</i> and still have a good story and/or setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Context matters, as it turns out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T13:53:25-07:00","id":1510402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1510396#post1510396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Jesus fucking christ, of course he did. Fucking Texas, man. I can't believe I used to be proud of my home state.</div> </div> </div> </div> Every place has its good and bad. One of many bad things about Texas is knowing Abbot is kinda awful, and still preferring him over Democrats. Seriously, I\u2019ve heard certain people complain at length about him, and then go and vote for him again. It\u2019s kinda depressing, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.th