":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T13:30:06-07:00","id":1514607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514604#post1514604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While Korea and China actually do have problems with racism, I'm not sure I'd have &quot;watch the live-action Little Mermaid&quot; as the metric for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to one of my friends who is from China is that huge portions of the people who reside in the villages are insular and never seen black people and trying to ease them to the fact gradually and dislike woke culture in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T13:38:12-07:00","id":1514610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514607#post1514607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to one of my friends who is from China is that huge portions of the people who reside in the villages are insular and never seen black people and trying to ease them to the fact gradually and dislike woke culture in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be part of the problem with racism in China, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T14:01:02-07:00","id":1514612,"title":"","content":"I'd personally object to measuring racism in terms of how one consumes corporate media. <i>The Little Mermaid</i> isn't inclusive; it's a product, calculated at the highest levels to generate the most amount of money possible for a near independent city-nation that is trying to own perpetual copyrights not just on its own IP but on the very concepts of &quot;childhood&quot; and &quot;nostalgia&quot; by renting your formative memories back to you but never letting you own them. If that's what you mean when you refer to &quot;political correctness&quot;--people who make performative displays around largely irrelevant issues because they would rather operate within a power structure than fundamentally alter it to redistribute some of that power to the social underclasses--then yes, I dislike that too.<br /> <br /> Now I'm going see if I can figure out how to flag my own post for moderation, because I can't tell if this is too political to be allowed to stay up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":".  Didn't do italics right. I did italics bad. 06-11-2023, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T15:15:18-07:00","id":1514621,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, because this has gotten under my skin, I'm going to dive more into it:<br /> <br /> If the issue is in suggesting that China and South Korea have problems of racism...I'm not even really sure what to do with that, given that many anti-&quot;woke&quot; actors usually use the argument that the United States can't have issues with racism because we obviously have it better than China does, how can we be those those things if we're not doing what China is doing (a bad and stupid argument, mind you, but that's not the point for this post). Keeping it in movies here, it's one of the reasons why Hollywood continues to be slow on the subject of diverse casting-because Chinese audiences make up a big portion of overall sales, alienating that audience loses production companies a lot of money, which (if they even bother to justify it) they'll argue means that they can't make as many productions that allow for more opportunities to have diverse casting (which they will then ignore moving forward). You only need to spend about ten to fifteen minutes researching movie marketing in China to see that racism in action.<br /> <br /> Now taking a step back to where I was agreeing with the complaint, raising a particular stink over that reaction to the live-action Little Mermaid is the sort of reactionary and excessive response that is not helpful for actually chasing progress-anyone who is actually interested in the business of securing protective rights for minorities across the world knew well in advance that China wasn't going to respond well to it, and is generally more interested in the overall problem than any particular one reaction to one movie (particularly a Disney movie, whose relationship to commiting to inclusive societal practices is best summarized as &quot;It took a state taking action that was fucking with their bottom line to otherwise actually commit any serious action to inclusive societal practices, no matter how much their movies try to tell you otherwise&quot;*). While some of this response will, of course, include those who are still learning and developing progressive lenses, that reaction is far more the corner of centrists who adopt progressive rhetoric as a way to maintain their social standing and otherwise cheaply &quot;contribute&quot; to social justice with all the care of treating a Molotov like a beer cup. When people complain about virtue signaling in &quot;woke culture&quot;, this is the sort of thing that pretty legitimately qualifies.<br /> <br /> *However progressive/&quot;woke&quot; you think Disney is, it pays to remember that they very frequently financially supported political figures that would put in laws and practices that helped them to make money, those candidates stances in support of racism, sexism, homophobia, etc. be damned. Disney is very much one of those organizations that will they say the support minorities one second and then stab them in the back the next, with the fight against DeSantis creating one of their major outliers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-11-2023, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T15:23:21-07:00","id":1514623,"title":"","content":"Can we at least all agree that the Chinese government has shown itself to be using overtly racist propaganda regarding this?<br /> <br /> They don't allow a free market of films: a tiny selection of foreign films are allowed to be released in China. They allowed the new Little Mermaid in. Then they went on their state news shows to attack the movie they allowed in for having a black woman as the lead character.<br /> <br /> I highly doubt this is really representative of how Chinese people as a whole feel about the film. But it's not a free society, and the government purposefully tanked the film using racism. I don't even think the Chinese government cares about it that much ideologically (they seem to care far more about pushing Hollywood around just to prove that they can), but they could do that using other options. They chose to go the racism route.<br /> <br /> And yeah, this isn't about political correctness or &quot;wokeness&quot; (sorry,but the &quot;evils&quot; of &quot;wokeness&quot; and &quot;woke culture&quot; is a fiction spread by US racists to try to normalize racism by co-opting an American Black slang word as an attack on people fighting against anti-Black racism in the US; they've admitted it already there's no need to debate that's exactly why &quot;woke&quot; is suddenly some big issue). It's about money. Hollywood wants Chinese money, and the Chinese government has their own financial interests in keeping a tight grip on what Hollywood films get into China and how they get marketed in China.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T15:24:19-07:00","id":1514624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514604#post1514604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While Korea and China actually do have problems with racism, I'm not sure I'd have &quot;watch the live-action Little Mermaid&quot; as the metric for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Someone bring up the actual and real tensions of multi-ethnic households in rural provinces of the Korean peninsula, accelerared by native population decline, then I shut up and listen. Someone try to do a \u2018witty\u2019 one-up with a fricking sales figure for a movie from Eagleland, then I start twitching.<br /> <br /> I mean, if they really wanted the race &amp; beauty issues up front, they could\u2019ve filmed something like The Other Mermaid; after Ariel\u2019s dramatic success becomes widely known in the ocean kingdom, princesses and maidens start fawning over their own ideas of becoming scooped up by a hot guy, and assorted beauty courses become a fad. Our leading girl is first In with the fad, experiences or observes a Problem, then rolls up her clamshell sleeves to Fix it. Maybe she gets the Boy, or the Girl, at the end if the plot allows for it. Done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T00:27:22-07:00","id":1514659,"title":"","content":"As a side the movie is complete garbage like all the live action remakes. My gf has waived her horror movie veto as way of apology for making us see it even after that fucking terrible Pinocchio movie.<br /> <br /> <br /> I resent being forced to stand up for this movie on race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T01:32:29-07:00","id":1514663,"title":"","content":"When I look at the reviews, I find myself constantly wondering (and this is true of most of the Disney remakes) if people forget that adults aren't the target audience here: kids are. This is not The Little Mermaid for people that grew up with the animation renaissance one, it for their kids who are dragging along parents that aren't going to like it compared to the &quot;superior&quot; older versions (my father made my sister and I watch one of the earlier takes on it where the ending matches the original fairy tale version before he'd let my sister drag us all to see the new one), who aren't going to care about so many of the things I've seen reviewers point out.<br /> <br /> It gives me the same vibes as when movie critics used to give out stars based on how Oscar-bait-like a film was, so even really good genre flicks always got garbage reviews because they weren't artsy high drama. Every parent I know that's taken their kid(s) to see it? Their kids loved it. And those kids are the target audience that fuel Disney's &quot;recycle stories instead of telling new ones&quot; core business model. It's on pace to make over a billion dollars, no matter how much critics dismiss it, and parents don't think it stacks up to the version they grew up with. Disney knows how to get parents to pay for their kids to enjoy Disney's Nth retelling of the same story... it's what made them so damned rich in the first place. Blumhouse movies tend to get shit reviews, but Jason Blum is raking it in because he knows how to get horror fans hand him money.<br /> <br /> Critics that don't account for genre and target audience are always going to look out of touch, because... they're literally being out of touch with the people the film is supposed to appeal to the most. Critics bashed Die Hard when it came out because they didn't think Bruce Willis's great turn from comedian to action star could make up for it still being yet another late 70s/early 80s action movie everyone was sick and tired of already. And then it was a giant success with audiences anyway, and now people consider it a classic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T01:47:24-07:00","id":1514668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514663#post1514663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I look at the reviews, I find myself constantly wondering (and this is true of most of the Disney remakes) if people forget that adults aren't the target audience here: kids are. This is not The Little Mermaid for people that grew up with the animation renaissance one, it for their kids who are dragging along parents that aren't going to like it compared to the &quot;superior&quot; older versions (my father made my sister and I watch one of the earlier takes on it where the ending matches the original fairy tale version before he'd let my sister drag us all to see the new one), who aren't going to care about so many of the things I've seen reviewers point out.<br /> <br /> It gives me the same vibes as when movie critics used to give out stars based on how Oscar-bait-like a film was, so even really good genre flicks always got garbage reviews because they weren't artsy high drama. Every parent I know that's taken their kid(s) to see it? Their kids loved it. And those kids are the target audience that fuel Disney's &quot;recycle stories instead of telling new ones&quot; core business model. It's on pace to make over a billion dollars, no matter how much critics dismiss it, and parents don't think it stacks up to the version they grew up with. Disney knows how to get parents to pay for their kids to enjoy Disney's Nth retelling of the same story... it's what made them so damned rich in the first place. Blumhouse movies tend to get shit reviews, but Jason Blum is raking it in because he knows how to get horror fans hand him money.<br /> <br /> Critics that don't account for genre and target audience are always going to look out of touch, because... they're literally being out of touch with the people the film is supposed to appeal to the most. Critics bashed Die Hard when it came out because they didn't think Bruce Willis's great turn from comedian to action star could make up for it still being yet another late 70s/early 80s action movie everyone was sick and tired of already. And then it was a giant success with audiences anyway, and now people consider it a classic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh. Doesn\u2019t really make up for the horrid lighting, Uncanny Valley on sea creatures, extraneous characters, humourous scenes cut off, oh and legitimately Horror-ish scenes that scared children.<br /> <br /> And the attitudes of thankfully few people who are utterly convinced that pointing out any of the above issues, based solely on the movie\u2019s internal issues rather than external ones, makes you sexist and racist. (I sincerely hope the latter is just me being hyperbolic and biased and Fascist, but Reality was unkind to me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T02:53:03-07:00","id":1514674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514663#post1514663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I look at the reviews, I find myself constantly wondering (and this is true of most of the Disney remakes) if people forget that adults aren't the target audience here: kids are. This is not The Little Mermaid for people that grew up with the animation renaissance one, it for their kids who are dragging along parents that aren't going to like it compared to the &quot;superior&quot; older versions (my father made my sister and I watch one of the earlier takes on it where the ending matches the original fairy tale version before he'd let my sister drag us all to see the new one), who aren't going to care about so many of the things I've seen reviewers point out.<br /> <br /> It gives me the same vibes as when movie critics used to give out stars based on how Oscar-bait-like a film was, so even really good genre flicks always got garbage reviews because they weren't artsy high drama. Every parent I know that's taken their kid(s) to see it? Their kids loved it. And those kids are the target audience that fuel Disney's &quot;recycle stories instead of telling new ones&quot; core business model. It's on pace to make over a billion dollars, no matter how much critics dismiss it, and parents don't think it stacks up to the version they grew up with. Disney knows how to get parents to pay for their kids to enjoy Disney's Nth retelling of the same story... it's what made them so damned rich in the first place. Blumhouse movies tend to get shit reviews, but Jason Blum is raking it in because he knows how to get horror fans hand him money.<br /> <br /> Critics that don't account for genre and target audience are always going to look out of touch, because... they're literally being out of touch with the people the film is supposed to appeal to the most. Critics bashed Die Hard when it came out because they didn't think Bruce Willis's great turn from comedian to action star could make up for it still being yet another late 70s/early 80s action movie everyone was sick and tired of already. And then it was a giant success with audiences anyway, and now people consider it a classic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> about two months ago I watched avatar the last airbender. Its probably one of the greatest tv shows ive ever watched and I really enjoyed the new jumanji movies a few days back.<br /> <br /> Its not a good movie full stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T04:43:11-07:00","id":1514678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514668#post1514668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn\u2019t really make up for the horrid lighting, Uncanny Valley on sea creatures, extraneous characters, humourous scenes cut off, oh and legitimately Horror-ish scenes that scared children.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I haven't been clear, I haven't seen it.. I didn't actually like the '89 movie all the much either. Though the '89 version has creepy scenes that scared younger children (esp. the Ursula ones) that are far tamer than the original story or some of the European versions from the 70s.<br /> <br /> It doesn't need to make up for most of what you're saying, because the target audience isn't going to care. Having babysat for my niece and nephew... despite my sister's best efforts, their tolerance for cinematography I find abhorrent is rather high, but I'm pretty sure my father felt the same way about plenty of things I loved as a kid.<br /> <br /> You've never made the case that kids - aka the target audience here - of the current day are going to be bothered by the same things we'd be bothered by. The box office returns don't really back up the idea the kids hate this film and aren't dragging their reluctant parents to it in droves; which is all the movie is really meant to accomplish in the end. Sure it's be even better if parents wanted to go (though reviews from parents aren't as negative as paid critics or adults watching a reboot/whatever of a classic from their childhood as far as I can tell).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514674#post1514674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">about two months ago I watched avatar the last airbender. Its probably one of the greatest tv shows ive ever watched and I really enjoyed the new jumanji movies a few days back.</div> </div> </div> </div>And?<br /> <br /> AtLA completely deserves it's status as an all-time great show... though I doubt it would be as beloved as a feature film because it needs the time it got to actually work. <br /> <br /> The Jumanji movies are great, but I think they're more aimed at slightly older kids than The Little Mermaid is, so that doesn't really address my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its not a good movie full stop. </div> </div> </div>It's not a movie you liked, full stop.<br /> <br /> Even if you just look at most of the critics on aggregate sites, the general view seems to be &quot;it's not as good as the '89 movie&quot; and either, &quot;but it's still a fun kids movie,&quot; or, &quot;and my nostalgia for the older version has me nitpicking the new one to try to justify why I don't like a movie that wasn't meant for me anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> IMDB's overall user rating for the movie is pretty high (mid-70s) despite them admitting they got review bombed. Rotten Tomatoes has it sitting as a mid-90s in audience positives reviews (however one feels about their verified audience system's attempt to stop review bombing, but possibly skewing audience reviews more positive than reality).<br /> <br /> Whatever it does wrong, it's not doing wrong is a fashion that's actually hurting it all that much. It's not a great movie? Whatever, most movies can't be great movies or great just becomes average. It's a &quot;good enough for what it's trying to do&quot; movie.<br /> <br /> Sometimes we're the people that don't like something that seems to be something everyone else loves. They love it despite flaws (and we're all guilty of defending things we love despite their flaws too). You're never going to find some magical argument that will stop people from making the new Little Mermaid film a giant cash success for Disney, and thus they're going to keep making live action remakes of their animation renaissance classics. Trying to &quot;prove&quot; it's a bad movie is pointless if we're just being unpaid film critics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T05:02:02-07:00","id":1514679,"title":"","content":"I haven't bothered looking up reviews for <i>the Little Mermaid</i> because I don't feel I have a stake in how well it does and I don't want to ruin my day by deliberately exposing myself to all the dogwhistles I gloomily expect to see, but I do reckon HeavyArms is on to something here. Remember the Mario movie? Critics mostly didn't like it, and I don't either. I personally find it boring, shallow, and too full of meaningless &quot;lol i know taht gaem&quot; moments that feel nakedly cynical. But the kids I went to the movie with had a good time, which is fine because the movie isn't meant for me.<br /> <br /> ...At least I don't think it is. I dunno, that &quot;here's Brooklyn laid out exactly like level 1-1 of Super Mario Bros&quot; sequence felt like it couldn't have possibly been intended for anyone under the age of forty--look, I'm straying from my point here. My point is, I do feel that critics either forget to take a movie's target audience into account or, probably more likely, deliberately ignore it because they're speaking to their own accumulated and/or cultivated audience, so they have to tailor their messages accordingly if they want their reviews to get picked up and spread around","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T05:35:23-07:00","id":1514684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514678#post1514678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not a movie you liked, full stop.<br /> <br /> Even if you just look at most of the critics on aggregate sites, the general view seems to be &quot;it's not as good as the '89 movie&quot; and either, &quot;but it's still a fun kids movie,&quot; or, &quot;and my nostalgia for the older version has me nitpicking the new one to try to justify why I don't like a movie that wasn't meant for me anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> IMDB's overall user rating for the movie is pretty high (mid-70s) despite them admitting they got review bombed. Rotten Tomatoes has it sitting as a mid-90s in audience positives reviews (however one feels about their verified audience system's attempt to stop review bombing, but possibly skewing audience reviews more positive than reality).<br /> <br /> Whatever it does wrong, it's not doing wrong is a fashion that's actually hurting it all that much. It's not a great movie? Whatever, most movies can't be great movies or great just becomes average. It's a &quot;good enough for what it's trying to do&quot; movie.<br /> <br /> Sometimes we're the people that don't like something that seems to be something everyone else loves. They love it despite flaws (and we're all guilty of defending things we love despite their flaws too). You're never going to find some magical argument that will stop people from making the new Little Mermaid film a giant cash success for Disney, and thus they're going to keep making live action remakes of their animation renaissance classics. Trying to &quot;prove&quot; it's a bad movie is pointless if we're just being unpaid film critics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really damns it with faint praise. I actually think you make it sound worse than I considered it. You way you describe it is capitalist mediocrity incarnate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-12-2023, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T06:25:58-07:00","id":1514690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514663#post1514663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gives me the same vibes as when movie critics used to give out stars based on how Oscar-bait-like a film was, so even really good genre flicks always got garbage reviews because they weren't artsy high drama. Every parent I know that's taken their kid(s) to see it? Their kids loved it. And those kids are the target audience that fuel Disney's &quot;recycle stories instead of telling new ones&quot; core business model. It's on pace to make over a billion dollars, no matter how much critics dismiss it, and parents don't think it stacks up to the version they grew up with. Disney knows how to get parents to pay for their kids to enjoy Disney's Nth retelling of the same story... it's what made them so damned rich in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a friend who runs an afterschool daycare. On movie days she lets the kids pick the movies. They almost always pick the newer live action versions of movies (the Lion King, Jungle Book, etc) over the animated ones. To them, these live action movies are their versions and they prefer them to the animated ones. You are absolutely right that Disney is making movies aimed at kids, not aimed at adults. And, for various reasons, the kids seem to prefer the newer versions to the older ones. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T07:51:36-07:00","id":1514699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514678#post1514678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I haven't been clear, I haven't seen it.. I didn't actually like the '89 movie all the much either. Though the '89 version has creepy scenes that scared younger children (esp. the Ursula ones) that are far tamer than the original story or some of the European versions from the 70s.<br /> <br /> It doesn't need to make up for most of what you're saying, because the target audience isn't going to care. Having babysat for my niece and nephew... despite my sister's best efforts, their tolerance for cinematography I find abhorrent is rather high, but I'm pretty sure my father felt the same way about plenty of things I loved as a kid.<br /> <br /> You've never made the case that kids - aka the target audience here - of the current day are going to be bothered by the same things we'd be bothered by. The box office returns don't really back up the idea the kids hate this film and aren't dragging their reluctant parents to it in droves; which is all the movie is really meant to accomplish in the end. Sure it's be even better if parents wanted to go (though reviews from parents aren't as negative as paid critics or adults watching a reboot/whatever of a classic from their childhood as far as I can tell).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that was a partial confusion on my part with regards to what you said, along the lines of &quot;Wait, this was for kids? Seriously?&quot; In retrospect, it wasn't really something meaningfully relevant to the topic. Sorry about the bother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:04:49-07:00","id":1514741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514679#post1514679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember the Mario movie? Critics mostly didn't like it, and I don't either. I personally find it boring, shallow, and too full of meaningless &quot;lol i know taht gaem&quot; moments that feel nakedly cynical.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the difficult paradoxes of the children's movie industry. For things like traditional TV and streaming, children's entertainment needs to pass the, &quot;parents pay enough attention to be OK with their kids watching it while they go do other parent things,&quot; test. There's minimal expectation that parents are going to sit down and actually watch; even if the parent is in the same room the whole time.<br /> <br /> A theatrical release doesn't afford parents that luxury. They've got to sit there and watch it too. Ideally, a great children's movie layers in stuff for parents to enjoy that's seamlessly woven into the film... but that's really hard to do. That's why the movies that pull it off are the &quot;greats.&quot; If a movie can't interweave stuff for parents into the story, they're going to prioritize what appeal to kids as the primary audience. That's how you get stuff like making the game, &quot;spot the Easter eggs from your own childhood&quot; stuff from the Mario movie. They're hoping parents can at least engage with that if they can't get into the movie, so they're not completely bored (obviously not necessarily so successful in that example) while indulging the kids.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514684#post1514684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You way you describe it is capitalist mediocrity incarnate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's... Disney. That's my bar for Disney. That's what I think about the '89 Little Mermaid too. Disney is a financial juggernaut built on capitalist mediocrity. They take public domain stories, sanitize them of anything meaningful, make it bright and colorful with catchy songs, and then rake in cash because kids love it, and parents cave into it.<br /> <br /> I guess the big disconnect here, is that I was never expecting The Little Mermaid to be anything more than this. There was nothing out there saying, &quot;hey this is one of the exceptions where Disney breaks the formula and did something more.&quot; I'm cool with Disney making the merfolk multiracial and having minorities as main characters, but I know it's because their marketing department says that's in, not because Disney is a champion of multiracial liberal democracy and is trying to take a political stance about it.<br /> <br /> But I also don't like people bashing stuff solely on the grounds that they're not the target audience.. I'm a SFF and horror geek from back when that was extremely uncool. One time a group of kids snatched my copy of the Fellowship of the Ring, ripped off the cover, and stuck it to my hair with duct tape and chewing gum. And those same kids grew up to complain about how wrong it was to turn The Hobbit into three movies because it would never live up to the LotR trilogy, and then try to cherry-pick quotes from Tolkien about what Hobbits look like to hate on the Rings of Power having a more diverse cast. <br /> <br /> Within some social limits, I want to be left alone to enjoy what I enjoy, and not watch what I don't want to watch. And I feel that means I should be held to the same standards. I don't know if The Little Mermaid is a movie I'd like or not, and I'm probably never going to know because I doubt I'm ever going to spend the time to watch it. But other people are watching it, and loving it, and more power to them. It might be corporate drivel, but it's also entertainment that's doing its job of entertaining people. That's good enough for me to not like people trying to justify not liking it beyond personal preferences.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514690#post1514690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a friend who runs an afterschool daycare. On movie days she lets the kids pick the movies. They almost always pick the newer live action versions of movies (the Lion King, Jungle Book, etc) over the animated ones. To them, these live action movies are their versions and they prefer them to the animated ones. You are absolutely right that Disney is making movies aimed at kids, not aimed at adults. And, for various reasons, the kids seem to prefer the newer versions to the older ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a big reason is changes in visual quality to create spectacle.<br /> <br /> In the 80s and early 90s... TV animation was garbage. I might have lots of nostalgia for things like Gen 1 Transformers and Hanna Barbera, but it's hard to look back at those and think the animation really holds up. The Disney renaissance films had animation that blew the Saturday morning cartoons out of the water. Animation that's still high quality today. That said, the &quot;Saturday morning&quot; style shows done with traditional animation are on that level of quality now too. A kid that's grown up with 2010s animation shows isn't going to see animated movies from the 90s as being massive leaps in visual appeal...<br /> <br /> But when you look at kids CGI based shows to things like the Disney live action/CGI remake era? There's that leap in visual quality again. Whatever flaws I can find in The Little Mermaid if I watch it, I can guarantee it's still orders of magnitude better visually than most of the CGI stuff spoon fed to kids right now. So, while I see live-action mixed with CGI that's mediocre to me, a kid is seeing something fantastic and amazing that makes the stuff they've been watching look like garbage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T10:02:47-07:00","id":1514855,"title":"","content":"I find it off putting that I will be called whatever ism if I don't go out to see a movie that don't appeal to me. I'm not into romantic comedy films in general and why would I go see Bros at all or Woman King where they try to ignore the fact that they were major players in the slave trade? I know it's Hollywood and they will take liberties with history but that rubbed me the wrong way just as Young Guns 2 did when they had Lou Diamond Phillps &amp; Keifer Sutherland characters were killed off and in truth they lived to a ripe old age.<br /> <br /> Though to be fair I knew it being a sequel that it wouldn't be quite as good as the first Young Guns, but still I wished they made a better effort with the history as I'm a fan of that time period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T12:07:43-07:00","id":1514867,"title":"","content":"Today I saw someone wearing a T-shirt with the word &quot;POKEMON&quot; written across the chest in large, striking letters, and just below it, on the belly, a big,vibrant picture of Tweety Bird.<br /> <br /> I am putting this story in this thread because I want that shirt so bad. Not as bad as I want a T-shirt with a picture of Spock and Khan fighting with lightsabers, but it's a very close thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T13:29:20-07:00","id":1514875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514855#post1514855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it off putting that I will be called whatever ism if I don't go out to see a movie that don't appeal to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't watched Bros, The Woman King, or new The Little Mermaid. Nobody's called me any mean names over it.<br /> <br /> Did Billy Eichner put his foot in his mouth about how Bros box-office performance? Yeah, he did. And plenty of gay people have called him out on it, and that trying to guilt trip straight people into watching LGBTQ+ films is the opposite of improving representation. Also the marketing wasn't inviting to straight people as it was sold as a gay movie for gay people... so yeah, straight people apparently got the message the marketing was selling even if not what the movie itself was selling (since people that actually saw the movie tend to say it's a really good rom com in if you're into rom coms). Like you, I don't like rom coms... and that's been plenty for people to be like, &quot;oh yeah, this probably wouldn't be your thing.&quot; &quot;I don't like Disney's regurgitated narratives that replace story with fireworks,&quot; has also been plenty to have no black people call me bad things for not seeing the new movie.<br /> <br /> That said, a lot of people get called mean things on the Internet about this stuff because they say things like what you just said about The Woman King. They can't just stop with, &quot;I don't like movies inspired by true events, esp. historical dramas, because I study a lot of history and all the factual inconsistencies made for a good story bug me to much.&quot; Stop there. Everyone can respect that, and you're clearly communicating something that's not just about a specific movie. When people start with things like &quot;but they were slavers too!&quot; it just comes off as cherry-picking which stories changing which parts of history actually bug the speaker; not the base concept itself. The &quot;don't you know Africans were part of the slave trade too!&quot; is a racist dog-whistle in the US. Black people have been dealing with centuries of cultural expressions about how their history starts with slavery, or how backwards Africans were before white people colonized them. Wanting some overall positive stories about their cultural heritage isn't bad, and certainly doesn't need some &quot;well actually...&quot; from white people.<br /> <br /> As an American Jew (though damn do I have horror stories about people that will try to make &quot;American Jew vs. Jewish American&quot; a thing), I can relate. Hollywood seems to think that Jewish stories are only allowed to happen starting with the Holocaust (maybe escaping the Stalinist pogroms too thanks to the Cold War), or be Fiddler on the Roof. Biblical stories are always told with a Christian slant to them (Ben-Hur being a perfect example), or worse (Passion of the Christ anyone?). I'd love to see a story about, say, the Bar Kokhba Revolt (who doesn't love a story about plucky freedom fighters trying to defeat foreign imperialists even if they lost?), but I do not want to deal with all of the &quot;well actually...&quot; when Roman legions aren't depicted with 100% historical accuracy, or people trying to downplay the actions of Rufus and Hadrian, or claiming the Roman persecutions following the revolt are exaggerated &quot;Zionist propaganda.&quot; Because that's what happens when Jews try to tell stories about Jewish history that don't fit into the pat narratives Hollywood deems worth telling about us. Nobody goes &quot;well actually&quot; regarding the fact that there's no surviving first hand accounts that Jesus ever existed (the Gospels were all written generations later based on retelling), but they'll nitpick everything that doesn't fit into the narrative that Jews only exist to be a precursor to Jesus founding Christianity.<br /> <br /> You're going to get called mean things on Twitter/etc. if you go about telling black people that The Woman King white-washes over African slave trading, because it isn't just apolitical historical fact checking, it's mean-spirited fact-checking even if you don't intend it to be. Because you're telling people that have been struggling for hundreds of year to reclaim the right to tell their own stories... that they don't have the right to tell their own stories how they want to tell them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T21:46:39-07:00","id":1514915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1514867#post1514867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today I saw someone wearing a T-shirt with the word &quot;POKEMON&quot; written across the chest in large, striking letters, and just below it, on the belly, a big,vibrant picture of Tweety Bird.<br /> <br /> I am putting this story in this thread because I want that shirt so bad. Not as bad as I want a T-shirt with a picture of Spock and Khan fighting with lightsabers, but it's a very close thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see you, I feel you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T15:40:27-07:00","id":1515025,"title":"","content":"The basement flooding decided to come in this year with a whole host of other problems as friends this year!<br /> <br /> I just am losing bandwidth for caring about things this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T17:45:49-07:00","id":1515037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1515025#post1515025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basement flooding decided to come in this year with a whole host of other problems as friends this year!</div> </div> </div> </div>Problems are cowards. They never face you one on one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:57:56-07:00","id":1515370,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I remember that there's so much about the universe that's not understood, and I'm not going to get to understand it. Like I was looking at the night sky once and I wondered about the weird stuff that exists in space where we can't see or reach it and subsequently had to deal with the fact that I'm not going to live long enough to see humanity discover all of that. Hell, humanity might not exist long enough to find out or even have the capacity to discover it all. I hate unanswerable mysteries; it's like an itch you can't scratch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:01:33-07:00","id":1515390,"title":"","content":"I'm worried that Warner Brothers could have financial problems down the road as they seem to be hitting a snag with profitable movies and I don't want them to go under like groups like Cannon Films or others because of having to many flops and not enough hits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T15:03:58-07:00","id":1515421,"title":"","content":"You're worried about a company that made about $2 billion net profits last year? Why? Because their Q1 23 numbers are a giant loss from their recent merger/acquisition process?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T10:07:20-07:00","id":1515461,"title":"","content":"I was going by how a number of there films weren\u2019t quite the commercial success that they thought it would be. When you run a movie studio you need a fair amount of hits to keep the power on and you can\u2019t have to many flops and that what did in Cannon Films","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-18-2023, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T12:42:45-07:00","id":1515469,"title":"","content":"The Cannon Group was a relatively small film company that only lasted ~25 years.<br /> <br /> WB is has been around for a century, and is part of a massive conglomerate worth over $130 Billion dollars. They're not going to go belly up over a few flops... or the DC movies would have finished them off well before The Flash fizzled.<br /> <br /> Every major studio is enduring the same issue: The post-COVID streaming era will not tolerate the height of the MCU where dozens of massive box office blockbusters in a row was a functional aim. Streaming services are becoming profitable because a lot of people found out that they like streaming over theaters, but media execs are still convinced that they can get people to do both. As usual, Hollywood is going to spend a decade fumbling about instead of just looking over at what the porn industry is doing; because just like every other major upheaval in the film industry, porn figured out the profitable solution well before anyone else because they had to to keep their business afloat instead of having massive bank accounts and a reliable bail out (at least for executives) that other studios would buy their libraries for giant sums of money worse case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T13:15:48-07:00","id":1515475,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that Yoriham the money guy wouldn\u2019t or couldn\u2019t keep his cousin in check when it came to funds and was more focused on quantity of films rather then quality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T16:15:05-07:00","id":1515578,"title":"","content":"Shopped at a local used-book store and actually found White-Wolf's RPGs there; they were Vampire: Dark Ages Books (<i>Core-book, Ashen Knight and Libellus</i>), all for 50% more or double, the original asking price, used. No thank you. I'm not spending $49 on a $17 book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T17:31:46-07:00","id":1515593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1515469#post1515469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cannon Group was a relatively small film company that only lasted ~25 years.<br /> <br /> WB is has been around for a century, and is part of a massive conglomerate worth over $130 Billion dollars. They're not going to go belly up over a few flops... or the DC movies would have finished them off well before The Flash fizzled.<br /> <br /> Every major studio is enduring the same issue: The post-COVID streaming era will not tolerate the height of the MCU where dozens of massive box office blockbusters in a row was a functional aim. Streaming services are becoming profitable because a lot of people found out that they like streaming over theaters, but media execs are still convinced that they can get people to do both. As usual, Hollywood is going to spend a decade fumbling about instead of just looking over at what the porn industry is doing; because just like every other major upheaval in the film industry, porn figured out the profitable solution well before anyone else because they had to to keep their business afloat instead of having massive bank accounts and a reliable bail out (at least for executives) that other studios would buy their libraries for giant sums of money worse case.</div> </div> </div> </div>THere is a joke about porn being our glorious leader in these troubling times and I cannot make it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T11:04:45-07:00","id":1516027,"title":"","content":"It was a sign that you knew you created something some good that the porn industry would do a version of it for there fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T09:32:37-07:00","id":1516221,"title":"","content":"I see what you mean on how how streaming services are making it hard for movie companies to make money the old way. Didn't Disney lose a whole whack of money due to streaming services being more popular then hoping of making big bucks at the theatres?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T15:33:37-07:00","id":1516267,"title":"","content":"It's not hard to make money the &quot;old way&quot; it's hard to make obscene piles of money and commit to the insanity of unlimited growth that way.<br /> <br /> The core problem is that the current economy doesn't consider &quot;sustainable income generation&quot; be good enough. You have to constantly be making more (beyond things like inflation) than before.<br /> <br /> You can't just make X profits consistently from quarter to quarter, you need to constantly do X+n where n is each new quarter. That's obviously unsustainable, but a bunch of people are making a lot of money until it all crashes; and they aren't going to be liable for it when it does.<br /> <br /> The aggravating factor is that the rich and business operate in a completely different type of economics from everyone else. It's very hard to megacorporations to actually lose money, because they purposefully carry enough debt that any project that ends up costing more than it makes can be used in write-offs to offset debt payments or taxes instead. <br /> <br /> If companies would restrain themselves to a small number of mega-blockbusters a year, and then put more focus on diversification (both in the sense of more smaller projects, and more diverse monetization of their libraries)... we'd never be hearing about how WB's DC division just bombed three movies in a row, after cancelling a finished movie that looked like it would have been very well received for a tax write off. But that would lead to steady sustainable income, not constant growth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T18:37:14-07:00","id":1516294,"title":"","content":"On a more small-scale note - summer is here. Fuuuuuck I hate the heat. Why does Hokkaido's weather function on such a pendulum?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T18:38:15-07:00","id":1516295,"title":"","content":"How hot does it get? With humidity factored in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T18:46:39-07:00","id":1516297,"title":"","content":"During the summer? Ranges from 60-90F, depending on the day. Humidity swings through the 40s to the 70s. Neither of which are <i>awful</i> -I've lived in worse- I just abhore the heat. Plus the house gets seems hellbent on retaining whatever temperature was outside for several hours after the fact, hot or cold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T07:05:22-07:00","id":1516333,"title":"","content":"Just saw the Vulture report on the Across the Spiderverse animators. Only thing I can say is that I really hope the delay petitions work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T09:00:28-07:00","id":1516346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1516333#post1516333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saw the Vulture report on the Across the Spiderverse animators. Only thing I can say is that I really hope the delay petitions work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously. I made a just-joking-but-not-really statement about how Spider-Verse movies are my favorite, but even I don't want them at the expense of the health of the people who make them; and more than that, the whistle blown makes me think I should probably stop praising any movie made by Lord and Miller. I hope they step up and make this right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:04:40-07:00","id":1516380,"title":"","content":"Interesting series of events over last night/today got me thinking. My partner had never seen Terminator so we were going to rent it online, however it was only for purchase seemed a bit steep (\u00a38) so we held off. This afternoon I found a physical dvd copy for \u00a31 in a charity store. This seems a bit of a disconnect in comparative value. In theory we really shouldnt be paying that much for a digital copy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-28-2023, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T06:16:01-07:00","id":1516446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1516346#post1516346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seriously. I made a just-joking-but-not-really statement about how Spider-Verse movies are my favorite, but even I don't want them at the expense of the health of the people who make them; and more than that, the whistle blown makes me think I should probably stop praising any movie made by Lord and Miller. I hope they step up and make this right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we ideally can love the movies' quality and protest the working conditions under which they were made without any paradox. There is no universal law that says these movies can't be just as good without breaking animators in the process. You just have to give them more time to work in, a more predictable schedule and encourage rest.<br /> <br /> I think the big thing in the way of that is the Hollywood release calendar and the short-term profits and growth motives undergirding it. Also, our veneration of &quot;uncompromising mad genius&quot; artists. <br /> <br /> if nothing is done about this though...i dunno what my response should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T08:44:02-07:00","id":1516461,"title":"","content":"Like I said before on another post is that maybe we should give the superhero genre a well earned rest and maybe have one every odd year and doesn't have to be a big mega blockbuster every time. Sometimes just a simple origin story with a modest budget can work just as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T14:35:25-07:00","id":1516528,"title":"","content":"The superhero genre can basically keep putting out movies weekly forever and not suffer. It just can't handle blockbusters.<br /> <br /> Like, the DC animated direct to home/video/streaming stuff? There's a truly massive library of it, makes consistent use of the DC's huge roster of characters and alternative Earths, and its worst entries are still generally better than 95% of the live action stuff. There's kid friendly stuff, there's more mature stuff, they're some great adaptations of the classic/keystone story arcs that don't ruin them in the process (even if there's a notoriously bad addition into a certain Batman story... it doesn't change the actual key story). DC fans tend to love the animated stuff, and consume it in droves, and thus it keeps getting made. It's been going non-stop for <b>30</b> years with a constant stream of content. It's so beloved by fans that the comics change to be more like it (the more obvious example being Harley Quinn being an original character to the 90s animated Batman TV show, and now she's one of their most popular characters and she's in everything).<br /> <br /> The appetite is there, the C-suite just needs to listen to the people that know how to feed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T15:48:42-07:00","id":1516537,"title":"","content":"The DC Animated films is one of the few things that they have done right in comparsion to there so so live action versions outside of Batman stuff and I think Cavill would have been a awesome Superman if he was given a great script. I view him like I view Pierce Bronson during his time as James Bond in that he he was perfect in the role but didn't get the awesome scripts he should've deserved for such iconic characters.<br /> <br /> My only concern was that they focused heavily on Superman, Batman and the Justice League way to often and not enough on the other characters such as Titans, Outsiders or even the JSA for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-28-2023, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:12:15-07:00","id":1516545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1516446#post1516446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we ideally can love the movies' quality and protest the working conditions under which they were made without any paradox. There is no universal law that says these movies can't be just as good without breaking animators in the process. You just have to give them more time to work in, a more predictable schedule and encourage rest.<br /> <br /> I think the big thing in the way of that is the Hollywood release calendar and the short-term profits and growth motives undergirding it. Also, our veneration of &quot;uncompromising mad genius&quot; artists.<br /> <br /> if nothing is done about this though...i dunno what my response should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>THe problem, particularly in the immediate context of Spiderverse being in theaters only (for anyone not willing to participate in piracy), is that glowing about how good the movie is creates an incentive for people to go see it, unethical management of the artists who made it be damned-and if you haven't noticed, there's a <i>lot</i> of chatter about how damn good Spiderverse. People don't want to miss out on seeing a movie that is this well hyped or be left out of the ongoing conversation about that excellent movie, and time and tide has shown that people will absolutely go a see movie like this regardless of the new information of the team's overwork.<br /> <br /> Because of this, it's going to be hard to convince the people at the top that they should even try to address the issue, because it's making money and bringing acclaim regardless, which can read as it not mattering. If the audience was actually that upset about the way it was made, <i>surely</i> they'd stop talking about it, <i>surely</i> they wouldn't keep buying tickets. After all, hasn't it been deomsntrated <i>so many times before</i> that if people object to something, they'll draw a picket line around it? No, all this success says that surely it's not actually that big of a deal, and surely the audience would much rather have Beyond The Spiderverse made in at least similar time then have it take more time or get more manpower to be made more ethically.<br /> <br /> it sucks, but like it or not, creating discussion around Spiderverse <i>of any sort</i> that isn't &quot;The way this movie was made is some god damned bullshit and needs to be fixed&quot; is basically giving a greenlight to do it again to the people who the power to <i>actually</i> give a shit about the production. Every person you get excited to watch it, enough to buy a ticket, is another push on the scale towards doing it again-and with how good it is, it's pretty hard to not excite people who haven't seen it.<br /> <br /> So, no, I don't think, at this moment, you can love the movie's quality if you also want to protest the working conditions. You can't divorce the quality from the production, because the production is what made the current quality, and more people than not are only going to care about that quality than it's production.<br /> <br /> Of course, the real tragedy is that it doesn't really matter at this point-Spiderverse has done so well that that message has basically already been sent, and there's no way it can actually be stopped now. Unless something is actually, drastically, done, the producers have no reason to really change course, and the audience is no longer at the point where they can take that drastic action.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, all of the above still applies-you can't talk about the quality without risking adding to the piles of reasons to do the same for Beyond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:17:47-07:00","id":1516547,"title":"","content":"I feel sorry for FX people for the more recent films that had to work fast to get the effects done and you see how subpar it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:19:54-07:00","id":1516548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1516380#post1516380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting series of events over last night/today got me thinking. My partner had never seen Terminator so we were going to rent it online, however it was only for purchase seemed a bit steep (\u00a38) so we held off. This afternoon I found a physical dvd copy for \u00a31 in a charity store. This seems a bit of a disconnect in comparative value. In theory we really shouldnt be paying that much for a digital copy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first two Terminator films will be classic films that will be fondly remember long after the cast and director have passed away. I refuse to acknowledge the follow ups as nothing then bad fan fiction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:50:43-07:00","id":1516553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1516446#post1516446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we ideally can love the movies' quality and protest the working conditions under which they were made without any paradox. There is no universal law that says these movies can't be just as good without breaking animators in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevertheless, I refuse to be part of the hype machine for a studio I find morally unacceptable. Or, you know, more morally unacceptable than the baseline exploitation I expect workers to be put through under our economic system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T13:01:59-07:00","id":1517301,"title":"","content":"(Probably super minor)<br /> <br /> Last Supper. Doesn\u2019t that strike anyone else as an odd name for a Graveyard plot? Like, I\u2019m not a funeral director, but that\u2019s a name I would use to be punny with a place run by ghouls, not something I\u2019d actually name somewhere where we put loved one\u2019s remains. Why name it something like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T13:22:33-07:00","id":1517307,"title":"","content":"I could <i>kinda</i> see it being the implication that this is the final time everyone will be together, but given that -as far as I'm aware- one doesn't tend to eat at the funeral home, it is indeed making me think this is a job for Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T05:35:10-07:00","id":1517344,"title":"","content":"I have been chasing my tail trying to get my damn military status sorted for <b><i><u>TWO GODDAMN MONTHS.</u></i></b> It took that long for them to finally get around to realizing &quot;oh, wait, the paperwork we had you submit was pointless&quot;, when that fact should have been BLATANTLY APPARENT from just LOOKING AT THE GODDAMN SCREEN THEY WERE INSTRUCTING ME OFF OF! And they wouldn't have even fucking made any move on it, <i>noticed that fact,</i> or even <i>told</i> me if I hadn't started badgering them! This has <i>directly </i>cost me two job offers, and indirectly cost me about a half-dozen more. Gaaaaaah!<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.tenor.com/8LMsyLOH0GoAAAAC/screams-externally-ahh.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/8LMsyLOH0GoAAAAC/screams-externally-ahh.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/8LMsyLOH0GoAAAAC/screams-externally-ahh.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T11:41:50-07:00","id":1517580,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar271_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"271\" data-vbnamecard=\"271\">JimB</a> are right, I accept it and I hate everything because of it. Fuck, it really was my favorite movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T00:23:51-07:00","id":1517687,"title":"","content":"Person &quot;Hey Robin, I believe the following. [Insert take here]. What do you think of that?&quot;<br /> <br /> Robin-&quot;Well its a negative and I disagree with your stance.&quot;<br /> <br /> Person-&quot; Well here's my rationale why I'm gonna ignore what you said.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Why bother asking me? I could have saved 20 minutes not knowing your take on something that doesn't affect me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T19:07:03-07:00","id":1517725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1516548#post1516548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first two Terminator films will be classic films that will be fondly remember long after the cast and director have passed away. I refuse to acknowledge the follow ups as nothing then bad fan fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved the Terminator films when I was a Tween and I would have wet myself if I saw Terminator: Salvation back then. I even had the comic books like, Terminator: Burning Earth. Now, I'll watch anything based off of Terminator, (even Abram's reboot was interesting), but not in the theaters. <br /> <br /> However, I never like Harlan Ellison's lawsuit over the franchise. Yeah, the opening scene of Terminator is like the opening-scene from The Outer Limits' episode, Soldier, and yes, Harlan may have written that, but, he didn't direct, or film or produce that scene. He only has acknowledgement because Cameron confessed to copying it, which a lot of film-students do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T08:36:03-07:00","id":1517780,"title":"","content":"My favorite is when a supervisor comes running to you to fix a problem that they caused and ignored what you said of what would happen if they did that.<br /> <br /> My take is that you created the problem and you ingored my advice and I have no obligation to help bail you out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T11:59:46-07:00","id":1517801,"title":"","content":"People who ignorantly assume that it is impossible to be law-abiding and moral in the absence of some kind of religious faith. They arrogantly assume that if you aren\u2019t in line with whatever claptrap they\u2019re peddling you must be inherently immoral and untrustworthy. Then when you point out that you obviously aren\u2019t wantonly stealing, murdering, or whatever else, they\u2019ll try to apply some kind of degenerate half-logic to \u201cprove\u201d their point using at best anecdotal nonsense and speculation. Hypocrites, all of them. These so-called moral and god-fearing creatures commit just as many (if not more) crimes as anyone who refuses to believe their nonsense. The only difference is that afterward they\u2019ll go running to some absentee, imaginary authority figure for a forgiveness they can\u2019t be bothered to offer anyone else. And it\u2019s not as if all that praying and chanting stops them from doing the same things later, they just think they can shed accountability through some primitive rituals. If anything that makes them LESS moral as they never take an ounce of responsibility for their own actions.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T12:20:31-07:00","id":1517806,"title":"","content":"Chronic health conditions can kindly <i>go to hell</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 07-12-2023, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T12:55:47-07:00","id":1517808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1517725#post1517725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I loved the Terminator films when I was a Tween and I would have wet myself if I saw Terminator: Salvation back then. I even had the comic books like, Terminator: Burning Earth. Now, I'll watch anything based off of Terminator, (even Abram's reboot was interesting), but not in the theaters.<br /> <br /> However, I never like Harlan Ellison's lawsuit over the franchise. Yeah, the opening scene of Terminator is like the opening-scene from The Outer Limits' episode, Soldier, and yes, Harlan may have written that, but, he didn't direct, or film or produce that scene. He only has acknowledgement because Cameron confessed to copying it, which a lot of film-students do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading S.M. Stirling trilogy of Terminator novels that I felt were quite good and caught the essence of the first two films quite well and filled in some gaps that James Cameron and crew didn't have time to flesh out. In that series of novels we learn whom the 800 series Terminator 101 model was based on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T08:49:40-07:00","id":1517946,"title":"","content":"Another pet peeve is when supervisors can not understand the notion that sometimes people have to take time off for personal reasons and demand to know what those reasons. We had one such supervisor get chewed out for that reason alone when he asked a coworker of mine what the reasons were wouldn't grant the time off unless he knew why. In the end the leave of absence was given and an email was sent to those of the supervisor level about what reasonable expectations of privacy is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T10:24:36-07:00","id":1517955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1517801#post1517801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who ignorantly assume that it is impossible to be law-abiding and moral in the absence of some kind of religious faith.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to work for an explicitly Christian company, directed by a guy with a doctorate in Christian studies and staffed with two ministers. One day my boss was talking to one of the ministers, saying that without fear of God there's no reason to behave morally, so atheists are incapable of morality. And because he was my boss, I couldn't say to him, <i>Do you have any idea how scary that makes you? That you can't understand someone who says 'I don't want to make anyone suffer' or even 'I've suffered, so I don't want to make anyone else suffer'? That if you ever have a crisis of faith, there's nothing inside you to make you hesitate being the worst version of yourself you could possibly imagine?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T16:13:00-07:00","id":1517986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1517955#post1517955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Do you have any idea how scary that makes you? That you can't understand someone who says 'I don't want to make anyone suffer' or even 'I've suffered, so I don't want to make anyone else suffer'? That if you ever have a crisis of faith, there's nothing inside you to make you hesitate being the worst version of yourself you could possibly imagine?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I talked to a distant relative once who I wish I could have said this exact phrase to. It perfectly sums up the sheer hypocrisy of these sorts of people.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:05:20-07:00","id":1518067,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how I feel about the Hollywood writers and actors going on strike now? On the one one hand I watch mostly independent and foreign films and don't watch many of there films anymore out of John Wick &amp; Mission Impossible as I'm a big Keanu Reeves &amp; Tom Cruise fan along with Nicolas Cage and Mel Gibson and will make an effort to watch there work. Then on the other hand I feel sorry for the people who work on the movie sets such as the carpenters, stunt people, electricans and others who are behind the scenes that make the films look good and don't have any work right now. It's a tough thing to hear about","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:23:34-07:00","id":1518072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1517955#post1517955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I used to work for an explicitly Christian company, directed by a guy with a doctorate in Christian studies and staffed with two ministers. One day my boss was talking to one of the ministers, saying that without fear of God there's no reason to behave morally, so atheists are incapable of morality. And because he was my boss, I couldn't say to him, <i>Do you have any idea how scary that makes you? That you can't understand someone who says 'I don't want to make anyone suffer' or even 'I've suffered, so I don't want to make anyone else suffer'? That if you ever have a crisis of faith, there's nothing inside you to make you hesitate being the worst version of yourself you could possibly imagine?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard people say before too, and it always seems so unhinged to me. It kinda scary...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:25:59-07:00","id":1518073,"title":"","content":"Welcome to the world of 2023 where everything seems unhinged and right is wrong, wrong is right, up is down and down is up and facts have been replaced by feelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T17:37:47-07:00","id":1518112,"title":"","content":"I feel pretty good about the strike, but I'd probably have to get too political to explain why, so I'll just leave it that I support any worker trying to keep more of the money their work creates","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T04:27:34-07:00","id":1518173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1518112#post1518112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel pretty good about the strike, but I'd probably have to get too political to explain why, so I'll just leave it that I support any worker trying to keep more of the money their work creates</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you! I hope they get a good deal out it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T10:14:02-07:00","id":1518184,"title":"","content":"I mean who would've thought that we would have a debate on the Senate floor about the biological differences between men and women and that having trans women playing the same sports with biological women should not be considered unwise as they are still biological males and even with hormone treatments reducing muscle mass somewhat. They still have a major advantage in terms of physical strength and this Kelly Robinson must have been totally unaware of the fact that the Williams sisters were beat in 1998 by Karstan who was ranked 203rd overall and the fact Serena admitted that she wouldn't win against a top male tennis player on a appearance on David Lettermen.<br /> <br /> Some of the stuff that came out the hearing was disturbing and eye opening to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T01:58:54-07:00","id":1518220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1518067#post1518067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then on the other hand I feel sorry for the people who work on the movie sets such as the carpenters, stunt people, electricans and others who are behind the scenes that make the films look good and don't have any work right now. It's a tough thing to hear about</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond the fact that lots of US stunt performers are part of SAG-AFTRA and thus are on strike, IATSE (the union that covers the majority of the other laborers for films and TV) has expressed complete solidarity with the WGA and SAG... because they all know that the C-suite folks making $20+ million a year are the ones that get the most for doing the least; not the writers and actors that make the industry possible at all.<br /> <br /> Labor solidarity works because unions/guilds/etc. know not to turn on each other. DGA and IASTE might not be striking, but if they know they all need to have each other's backs against the studio execs. Don't feel sorry for the carpenters, they have strike funds for these situations. Be angry at the studios for prioritizing a few dozen people being able to afford new yachts instead of paying the labor their industry is based on in a fair fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1518184#post1518184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean who would've thought that we would have a debate on the Senate floor about the biological differences between men and women and that having trans women playing the same sports with biological women should not be considered unwise as they are still biological males and even with hormone treatments reducing muscle mass somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>These debates are necessary because anyone throwing around &quot;biological&quot; male or female like this isn't educated enough at all to say anything that isn't just transphobic garbage in a lab coat.<br /> <br /> &quot;Biological sex&quot; isn't science. It's cherry-picking data to serve social norms. You're not protecting some sacred class of athletes either. AFAB cis--women have been denied access to international competitions because their natural testosterone levels were &quot;too male&quot; for them to be &quot;biologically female,&quot; despite being born with fully functional reproductive systems.<br /> <br /> Human sexes are not binary, they're bimodal. Being bimodal, there's always going to be people in the middle that don't neatly fit into male or female based on whichever biological benchmark you want to use. We society solves for that? Then we can have a non-transphoic debate about trans athletes. Until sexual bimodality is addressed in sports, keeping trans people out of sports based on wanting to compete as their gender isn't based on anything remotely scientific. If &quot;biological females&quot; can get banned from their sports for not being the right kind of &quot;biological female,&quot; any claims of transwomen having an unfair advantage is a smokescreen.<br /> <br /> How the Williams sisters did against cis-male tennis players isn't the point, because those men aren't on hormone treatments.<br /> <br /> If you were paying attention to the hearing, why not pick apart Riley Gaines for complaining about losing to Lia Thomas? Because Gaines was 5th, and Thomas was 4th, in their qualifiers. If Thomas has such a huge advantage for being trans... why did she lose to three cis swimmers? Oh, right, because that doesn't actually fit the narrative that transwomen are &quot;cheating&quot; with their biological advantages.<br /> <br /> Like I said, it's a smokescreen. It's an appeal to traditions and social norms, not facts and science. It's about changing the rules when minorities start winning on their own merit, so minorities go back to losing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T02:15:15-07:00","id":1518223,"title":"","content":"People put way too much stock in sports either way. Though as a gangly, uncoordinated homebody, I'm biased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T02:32:42-07:00","id":1518225,"title":"","content":"Eh? Sports are part of humanity. We've been doing sports for all of recorded history, across all cultures, and thus probably for far, far longer. Sports are useful even on a very detached level because they help us relieve a lot of instincts we don't let out much thanks to large scale civilization happening. The vast majority of the real problems in sports is... actually kinda like all the problems in the arts: it's entertainment done by people that happen to love what they do that lots of people love watching. Then a bunch of rich assholes worm into this and want to turn the love of the game, and the love of watching the game, into all the money for them. Once it becomes more about lining rich people's pockets with even more money, instead of the game being played, it always makes things worse.<br /> <br /> Curling is one of my favorite sports to watch. I think the fact that nobody gets full ride scholarships to university for curling, nobody's getting massive paychecks in professional curling, etc. is part of why. There's enough money so that the best of the best can compete at the top levels for the world to enjoy... but not enough money for corporate greed to start fucking it all up. There's a level of good sportsmanship you don't see in sports where so much more is on the line. It's a sport where there isn't a ref on the ice. An official only comes out if the captains can't agree and need a measuring stick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T03:08:26-07:00","id":1518226,"title":"","content":"While I get where you're coming from, the degree to which a significant chunk people seem to tie their identity to their favorite sports team still leaves me with a negative opinion.<br /> <br /> Though, again, I'm biased by being <i>utterly</i> uninterested in playing sports in the first place, let alone watching them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T03:37:06-07:00","id":1518229,"title":"","content":"I want to thank Heavy Arms for tackling the argument with much more tact than I could, and I would like to agree with/slightly expand upon one point in particular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1518220#post1518220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human sexes are not binary, they're bimodal. Being bimodal, there's always going to be people in the middle that don't neatly fit into male or female based on whichever biological benchmark you want to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>My motto these days is, &quot;Nothing is simple; everything is complicated.&quot; Sex is one of the most complicated things out there, to the point that I'm personally not even sure words like &quot;man&quot; and &quot;woman&quot; describe real things that exist in the real world, so they definitely don't <i>pre</i>scribe how people are or should be. We just let our attachments to these outdated and overly simplistic categories become so important in our minds that we'll get angry if reality doesn't neatly suit the preconceptions we try to force upon it.<br /> <br /> Words like &quot;man&quot; and &quot;woman&quot; describe concepts that were thought up by cavemen who thought thunder was made by sky-spirits battling each other and that an eclipse was a demon trying to eat the sun. Those categories are not terribly accurate and are being exposed as losing their usefulness, which is fine. That's how science works: we get better at detecting and identifying the components of reality, and update or abandon old ideas to suit our new knowledge. Our society is not beholden to keep incorrect ideas around just because they're old, let alone to persecute anyone in an attempt to deny how incorrect old ideas are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T10:05:02-07:00","id":1518251,"title":"","content":"I find all this media complaint about trans athletes more than a little hypocritical considering professional athletics is well known for being rife with \u201cperformance enhancer\u201d use across the board. Compared to that, the issue of whatever biological assignment seems moot by comparison.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s probably liberating to think that nothing in life is simple and everything has its own layered complexity, until you realize that those two things strip people of the things they actually got into this whole civilization for; stability and security. Endless fractal complexity does not make for a stable or secure environment, it just injects more and more complexity and anxiety into the mix. Technology and society both mutate faster than actual human beings can, and lets face it, every single year it gets worse as more and more exceptions and terms are discovered. It didn\u2019t surprise me that all these transphobic, and homophobic bad actors popped up in the US after the wave of additional parameters started spreading 20+ years ago. Once it became more than just man/woman or gay/straight you immediately lost all the simpler people who make up the general population and who don\u2019t want to have to spend additional effort trying to understand the identity politics of each and every individual they talk to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s tempting to dismiss the perspective of those people as uneducated, and uninformed, until you stop to consider the sheer volume of conflicting information there is on the subject. It is unrealistic and more than a little elitist to assume everyone can dedicate the time and effort to become a collegiate level expert on human sexuality theory in the modern day. Especially when any actual discussion of it is being cleared out of schools thanks to a far-right agenda, and you have to do it in your spare time. But then again, we\u2019re dealing with a world now that expects you to be a PHD-level expert in whatever field before you\u2019re allowed to have an opinion of your own, so I shouldn\u2019t be surprised.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can\u2019t wait to see how civilization collapses under all this bullshit this time.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T13:28:40-07:00","id":1518265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1518229#post1518229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sex is one of the most complicated things out there, to the point that I'm personally not even sure words like &quot;man&quot; and &quot;woman&quot; describe real things that exist in the real world, so they definitely don't <i>pre</i>scribe how people are or should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think it's important to remember that just because something is an artificial human construct doesn't mean it isn't &quot;real&quot; even if reality is complicated.<br /> <br /> To get away from more serious issues: Video game consoles are real, even though humans made them up; including the idea of putting value in a highly specialized computer just for playing video games. Now, there are lots of things to discuss where the differences between consoles and PCs don't matter, or the differences between the latest X-Box and Playstation don't matter. If you, say, want to improve the video game rating systems so parents can be better informed (since the ESRB sucks at its job)... you can ignore the complex reality of hardware specs and corporate-enforced exclusivity. If you're trying to figure out if you want to buy a video game console at all, and is so which, the nuances suddenly matter a lot more.<br /> <br /> I think part of accepting the complexity of reality is also accepting that scope dictates how much complexity we need to include in a given discussion. If the conversation participants all accept that human sexes are bimodal, then there's no reason to go into the complexities of why we know that's the case. We can focus on how to adjust society to accept that the outdated concept of a sex binary is outdated, and better accommodate people in the fuzzy middle between the two main modes that have historically been mistreated by society.<br /> <br /> Human experiences of artificial social constructs are also very real. Scientifically, &quot;race&quot; isn't real. There's no scientific way to match the social construct of &quot;race&quot; to a concrete set of biological metrics. But race is very real for people that experience discrimination based on it. Women, regardless of the fuzzy edges of what &quot;woman&quot; means, face real problems because of that label. It ultimately doesn't matter if the line used to divide the favored and the outsider is made up or not. The urge to discriminate is real and needs to be addressed as a far more pressing matter than if people are being discriminated against over &quot;real&quot; things like Downs Syndrome or &quot;unreal&quot; things like discriminating against people with CAH because they don't fit into one of two neat boxes regard &quot;biological sex.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1518251#post1518251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s probably liberating to think that nothing in life is simple and everything has its own layered complexity, until you realize that those two things strip people of the things they actually got into this whole civilization for; stability and security.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure that works. Part of the compromise of civilization is an increase in social complexity. That's the work communities put in to facilitate having complex high population societies. That complexity is what makes stability and security possible in the first place. That complexity allows for specialized members of society, or bureaucracy and cross-specialty cooperation to do more than we could when we lived in smaller communities where everyone had to contribute to everything. If you want police or a standing military for security, you need complex logistics to support having people that don't actively do things like grow crops, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once it became more than just man/woman or gay/straight you immediately lost all the simpler people who make up the general population and who don\u2019t want to have to spend additional effort trying to understand the identity politics of each and every individual they talk to. </div> </div> </div>1) It's always been more than man/woman and gay/straight. Your selling humans short a lot here. One of the reasons the US political system is so screwed up is that living in a low population rural area vs. living in a dense population urban area literally impacts people's brains and how they relate to other people. When you grow up in a dense population with high diversity, your brain turns on a bunch of pathways to navigate that more easily. If you grow up in a low populate and more homogeneous environment, your brain puts its energy to other things.<br /> <br /> 2) The idea that people have to &quot;understand the identity politics of each and every individual they talk to,&quot; is pretty BS. First, that's natural human instinct as social creatures anyway. Second, for the most part people don't expect random strangers to know or have to know all of that. People just want basic empathy and decency. I am in the ~20% of my country that isn't a member of the dominant religion. I don't expect every Christian in the US to be a religious studies major, but they could be a lot more empathetic that 1 out of every 5 people they interact with isn't going to be Christian, and doesn't want to be treated like a Christian until they have to say something. Just remembering that not everyone is the same as you, and not assuming that someone's the same as you when you talk to them is all people are looking for from their fellow citizens. PhDs and all that is for politicians and so on to have real debates about policy and law; and yes expertise should be part of all of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can\u2019t wait to see how civilization collapses under all this bullshit this time.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure climate change is going to do this civilization in far sooner than gender politics; even if both are plagued by political movements that have stigmatized expertise, facts, and logic to elevate &quot;sincerely held beliefs,&quot; as the most important factor in social organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T18:46:34-07:00","id":1518283,"title":"","content":"If I can offer a bit related commentary:<br /> <br /> I live in Colorado Springs, the place where Focus on the Family is headquartered, and has for the better part of my two decades has been conservative, complete with the religious types. I'm pre-op trans genderfluid and tall enough to be a basketball players, so when I go out presenting as femme, in the world of people who fear about out-of-control-wokeness, you'd imagine people would be tripping over themselves trying to make sure they properly understand at a glance that I am pre-op trans genderfluid, and also instantly know what gender I feel like regardless of what my presentation is, and what my sexuality and kink labels are.<br /> <br /> It's not what I want and it's not what happens. The grand majority of people I meet either default to ma'am/miss/she/her or they/them and I run with it (because those are accurate). Some people will say sir and I get stung but otherwise keep moving on. A few, more people than I would have expected, ask me how I like to be addressed. If anyone has felt trapped in trying to address me, the quickness of response that is normal has not relayed that fact to me.<br /> <br /> The one person I can think of who came close to it asked me if it was okay if they called me a guy because they had just asked me to explain it to them because they had never heard of this before, and they were a grandma well up in their years. I told her sure, I wasn't expecting her to get it right, with the usual note to myself that I didn't expect her to like it at all. She never once failed to refer to me as a woman.<br /> <br /> This &quot;labyrinth of identities&quot; thing that people get into is a farce brought up to feed the discomfort and unease people feel with something that is new or otherwise unfamiliar in an attempt to alienate the majority from the people who benefit the most it's implementation. The outraged non-typical gendered individual is likewise a farce for the same purpose-most people without a binary gender identity are honestly more afraid of standing up for who they are, because doing so has historically been an invitation for violence in a number of different forms.<br /> <br /> Gender identity isn't going to destroy civilization. Gender identity is flotsam on the actual ocean of things going on that are simply complicated in some form, nevermind actually harmful to civilization. That's why a lot of people want you to focus on it, on all side of the argument-it's for the most part superficial, and the making of it a major issue says a lot about how the actual problems are and are not is going to be handled.<br /> <br /> Capitalism destroying natural resources, including the people working within capitalism, faster than we can restore them, and paligenetic ultranationalism virulently attacking others within and without the societies leaning into it are the things that going to destroy civilization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T19:05:06-07:00","id":1518285,"title":"","content":"I really with there was a gender-neutral form between &quot;sir&quot; and &quot;ma'am&quot;. Like, a lot of my verbal tics are derived from the military, and you <i>have</i> to use one of the two when you're being polite or talking to a superior officer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T19:25:55-07:00","id":1518287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1518285#post1518285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really with there was a gender-neutral form between &quot;sir&quot; and &quot;ma'am&quot;. Like, a lot of my verbal tics are derived from the military, and you <i>have</i> to use one of the two when you're being polite or talking to a superior officer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being the leftist that I am, I would propose comrade as an alternative, but, with an exception where rank comes in, you might rely on the nearest role a person fills that immediately relates to in the scenario. Let me chew on it more and I might come up with some other useful alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T19:40:25-07:00","id":1518288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1518287#post1518287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being the leftist that I am, I would propose comrade as an alternative, but, with an exception where rank comes in, you might rely on the nearest role a person fills that immediately relates to in the scenario. Let me chew on it more and I might come up with some other useful alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>can</i> just do (Rank)(Surname) in place of Sir/ma'am, but it gets really cumbersome and people look at ya funny. Once or twice at the start of the conversation is fine, more than that gets weird. It's easier if you're talking to your subordinates - when talking <i>down</i> the chain of command, you can just use their first or last name. Can't do that going up the chain though.<br /> <br /> Funny, unrelated note! In Tagalog, the word for Sir or Ma'am is the same. In most Tagalog-English dictionaries, the translation gets transcribed as &quot;Ma'am/Sir&quot;. Quite a few Pinoy with a cursory understanding of English end up assuming that's one word. So growing up, lots of my parents employees would refer to them as &quot;Ma'amsir&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T22:37:35-07:00","id":1518413,"title":"","content":"My employers finally got my ticket home, which is part and parcel for the employment contract. I'm a touch salty that they finally got around to it twelve days before the flight though - I still need to get myself up to a city three hours away by public transport -with two stuffed suitcases containing my worldly possessions- and find myself a hotel for the two days prior, since my lease is up then. Which would be mostly just annoying, but given that I'm trying to find a room for ten days from now, prices skyrocket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T16:30:07-07:00","id":1518790,"title":"","content":"Ah, Limbus Company. Fxxks sake.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile it\u2019s a cold reminder that people don\u2019t always bother to know the sociopolitical issues of another country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T09:16:38-07:00","id":1518829,"title":"","content":"Heatwave weather is a drag and we need rain to help with the wildfires we have in our neck of the woods and an hour of heavy rain last night isn't just enough to deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T03:30:42-07:00","id":1519591,"title":"","content":"I finished that Secret Invasion TV show from Marvel today and there I was thinking &quot;It can't be that bad, can it?&quot;... nope, what a letdown of a show. 200 million dollars for... that?! Eurgh, it makes me really worried about how Loki season 2 will turn out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T12:57:10-07:00","id":1519653,"title":"","content":"I hate how I feel like I've wasted five years of my life and all I have to show for it was a severe mental breakdown right before things began going to shit with the pandemic in 2020 and the lockdowns exacerbating it.<br /> <br /> I've since recovered from all that trauma, I take medication that's helped me a lot and I have gotten married to a loving and caring husband, and I'm a lot better off now emotionally than I was two years ago or even one year ago but I still feel haunted by those bad memories all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T15:15:58-07:00","id":1519792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519591#post1519591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finished that Secret Invasion TV show from Marvel today and there I was thinking &quot;It can't be that bad, can it?&quot;... nope, what a letdown of a show. 200 million dollars for... that?! Eurgh, it makes me really worried about how Loki season 2 will turn out...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's superhero fatique at this point Knightingale. Sooner or later a genre will get overplayed and people get jaded and bored and will want to move onto new things. I remember reading an article quite a number of years ago around the time of Captain America Winter Solider about how the genre could at some point peter out like the western films that my parents watched when they were much younger and starting out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-08-2023, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T17:13:06-07:00","id":1519805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519591#post1519591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finished that Secret Invasion TV show from Marvel today and there I was thinking &quot;It can't be that bad, can it?&quot;... nope, what a letdown of a show. 200 million dollars for... that?! Eurgh, it makes me really worried about how Loki season 2 will turn out...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I finished it earlier this week and ugh. I didn't think it was too bad at first, but that last episode was not good, especially the ending. They just made some baffling choices with that series..<br /> <br /> I'm still excited for Loki though, and I'm looking forward to The Marvels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519653#post1519653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate how I feel like I've wasted five years of my life and all I have to show for it was a severe mental breakdown right before things began going to shit with the pandemic in 2020 and the lockdowns exacerbating it.<br /> <br /> I've since recovered from all that trauma, I take medication that's helped me a lot and I have gotten married to a loving and caring husband, and I'm a lot better off now emotionally than I was two years ago or even one year ago but I still feel haunted by those bad memories all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Sorry you're dealing with that, but I totally know how you feel. I sometimes think back on bad stuff too, and I hate that I do it. But, I'm glad you've at least got some good things to help distract from the bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519792#post1519792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's superhero fatique at the point Knightingale. Sooner or later a genre will get overplayed and people get jaded and bored and will want to move onto new things. I remember reading an article quite a number of years ago around the time of Captain America Winter Solider about how the genre could at some point peter out like the western films that my parents watched when they were much younger and starting out.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be a little fatigue, but I wonder if the quality has dipped a little too. I don't think it's helped that this current phase of movies and tv shows hasn't seem to led anywhere. But, I'd honestly be happy if they took a little time off, or released a few less things in a year. It's just too much sometimes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T17:31:32-07:00","id":1519809,"title":"","content":"Half the time I play Magic: the Gathering, I hate the experience. But I don't know any other social opportunities and have major sunk cost fallacy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T05:12:56-07:00","id":1519848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519792#post1519792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's superhero fatique at the point Knightingale. Sooner or later a genre will get overplayed and people get jaded and bored and will want to move onto new things. I remember reading an article quite a number of years ago around the time of Captain America Winter Solider about how the genre could at some point peter out like the western films that my parents watched when they were much younger and starting out.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that, it's more about the quality. But I don't go to the cinema anymore (unless friends want to go) in order to watch any of the superhero-movies. I guess that's a form of superhero-fatigue. It's the same with Star Wars. But then you got series like Andor (which was great) and I realize that it isn't just fatigue that is the cause for my growing disinterest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519805#post1519805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea, I finished it earlier this week and ugh. I didn't think it was too bad at first, but that last episode was not good, especially the ending. They just made some baffling choices with that series..<br /> <br /> I'm still excited for Loki though, and I'm looking forward to The Marvels.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> There's so much wasted potential in this show... I wonder if anything from this series will even play a role in The Marvels... or if we ever gonna see G'iah, Emilia Clarke's character, again. And considering what happened in the last episode maybe it's better if it's never gonna get addressed again (like the ending of Eternals).<br /> <br /> BTW a friend of mine showed me an <a href=\"https://tvline.com/news/cobie-smulders-secret-invasion-marvel-series-preview-maria-hill-1234880816/\" target=\"_blank\">interview</a> from over a year ago with Colbie Smulder (who plays Maria Hill) which is just funny now that the series has come out:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assaying how the small-screen series serves Maria Hill herself, Smulders would not say it necessarily gives us more of the character than we\u2019ve seen before in The Avengers, Endgame or Spider-Man: No Way Home. But \u201cit\u2019s the most <i>depth </i>I\u2019ve been able to show of Maria Hill,\u201d she asserted. \u201cThat\u2019s the beauty of these series that Marvel is doing, you\u2019re able to really get backstory of these characters. What are the conversations that happen when they\u2019re just sitting around drinking coffee? It\u2019s not like, \u2018We\u2019ve gotta get the bad guys! We\u2019ve gotta get the thing! We\u2019ve gotta save the world again!\u2019 It\u2019s like, \u2018Let\u2019s just have a chat, let\u2019s go for a walk.\u2019 We get to see those kinds of moments and be a bit more intimate with the characters.\u201d </div> </div> </div>Spoiler for anybody who hasn't seen the show: Her character dies in the first episode. But the MCU really has never made good use of Colbie Smulders over the years, I think... so in that regard who even cares if she died. A bit of a pity that the MCU hasn't done anything more interesting with Maria Hill as a character (and because Colbie Smulders is also a good actor).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T05:58:00-07:00","id":1519854,"title":"","content":"I have been able to both enjoy and figure out the message of every MCU product until Secret Invasion. This one I just can't figure out what anyone involved was trying to accomplish, and it frustrates me. My best guess is it's a reaction to questions and criticisms certain continuity-obsessed fans have of the thing, which I hope I'm wrong about because no one should ever make a story for those people; it always results in stilted, disappointing content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T07:39:02-07:00","id":1519860,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna go ahead and say it. I don't like the MCU. I never liked it to begin with. I even thought the 2012 Avengers movie sucked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T07:43:31-07:00","id":1519861,"title":"","content":"Last one I saw was Endgame. Thought it was fine, but that was my fatigue point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T10:00:51-07:00","id":1519877,"title":"","content":"I was more of DC fan growing up but I have to admit outside of Batman and Superman live action movies. Warner Brothers doesn't have a great track record in that regard and had better success in the animated series and movies and for awhile Marvel was doing quite well as much as pains me to admit that and I greatly enjoyed the first two Captain America films.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T10:05:08-07:00","id":1519879,"title":"","content":"I stopped going to theatres myself Knightingale as it was getting to expensive and I knew I was getting old when I found it to loud to enjoy the movies like I used and wait for it to come out on DVD/Blu Ray or on demand where I can enjoy it at more comfortable level.<br /> <br /> I'm aware of the quality drop off, but I always attributed to having so many movies being made by such and such a date that it would effect how well it would be put together and I also heard and read the special effects departments at both Disney and WB are understaffed and can't keep up with the work levels and as such we see poor CGI effects and etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T16:30:54-07:00","id":1519991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519848#post1519848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that, it's more about the quality. But I don't go to the cinema anymore (unless friends want to go) in order to watch any of the superhero-movies. I guess that's a form of superhero-fatigue. It's the same with Star Wars. But then you got series like Andor (which was great) and I realize that it isn't just fatigue that is the cause for my growing disinterest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to go out to the movies almost every weekend pre-pandemic, but now, I hardly ever go. I just finally realized the theater experience sucks, and it's just way easier for me to watch things at home where I don't have to deal with people.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519848#post1519848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's so much wasted potential in this show... I wonder if anything from this series will even play a role in The Marvels... or if we ever gonna see G'iah, Emilia Clarke's character, again. And considering what happened in the last episode maybe it's better if it's never gonna get addressed again (like the ending of Eternals).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to say if anything from this show will make any kind of impact. Fury ended up right back where he started, so I won't be shocked if none of this is mentioned in The Marvels.<br /> <br /> be nice if G'iah pops up at some point, but I won't be shocked if she doesn't..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519848#post1519848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW a friend of mine showed me an <a href=\"https://tvline.com/news/cobie-smulders-secret-invasion-marvel-series-preview-maria-hill-1234880816/\" target=\"_blank\">interview</a> from over a year ago with Colbie Smulder (who plays Maria Hill) which is just funny now that the series has come out:<br /> <br /> <br /> Spoiler for anybody who hasn't seen the show: Her character dies in the first episode. But the MCU really has never made good use of Colbie Smulders over the years, I think... so in that regard who even cares if she died. A bit of a pity that the MCU hasn't done anything more interesting with Maria Hill as a character (and because Colbie Smulders is also a good actor).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I hated they killed her off, but that interview is funny considering what happened...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519854#post1519854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been able to both enjoy and figure out the message of every MCU product until Secret Invasion. This one I just can't figure out what anyone involved was trying to accomplish, and it frustrates me. My best guess is it's a reaction to questions and criticisms certain continuity-obsessed fans have of the thing, which I hope I'm wrong about because no one should ever make a story for those people; it always results in stilted, disappointing content.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you! I have no idea what the overall message of the show was supposed to be. Honestly, not very much happened during the series. You'd think they would have at least setup the Skrull invasion a bit better, or shown some backstory about it, but nope... it's just so baffling.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T16:33:03-07:00","id":1519992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519879#post1519879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stopped going to theatres myself Knightingale as it was getting to expensive and I knew I was getting old when I found it to loud to enjoy the movies like I used and wait for it to come out on DVD/Blu Ray or on demand where I can enjoy it at more comfortable level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad I'm not alone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1519879#post1519879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of the quality drop off, but I always attributed to having so many movies being made by such and such a date that it would effect how well it would be put together and I also heard and read the special effects departments at both Disney and WB are understaffed and can't keep up with the work levels and as such we see poor CGI effects and etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yea, they're trying to pump out so much stuff the poor animators can't keep up with everything. I wish they'd scale it back it and give people a little room to breathe..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T16:34:00-07:00","id":1520162,"title":"","content":"I agree that the VFX departments in Hollywood are really overworked and not given enough time to get the job done properly Mr. Gone. Sounds like even the mainstream media is being somewhat supportive of the crew judging by some news articles I've read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T04:16:55-07:00","id":1520183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1520162#post1520162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the VFX departments in Hollywood are really overworked and not given enough time to get the job done properly Mr. Gone. Sounds like even the mainstream media is being somewhat supportive of the crew judging by some news articles I've read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it sounds like people are coming around on how much work VFX departments actually do! Almost every movie now uses way more VFX than people realize. I hear once VFX house is trying to unionize, and I hope that works out for em!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T07:38:14-07:00","id":1520196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1520183#post1520183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea, it sounds like people are coming around on how much work VFX departments actually do! Almost every movie now uses way more VFX than people realize. I hear once VFX house is trying to unionize, and I hope that works out for em!</div> </div> </div> </div>The behind-the-scenes stories of how the VFX-studios are treated are always horrifying. It's always some story about the director who's changing his mind every two weeks about what the VFX-people are supposed to animate and is treating the whole process like you're ordering from Mcdonald's or something. And the result is of course shoddy work like in the recent Flash movie where I genuinely felt like I was looking at PS3-era graphics at times.<br /> <br /> The good news is that people in that sector are starting <a href=\"https://fortune.com/2023/08/08/marvel-studios-visual-effects-workers-union-disney-bob-iger/\" target=\"_blank\">to unionize</a>. But I can also easily imagine Disney immediately making the decision that because of that all VFX-work is going to be done by studios in South-Korea from then on (that's also where anime-studios go when they want to outsource stuff and are looking for cheap animation-work).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T09:14:11-07:00","id":1520210,"title":"","content":"I mostly watch films from overseas now anyways as I don't find much from Hollywood that appeals to me anymore Knightingale. We the customers have the power and not the big studios in regards in that matter and if they want to insult me and call me whatever ism for not liking what they pump out, then I will take my business elsewhere and get my enjoyment from other venues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T11:56:25-07:00","id":1520226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1520196#post1520196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The behind-the-scenes stories of how the VFX-studios are treated are always horrifying. It's always some story about the director who's changing his mind every two weeks about what the VFX-people are supposed to animate and is treating the whole process like you're ordering from Mcdonald's or something. And the result is of course shoddy work like in the recent Flash movie where I genuinely felt like I was looking at PS3-era graphics at times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I hear ya! I feel so bad for anyone working in the field right now. They studios are making so many movies right now, and those people are extremely overworked. It's crazy...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1520196#post1520196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The good news is that people in that sector are starting <a href=\"https://fortune.com/2023/08/08/marvel-studios-visual-effects-workers-union-disney-bob-iger/\" target=\"_blank\">to unionize</a>. But I can also easily imagine Disney immediately making the decision that because of that all VFX-work is going to be done by studios in South-Korea from then on (that's also where anime-studios go when they want to outsource stuff and are looking for cheap animation-work).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad they're starting to unionize, but yea, I am afraid Disney (and other big studios) will try to outsource all that work. Might work for em in the short term, but for the long term that going to be such a bad move..<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T14:03:41-07:00","id":1520234,"title":"","content":"To go from the realistic CGI of the late Peter Cushing from Rogue One to what we see now is a huge drop off in terms of quality of Flash and other effects heavy movies Mr. Knightingale.<br /> <br /> Let's not even get into the ethical debate of using the likeness of dead actors &amp; actresses in future films with the use of A.I. that is happening and that was the unsettling thing about seeing Cushing looking lifelike in Rogue One then checking one's self and remember it's not really him on the screen and it's stand in with the late actor image mapped onto him &amp; using voice recordings to better sell the illusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-09-2023, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T20:21:46-07:00","id":1520258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1520234#post1520234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To go from the realistic CGI of the late Peter Cushing from Rogue One to what we see now is a huge drop off in terms of quality of Flash and other effects heavy movies Mr. Knightingale.<br /> <br /> Let's not even get into the ethical debate of using the likeness of dead actors &amp; actresses in future films with the use of A.I. that is happening and that was the unsettling thing about seeing Cushing looking lifelike in Rogue One then checking one's self and remember it's not really him on the screen and it's stand in with the late actor image mapped onto him &amp; using voice recordings to better sell the illusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>doesn't that happen because movies are rushed?<br /> i heard that if movies had the proper time to make the proper CGI,the CGI would be better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T01:23:00-07:00","id":1520269,"title":"","content":"I saw somebody on YT mentioning this... There is a reason for why Secret Invasion turned out the way it did: It had <a href=\"https://thedirect.com/article/mcu-secret-invasion-reshoots-disney-rumor\" target=\"_blank\">extensive reshoots</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why Are Secret Invasion's Reshoots So Long?<br /> <br /> A reshoot timeline of <b>four months</b> for any production is not ideal. <b>This length of time is usually what one of Marvel's Disney+ series would use to film their entire show</b>, which could sound alarming to some. However, there could be an explanation for this unfathomably long filming schedule.\u200b </div> </div> </div>And apparently, the reason is that the original story of Secret Invasion was too similar to the Ukraine-invasion. Funny thing is that this happened once before! With Captain America and the Winter Soldier they did <a href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/paultassi/2021/04/24/why-was-falcons-flag-smashers-storyline-so-weird-blame-a-possibly-cut-pandemic-plotline/\" target=\"_blank\">extensive reshoots as well</a> because the original Flag Smasher storyline focused on them as terrorists spreading a plague and this was during the Covid-pandemic, though.<br /> <br /> How were they able to stumble into this issue twice now...?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T08:41:36-07:00","id":1520300,"title":"","content":"Don't you me Falcon and Winter Soldier for the flag-smasher thing? And if it's an explanation of why you need; Hollywood has never really been that creative, and aren't they in yet another writer's strike right now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T09:40:57-07:00","id":1520304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1520300#post1520300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you me Falcon and Winter Soldier for the flag-smasher thing? And if it's an explanation of why you need; Hollywood has never really been that creative, and aren't they in yet another writer's strike right now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, sorry. I meant Falcon and the Winter Soldier, of course.<br /> <br /> Yes, right now both the WGA (writers) and SAG-AFTRA (actors) are on strike. But I wouldn't call it &quot;yet another&quot;. The last time this happened was in 1960.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T09:48:23-07:00","id":1520305,"title":"","content":"To be fair reshoots always seemed to be a fact of life for Hollywood movies as they have test audiences that they will screen for and find out what was right with the film and what could be fixed before it's final aired version. Now it seems just worse because it seems the era of modest budget movies are a thing of the past and now it's big blockbusters and the more expensive the film is the more money they have to make to break even or a profit. With already bloated budgets it makes it worse when reshoots have to be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T09:52:30-07:00","id":1520306,"title":"","content":"Still a four month timeline of reshoots is not something you want to be involved in any level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T09:56:28-07:00","id":1520307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1520258#post1520258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> doesn't that happen because movies are rushed?<br /> i heard that if movies had the proper time to make the proper CGI,the CGI would be better</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned that issue on the previous page on how the VFX departments of Disney &amp; Warner Bros are overworked and understaffed and can't keep up with the demand and how many youtube channels and even mainstream media is commenting on it and being supportive of them and talks of the departments being unionized Nicolas Milioni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T09:57:34-07:00","id":1520308,"title":"","content":"Yeah, reshoots are normal but what isn't normal is to do so many reshoots that you end up shooting a series twice. When your shooting-time has gone from 4 months to 8 in total, it's no wonder the series ends up costing more than 200 million dollars.<br /> <br /> And the series clearly suffered for it. The writing, direction and photography... it all suffered for being rushed through those re-shoots. Falcon and the Winter Soldier also had a really tepid finale where everything was resolved with some cringey speech. But overall, I liked that show still way more than Secret Invasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T10:02:50-07:00","id":1520310,"title":"","content":"That is awful news about having to shoot a series twice and costing the studio $200 million dollars and don't they have to make at least 3 times there budget just to break even now? Heavy Arms could give a better break down on how much a given movie needs to make based on there budgets and what not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-10-2023, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T16:53:24-07:00","id":1520338,"title":"","content":"I'm not concerned about Disney breaking even. They're effectively a sovereign entity at this point, they're so rich. I'm just bummed they wasted a lot of very good actors' (and other, less visible contributors') time and reputation on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T09:31:40-07:00","id":1520394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1520338#post1520338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not concerned about Disney breaking even. They're effectively a sovereign entity at this point, they're so rich. I'm just bummed they wasted a lot of very good actors' (and other, less visible contributors') time and reputation on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>For now, but they are losing money and are having to lay off staff and probably more will come down the line as the losses mount up. Even there theme parks according to many media outlets are seeing a drop off in attendance because nobody can really afford to go there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T09:53:29-07:00","id":1520822,"title":"","content":"Something I\u2019ve grown increasingly tired of is how all this ultra-modern electronic networking fails to be secure in any way and yet expects us to trust it. Every year for like the last 10 years I\u2019ve either read an article about a massive data breach or received a warning in the mail about one that may affect me. How is any of this supposed to inspire confidence in any of us to trust all this electronic insanity? I can\u2019t even remember the last time I even heard of an attempted bank robbery, but I know there\u2019s been a new data breach in a \u201csecured\u201d sensitive database every single year for the last 10 years. Clearly nothing is being done or nothing CAN be done, yet I\u2019ll bet if we all collectively pulled our money out of the network I'll bet several people in over-privileged cloisters would panic.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T10:45:57-07:00","id":1520824,"title":"","content":"Nothing is being done because the modern economy is too tied to those networks for enough people to just pull the plug and force change that way. Bad security just creates whole new industries to extract money from consumers for extra security packages, ID theft recovery services, and so on.<br /> <br /> Of course, none of this has ever really been that secure. Hacking is older than the Internet is. It's just been secure enough that we kept putting more and more important stuff in the networks without building significantly better ways to having security get ahead of cracking for once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T15:20:12-07:00","id":1520836,"title":"","content":"To be fair Darksolaeternium is that nothing is ever secure and criminal minded people will find ways around whatever security you put up and all you can truly do is lower your risks by following the basic quote. &quot;If it's to good to be true for you to hear. It's is and be wary.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T23:15:59-07:00","id":1521164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1520822#post1520822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I\u2019ve grown increasingly tired of is how all this ultra-modern electronic networking fails to be secure in any way and yet expects us to trust it. Every year for like the last 10 years I\u2019ve either read an article about a massive data breach or received a warning in the mail about one that may affect me. How is any of this supposed to inspire confidence in any of us to trust all this electronic insanity? I can\u2019t even remember the last time I even heard of an attempted bank robbery, but I know there\u2019s been a new data breach in a \u201csecured\u201d sensitive database every single year for the last 10 years. Clearly nothing is being done or nothing CAN be done, yet I\u2019ll bet if we all collectively pulled our money out of the network I'll bet several people in over-privileged cloisters would panic.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The reality is, modern day tech security is generally pretty good. The problem is that the people using it are very often incredibly stupid. Nearly every major data breach or hacking breaching in the last 10 years, where they've provided an account of what happened, has involved some individual being tricked into downloading a worm or a virus or something they weren't supposed to. It'd be like if the person at the bank was tricked into handing out the keys to the vault. That generally doesn't happen because people typically treat physical security at a higher level than technological data security. People who'd think twice before handing the vault keys over to a stranger claiming to be their boss don't hesitate to download something in an email from someone claiming to be their boss. <br /> <br /> At the same time, a bank vault probably only has one or two sets of keys. Now how many employees in a company have a company email account? If every bank employee had keys to the vault, you'd probably see more bank robberies and cash going to missing from banks because people would be losing those keys or get them stolen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T02:40:56-07:00","id":1521170,"title":"","content":"I think that analogy really sells short the disparity between physical and digital security.<br /> <br /> Social engineering,which is a decade old practice, doesn't work on getting a physical key to a physical lock, because that's too obvious a security threat. Social engineering works because digital security needs to interface with humans, and humans are not equipped for it. If we use passwords that are easy to remember, they're easier to break, if we use high security passwords we need some way to track them because we can't remember a randomize set of 16+ characters for every login. Which means there's a notebook, or a digital password vault, or something that can unravel the best security on the programming side of things. You can't phish for a physical key, but phishing attacks work great for getting digital keys, because it's a lot easier to make an email that looks legit than it is to sound legit in person.<br /> <br /> Digital security also gets really hard to explain, really fast. We have older generations that didn't grow up with it and just can't contextualize how to prioritize different digital security factors. We also have a younger generation that's so online and so used to their lives being automated, than they don't need to understand how any of it actually works inside the fancy boxes that we poke to do cool things.<br /> <br /> It's like how more and more people just don't know how to do all but the most basic car repairs and maintenance. There is a cultural factor, but there's also the fact that cars have gotten more and more complex making it ever more difficult for DIY folks to fix what used to be simple things without exceedingly expensive equipment that gets to the point where you might as well just ay someone else to do it. A lot of the reasons why are good! Better safety systems, better fuel economy, etc. are all things we want, but part of the cost in jamming all this stuff into a car is making the car too complex for most people to want to learn how to fix unless they plan to do so for a living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T11:28:31-07:00","id":1521207,"title":"","content":"I've been looking at old photos of my birth mom lately and honestly, I'm crying a bit right now as I type this. She was by all accounts a wonderful woman, beautiful in both looks and personality, and a very intelligent person too from what my Dad has told me. <br /> <br /> Sadly, I never got to know her before she was killed in a car accident when I was less than two years old. I spent years as the only child of a single father. My Dad's a great guy and did his best for me (hell, he still does to this day) along with my grandparents and uncle and I do love my stepmom and stepbrother too and they love me as well. But I do wish I could've known my Mom.<br /> <br /> There's a picture of her holding me when I was a newborn baby and I always break down and cry whenever I see it. <br /> <br /> I'm gonna be heading back to the East Coast to visit Dad next week and I also want to visit Mom's grave too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T14:23:34-07:00","id":1521223,"title":"","content":"My best friend got hurt in a car accident by a reckless driver who couldn't see that there was two cars at a stop sign waiting for it to be okay to continue and got whiplash, dizziness and headaches from a reckless lady driving at least 50-60 kmph yesterday. Some people shouldn't be allowed to behind a vehicle if they can't follow basic safety rules on the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T09:23:40-07:00","id":1521386,"title":"","content":"Tired of people who want to cancel songs, movies and books because it offends their 21st century beliefs and not wanting to acknowledge that these works were considered products of there time and should be viewed as such and not hidden away in some dark corner. You will never truly grow or learn from your mistakes if you don't acknowledge them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T14:49:50-07:00","id":1521404,"title":"","content":"That feels like both a mischaracterization of what a lot of people want, and a false dichotomy.<br /> <br /> The real end result the vast majority of people want is for extremely problematic historical art to be part of a well constructed educational system. It should be preserved, and taught, not locked in some vault, but it should also generally be a guided experience.<br /> <br /> You can't learn from mistakes if you're only exposed to mistakes by people telling you that they're good things actually. It's hard to learn the right lessons from mistakes by just exposing yourself to things (ask any therapists that works in exposure therapy about the laundry list of horror stories of people that thought they could do that on their own and just made things far worse). While there's an entirely separate rant to be had about how much teachers have been devalued in Western society (even in plenty of countries with far better performing education systems than the US has), well before and well beyond any valid criticism about better pedagogy techniques for a digital age, the whole point of having a teacher instead of just a text book is that we learn more full lessons with a human that knows the subject guiding us.<br /> <br /> I don't think, and I don't put much stock in the few attempts to make an argument for, the 1915 The Birth of a Nation film to just be out in the wild actually teaches anyone any lessons. I don't think anyone actually learns any good lessons from watching a racist propaganda film just for the sake of watching it. Sure, some people have the preexisting educational background to know enough context around the film to appreciate it for what it is, but most of them probably got exposed to on the way there anyway. The idea that it should be something you learn about in school, or at an educational institution like a museum, really shouldn't be that troubling a concept.<br /> <br /> If we want to remember our history, especially the bad stuff, for future lessons, I'd also point out that generally speaking historical artifacts are far safer in the hands of professional archivists, rather than in the hands of the highest bidder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T19:01:51-07:00","id":1521413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1521404#post1521404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That feels like [] a mischaracterization of what a lot of people want</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it is.<br /> <br /> Yes, reasonable people keep perspective. But a lot of people aren't reasonable. A lot of people--probably just a vocal minority,and probably mostly on the internet where outrage is cultivated for profit, but still--seem to only want to signal that they're on the right side of history by viciously attacking enemies they perceive for reasons they don't understand with no thought to how it impacts the marginalized communities in question. I've seen it so many times it's hard for me to not be suspicious that any given &quot;ally&quot; might not care about me or my well-being at all rather than the endorphin rush of declaring oneself righteous.<br /> <br /> That said, I do not think it is inherently bad to cancel harmful art (though for the record, I don't know which art we're talking about or what &quot;canceled&quot; means in this context), or that &quot;it's a product of its time&quot; is a valid excuse. Like, as an example, apparently Mark Twain didn't know to not call people the N-word, but it makes no sense to extrapolate out from there that no one of his era knew it either. I'm pretty sure the people being called the N-word knew it wasn't okay, so to claim that the time didn't know any better is to argue that black people don't count as participants in the culture they were being described as: it's a form of cultural imperialism aimed at history. As you say, there are a lot of legitimate criticisms. I just tend to be skeptical that people who make those criticisms are being sincere rather than shallow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T20:49:43-07:00","id":1521416,"title":"","content":"The thing is... people that are just in it to be provocative on the Internet inherently don't care about the actual solutions, or they wouldn't just be spouting off on social media. The US has seen a massive rise in the call to remove certain books from schools (including school libraries), but all those requests are public records. When people went and looked, it was a tiny group of people (like a few hundred across the whole country) spamming the system; not the thousands of people yelling about it online.<br /> <br /> So it's still a mischaracterization of the less reasonable people to say it's anything about their modern sensibilities being offended, when what they want is social clout with their Internet Tribe and saying &quot;cancel this&quot; and never acting on is what they're doing.<br /> <br /> Of course &quot;cancelled&quot; is yet another victim of the Internet massively speeding up appropriating language to make tribalism worse. &quot;Cancel&quot; was originally used to mean... cancel. Like cancelling your subscription to a magazine, a newspaper, or your cable company; just applied to social media where you unfollow/block/mute/ignore/whatever. It was a a declaration of personal choice. &quot;I'm not paying attention to So and So on these apps.&quot; Sure, making a deal about it wasn't just a matter of personal tastes. You were cancelling something for a reason, and you felt like it was a good reason, and you wanted to bring attention to that reason. George Bush Sr. publicly canceled his NRA membership after the NRA attacked him for a gun safety bill he signed as President during the NRA's transition towards being much more vocal absolutists about no gun-laws instead of being an organization that for a long time (aka what Bush Sr. grew up with) that helped promote positive gun ownership, taught gun safety classes, and generally backed what we'd now call &quot;common sense&quot; laws as a non-partisan issue. He wanted to warn people about how they were losing sight of their founding mission, and he had the platform to do it.<br /> <br /> Social media of course, gave us all platforms. So that didn't help with these sorts of things. And &quot;cancel&quot; became a warning, &quot;A lot of people are going to cancel you if you don't delete that fast&quot; which is still fine. People say dumb shit, and losing a bunch of friends/followers/etc. because you broadcast your dumb idea to the whole world is something a real world friend should tell you that you just did and you're going to want to undo as much as you can.<br /> <br /> The problem starts (and this is history repeating itself) when the word because a scary external threat instead of what's just basic human behavior adapting to a new form of interaction. You get people conflating been banned for violating a services ToS with being the victim of &quot;cancel culture&quot; because you got banned because the scary threat of people that disagree without.. not because you posted something bannable even though you totally did. Coopting language and using it to deflect is a very old part of human discourse.<br /> <br /> That said, I completely agree with not really buying into the &quot;product of the time&quot; thing. It an important part of literary analysis for sure, but to go with your example, people know what they're doing. If you live in a time when a white man calling another white man that word could be seen as such an act of provocation that shooting the man slinging it around would be justifiable homicide under extreme provocation, you know calling people that word is wrong. People in the past were just as capable as us of coming up with mental gymnastics to justify why doing the wrong thing in a given context was actually OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T07:52:47-07:00","id":1521427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1521386#post1521386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tired of people who want to cancel songs, movies and books because it offends their 21st century beliefs and not wanting to acknowledge that these works were considered products of there time and should be viewed as such and not hidden away in some dark corner. You will never truly grow or learn from your mistakes if you don't acknowledge them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen to that.<br /> <br /> I used to be part of the &quot;Condemn and criticize any media from the past that's even remotely problematic&quot; crowd for years until the misery and fatigue I suffered from combined with the massive amounts of gaslighting and utter abuse I suffered from those within the far-leftist circles I was part of eventually drove me to have a breakdown.<br /> <br /> Now I pretty much enjoy problematic media completely unconditionally and I'm a lot happier now than I was two years ago. Moralizers who constantly go on about &quot;injustice and bigotry&quot; now give me a knee-jerk reaction where it just makes me want to enjoy problematic media unconditionally even more just to spite them.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's knee-jerk and petty of me, but I honestly am sick of the puritanism and bullying that goes on in those circles. Far too often, I find that those kinds of moralizers are often too similar to the same people who mistreated me for years and gaslighted me about it the entire time.<br /> <br /> My capacity to care about social injustices and the intersectionality of it all is fully exhausted despite the fact I'm marginalized myself. I just can't go back to that any more.<br /> <br /> There was too much gaslighting, too much emotional abuse and bullying, too much psychological mistreatment, too much moral brigading, too many purity spirals and struggle sessions, and too much sexual mistreatment too.<br /> <br /> Plus there's a lot of creepy fetishization of marginalized people in those sorts of circles and I'm not even sure if most of these people are even aware of it.<br /> <br /> Not fetishization in the sexual way, mind you. It's more of a &quot;cargo cult&quot; sort of deal. Like the fact I'm Black and &quot;queer&quot; (tbh, I hate that term and I still personally see it as a homophobic slur) somehow imbues me with some sort of spiritual quality that less marginalized people somehow lack. It's creepy. \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Now I have developed the personal mindset of &quot;If everything is political, then NOTHING is!&quot;<br /> <br /> IMHO, I genuinely and unironically believe that hedonism, nihilism, escapism, apathy, and general amorality are a far preferable alternative for me. Again, this is just what works for me and my own personal lived experiences and life circumstances. Your Mileage May Vary, as always. Don't take my word for it alone.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm a nihilist. But it's not what you think.<br /> <br /> Far too many have this idea of nihilists being these brooding edgelord punks who all go on about &quot;Woe is me! Nothing really matters at all!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Those kinds of strawman nihilists can go fuck off and cry themselves to sleep while they listen to Ministry or some shit. Fuck them.<br /> <br /> When I'm more of the mindset of &quot;Hey...nothing matters at all! I'm free to party hard and live life to the fullest! I'm my own man because it don't matter. None of this matters! Celebrate good times, come on!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Qu6Dyn-c6M\" data-code=\"1Qu6Dyn-c6M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1Qu6Dyn-c6M/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 08-26-2023, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d