as I don't want trouble with the mods).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T04:18:31-07:00","id":1522395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1522304#post1522304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm totally not shocked at all by the news that Rotten Tomatoes is or was paying movie critics to praise their movies even when they knew that they were so bad and shouldn't see the light of day. Which begs the question is whom still listens to film critics anyway as I like to think that we are smart enough to know what movies we will like or not like and found 9 times out 10 that the movies they dislike, I find enjoyable in spite of it flaws or the ones they like I find slow and boring.<br /> <br /> Still it's fun to see peoples reactions when they learn about paid shills. ( I didn't want to use the actual description of what there called as I don't want trouble with the mods).</div> </div> </div> </div>I should be shocked by that, but I'm not...<br /> <br /> Though I never use Rotten Tomatoes and rarely listen to any critics. I just look at a trailer or a little info and if something looks interesting to me I'll see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T10:28:20-07:00","id":1522410,"title":"","content":"What I find particularly funny about the <a href=\"https://www.vulture.com/article/rotten-tomatoes-movie-rating.html\" target=\"_blank\">Rotten Tomatoes story</a> is how it's focused on the movie Ophelia (2018). This PR-firm called Bunker 15 that paid for the good reviews couldn't have been more inconsequential in the end. That movie is utterly forgettable and that article is probably the most PR this film has ever gotten. Sure, the paid reviews switched the score from &quot;rotten&quot; to &quot;fresh&quot; but here's the thing: 1. It only improved the score to land at 63% which is paltry as an indicator of critical approval. 2. This movie had a budget of 12 million dollars and made 228 thousand dollars at the box office (and that's internationally!). So this PR-firm paid reviewers to barely get this movie into fresh-Territory on Rotten Tomatoes. And in the end, the film was still a flop at the box-office. If anything, hiring that PR-firm was a waste of money.<br /> <br /> But there are troubling practices that I think are bigger problems like when Disney/Marvel are having these early screenings of Marvel-movies and handpick critics who are likely to give positive reviews. It's always the same: These handpicked &quot;critics&quot; go to an early screening of a Marvel-movie (before the public official release) and then they go on social media to give the most exuberant takes on the new Marvel-movie. The system works less well these days because of the amount of people who have just soured on Marvel-movies in general but this practice is a bigger problem in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T10:59:58-07:00","id":1522412,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that's why &quot;influencers&quot; have managed to become a thing that's just recreating independent critics again (though with nothing that's going to stop it from getting overly corporate all over again).<br /> <br /> While I'm not trying to be overly nostalgic, something I definitely miss from my younger year were local stores, owned by local business owners, that lived and died on their local reputations. My first real FLGS's owner 100% took the time and energy to know what he was selling, and what his regular customers wanted. My family could go in, and he'd already have a personalized pick for each of us from his most recent arrivals behind the counter. It was never just pushing the big new arrivals, because he knew our different tastes. His success rate was pretty much perfect, which of course means customers kept coming back because once you were a regular, you'd have something you'd never heard of waiting, hand-selected, for you that was definitely something you would enjoy. Algorithms on websites can try to replicate that, and they do OK, but the personal touch matters (both in real success rate,and psychological impact). We had a local independent video rental place that survived about five years longer than the chains like Blockbuster for the same reason: personal connections work better. If one of them suggested something a bit unusual that didn't sound my speed, I trusted they saw something in it that I would like, so I'd give it a shot.<br /> <br /> Social media infuencers are the closest we get to that sort of interaction in the current marketplace. They can't be as personal with the people in their comment sections or streamer chats, but they know they know what keeps people coming back is establishing that kind of trust. If their reviews/etc. are seen as bought and paid for by companies, viewers will go elsewhere (we can get that from websites that do more traditional reviews, or aggregators like RT and Metacritic, and get lots of paid reviews). They also need to cater to an audience to stand out. They need to establish a public perception of what their tastes are, that attracts viewers that feel that aligns with their own, and then that needs to be backed up with reviews/recommendations that feedback positively between influencer and viewer. And they're more likely to do things like differentiate between, &quot;the hype is real, day one this,&quot; and, &quot;this is good, but it'll be good if you wait for a Steam sale with a few patches under its belt too.&quot; Something that a lot of consumers care a bit more about than I think big business really recognizes.<br /> <br /> To me, the troubling practices are that the big entertainment conglomerates are already invading those spaces, because they can't stand a lack of control over their PR.. even though eventually public sentiment is going to happen regardless of spin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T11:39:35-07:00","id":1522415,"title":"","content":"I think the thing to do with critics is find voices that are either appealing in terms of style, insight and knowledge and/or seem to echo your own tastes in entertainment. The &quot;and/or&quot; is more about how art should challenge one at times and finding trustworthy voices that can guide one in experiencing that sort of art is worthwhile. You don't have to agree with the critic but the least a <i>good </i>critic can do is point you to stuff that's genuinely interesting.<br /> <br /> As a pure customer-experience-guide finding the critics who echo your own tastes is good because that person is sitting through a ton of shit to tell you what's good and what's not. And since that person's tastes echo your own, you can use the critic to watch the movies that said critic liked instead of having to deal with all the other stuff that's out there in terms of entertainment. That's why the &quot;influencer&quot;-style of having a more personal relationship with their audience is a good addition to being a critic, I think. It emphasizes that a critic at the end of the day (ideally) gives you an informed take on a media-product but acknowledges the subjective nature of their endeavor. With a good review, even if you disagree with it, you still understand where the reviewer is coming from and the reviewer gives insight into what the media-product is trying to do.<br /> <br /> Aggregator-sites like Rotten Tomatoes and Metacritic undermine the process in a way. Now it's all about the &quot;score&quot;/&quot;fresh/rotten&quot;-status. Something subjective and very personal has been turned into a &quot;number&quot; so-to-speak. At the same time, looking at a number on those sites is way more convenient than reading a whole review of course. And it isn't the old model of having particular critics (like Roger Ebert/Gene Siskel's show, for example) be the &quot;authority&quot; on what is good or bad was perfect either. But these sites like Rotten Tomatoes are clearly what spawned these ideas of &quot;gaming the system&quot;. It's just a number now after all. The same way you'd rig an election, just do it with a crowd of critics instead.<br /> <br /> But the interesting thing is how the Marvel-movie-franchise shows the limits of using PR (and less savory methods of influencing opinions). At some point, the state of things just becomes undeniable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T12:54:45-07:00","id":1522419,"title":"","content":"Double post from flag","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-12-2023, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T14:16:10-07:00","id":1522425,"title":"","content":"That personal touch does help when it comes to growing your business and a much smaller operation Heavy Arms. Like you when I was much younger and going to school and loved reading the Transformers &amp; Iron Man comics/ There was a local store owner who would keep an issue saved for. Now at Sun Rise Records the manager knows what type of music &amp; films I enjoy and will tell me to check out some upcoming merchandise that would be coming in and I mentioned on the Gush post about that from time to time that there is an owner of 2nd hand book store that sometimes doesn't charge me for any books I might pick up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T14:22:31-07:00","id":1522427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1522395#post1522395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should be shocked by that, but I'm not...<br /> <br /> Though I never use Rotten Tomatoes and rarely listen to any critics. I just look at a trailer or a little info and if something looks interesting to me I'll see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know the only Social Media personality I even really listen at all for watching movies is Space Ice and he isn't a movie critic per say and is more of a over the top roaster of films that he brings every Friday be it Nicolas Cage, Van Dam, Stallone, Breen, Snipes, Seagal and others. <br /> <br /> His idea of Blade being about a pissed off Fire Marshal who is upset at the lack of safety standards that the vampires have at there nightclubs was funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T14:30:24-07:00","id":1522431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1521761#post1521761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A while back I offered to check over grammar and spelling for an artist I back on Patreon. English isn't their native language, and going over somewhat generic speech bubbles for 4-5 variants of the same base image every week or two wasn't that time consuming. <br /> It has somehow evolved into me writing up all the dialog for them, including on their several recent, more ambitious 10+ page doujinshi. They seem to have health issues, and so from the start offered to do some free illustrations for me in lieu of pay, but I haven't seen hide nor hair of that. At this point it feels like I'm paying them to give me writing assignments...</div> </div> </div> </div> After the fourth day in a row of waking up to &quot;Hey, are you awake? Can you make some dialog for me?&quot;, I finally talked to the artist. Said that regardless of what happens I'm happy to check their work and offer edits, but if I'm going to write whole-cloth scripts then to either;<br /> <br /> 1. Credit me in the post whenever they have me write the majority of the dialog<br /> or<br /> 2. Formalize it to actually give me an illustration every few months, rather than just talk about it and never following through<br /> or<br /> 3. I cancel my Patreon backing going forward, so I'm not paying them to give me writing assignments.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, they refunded me the last three months of Patreon before I gave them those three choices. I appreciate that, especially since I emphasized that none of this was retroactive. On the other, they still haven't decided which if any of those choices they want. Like, even just a straight 