k Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-14-2023, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T12:37:20-07:00","id":1522586,"title":"","content":"I've been wanting to vent about this one for a while and it's a long one and a doozy. It's very graphic and discusses a LOT of sensitive and NSFW topics and issues, so I'm putting it in spoilers just to be safe.<br /> <br /> <b>CW: </b>Very frank and graphic discussions of gender dysphoria, sex, medical procedures, human anatomy, and mental illness.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm gonna admit it, even though I'm trans, I'm probably never going to get gender-reassignment surgery. Or at least not any kind of bottom surgery such as phalloplasty. While it may be good for my other trans brothers out there and I'm going to be in favor of full access to all forms of gender-affirming care, I don't feel that bottom surgery would help me that much with my specific issues if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> The dysphoria is bad but I'm just not comfortable with surgery of any kind. If it's medically necessary like emergency surgeries, I will undergo the procedures but otherwise it terrifies me. As does the post-surgery care. Due to some personal traumas in my past, the idea of a blade going through my body in any way kind of upsets me on a certain level that's hard to describe.<br /> <br /> Instead I've found ways to deal with my dysphoria in other ways. I dress more masculine and act more masculine though I always did that even before my transition. I let my body hair and pubic hair grow out. I sometimes get a wispy fuzzy mustache but I do shave it as I don't like facial hair in general, either for me or my hubby. I use men's deodorants, colognes, soaps, and body washes. My preferred brand is Brut, though Old Spice is pretty good too.<br /> <br /> I try to boost my testosterone levels in natural ways, either through diet and exercise and through taking specific vitamins, minerals, and nutritional supplements. It seems to have some effect as my testosterone levels are slightly higher than other natal females my age according to my doctor. But I hope to actually go on T proper.<br /> <br /> With that said, I've got other issues that make my doctor hesitant to prescribe me testosterone and that is understandable. I'm bipolar, autistic, and have ADHD. I'm also overweight, though I have lost nine pounds in the past month and a half thanks to my diet changes, walking and exercising more often, and taking nutritional supplements such as Vitamin D3, B Vitamin Complex, Vitamin C, Zinc, Green Tea Extract, Krill Oil, and Magnesium. What's been working for me the most lately is just eating a full pack of Starkist Tuna for breakfast every morning. It's 70 calories, high protein, and keeps you full most of the day. Walking for at least one hour every day also helps too.<br /> <br /> In terms of the body dysphoria, my main issues are my chest and my crotch. The former is far more of an issue than the latter.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna be blunt and say it. I've got large breasts but I don't like it one bit and it comes with the territory of being fat but even before I put on a lot of weight in my twenties, it was an issue that bothered me though not as much as it was afterwards. They remind me of the fact I was born in the wrong body, they will hurt my back sometimes and as much as my hubby and the other people I've been with may like them, I don't like having them. I've kinda shrugged and tried to accept it as best I can, wearing chest binders whenever I go out and trying to lose more weight in the hopes it'll maybe make my breasts a little smaller. Tbh, even if I had small breasts, I'd still hate having them. Aesthetically, I admit I like breasts on women, be they cis or trans, but I don't like them on me specifically. I'm a man, even if I was assigned female at birth.<br /> <br /> I've recently quit drinking alcohol or any sugary drinks. I still drink soda and energy drinks for now but I only will drink the zero-sugar versions of them. If I ever do get surgery in the future, it would only be top surgery.<br /> <br /> I don't like having a vulva either but it doesn't bother me as much as my breasts do. At least the stuff I have down there can be used to make me feel good more easily than what I have going up top. I'll admit, I like the feeling I get when my hubby gives me oral and I try not to think too much about that from a dysphoric angle, though sometimes it makes me uncomfortable and awkward right afterwards.<br /> <br /> I'd honestly rather have a penis and testicles like a natal male, but any penis that I'd get from phalloplasty would only ever be cosmetic and for me on a personal level, it wouldn't be the same. If it's only cosmetic, I'd rather just use a strap-on instead (and I have) or maybe stuff some cloth or paper in my undies to form a bulge when I'm not in the bedroom. Strap-ons or some bunched-up cloth in the front of your underwear requires a lot less care than a surgically-grafted phallus, which requires constant care and attention, along with any other surgical procedure.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the bedroom, I'm probably hypersexual to a degree. Not to the point that it completely ruins my life, but I've been fucking around a lot for almost twenty years. And I don't regret any of it, though I wouldn't recommend some of the stuff I've done. My high sex drive is unconnected to my gender dysphoria overall, but my dysphoria has affected my sex life in the past and I have found a way to modify my sex life in a way to help get around my dysphoria. Sometimes I will use strap-ons and peg my husband. Most of the time, I just take it in the ass or we give each other oral. Again, this is just what works for me on a personal and specific level and might not be good for others dealing with similar issues.<br /> <br /> I do enjoy anal sex and I think it helps me a bit emotionally as well as feel good physically, as weird as that may sound. It felt bad the first time I did it, but if you prep for it right, it's incredible. As cringe as this may sound, I feel it makes me feel more like the man I that I truly am, whether I'm topping my hubby or bottoming to him. I apologize if that sounds cringe or comes off as problematic, and let me stress once more that this only applies to me and my own personal life specifically.<br /> <br /> I haven't had vaginal sex in almost five months and hadn't had it for nearly two years prior to that. The last time I did was on my wedding night and that was more of a ceremonial &quot;seal the deal&quot; sort of thing that we both agreed to beforehand. It didn't feel that good and triggered intense feelings of dysphoria to the point I broke down crying afterwards, but hubby was able to comfort me and get me through those feelings, and we gave each other oral later that night.<br /> <br /> Having more anal sex, using my strap-on more often, and abstaining from vaginal sex altogether just feels more right to me. That's another small way I can treat my dysphoria, one of many ways until I can go on proper testosterone treatments.<br /> <br /> Ideally, these things, whether it be dressing more masculine, binding my chest, acting more traditionally &quot;manly&quot;, modifying my diet and exercise habits, taking supplements to improve my nutrition, having lots of specific types of sex, and trying to lose more weight and get in shape are just smaller &quot;life hacks&quot; to treat my dysphoria until I can fully go on T, though I'll still continue to do these lifestyle changes as they're generally good things to do even if you don't have dysphoria. Eating better and walking more and having a good emotional support system are just common sense good things to have in your life no matter what your gender identity is.<br /> <br /> I've probably got some undiagnosed PTSD from the abuse I suffered from former comrades of mine and I recently found out one of them was involved in an online transgender group I was part of, and both they and some of the others were giving me a ton of shit for not wanting to get surgery right away and trying to treat my dysphoria in other ways. it was very invalidating.<br /> <br /> I know for a lot of my trans brothers and sisters out there, Gender Reassignment Surgery is very much necessary and the only way for them to combat their own dysphoria and I will not judge anyone who does take that route when it comes to seeking gender-affirming care. But for me as an individual, the procedures feels too risky and invasive for me specifically. I just don't want to be invalidated for my specific and personal choices and trying to find other ways to treat and deal with my dysphoria. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Rant over. I apologize if that was too graphic or too intense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 09-14-2023, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T01:22:13-07:00","id":1522624,"title":"","content":"Wow, Fables (the DC-comics-series) as an IP is now <a href=\"https://billwillingham.substack.com/p/willingham-sends-fables-into-the\" target=\"_blank\">in the public domain</a>.<br /> <br /> Seems like DC just continued to try to take the IP away from the creator Bill Willingham and didn't want to pay him any royalties or consult him on how the IP was used... Why do companies like DC have to be so greedy...?<br /> <br /> Here's where Bill Willingham describes his experience with DC-comics:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Q: What Exactly Has DC Comics Done to Provoke This?<br /> <br /> Too many things to list exhaustively, but here are some highlights: Throughout the years of my business relationship with DC, with Fables and with other intellectual properties, DC has always been in violation of their agreements with me. Usually it\u2019s in smaller matters, like forgetting to seek my opinion on artists for new stories, or for covers, or formats of new collections and such. In those times, when called on it, they automatically said, \u201cSorry, we overlooked you again. It just fell through the cracks.\u201d They use the \u201cfell through the cracks\u201d line so often, and so reflexively, that I eventually had to bar them from using it ever again. They are often late reporting royalties, and often under-report said royalties, forcing me to go after them to pay the rest of what\u2019s owed.<br /> <br /> Lately though their practices have grown beyond these mere annoyances, prompting some sort of showdown. First they tried to strong arm the ownership of Fables from me. When Mark Doyle and Dan Didio first approached me with the idea of bringing Fables back for its 20th anniversary (both gentlemen since fired from DC), during the contract negotiations for the new issues, their legal negotiators tried to make it a condition of the deal that the work be done as work for hire, effectively throwing the property irrevocably into the hands of DC. When that didn\u2019t work their excuse was, \u201cSorry, we didn\u2019t read your contract going into these negotiations. We thought we owned it.\u201d<br /> <br /> More recently, during talks to try to work out our many differences, DC officers admitted that their interpretation of our publishing agreement, and the following media rights agreement, is that they could do whatever they wanted with the property. They could change stories or characters in any way they wanted. They had no obligation whatsoever to protect the integrity and value of the IP, either from themselves, or from third parties (Telltale Games, for instance) who want to radically alter the characters, settings, history and premises of the story (I\u2019ve seen the script they tried to hide from me for a couple of years). Nor did they owe me any money for licensing the Fables rights to third parties, since such a license wasn\u2019t anticipated in our original publishing agreement.<br /> <br /> When they capitulated on some of the points in a later conference call, promising on the phone to pay me back monies owed for licensing Fables to Telltale Games, for example, in the execution of the new agreement, they reneged on their word and offered the promised amount instead as a \u201cconsulting fee,\u201d which avoided the precedent of admitting this was money owed, and included a non-disclosure agreement that would prevent me from saying anything but nice things about Telltale or the license.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T04:20:02-07:00","id":1522625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1522577#post1522577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post