r b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1522624#post1522624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, Fables (the DC-comics-series) as an IP is now <a href=\"https://billwillingham.substack.com/p/willingham-sends-fables-into-the\" target=\"_blank\">in the public domain</a>.<br /> <br /> Seems like DC just continued to try to take the IP away from the creator Bill Willingham and didn't want to pay him any royalties or consult him on how the IP was used... Why do companies like DC have to be so greedy...?<br /> <br /> Here's where Bill Willingham describes his experience with DC-comics:</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the nature of working with big companies like this sadly as they have and will continue to screw talent over like they did to Siegal &amp; Shuster, Bill Finger and many others. Even the team on the Clownfish channel talked about their struggles in trying to get even published when people in the Executive level kept trying to change things in their novels that they like to write into directions that they weren't comfortable going into.<br /> <br /> <br /> Have a good legal team go over the contracts and find the small print that doesn't help you. In fact Backstreet Boys &amp; N Sync found out that their manager screwed them out a good deal of money as he listed himself as the sixth member of there bands and would get more the profits.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 0