o call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T19:49:26-07:00","id":1524671,"title":"","content":"While true, a good number of them at least claim to have educations that imply having the training in research and citation to know better. But social media is also driven by emotional engagement that tends to drive down incentives to use said skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T19:58:23-07:00","id":1524672,"title":"","content":"I got informed that an Ad-Blocker was not allowed on their website; OK: ads aren't allowed on my computer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T00:02:49-07:00","id":1524676,"title":"","content":"I am officially too introverted and too ace to enjoy a Rocky Horror Picture Show. If I had watched the movie before hand, it might have been better. But it was like one of those <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Vt4Dfa4fOEY?si=bfi-4mD1v2Y7jvPO\" target=\"_blank\">linguistic videos where everyone is speaking a made-up language to show how English sounds to non-speakers.</a> The crowd was <i>so damn loud</i>, and you could only clearly hear like one word in fifty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T05:52:20-07:00","id":1524686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1524671#post1524671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While true, a good number of them at least claim to have educations that imply having the training in research and citation to know better. But social media is also driven by emotional engagement that tends to drive down incentives to use said skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly a truth.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1524676#post1524676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am officially too introverted and too ace to enjoy a Rocky Horror Picture Show. If I had watched the movie before hand, it might have been better. But it was like one of those <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Vt4Dfa4fOEY?si=bfi-4mD1v2Y7jvPO\" target=\"_blank\">linguistic videos where everyone is speaking a made-up language to show how English sounds to non-speakers.</a> The crowd was <i>so damn loud</i>, and you could only clearly hear like one word in fifty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I would consider myself a fan of Rocky Horror or that I have an ardent reason for anyone to watch it, let alone give it a second chance, but yeah, the best way to watch it is definitely first with a small group of friends willing to laugh at the funny bits but not quote it. Crowd viewings definitely make that movie nothing but soup for the unfamiliar. I'm sorry that's how your viewing went.<br /> <br /> (Like, yeah, I get why Rocky Horror is a cult classic, but it's not my particular flavor of cult classic.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T11:18:56-07:00","id":1524694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1524659#post1524659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's certain social media apps changing algorithms, but I've been having a lot of people in my feeds lately citing Op-Eds as &quot;proof&quot; of their hot takes. Op-Eds are opinions, not facts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which sounds like about 90% of Social Media personalities like JosiahRises who is very clickbaiting with his videos and gives more or less emotional takes on issues and claims that he runs a movie studio called EpicVerse and I have yet to see anything from him. Daily Wire has at least made a couple of films which is more then this guy.<br /> <br /> I more or less have sworn off watching his videos as he comes across as a loud mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T11:22:47-07:00","id":1524695,"title":"","content":"Shocking thing today I got a notice from Facebook about a password reset on my deactivated account that I did about 5-6 years ago and that was unexpected to say the least as I haven't been on that site since then.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T11:25:02-07:00","id":1524696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1524662#post1524662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to get all collegiate here, but this what happens when you introduce platforms for essay-like dialogue without having a populace trained in learning how to research and find proper citation. People get the idea you can just build a mass concensus and that's the same as study and discernment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember back in school when you had to do a report or essay is that you had to show proper references to provide support for your side and so on. Now it seems it's optional and I wonder if it's even a thing in school anymore?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T13:16:17-07:00","id":1524706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1524694#post1524694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which sounds like about 90% of Social Media personalities like JosiahRises who is very clickbaiting with his videos and gives more or less emotional takes on issues and claims that he runs a movie studio called EpicVerse and I have yet to see anything from him. Daily Wire has at least made a couple of films which is more then this guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly less worried about &quot;personalities&quot; because like all celebrity their money is based on a persona. That persona could be well informed, well researched, and good communication of topics or it could be purposeful ignorance and divisive rhetoric. If there's an audience, there's someone that will make content for them out there.<br /> <br /> It's random people spouting off on things that they justifiably have strong opinions about, but want to be <b>right</b> about without putting in the time and energy to at least get good sources that bugs me enough to vent here about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1524696#post1524696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember back in school when you had to do a report or essay is that you had to show proper references to provide support for your side and so on. Now it seems it's optional and I wonder if it's even a thing in school anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is complicated. These sorts of assignments are absolutely still a thing in most modern education systems. However most modern education systems are still struggling to adapt to a world were students have access to near unlimited information, and educators have no time to check sourcing quality. The explosion of misinformation (both purposeful disinformation, and just the incidentals of things like chat-program generated content growing increasingly hard to separate from human sources) has only compounded the difficulty in training students on propped sourcing habits. Justifiably there's a lot stronger of a push for at least primary and secondary education to focus more on teaching students to assess source quality and then push traditional sourcing and research projects into late secondary/early tertiary education. Or in less academic terms, people that aren't going to be writing papers for a living are better served having more time as children learning how to spot crap sources, and those headed for higher levels of academia are going to get more time focusing on formal citation skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T13:17:29-07:00","id":1524707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1524696#post1524696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember back in school when you had to do a report or essay is that you had to show proper references to provide support for your side and so on. Now it seems it's optional and I wonder if it's even a thing in school anymore?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the realm of the anecdotal, but I didn't cite any sources in high school(2002-2007). Most essays at the time were just testing your willingness to type down a large number of words at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T13:20:37-07:00","id":1524708,"title":"","content":"I got an F on a High School assignment because I forgot to put one of my sources in the ending citations, despite giving it as a footnote citation. Granted, that was the International Bachelorette system, but it was still in 2012-13-ish time frame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T10:39:40-07:00","id":1524758,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1524706]<br /> <br /> I'm honestly less worried about &quot;personalities&quot; because like all celebrity their money is based on a persona. That persona could be well informed, well researched, and good communication of topics or it could be purposeful ignorance and divisive rhetoric. If there's an audience, there's someone that will make content for them out there.<br /> <br /> <br /> That is true and there is some social media personalities that are quite well informed about the topics that they like be it such as the lore of a particular IP or how movies are made and why they like such and such a story and not another and are way more articulate then me about it. Or you know that they are putting on a performance for there fans such as Space Ice who roasts good &amp; bad movies with glee and you know that he has put in lots of time and effort to put on a good video.<br /> <br /> It's random people spouting off on things that they justifiably have strong opinions about, but want to be <b>right</b> about without putting in the time and energy to at least get good sources that bugs me enough to vent here about it.<br /> <br /> That is my issue with channels like JosiahRises and others like him as it comes across as pure emotion and not much fact.<br /> <br /> I'll take your word about the school system struggling to teach the current generation about history and critical thinking skills.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T10:42:02-07:00","id":1524759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1524707#post1524707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in the realm of the anecdotal, but I didn't cite any sources in high school(2002-2007). Most essays at the time were just testing your willingness to type down a large number of words at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is different from back in my time in school, but I graduated high school in 1996 and took two years of college for what I thought I was going to and found out later I wasn't cut for that type of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T06:22:46-07:00","id":1524972,"title":"","content":"Storytellers Vault currently has 8 titles listing Midjourney as the artist. That\u2019s not counting people who list themselves as the artist and then on the credits page admit they used Midjourney or other AI Art programs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T10:39:13-08:00","id":1525079,"title":"","content":"I dislike when alleged adults are so thin skinned when it comes to legit constructive criticism and cry whatever ism they can think of.<br /> <br /> IE Director X crying about the terrible reviews of Robyn Hood and most of the complaints were about how poorly done the show is general and he goes on major social media channels to win arguments and I\u2019m wondering even if you do get your points out. Your show is not going to become better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T11:51:07-08:00","id":1525128,"title":"","content":"Over the years I have been increasingly burned by how modern retailers will have an appliance in stock which solves X problem, but then breaks down after only 2-3 years of regular use. Invariably it cannot be simply <i>repaired</i> as what will break down will be an unnecessary electronic component. Then when you go back to the same store to get another one, you find that they no longer carry said item or don't keep it in physical stock. Instead they prefer you to roam around online looking for something similar to what you already have so they can pressure you to have it shipped, handled, insured, and a host of other crap which ensures you pay 25-50% more than you did before. And that's only an option about a quarter of the time, usually they want you to buy a bigger, gaudier, more expensive version costing 2-3 times as much but having exactly the same lifespan. Where do these idiots think we're supposed to get the money for this kind of insanity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T16:29:13-08:00","id":1525136,"title":"","content":"Last stage capitalism is an insufficient concept to describe the idiocy of the fact that a pay-to-win game based <b>TV show</b> is now actually a real thing. I can understand the idea of having playing an app game be the new &quot;call or text your votes&quot; in for a TV show that uses audience feedback to influence episodes. Making the game ptw, when all you're winning is more votes on the show is... dumbfounding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T19:15:59-08:00","id":1525144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525136#post1525136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last stage capitalism is an insufficient concept to describe the idiocy of the fact that a pay-to-win game based <b>TV show</b> is now actually a real thing. I can understand the idea of having playing an app game be the new &quot;call or text your votes&quot; in for a TV show that uses audience feedback to influence episodes. Making the game ptw, when all you're winning is more votes on the show is... dumbfounding.</div> </div> </div> </div>FUcking hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T13:17:43-08:00","id":1525178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525136#post1525136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last stage capitalism is an insufficient concept to describe the idiocy of the fact that a pay-to-win game based <b>TV show</b> is now actually a real thing. I can understand the idea of having playing an app game be the new &quot;call or text your votes&quot; in for a TV show that uses audience feedback to influence episodes. Making the game ptw, when all you're winning is more votes on the show is... dumbfounding.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first sentence that came to mind when I read this was: &quot;Let's monetize the rot!&quot;<br /> <br /> Tricking some rich idiots into becoming whales for some dumb pay-to-win game show... Well, it's a living, I guess...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T10:10:55-08:00","id":1525209,"title":"","content":"To be clear, it's not a game show in the sense of something like a quiz show or a &quot;reality&quot; competition show. It's a traditional animated streaming show that works like a choose-your-own-adventure book or interactive fiction game. But rather than each person getting their own experience by playing on their own, everyone plays (or pays) to &quot;vote&quot; on a choice at set points in the narrative.<br /> <br /> It's even more silly because they're planning to release the first season (and hopefully only season) as a stand-alone interactive fiction game where you can play out all the other options once the &quot;canon&quot; picks have all been made. So if the story was any good (reviews of the first episode are that it's garbage), you could just wait a year or something and play it on your own; exploring all the different paths the story could take without the online-social aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T15:02:01-08:00","id":1525219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525209#post1525209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, it's not a game show in the sense of something like a quiz show or a &quot;reality&quot; competition show. It's a traditional animated streaming show that works like a choose-your-own-adventure book or interactive fiction game. But rather than each person getting their own experience by playing on their own, everyone plays (or pays) to &quot;vote&quot; on a choice at set points in the narrative.<br /> <br /> It's even more silly because they're planning to release the first season (and hopefully only season) as a stand-alone interactive fiction game where you can play out all the other options once the &quot;canon&quot; picks have all been made. So if the story was any good (reviews of the first episode are that it's garbage), you could just wait a year or something and play it on your own; exploring all the different paths the story could take without the online-social aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like I'm not missing much on streaming services Heavy Arms with what you just mentioned above.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's amazing how we get older and less likely to entertain new types of entertainment concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T15:04:13-08:00","id":1525220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525128#post1525128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over the years I have been increasingly burned by how modern retailers will have an appliance in stock which solves X problem, but then breaks down after only 2-3 years of regular use. Invariably it cannot be simply <i>repaired</i> as what will break down will be an unnecessary electronic component. Then when you go back to the same store to get another one, you find that they no longer carry said item or don't keep it in physical stock. Instead they prefer you to roam around online looking for something similar to what you already have so they can pressure you to have it shipped, handled, insured, and a host of other crap which ensures you pay 25-50% more than you did before. And that's only an option about a quarter of the time, usually they want you to buy a bigger, gaudier, more expensive version costing 2-3 times as much but having exactly the same lifespan. Where do these idiots think we're supposed to get the money for this kind of insanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>My best friend touched upon this somewhat with me as why computers, cell phones and games I guess breakdown after two years as the companies have to cut corners to get products out on such and such a date and it will be a shorter lifespan for parts in said items.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T09:08:41-08:00","id":1525251,"title":"","content":"Obsolescence is not an accident or an expediency. It's a very deliberate way to ensure that consumers need to constantly replace their products.<br /> <br /> It can even be found in things like how a lot of clothes are stitched.<br /> <br /> There are things like functioning light bulbs that are decades old, manufactured in a time when there were stricter regulations. Increasingly shoddy products can be traced directly back to the Reagan era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T10:21:39-08:00","id":1525257,"title":"","content":"It always raises my eyebrows Isator Levi when I hear people saying that we must have more deregulation of industries and we see them go down the tubes and either go bankrupt or ask the government to bail them out with taxpayer money. But that is debate for another type of format and not a place dedicated to all things gaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T10:28:05-08:00","id":1525258,"title":"","content":"I find it strange that some Youtubers are complaining about alternate timelines and Multiverses now and it's been a staple of Science Fiction &amp; Fantasy genres for as long as I can remember and now it's a problem for some of them.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T15:39:04-08:00","id":1525275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525251#post1525251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obsolescence is not an accident or an expediency. It's a very deliberate way to ensure that consumers need to constantly replace their products.<br /> <br /> It can even be found in things like how a lot of clothes are stitched.<br /> <br /> There are things like functioning light bulbs that are decades old, manufactured in a time when there were stricter regulations. Increasingly shoddy products can be traced directly back to the Reagan era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsolescence might be a marketing ploy, but there are real trade-offs in engineering products that aren't the result of corporate machinations.<br /> <br /> The old &quot;forever&quot; bulbs of the past have two very big problems:<br /> <br /> 1) You can't turn them off, because they're incandescent bulbs and the biggest failure point is the filament. The more you cycle filaments on and off, the faster they wear down and eventually break.<br /> <br /> 2) They are massive power-hogs. The highly durable filaments they use to last so long mean they take exponentially more energy to produce the same amount of light as &quot;shoddy&quot; standard commercial incandescent bulbs. If you're considering things like overall environmental impact, we'd be better going back to candles (including the risk of home fires) than using the light bulbs that can last decades (or even over a century as cool of a feat as that is).<br /> <br /> Deregulation and corporate greed are still major contributors to lots of problems, but unless we can figure out a way to produce hundreds, if not thousands, of times more electricity without burning fossil fuels, moving to the old ultra-long-lasting bulbs would be blocked by any sensible environmental regulations anyway. The same way lots of really important regulations to make cars safer when they hit things have lead to cars that are harder to repair and thus more likely to get replaced instead; but it's worth it because it means saving lives during car accidents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T01:11:53-08:00","id":1525296,"title":"","content":"This might be petty. <br /> <br /> But I just got banned by the Worm fanfic reddit thread, for 'posting a story idea' when I had a fic search. Yes, its a story summary in the post section, because I remembered the one-shot's plot! This isn't a story idea, I was posting the story plot so I can find the goddamned story again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T10:08:23-08:00","id":1525313,"title":"","content":"I know I'm getting tired of political figures comparing people that they don't like or agree with to Adolf Hilter (Sorry about the spelling mistake folks) as it cheapens the horrible acts of violence that he and his supporters inflicted on others. This is about as political I want to get on this board and I needed to vent about this action from certain folks who should know better and are in positions of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T11:19:46-08:00","id":1525354,"title":"","content":"I've seen that new Marvel-movie &quot;The Marvels&quot; and... it sucked. It's this chaotic mess of a movie. A script that went through multiple rewrites and a movie that went through lengthy reshoots: At least that's what it felt like watching it. Just this frantic pace of stuff happening. And all the characters felt underdeveloped. I also was laughing when the plan of the villain became clear. It's supposed to be serious but it's literally the same plot as President Skroob's plot in Spaceballs. It's a plot in Spaceballs because it's supposed to be absurd, of course, so why does The Marvels have the same villain-scheme...? And so many &quot;jokes&quot;, just SO MANY... I don't think Nick Fury had a single serious moment in this movie. Every single line was either a joke or a setup for a joke. Every. Single. Line. He didn't even seem like the same character from Secret Invasion so there goes the Cinematic Universe part... Seriously, what are they doing over there at Disney?!<br /> <br /> My friends wanted to see the movie so I tagged along but honestly, I kinda regret it. At least, it was one of the shorter Marvel movies coming in at under two hours. I didn't think I would get to see a Marvel-movie this year that's worse than Quantummania but here we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T11:37:06-08:00","id":1525355