[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T12:20:24-08:00","id":1525470,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Ragged Robin;n1525459]damned editing-rules of this forum. At the risk of coming across as an angry toxic bitch (as my girlfriend charmingly described me recently) I have some 'concerns' about some of my peers in the rpg community and their...well....intelligence. Considering I work with lower income children in education fine I feel this says something.<br /> <br /> (not in order of severity)<br /> <br /> Highlights since 2017, including some from other gamers.<br /> <br /> -rpg fans don't care about lore or fluff and expansions are pointless<br /> <br /> I actually don't mind taking creative liberties with the lore as we stay true to the setting of said game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -Being called a feminazi bitch and an alt right chud for the same post.<br /> <br /> <br /> I hate those type of trolling posts myself and most would agree that it has no place in a game or a debating board such as this site and with those terms being being used so much now. They have lost all meaning.<br /> <br /> <br /> -Being told the Lasombra are the best clan and the ventrue are the worst due to their comparitive capacity for fistycuffs...he later changed this to clan brujah<br /> <br /> Most clans have there good points and being able to withstand huge amounts of punishment is more important to me then being able to dish it out and usually I try not have my player character fight that way and try to use celerity, obfuscate and fortitude combos to get out of the danger zone.<br /> <br /> -Being told the Lasombra are the best clan because in game you intimated a ventrue player with how badass you are.<br /> <br /> Remind them that there is always someone who is more skilled and potent out there.<br /> <br /> -Somebody telling me they masturbated about becoming my mage PC irl. I mean their are better ways to realize/come out as trans my friend.<br /> <br /> I'd be saying to much information to the person and find healthier ways to express yourself.<br /> <br /> -The d&amp;d gm who wouldnt let you run black people even if you where from an exotic land<br /> <br /> They do know that this is a fantasy setting and should be no limits to your ideas?<br /> <br /> -The guy who used an anagram of the N-word as his pc name and thought I wouldn't notice.....or realize he wasn't black when he's got a link to his social sites embedded.<br /> <br /> Using slurs is crossing a line in most cases and I don't care what your color of your skin is. That needs to be stopped in general.<br /> <br /> -The girl who thought I'd tolerate groping of other girls because she's a girl<br /> <br /> Wow!<br /> <br /> -The fucking couple wanted to play a teenage girls then fuck lots of dudes.<br /> <br /> Even more crazy and I played online with one person who played her character like that. It got so bad that we banned her from playing not long afterwards.<br /> <br /> -The guy who stank of shit<br /> <br /> Ewww<br /> <br /> -The non-binary who stank of condoms, lube and sweat<br /> <br /> Eww<br /> <br /> -The player who wanted to play a greek tragedy and got mad when his pc died from his own hubris.<br /> <br /> Be careful what you wish for in other words.<br /> <br /> -","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T03:28:06-08:00","id":1525505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525465#post1525465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They wonder why we are so protective of our hobby from the casual tourists who are not serious about it like many of us are Ragged Robin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think the problem with that list of people is that they're not interested enough in roleplaying games? Or that it's just what the majority of people are like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T09:49:50-08:00","id":1525518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525505#post1525505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think the problem with that list of people is that they're not interested enough in roleplaying games? Or that it's just what the majority of people are like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember people who were known to play rpgs were looked down upon by the &quot;cool&quot; people of society and like to call us names and we had those hypes reports of D&amp;D inspired crimes by a media that loves to stir things up. Then with the successful comic book movies came out and we were seen as &quot;cool&quot; and they wanted in and then we got people who didn't like the setting or the people that were there and stirred up trouble and wanted the lore changed for no reason whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T13:08:43-08:00","id":1525534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525518#post1525518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember people who were known to play rpgs were looked down upon by the &quot;cool&quot; people of society and like to call us names and we had those hypes reports of D&amp;D inspired crimes by a media that loves to stir things up. Then with the successful comic book movies came out and we were seen as &quot;cool&quot; and they wanted in and then we got people who didn't like the setting or the people that were there and stirred up trouble and wanted the lore changed for no reason whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all entirely expected. Whenever something drifts into mainstream you have to know that suddenly there will be an infestation of this kind of petty, clout-chasing scum looking for recognition and validation. They wanna be seen as players so they can post about it and highlight their otherwise boring and banal little lives. They wanna change the settings and rules because they're too unsophisticated or even stupid to see why things are as they are. The latest of them are too used to airing out every little detail about themselves in search of attention so of course they'll start airing out their worst traits through their characters if need be. A lot of them are probably hoping to get in on a game that gets podcast or streamed so they can collect on that internet fame.<br /> <br /> And there's nothing that can be done about it because any gaming company will kill to hold on to all this exposure and product sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T16:46:41-08:00","id":1525552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525518#post1525518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember people who were known to play rpgs were looked down upon by the &quot;cool&quot; people of society and like to call us names and we had those hypes reports of D&amp;D inspired crimes by a media that loves to stir things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't, actually, I'm in my early thirties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then with the successful comic book movies came out and we were seen as &quot;cool&quot; and they wanted in</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like being stuck between a state of &quot;bitter about being marginalized&quot; and &quot;bitter about being popular&quot; is not something that ever has a satisfying resolution.<br /> <br /> Mind, roleplaying games probably owe a bit more to things that made examples of how they were played a bit more accessible, in a way to showcase what is uniquely fun about them. Streaming and podcasts and the like. The fact that one of the biggest video games of 2023 captures a lot of the texture of it.<br /> <br /> You might want to gatekeep, but unfortunately the gate of &quot;communications technology is bigger than it was in the 80s&quot; might be a tad too big for you, and it might just mean that a lot of people are learning about things to love in the medium that are exactly the same as what you did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">then we got people who didn't like the setting or the people that were there and stirred up trouble and wanted the lore changed for no reason whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm not too sure about settings. The biggest thing I'm aware of is more critical evaluation of stuff like the concept of Always Chaotic Evil races.<br /> <br /> And as far as people go, a sense of hostility to newcomers probably isn't the best way to make friends and influence people.<br /> <br /> I suppose that's the thing about gatekeeping; if one insists on walling people out, they can just effectively build the rest of the town around them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1525519#post1525519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and put our spin on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So wait, is people putting their spin on it good or bad now then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 11-16-2023, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T16:48:27-08:00","id":1525553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525534#post1525534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latest of them are too used to airing out every little detail about themselves in search of attention</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that as though there aren't people who have been playing and making games for decades who have become comfortable with coming out as not straight as that becomes a safer thing to convey about themselves.<br /> <br /> I do think it's ironic to get this kind of thing in a forum for White Wolf games, a thing that got derision back in the day from Dungeons and Dragons players as the sort of thing that supposedly brought in Goths and club kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T01:48:03-08:00","id":1525582,"title":"","content":"Personally I don't loose much sleep on populist appeal one way or another, I've known plenty of garbage nerds/goths/whatever and plenty of nice mainstream folks. If my brother-in-law suddenly liked vtm I wouldn't loose much sleep over it.<br /> What I do dislike is the inevitable dilution of product that comes with this as corporations try to net as many people are possible and artistic integrity of product goes down the toilet. Parawolfs handling of vtm shows that to a degree regardless of the surge of interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T02:45:43-08:00","id":1525583,"title":"","content":"I do get very frustrated when people conflate nostalgia with things like artistic integrity. <br /> <br /> For example, watching superhero movie fatigue hit pop culture pretty hard is not shocking to me, because that's exactly what happened to myself and a lot of my friends that grew up with superhero comics. Superhero comics were never some bastion of creative vision and artistic integrity. It was a world of creator egos fighting over credit whenever something go popular, while editors saturated the markets with nauseating repetition as they kept trying to recapture the spark of whatever the most recent popular (esp. popular beyond normal readers) trend was. <br /> <br /> The MCU isn't ruining things... is faithfully adapting the comics in their entirety: including the parts where most people get sick and tired of crossovers, multiverses, resets, spinoffs, and ever expansive lore that makes it harder and harder to know what's going on if you don't start at the beginning and play catch up. But so few people lamenting the downwards trends in superhero films bother thinking about how the source material was (and still is) a huge part of why it all turned out that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T05:59:06-08:00","id":1525589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525583#post1525583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The MCU isn't ruining things... is faithfully adapting the comics in their entirety: including the parts where most people get sick and tired of crossovers, multiverses, resets, spinoffs, and ever expansive lore that makes it harder and harder to know what's going on if you don't start at the beginning and play catch up. But so few people lamenting the downwards trends in superhero films bother thinking about how the source material was (and still is) a huge part of why it all turned out that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding of the comics was for a couple of years now, they've mostly been a prepping ground for the films. I suspect new girl captain marvels big push was partly due to them wanting both an equivelant of superman and wonder woman for the big screen and a lot of the guys were seeing hauled in now are actually comparatively new characters. Its been a while but my partner commented things got heated once the right weaponises this trend since the new heroes were a mixed bag in terms of writting quality.<br /> <br /> if I'm correct that they're using the comics to lay the groundwork for more movies the current struggles they're going through make more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T06:44:41-08:00","id":1525590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525589#post1525589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect new girl captain marvels big push was partly due to them wanting both an equivelant of superman and wonder woman for the big screen</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the timeline for that doesn't quite match up. As far as I understand, everything before a while after The Avengers was such a big success was still very tentative and cautious, while Carol Danvers had been a character with increasing prominence for a few years prior to that (starting just before Iron Man was released), with her being given the &quot;Captain Marvel&quot; moniker the same year that Avengers came out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T10:37:25-08:00","id":1525599,"title":"","content":"Carol was promoted to a main character from a side character to the original Captain Marvel back in the 70s because Marvel didn't have a Wonder Woman. But without the Golden Age history she got hit hard by the Dark/Iron Age era and didn't really come back as a major character and Marvel's main female hero until the mid-00s. She was already being pushed (successfully) to a major comics character before the MCU really took off.<br /> <br /> There is a lot of interaction between the comics and movies at this point, but which is following the other gets complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T10:50:21-08:00","id":1525600,"title":"","content":"The interesting thing that not many women went to see The Marvels and it was mostly guys which is understandable as it appeals more to men then women in general. In my neck of the woods and at the book store I work at a couple times a week, most the women are more into Manga where there is multiple genres to choose from then DC, Marvel or Image that works with the superhero genre mainly.<br /> <br /> Like I said before having certain social media personalities complaining about alternate timelines and universes is a strange one for me as it has been a staple for the science fiction/fantasy genre for as long as I can remember and they seemed unaware of it. Which makes me wonder if they truly knew the genre in general and were just causal readers and didn't follow it all that closely.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-18-2023, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T11:30:23-08:00","id":1525603,"title":"","content":"A sad vent rather than an angry one - I had some World of Warcraft gametime I could cash in, the next expansion looks interesting, and once Bobby Kotick is gone I'll have... fewer reservations about giving Blizzard money. So I gave it a spin.<br /> <br /> It's still got a lot of good points, but I've very much moved on in since I first played. Ignoring combat -which feels overly simple now that I've played stuff like Monster Hunter- there's <i>so much clutter</i>. The quests are a massive jumble that don't really guide you on a coherent narrative very well, even if you don't account for there being three or four prior expansion plots that keep pinging me to start them. A ton of stuff is time-locked or grind-locked, which makes some of the old stuff a <i>nightmare</i> to go back and do. And I don't really enjoy multi-player, so it's not like I'm there for the MMO- part, which <i>also</i> disbars me from a good chunk of content.<br /> <br /> There's good stuff mixed in there - I love a lot of the art, game models, and a <i>ton</i> of the background NPC stuff is neat to watch. But it just doesn't hold enough of my attention to justify a subscription, and i seriously doubt they'll ever release a singleplayer version (or at least a client-side game where you could mod/consol command). I kinda miss my childhood fascination with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T13:00:50-08:00","id":1525605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525603#post1525603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sad vent rather than an angry one - I had some World of Warcraft gametime I could cash in, the next expansion looks interesting, and once Bobby Kotick is gone I'll have... fewer reservations about giving Blizzard money. So I gave it a spin.<br /> <br /> It's still got a lot of good points, but I've very much moved on in since I first played. Ignoring combat -which feels overly simple now that I've played stuff like Monster Hunter- there's <i>so much clutter</i>. The quests are a massive jumble that don't really guide you on a coherent narrative very well, even if you don't account for there being three or four prior expansion plots that keep pinging me to start them. A ton of stuff is time-locked or grind-locked, which makes some of the old stuff a <i>nightmare</i> to go back and do. And I don't really enjoy multi-player, so it's not like I'm there for the MMO- part, which <i>also</i> disbars me from a good chunk of content.<br /> <br /> There's good stuff mixed in there - I love a lot of the art, game models, and a <i>ton</i> of the background NPC stuff is neat to watch. But it just doesn't hold enough of my attention to justify a subscription, and i seriously doubt they'll ever release a singleplayer version (or at least a client-side game where you could mod/consol command). I kinda miss my childhood fascination with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To bad that you didn't enjoy your experience with the revised version of WOW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T01:19:49-08:00","id":1525627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525600#post1525600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interesting thing that not many women went to see The Marvels and it was mostly guys which is understandable as it appeals more to men then women in general. In my neck of the woods and at the book store I work at a couple times a week, most the women are more into Manga where there is multiple genres to choose from then DC, Marvel or Image that works with the superhero genre mainly.<br /> <br /> Like I said before having certain social media personalities complaining about alternate timelines and universes is a strange one for me as it has been a staple for the science fiction/fantasy genre for as long as I can remember and they seemed unaware of it. Which makes me wonder if they truly knew the genre in general and were just causal readers and didn't follow it all that closely.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, something I have noticed is marketing actually struggles to lock onto what we actually like unless they luck out. The nerdy girls in schools I've worked at tend to be more into Harry Potter style stuff, manga, d&amp;d and whatnot. <br /> the ones who are into traditional superhero stuff go for shonin manga which follows trends with the boys and this is before you consider the ones who follow more conventionally femmine stuff like one kid who buries herself in classical literature.<br /> <br /> Even the trans kid is mostly about anne rice, horror and nu metal.<br /> <br /> Does anyone actually know any actual teenage girls who have much enthusiasm for marvel. I work with these little maniacs and I'm struggling here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T04:17:57-08:00","id":1525632,"title":"","content":"The mid-00s to mid-10s Young Avengers run reportedly sold well with girls (and the animated Marvel shows at the time which featured a lot of the same characters and a few other fan favorites were also generally above average for Marvel for that demographic). But when that line up was ended in 2012 with members either becoming full Avengers or just sort of existing around the various Marvel books, there wasn't a big conversion of fans to other books (which is usually the case, but Marvel and DC can never seem to learn that lesson). My experience matched this pretty closely, and most of the Marvel comics reading girls I know are now in their 20s and most of the comics they liked are long cancelled, and the MCU is floundering right as it gets to the stuff they liked when they were younger. Spider-Gwen is pretty much the only Marvel character I can think of that has any enthusiasm with girls I know right now (and the Spider-verse movies are a big part of that even though Spider-Gwen's comics have been going strong for almost a decade now).<br /> <br /> The MCU was also undercut a lot by Johnathan Majors domestic violence case, as Kang plays a rather large role in both Carol Danver's and the Young Avengers stories that were part of the core of their popularity height with a more diverse audience. Carol helping a morally dubious Kang variant fight an objectively horrible Kang variant was a big part of her shift to a leadership role on Earth instead of just solo heroing around the galaxy, while a good Kang variant (one of the only Young Avengers not introduced so far in the MCU, and one of the others is a former X-men character with all the issues with that not being settled until recently) is one of the founding members of the Young Avengers in part to gather allies to restrengthen Earth's heroes after Civil War and Secret Invasion so they can be ready to fight more Kangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T08:13:38-08:00","id":1525636,"title":"","content":"I feel like I read that the Young Justice cartoon was proving very popular with girls when it was first airing, which was why it got canceled the first time - it wasn't doing as well with the &quot;Young male&quot; target audience, whose toy purchases they were expecting to profit on. I may be mis-remembering though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T11:26:20-08:00","id":1525647,"title":"","content":"At Ragged Robin most women in my neck of the woods were more into Batman related stuff and Spider-Man or Deadpool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T14:08:34-08:00","id":1525658,"title":"","content":"&quot;I'm not obligated and you're not entitled&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T14:16:41-08:00","id":1525660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525636#post1525636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I read that the Young Justice cartoon was proving very popular with girls when it was first airing, which was why it got canceled the first time - it wasn't doing as well with the &quot;Young male&quot; target audience, whose toy purchases they were expecting to profit on. I may be mis-remembering though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is essentially correct. Young Justice was very popular with a wide range of viewers, but DC wanted it to be a merchandise mill and it's expanded viewership didn't lead to that. It wasn't unpopular with the toy buying audience, but it wasn't converting non-merch viewers into toy buyers (I have no idea why DC expected that to work, but Marvel and DC's corporate heads are a constant source of stupidity that is never corrected).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T09:48:22-08:00","id":1525733,"title":"","content":"I guess when you live so far removed from the typical family or everyday reality we get plans like this Heavy Arms and then they wonder why it didn't work at all and sometimes lash out and insult us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T11:50:06-08:00","id":1525739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1525733#post1525733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess when you live so far removed from the typical family</div> </div> </div> </div>What does that have to do with whether or not the people would buy merchandise?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">then they wonder why it didn't work at all and sometimes lash out and insult us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you said the things people were lashing out about were merely not well made.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T11:59:46-08:00","id":1525740,"title":"","content":"I would somewhat agree with Lysander on the mental removal from reality that goes along with being part of the C-suite class; even in entertainment business where connecting to audiences is supposed to be an essential skill.<br /> <br /> Ultimately things like popularity and quality (which aren't the same thing) are just labels that fans debate over. The executives constantly making obviously horrible decisions to the rest of us are using metrics designed solely around maximizing short term profits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T15:27:35-08:00","id":1525753,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Isator Levi;n1525739]<br /> <br /> What does that have to do with whether or not the people would buy merchandise?<br /> <br /> I mean that they don't really connect with what viewers really want and have a narrow focus and get tunnel vision and not see what people really like or are attracted to such as when Hasbro miscalulated the blowback when they first killed off Optmius Prime in the animated movie and Flint Dille admitted that were blind sided by that and thought they were dealing with a toy line with a cartoon series and saw this as a marketing choice. So being somewhat removed from everyday reality is expected by the execs<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I thought you said the things people were lashing out about were merely not well made.<br /> <br /> I'm referring to the people in the entertainment corporations that go nuts when you critic there products and start calling the people every ism under the book and devaluing the term and not considering that maybe that they are making subpar products. IE Director X referring to the folks like me who didn't like how poorly put together his Robyn Hood show was and called us racist and sexist and the majority of the posts were like mine which was focused on how bad the acting, storytelling, production values and general lack of awareness of how the police and business would act in the real world.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should have been more clear about that answer.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T11:20:12-08:00","id":1525854,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of mediocre media in existence, but only a certain subset seems to have a whole industry and subculture around heavily scrutinising and raking it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T02:11:45-08:00","id":1525874,"title":"","content":"Yesterday in Dublin, there was an incident in which a man with a knife assaulted several very young school children and some accompanying adults. A few hours after that, a congregation of men spewing far-right rhetoric in connection to the attack (the suspect in custody is a naturalised citizen) grew into a full-fledged riot, causing significant property damage and injury.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, nobody in the initial attack has died (although a woman and five-year old girl remain in critical condition), nor were killed in the riot. But it's still a highly disturbing occurrence. Things like this are basically unknown in Ireland, and while the potential for spontaneous acts of school violence is harder to predict, that there are enough people with that ideological hatred in communication with each other to act in such numbers and with such response time... It's disturbing, and I fear we may not have seen the last of it if we do not react quickly and proportionally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T14:45:49-08:00","id":1525935,"title":"","content":"Saw Ridley Scott's Napoleon... Man, they weren't kidding when they said this movie is historically inaccurate. Hopefully, this is another Kingdom of Heaven scenario where I will like the lengthier Directors Cut far more than the theatrical release.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it isn't so much the fudging of history and various details that bothers me so much about this film. It's that I still have no idea what exactly Ridley Scott's take on Napoleon actually is. The film ends with this numerical list of people who had been killed during his reign but Napoleon wasn't portrayed as a bloodthirsty (well... he was thirsty in other ways, though) despot during the movie. But the movie also didn't sell the idealized image of Napoleon (which is what enabled him to raise an army for the Waterloo battle). The battles looked cool, sure. But I feel like the movie missed some crucial aspects of what allowed Napoleon to be the big figure he turned out to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T11:46:32-08:00","id":1525970,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not shocked that Hollywood takes creative liberties with history Knightingale, it\u2019s an old practice and it won\u2019t change anytime soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T13:17:50-08:00","id":1525972,"title":"","content":"Humans have been taking creative liberties with history since we started the idea of keeping track of history. I always get confused when people complain about dramatized works of art not being historically accurate.<br /> <br /> That said, I think Knightinggale's complaint is more important: Taking liberties for the sake of a good story and stronger characterizations is one thing. Taking liberties that don't really make the story more compelling than watching a more accurate historical piece is off-putting. Being accurate has its place, as does being dramatic, but accomplishing neither is a waste of the audience's time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T14:21:52-08:00","id":1525978,"title":"","content":"That is the problem when trying to make a movie of a larger then life historical figure is that you can only cover so much details about them. IE Oliver Stone\u2019s Alexander The Great left out much of his rise to power and Ridley Scott would have the same issues. You can never get a sastfied feeling about watching a adaptation on the big screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T14:32:14-08:00","id":1525980,"title":"","content":"Given how many beloved movies are about fictionalized versions of real historical figures... I'm not sure the idea that somehow cinema can't do it (despite a huge body of successes on stage and the small screen as well) really holds up. Clearly people get entertainment satisfaction out of this genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T14:35:31-08:00","id":1525981,"title":"","content":"&quot;Based on a true story&quot; has always been a license to take a lot of liberties with what actually happened in Hollywood-movies. There are some scenarios where fudging the truth gets really egregious (like the Oscar-winning <a href=\"https://www.vox.com/culture/23832310/michael-oher-blind-side-adoption-tuohy-white-savior\" target=\"_blank\">Blindside-movie</a>) but overall... as long as the story's good, why not? But with that liberty, you need to have an answer to what you're trying to say. The thing about the theatrical version of the Napoleon movie is that I don't see any kind of interpretation of Napoleon. The movie emphasizes the Josephine relationship but I don't think it ends up feeling as meaningful as the movie believes it is.<br /> <br /> I like the longer Director's Cut version of Kingdom of Heaven but that doesn't excuse the fact that the theatrical cut version sucks.<br /> <br /> Also, beyond the historical inaccuracies, I wonder how able people without deep knowledge of Napoleon's history are to follow the movie. This movie really is attempting to zoom through the entire career of Napolean from Robespierre's Reign of Terror to Napoleon's eventual exile to St. Helena. That's... a lot of ground to cover, to put it mildly. Maybe the 4 hour version will be better, maybe not. I guess, we'll see...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T23:01:59-08:00","id":1525993,"title":"","content":"Reflecting on bonaparte I have to consider the limitation of movies as a medium with someone like him....I mean you could a film our the average Tuesday for napoleon.<br /> Perhaps a multi season hbo series could do him justice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-27-2023, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T02:13:26-08:00","id":1525995,"title":"","content":"There's been a rumor for a while now that Spielberg plans to revive Stanley Kubrick's version of a Napoleon-movie but as a limited series instead. A series would certainly work better to illustrate Napoleon's life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T09:48:35-08:00","id":1526011,"title":"","content":"I always felt that doing historical nonfiction or densely written novels like Dune worked better as a limited series to get the most out it for fans or people who are curious enough to want to learn more about the subject matter. IE Oliver Stone got me interested into reading more about Alexander The Great when he did the movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T10:16:44-08:00","id":1526012,"title":"","content":"These days I'm more interested in historical nonfiction, to be honest. The last couple years I've been listening to the <a href=\"https://podbay.fm/p/the-age-of-napoleon-podcast\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Napoleon</a> podcast, for example. Especially like that rather than just explaining the historical events surrounding Napoleon, you will have standalone-episodes like recently about what the administrative state under Napoleon was like and what Napoleon's relationship to sponsoring art was like. Or there was one about the different types of cavalry in the French military and how they compared to the other militaries in Europe at the time. Really interesting podcast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T17:25:02-08:00","id":1526092,"title":"","content":"Myself I have been reading more historical fiction books lately with Conn Iggudian being my current favorite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T08:49:05-08:00","id":1526112,"title":"","content":"Look. I know I'm a middle-aged white man with a buzzed haircut working a low-training job, and I know that sends certain unfortunate signals to people who see me. Maybe some of this is my fault; I <i>should</i> quit whinging about how much I enjoy the cost saved and the convenience of my hairstyle. I'm just saying I wish other middle-aged white men with bad haircuts and dead-end jobs would quit feeling comfortable coming up to me and talking to me about how much black people suck like they expect me to agree with them about it.<br /> <br /> ...Actually, if I'm wishing for a magical outcome that costs me basically nothing, maybe I should be a bit less selfish and wish instead that those people learn to be better, kinder humans. Yeah, pretend that was my point this whole time instead of me moaning about having uncomfortable conversations with people I dislike. Gosh, I wish I could go back and edit this post somehow to make me look like a less shallow, less inward-obsessed person, but alas, I don't know how to do that. I'm not good with computers. Add that to the list of things I'm venting about!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T08:52:39-08:00","id":1526113,"title":"","content":"Worst part of job-hunting is that I have to grow my hair out so I don't get mistaken for a skinhead. I miss being bald, my hairline is reminiscent of Dracula.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T10:35:48-08:00","id":1526120,"title":"","content":"Job hunting is the worst as you are waiting around hoping that your application is noticed and you will get a call or email that they want to talk to you or hire you on the spot. Applying is easy to do on any given day. It's the waiting that gets to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T11:40:02-08:00","id":1526191,"title":"","content":"Waiting? Nah, that\u2019s easy; just do something else while checking your contact method periodically.<br /> <br /> <br /> The worst part of job-hunting is the damned <u>interview process</u>. The whole thing is a thinly veiled attempt by a cadre of insular, tribalistic cretins to screen anyone who isn\u2019t sharing their particular set of idiosyncrasies out of any jobs. They invent newer and more idiotic questions about utterly irrelevant nonsense which has no bearing on the job itself or the work you\u2019ll presumably be doing, all just to find an excuse to weed you out for not being (x)* enough.<br /> <br /> And during this interview process, they\u2019ll waste your time by revealing they\u2019ve misrepresented the very job you applied for, probably because it\u2019s work no one would seek out if they knew what they\u2019d actually be doing. This is especially bad in white-collar sectors where they try to disguise a gopher or toadie as something important or enticing. Or when they like to inform you that the job is actually part-time or something less than what you were looking for.<br /> <br /> They\u2019ll also take this time to dash any hopes that whatever benefit or perk you were pursuing was actually a part of the job you applied for by informing you of a series of caveats. Like the 90-day wait for any sort of health benefit that seems to have become the universal corporate standard. That period of time is perfect for them to find piddling fault with whatever you\u2019re doing so they can fire you.<br /> <br /> <br /> (*Whereas \u201cX\u201d is a value of superficial quality used to discriminate others, one that could be worth a lawsuit if you had the resources/time.)<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T15:01:08-08:00","id":1526211,"title":"","content":"Yes the interview process is hard to go through as you got to wear outfits that you normally don't dress in and listen to them ask at times pointless questions, but I'm not looking for white collar jobs as I don't have the patience to deal with bs at that level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-30-2024, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T13:44:32-08:00","id":1526250,"title":"","content":"It's great that you have a give-out early in the morning, but I got to do the pick-ups on the morning and I need the van; you need your donnars; I know, you've got millions in your charity's bank-account; maybe you can spring for another van or a truck, maybe. And no, stores aren't going to wait until the afternoon; they want use there early in the morning to get rid of it. And no, it's going to be a van-load, your homeless-helper guy with the ankle-bracelet monitor, it won't fit in his pick-up truck. Needless to say I filled the van all the way up with about sixty-boxes I reckon. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1526112#post1526112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look. I know I'm a middle-aged white man with a buzzed haircut working a low-training job, and I know that sends certain unfortunate signals to people who see me. Maybe some of this is my fault; I <i>should</i> quit whinging about how much I enjoy the cost saved and the convenience of my hairstyle. I'm just saying I wish other middle-aged white men with bad haircuts and dead-end jobs would quit feeling comfortable coming up to me and talking to me about how much black people suck like they expect me to agree with them about it.<br /> <br /> ...Actually, if I'm wishing for a magical outcome that costs me basically nothing, maybe I should be a bit less selfish and wish instead that those people learn to be better, kinder humans. Yeah, pretend that was my point this whole time instead of me moaning about having uncomfortable conversations with people I dislike. Gosh, I wish I could go back and edit this post somehow to make me look like a less shallow, less inward-obsessed person, but alas, I don't know how to do that. I'm not good with computers. Add that to the list of things I'm venting about!</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're middle-aged and work a low-training, job, where you're on your feet, using your muscles, you're actually better off than most guys your age. health-wise. When I as a kid, my uncles were middle-aged and when I thought I was older, I'd be doing, &quot;Old-Guy&quot;, things like smoking, drinking, sitting around the bar gaining weight and watching sports.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T13:33:54-08:00","id":1526290,"title":"","content":"I see that the new look for Davros for Dr. Who has got people upset and I can see why as he had a good look and that even in a life support wheelchair and one working arm to assist him. he has more then enough power to make him a serious danger to all intelligent life and the fact that he has such physical limitations is all the more impressive in because of it.<br /> <br /> You can add even Darth Vader to the list as his body is more machine then flesh and he can\u2019t reach his full force powers didn\u2019t prevent him from being one of the most dangerous persons in the galaxy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-03-2023, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T14:01:49-08:00","id":1526292,"title":"","content":"Steven Moffat certainly overstayed his welcome with some of his ticks with the Capaldi-Doctor (although there were some truly great episodes during the Peter Capaldi Doctor run) and I was ready to get something new... but man, didn't like Chris Chibnall's direction for Doctor Who - at all. It wasn't Jodi Whitaker or any of the actors for that matter, it was the writing! That &quot;multiple companions&quot;-bit rarely worked, for example. And so I'm glad we had a switch in direction so soon again because I liked these two episodes so far with David Tennant coming back.<br /> <br /> Although it is pretty obvious nostalgia-bait to bring Tennant back for a season...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T23:02:22-08:00","id":1526344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1526290#post1526290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that the new look for Davros for Dr. Who has got people upset and I can see why as he had a good look and that even in a life support wheelchair and one working arm to assist him. he has more then enough power to make him a serious danger to all intelligent life and the fact that he has such physical limitations is all the more impressive in because of it.<br /> <br /> You can add even Darth Vader to the list as his body is more machine then flesh and he can\u2019t reach his full force powers didn\u2019t prevent him from being one of the most dangerous persons in the galaxy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno if it was a 'good' look, he looked like a exceptionally belligerent prune crossed with a dalek. But then again daleks don't exactly look menacing it's more how they're written.<br /> <br /> I dont really think the new look was needed and it reeks of divesity as envisioned by the (white, upper middle class) brass at the bbc but it's less cringey that the timeless child retcon and Dr who is historically hit and miss.<br /> <br /> Personally I always felt he outstayed his welcome following genesis of the daleks. Having them play second fiddle to an physically frail lunatic witn bad ideas which blow up in his face didn't feel right.<br /> <br /> Edit-all that said davros' classic style is a useful visual between the nazi human like aliens and the daleks as a missing link of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-05-2023, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T04:19:42-08:00","id":1526349,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to worry about how online I am.<br /> <br /> I just woke up from a dream. I was reading a Superman comic, and in it, some woman was crying for Superman's help because a woman had been menstruating in public. In the comic, this was depicted by the offender hiking one leg up onto the rim of a public fountain like Commander Riker used to do to Data and Wesley, then firing three bloody tampons out of her skirt like grapeshot from a shotgun. In my dream, I was pealing gales of horrified, hysterical laughter, and I needed to know whether the events being depicted were a hoax to lure Superman into some kind of trap or if the entire creative team--writer, artist, and editor--all thought that was how menstruation works, in which case I <b>needed</b> to make a Twitter account so I could submit this to Men Writing Women. I remember thinking that if I did submit it, I would get such a rush from the attention and admiration my discovery would garner.<br /> <br /> That seems worrisome. None of those ideas (except Superman; I love Superman and could build a career as a Superman scholar if there was a market for it) should be so deeply ingrained in my mind that I'd have dreams about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum