:03-08:00","id":1528434,"title":"","content":"I have the strangest feeling that my best friend and I are going to end like Stattler &amp; Waldorf from the Muppets when we retire and I hope our local theatre has a great balcony for us.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T12:45:50-08:00","id":1529730,"title":"","content":"I'm hearing a lot of comments in the pub about some deleted article about how endemic harrasment is in the rpg industry/community. Anyone know much about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T12:44:04-08:00","id":1529765,"title":"","content":"It's the first I've heard of it Ragged Robin. I know Wizards Of The Coast was laying off staff in recent weeks and I know long term players are not fond of some the changes made to some of the lore as somebody views some of it problematic because of political or idealogical reasons.<br /> <br /> I've also heard and I hope that this is not the case. Major publishing groups are turning away possible writers if they are white, straight and male and my first thought is how is that tied to my skills at writing a story in general? If this happening then what the future in writing will hold if it's not merit but what category you check off be it political, sexual orientation, skin color or gender that gets you a writing job then the future of the industry is not so hot looking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-31-2024, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T15:20:15-08:00","id":1529775,"title":"","content":"They\u2019re trying to emphasize diversity. But I agree, being white, straight and male is one possible facet in a truly diverse diversity and should not be entirely overlooked simply because of affirmative action. But neither should it be promoted or favored either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T17:34:13-08:00","id":1529782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1529775#post1529775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019re trying to emphasize diversity. But I agree, being white, straight and male is one possible facet in a truly diverse diversity and should not be entirely overlooked simply because of affirmative action. But neither should it be promoted or favored either.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why I'm hoping it's not true as I have heard about some freelance writers who submissions have been rejected for being simply a straight white male and nothing else. Also some questions seemed to verge on intruding on personal information.<br /> <br /> Sorry Mr. Publisher, but my skin color, gender, sexual orientation and what I believe in my personal life is not your business and doesn't have any bearing on my skill as a writer.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T17:43:13-08:00","id":1529783,"title":"","content":"On a different matter I wish entertainment would put away the woest me trope. In which the character makes a choice they later regret and given the chance to change there fate and decide to make the same choice anyway.<br /> <br /> Examples of this include Piper Haliwell from Charmed wishing she could have a normal life without demons and warlocks dropping for a quick fight and tea. She and her sisters were given away out of there life and they in the end choose retain their powers. And she whines about in the final few seasons about her choice and I'm thinking you gave up all rights to a normal life when you were given a choice to walk away. You can't have it both ways people.<br /> <br /> So what tropes do you wish that they would stop doing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-02T03:29:21-08:00","id":1529850,"title":"","content":"Feeling kind of moody today","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-02T12:42:07-08:00","id":1529862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1529850#post1529850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeling kind of moody today</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the feeling quite well when I see myself falling into the same hubris that I will judge others on comments or bad takes on things that interest me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T11:35:07-08:00","id":1529924,"title":"","content":"I feel sometimes that basic research skills seem to be a lost art for people of the 21st century as I lost count of the mistakes of the lore in the Sucide Squad game and seeing what looks like a revolver ejecting a spent casing and as someone who uses those types of guns at a shooting range on a regular basis, I was wtf is that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T20:20:26-08:00","id":1529955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1529924#post1529924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel sometimes that basic research skills seem to be a lost art for people of the 21st century as I lost count of the mistakes of the lore in the Sucide Squad game and seeing what looks like a revolver ejecting a spent casing and as someone who uses those types of guns at a shooting range on a regular basis, I was wtf is that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Suicide Squad is a mess on almost every level. It's a shame too, because Rocksteady produced one of the best video game trilogies of all time. I guess it goes to show that no matter how good the studio, they'll eventually start churning out garbage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T20:28:15-08:00","id":1529957,"title":"","content":"I'm getting annoyed at seeing commercials in my subscription services. One of the big reasons I dropped cable and moved to subscriptions was to get away from commercials. The worst part is, many recent shows aren't even created with the idea of commercial breaks, so when they add them in, the commercials will sometimes cut into the middle of a scene, or even into the middle of a conversation.<br /> <br /> Netflix managed to single-handedly reduce media piracy by a massive amount, since most people don't mind spending money, provided they get a decent experience. But now with the way so many companies are making their own subscription services and then raising prices while adding in commercials on top, you're seeing media piracy come roaring back.<br /> <br /> Also, as a bit of a related topic, I just canceled my Amazon Prime membership, which I've had for close to 20 years. The quality of Amazon has dropped off dramatically recently. So much stuff on there is just badly made knock-offs, or worse. I ordered a present for a friend for Christmas and got a box with a block of wood in it. I had to spent almost a month fighting with Amazon before they finally agreed to give me a refund. And then they keep increasing the cost of their Prime in order to fund their movie and show library and they're going to make me sit through commercials if I want to watch that stuff. I'm so done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T21:40:22-08:00","id":1529962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1529924#post1529924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel sometimes that basic research skills seem to be a lost art for people of the 21st century as I lost count of the mistakes of the lore in the Sucide Squad game and seeing what looks like a revolver ejecting a spent casing and as someone who uses those types of guns at a shooting range on a regular basis, I was wtf is that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, I liked it more than Gotham Knights. The traversal felt good with most of the characters and the story was interesting (well, the beginning at least.... the second half less so). But man, the live-service-stuff... At this point, there's like a 99% chance you will kill the soul of any game by making it one of these &quot;live-service&quot;-games. Unless it's an actual dedicated MMO, it hasn't helped any game to move to that model.<br /> <br /> I returned it on Steam and just watched the story on YT because the missions already started getting boring at the beginning. And I'm so glad... The game's story burdens you with multiple &quot;escort-missions&quot; during the latter half. Escort-missions are just such tedium... Thank god, I've only had to watch it on YT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T12:35:16-08:00","id":1529977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1529955#post1529955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Suicide Squad is a mess on almost every level. It's a shame too, because Rocksteady produced one of the best video game trilogies of all time. I guess it goes to show that no matter how good the studio, they'll eventually start churning out garbage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rocksteady isn't the same place anymore as most of the staff and some of the execs that were key into making the Batman Arkham games a hit are no longer involved with the company and are left with people who were not involved and seemed that that they couldn't bothered to learn the lore.<br /> <br /> That was my big issue with the game on how they handled the characters and most gamers hated the fact that the game was freeze up at any moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T12:41:16-08:00","id":1529978,"title":"","content":"It seems that knowing the difference between hate speach and speaches that you hate seem to have been lost if I was to go by the folks of social media comments. Anyone else noticed this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T13:19:30-08:00","id":1530048,"title":"","content":"I had to spend the last 6 hours calling around to every clinic and ER in town before I finally found one that accepts my shitty insurance and it's about 60 miles away. It's good I wasn't bleeding out or anything. Hopefully that ER isn't packed because I don't fancy sitting there for 8+ hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T14:59:05-08:00","id":1530209,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to dislike phone interviews now. So I'm getting a interview and if I do well and I get the chance for a in person interview and who thought this was a good idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T12:15:57-08:00","id":1530305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1530209#post1530209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to dislike phone interviews now. So I'm getting a interview and if I do well and I get the chance for a in person interview and who thought this was a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to that; a bunch of insular nepotists set to screen out anyone from work who isn't JUST like themselves. It's never been about getting the job done, they usually just dump more responsibilities on current employees without extra pay for that. Of course then they create vacancies in those positions because nobody wants extra work without more pay, leading to more need for applicants they won't hire without a gun to their head. And they wonder why their employee base never stabilizes.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> I\u2019m past tired of all the economics double-talk in the media. I read in the news constantly about the supposedly buoying economy here in the US, but nothing they gibber about has unraveled any of the difficulty for anyone working-class one iota. We still get laid off and furloughed, looking for a new job is still an obnoxious ordeal, not a single one of us receives a pay raise, and none of our benefits expand. And I\u2019m willing to bet that the prices for all goods and services, <i>already inflated beyond sense</i>, will increase yet again in response to all this so-called prosperity.<br /> <br /> They like to talk about jobs added to the mix, but none of those jobs are ever nearby, and they are almost universally jobs you CAN NOT make a living off of. Ultimately it looks like all this squawking about market status only ever affects the investors, shareholders, CEOs, and other bastards behind desks who never actually work. All the rest of us apparently don\u2019t matter as we never see any positive effect from any of this alleged good news.<br /> <br /> These petty despots worry about things like domestic terrorist organizations springing up and growing unrest, <b>especially</b> during an election year, but maybe that wouldn\u2019t be a problem if they\u2019d quit holding our lives hostage by destroying any job security for the sake of their own greed. It certainly doesn\u2019t help to hand over all applications to some computer programmed to screen out every possible external applicant so you can hold out for an internal hire. And a multi-tier interview process just indicates that you didn't want to hire anyone in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T05:02:18-08:00","id":1530434,"title":"","content":"It's still insane to me that it seems Warner Bros/Discovery has now for a second time decided to just delete a movie for tax-purposes rather than release it.<br /> <br /> From <a href=\"https://www.thewrap.com/coyote-vs-acme-update-offers-warner-bros/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;The Final Days of \u2018Coyote vs. Acme\u2019: Offers, Rejections and a Roadrunner Race Against Time&quot;</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Warner Bros., reacting to the hubbub, walked back its initial decision. Instead of canceling the movie outright, the studio would give the filmmakers the chance to shop it around. If another studio wanted to pick it up, they could.<br /> <br /> Now, months later, Warner Bros. had had enough. The call to DeFaria made that crystal clear.<br /> <br /> With Warner Bros. Discovery\u2019s fourth quarter earnings call scheduled for Feb. 23, \u201cCoyote vs. Acme\u201d is running out of time. Many on the film\u2019s team feel that the studio will use the ending of the quarter to get the movie off the books for good. \u201cCoyote vs. Acme\u201d is running up against something worse than a tunnel painted into the side of a mountain or a falling anvil. It will finally be silenced by a movie studio\u2019s balance sheet.<br /> <br /> In a truly inglorious end, a source close to the movie doesn\u2019t believe Warner Bros. would even announce that they hadn\u2019t found a home for the movie. They would unceremoniously delete it. Never to be seen again. </div> </div> </div>Imagine spending years working on a movie and then some bean-counter just deletes the whole thing because it looks good on a balance sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T05:11:35-08:00","id":1530435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1530434#post1530434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine spending years working on a movie and then some bean-counter just deletes the whole thing because it looks good on a balance sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know! It's so crazy to me! What's makes even less sense to me is them scrubbing whole movies and shows from streaming that have already been released! How can they do that!?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T05:21:35-08:00","id":1530436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1530435#post1530435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know! It's so crazy to me! What's makes even less sense to me is them scrubbing whole movies and shows from streaming that have already been released! How can they do that!?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, we know why they do that. You delete the already existing ones because you don't want to pay residuals to the people involved in the movies/shows. But of course, that's a decision purely driven by money/greed. Because in every other regard, it makes no sense. For example, why would you make your streaming-platform less appealing by removing content from it that could persuade people to sign up to the platform? It's really all about short-term financial gain.<br /> <br /> There's only one group that is satisfied and it's the only group that matters to these people: the shareholders. And the shareholders only care about one thing: The line has to go up. And it doesn't matter why the line goes up. Good movies, bad movies, good TV-shows, bad TV-shows, a user-friendly platform or an inaccessible one... none of that matters. Just as long as the line goes up. And hey, if it means deleting movies and turning them into tax-write-offs, who cares? Just as long as the line keeps going up...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T12:22:12-08:00","id":1530466,"title":"","content":"If we had politicians that could even work together for a simple feel-good publicity stunt of a bill, they would just pass a law requiring any media that's discontinued for tax reasons would have to be submitted to the Library of Congress (or appropriate body in other countries) and then made public domain. Our reduction in tax revenue should be getting us something out of all this, and the bottom line chasers aren't directly impacted by it (nor does it actually help creatives financially).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T11:17:01-08:00","id":1530571,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s nothing new about canceling movies after they been made. They canceled the Batgirl movie even though test audiences gave it a 60% approval rating and it showed that they had a good foundation to work from and there was no issues on the set. It was a financial choice to put it into limbo. I should add for greater context for audience reaction. Top Gun Maverick had a 90% approval rating with test audiences and the Birds of Prey movie had a 30% approval rating and with Batgirl being 60+% in test audience reactions. It certainly showed that with some fine tuning that Warner Bros could have a good commerical success if they went that route and having a &quot;normal&quot; street level crime involving Barbara Gordon chasing after Firefly for his crimes and the person who put him up to it would have made a nice break from the world ending threats that we have been getting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-14-2024, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T12:51:46-08:00","id":1530578,"title":"","content":"Movies have been canceled mid-production before or even towards the end of production. What's new is that with both Batgirl and Coyote vs Acme, we're talking about <i>finished </i>movies. Not only are they finished but there's nothing wrong with them. Once you put them out to the world, critics will have their say about the virtues and flaws to various degrees, I'm sure. But the movie-studio gave money to people to produce a movie, those people produced a movie and then presumably the movie-studio would release said movie. The new thing is the uncertainty that what Batgirl and Coyote vs Acme suggest is that you can go through this whole process of making a movie and making it ready for release but at the last minute it can just get canceled. What's also troubling is that Coyote vs Acme demonstrates that the movie itself, the produced piece of art, is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Here's from the article about Coyote vs Acme I linked before:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What made the situation even more appalling is that, according to a source close to the project, the four Warner Bros. executives responsible for making this decision \u2013 CEOs and co-chairpersons of Warner Bros. Motion Picture Group Michael De Luca and Pam Abdy, along with Warner Bros. Pictures Animation president Bill Damaschke and embattled CEO and president of Warner Bros. Discovery David Zaslav \u2013 hadn\u2019t even seen the finished version of the movie.<br /> <br /> Zaslav never saw the movie at all. De Luca and Abdy saw a \u201cdirector\u2019s cut,\u201d and Damaschke saw the first audience preview. Significantly, \u201cCoyote vs. Acme\u201d was developed and greenlit by a previous regime; the only executive that worked on the movie that is still at the company is Jesse Ehrman. These executives, who trumpet a filmmaker-first approach and have recently signed big deals with directors like Ryan Coogler and Paul Thomas Anderson (who conspicuously made their deals after the filmmaker-led backlash to Warner Bros. had subsided), were apparently prepared to trash a movie that they\u2019d never even watched.<br /> <br /> Even so, the reason for \u201cCoyote vs. Acme\u2019s\u201d cancellation remains damnably unknowable \u2013 even to those who made the movie. Publicly, Warner Bros. blamed the decision on a shifting \u201cglobal strategy to focus on theatrical releases\u201d and initially indicated it would take a tax write-off on the film, which is based on a New Yorker article by Ian Frazier from 1990. The problem, it seemed, was the movie was not strong enough for a theatrical release, and didn\u2019t fit anyone\u2019s streaming strategy in the WBD universe. </div> </div> </div>And here's when Batgirl is mentioned:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there was a precedent. When Warner Bros. announced that \u201cBatgirl,\u201d a $90 million superhero movie based on a beloved DC Comics property, would be deleted from existence, a new avenue opened up for the studio. According to a source close to \u201cCoyote vs. Acme,\u201d getting rid of a wholly finished movie became \u201can acceptable means of dealing with a problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> When they weren\u2019t sure what to do with \u201cCoyote vs. Acme\u201d \u2014 which originally had a release date later claimed by \u201cBarbie\u201d \u2014 the option to simply disappear it was taken, at least for a few days.<br /> <br /> What makes the situation with \u201cCoyote vs. Acme\u201d more baffling is that unlike \u201cBatgirl,\u201d the film consistently received great scores from test audiences. Several Warner Bros. executives have gone out of their way to claim that \u201cBatgirl\u201d was un-releasable; that simply wasn\u2019t the case with \u201cCoyote vs. Acme.\u201d\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T13:33:18-08:00","id":1530587,"title":"","content":"While cancelling finished movies does have a long history...it used to be something that only happened because the movie was somehow so bad people that made it were actively fighting to ensure it never got released (ex: Jerry Lewis and <i>The Day the Clown Cried</i>) or legal reasons (ex: The Stoker estate suing to get original <i>Nosferatu</i> pulled from theaters for copyright infringement). The dominate mindset for most of cinema's history has been that it's better to put out a dud and try to make back whatever money you can, than not release a movie after the considerable amount of outlay it takes to make one.<br /> <br /> With the changes in various economic factors, it's more profitable (for the C-suite folks and large shareholders with the ultimate power here, not necessarily the long term health of their companies, employees, or the services society pays them to provide) to simply delete films as detailed above. To hammer on the point a bit more, the &quot;new&quot; thing is that cancelling a movie is now based on extremely short term speculative profit influences that are very divorced from even the process of ensuring you have a healthy company next year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T20:46:10-08:00","id":1530609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1530587#post1530587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To hammer on the point a bit more, the &quot;new&quot; thing is that cancelling a movie is now based on extremely short term speculative profit influences that are very divorced from even the process of ensuring you have a healthy company next year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is a major ongoing issue, not just with movie companies, but with many others as well. Look at Boeing, which at one time was considered one of the safest, most reliable companies in the world. But then new leadership decided to chase short term profits and the cost of long term safety and stability. Every quarter they need to boost profits, which means cutting more and more corners, to the point that the company looks like it's going to implode, or at least be largely replaced by Airbus in the future. The thing is though, the leadership doesn't care because they'll be out the door before the company runs into huge problems.<br /> <br /> It used to be that the companies tended to keep the same CEOs for decades, and that ensured that those CEOs were interested in thinking about the long-term profitability of the company, but that seems to largely be a thing of the past. Now it's better to just focus on short term profits and when the company runs into financial difficulties buy out another company, spin off all the loans and losses onto that second company, then have that second company declare bankruptcy and the leadership can bail out with golden parachutes.<br /> <br /> We need to start pushing for heavier regulations of industry and corporate finances to encourage businesses to focus on long-term gains rather than short-term ones, because short sighted greed is not good for the long-term stability of an economy, or of a country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T23:37:12-08:00","id":1530613,"title":"","content":"While perhaps overly simplistic, we really could fix this by going back to having real wealth taxes for both rich people and rich companies.<br /> <br /> By taxing wealth, you disincentivize hoarding it (since hoarding wealth is a great way to get more wealth thanks to dividends and buybacks and so on), and adjust the profit calculus back to more reinvestment in the actual companies and their products as the main sources of profit for the folks at the top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T04:34:42-08:00","id":1530799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1530436#post1530436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, we know why they do that. You delete the already existing ones because you don't want to pay residuals to the people involved in the movies/shows. But of course, that's a decision purely driven by money/greed. Because in every other regard, it makes no sense. For example, why would you make your streaming-platform less appealing by removing content from it that could persuade people to sign up to the platform? It's really all about short-term financial gain.<br /> <br /> There's only one group that is satisfied and it's the only group that matters to these people: the shareholders. And the shareholders only care about one thing: The line has to go up. And it doesn't matter why the line goes up. Good movies, bad movies, good TV-shows, bad TV-shows, a user-friendly platform or an inaccessible one... none of that matters. Just as long as the line goes up. And hey, if it means deleting movies and turning them into tax-write-offs, who cares? Just as long as the line keeps going up...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know! And I think it's pretty messed up! It's just so crazy to me they can even do that, especially for things that are finished and have already been released.<br /> <br /> But I know, they only care about money, and money in the short term. It's crazy...<br /> <br /> And sorry being a bit late to the discussion. Everyone has made some great points!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T11:34:01-08:00","id":1530832,"title":"","content":"It's time to bring back the cocaine-fueled Hollywood-guys from yesteryear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vkc5-RI39Ho\" data-code=\"Vkc5-RI39Ho\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Vkc5-RI39Ho/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T12:51:09-08:00","id":1530837,"title":"","content":"Oh My God SCTV brings back memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T12:55:02-08:00","id":1530838,"title":"","content":"The sad thing is perhaps Hollywood may not be able to change course with all the choices they made. Critical Drinker recently did a video on how insane the budgets are for Hollywood movies and how hard it is to break even and let alone make a profit as the old guard are retiring and the replacements are very inexperienced and at times seem unwilling to learn from their mistakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T13:52:56-08:00","id":1530846,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hollywood&quot; isn't going to change on it's own, because it's not controlled by people that are actually involved in making movies (this is true across lots of industries now). Even directors and producers can't fix things if the megacorps that decide on who gets money decide nobody that's trying to fix it gets money to do so.<br /> <br /> The problem is eminently fixable. Even with lots of &quot;old guard&quot; retiring (keep in mind that cinema isn't exactly that old as an art form most of the old guard figured most things out the hard away as it was). The problem isn't getting fixed because the people with the power to enable it (they don't even have to do it, just get out of the way) don't want to make a few million less dollars a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T02:45:42-08:00","id":1530885,"title":"","content":"Aye, we saw that with the discussions around the strikes last year as well. Especially if you look at how the movie-studios/execs talked about AI during those negotiations... They were salivating at the prospect of replacing all background-actors with AI-powered CGI, for example. And there already have been precedents of &quot;reviving&quot; dead actors using CGI. Not that it will make movies better. We've already seen with the overreliance on CGI and green-screen, you rarely get something visually stunning like an Avatar II and instead, you get the overworked assembly-line-factories that give us these crappy-looking Marvel-movies.<br /> <br /> Also, CGI blood has never once looked good...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T13:06:54-08:00","id":1530922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1530846#post1530846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hollywood&quot; isn't going to change on it's own, because it's not controlled by people that are actually involved in making movies (this is true across lots of industries now). Even directors and producers can't fix things if the megacorps that decide on who gets money decide nobody that's trying to fix it gets money to do so.<br /> <br /> The problem is eminently fixable. Even with lots of &quot;old guard&quot; retiring (keep in mind that cinema isn't exactly that old as an art form most of the old guard figured most things out the hard away as it was). The problem isn't getting fixed because the people with the power to enable it (they don't even have to do it, just get out of the way) don't want to make a few million less dollars a year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes Critical Drinker mentioned some of what you said of how things can be easily solved, but it would require a big change in the mindset with the people in charge as you also mentioned and is &quot;Hollywood&quot; willing to do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T14:18:29-08:00","id":1530931,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can really talk about &quot;Hollywood&quot; as a monolith like that (at least unless you want to go rather far back in the history of movies). There are lots of different people involved, which means lots of different competing interests, and different levels of controls over the process","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T12:09:13-08:00","id":1530998,"title":"","content":"There are some differences between what streaming-services want from the movie-industry compared to the studios who are still invested in the older model of releasing movies in theaters. But the whole streaming-service has been built on sand from the beginning. I think one of the aspects about streaming-services that has helped them is that there's no third party who is checking their numbers. For example, when that movie with Dwayne &quot;The Rock&quot; Johnson, Ryan Reynolds and Gal Gadot came out called Red Notice Netflix hailed it as this great success (and there's even supposed to be a Red Notice 2 at some point, I believe). According to Netflix it was one of their most-watched movies. But the basis for those numbers was just Netflix saying &quot;Trust me, bro.&quot;. So, sure, these streaming-services are certainly striving to not have to compete with theaters when it comes to releases but who knows how long it will last... It's amazing it has lasted this long despite the sheen of fakery that all these Netflix-movies have (there's no way releasing something as forgettable as that Gal Gadot vehicle called Heart of Stone that gets released on streaming Day 1 is part of a sustainable business-model) but at some point that bubble is gonna burst... unless they're able to cut corners and keep things going with things like cheap AI-trickery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T11:43:41-08:00","id":1531030,"title":"","content":"I swear to fuck all of these thumbnails I have to see in my recommendations for videos of people whinging about this Madame Web movie. I do not give a shit about all of these people who are definitely sincerely passionate about some incidental Spider-Man character (and yet, somehow didn't seem to produce nearly so many videos so hung up on the Morbius movie, despite how much of an actual joke it became).<br /> <br /> Why am I even getting these, I haven't even watched anything movie related in months.<br /> <br /> (That's a rhetorical question, I'm well aware of why the algorithm eagerly soaks up and spreads around these particular kinds of pitiful crybaby videos)<br /> <br /> Just stop bothering me while I'm trying to scroll around looking for the latest variation on assembled Hazbin Hotel clips.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T02:04:10-08:00","id":1531050,"title":"","content":"The funniest part is that just as superhero-movies seem to be on the downslope in terms of public engagement and people are just getting tired of the endless stream of Marvel-movies, Sony is tripling down on its whole &quot;Spiderverse&quot;-superhero-stuff. Just look at <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sony&#39;s_Spider-Man_Universe#Future\" target=\"_blank\">the &quot;Future&quot;-section for this project on Wikipedia</a>. In this year alone we're getting two (!) more of these Sony-Spiderverse movies: Kraven the Hunter (from the way the trailer looks it's going to be a fitting companion-piece for Morbius and Madame Web) and Venom 3 (I think as long as Sony is willing Tom Hardy is gonna make Venom-movies for the rest of his life the way he's invested in making those movies). And then you get this huge list of &quot;planned movies&quot;.<br /> <br /> Then again, maybe it will just end up like the so-called &quot;Dark Universe&quot; from Universal... another failed attempt (more like <i>attempts</i>, plural, actually...) at a cinematic universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T11:38:18-08:00","id":1531064,"title":"","content":"I only watched Jesterbells review of Madam Web who called it one of those type of films that is so bad that\u2019s it\u2019s funny and mentioned the fact of why make a big budget film on a unknown Spider-man character that most people never heard of unless your a superfan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T06:14:13-08:00","id":1531108,"title":"","content":"Saw the True Detective Season 4 finale and well, I thought it was okay while watching but man... as a mystery, it's one of those shows where the plot makes less sense the more you think about it. And while I liked that the season brought back some of the creepiness from season 1, this season has some truly supernatural moments with no logical explanation.<br /> <br /> And what made me always roll my eyes were the hamfisted references to season 1. For example, one of the characters is related to one of the main-characters from season 1 - for no reason! And then in the last episode, a character even says &quot;Time is a flat circle.&quot; which is a direct quote from what a character says in season 1 during a popular scene (that has turned into a bit of a meme). Why?! It doesn't even make sense for the character in this last episode of season 4 to say that. The only reason to put that in there is so that the writers can point at it and say &quot;See, guys! The guy said the thing from the first season that you guys love so much!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T12:59:00-08:00","id":1531210,"title":"","content":"Saw the teasers for the X-Men cartoon series and already it's looks like it's something to avoid due to the artwork and some of the stuff that the showrunner has already said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T14:13:22-08:00","id":1531383,"title":"","content":"Hi. Sorry I haven\u2019t posted much lately. I got discouraged when you stopped Liking my stuff (though I understand why you did it). Just wanted to let you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https