tom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T13:58:07-08:00","id":1531542,"title":"","content":"I once felt anger towards social justice warriors in the beginging and now I just feel sorry for them as it seems that they are such unhappy folks who need a much healthier outlet. I can totally understand why lots of people are ending Twitter/X, Snapchat and whatever else because of the negativity. I totally see why Lindsey Ellis and Jesterbells have stayed off those channels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T00:21:21-08:00","id":1531602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1531542#post1531542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once felt anger towards social justice warriors in the beginging and now I just feel sorry for them as it seems that they are such unhappy folks who need a much healthier outlet. I can totally understand why lots of people are ending Twitter/X, Snapchat and whatever else because of the negativity. I totally see why Lindsey Ellis and Jesterbells have stayed off those channels.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a social justice hermetic (I'm socially conscious about me) I realised online social justice vs anti social justice is a co-dependant dynamic, often asinine and ultimately counter intuitive. I walked away and do irl politics instead. I do a lot more at defending women at the clinics from the God squad than arguing if orcs are racist.<br /> <br /> Edit-i mean the whole madame Web pushback is obviously a grift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-27-2024, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T11:51:37-08:00","id":1531638,"title":"","content":"Jesterbells had the right take on Madam Web Ragged Robin. It was one of those so bad it's funny films and left it at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T13:26:43-08:00","id":1531644,"title":"","content":"Madame Web does this weird thing where the movie is so hesitant in just getting to the good parts of its premise that it feels like you're watching the boring prequel of another movie that hasn't been made yet. It reminds me of that <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=snfOVpFV0d4\" target=\"_blank\">George Lucas bit from Patton Oswalt</a> mocking the idea of whether you really need to see Darth Vader in the past when he was a little kid. There was this movie Dracula Untold (2014) which was supposed to launch the franchise and so this movie instead of being about Dracula as a vampire, it's a movie about how Dracula became a vampire. Totally unnecessary and uninteresting. Similarly in Madame Web, you have these three teenagers who are destined to become these spider-super-heroes but the movie is essentially about them <i>before </i>they become those superheroes. First of all, it's weird that it's three. Dakota Johnson mentioned that the movie went through some drastic re-writes. Maybe they signed contracts with those three actors because, in that version of the script, that made sense and then they couldn't just boot them again after the script changed. But it's the same issue: There's no need to have a whole movie about those three teens <i>before </i>they become Spider-super-heroes. It also leads to another weird thematic issue with the movie regarding Madame Web's precognition because the movie isn't quite clear on whether it believes in predestination or that individuals can change their fate. Lots of things in the story point to the former belief which is a weird message.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T14:32:45-08:00","id":1531652,"title":"","content":"The problem seems to be that Sony thinks it can just force another &quot;spider-verse&quot; franchise into existence that's competing with the very well received MCU Spider-Man, and the very well received animated Miles Morales focused Spider-Man movies... when they can't use Spider-Man.<br /> <br /> They keep trying to build up all these villians/anti-heroes and supporting cast... without a main character. Whether or not superhero franchises are even a good idea right now, people can forgive a certain amount of &quot;building up a larger film&quot; eating into films if the pay off is something that seems intriguing. What's the pay off with the Venom (who's apparently not even in this universe anymore?), Morbius, Vulture (from the MCU though) and Madame Web? Where is it going? When Fury mentions the Avengers Initiative in Iron Man 1, people starting being very forgiving about some of the &quot;MCU world building&quot; intruding on individual stories because the pay off was getting an Avengers movie at the end of it.. and that worked out pretty well. There's no thread in the stories to follow to see where it leads. It's just, &quot;Spider-Man supporting cast and rogue's gallery characters&quot; going nowhere.<br /> <br /> It's also kinda weird to me because there's a Spider-Man antagonist that's basically been completely ignored for decades outside of the comics, who's big thing is that he can't take Spider-Man out on his own, so he's been behind the scenes manipulating both conflict between Spider-Man and other heroes (or at least potential allies like Morbius), and tormenting Spider-Man by helping a lot of his regular enemies out: the Jackal.<br /> <br /> The Jackal is basically the bad-guy version of Nick Fury for Spider-Man. While he's heavily associated with the much hated Clone Saga, that's skipped a mine-load of stories before that (and him cloning himself to constantly &quot;die&quot; or get captured while the original gets away was never really a problem).<br /> <br /> Setting up a &quot;behind the scenes manipulator&quot; showdown between The Jackal and Madame Web (who did not need her own origin story movie) while picking someone like Ben Reiley or Jessica Carpenter as their central Spider-Person could actually be interesting. Even for people that don't know the comics, they can get invested in the stakes of a battle over the fate of a hero (esp. one that's easier to sell as having potential to just go bad and stay there than Peter Parker) as one person in the shadows is trying to guide them onto the good path, and another is constantly creating enemies to throw at them until their too overwhelmed to stay on the straight and narrow. Bad guy stand alone movies like Morbius and Kraven can work a lot better if there's an expected pay off of them not being simple villains to beat up when the Jackal manipulates them into fighting the new core Spider-Person who has to struggle with want to do with complex moral questions around where the line is between hero and violent vigilante that talks big.<br /> <br /> But Sony would have to care about writers and directors more than short term financial lines going up to get to something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T15:01:42-08:00","id":1531653,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget: We're talking about the same &quot;geniuses&quot; here who looked at the mockery Morbius received and thought &quot;You know what? There are so many people talking about Morbius... Let's bring Morbius back into the theaters! It's Morbin Time - as the kids say.&quot;. And so Morbius was brought back into the theaters - only to bomb <i>again </i>at the box office.<br /> <br /> But Sony executives, if you're reading this, I'm ready to pitch to you guys my treatment for the movie about a character your Spiderverse-franchise needs: Stilt-Man! (Although I'm not sure if it's Sony or Marvel who has the rights to that character...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T17:29:48-08:00","id":1531657,"title":"","content":"That's the thing with some of the people on youtube or social media in general who lambast actors and actresses for taking roles in films that bomb and ask didn't they see how bad the script was? I mean how hard is it to look up the fact that scripts go through numerous rewrites before the first table read or the first day of principal shooting and it's not like they can back out of the film as they are under contract to do the film no matter how they feel about it and some will admit it was just a paycheque. In fact Michael Ironside said that about his role in Highlander 2 after all the rewrites to the story that he might as well get paid and have some fun with it.<br /> <br /> Or some never had a strong attachment with certain film characters and are shocked that fans loved them in those roles. IE Harrison Ford has never felt a strong attachment for Han Solo and Perhaps Indy as it was a job and nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-27-2024, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T17:30:56-08:00","id":1531658,"title":"","content":"My my I forgot about the Jackel Heavy Arms, but I try to block out the Spider-Clone saga as it did amazing damage to the brand and the attempt to fix it was even worse. I was more of Detective Comics fan, but my friends were big X-Men and Spider-Man fans and they told me how bad the clone saga was and I read the some trade paperbacks and I have to agree that it was just as bad as the Jean Paul Valley version of Batman that was happening in the same period. Then to fix it they decided to bring back Norman Osbourne back from the dead and you had to take a huge suspension of disbelief that he had a healing power and he woke up just before his autopsy and found a vagrant that looked like him to take his place and disappear.<br /> <br /> No wonder Kurt Busiek was so meh towards the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-28-2024, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T12:01:45-08:00","id":1532177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1531542#post1531542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once felt anger towards social justice warriors in the beginging and now I just feel sorry for them as it seems that they are such unhappy folks who need a much healthier outlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do often think about how unhappy Martin Luther King Jr must have been in his short time. I mean, look at a comment like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have almost reached the regrettable conclusion that the Negro's great stumbling block in the stride toward freedom is not the White Citizen's Council-er or the Ku Klux Klanner, but the white moderate who is more devoted to &quot;order&quot; than to justice; who prefers a negative peace which is the absence of tension to a positive peace which is the presence of justice </div> </div> </div>How miserable must that be? I don't know doctor, maybe you could have given negative peace that is the absence of tension a chance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T13:26:05-08:00","id":1532186,"title":"","content":"I'm more of believer that people should be judged on the content of their character and not the color of there skin, sex, or sexual preference. Those that do seem to be missing the point and might be part of the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T14:42:29-08:00","id":1532196,"title":"","content":"The thing about &quot;judging people on the content of their character&quot; is that it's an <b>aspirational goal</b>. We don't live in a world where people are treated equally based on things like color, sexual identities, or religious affiliations. In an unequal world, fairly judging people means you have to see the parts of them that advantage and disadvantage their lives. Identifying those aspects of society and working to eliminate them, or at least mitigate them, is what gets us to the just and equal society where we can only be concerned with the content of people's character and not have to take more into account.<br /> <br /> The line is from a speech referred to as the &quot;I Have a Dream,&quot; speech because it's a dream. It wasn't reality then, and it isn't reality now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T18:05:55-08:00","id":1532216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1532186#post1532186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more of believer that people should be judged on the content of their character and not the color of there skin, sex, or sexual preference. Those that do seem to be missing the point and might be part of the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there is a certain subset of people that only seems to know of that one line from that one speech that gets kind of paraphrased so that it becomes a general milquetoast comment of &quot;be excellent to each other&quot; rather than the actual statement of &quot;I dream of the far off day when my children (being used as an allegorical stand in for African Americans as a whole) will not be prejudiced against based on cultural narratives and general systemic handicaps&quot;.<br /> <br /> A speech that he made about six years before the end of his life, giving him plenty of time in which to say even more things, including a bit of reflection on that speech in particular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I must confess that the dream that I had that day has at many points turned into a nightmare,\u201d he said. \u201cNow I\u2019m not one to lose hope. I keep on hoping. I still have faith in the future. But I\u2019ve had to analyse many things over the last few years, and I would say over the last few months, I\u2019ve gone through a lot of soul-searching in agonising moments. And I\u2019ve come to see that we have many more difficult days ahead and some of the old optimism was a little superficial and now it must be tempered with a solid realism and I think the realistic fact is that we still have a long long way to go. </div> </div> </div>I wonder what he would think if he knew the legacy of that speech was to distil it down to a superficiality far beyond the actual words he employed himself, if the realism of his more cogent and deeper diving analyses became so widely a thing derided by people who would look to invoke him.<br /> <br /> Heh, &quot;part of the problem&quot;. &quot;who constantly says &quot;I agree with you in the goal you seek, but I can't agree with your methods of direct action;&quot; who paternalistically feels he can set the timetable for another man's freedom; who lives by the myth of time and who constantly advises the Negro to wait until a &quot;more convenient season.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shallow understanding from people of goodwill is more frustrating than absolute misunderstanding from people of ill will. Lukewarm acceptance is much more bewildering than outright rejection.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T18:44:10-08:00","id":1532218,"title":"","content":"At Heavy Arms. Oh I agree it's an ideal to aspire to and that we will never truly reach it. But the way we see the media spin things and others doing there part. It just seems like that we are not even trying to focus on what we have in common anymore and it feels disheartening to say the least<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T13:15:34-08:00","id":1532252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1532177#post1532177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How miserable must that be? I don't know doctor, maybe you could have given negative peace that is the absence of tension a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;order&quot; he was referring to, this <i>negative peace</i>, was the idea of the white people of the time having first access to literally everything hoarded unto themselves while leaving naught but crumbs and poverty for anyone else. It was blind acceptance of a hegemony that was fundamentally corrupt, unjust, and abusive towards all but a specific class of people. Put bluntly, the &quot;order&quot; was the problem, thus any acceptance of that &quot;order&quot; in the name of a <i>negative peace</i> was basically giving up the fight. The absence of tension for the oppressor isn't a solution for anyone other than the oppressor. <br /> <br /> It should go without saying that doing any favors for the oppressor isn't making progress. If they didn't want their &quot;order&quot; violated they should have built it without exploiting everyone around them like a bunch of parasites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T05:36:19-08:00","id":1532284,"title":"","content":"Sarcasm is the rhetorical device of employing caustic words in occasionally humorous fashion to mock something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T06:55:08-08:00","id":1532289,"title":"","content":"Scarasm is hard to depict on a message board Levi unless you tell us on the onset. I also should be more clear that I was commenting on the social media mob on X, YouTube and other platforms that seem to be spending there time attacking people who shock, shudder and gasp have different opinions then them or coming up with lies to sell there story without due diligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-09-2024, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T16:44:14-08:00","id":1532302,"title":"","content":"The problem is &quot;the social media mob&quot; isn't a thing. Social media encourages tribalism, but that means each &quot;tribe&quot; and &quot;bubble&quot; has it's own group of people incentivized to pile on whichever target the algorithm puts in front of them. When you focus on just one label, you don't sound like someone rationally decrying how social media has impact cultural disagreements; it sounds like you're taking a side and trying to complain that the other side is the source of all the problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T18:06:00-08:00","id":1532306,"title":"","content":"It's nice to see a civil debate on these boards Heavy Arms..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T14:01:17-07:00","id":1532391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1532289#post1532289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scarasm is hard to depict on a message board Levi unless you tell us on the onset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like &quot;the most esteemed civil rights activist in history should have been totally okay with the status quo so that he would have been less unhappy&quot; (as well as being familiar enough with King's words to quote him on a point other than the one thing the majority of people know that he said) is about as close to saying something from the outset as I can think of.<br /> <br /> People always bring up the supposed difficulty of conveying tone through text, and yet irony and satire have been effectively conveyed in writing for thousands of years. We don't have centuries of people looking at Socrates and scratching their heads over what his intended tone was.<br /> <br /> Never mind how I would think that my following post, that there was definitely enough time to read, would have provided greater clarity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also should be more clear that I was commenting on the social media mob on X, YouTube and other platforms that seem to be spending there time attacking people who shock, shudder and gasp have different opinions then them or coming up with lies to sell there story without due diligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the &quot;social justice warriors&quot; that you feel sorry for the mob who attack and come up with lies, or the people being attacked?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T14:14:08-07:00","id":1532393,"title":"","content":"I feel sorry for both groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T23:25:31-07:00","id":1532548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1532302#post1532302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is &quot;the social media mob&quot; isn't a thing. Social media encourages tribalism, but that means each &quot;tribe&quot; and &quot;bubble&quot; has it's own group of people incentivized to pile on whichever target the algorithm puts in front of them. When you focus on just one label, you don't sound like someone rationally decrying how social media has impact cultural disagreements; it sounds like you're taking a side and trying to complain that the other side is the source of all the problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, at this point when it comes to events or issues, it's often unclear if there is a &quot;mob&quot; on social media at all, or if it's just a handful of voices loudly amplified by bots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T01:02:51-07:00","id":1532552,"title":"","content":"The provocateur bots don't work if there isn't an existing &quot;mob mentality&quot; that's already present in a given tribe/bubble/echo-chamber or whatever. The algorithms social media platforms use want to maximize engagement, negativity drives more engagement than positivity, and a bunch of loud voices and bots stoke a lot of negativity. But you still need the mob to provide the engagement or the system will ignore whatever the loud voices are on about. It's woefully stupid... but that's why we're in the vent thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T10:20:44-07:00","id":1532583,"title":"","content":"The old adage that's it easier to destroy then create is a true one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T11:50:45-07:00","id":1532593,"title":"","content":"In that context, I just gotta mention a great word for this whole thing termed by Cory Doctorow: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enshittification\" target=\"_blank\">Enshittification</a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enshittification#cite_note-enshittocene-5\" target=\"_blank\">.</a><br /> <br /> That's the basic formula (from <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20240208152542/https://www.ft.com/content/6fb1602d-a08b-4a8c-bac0-047b7d64aba5\" target=\"_blank\">this article </a>by Cory Doctorow): &quot;It\u2019s a three-stage process: first, platforms are good to their users. Then they abuse their users to make things better for their business customers. Finally, they abuse those business customers to claw back all the value for themselves. Then, there is a fourth stage: they die.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the big-picture background for why these social-media-platforms aren't improving discourse but hinder it instead. In the search of squeezing money out of these platforms, things are just made worse and worse. More bots, more chaotic algorithms (anybody who's still on Twitter... ahem, I meant X-Dot-Com of course... notice what sort of ads you get these days...?) and ultimately it all just crashes and burns.<br /> <br /> Well, I guess, the one thing that keeps Twitter alive these days is that Elon Musk is too dumb to do the third stage of Enshittification.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","user":"Knightingale","date":". 03-14-2024, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T12:00:03-07:00","id":1532594,"title":"","content":"I mean, he did do the third stage, just in an &quot;innovative&quot; fashion that destroyed value for everyone instead of just his business customers. He just has enough money that the fourth stage is going to drag on along time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T12:09:42-07:00","id":1532597,"title":"","content":"At least there is some YouTubers who try to classy and present there arguments well and don't insult people who disagree with them and attempt to do there due diligence in reporting what is happening in entertainment or politics. Sadly they seem to be a very small number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T12:13:36-07:00","id":1532599,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, you're right, that's the innovative part: Normally you'd do the third and fourth stage knowing you secured the bag for yourself at least. And you, this one person at the center of the Enshittification-process, got richer somehow. Instead, Elon Musk is doing Enshittification but his own money is on the line as well and also because he's absolutely clueless and has no plan, it's happening <i>very</i> slowly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T18:24:37-07:00","id":1532628,"title":"","content":"i don't know if it said this before,but i absolutely despise Mao Zedong i find him to be perhaps the worst human being to ever live. But there's a type of people who i hate more<br /> Maoists. anyone who looks up who Mao was and wants to follow in his footsteps should be locked up,forever and and ever and ever","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T13:20:17-07:00","id":1532664,"title":"","content":"There's always going to be folks who will admire awful people or ideals and all we can do is try to stay wise to it and remind everyone why it turned out that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T01:11:22-07:00","id":1532686,"title":"","content":"Hmm, that reminds me of when I read Fanshen: A Documentary of Revolution in a Chinese Village by William Hinton a while ago. Really fascinating stuff. A bit of a dry read, I have to admit, but really interesting as a historical work.<br /> <br /> Here's the blurb:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More than forty years after its initial publication, William Hinton\u0092s Fanshen continues to be the essential volume for those fascinated with China\u0092s revolutionary process of rural reform and social change. A pioneering work, Fanshan is a marvelous and revealing look into life in the Chinese countryside, where tradition and modernity have had both a complimentary and caustic relationship in the years since the Chinese Communist Party first came to power. It is a rare, concrete record of social struggle and transformation, as witnessed by a participant. Fanshen continues to offer profound insight into the lives of peasants and China\u0092s complex social processes. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T17:05:43-07:00","id":1532827,"title":"","content":"Reading historical bios on famous figures and older empires is always interesting and seeing how much has changed and how much has not changed and currently I'm reading another book on Alexander The Great on his early years and trying to piece together the mosiac of the past when so few things have survived to the modern age. It makes it great for civil debating when the need comes around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T01:29:57-07:00","id":1532837,"title":"","content":"Regarding Alexander, I heard recently <a href=\"https://podbay.fm/p/tides-of-history/e/1695884460\" target=\"_blank\">this historian John Hyland on a podcast</a> who has researched the Greco-Persian wars from the Persian perspective. Really fascinating stuff. He also has a book called Persian Interventions but man, 40 bucks for a 400 pages softcover... typical academic books pricing<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T02:34:43-07:00","id":1532839,"title":"","content":"I saw a title for an article today that I didn\u2019t even bother to open because it echoed the same stale propaganda I\u2019ve seen crop up everywhere since the Pandemic was declared over. Just another cry against change by corpo-america that made me want to set things on fire.<br /> <br /> <br /> During the pandemic America discovered, to its relief and delight, that many office jobs could be performed from home by working remotely. All the technology was not only there, it was over 10 years old. And you could find various bits in the media signing the praises of just how much money would be saved in gas, child care, and the myriad other financial concerns of the workers which mid and upper management types totally ignore. While the plague was upon us, there were no real complaints by the damned corpos, as they had no other choice. In time they could recoup or mitigate losses incurred by plague and people could still work. But as soon as the pandemic ended, they were immediately buying up article space to spread their inane propaganda against working from home in a desperate attempt to chain us all to desks in cubicles once more.<br /> <br /> <br /> It had already been proven that productivity was not affected by remote work years prior, but as soon as they thought the coast was clear, they sought to manufacture ridiculous pseudo-science and sketchy economics in order to justify trying to force everyone back into the office. The only real problem that they could cite was them wasting thousands of dollars building a gilded cage to keep their wage-slaves in so they could try to forget about the lives they had been neglecting at home from various draconian office policies. It all boils down to them crying over a poor investment that failed to account for the future, and then trying to pass off their failure to the whole workforce. There\u2019s also the underlying issues of the management class and their need to feel empowered and self-important by having a staff of underlings they can silently \u201crule\u201d over in an office setting like some pathetic farce of nobility. It\u2019s never been about getting the work done, that\u2019s already been proven to happen either way.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will never cease to be amazed at how completely deluded the people of this nation are that they would sacrifice any progress to languish in some archaic system that lets them revel in the illusion of power and prestige. How could they be surprised at all the \u201cquiet quitting\u201d and general unrest when they tried to end what was already working for the people? Now there are so many repeating \u201cthink pieces\u201d about how lazy and entitled Gen-Z and the late-term Millennials are for not wanting to be chained to this stale office rhetoric when we\u2019ve already seen better ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder if they\u2019d react differently if there wasn\u2019t an occupation of wall street and they\u2019d tried burning it down instead? Squatters just get ignored, firebombs make wolves of wall street cringe and whine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T12:29:42-07:00","id":1532864,"title":"","content":"Even more annoying is companies wanting people to work 8 or more hours in a day, when studies have shown that staff productivity starts to decline after the 4-5 hour mark and more mistakes are made afterwards, but don't tell them that.<br /> <br /> On another note I found a interesting book that was called 1776 BC when civilizations around that time went into decline and I couldn't find a price anywhere on it and I have enough books right now to read and I don't want to add to the growing pile that is starting to grow and I wouldn't be shocked that it would nearly reach my bedroom ceiling.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-19-2024, 03:34 PM"},"a