ting to grow and I wouldn't be shocked that it would nearly reach my bedroom ceiling.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The book is <i>1177 B.C.: The Year Civilization Collapsed</i> by Eric H. Cline, it's really good! It's about the bronze age collapse.<br /> <br /> Cline has a few lectures posted on youtube you can search for that are well worth watching, he's a really entertaining speaker and great about not being dogmatic and open about areas where there is debate in the academic community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T11:25:38-07:00","id":1532911,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the minor correction on the title as I wasn't sure what the exact title of the book and from the book jacket and the first two chapters that I read that it looked like a good read, but I didn't know the price of the book and I should put this is the Gush section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T18:06:54-07:00","id":1532976,"title":"","content":"I hate false narratives that are starting to creep up again as I recently saw a meme of showing the recent action films that had a female lead being the reason it bombed from some group of people that need a better outlet for whatever issues they have. Sorry but Madam Web, Captain Marvel and other recent films didn't bomb because of who was cast in the lead. They bombed as the storytelling, directing and special effects were not that good and the characters were bland, perfect and unlikeable.<br /> <br /> I'm old enough to remember liking Silence Of The Lambs, Buffy, Aliens, Terminator, Charmed, The Long Kiss Goodnight, Thelma &amp; Loiuse and few others as the female leads were interesting and flawed and nobody had much of a problem with the films with a lady taking centre stage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T03:54:17-07:00","id":1532994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p