"signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T11:51:31-07:00","id":1533176,"title":"","content":"It's a parody. But what I like about that one is that it really nails the uncanny valley of almost making sense. And that's what makes it a good parody. I mean, is that clip any crazier than the Sydney Sweeney discourse that happened on the right in the last few weeks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:02:20-07:00","id":1533178,"title":"","content":"The stars of Madam Web were a breathe of fresh air of poking fun on how bad the film was with Ms. Sweeny saying on SNL that you didn't see her in the film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:14:11-07:00","id":1533185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1533178#post1533178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stars of Madam Web were a breathe of fresh air of poking fun on how bad the film was with Ms. Sweeny saying on SNL that you didn't see her in the film.</div> </div> </div> </div>The right-wing discourse was markedly not about what Sydney Sweeney was saying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ...<br /> <br /> But I feel a bit bad because I think Sydney Sweeney should get better roles than teen-superhero-wannabe # 3. Also, I don't think she was well cast to play the nerdy girl in Madame Web. Maybe if they gave her more room to make the role her own, this could've worked but this is Madame Web we're talking about. This shit was only ever gonna roll in one direction - downhill. Sucks to be caught up in that - no matter what actor we're talking about. Well, I mean, on the other hand... at least it pays well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:16:39-07:00","id":1533186,"title":"","content":"To be fair none of them were well cast in a film that wasn't going to be a success as we are seeing the superhero genre starting to play itself out and whatever the new thing will be to take it's place. But at least we are seeing actors and actresses having a sense of humor or being humorless or making excuses of why such and such film bombed or attacking the fans or taking the bait by activists who want to spin a bad narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-26-2024, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:24:04-07:00","id":1533189,"title":"","content":"Also, Morbius, Madame Web, that upcoming Kraven the Hunter movie... Who even knows what's going on over there at Sony... You'd think they would do a better job of capitalizing on letting the MCU use Spider-Man and yet here we are...<br /> <br /> Well, at least we got Tom Hardy falling in love with Venom as a character out of this, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:30:00-07:00","id":1533191,"title":"","content":"They might think that they milked the flagship characters of Marvel as much as they could and feel they should go with the lesser known IP's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:37:30-07:00","id":1533194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1533191#post1533191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might think that they milked the flagship characters of Marvel as much as they could and feel they should go with the lesser known IP's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the situation has more to do with licensing. Ignoring the reasons and events for how we ended up in the current situation, the thing to keep in mind is that Sony has the rights to Spider-Man and all characters linked to him. Disney/Marvel couldn't use Spider-Man because of that - untile they made a deal with Sony. They did. That's why Tom Holland Spider-Man was in a bunch of movies. Sony tried to capitalize on that by using its license for all those other Spider-man side-characters/villains. Venom worked well and so after that we got more... Morbius, Venom II, Madame Web and soon Kraven the Hunter.<br /> <br /> Of course, the irony is that Sony couldn't have picked a worse time to do this. People are sick and tired of superhero-movies. Especially when they suck. And Morbius and Madame Web suck as movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T14:13:15-07:00","id":1533199,"title":"","content":"A different perspective: people aren't sick and tired of superhero movies, they're tired of companies milking the whole &quot;cinematic universe&quot; concept.<br /> <br /> There's a few key factors:<br /> <br /> 1) Volume of content. This is really the biggest problem. Watching the entire MCU film catalog (so not even getting into all the streaming shows) is ~80 hrs. Phase 4 alone is ~50 hrs. That is why people burnt out in a nutshell. It takes less time to watch all the Phase 1-3 films than it does to watch just the Phase 4 ones. If you wanted to watch every last bit of MCU film and TV show right now, it would take you ~50 days without any breaks. To give some perspective on this, Sazae-san, the longest running anime ever (and still in production so that title isn't going anywhere) with a whopping 2,640 episodes (at normal Japanese format for a 30 minute show with ads) would take under 38 days to watch all of. The MCU has more content than a children's show that's been ongoing for 55 years. And most of that content has come recently, all in a big wave of releases.<br /> <br /> 2) Streaming fragmentation. This is something that's not unique to the concept of cinematic universes, but it impacts them hard. Esp, with the Sony-verse and MCU crossing over, and the X-Men/Deadpool vs. possibly coming to the MCU, the giant heft of watching all of this stuff is compounded by it not all being in one place. Loved seeing the three live-action Spider-men teaming up and want to go back and watch the older movies? Well... which streaming services do you have? Loved the Kingpin and want to go back and see his earlier introduction.... well.... hmmm... how's Netflix feeling about unlocking those again? How about Agents of SHIELD? Woo boy. Of course this leads into:<br /> <br /> 3) Licensing! One of the biggest problems is that Disney can't get everything under one roof. It's kinda ridiculous, but considering how much we're seeing companies just wipe shows/movies from services and locking them up in digital vaults, there's clearly more money in owning and not showing something than showing it,or licensing it to someone that will. Even WB with the DC franchise films more solidly locked up in ownership still can't seem to get its house in order on what to watch where.<br /> <br /> 4) Superheroes are still doing well when companies play to the strengths of the genre. The Boys got successful spinoffs. Invincible did well. The Marvel and DC animated stuff continues to be high quality and well loved by fans. The audience is there. The want is there. But this goes right back to 1: the time isn't there for what the big studios are trying to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T17:44:03-07:00","id":1533222,"title":"","content":"Interesting notion on the volume of content and that is something I always been grumbling about for the last several years. You don't need to have a superhero movie every year or with a huge budget, sometimes going small and taking a break between films is needed. That is what hurt Batman in the late 1990's when WB had practically back to back movies with Val Kilmer and George Clooney and not enough time to come up with a decent story or character protrayals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T01:20:50-07:00","id":1533236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Licensing! One of the biggest problems is that Disney can't get everything under one roof. It's kinda ridiculous, but considering how much we're seeing companies just wipe shows/movies from services and locking them up in digital vaults, there's clearly more money in owning and not showing something than showing it,or licensing it to someone that will. Even WB with the DC franchise films more solidly locked up in ownership still can't seem to get its house in order on what to watch where. </div> </div> </div>That goes back to the 90s when Marvel was in real dire straits financially and so they sold off the movie-rights to their characters all over the place piecemeal-style. That's how you ended with Sony having the rights for Spider Man and you got out of that the Sam Raimi Spider Man movies. X-Men meanwhile was sold to Fox and that's how you got the Bryan Singer X-Men movies. Hell, even Iron Man could only happen in its 2008 form because the licensing lapsed and reverted back to Marvel. We could've all very much ended up in a parallel universe where the people with the Iron Man license had gotten their shit together and put out an Iron Man movie in the early 00s and then Marvel wouldn't have had the license to do the 2008 movie.<br /> <br /> So, all things considered, I think Disney did pretty well. Only a juggernaut of a company like Disney could've wrangled that mess to the degree that it has. I mean, they got the rights for X-Men into the MCU-tent by buying Fox wholesale. Can't imagine many other companies doing that.<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________<br /> <br /> And I would add a fifth point:<br /> <br /> 5) The Marvel Production Process: It's connected to point 1 as volume is part of the problem here but at this point it's gotta be said: The Marvel-production process stinks! It's costly, inefficient and doesn't produce quality. The first thing that needs to change is that they need to invest more in their special-effects-department. Those people are overworked, underpaid and need to have more of a voice when it comes to deciding what special effects you get in these movies (there was that story about Taika Waititi not being able to make up his mind what the special effect was supposed to look like, for example, and so a lot of work ended up being a waste of time). Then there's the whole issue with the reshoots. Right now with both the movies and the TV-show they film the whole thing and only then start to reconsider whether the movie/TV-show worked or not. Even the latest movie that's in production, Captain America: Brave New World (they renamed the movie as well) is yet another thing that's going to have extensive reshoots. Secret Wars, Marvels, Quantummania... the one thing they all had in common was their budget ballooned thanks to extensive reshoots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T02:28:10-07:00","id":1533239,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure you can really separate out the production issues from the bloated content issues. If the MCU was still operated at the same pace as Phase 2, it would be a lot easier to manage everything for quality control and so on.<br /> <br /> I also think there has to be a bit of room to acknowledge that the MCU got thrown completely off track when the actor playing their next big bad is currently in prison. While Kang is possibly one of the easiest villains to recast ever, everything that was supposed to build up to that - and not having a new direction yet - leads to a lot of mess you just can't foresee. For any projects significantly in process, that means messy reshoots, rewrites, and budget bloats.<br /> <br /> Of course... that's part of why people are sick of the whole cinematic universe thing, not the superheroes specifically thing. When you're just making cool superhero stories that just need to stand on their own, you don't need to worry about all this extra stuff that is great when it works, but a huge turd when it doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T03:02:55-07:00","id":1533240,"title":"","content":"The reason it should be separate is because at this stage they're not stumbling into these production-problems because of bloat but because they embrace them as a policy. They don't just accidentally keep having to do these messy reshoots again and again because of bloat but because they're completely accepting of that being part of the process. And as the money kept rolling in for Phase 3, they just continued doing it in Phase 4 and well, now we're here. The problem is that somewhere along the way they convinced themselves that any issues any movie might have can all be fixed with reshoots. The process is a separate point because of how uncritically Marvel put their faith in it just working as they went from Phase 2 to 3 and 4. And so they kept up with a formula that was problematic from the very beginning.<br /> <br /> And yeah, you had the thing with Jonathan Majors, also doubt anybody had the tragic death of Chadwick Boseman on their bingo-card. Also wonder how many actors at this point would be actually willing to sign one of those Marvel contracts where you as this character have to show up in multiple movies and TV-shows. Years of your career just lost to this whole mega-project that might make you famous like Chris Hemsworth or Chris Evans or you get stuff like Elizabeth Olson's stint as Wanda where she put in all that work for the TV-show and for whatever reason when she did the movie, the people who worked on that weren't invested in what exactly had happened in the TV-show. Or Scarlett Johansson's role of Black Widow... I doubt she looks fondly back on how the MCU treated her character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","user":"Knightingale","date":". 03-27-2024, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T12:43:59-07:00","id":1533267,"title":"","content":"Reshoots have been part of cinema since the beginning. &quot;We'll fix it in post&quot; has been part of the policy of pretty much every major studio for over a century. There's nothing new to doing reshoots. There's nothing new to reshoots ballooning budgets. There's nothing particularly unique to Disney or Marvel here either (Justice League and Suicide Squad....).<br /> <br /> Reshoots are one of those things that the general public only really notices or cares about when trying to explain why something is wrong with a movie. Nobody sits around and says, &quot;man, Back to the Future really blew it by doing three weeks of reshoots,&quot; because the end result was seen by everyone as for the better (Eric Stoltz probably wasn't happy about it at the time, but he doesn't seem bitter about it) and the movie made a ton of movie. Speaking of Disney, Rogue One had a huge amount of reshoots by their standards, and is considered one of the better Disney era Star Wars films.<br /> <br /> They're just parts of the business. Everyone does them, they're not controversial on their own. Most of the time you don't even notice them (esp. when everything is still within budget), sometimes they are vast improvements, sometimes they manage to make a bad movie worse. Extensive reshoots can make a bleh movie good, but cost too much to net a profit despite increased sales for having a better movie, and they can flip a movie that was going to bomb to at least do OK and be worth the expense.<br /> <br /> Focusing on reshoots is, like focusing on superheroes to me missing the core problem. The core is the &quot;cinematic universe&quot; because it's a balancing act between creative teams with a strong identity and a cohesive franchise that all of those different creatives need to be making at the same time. The more projects, the harder it is for the people at the top to work with each team individually. Extensive reshoots are just a symptom of trying to keep the &quot;cinematic universe&quot; cohesive when you can't ensure producers are as involved on each project as much as they should be. It gets to the point where it's easier to &quot;fix&quot; things later than try to manage four different $100+ million projects hands-on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T13:07:51-07:00","id":1533269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1533267#post1533267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reshoots have been part of cinema since the beginning. &quot;We'll fix it in post&quot; has been part of the policy of pretty much every major studio for over a century. There's nothing new to doing reshoots. There's nothing new to reshoots ballooning budgets. There's nothing particularly unique to Disney or Marvel here either (Justice League and Suicide Squad....).<br /> <br /> Reshoots are one of those things that the general public only really notices or cares about when trying to explain why something is wrong with a movie. Nobody sits around and says, &quot;man, Back to the Future really blew it by doing three weeks of reshoots,&quot; because the end result was seen by everyone as for the better (Eric Stoltz probably wasn't happy about it at the time, but he doesn't seem bitter about it) and the movie made a ton of movie. Speaking of Disney, Rogue One had a huge amount of reshoots by their standards, and is considered one of the better Disney era Star Wars films.<br /> <br /> They're just parts of the business. Everyone does them, they're not controversial on their own. Most of the time you don't even notice them (esp. when everything is still within budget), sometimes they are vast improvements, sometimes they manage to make a bad movie worse. Extensive reshoots can make a bleh movie good, but cost too much to net a profit despite increased sales for having a better movie, and they can flip a movie that was going to bomb to at least do OK and be worth the expense.<br /> <br /> Focusing on reshoots is, like focusing on superheroes to me missing the core problem. The core is the &quot;cinematic universe&quot; because it's a balancing act between creative teams with a strong identity and a cohesive franchise that all of those different creatives need to be making at the same time. The more projects, the harder it is for the people at the top to work with each team individually. Extensive reshoots are just a symptom of trying to keep the &quot;cinematic universe&quot; cohesive when you can't ensure producers are as involved on each project as much as they should be. It gets to the point where it's easier to &quot;fix&quot; things later than try to manage four different $100+ million projects hands-on.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand my point. You're also ignoring the huge problem that's hidden in your description and why I mentioned that fifth point: The delusion that the so-called &quot;Marvel-Method&quot; is the end-all-be-all of movie-making. Reshoots have always been part of moviemaking. What you're misunderstanding is the problem of Marvel buying into its own hype. They think they've got it all figured out. That's <i>how </i>you get to the bloat without anybody raising the alarm. That's the logical gap in your description. The bloat as a problem wouldn't exist without that blind faith in their overreliance on reshoots. They had so much faith in their process, they didn't even bother accounting for scale.<br /> <br /> But also that process sucks. Oh, sure, you can point to the times when movies worked despite being a total hellhole in terms of production. And for every one of those, you have countless others that were failures during production and then ended up being failures at the box-office. You don't get the failures of the latest Marvel-Phase without that blind faith in a flawed process.<br /> <br /> And Rogue One is a <a href=\"https://variety.com/2023/film/news/rogue-one-gareth-edwards-inaccurate-reports-reshoots-tony-gilroy-1235741792/\" target=\"_blank\">bad example</a> to cite here because the whole narrative around that film is disputed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T14:06:13-07:00","id":1533273,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms &amp; Knightingale have either of you read the book When Titans Clash on how it detailed the events that caused Marvel Comics to declare Chapter 11 bankruptcy? It made for an interesting read and some of the choices that were made were incredible. But on another note if your going to make another superhero film at all, it should be viewer friendly as possible and that you don't need to go watch previous films to get a handle on what this film is about. The old James Bond films did that perfectly before they tried to tie events more with the Daniel Craig run and maybe WB &amp; Disney need to go back to that idea after they take a break from live action films and maybe do some animated films.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T14:07:03-07:00","id":1533274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1533269#post1533269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstand my point</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, I have no idea what you're even trying to say. You keep changing focus and aren't clarifying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The delusion that the so-called &quot;Marvel-Method&quot; is the end-all-be-all of movie-making. </div> </div> </div>If this was unique to Marvel/Disney, I'd consider this more important. But as it's not, I don't see the point.<br /> <br /> Also the &quot;Marvel Method&quot; is a comic book scripting scheme Stan Lee came up with decades ago. While nobody claims it's the &quot;end-all-be-all&quot; it's the core &quot;character&quot; to Marvel properties and is actually important to translating Marvel properties to other media because if you don't understand the Marvel Method you don't understand how the fan favored characters and plots were constructed in the first place; which you need to do if you want to adapt them well.<br /> <br /> The Marvel Method is also pretty useful for film. What made it so revolutionary was trusting artists to do their jobs. Before Stan Lee implemented it, the industry standard was &quot;Full Script.&quot; The writers/editors of the comic companies would hand the artists a complete script with action direction and page layout demands, and the artists were just there to make it happen on page. The Marvel Method was to just give them a broad outline of major story beats (either visual or text) that needed to be hit, and let more get filled in collaboratively by the people actually putting it to paper.<br /> <br /> This approach to collaborative story making helped Marvel stand out as not being nearly as cookie-cutter as DC was at the time, and allowed a lot of break out characters that were created to fill various plot needs to have room to get turned into future major icons of the company. The whole point is to avoid things feeling like they're designed by a bunch of executives and let the creative flair of individuals shine through to help give titles their own character and feel... because the executive in question literally didn't have time to keep up the Full Script method for all the books Marvel was trying to make at the time and had to cut his oversight and trust in his creatives more.<br /> <br /> It might have some major issues translated to film,but at the same time, who's done a massive film franchise better exactly? Just because the MCU started down a bad path to keeping up what it created, doesn't mean other methods have produced a better approach to a massive cinematic franchise yet. The biggest comparison I can think of is the James Bond franchise, but what they didn't do is content bloat. People constantly question if James Bond should just finally be retired, new eras come in. There's high points. There's low points. But the argument to not make another James Bond movie never seems to be correct. The formula works....but it wouldn't if we were getting two Bond movies a year, a spin off streaming show every quarter, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you're misunderstanding is the problem of Marvel buying into its own hype. They think they've got it all figured out. That's <i>how </i>you get to the bloat without anybody raising the alarm. That's the logical gap in your description. The bloat as a problem wouldn't exist without that blind faith in their overreliance on reshoots. They had so much faith in their process, they didn't even bother accounting for scale. </div> </div> </div>Do you have some actual insight on this, or are you just wildly speculating that reshoots specifically are the fault here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Rogue One is a <a href=\"https://variety.com/2023/film/news/rogue-one-gareth-edwards-inaccurate-reports-reshoots-tony-gilroy-1235741792/\" target=\"_blank\">bad example</a> to cite here because the whole narrative around that film is disputed. </div> </div> </div>Why? None of the disputed narratives are about if the reshoots happened, if they were extensive, and if they were good. It's all about how much &quot;drama&quot; there was about them.<br /> <br /> Everyone agrees the Vader corridor scene was great. Fans love it. But that was a complete reshoot addition. There's no dispute over that. There's no disputing that was an expensive thing to add to reshoots because it's an action scene with lots of SFX on a whole new set. &quot;Tony Gilroy swooped in and saved the movie from being trash,&quot; vs. &quot;Gareth Edwards and Tony Gilroy worked hand-in-hand to finish an extensive reshoot schedule that made the film much better in the end,&quot; doesn't change the value of the example to my point. The five weeks of expensive reshoots making the film better is my point; not who's responsible for which scenes created during the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T14:09:59-07:00","id":1533276,"title":"","content":"I didn't like the scene with Vader at the end of Rogue One as it made him more dangerous then he really was and he did need the Storm Troopers to gain control of Princess Leia's ship and what you saw with Rogue One is that he is nearly a one man army and made the troopers needless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T14:53:46-07:00","id":1533282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1533274#post1533274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this point, I have no idea what you're even trying to say. You keep changing focus and aren't clarifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I feel the same way about your responses. Somehow we just keep talking past each other. I don't feel like we even disagree with each other for the most part.<br /> <br /> Let's just move on...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T05:28:59-07:00","id":1533309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1533276#post1533276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't like the scene with Vader at the end of Rogue One as it made him more dangerous then he really was and he did need the Storm Troopers to gain control of Princess Leia's ship and what you saw with Rogue One is that he is nearly a one man army and made the troopers needless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note, in Episode 1, Vader attacked Leia's ship to capture Leia, but primarily to recover the Death Star plans. If he was just looking to kill everyone, then yeah he probably could have done it all on his own (though likely still slower than he would have with a bunch of Stormtroopers assisting him). But chasing a bunch of rebels through a ship in order to capture them, then interrogate them, and then tearing the ship apart to find the plans, isn't something that one person, even Darth Vader, would be able to accomplish easily. So those Stormtroopers were were very useful and important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T12:27:00-07:00","id":1533527,"title":"","content":"Is social media outlets filled with bots or paid trolls to stir up contraversy? I just ask with the recent IGN France atricle on Steller Blade attacking the designer as somebody who never seen a real female and getting ratioed when it discovered that said designer has an attractive wife who is an artist for the game and that they used a attractive Korean model as the template for the heroine and is most likely going to get more such jobs in the future. I mean how hard is it to do basic research on a IP, books or movies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T15:07:12-07:00","id":1533535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1533527#post1533527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is social media outlets filled with bots or paid trolls to stir up contraversy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Though I'm not quite seeing the connection to the rest of your post. Social media makes money off of engagement. Negativity drives more engagement than positivity. Social media outlets thus have no incentive to really do anything about all the shit-stirring (bots, paid trolls, trolls doing it for the clicks, etc.) because as long as it doesn't get too bad, they make more money even without being the ones doing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just ask with the recent IGN France atricle on Steller Blade attacking the designer as somebody who never seen a real female and getting ratioed when it discovered that said designer has an attractive wife who is an artist for the game and that they used a attractive Korean model as the template for the heroine and is most likely going to get more such jobs in the future. </div> </div> </div>So, yeah, what does this have to do with bots and trolls? Even IGN France agrees they deserved to get ratioed for that comment and have issued a public apology for it. It was a dumb take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean how hard is it to do basic research on a IP, books or movies? </div> </div> </div>That's... not really the same thing? Like, I don't need to research into Rob Leifield's personal life to criticize his art style. It's just a lot less controversial to diss his work because it was at best a matter of taste back in the '90s, and it's easy to criticize without running afoul of Internet culture wars now. Not even his staunchest defenders is going to get huffy about his inability to draw feet, his obsession with putting pockets/pouches everywhere on costumes, and a complete lack of understanding of the human spine (regardless of a character's sex).<br /> <br /> I don't need to know anything about Kim Hyung-tae to be worried that the demo for Stellar Blade doesn't do a great job of selling Eve as a character. Making her bland emotionally but hot physically is unappealing to me and plenty of other people. Taking a pot shot at the man just distracts from what the demo augurs for the final product. Whether Eve is a beloved character or a forgotten one is going to rest on the writing and acting, not her digital model attractiveness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T15:18:30-07:00","id":1533536,"title":"","content":"It just seems like that people just seem they like fan flames of outrage. For Rob Liefeild I never had an issue with him as a pro and I remember that he got into drawing to help out with family medical expenses and I can't fault him for that and he seemed to be a pleasant person according to many that met him. But I agree his art style isn't my favorite either.<br /> <br /> I used to dream to be a journalist when I was much younger and now it seems that I wouldn't fit in as I would make an effort to be as through and detailed as possible if I did a report, now it seems like anyone could be called a journalist.<br /> <br /> It's just sad to see stuff that I held in high regard become so poorly done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T15:19:50-07:00","id":1533537,"title":"","content":"I mean the culture can't be this insane Heavy Arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T17:16:56-07:00","id":1533545,"title":"","content":"We're talking about video games. &quot;Video game journalism&quot; has always been a pretty questionable part of things that's tried to give itself the air of being serious journalism while generally being nothing more rigorous than food and film critics, and even more prone to pay-to-play access influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T19:56:21-07:00","id":1533549,"title":"","content":"Sad but true Heavy Arms and I just wish that it wasn't the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T01:27:40-07:00","id":1533553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1533537#post1533537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the culture can't be this insane Heavy Arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let 'er cook, it'll get there soon enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T03:58:18-07:00","id":1533556,"title":"","content":"I would think that people would tend to take a comment like &quot;has never seen a real woman&quot; as more rhetorical than literal, a comment on a tendency to preference images of women that go to a particular extreme of attractive features regardless of context in a manner that ends up being a tad absurd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T11:49:14-07:00","id":1533566,"title":"","content":"While it was most certainly a rhetorical comment, it's still pretty crass to say about a video game character directly modeled off of a real woman. It's certainly the case that the game does also exaggerate things (though how is that any different than how models are exaggerated all the time in photo-shoots, or actors are exaggerated using costuming/etc.?), but it's also a French writer lecturing a team of Korean creatives on what beautiful Korean women &quot;really&quot; look like.<br /> <br /> While Eve can certainly get into the absurd levels (esp. because of the shameless jiggle physics) if she was a new entry in a fighting game franchise like Dead or Alive or Street Fighter, you wouldn't notice.<br /> <br /> Like I said above, the problem is the demo was pretty underwhelming. Tomb Raider didn't become a big franchise because of Lara Croft's absurdly large polygons. If that's all the games had going for them it wouldn't have really worked. Tomb Raider had giant polygons and a good game with a character people liked. If Stellar Blade's demo hasn't really left much to talk about besides Eve's looks.. that's a problem because you want people to be saying, &quot;hey this combat system is great and it would be great no matter what Eve looks like.&quot; Which would be a stretch because it's not a bad system... but it's not really an impressive one either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T12:19:34-07:00","id":1533569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1533566#post1533566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While Eve can certainly get into the absurd levels (esp. because of the shameless jiggle physics) if she was a new entry in a fighting game franchise like Dead or Alive or Street Fighter, you wouldn't notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I don't think I've ever seen a new game from those series (plus Tekken) come out where, in the event of a new female character with the same standard of exaggerated physique, there haven't been people who make a point of how they're not really developing in new directions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said above, the problem is the demo was pretty underwhelming. Tomb Raider didn't become a big franchise because of Lara Croft's absurdly large polygons. If that's all the games had going for them it wouldn't have really worked. Tomb Raider had giant polygons and a good game with a character people liked. If Stellar Blade's demo hasn't really left much to talk about besides Eve's looks.. that's a problem because you want people to be saying, &quot;hey this combat system is great and it would be great no matter what Eve looks like.&quot; Which would be a stretch because it's not a bad system... but it's not really an impressive one either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've also seen people that have had positive feedback about the fighting system, although I'm starting to think that the extent to which this is becoming a culture war focal point makes it hard to assess their objectivity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T12:21:57-07:00","id":1533570,"title":"","content":"Sadly it's not the first time that a foreign media tried to dictate what they thought another country's beauty standards should be. I remember that last year we had trolls who were mad that the winner of Miss Zimbabwe was a white lady and not a black lady and it didn't matter that she was a native of the country and the residents didn't mind and were shaking there heads at the so called outrage by some hack media personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-04-2024, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T16:18:55-07:00","id":1533578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1533569#post1533569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also seen people that have had positive feedback about the fighting system, although I'm starting to think that the extent to which this is becoming a culture war focal point makes it hard to assess their objectivity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's also a demo. The combat is good for what the demo offers. But there's nothing really special about it either. If combat is like that for a full dozens of hours game? That's going to get old fast. If the RPG aspects of the game help add more depth and versatility to it... it could be fun.<br /> <br /> I'd be more worried about the objectivity of anyone trashing the combat system. Even if it isn't great in the final product, just what's in the demo is solid enough that the game could knock other things out of the park and you wouldn't mind it not being revolutionary in fighting mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T16:34:28-07:00","id":1533580,"title":"","content":"Like it's been said it's a demo and they will probably refine the system and setting before the release date. Also some good news out of the Stellar Blade story is that IGN France did issue an apology to the creatives of the game which is something of a surprise as I expected a doubling down of the narrative of toxic gamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-04-2024, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T18:48:30-07:00","id":1533675,"title":"","content":"I will say that the thing that stands out to me about Stellar Blade isn't the gameplay, or even the cheesecake, so much as it being another entry for the trope of &quot;fighting force composed exclusively or primarily of exaggeratedly attractive women* with superhuman capabilities, but not to an extent that they don't experience really high casualties that have a particular tendency to entail being horrifically cut down (with especially traumatised expressions), because that compounds the tragedy of it I guess&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which as a source of drama in anime and animesque video games, I do feel is kind of played out, and somewhat cheap.<br /> <br /> I can't say offhand whether or not NieR: Automata should be considered more sophisticated than this, but it definitely still seems like something that is really trying to follow in NieR's footsteps in a way that is perhaps going a little beyond inspiration.<br /> <br /> * Occasionally substitute in children hovering somewhere around puberty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T10:35:08-07:00","id":1533707,"title":"","content":"At least it seems Elon Musk wants to do something about bot accounts for X and hopefully it will make it harder for trolls to inflate the number of supporters they claim to have when they engage on personal attacks on people they don't like or push a &quot;false&quot; narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T10:40:08-07:00","id":1533709,"title":"","content":"Elon Musk is now promising to deal with bots because the issue <i>has gotten worse</i> since his takeover. His management has only made things worse for Twitter/X so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T12:31:34-07:00","id":1533712,"title":"","content":"It would be nice that the social media sites could do more about bots in general as they seem to be a scourge on the sites I go for enjoyment or different viewpoints on whatever political or entertainment site I like to visit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T19:17:10-07:00","id":1533782,"title":"","content":"Twitter was doing a lot about it... Musk literally fired the whole team responsible for trying to combat bots and trolls (because too many of his fans are trolls).<br /> <br /> The problem is that doing more is expensive. The reduction in bots/trolls/etc. has to improve the experience enough to increase ad revenue/etc.or a business has no reason to really invest in it.<br /> <br /> Wikipedia is really good at keep trolls and bots at bay because it's a non-profit run website and thus their calculation isn't burdened by turning a profit or stock prices needing to go up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T19:30:52-07:00","id":1533786,"title":"","content":"I knew that it was a complex problem, but I had no real idea of the scope of problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T05:37:44-07:00","id":1533810,"title":"","content":"When I see statements to the effect of &quot;I just can't understand why people are impassioned and proactive about their positions, which keep having expectations of others and wanting to create social systems to help make those expectations the norm&quot;, my mind often goes back to another quote that reaches beyond the boundaries of &quot;I have a dream that one day people will stop being so judgemental of those white people who are uncritical of the systems and historical precedents that disproportionately benefit them&quot;.<br /> <br /> To whit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the greatest problems of history is that the concepts of love and power are usually contrasted as polar opposites. Love is identified with a resignation of power and power with a denial of love. What is needed is a realization that power without love is reckless and abusive and that love without power is sentimental and anaemic. Power at its best is love implementing the demands of justice. Justice at its best is love correcting everything that stands against love. </div> </div> </div>I often think about one of the particular turns of phrase in there: &quot;sentimental and anaemic&quot;. It's such a scathing indictment of the idea that people might care about things but then not actually <i>do</i> anything to bring it into effect.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T07:31:29-07:00","id":1533814,"title":"","content":"I keep seeing these pathetic screeds written trying to blame either the Boomers, Millennials. or Gen-Z for the level of sheer idiocy in the world today. Being a (forgotten) Gen-X myself and in a position to see the whole argument, it surprises and irritates me that people can\u2019t seem to focus on the real problem. It\u2019s not <i>any</i> generation, it\u2019s corporate execs. It\u2019s ALWAYS been the corporate execs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Who decided to send jobs overseas instead of leaving them here stateside? Corpo execs.<br /> <br /> Who shorts your pay growth every single year to fluff up their bottom line? Corpo execs.<br /> <br /> Who inflates prices on all goods and services for the sake of satisfying greed? Corpo execs.<br /> <br /> Who creates the layers HR of bullshit between you and getting hired for a job? Corpo execs.<br /> <br /> Whose decisions tank the market and screw up the economy for everyone? Corpo execs.<br /> <br /> Who keeps lobbying to rewrite the law so that they get away with their crimes? Corpo Execs.<br /> <br /> <br /> They aren\u2019t a generation; they\u2019re a tiny group of people sitting in offices of inscrutable power, making wide-ranging decisions that ruin the rest of us for their own sake, who are utterly insulated from the very concept of accountability for no rational reason. Doesn\u2019t matter how much money you make, monsters are still monsters, trash is still trash.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T14:48:57-07:00","id":1533853,"title":"","content":"Eh.... while it's not strictly generational, it's also letting a lot of people off the hook to just say corpo is the problem.<br /> <br /> Corpo is the problem because we let it be. Corps only have the power we let them have. Boomer as a generality do deserve a lot of blame because their generation elected a a series of governments that resulted in the sheer amount of corpo power that exists now. One of the reasons Gen-X is forgotten in this context is that by the time Gen-X was old enough to really exercise political power, Reagan, Bush Sr. and Clinton had overseen a near total dismantling of virtually all of the New Deal era corporate regulations that were put in place after the Great Depression because... the Silent Generation was very on board with regulating the businesses that screwed them over back before there were the New Deal safety nets.<br /> <br /> Corps might be bad (if anyone doesn't feel like listening to lefties on the matter, please read Adam Smith's <i>The Wealth of Nations</i> as the father of modern capitalism outlined exactly how corporations instead of private ownership leads to all the stuff Darksol outlined), but they get away with what they get within the bounds of the laws passed by the people we elect. Democracies don't work if the citizenry don't take some ownership of what their elected representatives do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T16:47:05-07:00","id":1533861,"title":"","content":"The only thing I can say now is outside of the final Mission Impossible film and Godzilla minus 1 and the Godzilla/Kong movie is I don't see much coming down the road to really interest me to go to a movie theater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T20:53:39-07:00","id":1533871,"title":"","content":"I shouldn't be shocked that some people can say awful stuff and still have a job. I'm making a reference to the Community Manager of Complusion Gaming that made disparaging remarks about white gamers and called asians white adjacent and wasn't fired right away.<br /> <br /> If I as a white male said such things on such a platform, I'd be out of a job so fast I would get whiplash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T11:16:05-07:00","id":1533984,"title":"","content":"At least the rest of the world is starting to ask why are people making issues out of nothing. I just saw a Koren news outlet address the Stellar Blade article from IGN France and ask how that a game character based off a real person be considered unrealistic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T23:54:49-07:00","id":1534386,"title":"","content":"Now this is just bad marketing... From <a href=\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/a24-civil-war-posters-controversy-1235876340/\" target=\"_blank\">Hollywood Reporter</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A24 has released a series of epic new posters touting its acclaimed film Civil War.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s just one problem. Well, perhaps more than one. Or none, depending on your point of view. We\u2019ll explain.<br /> <br /> The five images (below) tease postapocalyptic scenes in major United States cities that have been torn apart by conflict. The Sphere is blackened wreck amid a smoldering Las Vegas. There is a floating gun unit in a lake outside Los Angeles. There are troops on patrol in San Francisco. A Miami street lays in ruins. There are tour boats full of refugees on the Chicago River. All scenes suggesting war-torn destruction in iconic locations.<br /> <br /> <b>Except</b> \u2026 none of these scenes are actually in the movie. They\u2019ve caused some to wonder if the campaign is giving potential moviegoers a false expectation of what they\u2019ll see in the film. Civil War is A24\u2019s most expensive production to date, costing around $50 million. Yet the images make the film look like a movie with twice that budget. </div> </div> </div>That's true. I've seen the movie and none of these images are part of it. And then there's of course the whole AI-angle... Man, they're really gonna end up embracing the whole AI-image-generation thing when it comes to things like marketing, won't they? All in order to cut corners and save a couple of bucks...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T07:41:38-07:00","id":1534394,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> Of course they will. That's the new corpo wet-dream; replace every possible worker with AI or robots in a desperate attempt to reduce their cost of doing business. They somehow think this will mean huge profits from now on, and forget that without an income nobody can buy their products or pay for their services. After they carve the employable workforce down to like 10% of itself, then the whole country will economically implode and they'll be to blame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T12:00:18-07:00","id":1534402,"title":"","content":"I think it's a bit overhyped? This is hardly the first time trailers have used material that wasn't in the final film; esp. in the era of extensive digital effects. It's not the first time it's been done purposefully to impact audience expectations in ways that feel exploitative instead of evocative.<br /> <br /> Even the one novel part probably is overblown in terms of how much money they might have saved. &quot;We want 5 seconds of a fly over of a photorealistic postwar Las Vegas&quot; isn't some massive payday for a digital artist. It's certainly more expensive to have a human do it (with plenty of assistance from &quot;dumb&quot; algorithms), but having a human do the prompts and then either that same person or someone else actually make the final product look good-enough still means paying for work.<br /> <br /> I feel like Disney/Marvel's doing the whole opening credits sequence like this for Secret Invasion (and it being so underwhelming for it) is a much better example of how this is going to be done poorly by giant companies, and how it's going to really negatively impact the final product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T12:45:15-07:00","id":1534404,"title":"","content":"They did say Hollywood is something of a slump as writers are finding it harder to get jobs now and maybe they might have priced themselves out a job according to more reasonable media sites like Jesterbells who avoids click baiting and tries to present a clear picture with the info she has at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T12:55:36-07:00","id":1534407,"title":"","content":"It also be interesting why the studio execs thought some of there movies would be huge blockbuster successes that would make a billion or more and they were good films in general like the last Mission Impossible movie, but it didn't make those numbers at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T13:24:24-07:00","id":1534410,"title":"","content":"I would need some serious convincing to consider the writers negotiating a pay raise the problem with Hollywood right now (the movie studio CEOs pay rates aren't secret, and they clearly don't feel like tightening their belts).<br /> <br /> If there's a serious slump, there's two vastly bigger factors that Occam's Razor points to over anything else:<br /> <br /> 1) The continual dissociation between the C-suite and what the company actually does. This is something we see across multiple sectors. The people at the top have been increasingly divorced from any real connection to the products their companies make, and are thus far more focused on what they do know: making the money line go up. What's going on at Boeing is a great example: A few decades ago most of the corporate executives at Boeing were engineers or pilots at some point in their careers. Since the people that understood why certain costs were important to keep paying to keep making great airplanes were in positions of authority, Boeing maintained its status as a high quality brand. However, the company (specifically after a major merger in '97) has steadily been taken over by people who only know business. Since they don't understand why this redundancy is important, or why you can't increase the interval between checks any further without increasing risks to unacceptable levels, Boeing is now famous for planes that fall apart midair.<br /> <br /> We're seeing this all over the place. There's plenty examples in Hollywood just looking at the utter mess of a company Warner Bros has turned into.<br /> <br /> 2) The impact of Covid on audience viewing habits and a failure of big movie studios to adjust. 2020-2023 have been the worst box office grossing year since 2005. While people not going to the movies seems to be changing, we're still well below where the trend line was headed from 2015-2019. A lot of people like streaming the newest movies at home. &quot;Going to the theaters&quot; is more of a thing done once a month or two, instead of a few times a month Studios have generally been failing to entice people to go back to the older ways of consuming films.<br /> <br /> The only major adjustment (and this started during Covid, not after the recent WGA strike) is that the studios are putting out less films. Though an interesting note is they're averaging better returns. That is, with less films to go see, people are actually going and seeing more of what comes out each year. So if the lesson the big studios has gotten is less films and focus on ones that make the most money, the &quot;slump&quot; is just a reaction to the 2010s completely over saturating the market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T13:45:12-07:00","id":1534413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534402#post1534402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a bit overhyped? This is hardly the first time trailers have used material that wasn't in the final film; esp. in the era of extensive digital effects. It's not the first time it's been done purposefully to impact audience expectations in ways that feel exploitative instead of evocative.<br /> <br /> Even the one novel part probably is overblown in terms of how much money they might have saved. &quot;We want 5 seconds of a fly over of a photorealistic postwar Las Vegas&quot; isn't some massive payday for a digital artist. It's certainly more expensive to have a human do it (with plenty of assistance from &quot;dumb&quot; algorithms), but having a human do the prompts and then either that same person or someone else actually make the final product look good-enough still means paying for work.<br /> <br /> I feel like Disney/Marvel's doing the whole opening credits sequence like this for Secret Invasion (and it being so underwhelming for it) is a much better example of how this is going to be done poorly by giant companies, and how it's going to really negatively impact the final product.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, in the context of the movie Civil War it is misleading. It's not that type of movie. It's been done before...? Okay, still doesn't make it a good thing. And using AI is an additional issue. The images, if you look closely, have the same issues as the Marvel Opening sequence because those images look horrible if you look at the details in the images. And a digital artist wouldn't be that much more expensive than the AI-guy...? That's one hell of a stupid argument. First of all, those artists deserve to be paid more and second of all, that doesn't make AI-art a good thing to use instead.<br /> <br /> I think the &quot;overhyping&quot; is coming from you. You're blowing things way out of proportion with what you describe there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","user":"Knightingale","date":". 04-18-2024, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T15:43:49-07:00","id":1534417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534413#post1534413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, still doesn't make it a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In response to the vast majority of your post:<br /> <br /> I never said it was a good thing. I was arguing that in the broad scheme of things it's a relatively minor thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all, those artists deserve to be paid more... </div> </div> </div>OK, on top of the goal post shit:<br /> <br /> Lets say a digital artist would have gotten $5K for the job, should have gotten paid $10K for the job, and the studio cut corners and only spent $2K on the job. The idea that the use of generative algorithms was picked so the studio could save money just doesn't make sense if it saved them $3K on a $50m film.<br /> <br /> The picked it because it's faster and they could pump out a trailer while the movie wasn't finished. Which isn't good, but if you feel so strongly about these things, knowing why bad choices are being made is important to understanding how to work towards solving the problems<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the &quot;overhyping&quot; is coming from you. You're blowing things way out of proportion with what you describe there. </div> </div> </div>I literally have no idea what this is supposed to mean.<br /> <br /> Do you think I'm overhyping how common misleading trailers are? If so, check of &quot;Never Trust a Trailer&quot; on TVTropes... a site that's hardly some exhaustive list of such things. It had to be subdivided into all the ways trailers can be misleading (including using footage filmed for the movie but cut later vs. stuff made just for the trailer). Since it came up, the MCU has it's own sub-subpage on it. Misleading trailers are very common. Enough that I think it's weird if people think it's news worthy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T16:07:18-07:00","id":1534418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In response to the vast majority of your post:<br /> <br /> I never said it was a good thing. I was arguing that in the broad scheme of things it's a relatively minor thing. </div> </div> </div>And I never said it was the worst thing ever...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OK, on top of the goal post shit:<br /> <br /> Lets say a digital artist would have gotten $5K for the job, should have gotten paid $10K for the job, and the studio cut corners and only spent $2K on the job. The idea that the use of generative algorithms was picked so the studio could save money just doesn't make sense if it saved them $3K on a $50m film.<br /> <br /> The picked it because it's faster and they could pump out a trailer while the movie wasn't finished. Which isn't good, but if you feel so strongly about these things, knowing why bad choices are being made is important to understanding how to work towards solving the problems\u200b </div> </div> </div>I was simply responding to your downplaying of the situation and your &quot;Fuck artists. AI Art is just as good!&quot;-attitude. But you akcnowledged it isn't good so thank you for just repeating to me what I've already said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I literally have no idea what this is supposed to mean.<br /> <br /> Do you think I'm overhyping how common misleading trailers are? If so, check of &quot;Never Trust a Trailer&quot; on TVTropes... a site that's hardly some exhaustive list of such things. It had to be subdivided into all the ways trailers can be misleading (including using footage filmed for the movie but cut later vs. stuff made just for the trailer). Since it came up, the MCU has it's own sub-subpage on it. Misleading trailers are very common. Enough that I think it's weird if people think it's news worthy.\u200b </div> </div> </div>You think if a bad thing is considered &quot;commonplace&quot; there's no value in talking about it?! That's an insane take... You used the word &quot;overhype&quot; to downplay bad practices in the industry! Just because you're so cynical that &quot;good&quot; and &quot;bad&quot; are meaningless words to you now doesn't mean conversations about bad stuff should get shut down!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T18:19:00-07:00","id":1534420,"title":"","content":"Quality is way important the quantity for sure Heavy Arms and Jesterbells was commenting on the notion that Hollywood was counting on system that might not be sustainable anymore with changes in the medium and viewing habits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T18:37:17-07:00","id":1534423,"title":"","content":"Movie Trailers are very misleading and I've lost count how many times I was disappointed how poor a film was due to an awesome trailer or how poor a trailer was for a really good movie that we watched at home or in the theatres which is a rare thing for me as I find it to noisy and cold to enjoy the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T20:46:46-07:00","id":1534431,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Please keep it civil </b></span>(no pun intended.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T04:01:55-07:00","id":1534438,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a><br /> <br /> I would love to have an actual conversation about this. The problem is that you're not responding to what I'm actually saying. If you want to have a discussion, where you're going to actually take what I typed in it's totality, and respond to it with reasoned points? Let's go for it If you're going to keep slinging ad hominem snark at me while beating up strawmen, you've successfully shutdown the conversation all on your own.<br /> <br /> I understand just fine how a post can stick in the craw and make someone want to let another poster know it... but I cannot, for the life of me, see what I said that instigated this ramping up so intensely and so fast. So whether we try again, or just drop it, if you're willing I'd still like to know because I'd prefer we not repeat this outcome on the next disagreement we're bound to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T10:41:14-07:00","id":1534448,"title":"","content":"So Heavy Arms what ideas do you have to improve the Entertainment business as we are seeing such a drastic change in the last few years since Covid 19 changed things so much along with streaming services? I know it's not any one thing that is causing such a decline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T14:26:19-07:00","id":1534460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534438#post1534438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a><br /> <br /> I would love to have an actual conversation about this. The problem is that you're not responding to what I'm actually saying. If you want to have a discussion, where you're going to actually take what I typed in it's totality, and respond to it with reasoned points? Let's go for it If you're going to keep slinging ad hominem snark at me while beating up strawmen, you've successfully shutdown the conversation all on your own.<br /> <br /> I understand just fine how a post can stick in the craw and make someone want to let another poster know it... but I cannot, for the life of me, see what I said that instigated this ramping up so intensely and so fast. So whether we try again, or just drop it, if you're willing I'd still like to know because I'd prefer we not repeat this outcome on the next disagreement we're bound to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know why I made the initial post about that Civil War marketing? Because it's <i>recent</i>. I wasn't writing a manifesto about the usage of AI-art or the unreliability of movie-marketing for all of movie-history. I was just mentioning something that happened <i>recently</i>.<br /> <br /> And then you come in. You say it's &quot;overhyped&quot; and &quot;Hey, trailers have been misleading in the past. No big deal.&quot; and &quot;Look, there have been worse instances of AI-art actually, you know. So, again, no big deal what happened here.&quot;. But it was the first word that really ticked me off... &quot;overhyped&quot;. You just reminded me of a person who was defending horse-armor in Elder Scrolls Oblivion and that this microtransaction isn't that big of a deal (in other words, &quot;overhyped&quot;). And now all these years later we know that it was the first step in a long line of escalations to where we are now.<br /> <br /> So, I apologize for the ad hominems but it pisses me off to see someone look at a bad thing and ignore the context and potential consequences... and then just dismiss it as &quot;overhyped&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T17:13:21-07:00","id":1534468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534448#post1534448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Heavy Arms what ideas do you have to improve the Entertainment business as we are seeing such a drastic change in the last few years since Covid 19 changed things so much along with streaming services? I know it's not any one thing that is causing such a decline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really address this because the premise and phrasing isn't something I agree with.<br /> <br /> Entertainment, as a business, is doing great by the metrics businesses use: what makes executives and investors more money. Even all the stuff consumers find bad isn't so bad that it's causing the money line to go down. There isn't a decline in the business, even if there was a Covid slump and recovery is slower than projected: slower recovery still means the money line is going up for the business.<br /> <br /> Improving the entertainment we as consumers get, and improving the lives of the workers that make it? Those involve &quot;hurting&quot; the business with things like regulations (if not rejecting the idea of entertainment as a privatized business as appropriate at all) in order to recalibrate corporate incentives to be more responsive to the need to make high quality products in order to cultivate an enduring industry that can afford to pay its employees well.<br /> <br /> Or tl;dr: the problem with the entertainment business is that it's a business in the current economy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534460#post1534460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know why I made the initial post about that Civil War marketing? Because it's <i>recent</i>. I wasn't writing a manifesto about the usage of AI-art or the unreliability of movie-marketing for all of movie-history. I was just mentioning something that happened <i>recently</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you really think I can't keep this to recent things? A24 was yelled at on the Internet in 2021 for the Green Knight trailer being misleading as the trailer makes it look like a low fantasy modern take on the old poem, and it's... very much not a fun fantasy adventure based on an Arthurian epic poem.<br /> <br /> Madame Web (just this year) was made fun of for it's trailer being just another part of how sloppy the movie was as the trailer has a few prominent moments of things in it that got cut from the final film.<br /> <br /> Something that I think is good news even if I also think the case was rightfully dismissed: 2022-23 saw resolution of a 2019 lawsuit of misleading trailers being false advertising,which included at whole drawn out legal battle over whether trailers can be sued as false advertising.. and at least in California? They can be. There's actually a tool now for consumers to push back against misleading trailers even if the bar for misleading advertising is fairly high to meet. I mean it's mind-boggling to me that trailers... which are literal marketing tools to promote a product... took years to resolve fell under false advertising laws... but at least it actually did finally get resolved recently.<br /> <br /> But history also gives us context. Misleading trailers can be complicated in how they're received. Movies with twists in them, or surprise cameos in them, frequently &quot;mislead&quot; to avoid revealing something they want the audience to experience during the film. The original Black Christmas trailer is beloved despite being entirely original footage because it's basically a short film version of the story full of fun slasher moments that are entirely different from the kills in the movie that doesn't give away the real movie's major twist. While people were generally annoyed at Disney/Marvel for trying to by coy about Tobey Maguire and Andrew Garfield being in Spider-Man: No Way Home well after the cat was out of the bag (including digitally editing non-Tom Holland Spider-Men from shots in the trailer that are in the final film)... for the most part people just thought it was silly that the marketing team kept trying to keep something secret.<br /> <br /> Misleading trailers just aren't inherently bad. Sometimes movie goers appreciate that the trailer was tricky about something because there was a positive pay off when watching the film. Most of the time people just don't care, because the misleading parts were inconsequential to experiencing the film and trailers are generally made before movies are finished so small discrepancies are bound to happen (2024's Godzilla x Kong: New Empire's trailer ran into this). Sometimes that are bad because they're manipulative and make watching the movie worse from the false expectations.<br /> <br /> But there's also a subjective aspect to this. Most people did not think Ana de Armas being in the trailers for a movie but her character being cut in the final edit of the movie - the basis of the 2019 lawsuit - is not something all that detrimental to enjoying the film... but two guys who apparently only saw the film Yesterday because she was in the trailer went so far as to sue over it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And now all these years later we know that it was the first step in a long line of escalations to where we are now. </div> </div> </div>But the Civil War trailer isn't some first step down a slippery slope. That's why I brought up all those other things. It's not a sign of trailers getting more misleading. It's not a sign of generative algorithms being used in intensely bad ways. It's not the fucking horse armor.<br /> <br /> As well, I think trailers are a place where generative algorithms can be used positively (with appropriate protections for human workers like the SAG and WGA strikes fought for if not as great as a final deal as possible). The artists and editors that make trailers get handed 4-6 hours of partially finished movie, a pile of notes from directors, producers, and marketing execs that all want different things in the trailer, and have to make a tiny ad out of it to sell the movie with. These are people who generally do not have a budget to go shoot scenes just for the trailer, or do a full photorealistic digital animation. They don't have the power in the scheme of things to ask for more material and are already trying to figure out how to make something out of all the stuff they already have... frequently having to already plan to touch up shots they have key dialogue or images for the trailer but haven't been finalized by the main film editors.<br /> <br /> I'm very aware there are probably big issue with things like whatever the algorithm was already trained on being ethically dubious at best. But papering over a few seconds in a trailer to get something in when the studios didn't provide them with the materials to match the ask? Why is this a bad place for this set of tools? Like any tool how you use it matters, but where is this a slippery slope towards? What's the problematic end result of trailer makers having tools to do their jobs better as a group that could really benefit from applications here? Yes, make sure there's humans, and yes, make sure they're paid properly. But not every generative algorithm use is actually bad. What is so bad as a potential consequence of being able to use this tech to fill in gaps in trailers... something that's lead to a century of bad trailers because no other tool has solved the problem yet?<br /> <br /> I'm open to the argument here, but I'd like to hear one that isn't &quot;AI bad, all uses must be fought, or more bad will happen.&quot; The article and your posts don't have any more context than that. There's no statement of what the risk is, what the problem will be in 10 year... just some very bad posters for a movie because they have images that don't make sense. How can I be ignoring something unstated? What's the consequence of A24's decision here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I apologize for the ad hominems but it pisses me off to see someone look at a bad thing and ignore the context and potential consequences... and then just dismiss it as &quot;overhyped&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the intent of the apology here, but the heavy caveat is... hard to ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T18:22:01-07:00","id":1534472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534468#post1534468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you really think I can't keep this to recent things? A24 was yelled at on the Internet in 2021 for the Green Knight trailer being misleading as the trailer makes it look like a low fantasy modern take on the old poem, and it's... very much not a fun fantasy adventure based on an Arthurian epic poem.<br /> <br /> Madame Web (just this year) was made fun of for it's trailer being just another part of how sloppy the movie was as the trailer has a few prominent moments of things in it that got cut from the final film.<br /> <br /> Something that I think is good news even if I also think the case was rightfully dismissed: 2022-23 saw resolution of a 2019 lawsuit of misleading trailers being false advertising,which included at whole drawn out legal battle over whether trailers can be sued as false advertising.. and at least in California? They can be. There's actually a tool now for consumers to push back against misleading trailers even if the bar for misleading advertising is fairly high to meet. I mean it's mind-boggling to me that trailers... which are literal marketing tools to promote a product... took years to resolve fell under false advertising laws... but at least it actually did finally get resolved recently.<br /> <br /> But history also gives us context. Misleading trailers can be complicated in how they're received. Movies with twists in them, or surprise cameos in them, frequently &quot;mislead&quot; to avoid revealing something they want the audience to experience during the film. The original Black Christmas trailer is beloved despite being entirely original footage because it's basically a short film version of the story full of fun slasher moments that are entirely different from the kills in the movie that doesn't give away the real movie's major twist. While people were generally annoyed at Disney/Marvel for trying to by coy about Tobey Maguire and Andrew Garfield being in Spider-Man: No Way Home well after the cat was out of the bag (including digitally editing non-Tom Holland Spider-Men from shots in the trailer that are in the final film)... for the most part people just thought it was silly that the marketing team kept trying to keep something secret.<br /> <br /> Misleading trailers just aren't inherently bad. Sometimes movie goers appreciate that the trailer was tricky about something because there was a positive pay off when watching the film. Most of the time people just don't care, because the misleading parts were inconsequential to experiencing the film and trailers are generally made before movies are finished so small discrepancies are bound to happen (2024's Godzilla x Kong: New Empire's trailer ran into this). Sometimes that are bad because they're manipulative and make watching the movie worse from the false expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cMisleading trailers trailers just aren\u2019t inherently bad.\u201d I noticed you never mentioned the movie we\u2019re actually talking about here. Have you even seen Civil War and can judge the marketing based on that? I was talking about Civil War and an issue with its marketing. That\u2019s it.<br /> <br /> This was never supposed to be about the idea of misleading trailers in general. It was about how this specific marketing for this specific film is bad. And the potential for it to get worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534468#post1534468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Civil War trailer isn't some first step down a slippery slope. That's why I brought up all those other things. It's not a sign of trailers getting more misleading. It's not a sign of generative algorithms being used in intensely bad ways. It's not the fucking horse armor.<br /> <br /> As well, I think trailers are a place where generative algorithms can be used positively (with appropriate protections for human workers like the SAG and WGA strikes fought for if not as great as a final deal as possible). The artists and editors that make trailers get handed 4-6 hours of partially finished movie, a pile of notes from directors, producers, and marketing execs that all want different things in the trailer, and have to make a tiny ad out of it to sell the movie with. These are people who generally do not have a budget to go shoot scenes just for the trailer, or do a full photorealistic digital animation. They don't have the power in the scheme of things to ask for more material and are already trying to figure out how to make something out of all the stuff they already have... frequently having to already plan to touch up shots they have key dialogue or images for the trailer but haven't been finalized by the main film editors.<br /> <br /> I'm very aware there are probably big issue with things like whatever the algorithm was already trained on being ethically dubious at best. But papering over a few seconds in a trailer to get something in when the studios didn't provide them with the materials to match the ask? Why is this a bad place for this set of tools? Like any tool how you use it matters, but where is this a slippery slope towards? What's the problematic end result of trailer makers having tools to do their jobs better as a group that could really benefit from applications here? Yes, make sure there's humans, and yes, make sure they're paid properly. But not every generative algorithm use is actually bad. What is so bad as a potential consequence of being able to use this tech to fill in gaps in trailers... something that's lead to a century of bad trailers because no other tool has solved the problem yet?<br /> <br /> I'm open to the argument here, but I'd like to hear one that isn't &quot;AI bad, all uses must be fought, or more bad will happen.&quot; The article and your posts don't have any more context than that. There's no statement of what the risk is, what the problem will be in 10 year... just some very bad posters for a movie because they have images that don't make sense. How can I be ignoring something unstated? What's the consequence of A24's decision here?<br /> I appreciate the intent of the apology here, but the heavy caveat is... hard to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that we\u2019re not really talking about \u201cartificial intelligences\u201d here, with an emphasis on \u201cintelligence\u201d. ChatGP, Siri, Alexa\u2026 they\u2019re all dumb as rocks. They\u2019re algorithms that recognize patterns and respond to that \u2013 but they don\u2019t think.<br /> <br /> So you just gotta feed more data to the algorithm \u2013 except we can\u2019t. There just isn\u2019t enough. Yep, even with all the surveillance we suffer through, these algorithms need even more data. In trying to make the algorithms better, <a href=\"https://www.appen.com/blog/data-crisis-in-the-ai-economy\" target=\"_blank\">they're gonna run into a brick wall</a>.<br /> <br /> And if you don\u2019t deliver even more data to refine the algorithms\u2026 well, then these algorithms just start cannibalizing each other and start hallucinating all over the place. And \u201challucinations\u201d in this case means stuff like producing art of humans with 13 fingers or a text-language-models recommending books to someone that don\u2019t exist. All because these algorithms don\u2019t actually think. They just operate based on the data they have and make shit up that fits the answer. The less data, the more bullshit you get. And because they can't get the amount of data they need, these algorithms will always produce bullshit from time to time.<br /> <br /> My position is that you can't rely on this technology at this moment. It's not reliable enough to be usable for professional scenarios. These algorithms that are available now don't think and are prone to failure. Because in the long run the algorithms are gonna get worse, not better because of the need for data-sets and the way it then starts pulling in old AI-generated data for new AI-generated data which corrupts the whole thing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","user":"Knightingale","date":". 04-20-2024, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T11:59:26-07:00","id":1534497,"title":"","content":"Games Workshop wants to be more inclusive and all I can say is how about you make your sourcebooks and miniatures less expensive for the people who are interested in the setting. That might improve interest in your product in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T12:01:23-07:00","id":1534498,"title":"","content":"You said Warner Bros is having trouble in one of your posts Heavy Arms? Can you explain further as I remember you telling me that having a bunch of flops in a row wasn't worrisome in of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T13:18:59-07:00","id":1534507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534472#post1534472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you even seen Civil War and can judge the marketing based on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I plead the 5th, but will note that the only movie theater with in a reasonable distance from me was featured in a Daily Show segment of Jordan Klepper out interviewing people at a political rally and since then I haven't had a good way to legally watch films in theaters without giving money to a local privately owned business that decided to strongly express their political views at the risk of losing business from folks like me.<br /> <br /> That said, I do feel very confident for strictly hypothetical reasons, that Civil War is a film that tried to be a more mature version of The Purge or a less religion focused Red State, but in its technical excellence and superior artistry, managed to produce a far blander end result of a very long PSA of how somehow an egg in a frying pan represents the brains of well armed people poisoned by tribalism.<br /> <br /> Had the inexplicable giant swan actually been in the film, and never actually addressed (along with so many things that would be vital to explain to actually make a point, but are never really explained) I would, hypothetically, consider it an improvement.<br /> <br /> So, yes, if we're &quot;just&quot; talking about the film, my disappointment in the final product is certainly part of my bias regarding how much I care about it's marketing campaign's quality. There's also not a whole lot to say if we all agree it was bad, and are just differing on how bad it was (or apparently could get later).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was about how this specific marketing for this specific film is bad. And the potential for it to get worse. </div> </div> </div>This is inherently self-contradictory and feels like a lot of the sources of conflict in our posts about this.<br /> <br /> We cannot just be talking about one film's marketing campaign in isolation (I would object to the idea that you can actually do that anyway), while also be examining the potential for movie marketing to get worse. The bigger picture of &quot;potential for it to get worse&quot; means we're not just talking about Civil War.<br /> <br /> For me if feels like an easy rhetorical dodge. Any time you might have to make a subjective case on the quality of Civil War's marketing campaign (objectively however weird some of the posters are, the movie is number 1 in the box office two weeks in a row and is on pace to have put enough butts in seats to be profitable, which is marketing's job), you can deflect to how that's not grappling with the bigger implications of what this all mean. When I press on what the consequences you're worried about actually are... deflect back to &quot;this is just about Civil War.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that we\u2019re not really talking about \u201cartificial intelligences\u201d here, with an emphasis on \u201cintelligence\u201d. ChatGP, Siri, Alexa\u2026 they\u2019re all dumb as rocks. They\u2019re algorithms that recognize patterns and respond to that \u2013 but they don\u2019t think. </div> </div> </div>Do you think I've been typing out &quot;generative algorithm&quot; so much for no reason? That I've avoiding using &quot;AI&quot; to describe things when discussing my personal positions randomly?<br /> <br /> Though I do really dislike this equivocation. I do very much understand the potential dangers of the technology involved, but debates about what AI really is have been going on since before we had digital computers, partially because we can't even scientifically define &quot;natural&quot; intelligence in a functional manner to then gauge artificial intelligence's parameters.<br /> <br /> I remember back when Apple decided to include ELIZA on computers intended for use in schools, and a lot of hand wringing about exposing children to AI because who knows what a chatbot designed to beat the Turning test without access to the Internet might do outside of computer science labs. I remember when nobody would get huff about people referring to NPC scripting in video games as the game &quot;AI.&quot; As long as we've had a concept of digital computers, there has been a conflict between &quot;AI&quot; as a term for using computers to approximate intelligence well enough for a given application, and &quot;AI&quot; as a term for the digital singularity where algorithms finally achieve a state of intelligence independent of humanity's inputs and controls.<br /> <br /> While I'm certainly cynical and jaded, I'm also just in a position to have lived through multiple &quot;AI&quot; to-dos to see that the positives are never as good as we hoped, but the negatives have never been as bad as people feared at the time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you just gotta feed more data to the algorithm \u2013 except we can\u2019t. </div> </div> </div>OK, you're overgeneralizing here. Generative algorithm models do not, inherently, require a constant influx of data. Bullshit like ChatGPT and all those do, because of how they're being applied. They're the digital version of corporate executives that want to keep making the arbitrary line going up and up despite how ridiculous that is. Just like you can run a company without being focused on making the magic money line increasing every year, you can run a generative AI on a limited data set; and your product will probably be better off for it.<br /> <br /> When we look at the good things people have done with generative algorithms (something that's actually been around since the 60s), it generally comes from highly curated limited datasets because they're using the right tool for a specific job. They don't need, or want, extraneous data because that would make the results worse.<br /> <br /> If we want to get back to movies, want to know why the CGI in movies like Jurassic Park and the first Matrix looked so good? Interpolation. Digital interpolation in film editing is the process of digitally creating frames that we never filmed to smooth out the interactions between filmed and digital elements. The Matrix is a better example. The first bullet time rigs had one major problem... there were gaps that made the initial filming look really choppy because the technology at the time forced them do use a static array of cameras and each gap between lenses lead to a gap in the film and visual chops. So, digital interpolation was used to look at frames before and after each break, and digitally fill in frames to create the illusion of a seamless camera movement.<br /> <br /> How? Generative algorithms. A computer did that work, not a human sitting there drawing each extra frame digitally. It's the exact same technology that the new wave of &quot;AIs&quot; use, and one digital artists have been using for decades, but appropriately used to a specific application and highly curated dataset to ensure the best possible results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In trying to make the algorithms better, <a href=\"https://www.appen.com/blog/data-crisis-in-the-ai-economy\" target=\"_blank\">they're gonna run into a brick wall</a>. </div> </div> </div>First, just to note, you linked to an ad for a company.<br /> <br /> Second... this is kinda my point? The potential dangers and consequences are inherently constrained by the limitations of the technology. How worried should I really be about ChatGPT when ti's eating itself into oblivion from scrapping up all the data? I'm not worried about these systems replacing human artists because these systems generally produce mediocre work at best. I'm worried about things like the massive amount of e-waste and energy production going into powering them. I'm worried about the exploitation of data scrapping. Though most of these are problems with every tech-fad now.<br /> <br /> The future is customer service calls where to consumer frustration it's harder to tell if we're talking to a machine or a human because we'd rather know, even as companies tell us that the user experience is better the longer it takes to figure it out (or the ruder we are to living people trying to pay rent and buy food to test them). Because it's a limited data set. &quot;Customer service voice&quot; is a thing where call center employees are already encouraged to homogenize their voices. They only need to be able to make small talk and then be able to answer questions about the product the company sells/services so they don't need to care about regurgitating all of Wikipedia on demand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you don\u2019t deliver even more data to refine the algorithms\u2026 well, then these algorithms just start cannibalizing each other and start hallucinating all over the place. </div> </div> </div>Again, it's about application. Using them to speed up research into protein folding was highly successful and the protein folding algorithm didn't go off the rails because of it's limited data set and start making up new molecules that defy the laws of physics. It kept to what it was made to do, because nobody tried to make it do something else.<br /> <br /> Computer scientists have known this for ages. This is part of the plot of 2001: A Space Odyssey. HAL 9000 didn't just flip out because AI's inherently go data-crazy without proper inputs. It got contradictory inputs and processed them to the best of its abilities. The scary thing about HAL wasn't that it defied orders... but that it followed them as optimally as possible.<br /> <br /> Garbage in, garbage out. That's the phrase for a reason. Data set size is not part of that phrase for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My position is that you can't rely on this technology at this moment. It's not reliable enough to be usable for professional scenarios. </div> </div> </div>And my position is that people that know what they're doing have been successfully using this technology in profession scenarios for decades, and for even longer we've know the primary source of instability in automated functions is the humans, not the algorithms. Fad generative algorithms are made by people that aren't trying to do something specific, creating a design-side gigo problem, and were then released to the wild with minimal controls creating a user-side gigo problem. Ones designed by professionals for professional use consistently perform to expectations by reducing gigo as much as possible.<br /> <br /> The fact that Elon Musk can't make a successful line of trucks does not mean trucks are a flawed concept nobody should be using.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T13:24:44-07:00","id":1534508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534497#post1534497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Games Workshop wants to be more inclusive and all I can say is how about you make your sourcebooks and miniatures less expensive for the people who are interested in the setting. That might improve interest in your product in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>GW is as inclusive as they've always been. They've just stepped up their efforts to remind people of it.<br /> <br /> Also... GW's employees need to make a living. If I hear complaints from them that GW's raising prices and the top folks at the company are just pocketing it? I'll be mad. Right now their production costs are up, cost of living for their employees are up, and asking them to reduce prices means you're asking them to sacrifice quality or employee compensation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T13:10:59-07:00","id":1534603,"title":"","content":"I know that Games Workshop is in some hot water with the recent choice to have female Custodios in the setting and people are pointing out that it goes against the lore and asking why they didn't expand on the Sisters Of Silence and Sisters Of Battle who are pretty cool and bad ass factions that work well with the Space Marines &amp; Custodios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T16:41:07-07:00","id":1534666,"title":"","content":"&quot;In hot water&quot; is a bit much for a bunch of people on X-Twitter whining about lore they don't actually care about treating as sacred unchangeable material.<br /> <br /> The Custodes (like lots of Imperium units) were written as male-default and this lead to the conclusion that they were male exclusive. Nothing in the current lore makes the existence of female Custodes conflict with anything other that unit descriptions defaulting to using male pronouns to describe them.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that this is nothing compared to the complete retcon the Custodes had from early WH40K (where they didn't use superior versions of Space Marine gear, but were actually sparsely armed and armored), and instead of being the most loyal humans to the Emperor in existence, they were treated closer to the historical Roman Praetorian Guard and had the power to overthrow the Emperor making them a more nuanced political group in the setting.<br /> <br /> The whining on the Internet is also self-contradictory to people complaining about female Space Marines outside of specific Legions too. One of the main arguments on why the Legions are mono-sex, is that they're basically clones with some gene-modification every once and a while. The Custodes aren't clones, but rather modified individuals that were hand selected by the Emperor early in his reign. Their creation killed thousands for every successful gene-modification and near immortality granted from the Emperor... Custodes couldn't really be that picky about sex compared to picking those that have a chance to survive the process.<br /> <br /> In other words, it's not about the lore. They cherry pick lore to try to hide behind the lore as their reasoning. It's about not liking excuses to gatekeep the hobby being taken from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T00:09:30-07:00","id":1534683,"title":"","content":"I think it's just a case of bad PR. What made it go from bad to worse was the ill-advised Tweet from the Warhammer-account saying that there have always been female Custodes. That of course isn't the case. Both Space Marines and Custodes have been described as exclusively male for the last ten years or so and their creation-process of taking humans and changing them has also specifically referenced male candidates.<br /> <br /> But could female Custodes be introduced? Sure. It wouldn't be any bigger of a change than introducing Primaris Space Marines. Or could you just retcon it and say &quot;In this version there have always been female and male Custodes.&quot;? Sure. The Necrons got a huge retcon for their whole faction a couple editions ago, for example. So it's not like this sort of thing never happens with Warhammer lore.<br /> <br /> What made it blow up was to act like it isn't a change. And then you had the whole &quot;go woke, go broke&quot;-crowd coming in who made it all about &quot;woke&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T04:41:57-07:00","id":1534686,"title":"","content":"GW is a publicly traded company, so we know a lot more about it's finances than most gaming hobby companies.<br /> <br /> This, like other &quot;woke&quot; moves in the past year aren't bad PR for them. The &quot;controversies&quot; reveal the people opposed to the shifts in the game are a small group of people relative to the total fanbase; which comes out in droves to show how much they want to sit down any play the game, compare painting tips, and so on, and have fun instead of getting into lore flame wars. Which seems to be doing great for GW as their sales figures have stay relatively strong after a massive boost during the Covid lock downs (apparently a lot of people decided to make WH40K model work a Covid to-do item) with a small correction as places opened back up and everyone didn't have quite as much free time.<br /> <br /> GW is the exact opposite of &quot;go woke, go broke,&quot; since their stock price is currently more than double it's best value in 2019, and is near the highest it's been ever (and has been holding fairly strongly there for the past two years). The company literally got much richer.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, they're not in hot water. It wasn't a &quot;bad PR move.&quot; For all the angry digital posts out there, GW is coming off looking good to far more consumers than they're pissing off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T05:12:20-07:00","id":1534687,"title":"","content":"It is a bad PR move in the sense that they made a claim that isn't true and in terms of transparency and consistent worldbuilding, it isn't nice. If they want to retcon something, they should just say so. That's the part that's bothering me. At least show some consistency with the setting. There's currently no in-universe reason for female Custodes. Like I said, it's not like you can't do it. But they could've at least tried to make it make sense.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;go woke, go broke&quot;-crowd... I mean, they do their usual thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T08:02:01-07:00","id":1534693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534687#post1534687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's currently no in-universe reason for female Custodes. Like I said, it's not like you can't do it. But they could've at least tried to make it make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I freely admit I know virtually nothing about Warhammer lore, but I'm curious as to the reasoning that they have to &quot;try to make it make sense&quot; when a woman (or anything that's not a white male) shows up in a specific role. Why does any human need an elaborate story to justify what as near as I can tell amounts to a job description with some sci-fi benefits. That reasoning seems super faulty and extremely gatekeepy to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T08:57:24-07:00","id":1534697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534693#post1534693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I freely admit I know virtually nothing about Warhammer lore, but I'm curious as to the reasoning that they have to &quot;try to make it make sense&quot; when a woman (or anything that's not a white male) shows up in a specific role. Why does any human need an elaborate story to justify what as near as I can tell amounts to a job description with some sci-fi benefits. That reasoning seems super faulty and extremely gatekeepy to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, as a fan of Warhammer lore without getting too much into it, the first thing is that it's supposed to be a flaw in the Emperor's vision. The Primarchs are all male... the Thunder-Warriors (which was a previous version of the Space Marines that were then killed by the Emperor as he developed the idea for the Space Marines), the Space Marines, the Custodes, same deal. And that's a flaw. The whole technology for making all these gene-crafted warriors comes from this specific class of all-female gene-crafters who lived on Luna (in other words, the moon) and the Emperor spared them in his conquest of Terra in exchange for their knowledge. And there's a conversation in one of the books with these gene-witches who have some doubts about the Emperor's vision and that making these transhuman warriors all-male wasn't the smartest idea.<br /> <br /> But what also gets covered in the Horus-Heresy-book-series is that to the Emperor they're all just tools. The Primarchs, the Thunder-Warriors, Space Marines... they're all male because they're tools for war and men are better at war. Of course, that's a very reductive look at this. But there's also the question in the Horus-Heresy-series at the beginning before the whole civil war breaks out where the Primarchs wonder that if the Emperor were to succeed and conquer the whole galaxy, would he just kill all the Space Marines because he doesn't need them anymore in the same way he ordered the death of the Thunder Warriors after the conquest of Terra. That's the kind of person the Emperor is. Like there's a scene in one of the novels where the Emperor tells someone that he lets the Primarchs call him father because it's convenient and makes it more likely that they stay loyal but he has never thought of himself as their father. The Emperor isn't a good guy in the 40k lore. Neither the Emperor's vision in this regard nor the idea of these transhuman beings all being male are supposed to be good things.<br /> <br /> That's of course a tricky thing. What you're trying to balance here is a showcase of how the lack of diversity is a bad thing but then you get your various chuds who unironically think that this is a good thing. Also, a part of a good Space Marine story is that they may be transhuman but they aren't exactly better than normal humans in all aspects. In some ways, they're worse. And the same applies to the Custodes and the Primarchs. They're supposed to be deeply flawed beings.<br /> <br /> And the diversity has gotten better. The Sisters of Battle are now a full-fledged playable faction, there's the Sisters of Silence, Space Marines don't have to be white and pretty much all the other factions can be diverse - with Orks and Tyranids being the exception, I guess. They don't really have genders.<br /> <br /> But as stated before: You can do it. Here's how I would integrate it from a lore-perspective, if, for example, it's a game of Wrath and Glory and somebody wants to play a female Custodes:<ul><li>After Primarch Guilliman's return the Custodes have left Terra for the first time in ten thousand years. Now that they're seeing more combat and more casualties, they take both sons and daughters from Terra and try to turn them into Custodes.</li> <li>The process of making a Custodes is so radical that it doesn't matter whether you take young girls or boys. They come out the same way if they survive the process. Huge height, deep voice... A Custodes who was born as a girl is indistinguishable from a Custodes who was born as a boy.</li> <li>To add to that: One thing about Custodes is that they have hundreds of names, so whether their preferred names are male- or female-coded can also be easily explained.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","user":"Knightingale","date":". 04-25-2024, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T12:12:58-07:00","id":1534710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534693#post1534693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I freely admit I know virtually nothing about Warhammer lore, but I'm curious as to the reasoning that they have to &quot;try to make it make sense&quot; when a woman (or anything that's not a white male) shows up in a specific role. Why does any human need an elaborate story to justify what as near as I can tell amounts to a job description with some sci-fi benefits. That reasoning seems super faulty and extremely gatekeepy to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I can't find it on my current device, but I read a great piece about what makes Star War's Clone Troopers (and later how that impacted the normal Storm Troopers) all male good even in a modern context, and why trying to cling to the old lore of WH40K isn't. And while it addressed a lot of specifics, it really comes down to a simple point: the narrative intent of the setting.<br /> <br /> The Clone Troopers weren't just an attempt to make an army fast, but an large scale experiment in forced conformity. They all look the same (even outside of uniform), speak the same, they don't have names, they're all the same sex, etc. But part of the narrative intent is that individuality will find a way no matter how much an authoritarian tries to stamp it out. The Clone Troopers started getting unofficial names (in-universe), getting tattoos, having different hair styles, etc. as rebellion (Star Wars, rebel = good) against their forced conformity. Palpatine, unlike Tarkin apparently, learned his lesson and with the Storm Troopers recruited from the general population instead of using clones, loosened his grip so less would slip through his fingers. He created the Storm Troopers to have small illusions of individuality; just enough to keep them psychologically content without loosing the purpose of forcing people into a box. So a female Trooper would take some elaborate story to justify because being a Trooper isn't just a job description, it's a managed part of a tyrant's projection of power and elevation of an ideal citizenry. Being too short got you denied service as a Storm Trooper because it meant you weren't within the physical parameters to fit the propaganda.<br /> <br /> Early WH40K did actually have some narrative intent for satirizing military chauvinism and patriarchy that made the default all male human soldiers of the early material more sensible. There was a time in the lore where excluding AFAB individuals from serving in a job was part of WH40K satirical elements on how military machismo is symbiotic with fascism. But that was also a long time ago, many retcons ago, and so on (if one wants to put a delineation on it the current &quot;now&quot; of WH40K's narrative intent started in 2009's Rogue Trader by most reviews). The state of the game not just in the most recent edition, but where the game's been headed for over a decade, has included a slow but major shift in narrative intent that has eroded the original satire to something else (not bad, just different). Having female Custodes or Space Marines don't actually matter to the lore of WH40K as it's stood throughout the 2010s into now. Demanding it address the lore before that despite the lore shifting significantly is, very much, faulty and gatekeepy.<br /> <br /> Which is basically the problem. Well the problem for people complaining. GW is, as mentioned, doing great with sales so PR (who's job is ultimately marketing to drum up sales) isn't a problem if they're selling more stuff than ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T12:31:08-07:00","id":1534714,"title":"","content":"As a Warhammer fan, I can just say that's factually wrong and very clearly based on a serious lack of information and understanding. It's uninformed to the point of being a lie.<br /> <br /> The whole point of the Horus Heresy book series, which is this 60+ novel series plus the Siege of Terra series which is another 10 books or so, is that the Empire of Mankind is bad. And it was bad even before Horus Heresy. Some of the best recent novels by Black Library is about the depression of Chaos Space Marines in 40k who have realized that it was all bullshit from the very beginning as they're trying to survive. 10+ years of writers putting in the work to have a critical and progressive perspective on WH40k lore as it describes the events in 30k that led up to the Horus Heresy and what unfolded during it.<br /> <br /> So, great, now we have one side who's saying &quot;Warhammer is woke now! Burn it all down!&quot; and another side who's saying &quot;Warhammer was never woke! Burn it all down!&quot;. Oh well... just two completely uninformed groups of people shouting at each other. I'm sure this will go well...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T12:41:18-07:00","id":1534717,"title":"","content":"Yeah, nothing I've seen here screams &quot;aha! This is why women can't be x!&quot; The whole thing seems super gatekeepy based on outdated lore. In a world that racks up contradictions with every book they release, people only getting bent out of shape when the &quot;contradiction&quot; is due to increased diversity aren't actually upset about the lore issues, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T12:50:29-07:00","id":1534718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534717#post1534717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, nothing I've seen here screams &quot;aha! This is why women can't be x!&quot; The whole thing seems super gatekeepy based on outdated lore. In a world that racks up contradictions with every book they release, people only getting bent out of shape when the &quot;contradiction&quot; is due to increased diversity aren't actually upset about the lore issues, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the point is that they should explain it. And it's SO EASY!<br /> <br /> And it isn't outdated lore. Female Custodes did not exist before the latest Codex. It was understood that exclusively boys were used as recruits. That's what the Custodes Codex in January 2022 said. But the latest Codex also doesn't provide any new or extra lore to explain the existence of female Custodes. That's the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T12:51:37-07:00","id":1534719,"title":"","content":"It also should be noted that Space Marines and the Emperor personal guard have given up there basic humanity in the defense of the Imperium and don't have families or spouses to go home to see and when they are not fighting in battles, then they are training and the ruler of humanity had put in a flaw in his creations that prevent them from reproducing. In fact it's not unheard of that if they make it through the process that they lose chunks of there previous memories. So with the personal guards that have been selected from the first born males of the royal families of old Earth you run into the trouble of ending family lines going through this route. It can be done if Gulliman deciding that they need to expand the pool of recruits that stand out as he has woken up into a world that is drastically different then what he knew and what his &quot;father&quot; intended.<br /> <br /> When you create a Space Marine they are implanted with a gene seed of a the Primarch and they have been all been male and if a female was given that, she would lose much of her female attributes with all the genetic, cybernetic and psychological conditioning and here is the following of what you get as a space marine muscle mass is greatly increased, body fat is dramatically, extra vital organs are created and in general you are made into a super solider and a female space marine would be nearly indistingable unless she takes off her armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-25-2024, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T12:55:42-07:00","id":1534721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534718#post1534718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but the point is that they should explain it. And it's SO EASY!</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I don't think we need an explanation when anyone represented in the real world shows up in game. I think it is 100% fine to expand diversity without stopping or using precious word count to justify it. I reject that notion entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534718#post1534718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And it isn't outdated lore. Female Custodes did not exist before the latest Codex. It was understood that exclusively boys were used as recruits. That's what the Custodes Codex in January 2022 said. But the latest Codex also doesn't provide any new or extra lore to explain the existence of female Custodes. That's the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...the new Codex updates the lore. This makes contradictions in previous editions outdated, doesn't it? What am I missing here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T13:03:14-07:00","id":1534722,"title":"","content":"It's how they went about it by saying that they were always there and you just didn't know it. It could have been handled better and that returned Primarchs Roberto Gulliman and possibly Lionel Johnson at the behest of some vision from the Emperor decided to adjust there recruitment pool, but choose the best of the best female recruits that could handle the enchancements. They could have gave more the Sisters Of Silence &amp; Sisters of Battle who's training and equipment is on par with the two groups more screen time so to speak or even gave slight genetic reenginering to make them more deadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T13:27:43-07:00","id":1534726,"title":"","content":"Any explanation is likely to involve fictionalized Lego-style genetics and terms that would make no sense. How much of an explanation do you need when it's not going to actually make sense in the first place without jumping to the end result of &quot;The new unit type exists!&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T13:40:28-07:00","id":1534729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534721#post1534721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. I don't think we need an explanation when anyone represented in the real world shows up in game. I think it is 100% fine to expand diversity without stopping or using precious word count to justify it. I reject that notion entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I disagree. Worldbuilding matters more in that regard. I understand the value of adding diversity and representation but that has limits. Or are you saying that the Sisters of Battle faction in WH40k needs to have more male models in its army for the sake of diversity? I don't think Sisters of Battle players would be happy if you told them that there's this unit of prayer-brothers or something that's part of their army now.<br /> <br /> Also, with Custodes you have your diversity right there because in reality they're Custodes + Sisters of Silence. Of course, you don't see a lot of Sisters of Silence because one, their rules aren't very competitive, two, their models are quite old and/or not very impressive and three their model range is quite limited. From a financial standpoint, I get the idea of female Custodes... these Custodes probably sell way more than the Sisters of Silence models. But it's not like GW is really trying to sell people on fielding Sisters of Silence armies.<br /> <br /> And funny thing is... GW already did that. The Stormcast Eternals in Age of Sigmar are fantasy Space Marines and now it doesn't matter who's in the armor-suit, male or female. They are these souls from dead people who are particularly virtuous and Sigmar as a God plucks them out and puts them into armor-suits to fight for him. Those are the Stormcast Eternals. Their tragedy is that while they're definitely on the side of good in their warfare, every time they die a little bit of their humanity dies and yet Sigmar will revive them and send them into battle again untile they are hollowed out husks. And at that point, another soul gets grabbed to fill the armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534721#post1534721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean...the new Codex updates the lore. This makes contradictions in previous editions outdated, doesn't it? What am I missing here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the thing... they didn't update the lore. The whole female-Custodes-thing comes from a two-page short story they put into the newest army-Codex with a female Custodes while the rest of the book acts like female Custodes aren't a thing. That's the problem. All of a sudden you get this short story while nothing else has changed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T14:16:05-07:00","id":1534735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534729#post1534729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>We fundamentally disagree here. No point continuing a back and forth on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534729#post1534729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's the thing... they didn't update the lore. The whole female-Custodes-thing comes from a two-page short story they put into the newest army-Codex with a female Custodes while the rest of the book acts like female Custodes aren't a thing. That's the problem. All of a sudden you get this short story while nothing else has changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it mention gender specifically in the current codex? Did it mention it specifically in previous codices? If those answers have changed: they *did* update the lore. If they don't mention gender in previous editions, then there's been a whole lot of word count in this thread and beyond dedicated to a totally made up reason to be upset. If they mention gender in previous editions, omit it in the &quot;lore&quot; of this edition, but include a female character in a short story (which, not to put too fine a point on it: absolutely *is* lore) then they've updated the lore.<br /> <br /> You're arguing both sides to justify being irritated. Maybe take a minute and examine that and why that is. It cannot be both. Either the lore is updated or it isn't. If it is, and you don't like it, that's fine. But don't try to say in the same argument that it isn't. It has to be one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T14:59:54-07:00","id":1534737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534735#post1534735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it mention gender specifically in the current codex?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, in three ways. One is about a group of Custodes as they/them, then otherwise as he/him when individuals are mentioned (for unit descriptions and the background-section). And then you have the short story which uses she/her to describe the female Custodian. That's the only difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534735#post1534735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did it mention it specifically in previous codices?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. No question. It was all-male and it was described as such.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T00:58:04-07:00","id":1534753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534719#post1534719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also should be noted that Space Marines and the Emperor personal guard have given up there basic humanity in the defense of the Imperium and don't have families or spouses to go home to see and when they are not fighting in battles, then they are training and the ruler of humanity had put in a flaw in his creations that prevent them from reproducing. In fact it's not unheard of that if they make it through the process that they lose chunks of there previous memories. So with the personal guards that have been selected from the first born males of the royal families of old Earth you run into the trouble of ending family lines going through this route. It can be done if Gulliman deciding that they need to expand the pool of recruits that stand out as he has woken up into a world that is drastically different then what he knew and what his &quot;father&quot; intended.<br /> <br /> When you create a Space Marine they are implanted with a gene seed of a the Primarch and they have been all been male and if a female was given that, she would lose much of her female attributes with all the genetic, cybernetic and psychological conditioning and here is the following of what you get as a space marine muscle mass is greatly increased, body fat is dramatically, extra vital organs are created and in general you are made into a super solider and a female space marine would be nearly indistingable unless she takes off her armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the thing to consider wouldn't be how evident being female is at the end, but at the start.<br /> <br /> If it's a Chapter that has something like an open recruitment policy, why should they turn away somebody who is determined to attempt to go through the gauntlet of all of that out of dedication to the Imperium (and perhaps admiration for the Chapter) just because they happen to be a woman? If it's a Chapter that kind of extracts its recruits out of a populace at will, why should they assume that any given woman in their selection pool is any less suited to going through the filtering process than any given man? If the process ultimately homogenizes them, then doesn't that mean there's no distinction on which to base gatekeeping at the first juncture?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T08:17:06-07:00","id":1534760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534737#post1534737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, in three ways. One is about a group of Custodes as they/them, then otherwise as he/him when individuals are mentioned (for unit descriptions and the background-section). And then you have the short story which uses she/her to describe the female Custodian. That's the only difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're arguing that because he/him pronouns are treated as the default individual...as they are and have been (far too commonly) for decades if not centuries, that somehow that exudes women as possibly being among the ranks? If that's the case that is paper-thin reasoning at best, confirmation bias at worst.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534737#post1534737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. No question. It was all-male and it was described as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case then they absolutely changed the lore, therefore the old lore is outdated. That's my point.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T10:34:29-07:00","id":1534769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534760#post1534760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you're arguing that because he/him pronouns are treated as the default individual...as they are and have been (far too commonly) for decades if not centuries, that somehow that exudes women as possibly being among the ranks? If that's the case that is paper-thin reasoning at best, confirmation bias at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would say that for the sake of being more gender-sensitive, it would be good to get away from using &quot;He/Him&quot; as a default in general. Especially in light of the lore-change, things like alternating pronouns or using they/them would also help in establishing the new idea that Custodians are both men and women now. Additionally, what would have also cemented the idea would have been the release of a model of a named character who is a female Custodian alongside the Codex-release. As shown by this current situation, these lore-changes sometimes can come hard and fast. Having a model that showcases the lore-change would be a great help. Otherwise, there's always the potential of a couple years down the line when the 11th edition Codex comes out that GW is just like &quot;Now that we've thought about it... let's not do the female Custodes thing after all.&quot;. At the end of the day, the only real thing GW cares about is selling models, so the one way where you can be sure GW won't change its mind again is if a lore-change is tied to an opportunity to sell more models.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534760#post1534760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case then they absolutely changed the lore, therefore the old lore is outdated. That's my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which brings us right back to the beginning. It's a lore-change. And my argument is that they should've done a better job of worldbuilding. You could've added to the lore that recruiting female Custodes is a new thing. And if it's a retcon, they should've done an article on their website like they usually do. Like, when at the start of 9th they decided to turn back the clock in the setting and now instead of &quot;present-day&quot; being after the Indomitus Crusade, the new &quot;present day&quot; would be at the very beginning of the Indomitus Crusade. And then they made Guy Haley rewrite two novels to get those in line with that change. They have done big retcons in the past and usually, they're not shy about saying out loud that they're doing that. For whatever reason, they didn't do that this time.<br /> <br /> Additionally the natural follow-up of &quot;There have been female Custodes from the very beginning.&quot; is &quot;So why haven't there been female Space Marines from the very beginning?&quot;. You kinda have to look then at all the Emperor-stuff and rework it accordingly. You have to bring it all in, female Thunder-Warriors, female Primarchs and female Custodes. Because it doesn't make sense for the Emperor to make no exceptions in who's getting taken to be changed for one of those factions but not the others. And if he's aware of this, why would he insist on making the Primarchs all male?<br /> <br /> And the all-male-thing is dumb. That's the point of the lore and all the writing in the novels you get on that these days. You're taking children and reforge them on a cellular level to be transhuman warriors. Who gives a shit what gender that child has, right? But they kept the all-male thing because it was the established lore from the 90s and the way it gets addressed these days in the fiction is to call it out as a dumb idea.<br /> <br /> &quot;Female Space Marines&quot; is of course the true Pandora's Box here. I think if they want female Custodes to be a thing and maintain that, they should do a retcon and introduce female Space Marines next. With that new status-quo in mind, that just makes sense. But of course, the outcry from the usual suspects would be ten times louder if they were to cross that Rubicon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T12:52:50-07:00","id":1534772,"title":"","content":"The lore Isator Levi in the past have said that the reason why females were excluded from the selection process was that the tech priests of the Mechanicus found that females had a much lower chance of surviving the selection and implanatation process and in fact even males don't have a 100% chance of surviving the selection and implantation process either only that they stood a better chance. Interestingly enough with them being unable to sire or bear children would make some say that it violates reproductive rights and I found that fact as a point of contentation.<br /> <br /> Of course with the creation of Primaris Space Marines and slight advancements of the technology of the human ruled Imperium thanks to Belesarius Cawl of the Adeptus Mechancius work that it could be feasible to add females to previously all male groups. But they choose to say that they were always there, but countless novels and sourcebooks say otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-26-2024, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T13:01:09-07:00","id":1534775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534769#post1534769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I would say that for the sake of being more gender-sensitive, it would be good to get away from using &quot;He/Him&quot; as a default in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, me too. That was my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534769#post1534769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings us right back to the beginning. It's a lore-change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also my point. The lore is changed. Could they have fleshed it out more? Sure. And maybe they will, but the lore has changed with this codex.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T13:09:33-07:00","id":1534776,"title":"","content":"So any bad experiences at work that people want to vent about or job interviews that the lines of communication were bad? I came from a job interview where I learned that upon arriving that the job had been filled and I who had booked the interview a week in advanced wasn't given an email or any sort of notification of this change. The bright spot was that I got interviewed by another company on the same day and they seemed quite impressed by my qualifications and answers to scenarios they put fourth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-27T12:05:24-07:00","id":1534813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534772#post1534772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lore Isator Levi in the past have said that the reason why females were excluded from the selection process was that the tech priests of the Mechanicus found that females had a much lower chance of surviving the selection and implanatation process and in fact even males don't have a 100% chance of surviving the selection and implantation process either only that they stood a better chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside questions of those being made up rules which may well have been devised post hoc anyway... do Space Marines care? They obviously don't value human life in a way that would prevent them from bringing recruits into a process with a high chance of killing them anyway, so what would it matter? Just increasing the casualties created by the process? Except for the fact that they probably don't care about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly enough with them being unable to sire or bear children would make some say that it violates reproductive rights and I found that fact as a point of contentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe that there's anybody who is serious about reproductive rights that thinks that something elective, as Space Marine recruitment is still frequently portrayed as being, is a violation of them. Indeed, the issue is often quite the opposite; try looking up how many women attempt to get elective procedures that will permanently render them incapable of having children (either as a form of birth control or for health reasons such as cancer prevention) and struggle to find doctors that will not just straight up refuse.<br /> <br /> Not that Space Marine transformation is exactly concerned with medical ethics in the first place, but it would still be the kind of thing any given hypothetical woman volunteer could already be aware of and take into consideration before going forward for the procedure (and probably ultimate a fairly insignificant consideration against everything else that they'd give up).<br /> <br /> Really, bringing in the subject of reproduction in the first place strikes me as a little odd. Why does whether or not they'd be able to have children afterwards matter to the question of what the outcomes of an alternate take on the setting where women could become Space Marines would be?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T12:18:39-07:00","id":1534912,"title":"","content":"I'm just pointing out that we hear about reproductive freedoms all the time in the news channels and women should be allowed to make there own choices in regards to that and here GW wants to create a scene where this is what is going to happen is that said women will have that choice taken away from them. I know that they want to have more women in the hobby which is unlikely and when they hear that. You know that they will raise there eyebrows for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T12:22:46-07:00","id":1534914,"title":"","content":"They made a remake of Road House with Jake Gynehall and Conner Mcgregor and nobody thought that maybe we shouldn't as it was pure camp and wouldn't work today as nobody but the late Patrick Swayze could make it work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T13:46:28-07:00","id":1534918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1534912#post1534912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just pointing out that we hear about reproductive freedoms all the time in the news channels and women should be allowed to make there own choices in regards to that</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the fact that plays out in reality in the form of &quot;preventing women from ending pregnancies they do not want&quot; rather than non-consensual sterilisation has some relevance here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">GW wants to create a scene where this is what is going to happen is that said women will have that choice taken away from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that the two biggest things I'd have to say to that are asking for a response to what I've said about how attempting to become a Space Marine is frequently elective, and that being sterilised is not only probably not the biggest violation that comes from non-consensual transformation, but isn't quite relevant to anxieties about reproductive freedom considering that it doesn't reinforce inequality along gender lines. A woman losing her reproductive capacity in becoming a living engine of death as a result of something like feudal obligation rather than volunteering does not place her in a lesser social position to men.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that they want to have more women in the hobby which is unlikely</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely based on what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">when they hear that. You know that they will raise there eyebrows for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that. To me, that sounds at best like a hypothetical woman verging on a caricature, disconnected from firsthand personal accounts of actual people and their concerns over reproductive freedoms (which includes what I have said before about the number of women who are actually quite eager for elective procedures that would sterilise them which society denies).<br /> <br /> At worst, it comes off as an attempt to have credibility or rob it from opposing positions by invoking a distorted, truncated perception of feminist talking points, in pursuit of a &quot;gotcha&quot; or superficially clever turnaround.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T14:24:36-07:00","id":1535087,"title":"","content":"Personally I just chalked it down the martial societies tending to be patriarchal so the imperium would probably slant that way on a number of roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T16:38:55-07:00","id":1535093,"title":"","content":"Nobody was against the idea of female Custodes or later Space Marines Ragged Robin, but they marketed it wrong by saying that they were always there and the lore said otherwise and they could have went with the Imperium having to adjust with the huge victories that the Chaos Marines and there followers were having and Gulliman knowing that they needed to expand the recruitment pool Ragged Robin to stand a better chance of surviving. Then you have people dissing the Sisters Of Silence and Battle as either boring or to religious for thee tastes and I think that they didn't read the setting where the Emperor is viewed and worshipped as a God and the human society is strongly religious despite the scraps of advanced tech..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T22:54:37-07:00","id":1535096,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a passable rationale. It's a bit obviously meta to do it ala the carmarilla tech ban or the lasombra defection but its plausable .<br /> <br /> Something I actually noticed about female space marines is its more about the most popular group being single gender than the specific group. Nobody seems to care the orcs are all coded as male for example and prior to this my gf commented female custodes wasn't much of a talking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-03-2024, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T16:43:24-07:00","id":1535117,"title":"","content":"The Custodes barely left the Imperial Palace for 10,000 years and one of the talking points is why them and not a more visible group like the marines who are fighting for humanity on the front lines? I read the Sisters of Silence and Battle and I enjoyed the novels dedicated to them and hoped for more updated lore on them which is why I'm disappointed by this path they went with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-06T09:54:06-07:00","id":1535193,"title":"","content":"Something I am BEYOND tired of is banks, insurance providers, and various other &quot;money-related&quot; sites developing annual issues that lead me in circles trying to access my accounts. It's clear they aren't committed to anything other than the outward appearance of security seeing as how there's a new notice of data breaches every single year (sometimes multiple times a year). And I'm beyond sick of constantly changing my passwords and login information just because a bunch of unqualified hacks want to protect their jobs by meddling with a system that already works. This country gives too much credit to these electronic charlatans and won't hold them accountable when their idiocy creates more inconvenience for us all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-06T12:36:01-07:00","id":1535200,"title":"","content":"I'm personally getting tired by poor lines of communication between job agencies and human resources of any company that I get a nibble from and set up an interview only to show up with others and find out that the job is no longer on the table and we just wasted time driving down and all of us and the person who is doing the interview are left standing around what should we do next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T10:01:52-07:00","id":1535218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1535200#post1535200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally getting tired by poor lines of communication between job agencies and human resources of any company that I get a nibble from and set up an interview only to show up with others and find out that the job is no longer on the table and we just wasted time driving down and all of us and the person who is doing the interview are left standing around what should we do next.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;what we should do next&quot;; Riot. The answer is riot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T11:22:14-07:00","id":1535221,"title":"","content":"Or at least get on board with the UAW's call for organizing a national (or even international if they can make it happen) general strike in 2028; largely because the fallout of the 08 financial crisis and then Covid lend to a lot of labor actions and revitalized sense of labor solidarity, but labor organizers needs some time to solidify the gains and recharge strike funds before a large scale organized cross-sector movement.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> On a completely separate tangent: While I appreciate Macklemore's new track, and even agree with 99% of it, the answer to his probably rhetorical question is 1902-1903. And anyone that doesn't understand how that's an actual answer to the question he posed probably needs to study history more instead of sloganeering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T14:02:12-07:00","id":1535230,"title":"","content":"We got enough riots happening in the world and I don't see how it would help in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"typ