//forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T11:51:16-07:00","id":1535655,"title":"","content":"I'm sad that people seem to take themselves so seriously and get offended easily over little things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T12:25:49-07:00","id":1535661,"title":"","content":"Time. It is the only thing I can not control and it leaks through my fingers. Idea that I'm running out of it where's so much to do and I'm closer to the end it's a weight that's heavier each day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T12:16:08-07:00","id":1535790,"title":"","content":"I have to do an online job interview for a company and I'm uneasy as I prefer in person or group interviews myself? Have any of you had that happen to you and is it worth going through at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T14:33:28-07:00","id":1535867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1535790#post1535790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to do an online job interview for a company and I'm uneasy as I prefer in person or group interviews myself? Have any of you had that happen to you and is it worth going through at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done a couple<br /> <br /> -do a practice run with someone to get you used to it.<br /> -make sure your cat is out the room.<br /> -do something relaxing for 20 mins beforehand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T12:04:11-07:00","id":1535912,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the tips.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T12:20:03-07:00","id":1535916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1517687#post1517687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Person &quot;Hey Robin, I believe the following. [Insert take here]. What do you think of that?&quot;<br /> <br /> Robin-&quot;Well its a negative and I disagree with your stance.&quot;<br /> <br /> Person-&quot; Well here's my rationale why I'm gonna ignore what you said.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Why bother asking me? I could have saved 20 minutes not knowing your take on something that doesn't affect me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The exiting sequal<br /> <br /> Thread-Why do you feel about [blank] the way you do<br /> <br /> Ragged robyn-well here's why i feel the way i feel<br /> <br /> Some guy-heres why that isnt a big deal and some workarounds about that thing you consider it.<br /> <br /> 1-did i Ask?<br /> <br /> 2-why do you presume i havnt considered your perspective.<br /> <br /> 3- <a href=\"https://youtu.be/43z-5FBIhZw?si=BHroxrAEAqQHJ1_M\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/43z-5FBIhZw?si=BHroxrAEAqQHJ1_M</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T11:46:00-07:00","id":1536073,"title":"","content":"A follow up thread<br /> <br /> I feel triggered by what you said and I hate you for it.<br /> <br /> Me. All I did was point what you said wasn't historically accurate and I wanted to correct it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T12:23:27-07:00","id":1536111,"title":"","content":"I've been watching Quiet On The Set on the Investigative Channel on what was happening at the Nickalodeon Studios and all I can say is wow that this so disgusting and how it was covered up for so long by the powers that be in Hollywood. Now I wasn't the target audience for the studio as I wasn't a teen or a young adult when it was at it's peak but seeing how thirteen or fourteen year old teenage girls being over sexualized was disgusting and tragic and how some of the abusers got job at places like Disney was shocking to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T12:57:30-07:00","id":1536458,"title":"","content":"Oh dear.<br /> <br /> So at Christmas, somebody in my extended family purchased tickets for my immediate family to all go to see a show together. I've been aware of it, but not quite invested in it enough to have given it a lot of thought or keep something like the date committed to memory in a way that would help me to, like, keep it in mind while at work.<br /> <br /> Which then means that I get snuck up on with the fact that it's this Sunday when I'm scheduled to work, and I never got to booking the time off for it.<br /> <br /> I guess I'll have to try and see if there's any chance when I go back in on Friday, but it's such an awkward position to be in. On both sides of the aisle. Like, I'm caught between needing to go to my boss and appeal for last minute time off, and my family who are not going to be happy with me flaking out like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T17:12:31-07:00","id":1536593,"title":"","content":"Wow former President Donald Trump found guilty on all counts and I don't think it will matter to his base and he will still be the Republican front runner for President.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T09:08:57-07:00","id":1536749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1536593#post1536593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow former President Donald Trump found guilty on all counts and I don't think it will matter to his base and he will still be the Republican front runner for President.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take whatever I can get at this point, his base is a lost cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T10:46:12-07:00","id":1536753,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be shocked if he is elected President again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T15:13:52-07:00","id":1536762,"title":"","content":"It shouldn't be shocking. While getting into some sort of moral debate of who was worse is pointless to me, we elected Bill Clinton twice. There are, unfortunately, certain types of bad behavior that the general public considers &quot;baked in&quot; when it comes to the powerful and it we find ways to excuse it when convenient. Bill Clinton was already known as &quot;Slick Willy&quot; for all his womanizing and sketchy real estate dealings while he was still Governor of Arkansas. We would have been more shocked if he'd managed to last eight years without cheating on his wife.<br /> <br /> We just expect the rich and powerful to be more discreet in their bad behaviors. Though we also expect them to feign contrition and then get slaps on the wrists instead of really fighting when they do get caught. So we'll see what happens I guess.<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> On something less toeing the line of getting into politics:<br /> <br /> I really wish we had a functional economic feedback loop where companies were forced to change when it's clear they're the problem, not anything else. If 2024 continues on trend, somehow we're going to have a massive year of tickets sold for movies and at the same time have a record breaking number of box office bombs (and 2023 was already pretty much like that). If sales are going up, but profit is going down, it ain't the product or the customers that have a problem in the equation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T16:08:59-07:00","id":1536765,"title":"","content":"Getting mildly annoyed at some of the posts about the Mad Max prequel and I'm seeing the same nonsense that was posted 9 years ago when Fury Road came out and I hoped all the bait and switch claims was put to rest. How naive on my part to see it rear up again for Furioso and my only concerns that it being a prequel and it coming out so many years would hurt it's performance.<br /> <br /> But I know that it was allegedly going to come out in a couple of years after Fury Road but George Miller had some legal trouble with Warner Bros and for those who want Mel Gibson to reprise in his role. It's not happening as he has stated that he feels that he is to old for such roles now and even felt the same way when he was offered the lead role for Gladiator over twenty years ago and please respect his choice.<br /> <br /> In addition I would like to see Hollywood take more risks again with film making and not play it safe like they do now. Falling Down wouldn't be made today or at the very least not by a major studio like Warner Bros, Universial or Disney .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-03-2024, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T21:28:44-07:00","id":1536783,"title":"","content":"I really don't like the &quot;X wouldn't get made today.&quot; Falling Down wouldn't get made today because it's a commentary on its time. While some of its themes are still relevant and worth exploring today - because art can transcend its original time - the core issues of the main character aren't as resonant 20 years later. We shouldn't want Hollywood to make Falling Down now. We should want it to make new stories for now. And like... it does. It's just not 20 years later when people will be complaining about how they don't &quot;take risks&quot; anymore with movies we have no idea now that will be seen that way in the future. And all the major studios have subsidiaries for anything they don't want to slap their main brand on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T04:10:15-07:00","id":1536793,"title":"","content":"Heh, Wasn't it Mel Brooks that said his movies couldn't actually be made in <i>their</i> time? Apparently he got them done anyway, so it doesn't look like hollywood has that much of a say. Whole indy films can appear in YouTube of all things if someone really wants them out there.<br /> Hollywood is probably just spooked that people can now dissect, complain about, and ultimately discard/boycott anything that's put out in real time thanks to the existence of social media, making the concept of a &quot;timeless classic&quot; nearly mythological in the modern day. They must have taken note of how most of these people just wait for someone with a strong personality to hand them their opinion so they have something to argue about and rally around. And that most of those with these &quot;strong personalities&quot; tend to be degenerate basement trolls looking for validation on the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T07:31:55-07:00","id":1536799,"title":"","content":"It certainly looks that way Darksol and not to mention that they are hiring people not based on merit but fill of checkbox that will get them praise and funding from companies like Black Rock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T20:13:39-07:00","id":1536828,"title":"","content":"My, &quot;R&quot;, key just popped off of my laptop; this is very disturbing for me. <br /> <br /> What type of glue should I use to reattach it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T22:13:20-07:00","id":1536832,"title":"","content":"That's not good Iguazu. Maybe use gorilla glue to fix the R key.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T00:08:03-07:00","id":1536834,"title":"","content":"Repairing a keyboard very much depends on the style of keys. Gluing is generally not a good idea because keys need to be able to move up and down, and the glue will lock them in one position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T15:01:59-07:00","id":1536850,"title":"","content":"Maybe taking your keyboard to a store that repairs computers might be your best bet as they would know what to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T11:37:26-07:00","id":1536894,"title":"","content":"I swear some people have to much free time on there hands and look to create trouble. Lately I have been reading some Sarah J. Maas books with the Crescent City series being my favorite and I saw some Reddit people complaining that she doesn't have any bisexual people of color or LBTQ in her stories.<br /> <br /> Who are you to tell her what kind of characters she should have in her book and more importantly maybe it's not something she is interested in doing at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T12:28:08-07:00","id":1536897,"title":"","content":"I don't bother going to Reddit for... well much really. But it took me less than a minute to see a quote of Sarah Maas citing multiple inspirations that feature prominent LGBTQ characters. It's more than a bit of a disconnect to say, &quot;I was really inspired in my writing by all of these LGBTQ stories,&quot; and then not include any LGBTQ characters in your work. Even if it doesn't deserve normal Reddit flame wars, it is at least setting yourself up for some valid criticism if you do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T14:03:59-07:00","id":1536902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1536897#post1536897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't bother going to Reddit for... well much really. But it took me less than a minute to see a quote of Sarah Maas citing multiple inspirations that feature prominent LGBTQ characters. It's more than a bit of a disconnect to say, &quot;I was really inspired in my writing by all of these LGBTQ stories,&quot; and then not include any LGBTQ characters in your work. Even if it doesn't deserve normal Reddit flame wars, it is at least setting yourself up for some valid criticism if you do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sarah J. Maas doesn\u2019t have any LGBTQ characters in her books? That\u2019s a little troubling. Maybe I won\u2019t read A Court of Thorns and Roses after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T15:22:54-07:00","id":1536904,"title":"","content":"Never really had a lot of interest in Sarah J. Mass' series. It's high fantasy with a stronger focus on romance, right...? That's the pitch... I think. At least, that has been my impression from afar. But reading <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> post, I did some googling and uhm... It seems she wants to be seen as a liberal but she's a bit tone-deaf when it comes to representation. One of the things besides her lack of representation in her novels is, for example, that she used the cover-reveal-post for her novel A Court Of Silver Flames to talk about the Breonna Taylor case and to talk about voting (the post happened in 2020). And the post didn't link to any activist-organizations or donation-funds. She seems to have good intentions but she's struggling. She's not very good at this or shows an understanding of what representation exactly means these days. It seems the representation has gotten better as this <a href=\"https://thestray.org/2022/02/22/queen-of-fantasy/\" target=\"_blank\">blog-post</a> mentions: &quot;Crescent City is Maas\u2019s latest series, a trilogy that is being marketed as adult fantasy, stepping away from her YA success. The first instalment, House of Earth and Blood, largly followed the same trends as her other texts, with a white, heterosexual protagonist. However, there has been some POC and LGBTQ+ representation in the characters of Fury and Juniper, Maas\u2019s first lesbian couple, the latter being a POC. There is also Isaiah, our first male gay character, who also is a POC. Whilst Maas is making progress in the diversity of her novels, these characters barely feature in the narrative, but instead occupy the margins.&quot; So, it seems like she's getting better at this... very slowly.<br /> <br /> She's also gotten into trouble in the past because she did some interviews where she had some glowing remarks about Israel, going on a Birthright-trip and how proud she was of her grandma to still do volunteer-work for the IDF (Israeli Defense Forces). That was in 2015/1016. Well, we all know what's going on over there and why that would have come up quite a few times over the last couple of years. But from what I've seen she hasn't talked about that topic since then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T15:56:52-07:00","id":1536907,"title":"","content":"Yes Sarah J. Maas is high fantasy with romance in it, but I find her world building skills quite good and perhaps in the later Crescent City books said characters might play a bigger role, but they're supporting characters and not lead characters and maybe she wants to flesh them out more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T17:02:33-07:00","id":1536909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1536904#post1536904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never really had a lot of interest in Sarah J. Mass' series. It's high fantasy with a stronger focus on romance, right...? That's the pitch... I think. At least, that has been my impression from afar. But reading <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> post, I did some googling and uhm... It seems she wants to be seen as a liberal but she's a bit tone-deaf when it comes to representation. One of the things besides her lack of representation in her novels is, for example, that she used the cover-reveal-post for her novel A Court Of Silver Flames to talk about the Breonna Taylor case and to talk about voting (the post happened in 2020). And the post didn't link to any activist-organizations or donation-funds. She seems to have good intentions but she's struggling. She's not very good at this or shows an understanding of what representation exactly means these days. It seems the representation has gotten better as this <a href=\"https://thestray.org/2022/02/22/queen-of-fantasy/\" target=\"_blank\">blog-post</a> mentions: &quot;Crescent City is Maas\u2019s latest series, a trilogy that is being marketed as adult fantasy, stepping away from her YA success. The first instalment, House of Earth and Blood, largly followed the same trends as her other texts, with a white, heterosexual protagonist. However, there has been some POC and LGBTQ+ representation in the characters of Fury and Juniper, Maas\u2019s first lesbian couple, the latter being a POC. There is also Isaiah, our first male gay character, who also is a POC. Whilst Maas is making progress in the diversity of her novels, these characters barely feature in the narrative, but instead occupy the margins.&quot; So, it seems like she's getting better at this... very slowly.<br /> <br /> She's also gotten into trouble in the past because she did some interviews where she had some glowing remarks about Israel, going on a Birthright-trip and how proud she was of her grandma to still do volunteer-work for the IDF (Israeli Defense Forces). That was in 2015/1016. Well, we all know what's going on over there and why that would have come up quite a few times over the last couple of years. But from what I've seen she hasn't talked about that topic since then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least she\u2019s trying. Maybe I\u2019ll give her a chance after all. ACOTAR does look good.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T07:00:23-07:00","id":1536981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1536894#post1536894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who are you to tell her what kind of characters she should have in her book and more importantly maybe it's not something she is interested in doing at all?</div> </div> </div> </div> How big is the cast of these stories?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T09:35:19-07:00","id":1536987,"title":"","content":"In general Sarah J. Maas has two or three main lead characters and several supporting characters of various degrees of importance and some that will play larger roles in future books in any series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T13:21:06-07:00","id":1537026,"title":"","content":"Well I can't say from that whether it passes a certain threshold, but there <i>is</i> a threshold past which your number of characters having a limited range becomes a choice (even if it's a choice from lack of consideration rather than deliberate exclusion), and I would say that's a thing worth commenting upon.<br /> <br /> Even if a story is concerned with things other than exploring those topics, people like that can just be... around.<br /> <br /> Mind, that's a consideration at the baseline, never mind somebody who might be drawing inspiration from queer stories.<br /> <br /> This is the kind of point I think would be easily recognised in a space dedicated for tabletop roleplaying games of all things. Like, some people look at stuff going out of its way to pointedly include a range of people and respond &quot;oh, stop being so in my face with your agenda&quot;, and person if you think you can go to any gaming convention and not having a significant percentage of queer people, out or otherwise, have I got news for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-08-2024, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T14:34:41-07:00","id":1537034,"title":"","content":"It's general writing 101 of having a small cast of characters to work with as it's easier to flesh them out before expanding on adding others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T14:49:08-07:00","id":1537036,"title":"","content":"I think the threshold is also influenced a lot by the very broad spectrum of what a &quot;supporting character&quot; can be. In the LotR books, Samwise, Merry, Pippin, and Gollum are all supporting characters to Frodo's status as the protagonist of at least one part of the story. But they are not equals in their narrative weight, and what details about them mean to emotional reactions. If you were <i>Yesterday</i> style sent to a world where LotR was never written but was also otherwise basically the same as ours somehow, making Merry and Pippin more that good friends would feel a lot more token-representation than it would mean if Sam was romantically in love with Frodo and part of the whole journey is Sam coming to grips with Frodo just not really caring about that sort of thing and Sam needing to find fulfillment with someone that's actually going to reciprocate his feelings (and lets be honest that's not exactly a huge stretch from the original anyway). I think most people would also get the backlash if Gollum was somehow the only minority coded supporting character.<br /> <br /> I feel like most minority groups that want representation appreciate if an author just says, &quot;I don't think I can authentically write my central character as having experiences that I don't really understand.&quot; But if you can only do representation via Merry and Pippin supporting characters where that basically never really matters, it's not a good look. You should at least be able to create a character that has deep emotional bonds with people of very different backgrounds than your protagonists... because humans in general have deep emotional bonds with people that are different from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T15:58:08-07:00","id":1537040,"title":"","content":"Johnathan Kellerman has been writing since 1986 and for several years focused on three characters before he decided to create other lead characters and see if people would like them enough to keep them and he has kept in several of his most recent novels and created fully fleshed out diverse characters that will interact with his original three leads. So experience and level of comfort plays apart of expanding lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-27T13:52:54-07:00","id":1537801,"title":"","content":"I really wish at times that we as humanity didn't invent Social Media at times as crazy concpiracy theories got a new life as already with the death of former front man for Crazy Town Shifty Shellock died a few days ago and already we have anti-vaxxers saying it was the jab that killed him. Sure anti-vaxxers that was the reason and not the twenty plus years of drug addictions that he battled and the number of overdoses he had and how his habit took a huge toll on his health and appearance that might be way more possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-27T13:56:54-07:00","id":1537802,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to think that creating social media was a bad move for humanity in general as crazy theories got a new life and people will believe and the most recent one was the death of former Crazy Town front Man Shifty Shellock passing away this week and anti-vaxxers are already out saying it was the jab that killed him and not you know the twenty plus years of drug addictions that he battled and the overdoses he had or how it took a huge toll on his health and appearance. Sometimes I weep for humanity future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-27T22:46:07-07:00","id":1537811,"title":"","content":"Youtubes moderation bots are pretty fun.<br /> <br /> Proactive support of white supremacy-a ok.<br /> <br /> But some calls him a knob head? Thats a bannin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T10:24:17-07:00","id":1537832,"title":"","content":"Hello I work in a metro centre large school in southern England as a teacher, While the work has been challenging I've always felt supported and working as part of a larger team and in turn have always tried to go above and beyond with my colleagues. However I've recently noticed one of my colleagues from another department seems to dislike me and is quite passive aggressive about it. Short conversations, generally curt and barely acknowledging my presence outside of but generally being professional this is naturally 'fine' and I've taken the hint.<br /> Today however I was tacitly left out off a the traditional Friday pub visit which a formerly friendly clique I engage with and I suspect it's partly her (she is more socially popular than me....which is an absurd statement to make on reflection) doing due to a number of odd coincidences and them walking straight past me on the way out. While I'm personally saddened by this is has been something of a reminder that these people arnt really my actual friends (of which I have many) and I should re-consider my perspectives.<br /> So far my thoughts on my response<ul><li>Re-establish work boundaries as 'professional' rather than professional-friendly/supportive. These people are obliged to my hours they're not obliged to my blood sweat and tears especially as their are colleagues (and pupils) which do appreciate my support.</li> <li>Keep an eye out for any shift in treatment to me in a professional context. They're not obliged to like me but I am a peer in a professional context and will not tolerate workplace hostility. I may take a record if I see an actual shift.</li> <li>I've reminded myself I don't need personal affirmation from these people and this reflects more badly personally on them than it does me. I have plenty of actual friends, a healthy relationship, family irl (who've already described them using several colorful nouns) and am well liked by the staff in general.</li> </ul>Thanks for listening had to get this off this my chest, if you any useful suggestions or similar experiences feel free to share.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T12:11:17-07:00","id":1537835,"title":"","content":"Well Ragged Robin a few years back we had a supervisor who thought he was above treating experienced workers with any respect and manners and was shocked when everyone mouthed off to him and didn't do any work properly for him and got canned after he pissed off the wrong worker that nailed him on the spot with a punch and add that with all the issues he caused. His bosses got rid of him in a hurry. <br /> <br /> The gist was if we fire the guy you pissed off we lose an excellent worker who knows nearly every division of the warehouse and is worth five of you. Or we fire you due to your poor employee relation skills and all of our problems are solved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T16:22:36-07:00","id":1538260,"title":"","content":"It's fun to see some people complaining about why people are focused on what killed WCW. Why shouldn't people talk about it as it seemed on the surface have all the parts to be successful and give Vince McMahon his first real threat in the sports entertainment industry.<br /> <br /> Not only that it's makes a good primer for what not to do for running a business just like the long gone Enron corporation and how a series of wrong choices can doom a company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T18:57:33-07:00","id":1538271,"title":"","content":"The fall of WCW is.... pretty old news? I have a feeling the complaints about people suddenly talking about it more is that the company finally falling apart got the current day documentary treatment so it was on people's minds (including for many people that probably have no idea about it otherwise).<br /> <br /> Though comparing the mismangement of WCW to Enron feels... very poor in options. WCW's failures are really relevant to understanding the current media climate because WCW went south largely because corporate mergers (Warner Bros didn't start doing this shit a just a few years ago) and putting corporate execs with no idea of the industry in charge; not a massive criminally fraudulent scam. WCW should be talked about because it's a great example of how much the consumers suffer during eras of corporate consolidation if for no other reason. It's not like there's no space for a competitor to the WWE... AEW is doing rather well for itself as the other big promotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T22:01:06-07:00","id":1538286,"title":"","content":"It might be old news Heavy Arms, but with the recent coverage of it thanks to a documentary by the Rock it's fresh on people's minds and they even talked to more people behind the scenes that didn't comment on it when Death of WCW was published. I brought up Enron because like WCW at first that on the surface it looked like a very successful business but it was really a house of cards and both failures are noteworthy because of how you peeled away the layers and saw how poorly run everything was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T00:52:41-07:00","id":1538289,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the list of failed companies that went down in flames due to well hidden mismanagement is staggeringly massive because of the history of ever-growing corporate power. When you can make just as much money (if not more) running a company into the ground and are protected from criminal or civil liability, why bother building a company that will actually endure?<br /> <br /> Enron wasn't an onion of peeling off odorous layers of incompetence. It was an extremely well run criminal enterprise disguised as a business until they finally got caught. I'm not sure why this difference is hard to grasp as important to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T21:56:40-07:00","id":1538461,"title":"","content":"Heatwaves are awful and I don't how folks in Nevada, Utah, New Mexico, Arizona can live in such hot places. I find +25 temperature hard to work in let alone when it hits +35 like yesterday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T10:57:29-07:00","id":1538529,"title":"","content":"Talk about being shocked by how quickly the Alec Baldwin involtary manslaughter case getting dismissed because of suppressed evidence. I guess next will be a civil case for Mr. Baldwin and I can't see him winning that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T08:56:03-07:00","id":1538565,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't want to be in the Secret Service shoes right now as we saw the attempted assassination of former President Trump yesterday and how the shooter got as close as he did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T12:37:16-07:00","id":1538579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1538565#post1538565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't want to be in the Secret Service shoes right now as we saw the attempted assassination of former President Trump yesterday and how the shooter got as close as he did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a common adage that there are ultimately few security measures that can protect a public figure from an attacker who is both very dedicated and has little regard for their own survival. The greatest protection against such a thing is that, ultimately, very few such people actually exist.<br /> <br /> For my money, I think this person was more likely driven by the same impulse as many other random shooters, including at least one who has attempted to kill another president or president adjacent person; a general desire for infamy arising from unstable personality, that can effectively latch on to a figure either widely beloved or despised.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose that Trump technically qualifies as both, unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T15:03:03-07:00","id":1538589,"title":"","content":"The Secret Service should be lauded for getting to Donald Trump the moment shots were fired and getting him out of harm's way. But the fact that his detail missed the sniper until it's was almost to late does raise questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T17:37:16-07:00","id":1538591,"title":"","content":"Combining the US's overly lax gun laws, and a candidate that actively campaigns frequently in rural areas outside, where controlling every sight line is nearly impossible, there's only so much the Secret Service can do.<br /> <br /> It was also, considering what did happen, too late. It was just a case of luck that there wasn't more death than there was. If a bullet could hit someone in the ear, it could have hit them fully in the head with a slight adjustment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T23:28:32-07:00","id":1538645,"title":"","content":"It's almost like the fool didn't learn from the last time someone tried to off him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T14:20:43-07:00","id":1538677,"title":"","content":"It would be nice if we saw a cool down on the extreme political speaches from both sides after what happened to Donald Trump and certainly in Canada we had nearly every poiltical leader condem the attack and calling for more civility in debates. But I don't think that it will happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T16:08:31-07:00","id":1538681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1538677#post1538677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be nice if we saw a cool down on the extreme political speaches from both sides after what happened to Donald Trump and certainly in Canada we had nearly every poiltical leader condem the attack and calling for more civility in debates. But I don't think that it will happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't both sides this, the escalation of violence is a Trump and Trump-run Republican party thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T17:34:33-07:00","id":1538683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1538677#post1538677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be nice if we saw a cool down on the extreme political speaches from both sides after what happened to Donald Trump</div> </div> </div> </div>Has Trump being shot at changed the contents of Project 2025?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T18:06:32-07:00","id":1538684,"title":"","content":"Still, this is after all a thread for venting, so I best ought to vent.<br /> <br /> With the Republican National Convention ongoing, I felt compelled to look back at the Last Week Tonight breaking down the details of prospects of a second term for a Donald Trump presidency. <br /> <br /> And a large amount of its focus was on the degree to which Trump and Republicans wish to more firmly subordinate the federal government to the presidency, to gut it of people who place expertise over loyalty, to annihilate the Department of Education, all that nasty stuff. Certainly terrible, and it offends my sensibilities as a person of liberal ideology and some of the aspects of what I recognise about what the United States requires to be functional along those lines.<br /> <br /> But the thing that sickens me is the clip it includes of Trump declaring an intent to get Congress to pass a bill to declare male and female the only two genders and that they are assigned at birth. To expressly state a wish to annihilate the concept of transition and non-binary from legal recognition in that country.<br /> <br /> And I don't know if that's possible or plausible or constitutional (assuming this Supreme Court would uphold that part of the constitution), but I think about every single person whom I know across two forums and a few other places that would be harmed by such a thing, by the very <i>notion</i> of such a thing in the highest echelons of power.<br /> <br /> I don't want Trump to be shot at for politically motivated reasons. I don't want that to be introduced as a feature of the political discourse of the world's most powerful liberal democracy any more than it already has been by a violent uprising motivated by the desire to overturn an election.<br /> <br /> But I want people to hear about things like that sort of hostility towards transgender and related people and remain <i>loud</i> about how that is a thing that cannot be accepted, that must be opposed fiercely and unrelentingly to the greatest extent that is permissible.<br /> <br /> That's my vent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T04:02:00-07:00","id":1538723,"title":"","content":"And now I'm going to vent about the fact that I'm never able to know who it is that ever down votes my posts in which I'm critical of transphobia so that I can identify some people to have nothing to do with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T09:13:37-07:00","id":1538760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1538677#post1538677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be nice if we saw a cool down on the extreme political speaches from both sides after what happened to Donald Trump and certainly in Canada we had nearly every poiltical leader condem the attack and calling for more civility in debates. But I don't think that it will happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>They say that because it is expected of them, and everyone <i>knows</i> it is expected of them. Which is why the extremism will only escalate.<br /> <br /> This project 2025 disease won't stop at the trans community, it WILL be the first step to their long-held wet dream of making every other ethnicity other than white into non-citizens. And that's a move that only gets corrected with blood and violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T20:23:38-07:00","id":1538810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1538677#post1538677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be nice if we saw a cool down on the extreme political speaches from both sides after what happened to Donald Trump and certainly in Canada we had nearly every poiltical leader condem the attack and calling for more civility in debates. But I don't think that it will happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I haven't seem much from the left that equals what you hear from the right. Like, remember that time Trump was retweeting people saying, &quot;The only good Democrat is a dead Democrat?&quot; I don't know that Biden or any other major Democrats have said or quoted anything that dangerous or reprehensible. Lt. Gov. Mark Robinson of North Carolina said, &quot;some people need killing.&quot; Again, I don't know of any major Democrats expressing similar views. If &quot;both sides&quot; are engaging in similarly dangerous rhetoric, it seems like it's 90% from conservatives and 10% from liberals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T05:28:46-07:00","id":1538825,"title":"","content":"Yeah, like, it's hard to not have some degree of harsh words when one side is saying &quot;all of our political opponents are vermin who are actively motivated to destroy America&quot; and the other side responds with &quot;having people who call their political opponents vermin is a threat to the very conduct of democracy&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T13:07:30-07:00","id":1538856,"title":"","content":"Thumbsdown Poster strikes again! Such a blow for &quot;freedom&quot;!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T18:41:37-07:00","id":1538884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1538856#post1538856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thumbsdown Poster strikes again! Such a blow for &quot;freedom&quot;!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine. You can't throw out facts without hurting some snowflakes feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T14:18:31-07:00","id":1538920,"title":"","content":"Mark Hamil and Jack Black certainly got into hot water for saying what they did about the attempt on Donald Trump's life, even if you don't like the guy personally he is still someone Dad, Husband, Grandfather and that he is still human with loved ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T14:28:37-07:00","id":1538922,"title":"","content":"It's been said enough times that people are so hurt over the most trivial things and even stuff that has nothing to do with them or will never affect them in the slightest and try to judge previous generations and soceities from current standards. Social Media has been a boon for them and along with bot accounts make them seem much larger then they truly are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T16:28:52-07:00","id":1538928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1538920#post1538920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">he is still someone Dad, Husband, Grandfather</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside anything one might say about Trump in particular, I've always found this a frankly bizarre thing to offer in an individual's defence.<br /> <br /> Both on the grounds that it doesn't say anything by itself about what the actual details of those relationships are (the world brims with men who are monsters to their children and spouses), and that a capacity to form close relationships with other individuals has no bearing on one's larger impacts and the manner in which they wield power.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T16:31:07-07:00","id":1538929,"title":"","content":"Anyway, at this moment I find myself coming away from looking at a conversation that continued in my absence struck with the twin frustrations of how, despite the likely ultimate benefits to mental health, it is supremely annoying to feel as though one is letting terrible viewpoints by bad faith actors have the floor unchallenged, and the extent to which blog comment threads are just the worst format to try and maintain a conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T16:34:30-07:00","id":1538930,"title":"","content":"It's kinda strange to applaud people getting dragged for ridiculous reasons (Mark Hamill for taking down a tweet that has nothing to do with Trump but it was sent out with very bad timing regarding the shooting, Jack Black for what his bandmate Kyle Gass said on stage even after Jack Black cancelled their tour in response), and then complain about how social media is enabling said behavior.<br /> <br /> The people trying to put Hamill and Black in &quot;hot water&quot; are the kind of &quot;hurt over trivial things&quot; people you're complaining about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T14:17:39-07:00","id":1539051,"title":"","content":"I don't know if Rachel Maddow is just trolling or is being serious, but according to her Lord Of The Rings is right wing politics and it's because of Donald Trump's running mate J.D. Vance is a fan of the series. Well she isn't a real journalist and is just a talking head/entertainer and that is what protects her somewhat from libel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T14:48:12-07:00","id":1539057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1539051#post1539051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if Rachel Maddow is just trolling or is being serious, but according to her Lord Of The Rings is right wing politics and it's because of Donald Trump's running mate J.D. Vance is a fan of the series. Well she isn't a real journalist and is just a talking head/entertainer and that is what protects her somewhat from libel.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s crazy! I love Lord of the Rings and I\u2019m not right wing at all. Knowing that J.D. Vance likes that series makes me like him a little more (that and he\u2019s married to a lovely Hindu woman and they have three biracial kids), but I still would never vote for him because of his views on abortion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T16:04:03-07:00","id":1539062,"title":"","content":"It's crazy because it's not true.<br /> <br /> She commented that a number of far-right folks in the tech-fiance economy (particularly Peter Thiel, JD Vance's primary financial backer) like using LotR for a source of names for their companies (Thiel started a company called Palantir, Vance started a company named Narya).<br /> <br /> She never said hat LotR is &quot;right wing politics,&quot; or even somehow tainted as a cultural work somehow. She just noted it's something that's very popular amongst a group of influential people that makes it easy to spot their stamp on things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T20:52:02-07:00","id":1539080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1539062#post1539062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's crazy because it's not true.<br /> <br /> She commented that a number of far-right folks in the tech-fiance economy (particularly Peter Thiel, JD Vance's primary financial backer) like using LotR for a source of names for their companies (Thiel started a company called Palantir, Vance started a company named Narya).<br /> <br /> She never said hat LotR is &quot;right wing politics,&quot; or even somehow tainted as a cultural work somehow. She just noted it's something that's very popular amongst a group of influential people that makes it easy to spot their stamp on things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T23:19:16-07:00","id":1539084,"title":"","content":"To give the full context, here's what she said (via <a href=\"https://www.mediaite.com/tv/rachel-maddow-connects-jd-vance-liking-lord-of-the-rings-to-far-right-its-aryan-but-you-move-the-n-to-the-front/\" target=\"_blank\">Mediaite</a>):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mr. Vance then was able to go and start another venture capital firm with, surprise, yet more help from Peter Thiel,\u201d began Maddow. \u201cLike Mr. Thiel, who has named his companies after things in the Lord of the Rings series of J.R.R. Tolkien books. Lord of the Rings is a sort of favorite cosmos for naming things and cultural references for a lot of far right and alt right figures, both in Europe and the United States. Peter Thiel names all these things after Tolkien figures in places like his company Palantir, for example.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike his mentor, like Peter Thiel, who had given him all his jobs in the world, Mr. Vance also when he founded his own venture capital firm with help from Peter Thiel, named it after a Lord of the Rings thing. He called it Narya, N-A-R-Y-A, which you can remember because it\u2019s Aryan, but you move the n to the front,\u201d she continued. \u201cApparently that word has something to do with elves and rings from the Lord of the Rings series, I don\u2019t know.\u201d </div> </div> </div>I took it more as her dismissively saying &quot;Look at those dorks liking Lord of the Rings.&quot;. But it's also a bit silly. Who cares...<br /> <br /> But now there are tons of articles out there with headlines saying &quot;Maddow claims LotR is far-right&quot; (a lot from right-wing publications). So the idea has been making the rounds. For example, Politico released an article titled <a href=\"https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2024/07/19/lord-of-the-rings-jd-vance-00169372\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;How Lord of the Rings Shaped JD Vance\u2019s Politics&quot;</a> which fruitlessly tries to make that claim from the headline stick. The idea that all of JD Vance's politics come from Lord of the Rings is obviously a bit far-fetched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T03:13:49-07:00","id":1539093,"title":"","content":"I've heard the audio, there's really not anything &quot;Look at those dorks liking Lord of the Rings,&quot; to it. She's also rather well know for calling herself thing like &quot;dork,&quot; &quot;nerd,&quot; and so on, as she has her own things that she tends to geek out about. It's really more of a, &quot;so, this is a thing I noticed looking up stuff about these guys trying to quickly put stuff together after Vance got the VP pick quickly and I'm a cable talking head that needs to fill an hour.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T03:24:21-07:00","id":1539094,"title":"","content":"That's how it seemed to me. But subjective opinions can differ on that.<br /> <br /> Not that any of it matters, to begin with. Who cares if they like Lord of the Rings or not and what they think the books are about. Their actual political views are more important than interrogating their takes on Lord of the Rings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T05:03:40-07:00","id":1539096,"title":"","content":"Still sounds really dismissive of Lord of the Rings. Makes me like Rachel Maddow less. Luckily I\u2019m not voting for her either.<br /> <br /> Let me explain. I don\u2019t dislike Rachel Maddow because of her politics. I dislike her because she spoke disparagingly about Lord of the Rings and didn\u2019t even know what Narya was (it\u2019s one of the elven rings), even though she claims to be kind of nerdy herself. Tbh it\u2019s unlikely that I\u2019ll dislike her for this reason forever. I\u2019m pretty forgiving. I\u2019m just a little annoyed with her rn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 07-23-2024, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T10:01:23-07:00","id":1539103,"title":"","content":"The way I read it there are two ways to think of this: One, liking LotR is actually crypto-right-wing behavior because Peter Thiel and JD Vance like LotR and they're right-wing. That would be an insane claim so I doubt that was the goal. Two, she's just trying to make fun of those two guys being so into LotR that their company-names are references to Tolkien's work because LotR is nerd-stuff. If you aren't trying to do either of those things, why even bring it up in this fashion?<br /> <br /> If this were a segment kind to Tolkien's work and people who are fans of it, the obvious approach would've been to just counter their love of LotR with other LotR-references, like for example, comparing JD Vance to the Mouth of Sauron or something. But &quot;Narya, more like Aryan, get it? And Narya has something to do with elves and rings. I don't know. That guy's just really into LotR.&quot; - that's some lame-ass boomer-humor. Another program I could absolutely see doing this the right way would be Last Week Tonight with John Oliver but that one is of course not the same type of show as Rachel Maddow's. But John Oliver's show is much better at tackling this sort of thing with humor in my opinion.<br /> <br /> And if it's supposed to be just serious coverage, the whole thing was just a waste of time anyway. Obviously, there are financial ties between Peter Thiel and JD Vance that are worth exploring for what they mean. Their love for LotR, though, is completely irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T12:51:40-07:00","id":1539109,"title":"","content":"It is actually still really easy for a lot of American and European reactionaries to appropriate Lord of the Rings to their ideology, some of the reasons for which aren't the work's fault and some of which... kind of are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There are nuances behind things like the ethnographic make up of that book's setting and how it aligns with the central conflict that a good faith analysis and conversation can recognise and evaluate, but I also think reading in good faith will recognise those nuances with things like how it's still unfortunate that people coded as African and Asian are framed entirely on the side of evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T13:15:37-07:00","id":1539111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1539109#post1539109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is actually still really easy for a lot of American and European reactionaries to appropriate Lord of the Rings to their ideology, some of the reasons for which aren't the work's fault and some of which... kind of are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There are nuances behind things like the ethnographic make up of that book's setting and how it aligns with the central conflict that a good faith analysis and conversation can recognise and evaluate, but I also think reading in good faith will recognise those nuances with things like how it's still unfortunate that people coded as African and Asian are framed entirely on the side of evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the thing with the Easterlings and the Haradrim being all on Sauron\u2019s side always bothered me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T15:59:20-07:00","id":1539115,"title":"","content":"Certainly lots of youtubers like Clownfish TV and others certainly did there take on how dumb Maddow was to make fun of J.D. Vance and Theil love for the books and not knowing the lore of the books and coming across as a buffoon. But she can't be sued for libel by the family as the one time she was sued at all, the court ruled that she is an entertainer and not a journalist.<br /> <br /> Which is fair as for the most part I don't view anchor people as legit reporters at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-23-2024, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T16:43:06-07:00","id":1539118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1539096#post1539096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike her because she spoke disparagingly about Lord of the Rings and didn\u2019t even know what Narya was (it\u2019s one of the elven rings), even though she claims to be kind of nerdy herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked &quot;nerdy&quot; doesn't mean being a hardcore LotR fan. Most people can't name the three rings given by Sauron to the Elves even if they generally enjoy the LotR books and associated media.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1539115#post1539115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly lots of youtubers like Clownfish TV and others certainly did there take on how dumb Maddow was to make fun of J.D. Vance and Theil love for the books and not knowing the lore of the books and coming across as a buffoon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is?<br /> <br /> Thiel and Vance don't give a shit about LotR. They name their stuff after LotR because they think it makes them more endearing to their perception of the kind of people that work in programming and associated engineering areas.<br /> <br /> I can't find the quote, but to paraphrase something I once heard about Thiel: He'd start a military software company named Isengard, name the AI program Saruman, and simultaneously be shocked when he's responsible for creating Skynet and not get the irony of it. Their own peers diss them precisely because they're fake-fans that want to sound &quot;cool&quot; to nerds and geeks, not people that pay any attention to what the names they're using actually mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T16:52:48-07:00","id":1539119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1539115#post1539115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly lots of youtubers like Clownfish TV and others certainly did there take on how dumb Maddow was to make fun of J.D. Vance and Theil <b>love for the books</b> and not knowing the lore of the books and coming across as a buffoon. But she can't be sued for libel by the family as the one time she was sued at all, the court ruled that she is an entertainer and not a journalist.<br /> <br /> Which is fair as for the most part I don't view anchor people as legit reporters at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how I'd characterize their streak of naming things after LotR material. More like they have a sense of odd exclusivity in their fandom and dedication, and consider themselves &quot;high brow&quot; or &quot;elevated&quot; over people who don't share their fandom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T08:09:46-07:00","id":1539144,"title":"","content":"Yeah, gatekeeping over the extent of insight into Tolkien legendarium, or even liking the Lord of the Rings at all, is not exactly the best look if anybody is of a mind set of &quot;it's wrong for people with nerdy interests to be made fun of&quot;.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I'm not at all sure why the word &quot;libel&quot; has entered this conversation. Libel is a crime based on assertions you make about a person that are supposedly factual, not having low opinions of them. In the United States, people are perfectly within their First Amendment rights to put it in writing that a person is a buffoon and their motives for how they name companies are ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T09:12:41-07:00","id":1539146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1539144#post1539144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, gatekeeping over the extent of insight into Tolkien legendarium, or even liking the Lord of the Rings at all, is not exactly the best look if anybody is of a mind set of &quot;it's wrong for people with nerdy interests to be made fun of&quot;.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I'm not at all sure why the word &quot;libel&quot; has entered this conversation. Libel is a crime based on assertions you make about a person that are supposedly factual, not having low opinions of them. In the United States, people are perfectly within their First Amendment rights to put it in writing that a person is a buffoon and their motives for how they name companies are ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under U.S. defamation law as interpreted by the Supreme Court, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> is absolutely right. I may not like what Rachel Maddow said about Lord of the Rings, but it is in no way libelous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T16:13:58-07:00","id":1539174,"title":"","content":"The libel stuff was brought up because it was mentioned on a number of popular youTube channels and most agree with what Isator said Amethyst and it was brought up that Maddow did have a libel suit in the past and the judge threw it out by stating that Racheal isn't a journalist by any definition and was an entertainer/talking head who didn't to be truthful in her shows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T17:10:35-07:00","id":1539177,"title":"","content":"Um, the libel suit against Maddow was dismissed, by multiple judges, on the merits of the case (that is, her statements weren't defamation and fell squarely under the First Amendment). She was giving her own commentary on reporting made by a third party and disputing the findings of an independent journalist doesn't prove defamation by someone relating that journalism to her audience. Multiple judges said that the full context of her segment made it clear she was not making a factual claim to now the matter as true from her own reporting, but was clearly expressing her opinions on existing reporting.<br /> <br /> Are you sure you're not confusing her libel case with Tucker Carlson's? Carlson's lawyer actively argued that he's untruthful and therefore nobody would reasonably consider anything on his show to be factual. That wasn't Maddow's defense in court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T13:13:13-07:00","id":1540097,"title":"","content":"Former performer Kevin Sullivan passed away today.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It sucks that the people we grew up watching in music, sports and entertainment are getting older and passing away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T23:20:49-07:00","id":1540415,"title":"","content":"I'm so pissed off and annoyed. I used to enjoy things and be happy. And now, everything feels terrible all the time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:32:26-07:00","id":1540461,"title":"","content":"Depression &amp; anxiety are no joking matter and can be a hard thing to live with and cripple you from doing anything. I know medication and talking to someone does help considerably and finding simple things to enjoy makes all the difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T18:39:24-07:00","id":1541047,"title":"","content":"Another professional wrestling I used to watch and somewhat enjoy passed away today at the age of 63 from cancer. I watched him during his time at WWF/WWE as Pyscho Sid and chuckling with some of things he would say in his promos such as saying that he had half the brain of the person he would be wrestling.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T11:56:38-07:00","id":1541206,"title":"","content":"To the person who gave a thumbs down on my comment on how depression and anxiety is a serious matter and how it can greatly impact the lives of people suffering from it and there loved ones. I hope that you don't find yourself in a situation and learn how it's poor form of what you did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T16:48:22-07:00","id":1541417,"title":"","content":"It's hard to listen or read media channels where you get called every ism under the sun to stifle legit criticism and now it's more of a badge of honor when you get called that.<br /> <br /> Example. The Acolyte was bad filmmaking as the fight scenes were poorly shot, the storyline was weak and most of the cast were not that great and the couple who had talent could only do so much with the material they were given.<br /> <br /> Nothing about politics, race or sex in the above statement, but I would get called every ism under the sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T06:37:41-07:00","id":1541443,"title":"","content":"I swear to God the number of times people in roleplaying games seem to insist on creating their own problems to then complain about the games doing.<br /> <br /> It stands out to me prominently with Exalted.<br /> &quot;Oh, character creation with this many Charms is such a burdensome task.&quot;<br /> ...Why? You only take a small minority of those Charms at character creation? Hell, most of them aren't even available as an option at character creation.<br /> &quot;They're a problem because they make it so hard to plan out the entire trajectory of my character from the beginning! How can I make decisions if I don't run the projections of every possibility and pitfall of where I build out from those decisions?!&quot;<br /> Can't you just... not do that?<br /> &quot;No, it's completely impossible!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> I am begging people to, if they're going to insist on being their own worst enemies, at least know where the blame lies for that rather than acting as though it's something the game is making them do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T11:29:55-07:00","id":1541472,"title":"","content":"That feels kinda like a massive excluded middle/false dichotomy. Exalted might not require that much preplanning, but the persistence of LCQA + BP/XP means the system incentivizes a lot of consideration over how you spend your creation points given how widely divergent the outcomes can be.<br /> <br /> As well, people are people. They have preconceptions from other games (the most popular TTRPG is very punishing for people that don't engage in character planning), other GMs/DMs/STs/etc., play groups, and so on. As well as person quirks that modify how they react to &quot;this is the rule&quot; vs &quot;this is just a guideline, but there's a lot of system mastery necessary to understand the full picture.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm certainly someone that overthinks Exalted char-gen (and char-gen in general), and plenty of that is me. But saying the games are blameless doesn't fly. How long I spend on Exalted characters could be dropped considerably with some rules alterations (many of which are very popular house rules for broader reasons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T15:50:39-07:00","id":1541491,"title":"","content":"Talk about deja vu. Florida is banning books again and among them is Mark Twain Tom Sawyer. I remember back in high school in the 1990's that this was a topic of debate that are teacher wanted to talk about and the overwhelming response was that banning his work was foolish as it was a product of it's time and we shouldn't shy away it all. Also insanely enough is that the Diary of Anne Frank is also on the 