reasonable people will make smart choices and not political hacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea... banning books is always bad. Ugh...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T08:39:45-07:00","id":1541532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541522#post1541522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea... banning books is always bad. Ugh...</div> </div> </div> </div>For anything but black market sales anyway....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seriously, the state of florida seems to have become synonymous with abject stupidity, along with texas. And I struggle to pinpoint exactly when that degeneration began, cuz it certainly didn't start with trumpism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T09:39:44-07:00","id":1541536,"title":"","content":"For the longest time people have been saying that the United States is going along parallel tracks that ended the Roman Empire. Such as greater concentration of political power and lack of compromise of giving up a little power but maintaining there authority in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T18:14:35-07:00","id":1541552,"title":"","content":"While it's informative to study history, including how major nations rose and fell, there are limitations in such comparisons. Rome in particular feels like a very weird choice because Rome and the US never really had that many similarities. The Roman Empire took longer to fall from its height under Trajan, to the division into the Eastern and Western Empires than the US has existed.<br /> <br /> If we want to look at Roman history, the Eastern Empire/Byzantium is a more interesting comparison. While Byzantium lasted a very long time after its significant decline after a few extremely prosperous centuries not having to send resources to prop up the western provinces any more (the Roman empire's agriculture centers were in the east), it's decline was driven by the rise of new empires that changed the focus and balance of power between nations (compare the US during WWI to WWII vs. the post Cold War era), a plague (compare to COVID), and increasing ideological divisions (Byzantium becoming a Christian nation followed by Islam's rise in power leading to serious diplomatic tensions, and isolated Byzantium from later Christian nations that arose to their west, compare to the US having to handle diplomacy with BRIC despite major cultural issues, and how the US has diverged from the course of liberal democracy in Europe).<br /> <br /> It's not a rosy picture (of course, we're assuming a comparison to a nation in irreversible decline is valid), but probably more informative to what's really worth considering about what lessons from history can help inform decisions now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T20:50:39-07:00","id":1541565,"title":"","content":"I wish we had the ability to review events from history like the device out of Fringe where Walter and Bell could observe the alternate Earth and learn about new technologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T04:20:26-07:00","id":1541568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541552#post1541552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's informative to study history, including how major nations rose and fell, there are limitations in such comparisons. Rome in particular feels like a very weird choice because Rome and the US never really had that many similarities. The Roman Empire took longer to fall from its height under Trajan, to the division into the Eastern and Western Empires than the US has existed.<br /> <br /> If we want to look at Roman history, the Eastern Empire/Byzantium is a more interesting comparison. While Byzantium lasted a very long time after its significant decline after a few extremely prosperous centuries not having to send resources to prop up the western provinces any more (the Roman empire's agriculture centers were in the east), it's decline was driven by the rise of new empires that changed the focus and balance of power between nations (compare the US during WWI to WWII vs. the post Cold War era), a plague (compare to COVID), and increasing ideological divisions (Byzantium becoming a Christian nation followed by Islam's rise in power leading to serious diplomatic tensions, and isolated Byzantium from later Christian nations that arose to their west, compare to the US having to handle diplomacy with BRIC despite major cultural issues, and how the US has diverged from the course of liberal democracy in Europe).<br /> <br /> It's not a rosy picture (of course, we're assuming a comparison to a nation in irreversible decline is valid), but probably more informative to what's really worth considering about what lessons from history can help inform decisions now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with the conservatives on this one, but there are some similarities. America is a Republic where both parties are saying that if the other party wins, it will be transformed into a despotic empire. Also, from the height of the empire under Trajan to the division under Diocletian is only 170 years. The U.S. has existed for almost 250 years. However, from the time of the decline of the Roman Republic and the age of Julius Caesar to the eventual fall of the Empire is over 500 years. A very long time indeed.<br /> <br /> Sorry <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>. I\u2019m mostly just taking pedantic issue with your dating system while agreeing with your general conclusion.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 09-05-2024, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T05:59:05-07:00","id":1541571,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the pedantry. I was just going from the death of Trajan to the death of Theodosius I (~270 years); as Theodosius is considered the last Emperor of the entire Roman Empire, and Diocletian divided the nation as more of an administrative issue than the Western and Eastern parts of the Roman Empire actually becoming separated nations (since, you know, they kept having one shared government between the two of them for over three centuries after Diocletian in the form of the Dominate). Plus if we're being pedantic Diocletian divided the Roman Empire into four administrative territories... but the Tetrarchy lasted all of 30 years, went back to the old provinces for 70 years, and then divided up into two for good when Theodosius died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T07:00:53-07:00","id":1541576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541571#post1541571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind the pedantry. I was just going from the death of Trajan to the death of Theodosius I (~270 years); as Theodosius is considered the last Emperor of the entire Roman Empire, and Diocletian divided the nation as more of an administrative issue than the Western and Eastern parts of the Roman Empire actually becoming separated nations (since, you know, they kept having one shared government between the two of them for over three centuries after Diocletian in the form of the Dominate). Plus if we're being pedantic Diocletian divided the Roman Empire into four administrative territories... but the Tetrarchy lasted all of 30 years, went back to the old provinces for 70 years, and then divided up into two for good when Theodosius died.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually didn\u2019t know that. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T07:35:45-07:00","id":1541588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541472#post1541472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That feels kinda like a massive excluded middle/false dichotomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but this is not the &quot;Feel Free to Nuance&quot; thread, and while I of all people don't have too much ground to stand on for the matter of not picking apart people's vents, I at least try to reserve it for things I think have more objectionable undertones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T09:41:28-07:00","id":1541591,"title":"","content":"Reading about the Roman Empire or Sparta is always good way to spend the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T14:48:51-07:00","id":1541603,"title":"","content":"Florida is even banning Stephen King's novels and at least 23 of them are on the list. I've read many of his books and I'm at a loss of what the issue is at all as it's marketed towards an older audience such as junior and high school \ud83c\udfeb.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't like his politics or find his writing meh I just don't see why he is on the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T17:20:49-07:00","id":1541616,"title":"","content":"Because when you make it insanely easy to ban books so you can ban the books you hate, you let loose anyone to ban anything. Florida book ban applications have included open admissions that the person seeking the ban has never read the book in question. For example, Stephen King has voiced his approval of the IT movies having Richie's true fear being his sexuality (as he himself admitted Richie was the weakest character in the original novel in regards to having a relatable fear with real depth to it), and including an act of homophobic violence in the second movie as a bad thing to have one person in Florida decide King is part of the &quot;evil woke agenda&quot; and thus all his books need to be banned over stuff added in a movie that's not even in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T18:54:40-07:00","id":1541624,"title":"","content":"You knew something was to easy when I saw that works of Mark Twain and The Diary of Anne Frank was on the banned list in Florida. What's next the literary works of Sir Arthur Conan Doyle because he probably held the common viewpoint of somebody from Victorian era England?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T23:03:10-07:00","id":1541634,"title":"","content":"Well, that would probably be something more Puritanical like &quot;Sherlock Holmes was a high functioning drug user,&quot; even though Doyle included that as a character flaw despite it being well before modern drug prohibitions while lots of people thought many drugs were valid medicines for home use.<br /> <br /> While this is being done by a rather small group of people (with the enabling of the state), it isn't the usual random quacks that have been trying to ban books in the US for ages but were generally rebuffed because... duh banning books is dumb. The book bans in Florida are being organized by a coalition of people with a specific agenda which is broadly bigoted, and promoting revisionist history to hide that from the students they're trying to deny a full education to. We know it's not actually just because they made the process easy, but also extremely biased: people have tried to get the Bible banned (all the rape, murder, incest, witchcraft, and so on that's used to justify banned other books cited as why), along with things like dictionaries as a protest, but it doesn't work because the decision makers don't have any ethical standards or review they have to muster. So they'll ban Anne Frank because her diary is a teenage girl's diary and includes her private thoughts on her maturing body as &quot;inappropriate sexual content&quot; and &quot;conveniently&quot; also get rid of a book that has helped generations learn about the Holocaust on a more personal instead of abstract level, and then OK a story about a king who purposefully orders one of his generals into a suicide mission just so said king could marry the general's widow because that's wholesome traditional values or something.<br /> <br /> While we have no idea how far this travesty is going to go before thinking-minded people prevail, it's not random. We know the content being targeted because the people that changed the laws to make this all possible, and the people filing the bans, openly worked together and openly said what content they're after. It's not random, nor is it a spree of every ideological partisan trying to ban all of the books their group doesn't like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T00:03:13-07:00","id":1541636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541603#post1541603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Florida is even banning Stephen King's novels and at least 23 of them are on the list. I've read many of his books and I'm at a loss of what the issue is at all as it's marketed towards an older audience such as junior and high school \ud83c\udfeb.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't like his politics or find his writing meh I just don't see why he is on the list.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because of his politics (or more accurately the political beliefs of the people going after his books). His books have been on the shelves for years. But he's been putting a target on himself lately by arguing with, and insulting, popular conservative superstars like Musk amd Trump. So people are going after him.<br /> <br /> Ultimately everything is political, even if you v don't see something as political, someone else will.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T09:05:30-07:00","id":1541651,"title":"","content":"I'm aware that Stephen King isn't a fan of Elon Musk and Donald Trump, but that is no reason to start banning his books and where do they go afterwards. Do they target Jonathan Kellerman because one of his main characters Detective Milo Sturgis gay and has been since he introduced him in 1986 and it's just a small part of whom he is and you could relate to him with no problem as he is on call and struggles to maintain relationships with his other half.<br /> <br /> I can picture that the publisher tried to get Kellerman to get rid of the Detective Milo or change his sexual orientation as this was back 1986.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T09:44:57-07:00","id":1541654,"title":"","content":"You make it sound depressing Heavy Arms that it will get worse before some sort of lucidity is regained.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T11:04:24-07:00","id":1541655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541651#post1541651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware that Stephen King isn't a fan of Elon Musk and Donald Trump, but that is no reason to start banning his books and where do they go afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is for the people responsible for the mess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they target Jonathan Kellerman because one of his main characters Detective Milo Sturgis gay and has been since he introduced him in 1986 and it's just a small part of whom he is and you could relate to him with no problem as he is on call and struggles to maintain relationships with his other half. </div> </div> </div>You're applying a style of logic coherence that isn't part of the thinking of the people we're talking about. Remember, they don't actually care about the topics. The goal is to use childhood education to promote their ideologies at all costs. The bald hypocrisy of claiming that it's an issue of &quot;parental rights&quot; to ban books about minorities despite that not respecting the parental rights of minority families is not a problem to their way of thinking; that's the point. The Alex Delaware series isn't exactly flying off the shelves in public school libraries, nor is it aimed at a younger audience, so it's not on their radar because it's not something perceived as &quot;influencing&quot; the youth.<br /> <br /> These are people that wanted to ban Harry Potter books because those are books aimed at kids... right up until Rowling made her political stances public and suddenly those books are safe. You can't understand this if you don't put it in the context of its intentions.<br /> <br /> And yes, it's depressing... because it's not getting better any time soon. The platform of one of the two meaningful US political parties currently includes gutting the federal agency that's trying to end it, and that same party appointed 2/3s of the highest court in the land that recently ruled to weaken those agencies anyway.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's going to get worse. The people doing it wouldn't be so brazen about it if it wasn't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T12:08:58-07:00","id":1541656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541591#post1541591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading about the Roman Empire or Sparta is always good way to spend the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's what I wrote my MA one, it makes me somewhat obsessed with societal collapse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T12:37:14-07:00","id":1541657,"title":"","content":"I remember when they went after Harry Potter books back in the 1990's and just rolled my eyes of here we go again and your right that I should apply rational thinking to a group that is not rational and come across as unhinged but this group like you said seem to be a different breed from went on before.<br /> <br /> I'm waiting for them to go after SlipKnot, Blink-182 and other musical groups because they wrote and sang about something they didn't like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T14:26:32-07:00","id":1541703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541532#post1541532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For anything but black market sales anyway....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, gooo point! I'm sure they make a killing on some of that stuff...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541532#post1541532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But seriously, the state of florida seems to have become synonymous with abject stupidity, along with texas. And I struggle to pinpoint exactly when that degeneration began, cuz it certainly didn't start with trumpism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I hear ya! It seems pretty crazy down there and has been a for a loooong time...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T04:28:54-07:00","id":1541772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541616#post1541616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, Stephen King has voiced his approval of the IT movies having Richie's true fear being his sexuality (as he himself admitted Richie was the weakest character in the original novel in regards to having a relatable fear with real depth to it), and including an act of homophobic violence in the second movie as a bad thing to have one person in Florida decide King is part of the &quot;evil woke agenda&quot; and thus all his books need to be banned over stuff added in a movie that's not even in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beg pardon, I'm finding some of the ordering in this a little ambiguous. Is this saying that the hate crime seen at the start of Chapter Two is another thing original to the films?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T06:21:04-07:00","id":1541775,"title":"","content":"Technically it's not original, but it was heavily modified from the events in the novel. The novel presents things from the sheriff's perspective as he investigates the body (notably the gay couple in the novel are significantly older while their attackers are actually younger which leads into); which was both beaten severely and tossed into the canal, but also had a suspicious wound on his chest. The teens all claim they did harass the couple, but a psycho clown did the killing; as the adults of Derry are under IT's influence they don't normally acknowledge Pennywise's actions and rationalize them away. In the novel, since it's mostly related in-character after-the-fact, what really happened isn't fully clear (though the movie's version of events is entirely in-keeping with what the novel's imply through the other gay man Don's version of events). Obviously multiple interviews would have eaten up a lot of screen time, and the movies drop the C-plot of the sheriff starting to believe in Pennywise/IT again which threatens the hold on the minds of the town's adults slip so presenting it in the form of the investigation doesn't have the same narrative importance.<br /> <br /> So, in the novel, there's significant room for interpretation (though it's clear Derry has a significant homphobia problem though given when the book was written it's a bit more matter of fact as homophobia was far more tolerated in 1984 and Don is a Derry native that decided to be much more obvious about his sexuality than the police are presented as finding &quot;appropriate&quot;) on how far the altercation went before Pennywise got involved due to it happening essentially &quot;off screen;&quot; though even the worse interpretation of what happened in the books is less vicious than the movies. As the whole book is an allegory for how bigotry insinuates its way into culture and adults internalize discrimination as normal and thus unremarkable instead of actually stopping the social ills that keep new generations locked in violent belief systems, the book repeatedly tells us to take the children (even teens old enough to be charged as adults in a murder case) at their word since they don't have the same blinders the adults do. Thus readers that want do not engage with the subtext of the whole story, and specifically this section of it (which in the novel comes in fairly early in the manuscript), can just take the teens' side of events that Pennywise bares the majority of the blame and the thus read the story as the attack didn't really get physical unlike the movie.<br /> <br /> NB: The miniseries from the 90s also completely cut this whole incident as well, which could influence people perceiving it as the movies making more of a political statement by adding on screen homophobic attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-09-2024, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T09:27:03-07:00","id":1541782,"title":"","content":"I'm old enough to remember the scandal when actress Ellen DeGeneres came out as a lesbian and was in a relationship with the late Anne Heche and some of the horrible names Ellen was called by religious conservatives and cheering when her show was cancelled back in the 1990's or I seem to remember that around the same time the creator of Gen 13 turned one of the popular male heroes gay and fans weren't pleased by it.<br /> <br /> It's shocking how much things have changed in such a short period of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T14:32:44-07:00","id":1541799,"title":"","content":"I remember when HIV/AIDS was something people claimed was proof of divine punishment against the &quot;sin of homosexuality&quot; and it was a considered a bit overboard instead of rank bigotry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T14:47:33-07:00","id":1541802,"title":"","content":"And now all we do is have entire US states become adamant about banning books with so much as a whiff of the subject and continuously infer that homosexuality entails a form of grooming. How far we've come.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541775#post1541775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the novel, there's significant room for interpretation (though it's clear Derry has a significant homphobia problem though given when the book was written it's a bit more matter of fact as homophobia was far more tolerated in 1984 and Don is a Derry native that decided to be much more obvious about his sexuality than the police are presented as finding &quot;appropriate&quot;) on how far the altercation went before Pennywise got involved due to it happening essentially &quot;off screen;&quot; though even the worse interpretation of what happened in the books is less vicious than the movies. As the whole book is an allegory for how bigotry insinuates its way into culture and adults internalize discrimination as normal and thus unremarkable instead of actually stopping the social ills that keep new generations locked in violent belief systems, the book repeatedly tells us to take the children (even teens old enough to be charged as adults in a murder case) at their word since they don't have the same blinders the adults do. Thus readers that want do not engage with the subtext of the whole story, and specifically this section of it (which in the novel comes in fairly early in the manuscript), can just take the teens' side of events that Pennywise bares the majority of the blame and the thus read the story as the attack didn't really get physical unlike the movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I'd always seen things like wiki summaries frame it as something much more direct and unambiguous.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T15:15:54-07:00","id":1541804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541799#post1541799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember when HIV/AIDS was something people claimed was proof of divine punishment against the &quot;sin of homosexuality&quot; and it was a considered a bit overboard instead of rank bigotry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that also and I remember the heartbreaking story of Ryan White who got HIV/AIDS due to a blood transfusion and people were scared to have their children going to school with him. Despite the fact that even then it was known that you couldn't get the virus through causal contact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T16:11:47-07:00","id":1541810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541802#post1541802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. I'd always seen things like wiki summaries frame it as something much more direct and unambiguous.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kinda like the shower scene in Psycho or the opening scene of Jaws. It feels extremely graphic and violent due to the skill in its execution, but if you watch it closely, you see how much the art is in letting people fill in the details. King's own public statements on it are also fairly blunt and unambiguous precisely because he got annoyed at people that refused to read into the subtext of the chapter's presentation and how it helps build up to the revelation of just how deep the rot in Derry goes. The attack comes up in the second chapter of the book, by the end of reading the book, what happened is fairly unambiguous, but it's part of building up the suspense and horror that early parts of the story only feel so obvious after you've finished the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T16:31:33-07:00","id":1541815,"title":"","content":"Stephen King is a master of letting his readers fill in the details in his stories and I remember that his horror novels are not all that graphic in comparison to his peers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T18:54:39-07:00","id":1541827,"title":"","content":"Why is my browser home page news feed constantly churning up Daily Mail headlines?<br /> <br /> I seriously do not want to be given constant reminders that there are some British conservative so-called journalists salivating over the idea of Donald Trump becoming US president again, or otherwise expressing their disgust at the existence of a woman of black and Indian heritage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T16:08:31-07:00","id":1541935,"title":"","content":"Hard to believe that today is the 23rd anniversary of 9/11 and being shocked by how much time has passed and learning that we would be fighting another war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T13:54:21-07:00","id":1541986,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how the above statement warrants a thumbs down, but all I can is how disappointed to see after the anniversary of such a tragic event that cost the lives of 3,000 people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T09:04:49-07:00","id":1542053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1541986#post1541986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how the above statement warrants a thumbs down, but all I can is how disappointed to see after the anniversary of such a tragic event that cost the lives of 3,000 people.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the wake of that one incident, stupidity in America increased every year until we got to where we are now. That may be a reason if you want one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T09:26:23-07:00","id":1542056,"title":"","content":"Not to mention how much easier it's now to spread misinformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T09:35:32-07:00","id":1542059,"title":"","content":"Disney can't seem to get a break from legal troubles with now the latest trouble over the use of Peter Gushing image in Rogue One that they didn't have proper permission and this had been in the courts for a few years until the story broke last night when the Judge ruled that there was a case to be made.<br /> <br /> On a more sad note. A moment of silence for actor James Earl Jones who played the voice of Darth Vader<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-13-2024, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T19:42:19-07:00","id":1542086,"title":"","content":"I... can't work up any sympathy towards Disney getting sued considering how litigious the House of Mouse is, and how much damage they've done to US intellectual property rights (both to the rights of the actual humans that create things, and the rights of the public for things to enter public domain after a reasonable amount of time). Major Disney lawsuits have their own Wikipedia page. If they didn't want to operate in a world where everyone in creative spaces needs to be ready to be sue and sue in return over the smallest things, they shouldn't have fought so hard to bring that world into being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T20:04:22-07:00","id":1542087,"title":"","content":"Oh I agree that Disney has done itself no favors in recent years with there litigious attitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T19:53:59-07:00","id":1542217,"title":"","content":"Hard to fathom that we had a second attempt on former President Trump in less than a month. Maybe we need to dail down the retoric as people can believe crazy things and act out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T00:37:01-07:00","id":1542233,"title":"","content":"It's... not that hard to believe. It's just that most attempts on US presidents or presidential candidates don't make the news because they're stopped before there was a chance for anything to happen. While the recent attempt on Trump was a close call, the Secret Service spotted the guy, were the ones doing all the shooting, and he fled before getting caught later.<br /> <br /> Given what little we know about the guy in this one... I'm not sure what the &quot;toning down the rhetoric&quot; thing would have really meant. If someone is willing to try to kill a politician over policy (still fairly speculative, but many news agencies say the guy was increasingly violent in his personal expressions about the Republican party's actual legislative actions and stated future policies regarding Russia's invasion of Ukraine)... there's not much rhetoric matters. There's no nice way to say, &quot;I'm going to pass this law,&quot; to someone that is willing to kill a politician for trying to pass that law. And that's even if there's a motivation that correlates at all to rhetoric or policies. &quot;I just wanted to be famous&quot; is a scarily common motivation of people trying to off US presidents/candidates... something that points to issues far beyond things like the tone of the political rhetoric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T06:34:41-07:00","id":1542244,"title":"","content":"Certainly doesn't help that the legal system has proven woefully impotent at dealing with the target and his set of people's litany of crimes. This new shooter may have assumed that there was no other chance for actual justice, rhetoric or no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T18:46:45-07:00","id":1542284,"title":"","content":"I hope that both candidates protection details have been augmented by recent events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T06:17:31-07:00","id":1542309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1542217#post1542217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard to fathom that we had a second attempt on former President Trump in less than a month. Maybe we need to dail down the retoric as people can believe crazy things and act out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said back when Trump proudly bragged about being a Nationalist, and again when he declared he would be a dictator, that he was playing with fire. There are a lot of people (mainly conservatives) in the US who believe that we have the 2nd Amendment for the specific purpose of being able to kill government agents when they or the government begin to lean into tyranny, even over personal home defense. So declaring you want to be a tyrant is maybe not such a great idea. Importantly it appears like both of the people who have tried to shoot Trump were conservative leaning Republicans and part of the crowd with strong beliefs about what the purpose of guns in relation to politicians is.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I think this is more of an issue with guns than it is with political rhetoric. At the least, it seems like most of the inflammatory rhetoric comes from the right - I don't know of anything that Biden or Harris have said that compares to, for example, Trump retweeting people saying that the only good Democrat is a dead Democrat. You generally don't hear that sort of rhetoric coming from the highest levels of the Democratic party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T09:16:16-07:00","id":1542318,"title":"","content":"....I hate this (not the assasination). <br /> <br /> I don't talk with my family. Ever. Mostly because whenever I go close to them in a place I can't run away from, it always ends with angry and bad feelings and yelling. So I just try to avoid them. <br /> <br /> What happens? They look for me and invite me over to go with them to places. And I, like a fool, agree. Yelling occurs again, and now they're telling me I'm cruel for not wanting to talk to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T11:49:42-07:00","id":1542330,"title":"","content":"I fully expect to see the Democracts follow suite and become more theatrical just like politics in general. Yesterday I saw Prime Minister Trudea and Opposition Leader Polieve putting on a great performance of political theatre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T14:17:45-07:00","id":1542336,"title":"","content":"O...K... but most of the public face of politics is theater and performance because humans aren't very rational in how they select their leaders in aggregate, and humans really don't like watching the legislative process (because it's slow, mired in procedural and traditional complexities, and just generally boring) actually happen. But in a system with even the trappings of democracy, politicians need to get votes, so they need to do things that appeal to their human constituents to get those votes. So a lot of theater happens because that's what works for the getting votes part and keeping their cushy jobs, even if it means their actual job performance suffers for it.<br /> <br /> Democrats are plenty theatrical as it is. The DNC put Bernie Sanders denouncing the billionaire class on stage right before JB Pritzker, a billionaire who used his status as richer than Trump to make jokes at Trump's expense, got up to talk... and while some people found that a bit odd, for the most part the theater worked and the seemingly disparate performances didn't turn people off.<br /> <br /> What's unlikely to happen is the Democrats getting more bombastic. Their theatrics are going to stay more subdued because that's the current brand: the Dems are the &quot;normal&quot; party that does normal things that will make everyday life better. That's a hard act to pull off if they start getting as off the rails as their opponents have been getting. It's a hard act in general because, &quot;we're the party of vital changes to fix things,&quot; and &quot;we're the party fighting for the normal status quo stuff everyone likes,&quot; aren't really compatible even if you can convince enough people that they'll get whichever they want if you sell it right. NFT digital trading cards, signed bibles, and limited run shoes aren't the kind of theatrics that do that sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T04:31:40-07:00","id":1542361,"title":"","content":"On a different subject: I\u2019m super busy with work this week and next. Wish I had more time to hang out on here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T09:28:33-07:00","id":1542370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1542361#post1542361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different subject: I\u2019m super busy with work this week and next. Wish I had more time to hang out on here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T14:30:52-07:00","id":1542396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1542361#post1542361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different subject: I\u2019m super busy with work this week and next. Wish I had more time to hang out on here.</div> </div> </div> </div>This happened to me as well in the last two weeks. Somebody at work is now gonna be away for a while... And it sucks especially because it's due to him getting a cancer diagnosis (it's lung-cancer... his heavy smoking past is catching up to him, I guess). Hopefully, it's just for a while, and this isn't too bad. Although, we're talking about cancer, so yeah... The whole situation at work just sucks right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T17:11:32-07:00","id":1542401,"title":"","content":"For myself I'm going have to adjust to a new work place and learn the ins and outs of it and try to make it pass probation and hope they will keep me on afterwards. For me it's pre-work nerves and reminding myself that I have done this type of work before and I'll catch on fairly quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T03:57:30-07:00","id":1542451,"title":"","content":"Something i find annoying is when you're pretty confident something someone said is bullshit but its academic bullshit so its going to take a lot of research to pick apart. Its partly why i find creationism and quack history so annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T12:05:06-07:00","id":1542488,"title":"","content":"I find Creationism and it's new face Intelligent Design and Pusedo History so annoying as it's just trust us and don't bother asking for us to provide actual sources to back up our claims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T13:35:00-07:00","id":1542496,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, it's not exactly great to let bad faith actors define the terms of a conversation. There are billions of people on Earth that believe in some form of Creationism as a religious/spiritual matter; and as such are content to have their beliefs and just want to have their beliefs treated with the same respect as any other belief. They have far more important and productive things to do than engage in debates that nobody can actually &quot;win&quot; because nobody can actually prove things one way or the other. Just like how plenty of agnostics and atheists hate it when a bunch of loudmouths act like they're being morally superior by treating people of faith like stupid rubes that can't possibly have reasoned belief systems.<br /> <br /> The problem is virtually always the assholes that go around trying to force everyone to bow to their way of thinking, not whatever philosophy they've latched onto (and generally misrepresent anyway). The way to avoid all the cluttering of such debates is simple: if a person is arguing a matter of doctrine is a matter of fact, point it out and let them deal with it. Either they can't and admit it, can't and aren't worth engaging with further, or can and maybe have something worth interrogating.<br /> <br /> Quack history is a problem but a different one because most of history isn't well documented. Historians spend years studying disparate and contradictory records and accounts trying to use a justifiable methodologies to try to establish the most likely way things happened. But the massive gaps, and reevaluations whenever there's a major discovery, this invariably leaves is always going to be a problem because you can plug the same facts into a different methodology and get a different answer. While there's plenty of things that are obviously quackery, the lines gets very blurry very quickly when you look at how many of the historical record is a matter of interpretation trying to string together rare well documented and well attested events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T23:39:10-07:00","id":1542506,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the one good thing that came from the information age was the fact that everything could be documented, uploaded, and archived in the internet to be perused in real time. But that only lasted for the historical equivalent of an eye blink before we entered the<i> disinformation</i> age, and suddenly deepfakes, AI, and every conceivable media creation kit allowed those same bad actors to flood the works with a near-continuous stream of utter bullshit. Now we are left with nothing being credible, nothing being trustworthy, and the effort necessary to untangle the mess is so monumental that it's not even worth it most of the time. <br /> The world is now infested with creatures that seek to lead all of civilization down a road of enhanced ignorance just so they can crawl their way into power they don't understand how to use, or prestige they don't deserve, or advantages that are momentary compared to the duration of their fallout. Of course, once it starts looking like people just want to burn everything to ash and leave nothing to profit from, <i>then</i> they'll start making little mewling noises about trying to de-escalate the rhetoric, or appeal to the common sense they already sabotaged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-23T14:48:49-07:00","id":1542534,"title":"","content":"Getting real tired of popping into the forums and seeing my notifications full of whichever wag decided the thing to do with their time was to thumbs-down react medium to large batches of my posts in semi-arbitrary fashion.<br /> <br /> I know I am Disagreeable\u2122 to some folks' sensibilities, but a lot of these downvotes are just my most recent posts regardless of their tone or content, and they've also branched into tagging some of my posts from multiple years ago in a similarly haphazard fashion. Assuming it's all the same person, they've been at this for the better part of half a year now, but it's a bit hard to report harassment with an anonymized feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T12:05:29-07:00","id":1542569,"title":"","content":"I know the feeling well Satchel as I've been on the recieving end of the thumbs down vote even for posts that are very general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T11:49:39-07:00","id":1542970,"title":"","content":"The innate dichotomy of American life is that our \u201cculture\u201d encourages wanton individualism so as to prompt new spectacle for our mindless consumer-based economy to react to. But at the same time we\u2019re prompting all this \u201crugged individualism\u201d, every bureaucratic system this country needs to actually function resists and despises such individualism. The more you deviate from a norm established decades ago, the more the system hates you and causes you grief for not conforming. Having worked in education for a decade now I keep seeing the same things pile up. Anyone with an even vaguely unstable lifestyle sees a drastic increase in the amount of paperwork they\u2019ll need to muddle through to get something done. If you move around a lot, the system hates you. If you can\u2019t stay in a stable marriage, it hates you. If you have a non-standard family for whatever reason, it hates you. If you can\u2019t secure a stable income and have to do a bunch of side-hustles or get paid under the table, it <b>hates </b><b>the hell out of </b><b>you</b>. Sure, it isn\u2019t helped that most of the population doesn\u2019t seem capable of actually reading the forms as opposed to skimming them, and yes, many of these people\u2019s brains shut down if they read 3+ lines of dry text, but that\u2019s another problem. Ultimately the whole system is just intolerant of change or deviance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The worst part is, <i>there is no way to fix this</i>. Any politician who claims otherwise is lying. No one will ever design a system so inclusive that it\u2019s capable of keeping up with the chaotic and/or irresponsible vicissitudes of people\u2019s lives, and there\u2019s no way to impose a permanent standard of behavior and life that will ever work. There will never be some legendary ruler or cabal of rulers capable of corralling this level of insanity, and anyone who thinks they can try is just lost in their own hubris. And yet, we are awash in idiots these days who think they can accomplish this clearly impossible feat by crushing everything they can\u2019t control or understand, which turns out to be A LOT.<br /> <br /> <br /> One wonders who they\u2019ll be crying to when they\u2019re left sitting in a field of ash with no one else to harass, enslave, exploit, swindle. or even interact with after everything burns down from their attempted tyranny.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T15:48:13-07:00","id":1542983,"title":"","content":"While I am extremely sympathetic towards... all of that... having worked on too many failed educational &quot;fixes&quot; at this point in my life... a big fix to US culture would be to sell the ends of means testing as a way to ensure individual freedom. Right now means testing is the source of the vast majority of bureaucratic red tape, but far too many Americans are sold on the idea that we need to means test everything to make sure the &quot;wrong&quot; people don't get stuff... no matter how many people that really need it don't get it because the system is busted, and how much we waste enforcing these rules that don't actually produce the results we want.<br /> <br /> Means testing is one of those things that kind of sounds good on an intuitive level (only poor people need food stamps, so lets make sure people asking for food stamps are poor), but in reality they always makes the system worse in aggregate. It is not hard to frame this as an attack on individualism and personal freedoms... because it is. It reduces people to numbers and strips them of context, so they can be spat of the system without the help they need to &quot;save money&quot; (even if it costs more to reject them than it would have to help them), to the point where there are people that can't get married, or buy a new car, or get a new job, because the system would screw them if they did! The government is threatening to hike your taxes for starting your own business to get out of poverty? That's an insult to American ruggedness!<br /> <br /> But that's not how it gets sold to the public at all. If it was, we could actually fix a lot of problems by getting rid of the bureaucracies that stand in the way by getting rid of the rules they exist to enforce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T12:37:27-07:00","id":1543024,"title":"","content":"I watched Francis Ford Coppola's newest film Megalopolis. And all the commentary that it's bad, stupid and absurd just made me curious. I didn't want to spoil it for myself and so I didn't read too many reviews. But I've read a few. After having seen the movie, I'm baffled why not every review mentions that this movie is clearly a love letter to Ayn Rand and her philosophy...? The credits might as well say &quot;Inspired by Atlas Shrugged&quot;.<br /> <br /> The movie's also silly, disjointed and there are quite a few scenes where the actors are just chewing the scenery with over-the-top-performances. I could live with all that but this is also a movie where &quot;Power to the people&quot; is the slogan of the bad guys (they made two cousins of Caesar/Adam Driver the Gracchi brothers, sort-of) and Adam Driver as the Ayn Randian super-genius-protagonist seems absurd as the savior of the human race. Adam Driver has quite a few scenes where &quot;chewing the scenery&quot; is an understatement of what he's doing. He reminded me of Nicholas Cage to be honest. It was that type of high-strung performance.<br /> <br /> One big element of the movie is also that the city in the movie is called &quot;New Rome&quot;, Adam Driver's character is called Caesar... you can probably already guess what the movie is trying to do at this point when you read just that. But of course, it's not wholly drawing parallels with ancient Rome because Crassus (played by Jon Voigt) is portrayed as a greedy old man at the beginning and the movie ends with him redeeming himself and exclaiming that he now should be known as &quot;Crassus The Generous&quot; because he intends to donate all his money to Adam Driver's Caesar-character (and that of course makes him a good guy as far as the movie is concerned). Crassus... If you know anything about the real guy, you know that he was a capital-A Asshole.<br /> <br /> What a bizarre movie...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T17:10:09-07:00","id":1543039,"title":"","content":"Still super busy with work. I probably won\u2019t get much of a chance to relax and hang out on here till sometime next week at the earliest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T22:02:02-07:00","id":1543048,"title":"","content":"It sounds like Francis Ford Coppola ambitious film Megalopolis isn't living up to the hype if you go by audience ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T15:04:15-07:00","id":1543166,"title":"","content":"I tried to watch the Joker sequel and I should have stayed away when I learned with Lady Gaga being in it and musical numbers. Gaga isn't a good proto Harley Quinn and her acting isn't all that good and this film shouldn't have been green lit as Joker works as a one off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T15:42:00-07:00","id":1543221,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to think that maybe we should up the driver's license age by a few years as I've been seeing way to many bad drivers on the road that forget about looking both ways before heading out into traffic or that pedestrian have right away or you can't slow down in a high traffic area to gaze at stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T23:59:50-07:00","id":1543254,"title":"","content":"It'll never happen... but I'd rather just have regular drivers tests. The idea that you take a test once as a relative kid and never have to show you've retained the skills and there's no testing for impairments is.... kinda ridiculous considering how dangerous driving can be. My grandmother was lucky she never killed anyone because she refused to move to a facility that would involve giving up her license, and insisted she was fine to drive despite racking up enough tickets and even getting arrested twice before her license was finally revoked by the state. Meanwhile, without any testing or oversight, in about 10 years I'll be subject to having my license revoked pretty much whenever the state feels like it (though they might never do it so... yay?) because I play by the rules and a medication I use that actually improves my ability to drive is abused by others and the age/dosage combo will have me classified as under the influence that was designed to stop people that don't need it.<br /> <br /> The current system is just too prone to failing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T09:51:37-07:00","id":1543269,"title":"","content":"Well maybe having a practical drivers exam every five years to see how much you have learned since and breaking any potential bad habits that endanger the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T15:32:24-07:00","id":1543291,"title":"","content":"I'm really getting tired by social media hacks blaming us the fans when movies, games or tv shows fail badly because we thought it wasn't well thought out, written, directed or acted or that it ignored lore from previous adaptations and we call them out on it.<br /> <br /> Everyone with some degree of critical thinking skills look at audience ratings instead of the critics who shill for anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T16:29:30-07:00","id":1543295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1543269#post1543269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well maybe having a practical drivers exam every five years to see how much you have learned since and breaking any potential bad habits that endanger the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, never going to happen. It's not a functional system because too many people need to drive to live in the US economy.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons for my general pessimism around this is because it would not be hard to change if people actually wanted to do it. There's nothing like the 2nd Amendment to dance around regarding smarter gun laws. And in fact, the US system is already built in a fashion that allows the government (well the states individually when it comes to road vehicles but interstate truck shipping is too important for any state to be too different from the rest): in the US, having a license doesn't guarantee you are legally allowed to operate a vehicle. Many vehicles require additional certifications, and those certifications can have requirements such as regularly physical exams, hours of time operating said vehicles safely, and continuing education. If you want to operate something that flies that's more complicated than a hot air balloon, the default is that you need a certification (and certs aren't inherently transferable from one class of flying vehicle to another). Driving is the opposite where the default is that you can drive something if you have a license, and certs are for more specialized cases (commercial truck drivers being the big one).<br /> <br /> Much like it wouldn't fix everything, but it would change a lot, when it comes to marijuana if the government would reschedule it to a different classification of drug, reclassifying road vehicles could open up lots of ways to regulate cars more effectively without having to completely redo the system and try to get tons of laws passed. Though there's still a huge need for this to be handled carefully because these sorts of rules changes have been used very poorly in the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1543291#post1543291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone with some degree of critical thinking skills look at audience ratings instead of the critics who shill for anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure people with any degree of critical thinking skills don't trust Internet aggregate rating systems broadly. We've seen movies get review bombed with more negative audience reviews than tickets that were sold at that time. The fact that review bombing is a thing, and that audience reviews rarely try to garner any sort of insight beyond a score (did a superhero movie do bad because it wasn't good, or because of superhero movie fatigue.... audience scores aren't going to tell you because there's no serious study of such things to figure out if there's any sort of audience consensus on why something's bad).<br /> <br /> While it's fair to be frustrated when you have a legitimate dislike of a film get lumped in with bad faith crap out there, at the same time it's not fair to say there's no issues with social media's outrage content machine and how it skews how people discuss media they consume at the same time. If the bad faith &quot;reviews&quot; out there have gotten so good at hiding among the real reactions people are having, that it's increasingly hard to tell the difference between the two, there is a social media problem. One person claiming to speak for the &quot;fans&quot; is one of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T17:13:05-07:00","id":1543298,"title":"","content":"It's frustrating to have legit dislikes for a game, movie, tv show or graphic novel and you try to calmly list why you don't like it and you get lumped in with bad faith people. Even critics like Jesterbells who isn't very political in her reviews gets called every ism under the sun. <br /> <br /> She just does her job of reviewing and listing the things she likes and dislikes. For instance she is a big fan of classic Harley Quinn and lists why she prefers that incarnation over the current one and why she thinks it doesn't work. But admits that it's just her take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T21:15:24-07:00","id":1543317,"title":"","content":"I admit I don't watch her videos because I try to have some sort of time in my life that isn't just binging social media content...<br /> <br /> But there's a very simple example of the problem (and it's not against her specifically, but she's not helping herself out either): She has a video about how The Marvels is &quot;the end&quot; of the MCU, and many videos about how Hollywood is &quot;ruining&quot; female characters. At the same time she has a video about how Joker 2 is a way worse movie (and the thumbnail directly compares it to The Marvels, that's not me drawing the comparison), but there's no series of videos about how the mistreatment of the Joker and multiple videos on Harley (and I get that if you primarily consume superhero stuff from a film makers perspective but the comics have done all sorts of crazy shit to both characters far beyond what the movies have done in their reinterpretations). There's no videos about how &quot;Hollywood as ruined...&quot; male characters, or how male lead movies are going to kill a franchise... then it's just how bad Hollywood (as a stand in for mainstream film companies in general regardless of location) is being screwed by the executive class.<br /> <br /> It plays directly into the social media outrage machine (though like any content creator she needs her clicks and views and she can only push back so much against it if she wants to) because it's still feeding off the perception that failures by women lead creatives and women lead films are somehow more insults to the fans and whatever; while duds from the dudes aren't as bad.<br /> <br /> Just like Megapolis isn't going to generate dozens of video essays on how the mystique of the auteur male film director that in no way actually generates quality films over the extreme oversight of studio films is actually bad for film making; and also helps cover up a lot of creepy behavior (from Coppola's own known issues for being handsy with female extras, to far more egregious cases like Woody Allen and Roman Polanski who get to be revered film makers but also people guilty of sexual violence).<br /> <br /> People are going to write those think pieces, I'm sure some of them will be made into YouTube videos or whatever, but those nuanced reviews that also point the finger at those who critique media and their own biases don't generate the ad revenue like &quot;STOP HATING FANS!&quot; will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T22:10:26-07:00","id":1543320,"title":"","content":"My YouTube habits have changed drastically in the last year or so. I just now watch Space Ice for his roasting of movies and Jesterbells for film reviews. The others such as Ryan Kinel and his ilk seem to love finding outrage and saying buzzword bingo and it gets tedious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T15:51:34-07:00","id":1543455,"title":"","content":"It's unsettling to see pro Hamas and Hezbollah supporters in Canada and the United States calling for our deaths and call out not to respect the laws of our respective countries because we are infidels. My knee jerk reaction is you should be thankful that you are allowed to express your opinions at all. You think places like China or the Middle East would tolerate calls for violence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T16:06:48-07:00","id":1543459,"title":"","content":"Hollywood really needs to remember to stick with entertaining the masses and not involve themselves into politics as they might wholly unqualified for such matters and given that they were willing to turn a blind eye to Harvey Weinstein, Woody Allen and Roman Polanski actions. They are the last people to tell us how to run our lives.<br /> <br /> At least a few keep mum on political matters when asked about it or sidestep the question when asked by a &quot;Journalist.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T18:57:36-07:00","id":1543480,"title":"","content":"That's a hell of a whiplash... &quot;People should be grateful the First Amendment protects their right to say bad things!&quot; and, &quot;People saying things I don't like need to shut up and stay in their lane.&quot;<br /> <br /> Despite the fact that the US is in theory a democracy, it doesn't make the vast majority of citizens particularly qualified to talk about things in any detail. People that make entertainment for others have every right to their personal political beliefs and every right to advocate for them as they see fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T04:50:44-07:00","id":1543616,"title":"","content":"Getting notifications that somebody quoted in response to something you wrote is often useful to keep a conversation going, but it can be frustrating at times to anticipate what thing you might have said that could have provoked a potentially interesting response only to find that it was something kind of pedantic that doesn't seem to have fully read you in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T14:57:18-07:00","id":1543643,"title":"","content":"Some what dissatisfied with the recent Vincent McMahon documentary as there's not much in the way of new reports or behind the scenes stories that if you followed somewhat that you didn't already know. Still for those who don't follow the industry and will be a eye opener of how cut throat the business is and how McMahon certainly gambled on the success of the WrestleMania showings in the early days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T21:44:14-07:00","id":1543729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1543480#post1543480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People that make entertainment for others have every right to their personal political beliefs and every right to advocate for them as they see fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine somebody trying to tell Frank Sinatra not to be political.<br /> <br /> Like, to his face. Maybe while he's actually hanging out with Sammy Davis Jr.<br /> <br /> You could almost admire the audacity of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T22:48:23-07:00","id":1543734,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to make a good live action adaptation of a popular video game at all? I learned that they did a Borderlands film with Kate Blanchett, Jamie Lee Curtis and Kevin Hart and from what I saw of the trailer and Space Ice roasting it the other day and I have hard time seeing Hart as Roland who is quite a serious character and is a big powerfully built fighter and both Jamie Lee Curtis and Kate are quite a lot older than the characters they protray.<br /> <br /> Couldn't they at least get a cast that looked closer to what they were in the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T01:23:24-07:00","id":1543741,"title":"","content":"Sure. Though it's hard to please everyone. Sonic the Hedgehog just had two really good movies, but they're not exactly representative of the video games at the same time.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem that's plagued adaptations is that popular games tend not to be styles of games that lend themselves well to film storytelling. Either what little narrative structure is in the game (ex: most fighting games) doesn't really work for ~2 hrs of story to go with replicating whatever genre appeals you're making to the original game (cont. ex.: fighting games need movies that justify a lot of fighting), and some games that have an adaptable narrative, but it's way too much to fit into a single movie (ex: The Last of Us working just fine as a TV series instead).<br /> <br /> Even if you include animated adaptations, there's also trying to walk the line between something that only makes sense to existing serious fans of the franchise (ex: the Pokemon animated films don't really work unless you watch enough of the Pokemon anime), and something that can capture wider audiences the only know a little bit about the franchise from pop culture.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue with studios thinking they need to go after huge video games. Probably one of the better live action video game adaptations recently was Werewolf Within... which didn't even bother really marketing itself as an adaptation. It kinda flew under the radar, but it's also working with a premise and style that you can make work in film. For those unfamiliar, Werewolf Within is a variation on the basic &quot;find the traitor&quot; games that have been around for ages were some players are secretly bad guys and the good guys have to figure out who the traitors are before it's too late (in this case, using werewolves as the bad guys). As a who-done-it style genre in the first place, it's easy to mold into a film, and a smaller lesser known game (than, say, Among Us) has more freedom to not trip up over fan expectations of the game.<br /> <br /> When you look at something like Borderlands... it was never going to work as a single film. The Borderlands games usually take 10-20 hours for relatively new players to beat the main campaigns without doing all the side quests/etc. There's no casting your way out of squeezing 10 hrs of narrative into a 2 hr film.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T09:31:19-07:00","id":1543759,"title":"","content":"Movies based on fighting games show a marked tendency to overthink the premise rather than follow the path of least resistance to &quot;a lot of early fighting games took their cues from Enter the Dragon&quot;.<br /> <br /> And I think that, depending on cutscenes, something like Borderlands at least has a running start to adapting 10+ hours of campaign gameplay when something like an action sequence lasts an average of four minutes rather than three hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 10-14-2024, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T04:22:28-07:00","id":1544084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1543734#post1543734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to make a good live action adaptation of a popular video game at all? I learned that they did a Borderlands film with Kate Blanchett, Jamie Lee Curtis and Kevin Hart and from what I saw of the trailer and Space Ice roasting it the other day and I have hard time seeing Hart as Roland who is quite a serious character and is a big powerfully built fighter and both Jamie Lee Curtis and Kate are quite a lot older than the characters they protray.<br /> <br /> Couldn't they at least get a cast that looked closer to what they were in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>While there aren't a ton of great video game adaptions, The Last of Us and Fallout were both great series that seemed to adapt the games fairly well. Fallout wasn't necessarily the same plot as the game though, which may have helped it. The Last of Us was great too though, and followed the story of the game I believe.<br /> <br /> As far as movies go though, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> mentioned, it's hard to cram a lot of video game story into a single movie... but there's been a few at least. Like Mortal Kombat, and Sonic the Hedgehog. Even Doom wasn't too too bad, all things considered. It wasn't great mind you, but it had it's moments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T05:28:59-07:00","id":1544345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1544084#post1544084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fallout wasn't necessarily the same plot as the game though, which may have helped it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any prospective adaptation of Fallout is probably helped a lot by the fact that it's already a setting predicated in telling largely unrelated stories that play off of its particular quirks and where sequels are usually telling the story of the evolution of the world rather than any given characters within it.<br /> <br /> Like, those game sequels are already often set decades apart.<br /> <br /> New Vegas shows that it doesn't even need the consistent element of a protagonist who came out of one of the Vaults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T13:42:10-07:00","id":1544355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1544345#post1544345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any prospective adaptation of Fallout is probably helped a lot by the fact that it's already a setting predicated in telling largely unrelated stories that play off of its particular quirks and where sequels are usually telling the story of the evolution of the world rather than any given characters within it.<br /> <br /> Like, those game sequels are already often set decades apart.<br /> <br /> New Vegas shows that it doesn't even need the consistent element of a protagonist who came out of one of the Vaults.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said! I've played Fallout 4, but I know a bit about the other games, so I'm with you on how stories work in that world, and that's why the tv series worked as well as it did!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T14:22:36-07:00","id":1544357,"title":"","content":"Even within the boundaries of how the franchise ought to stay within the confines of corny Americana, even the games still have vast amounts of untapped potential for settings and narratives. Make a Fallout set in Texas! The Great Lakes region. The Pacific Northwest. Do it with your TV series or your novels or your choose your own adventure mobile games. The 3000 miles between sea and shining sea is your oyster for that premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T13:28:41-07:00","id":1544425,"title":"","content":"I did like the DLC's for Fallout New Vegas where you encounter Joshua Graham who was the Malpis Legate for The Legion before Lanis and learn more about the origins of the faction. The other was when you encounter Ulysses who was suspposed to deliver the Platnium Chip to Mr. House and passed the job onto you out of resentment of causing the death of a community that he was fond of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T09:13:30-07:00","id":1544797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1544345#post1544345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any prospective adaptation of Fallout is probably helped a lot by the fact that it's already a setting predicated in telling largely unrelated stories that play off of its particular quirks and where sequels are usually telling the story of the evolution of the world rather than any given characters within it.<br /> <br /> Like, those game sequels are already often set decades apart.<br /> <br /> New Vegas shows that it doesn't even need the consistent element of a protagonist who came out of one of the Vaults.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Fallout's got an entire nation, and 2 entire centuries to fit inside them. You can tell plenty of stories. Tales of horror, heroism, freedom, slavery, kings, presidents, even just slice of life involving mole rats and trying to grow crops on irradiated soil...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T23:50:43-07:00","id":1545198,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m really nervous about the election","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T08:53:29-07:00","id":1545211,"title":"","content":"It's a very close one for sure and us Canadians are also watching with great interest as trade relations with us and Mexico will be altered in the aftermath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T08:27:39-08:00","id":1545310,"title":"","content":"That this could potentially be America's third <b>failed</b> intelligence check is both nerve-wracking and infuriating. It's costing some of us in sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,