d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T09:23:49-08:00","id":1545477,"title":"","content":"Knowing now that the country is stupid enough to allow for this sort of idiocy to happen yet again is proof that our country is so corrupt it may as well fall. I wonder what the MAGA cultists will do now that they've proven to everyone that the rule of law is pointless? It's not as if they're the only ones who can form violent uprisings and tear everything down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T11:48:04-08:00","id":1545481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1545452#post1545452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn\u2019t say that. A lot of states passed their own constitutional abortion measures.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) This doesn't mean as much as it sounds like. 10 states had a measure up, and six went according to the main politics of the states, with two in swing states (AZ and Nevada) passing, and only two passing in states where anti-abortion politics are mainstream.<br /> <br /> 2) Being a pro-abortion candidate in states that wanted abortion didn't seem to do much. If everyone that voted for those measures voted for the pro-abortion candidates (keeping in mind one of the failed measures was in a state where they need 60% to pass, not 50% like a candidate does), control over the White House and Senate would be looking very different from current projections. <br /> <br /> 3) Ballots measures mean nothing if the presumptive incoming administration does as it has indicated and start to enforce the Comstock Act; so abortion will be meaninglessly legal as getting the equipment or drugs to perform abortions will be impossible in any state that can't manufacture them from scratch, and will somehow cover the costs of patients getting access. This requires no act of legislation, so it can't be filibustered to death in the heavily divided Senate like a nationwide abortion ban would be if tried (assuming that the filibuster survives anyway). Nor does there seem to be any indication that the current SCOTUS would strike down the entire Comstock Act for being unconstitutional just because some parts of it are.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Worse the ballot measures really just show how broken the US system has become. The whole job of politicians is to enact and enforce legislation, but what policies candidates espouse have become wildly divorced from what gets them elected. Democracy can't function if 55% of a state votes they want X as a ballot measure, and then the candidate running anti-X gets 55% of the vote. And every bit of evidence people have tried to gather keeps showing that this isn't some single issue thing.<br /> <br /> A system that operates by having the general public enact laws politicians aren't, and then they elect people that try to undermine and thwart those laws however possible... is going to implode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T12:06:36-08:00","id":1545482,"title":"","content":"All I can say with any real degree of certainty. Is that the next four years will be interesting and what political parties will be in charge of the House &amp; Senate and what will or won't be done that will anger voters. It's interesting how well President Trump is liked by the middle class considering that he grew up in a wealthy household himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T12:08:53-08:00","id":1545483,"title":"","content":"To be fair Darksol is that many voters went with Donald Trump because they got tired of being called names by the left and the lazy media for not being in lock step with them.<br /> <br /> Also on CTV a political analyst wisely pointed out that the voters are way smarter then the media and political elite like to think and voted with there wallets. Having musicians and actors and actresses endorsing candidates don't mean much when they see how much the cost of living is going up and we're more concerned about that then what Taylor Swift or Beyonce Knowles think of Kamala Harris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-06-2024, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T12:38:34-08:00","id":1545487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1545483#post1545483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair Darksol is that many voters went with Donald Trump because they got tired of being called names by the left</div> </div> </div> </div>Now why would people who had never said or done anything objectionable at all in their lives ever be called names by anybody?<br /> <br /> Poor innocent lambs.<br /> <br /> Well, I'm sure a little assertion of their self-respect is really worth things like the ethnic cleansing of the country that the new president has consistently proposed.<br /> <br /> A president who has referred to immigrants as poisoning the blood of the nation, and his political opponents (with their ideals such as &quot;transgender people should exist&quot; as vermin. But I'm sure his supporters have been called far worse things that certainly were much more evocative of rhetoric from 1930s Germany.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the voters are way smarter then the media and political elite like to think and voted with there wallets. Having musicians and actors and actresses endorsing candidates don't mean much when they see how much the cost of living is going up</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure tarriffs across the board are really going to help ease that one off.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, also the extent to which they may very well have to start paying for early warning data on things like hurricanes, which are liable to become even more consistent and severe than they have been getting over the past few years when he once more removes the brakes on any kind of climate action.<br /> <br /> I'm sure he'll be motivated and capable to put together something that will ease the financial burdens of all the additional healthcare that climate change is going to entail as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 11-06-2024, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T13:06:52-08:00","id":1545489,"title":"","content":"Americans (broadly) are not &quot;smart&quot; when it comes to voting for their wallets. The very problem is that American voters are extremely short-sighted when it comes to the economy, and end up voting on immediate reactions instead of long term planning. Penny wise, and pound foolish is pretty much how Americans have been voting for decades. It's not subjective, it's not the &quot;elites,&quot; it's just objective fact if you look at voting trends and actual economic performances.<br /> <br /> Even in super liberal elite coastal places like San Fransisco and New York City the general public balks when it comes to voting for programs that have some up-front costs but will be massive improvements in the future, or voting out one politician the moment things are getting good because things haven't gotten good enough even though the new politician is basically going to make things worse based on what they're actually running on.<br /> <br /> I will believe Americans are broadly smart about economic voting when I see a lick of evidence that's the case; esp. when you consider the economic impact of issues that aren't treated as economic ones. In the meantime, I'll keep the mountain of evidence that most Americans (of all political stripes) will gladly piss a hundred dollars away to make sure the &quot;wrong&quot; kind of people don't get a single cent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"att