ank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T17:25:33-08:00","id":1545543,"title":"","content":"I almost had a nervous breakdown yesterday, but I feel better today and I\u2019m ready to go on with my life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T19:50:03-08:00","id":1545546,"title":"","content":"Good thing that you are feeling better Amethyst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T20:11:32-08:00","id":1545548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1545546#post1545546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thing that you are feeling better Amethyst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T21:39:37-08:00","id":1545551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1545535#post1545535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that we as a society that we might be spending to much time on Social Media and have become comfortable saying hurtful or disrespectful things that would get us punched in the face as ex boxer Mike Tyson would say..</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so it occurred to you then, that this might be the whole plan? The level of belligerent stupidity you find posted in chats or comment sections today never fails to remove any sympathy I might have for people. It makes it really easy to un-person someone and callously dismiss their existence, perfect for gathering an army of thugs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T22:44:43-08:00","id":1545555,"title":"","content":"Oh I know Darksol, but I still have some kernel of faith in humanity as most of us regardless of what political views we may have in a society will reject extremism as the dangerous behavior it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T23:19:11-08:00","id":1545561,"title":"","content":"To echo myself in the gush thread: there's a difference between not agreeing with extremism, and actively rejecting extremism (esp. acknowledging and pushing back against extremism from those you otherwise agree with). It's easy to have faith that humanity will say that extremism is bad. It's hard to say that most of humanity writ large is going to stand up and reject it in a fashion that actually matters. History just doesn't bare that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T11:33:51-08:00","id":1545577,"title":"","content":"Fair point Heavy Arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-09T14:52:35-08:00","id":1545624,"title":"","content":"I overheard some idiot talking about the &quot;destiny of people&quot;, and it made me mad enough that I almost set him on fire.<br /> <br /> I think I might truly despise the very idea of \u201cdestiny\u201d, that everyone has a specific role setup they\u2019re supposed to play. Because it\u2019s always well-to-do, privileged people who talk that nonsense. And it\u2019s always when they want to try to remind people of where they are supposed to be (namely beneath them) that they bring that nonsense up. You want me to believe that I\u2019m supposed to just be happy with whatever spare scraps are left over when some entitled trash run off with everything of value, cuz it\u2019s my \u201cdestiny\u201d? Somehow I\u2019m supposed to just be happy with a life of constantly being blocked by a bunch of pretentious morons and their systemic biases, cuz \u201cdestiny\u201d? And the degree to which they\u2019ll make up bullshit to prop that spiel up is disgusting; making up gods, philosophies, and other dogmatic crap to justify it. So you and your so-called god want me to believe that living with my face forced into the mud is absolutely vital to some cosmic plan for mankind? Bullshit. Your society wants me to think it\u2019s absolutely vital that I soldier on with only the merest pittance in return, and that it\u2019s absolutely vital that I not make any waves? More bullshit. Everything about that sounds like a scam designed to prop someone useless up at my expense when they did nothing to deserve it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T04:48:17-08:00","id":1545686,"title":"","content":"Reject moral authoritarianism<br /> <br /> Embrace hedonism and positive nihilism<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, as a nihilist myself, I despise how so many people assume that all nihilism is negative nihilism. This stereotype of nihilists being overly edgy brooding anarchist punks who cut themselves, wangst about everything, and listen to shitty music because &quot;nothing really matters&quot; is a gross and very inaccurate strawman.<br /> <br /> But I'm an actively positive nihilist who's not really cut from the same cloth as terminally online doomers.<br /> <br /> My two main mantras in life are &quot;I am cringe but I am free&quot; and &quot;You Only Live Once&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 11-11-2024, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T14:27:42-08:00","id":1545711,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I should laugh or cry about the trouble that Mattel is in with having to recall the dolls from Wicked as they provided the address to a porn site. Was it intentional or simple ineptitude, either way it's not a good day for company executives who might be out of a job.<br /> <br /> To there credit the people who run the Wicked adult site acted quickly to filter out the photos of the models when the news broke. But this will be a financial loss for Mattel as they fix the problem it will be to late to make money when the film comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-11-2024, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T20:08:51-08:00","id":1545830,"title":"","content":"Trump's really just going to assemble a who's who of the absolute worst people to fill government positions, eh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T23:07:02-08:00","id":1545833,"title":"","content":"You already have to be in the worst of the worst to consider taking the jobs in the first place... everyone that thought they could steer things in a better direction by being at the table is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T05:47:30-08:00","id":1545850,"title":"","content":"Ah, and now I'm hearing some people actually describing their motives for voting for Trump now, in which the consistent line was &quot;things were less expensive during his presidency&quot;.<br /> <br /> So it wasn't so much voting with their wallets in terms of any kind of coherent sense for what his policy propositions might do for them* as it was a fanciful hope that electing the same president again would cause things to go back in time.<br /> <br /> It's nice to know the driving motivation behind everything that is going to come of that.<br /> <br /> * As might be evidenced by stories coming out that within the last week there has been a very high incidence of people Googling &quot;what are tariffs&quot;. Incidentally, I sure hope that nobody was voting with a wallet that hoped to have any room to spend on RPG products, because quite a lot of that shit gets made in China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T08:03:50-08:00","id":1545852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1545830#post1545830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trump's really just going to assemble a who's who of the absolute worst people to fill government positions, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's rewarding those who stayed loyal to him, and unfortunately by default, those who stayed loyal to him are pretty terrible people. There will be a lot of problems from filling government positions with people who are loyal rather than those who are capable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T09:18:37-08:00","id":1545856,"title":"","content":"This first of those problems will be that America as a democratic republic ceases to be, and a christo-fascist dictatorship forms where it used to be. There's been a lot of angsting over what the dems did wrong all over the place, but the main problem is this; they thought america was populated mostly with rational, educated, empathetic, human beings. It is <i>actually</i> populated with ignorant, self-serving, opportunistic trash. The idiots googling &quot;how to change my vote&quot; and &quot;what's a tariff&quot; are just the first indicator of how stupid these people have become. Sooner or later it's going to dawn on them that there's no going back, and it's all their fault. Already people are seeing mass-layoffs and economic woes blight their lives, and I'm fresh out of sympathy for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T13:36:26-08:00","id":1545875,"title":"","content":"Calling people who voted for President Elect Trump as igorant and uneducated is not a good way to bring your point across and in fact it was statements like that that gave him the popular vote and electoral college votes in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T19:34:20-08:00","id":1545907,"title":"","content":"It's far too late for me to give even a<i> fraction</i> of a damn about how butt-hurt they may or may not be. Thanks to them, we ALL have to live with the aftermath of their bad decision-making. Prices are already rising, jobs are being pre-emptively dropped, already the backlash has started. If they wanted any kind of respect, any kind of sympathy from the rest of us, then they shouldn't have voted an <b>obvious</b> dictator into office and ruined the country for everyone. If they thought they were going to get away with people just casually letting that go, then &quot;idiot&quot; is too soft a word to describe them. Actions have consequences, now they can deal with theirs. This undercurrent of assumption that they're not supposed to be held accountable is just a testament to the very stupidity they are accused of.<br /> <br /> I've heard there are now wives divorcing husbands, families splitting up, and something called 4B importing from Korea thanks to the corruption they've unleashed. And I'll bet these people will tell themselves a litany of excuses for how it's somehow NOT their fault <b>every single day</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T20:02:28-08:00","id":1545910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1545875#post1545875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling people who voted for President Elect Trump as igorant and uneducated is not a good way to bring your point across and in fact it was statements like that that gave him the popular vote and electoral college votes in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn that it was pretty commonly known in the US that the previous administration sets the economy for the next one, so what, then, do we say to people who didn't like this economy but then just voted back in the person who's going to wreck it again? That goes beyond being penny wise and pound foolish. It's some serious, next level form of self-injury. The best that we can hope for is that Trump just ends up <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gAqE_GxsqMo\" target=\"_blank\">goofing off and eating candy.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T21:17:31-08:00","id":1545914,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">The OP had asked thsi thread be kept apolitical. I realize the political situation is a hot topic at the moment, but let's keep it out of this thread, please. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T13:02:36-08:00","id":1545959,"title":"","content":"Alrighty, here's something else that fills my soul with rancor; <b>Leaf Blowers</b><br /> <br /> The use of a leaf blower seems to indicate a startling lack of common sense or rational thought. Why does one employ such a device? Because leaves from trees fall into your yard. And why do those leaves fall? BECAUSE THAT'S HOW TREES WORK! If it is such an offense to have leaves fall onto your yard it makes more sense to move somewhere that has no such foliage, not to live in a city where trees are on every corner and in almost every yard. The instant the wind blows, which it will, all that &quot;work&quot; you just did with a leaf blower is undone and there is nothing you can do to stop it. All you accomplish by using one of those things is; filling the air with more greenhouse gasses (I've never seen an electric one) and making more noise than any one person deserves while disturbing everyone else around you. I can only conclude that the owners of such devices are attempting to look like they're being useful to cover up the fact of their utter uselessness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T16:15:42-08:00","id":1545972,"title":"","content":"I have an electric leaf blower (though it's not exactly quiet), and I need it because I get fined if my yard isn't kept to an acceptable level of tidiness.<br /> <br /> Also the wind really isn't as big of a problem as you think, because the idea isn't just to make a big pile of leaves: you then do something with them. During the big drop in the fall I mulch them, and then spread them back on the ground so that they can decompose (returning important nutrients to the soil, and a few invasive species need bigger leaves to over winter, so it cuts down on those) which reduces the use of artificial chemicals to keep things healthy. The rest of the year it's just a quick way to clean off walk-ways and such after a storm or heavy yard work.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that people were clearing leaves before we had power tools... people used to just use rakes to do the same work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-20T13:00:33-08:00","id":1546204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1545972#post1545972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an electric leaf blower (though it's not exactly quiet), and I need it because I get fined if my yard isn't kept to an acceptable level of tidiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I have an electric one just to clear off the grass from the driveway after I mow.<br /> <br /> I don't deal with a ton of leaves so I just let em stay where they fall.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-20T13:58:17-08:00","id":1546208,"title":"","content":"Winter is here and time for everyone to get used to winter driving again, but at least I don't live in Calgary as they were hit by a huge blast of snowfall early this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T13:39:34-08:00","id":1546257,"title":"","content":"I'm annoyed at Google as sometimes before I even text in what I want to look up in the search engine, I have to prove that I'm not a bot at all and go through whole bunch of hoops and I ask what is up with that? If it's to drive away potentiiol users from using the platform then it's working like a charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T17:19:05-08:00","id":1546266,"title":"","content":"Google's excuse is that it's designed to stop malware from spreading by flagging suspicious activity.<br /> <br /> The most common causes are blocking Google cookies, and using a VPN, ad blocker, or other privacy software. Basically, 99% of the time this happens, Google is try to harass someone into making it easier for Google to watch what they do, and feed their data into the ad service. If you're using something like that, you'll have to at least turn off your protective extensions for a search before turning them back on before Google will stop... though that's not always a guarantee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T01:27:17-08:00","id":1546330,"title":"","content":"Something which saddened me recently was how much recent trends in WoD and the community have killed the idea of the fandom for me. Chunks of the fandom are toxic and spiteful with their implicit disdain for Sabbat players or 'vampions', the game designers themselves often seem to implicitly endorse those outlooks on occasion. Ultimately these voices seem to dominate the conversation because the game supports their outlook and that's before we consider the relentlessly bitter infighting.<br /> <br /> It feels like looking at my childhood treehouse and it rotted and covered in racist graffiti.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-24-2024, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T19:48:49-08:00","id":1546363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546330#post1546330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something which saddened me recently was how much recent trends in WoD and the community have killed the idea of the fandom for me. Chunks of the fandom are toxic and spiteful with their implicit disdain for Sabbat players or 'vampions', the game designers themselves often seem to implicitly endorse those outlooks on occasion. Ultimately these voices seem to dominate the conversation because the game supports their outlook and that's before we consider the relentlessly bitter infighting.<br /> <br /> It feels like looking at my childhood treehouse and it rotted and covered in racist graffiti.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit i haven't really played any of the newer editions of WoD (mostly from lack of any interest in my group) but I do remember back in college there was a distinct favor in all their writing for the Anarch faction. The Gehenna supplement continually berated anyone for being anything sabbat, expounding on all the ways they were screwed over and contributed to the ending of the world. It was even in the VtM Bloodlines computer game, there were no truly &quot;good&quot; endings for your character without going either Anarch or Autarkis. You'd think this was nothing new, but it's somewhat disheartening to know they're still fighting about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T14:48:58-08:00","id":1546407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546330#post1546330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something which saddened me recently was how much recent trends in WoD and the community have killed the idea of the fandom for me. Chunks of the fandom are toxic and spiteful with their implicit disdain for Sabbat players or 'vampions', the game designers themselves often seem to implicitly endorse those outlooks on occasion. Ultimately these voices seem to dominate the conversation because the game supports their outlook and that's before we consider the relentlessly bitter infighting.<br /> <br /> It feels like looking at my childhood treehouse and it rotted and covered in racist graffiti.</div> </div> </div> </div>W5 gives me the same feeling, only that it set fire to the treehouse without caring what happened to the tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T16:51:11-08:00","id":1546413,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to figure out what we are doing wrong in our work career as I learned that MSNBC host Rachel Maddow was making $30,000000 a year for an hour long show that she would do once a week. Now it's twenty-five million a year and I got to find out soon how much other media people make.<br /> <br /> I just found that the average Canadian News Anchor people make about $64,000 a year and I'm guessing the more well known ones easily earn twice that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-25-2024, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T21:46:19-08:00","id":1546420,"title":"","content":"Most US anchor people make less than Canadian ones do (median here is ~$55K, though it's worth checking to see if your sources account for the differences in value of the two countries currencies).<br /> <br /> The problem is that you're comparing someone that was while she was hosting five times a week (and even kept a good sized viewship after she dropped that, though keep in mind she works on MSNBC's digital side more now with podcasts and the like) was frequently in the top 10 most viewed TV news/pundit types on cable. You can't put her (or her peers on Fox or CNN) at the same level as local news anchors. It's like comparing the CEO of a major car company to the CEO of a local car dealership. One being paid obnoxiously more than the other is how capitalism works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-26T19:58:43-08:00","id":1546440,"title":"","content":"Working in retail, it still somehow surprises me every year when the holiday season starts up, sooner and quicker each time! Or at least it feels like it does...management tells me that we got started with the Christmas stuff sooner last year, apparently we were behind schedule this year...!<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but we should not have Christmas stuff up, and music playing on the overhead, while Halloween is still ongoing and Thanksgiving has yet to even happen! Who is this all even for?? Even folks who adore Christmas still want it to maintain it's proper place, and all I see are workers AND customers rolling their eyes and complaining about it! I know TPTB get the most $$$ out of X-Mas, and I get that reason, but this isn't making anyone feel &quot;happy for the holidays&quot;, it just exposes how nakedly GREEDY the corporations really are...<br /> <br /> I feel like nothing's gonna change unless people sent a strong message to corporate America, maybe not a full-on boycott, per se, but just refusing to buy most stuff until after Thanksgiving, or around then. Maybe that would get them to lay off a bit? It's not like people *aren't* gonna buy a ton for X-mas, just give us the chance to ease into it, jeez!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (At this rate, Cowboy Bebop the Movie is gonna be correct, and Halloween/Thanksgiving/Christmas really will all just merge into one long holiday!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T11:42:25-08:00","id":1546456,"title":"","content":"The other day I ordered a PS4 game from Amazon, since I was about to finish one and wanted to play the sequel.<br /> <br /> I finished the game last night, and the new one was due to come today. Perfect timing!<br /> <br /> I get the package today and they sent me the damn Xbox version... ugh...<br /> <br /> So now I gotta return it and hope they send the right one...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T17:34:57-08:00","id":1546547,"title":"","content":"That is bad news Mr. Gone, I hope that you have better luck with the next order from Amazon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T17:48:27-08:00","id":1546549,"title":"","content":"At Heavy Arms. I was using Google to see how much your typical Canadian News Anchor person made per year and I didn't think to look up what there American counterparts make.<br /> <br /> I did learn that one of the ladies of The Social tv show who has been there for years. Her name is Melissa Grelio and in addition her job there and her other interests clears about $500,000 annually.<br /> <br /> Still compared to Rachael Maddow yearly salary, that is quite modest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T18:37:31-08:00","id":1546552,"title":"","content":"It's still a pretty apples and oranges comparison. The View, which is a more comparable US show to The Social, pays its hosts in a similar range as what Melissa Grelio makes. Daytime shows are seen as less prestigious, and bring in less viewers, than prime time news shows do... so it's less well paying (also since they tend to have multiple hosts that all demand relatively large paychecks instead of one personality, it's only functional if they all take &quot;smaller&quot; salaries).<br /> <br /> Does Rachel Maddow make an obscene amount of money? Sure. But she's an outlier at the top of her industry (and even then, she's a prime time host, a podcaster, and regularly writes out non-fiction books, so she's putting in a lot of hours compared her bosses that get paid even more for making decisions like &quot;our core audience likes Rachel Maddow, keep her well paid so she stays on the air,&quot; and then consider that a days work.<br /> <br /> Income disparities in the US are horrific, but the tiny fraction of individuals that actually work hard and get big paychecks for it are not the problem compared to all the corporate execs that draw huge salaries while not doing any hard work. Do we pay the top tier of entertainers too much? Probably. Do we let entertainment executives demand ridiculous compensation packages despite not even doing any of the work that makes their companies profitable? Yes. Is the second the bigger problem? Very much yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T19:55:02-08:00","id":1546554,"title":"","content":"Income disparity in Canada are equally as bad Heavy Arms and I agree that we do pay the top tier actors and actresses way to way to much money and maybe there should be a salary cap for them like they have in sports and execs always seems to fail upwards or get a generous severance package when they screw up so much that it can't be ignored.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't even know where to start to fix the problem as it seems so deeply imbedded in the culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-03-2024, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T00:35:26-08:00","id":1546557,"title":"","content":"Salary caps are something sports implement of their own volition because it's good for their bottom line: they don't have to pay players as much, and avoiding richer teams from buying up the contracts of all the best players helps ensure seasons are competitive so audiences have investment and don't disengage because a few teams win everything predictably.<br /> <br /> There's no reason for that in other industries.<br /> <br /> The problem is that this is a feature, not a bug, in capitalist systems. If this isn't happening, a capitalism based system would be collapsing. Since we're reaching the limits of Keynesian economic's ability to restrain capitalism via mixed economy checks via socialist backstops, the inevitable thing that needs to happen is a new economic system; likely a socialism basis with capitalist policies layered on top (because people don't really like pure socialism... people like a bit of inequality because they want to feel like people that work harder get more) instead of our current approach. But who knows what'll happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T20:45:49-08:00","id":1546575,"title":"","content":"I was just spitballing about how to keep A-list actors and actresses salaries more reasonable. Maybe a base salary and a cut of the movie profits if it's successful and provide a more competitive setting and everyone gives there best work and don't phone it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T23:39:59-08:00","id":1546578,"title":"","content":"Why though? There isn't much evidence of actor salary correlating to &quot;phoning it in;&quot; esp. since A-listers tend to already have some level of success-based pay as it is. Contracts can certainly lead to this, but that's frequently when a studio locks in someone for X films and the only motivation to be in the movie is to not be the one in breach of contract (the same thing happens in the music industry where artists will shovel out a bunch of mediocre records to end their deal with their current label in order to move to a new one or renegotiate their contracts).<br /> <br /> Recent entertainment spats aren't going to have actors get behind any sort of scheme that makes them even easier to screw over. Scarlett Johansson sued Disney because Black Widow got shifted from an in-theater only release to a simultaneous theater and streaming release, which cost her a lot of box office residuals in the process. The whole thing where the Batgirl movie was just tossed in the trash for a tax write off despite being finished means all the actors in it would have gotten base pay plus zero through no fault of their efforts.<br /> <br /> Again, I don't get the idea of going after the people that are at least creating and working for our collective benefit by giving us entertainment to enjoy; even if their salaries are ridiculously huge. Celebrity paychecks aren't destroying the economy or driving wealth inequality.<br /> <br /> Lets put this in a bit of perceptive: Keanu Reeves has the public record for the highest income for a single production (unadjusted for inflation because this combines salaries as well as residuals); that is one period of filming for a project even if it is not published as a single work. Namely the Matrix 2 and 3 where were shot at the same time. He has (so far!) made ~$156 million dollars for his work on those two movies. That's his total pay for everything for the whole film which took months to do (keeping in mind that includes him getting paid to go do press junkets to promote the films too). This is also a gross figure that doesn't include things like how much his agent got and all the other expenses A-list actors have as part of their jobs.<br /> <br /> Jeff Bezos makes more than that in a day. Not a day of work. He makes more than that sitting on his ass doing nothing for a day. Every day. And he's only getting richer, so that number keeps going up every year too.<br /> <br /> Why worry about how to control actor salaries in a world where the highest paid actors in the world are still make in a year what one guy makes in a day or two (Dwayne Johnson holds the record for most earnings in a single year, but keep in mind that's multiple films releasing over a short time frame regardless of shooting schedules). <br /> <br /> How much they make is a symptom of the problem, not the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T18:55:07-08:00","id":1546619,"title":"","content":"Not so much a vent, but some degree of disappointment of what Star Wars 7,8 and 9 could have been with some of the ideas that George Lucas had. This is from the YouTuber Bullets and Blockbusters who does deep dives into what were some of the initial ideas for movies that get made.<br /> <br /> Here's some of the ideas that George Lucas had for the sequels.<br /> <br /> The major theme is reconstruction of galactic civilization after decades of war with the Empire. They did have a major and decicive loss at Endor, but they were far from defeated and would continue to plague the New Republic for many years until that they couldn't hold onto their former holdings.<br /> <br /> The Empire would be now a group of small cells that would target the region's of the New Republic and be a general pain in the ass but far from a galatic threat. Until suddenly they became more organized and make serious gains against a still newborn Republic.<br /> <br /> There's was no Supreme Leader Snoke in the initial version but this new imperial threat was being led by a much older Darth Maul and a female Sith Lord named Talon.<br /> <br /> Ben Solo was being slowly seduced by Darth Talon and would still join the dark side but he wouldn't be acting like what he saw as Kylo Ren.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThat action would cause Han Solo and Liea to be estranged for a period of time but he wouldn't be a deadbeat Dad who lost track of ship for thirty years.<br /> <br /> In some early versions Finn was white and Poe was black. Finn was still a Storm Trooper who would defect as he didn't like what he saw and would be a Jedi student later. In some versions was that Poe would die during their escape from a Star Destroyer.<br /> <br /> Luke wasn't a surly bitter hermit as we saw in the films, but he was trying to figure out what he missed in creating his academy and was at the first temple trying to learn from the old scrolls.<br /> <br /> There was a going to be a female scavenger on the junk planet, but she was going to have more of Kylo Ren's hot headed demeanor.<br /> <br /> All in all there's some good story ideas that could have been used. If anything it shows that Kathleen Kennedy and J.J. Abrams didn't have a real vision and were doing things on the fly.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T20:11:48-08:00","id":1546621,"title":"","content":"That actually sounds incredibly boring to me. There's a reason why American entertainment basically acts like nothing happened between The US Civil War and WWI... while the Reconstruction era was intensely important to history... isn't not really a &quot;fun&quot; story you want to watch. The conflicts are too abstract, and the politics are too messy for a good narrative, and hand-waving just how difficult it is to reintegrate a divided society back into a single whole with a literal Chosen One undermines any real point of exploring a reconstruction allegory. I really don't think Star Wars fans would actually enjoy an Aaron Sorkin film written for space wizards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T20:51:04-08:00","id":1546622,"title":"","content":"In the hands of a good director it could work, but who is good enough to strike the right balance between politics and space opera. I can't think of to many off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T00:49:41-08:00","id":1546630,"title":"","content":"There's another problem really: Star Wars is a franchise that's been stuck in one continuity for too long. <br /> <br /> Something I watched a bit ago about the Halo video game franchise is that having one long on going continuity for 20+ years only hurts it in the long run, and Star Wars is basically in the same position despite the Disney Legacy cutting back of old canon. When everyone is wed to the original creator(s)'s vision and continuity in perpetuity, well after they're not working on it any more, it's a creative trap. If you stray too far from canon to make something you want to do, fans hate it for not being true to the franchise. If you stick to things as they've always been, it gets stale as you're just copying someone else's ideas without being them with their peculiar and individual passions and quirks.<br /> <br /> In franchises where reboots/resets/whatever are quickly established as normal, and fans are used to it, each new creative team has a lot more freedom to make the best iteration of the franchise they can do. It might still suck, it might be divisive, it might be beloved. But you only get beloved when new teams get a chance do to their own spin on things instead of having to take 20 or 30 or more years worth of lore and make sure you stick to that script. If you're a fan of Spider-man or Batman, you might not like the current blockbuster movie, but there's probably a TV show or cartoon right up your alley, because both characters get fresh takes all the time. Or worst case you just wait a bit and eventually there's going to be a new movie or show with a new team and a new take that's your speed. <br /> <br /> I think that's why most of the best Star Wars stuff right now comes out of the grab bag that is the Disney streaming shows. Each show's creative team gets a lot more leeway to tell their Star Wars story without worrying about what it means for the big Cinematic Universe that's been building off of the original movie. Some of the shows to focus on that part of it, but others basically get away with having nothing to do with the Skywalkers and their epic space opera.<br /> <br /> Or, another example that's the source of my handle and avatar: the Gundam franchise has a &quot;core&quot; continuity in the Universal Century that has, by far, the most stuff set in it. But they toss completely new settings with radically different premises into the mix on a regular basis. If a story doesn't work as a UC story, you just make a new timeline that it does work in. Again, some are duds, and some are masterpieces, but the room to experiment nets a better overall result than if everything had to stick to the UC canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T13:49:44-08:00","id":1546663,"title":"","content":"So God Of War co creator David Jaffe goes after Vara Dark on YouTube who mostly live streams games and gives her take on it both good and bad.<br /> <br /> Basically he said that she only is successful because of her looks and sex. I thought he was a crusader of progressive views, but this comes across as sexist and he got rightly condemned for it and now he said he was stirring the pot to get more views for his channel.<br /> <br /> I'm going with my first impression was that he was showing his true colors and couldn't believe that he is becoming increasingly irrelevant in the gaming media and lashed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T15:15:21-08:00","id":1546666,"title":"","content":"Eh, he was like this a decade ago when he got into trouble for claiming Twisted Metal is such a good game that if you give it to your girlfriend for Valentine's Day she's going to become extremely amorous, and it works even better if you trick her into thinking she beat you in multiplayer. At best, he's always been what was later coined &quot;dirtbag left,&quot; where his stated positions are to the left/progressive side of things, but presented with purposeful crassness and vulgarity. As is frequently the case with such types on the Internet, they invariably use their history of crude language as an excuse to cover up whenever they cross the line into hurtful statements - that would be just as bad if phrased politely, if not worse when stated more plainly - as people just getting offended at the word choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T21:56:29-08:00","id":1546678,"title":"","content":"He just showed his true colors and actually gave Vara Dark more subscribers and you know he won't get into a debate with the other side as he has no legit arguments to make.<br /> <br /> In fact that he admitted to doing this to create trouble is in fact a red flag and nobody will take him seriously for any debate whatsoever outside of him being a bitter troll with bad takes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-06-2024, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T04:45:06-08:00","id":1546683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546547#post1546547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is bad news Mr. Gone, I hope that you have better luck with the next order from Amazon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! They did ship me out the correct version, so that was good at least.<br /> <br /> But, earlier this week they shipped me the wrong movie and I had to return it and get a replacement.. LOL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T12:17:26-08:00","id":1546700,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat taken back by the vitriol towards singer Lizzo for her recent weight loss. I'm not into her type of music and I find body positivity as no excuse for not eating healthy and trying to work out and live a healthier lifestyle and reduce your risks for certain health problems.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that she had a major health scare that made her rethink her stance on body positivity and wants to change that in her personal life.<br /> <br /> But some people can't understand that notion of different viewpoints or that being overweight and out of shape is not a good thing to embrace as a lifestyle.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-07-2024, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T15:14:35-08:00","id":1546704,"title":"","content":"You don't need to guess, she's been pretty public about what happened:<br /> <br /> 1) It wasn't some sort of life changing medical scare, but a few years ago she injured her back and some of her physical therapy turned out to be exercise she found enjoyable and added to her long term routine.<br /> <br /> 2) She's dropped being vegan because she found it was easier for her to balance her diet and her emotional needs with lean animal proteins back on her menu.<br /> <br /> 3) For a number of reasons she wasn't as active on social media and in public appearances, so ~4 years of weight management (as she's pointed out she doesn't have a weight goal, her aims are to be healthy for whatever weight she is) came off as more sudden once she started getting back to her old level of public profile; making her weight loss look far more drastic than it was from her perspective.<br /> <br /> 4) Her thoughts on body positivity have shifted. To paraphrase her: some days she's happy with her body, and some days she's not. It's not healthy to deny when she's not happy, so she's made sure to adapt her life to have successful and healthy outlets for those times.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, screw anyone that has a problem with that. That's a positive way to approach life, and anyone that wants to publicly shame her for it is the one with positivity problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T18:51:01-08:00","id":1546711,"title":"","content":"Thanks for filling in some of the details on Lizzo story Heavy Arms. As I mentioned I'm not really all that into her music and didn't know about her back injury and that she found out some physical activities that she likes and eating better. I just knew that she was looking better then previous appearances and I thought like Adele was a good thing that they decided to eat healthy and excerise more.<br /> <br /> It's the people who seem to have problems with others promoting healthy lifestyle and losing weight and being called fatphobic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-07-2024, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T13:35:57-08:00","id":1546742,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm being blind &amp; foolish but did anyone really think Orc's were code for black people in roleplaying games? I never thought that and saw them simply as a race of aggressive raiders and fighters and I'm just curious what people thought of some these statements from the twitter mob? Please no flame wars and being disrespectful towards other people ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T13:37:14-08:00","id":1546743,"title":"","content":"Also on a different topic of which is you know that you are getting old when you start feeling more aches &amp; pains on a normal basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T16:09:21-08:00","id":1546749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546742#post1546742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm being blind &amp; foolish but did anyone really think Orc's were code for black people in roleplaying games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically he said it about Native Americans not black people, but yes: one dude named Gary Gygax definitely thought that. And his logic was that of European colonial racism, so who the non-white group in question is doesn't really matter, it's whoever's land was being stolen and then being painted as violent savages for defending themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T16:47:23-08:00","id":1546752,"title":"","content":"Interesting Heavy Arms, I also remember having to tell one poster that the Dark Eldar in Warhammer 40K are given that title has nothing to do with their flesh which is pale due to weak amount of sunlight that there interdemonsional city has but more to do with their dark and cruel inhuman nature and how they view everyone else as inferior and have no moral qualms about killing or torturing for amusement and feeding off the pain.<br /> <br /> I just brought this initial topic as I thought it was strange takes and thought where do they come up with these ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-13-2024, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T16:52:48-08:00","id":1546755,"title":"","content":"Gary Gyrax is a product of his time and probably knew his history better then most and drew up many myths in the creation of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T19:36:41-08:00","id":1546757,"title":"","content":"I really don't like the uncritical use of &quot;product of their time.&quot; Everyone is a product of their time, and everyone also has the ability to think for themselves. Being a product of his times explains why he couched things in terms of bioessentialism, but it doesn't change that bioessentialism is retread eugenics with all the racism and sexism that implies. It doesn't excuse not seeing it for what it was like lots of people at the time did.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't matter to your question. It's not just &quot;Twitter mob&quot; stuff. Regardless of Gygax's birthday, he pushed heavily for D&amp;D to include bioessentialism successfully, and thus modern RPGs were saddled with racist coded monsters from the beginning.<br /> <br /> His knowledge of history makes this worse, not better. He was asked, publicly, about what many people see as a paradox in how D&amp;D is constructed: creatures with low Intelligence are True Neutral because they lack the capacity more moral thought. Playable races had enough intelligence for moral thought and could fall along the spectra of alignments. Monster races could be intelligent enough for for mortal thought, but where hard coded as Evil. Should they be &quot;soft coded&quot; as Evil and if you raised an Orc in a Good society they'd be Good despite the books saying Orcs are always Evil? No, because to a bioessentialist that isn't a paradox. You can't raise Orcs to be Good, it's in their fundamental nature (biological essence) to be Evil despite their intelligence.<br /> <br /> And to drive home the point about this not being fantasy but related to real world views, Gygax referenced a Confederate officer and Indian hunter on the need to <u>kill Native American children to ensure their inherent savagery would be eliminated from the world</u>. So, Gygax himself, said Lawful Good D&amp;D characters should think like a slave owning proponent of genocide; and that's morally acceptable because bioessentialism means some races are just irredeemable like that. He knew his history and referenced that figure specifically. Nobody pulled a &quot;gotcha&quot; on him. He chose to say it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T20:24:07-08:00","id":1546758,"title":"","content":"This is quite illuminating Heavy Arms about D&amp;D as my first real experience to roleplaying games was the Dragonlance and R.A. Salvatore novels. The first roleplaying games I played were Shadowrun and Palladium Books where Kevin Siembada took a more nuanced approach to races and alignments and I thought D&amp;D followed the same thing.<br /> <br /> Gary Gyrax reference to a Confederate officer and Indian hunter is disappointing as I grew up near a reservation and had many friends there.<br /> <br /> Because of Shadowrun and Palladium Books I saw even monster races that were playable as people with there own history with good and bad folks.<br /> <br /> Like I know that in general that the Drow elves are generally and rightly seen as raiders and slavers, but you had exceptions to the rule like Drizzit and his late father and a decade and change ago we had a daughter of Be-Naire who took her own path into the surface world and even they struggled to be accepted by the people of the surface.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T21:44:30-08:00","id":1546759,"title":"","content":"Of course. Gygax was one dude. D&amp;D wasn't really just him, and that was decades ago... longer than most active TTRPG players have been alive ago. While the industry hasn't been perfect in its trend away from not-great-things being put into games (WoD 1e aged very poorly, and the attempts to fix it didn't age that much better), it has steadily been trending towards acknowledging how framing fantasy elements matters because authors and designers are real people and make real connections between fantasy and reality without always even intending it (or intending the way it came out in the end... ex: Beast the Primordial and it's mess of a core book).<br /> <br /> The thing about progress though, is that sometimes people kinda forget the need for it in the first place after a better normal has set in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T10:45:18-08:00","id":1546845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546742#post1546742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm being blind &amp; foolish but did anyone really think Orc's were code for black people in roleplaying games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one should consider it in terms of how the elements that orcs were written with have been applied in real life, what values those ideas have been used to promote, and how that might be experienced by people who find it reminiscent of either ways they've personally been treated, ways they know people in their background have been treated, or things that constitute part of the legacy of different ways they're currently treated.<br /> <br /> The extent to which Gygax very much intended them as a fantasy skin for Wild West narratives with American Indians notwithstanding, the idea of &quot;monstrous race of aggressive raiders who aggressively raid just because&quot; is not a neutral concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T18:14:17-08:00","id":1546853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546742#post1546742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm being blind &amp; foolish but did anyone really think Orc's were code for black people in roleplaying games? I never thought that and saw them simply as a race of aggressive raiders and fighters and I'm just curious what people thought of some these statements from the twitter mob? Please no flame wars and being disrespectful towards other people ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never really seen it. When Gygax was making D&amp;D, he basically just lifted everything out of Lord of the Rings. D&amp;D was &quot;wargaming in Middle Earth&quot;. Of course, over time Gygax started separating D&amp;D from Lord of the Rings, but it's pretty clear LotR was the primary foundation for D&amp;D. And Tolkien never intended for orcs to be stand-ins for black people. In Lord of the Rings there were some vague real-life inspirations for a few groups, like Hobbits represented British people who wanted to keep their heads down and avoid conflict, but for the most part there aren't very many strong parallels between racial groups in Lord of the Ring and racial groups in real life. There have been people who written that Tolkien was racist and such, but I don't feel that orcs were ever intended to be stand-ins for black people (or Asians or any other real-life racial group) in his writing.<br /> <br /> Now in early D&amp;D, one of the basic concepts was &quot;natural evil&quot; that is, races (like orcs) were naturally born evil and even via nurture they could never rise above that. And Gygax made comparisons of orcs to Native Americans, in the idea that they raid and attack towns and such. But that was something that quickly became outdated and even by early 2nd edition D&amp;D you were starting to see exceptions to that concept and seeing the occasional member of an evil race that was of neutral or good alignment. And then towards the end of 2nd edition edition you were beginning to see that those exceptions weren't very exceptional. <br /> <br /> These days, of course, any links between real-world groups and fantasy groups in D&amp;D are gone, and most all of the &quot;traditionally evil&quot; races have large non-evil subgroups, and the gameline goes out of its way to make it clear that nobody is &quot;born evil&quot; but rather it's due to societies (usually under the sway of evil gods) that cause certain races to be largely evil, so those concepts no longer exist within the gameline. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T20:42:04-08:00","id":1546855,"title":"","content":"While Tolkien didn't intend for orcs to be black, the framing wasn't great. That said, there is a lot of intentional coding in the LotR. Tolkien might not have meant it as derogatory, but it always suffers from what happens when a person with zero connection to minority or foreign cultures tries to include them as fantasy parallels: you get stereotypes that are insulting even if the intent was a compliment. It's pretty hard to escape things like Tolkien saying that his dwarves were meant to be coded as Jews. His decision to make the Christian coded peoples of the West (elves, hobbits, some men) as being more resistant to Sauron's influence because of their spiritual connections to Eru Iluvatar, while Southrons (aka men from Middle Earth's equivalent to North African/Middle Eastern peoples) are easily corrupted by Sauron by rejecting the Valar, is not something you can just handwave away as innocent. You can try to repeat one of the countless arguments against the simple facts of the matter, but it's easier to just accept that LotR definitely promotes European Christians as correct and thus other peoples and cultures are inferior and should be ruled over by the divinely ordained true Numenorians.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> The problem with, &quot;and now the old links are gone,&quot; is that they aren't gone, just finally more history than current reality. The more people push to just have inclusive fantasy because it's fantasy and who cares if you want to have more diversity in characters, the more there's push back to return to the &quot;proper days&quot; of RPGs where things like Gygax's bioessentialism was normal. This links are like persistent weeds: you need to keep tending the garden and pulling the weeds up before they spread, or unfortunately there's more than enough people out there that will gladly have weeds to make the garden too ugly for others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T03:23:47-08:00","id":1546857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546855#post1546855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's easier to just accept that LotR definitely promotes European Christians as correct and thus other peoples and cultures are inferior and should be ruled over by the divinely ordained true Numenorians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that there's a lot that needs to be critically examined in the topic of race in The Lord of the Rings, up to and including appendix descriptions of how Aragorn continues to make war on eastern and southern neighbours for the sake of Gondor's security.<br /> <br /> But I will also say that it was pretty textual that the Numenoreans being imperialistic over Middle Earth is framed as a moral failing and their divine favour didn't entail them having authority over other people, as well as the idea that Numenor is gone and its legacy is finite within Middle Earth. The latter is often framed as a eugenics kind of thing, but Tolkien is on record with the point that it's really more that the more integrated Numenorean descendants become with inhabitants of Middle Earth, they more they become wedded to that land and its prosaic qualities, as the memory of their divinely gifted homeland fades away.<br /> <br /> Given things like the Kinstrife and Faramir's critique of how cloistered and out of touch many high families of Gondor are becoming as they obsess over the past and guard their lineage to the point of having no families at all, I think Tolkien was depicting mixing with other peoples of Middle Earth and letting the memory of Numenor go as the better option.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T05:39:16-08:00","id":1546860,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that really goes with what Tolkien's writings imply... though he waffled a lot about the Fourth Age and whether he wanted a cyclical myth or the Fifth Age and later to shift from the mythic past of Middle Earth into the modern history of our world.<br /> <br /> He never really presented the Numenoreans as not having a divine right to rule (Aragon was made king for exactly this reason, and he and his son alone ruled for as much of the Fourth Age as Tolkien ever decided on as &quot;proper&quot; noble rulers that reunited the Numenorean kingdoms and shepherded in an age of prosperity and peace for the hobbits and middle men of the west), just that they were still flawed, and many mistook imperialism for their duty towards true nobility. The Kin-Strife happened well before the events of LotR, and Aragorn's ascension and ideal dynasty kinda refute the idea that Numenor was best forgotten.<br /> <br /> I don't think the eugenics critique works in the slightest... royals have been picky about their bloodlines for thousands and thousands of years in reality for the simple reasons of practical inheritance and the more ephemeral narratives used to justify absolute hereditary monarchy. Eugenics isn't about ensuring the royals and noble aristocrats have their bloodlines in order, but the entire society needs to be &quot;pure.&quot;<br /> <br /> It still doesn't really escape that the Westrons via the Numenoreans got the objectively correct religion of Eru, and were purposefully coded by Tolkien to be the secret mythological ancestors of the Germanic peoples of Europe. Who would then find the right religion again, and the British Empire would become (by most metrics) the largest empire in non-mythological history just in time for Tolkien to be alive. I don't think his writings and known comments really adamantly state that he really meant that to be the overt message in all this, but at the same time I really don't think he did much to avoid the implications of the narrative he set up. However much he was public in his disgust at folks like Wagner for using mythology to base German propaganda and well know stories, Tolkien was at best very blind to how much his own work played into British propaganda. As you said, the perspectives of those that experienced European colonization of their lands are going to view the work in a very different light than the people that benefited from colonialism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T12:32:26-08:00","id":1546873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546860#post1546860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He never really presented the Numenoreans as not having a divine right to rule (Aragon was made king for exactly this reason</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's a Numenor specific thing so much as it is being a descendant of kings thing.<br /> <br /> Although even then, there's more to it than just the family line; if Gondor was okay with that, they would have accepted an heir from the Northern kingdom long before. Aragorn at least had to do a lot of legwork to demonstrate himself as a king worth accepting to people of standing and esteem in Gondor in addition to having a claim to press by right of ancestry. And Aragorn had spent his life acting in a manner to be so impressive because Elrond said it was the only thing that would make him worthy of being a husband for Arwen, so he put a lot of effort into it rather than coasting on anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">refute the idea that Numenor was best forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe forgotten wasn't the best word, but certainly accepted as something past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the eugenics critique works in the slightest... royals have been picky about their bloodlines for thousands and thousands of years in reality for the simple reasons of practical inheritance and the more ephemeral narratives used to justify absolute hereditary monarchy. Eugenics isn't about ensuring the royals and noble aristocrats have their bloodlines in order, but the entire society needs to be &quot;pure.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, there were probably commoner Numenoreans who were on those refugee ships as well, plus those who had been settled already in the colonies that became Arnor and Gondor.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about people reading a eugenics angle into the fact that they stopped living dramatically longer than other humans, as well as the ultimate loss of the other preternatural capabilities implied to have been possessed by them, which was given <i>some</i> attribution to intermarriage with other people of Middle Earth.<br /> <br /> That Aragorn then goes on to live far longer than any of his other more recent ancestors read to me as being a whole &quot;special divine reward for being instrumental in the downfall of manifest evil&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still doesn't really escape that the Westrons via the Numenoreans got the objectively correct religion of Eru, and were purposefully coded by Tolkien to be the secret mythological ancestors of the Germanic peoples of Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does raise some interesting questions about the absence of much overt religion in Tolkien's work as a whole (even in actual Numenor, the most religion they ever seemed to have was a single annual thanksgiving ritual conducted by the king towards God), but that's getting far too much more off track.<br /> <br /> I think the rest of what you're saying does get back towards the valid direction of the problematic implications of Tolkien's depiction of race, I just don't think it carries the specifics of the specific subset of white people having a textual anointed right of authority over all other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T17:18:24-08:00","id":1546884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546873#post1546873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that's a Numenor specific thing so much as it is being a descendant of kings thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure these are separable for the LotR. Aragorn was almost 90 when he became king (so he was already long lived before joining the Fellowship and getting rewarded for all that). The only reason he had the chance to do so many awesome things to prove his worth beyond his ancestry was because of his Numenorean blood (on top of some of the deeds also requiring that to work regardless of his age).<br /> <br /> A lot of proving himself worthy to the nobles of Gondor was proving himself a worth successor of the Numenorean legacy. Numenor might be the past, but it's cultural impact is still vital to the image of the kingdoms of the Westrons. Just like ancient Athens and the Roman Republic are long gone, we still cling to their legacies as part of the cultural mythology that creates the social attachment to western democracy. And while appreciating our history and legacy is important and can be very educational, it's also easily twisted to ugly means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That does raise some interesting questions about the absence of much overt religion in Tolkien's work as a whole (even in actual Numenor, the most religion they ever seemed to have was a single annual thanksgiving ritual conducted by the king towards God), but that's getting far too much more off track. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it's that interesting: Tolkien wanted Middle-Earth to appeal to a wide audience and didn't want to make a religion that was too specific, and as an academic he was well aware that religion worked a lot differently in the past. &quot;Going to church every Sunday,&quot; is a fairly recent invention in the history of religion, compared to very personal and private spirituality combined with seasonal major ruler-class lead community rituals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the rest of what you're saying does get back towards the valid direction of the problematic implications of Tolkien's depiction of race, I just don't think it carries the specifics of the specific subset of white people having a textual anointed right of authority over all other people. </div> </div> </div>Again though, audience experience colors interpretation. I hear, on a fairly regular basis, about how white Christian men should be the only default citizens of the US and everyone else should only have a say in the rules if we prove ourselves loyal enough to earn a seat at their table. Their reasoning sounds a lot like everyone explaining why Middle Earth needed Aragorn to become king instead of just getting rid of monarchs and everyone just becoming like the hobbits instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-12T23:01:10-08:00","id":1546914,"title":"","content":"As i recall western men wernt particulary resistant to evil im lotr with serveral cultures falling (the celtic hillmen, the majority of numerorians) and examples of personal corruption (grima and boromir). The andorians, gondorians are also painfully fallable to the point non western peoples support of sauron is partially rooted in legitimate greviances.<br /> <br /> I suppose he could have added a nice non western faction but that'd be more a writting decision based on contempory moral concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T04:28:49-08:00","id":1546921,"title":"","content":"That's the thing I try to be mindful of is not judging older societies based on present day moral values. Be it movies, books or ideals I try to remember that reality and not fall to what some with cool wits call smugness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-13-2024, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T08:34:17-08:00","id":1546925,"title":"","content":"Delete please. Irrelivant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-13-2024, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T10:38:38-08:00","id":1546930,"title":"","content":"On a different note. I try my best to seperate the art from the artist ideal, but there are times when I cannot do that at all. Is there any particular people that you just unable to do?<br /> <br /> For example I can't overlook the fact that Roman Polonsky had sexual relations with a 13 year old girl and had to flee the country and still makes movies and I can not believe that he is still alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T15:28:45-08:00","id":1546934,"title":"","content":"As someone that doesn't think Death of the Author is an &quot;ideal&quot; to strive for, and is only useful as a partial examination of any given work, I have quite a large list of media creators I refuse to separate from their art.<br /> <br /> Woody Allen is a specific example mostly because <i>Manhattan</i> left me stunned at how much people were willing to overlook the horrifically disturbing plot being treated as a character-study comedy even before people starting believing Mia Farrow more about how badly Allen acted in his private life. People were shocked that a guy that wrote a story where a character that's basically him - a 42 year old - is dating a 17 year old, and everyone that knows treats it like a midlife crisis where instead of buying a fancy car he's dating a girl that he can't leave NY with because he'd end up breaking the law in those states (and federal trafficking laws)... and then he cheated on his long-time partner (with whom he had shared custody of some of her children) with her daughter, with an even wider age gap than his fictional counterpart... and he still had people that defend him and people that actively want to work with him because the &quot;art&quot; is worth it? Nah. There's more than a enough good art to engage with that doesn't involve lessening yourself to indulge at best an extremely creepy man.<br /> <br /> There is this very weird phenomenon where artists can basically get away with being horrible people by making art about themselves; the desire to separate the art of the artist always seems to come up as a primary justification for why either nobody paid any attention or worse nobody believed victims despite said artists telling on themselves. Woody Allen's career was an eye opener to me about how bad that was back in the 90s, and in 2024 I don't see all that much having changed even with the impact of MeToo leading to more and more influential people in the entertainment industry being revealed for their atrocious behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T15:47:48-08:00","id":1546935,"title":"","content":"Yes I remember back in the 1990's when the Woody Allen story broke about him being in a sexual relationship with Sun Yi who was his adopted daughter with Mia Farrow and being so shocked by the story and how he still had a career after that.<br /> <br /> Hollywood was and is still willing to overlook terrible things like that if the money is good. Look at Harvey Weinstein and what he got away with for years until they couldn't overlook it anymore and I I read the eye opening book from Ronan Farrow who covered the story","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T16:27:47-08:00","id":1546941,"title":"","content":"Banality; I think of all these cool things I can create on my computer (cool to me), and when I get home, I just lose interest and resort to playing video-games. Sigh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T05:20:28-08:00","id":1546960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546941#post1546941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banality; I think of all these cool things I can create on my computer (cool to me), and when I get home, I just lose interest and resort to playing video-games. Sigh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to treat video games as a reward for something, this motivates me quite well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T12:47:46-08:00","id":1546974,"title":"","content":"It happens to all of us Iguazu as I want to flesh out my fictional city more and I get tired from work and I want to color, read a novel or watch a film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-14-2024, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T09:03:59-08:00","id":1547060,"title":"","content":"Ever wonder how the world would fare if suddenly all music and art were to suddenly be packed up and redacted from public consumption? All the images people sift through online, all the music from recording artists both mainstream and amateur, all the sculpture, the graphic design that goes into ads, the fashions, the movies, all suddenly just halted? I only wonder because it doesn\u2019t really seem like the world actually gives a damn about any of that. Rather it takes these things for granted to the point it can\u2019t even properly gauge their value. People mostly just pirate music and images online, and even if they don\u2019t, AI programs certainly do now. I wonder how long it\u2019ll be before all these things just dissolve away into bland, rehashed, AI-driven garbage.<br /> <br /> <br /> The only time you hear about any kind of fine art pieces in media are when they\u2019re being wrecked, or when they\u2019re found as part of some rich bastard\u2019s stash, or a criminal\u2019s attempt to launder money. If you\u2019re a musician and you aren\u2019t topping charts then you\u2019re just making noise as far as anyone else around you seems to care.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T15:25:54-08:00","id":1547076,"title":"","content":"While a lot of artists are going to suffer, I think in the end this current period of devaluing artists to maximize profits is definitely going to result of a morass of &quot;AI&quot; slop that will eventually have people desperate for human made art; esp, independent art that doesn't go through corporate hands.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem is that gauging the value of art is impossible. Art doesn't have intrinsic economic value (sorta by definition). Art tends to flourish when people have enough free time that creative people can earn a living and have plenty of time and energy to make art as well (removing the need for value or wide-scale public affirmation to factor into why an artists decides to make something), or society values art enough that &quot;base line&quot; art that is bland but nice enough to purchase is still assigned enough aesthetic value to price at a sustainable point.<br /> <br /> As society is currently in the process of thoroughly trashing the ability of artists to make a living be society decided art is valuable, our hope for the future of art is more in independent and folk art traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T16:46:23-08:00","id":1547078,"title":"","content":"I'll tell you, if I had a nickel for every time somebody felt the need to come along and &quot;um, actually&quot; me about something that I said about three months ago, I'd have two nickels.<br /> <br /> Which isn't a lot, but it still pisses me off that it happened once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T16:46:47-08:00","id":1547079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1547076#post1547076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a lot of artists are going to suffer, I think in the end this current period of devaluing artists to maximize profits is definitely going to result of a morass of &quot;AI&quot; slop that will eventually have people desperate for human made art; esp, independent art that doesn't go through corporate hands.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem is that gauging the value of art is impossible. Art doesn't have intrinsic economic value (sorta by definition). Art tends to flourish when people have enough free time that creative people can earn a living and have plenty of time and energy to make art as well (removing the need for value or wide-scale public affirmation to factor into why an artists decides to make something), or society values art enough that &quot;base line&quot; art that is bland but nice enough to purchase is still assigned enough aesthetic value to price at a sustainable point.<br /> <br /> As society is currently in the process of thoroughly trashing the ability of artists to make a living be society decided art is valuable, our hope for the future of art is more in independent and folk art traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well said! I keep hoping the AI Slop is gonna die down... but sadly doesn't seem like it's going to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-18T18:29:55-08:00","id":1547138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1546974#post1546974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It happens to all of us Iguazu as I want to flesh out my fictional city more and I get tired from work and I want to color, read a novel or watch a film.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's been happening to me lately; mostly though, I don't have a problem creating something; just half-way through it, I get an even cooler idea and I leave that project and start working on my new idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":2521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","user":"Iguazu","date":". 12-18-2024, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T00:08:41-08:00","id":1547298,"title":"","content":"Changed phone, moved country, and now the goddamned kindle app on my phone is refusing to give me back my books. Maybe I shouldn't have bothered buying things, and should have just flat out pirated it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T07:04:47-08:00","id":1547304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1547298#post1547298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changed phone, moved country, and now the goddamned kindle app on my phone is refusing to give me back my books. Maybe I shouldn't have bothered buying things, and should have just flat out pirated it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the whole, &quot;You don't own the stuff that buy,&quot; is bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T15:39:07-08:00","id":1547315,"title":"","content":"In this case, it can also just be a distribution-by-area issue. Even when there's less hiding behind &quot;purchase doesn't mean you own it,&quot; like Netflix where you're much more clearly paying for access, you can run into issues when you travel to a different country because Netflix might distribute a property in one country but not another.<br /> <br /> While it's not a great use of one's data plan, most VPNs come with geospoofing these days, so you should be able to set your location to the country where you &quot;bought&quot; your Kindle files, and most likely be able to download them and then access them locally once you turn geospoofing off (because that can be hell on using your phone as a phone). It's not optimal, but it could at least be a solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T17:32:26-08:00","id":1547508,"title":"","content":"I used to think that entertainment executives were way too dismissive of the average movie goer intelligence, but as I get older and see how people need to have their hands held to have plot points explained and if YouTube movie reactors are a sample of typical audience members. Then I'm getting more depressed about that.<br /> <br /> For instance the Constantine movie with Keanu Reeves and how they didn't even know the basics of who Lucifer Morningstar is when he appears or know what he is doing to John after he saw his throphy slipping away from the selfless act he did or thinking that Gabriel went to Hell after her attack on the Devil failed and we saw the loss of wings and the seeing her clearly falling into the pool.<br /> <br /> When we go to the theater I'll hear statements of what just happened and I'm thinking did you fall asleep, go to the bathroom or get food? Please pay attention to the exposition scenes as they help tell you what the story is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-07-2025, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T13:49:00-08:00","id":1547556,"title":"","content":"I'm glad to hear that former actor Jake Llyod is doing better now as he has been battling mental illness for years and that his mother and himself have pointed out that it wasn't due to so called toxic fandom that caused it as it runs in the family and enjoyed his time playing Anakin Skywalker in the Phantom Menace and likes the older games still.<br /> <br /> We really need to battle the stigma of mental illness and point out that it's not weakness to admit that you need help especially over things that you can't really control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-06-2025, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T08:45:53-08:00","id":1547588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1547556#post1547556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We really need to battle the stigma of mental illness and point out that it's not weakness to admit that you need help especially over things that you can't really control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth. We used to worry about the stigma of intellectual and developmental disabilities, because it was easy to marginalize those folks - they looked and acted different. Now the marginalization of those with metnal health issues is way too easy. The &quot;just power through it&quot; crowd has a loud voice. The more high profile people talk about it the better!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28688-rredmond","name":"rredmond","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28688_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T11:34:55-08:00","id":1547595,"title":"","content":"Some are speaking about it. Actor Jean Claude Van Damme has been open about dealing with rapid cycling bio polar disorder when he was diagnosed with it when he hit middle age. From what I recall that it can show up later in life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T11:37:43-08:00","id":1547596,"title":"","content":"While I don't disagree, we can't ignore that destimgatization without fixing the issue with access to mental health care accomplishes very little (and really makes the stigmas harder to deal with). Convincing people that need help to get it is hard enough without the process of getting it potentially taking months or years only to find out insurance doesn't cover it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T22:18:42-08:00","id":1547611,"title":"","content":"I know that we had a family member who was diagnosed with Vascular Dementia and he denied it for the longest time. Denial we learned can be very powerful and dangerous to behold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-08T17:35:55-08:00","id":1547640,"title":"","content":"A pity that the Transformers game has been more or less cancelled, I hope that we are not seeing a decline in the property as I'm a big fan of the universe and I'm enjoying the current Image Comics run by Robert Kirkman team.<br /> <br /> But I have seen the toys in my place have not been selling well and are taking up space on the shelves. Price and Christmas probably played a part in it or is the newer generations not all that keen on the IP?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-11T09:03:25-08:00","id":1547680,"title":"","content":"Something tells that heads are going to roll with the aftermath of the California wildfires and how unprepared they were for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-11T13:06:25-08:00","id":1547685,"title":"","content":"The problem is that while certainly someone is going to get thrown under the bus for this, it's invariably going to be the wrong person/people.<br /> <br /> 1) The fires are a regional event over multiple jurisdictions. No matter how well prepared, there's invariably time lost in managing responses across nearly a dozen different groups. I'm sure lots of people are going to try to weigh in on the LAFD and city budget negotiations, but neither the LAFD, the LA city council, or mayor Bass seem to think the yearly budget adjustments would have made a significant difference; calls for accountability though are unlikely to care about that.<br /> <br /> 2) The fires growing so large are a product of multiple problems that have been getting worse for decades if not centuries all hitting at the same time. There's limits on what you can prepare for when it comes to natural disasters in general, and even less you can do when you've been handed the shit-end of a stick that combines multiple facets of climate change, underfunded forest management, and flat out racist laws that nobody paid much attention to until recently as California fires have been getting worse (specifically in the 1800s the state outlawed the controlled burning methods used by indigenous peoples of the area for &quot;scientific&quot; methods proposed by colonial settlers, which has be quietly making that controlled burns the state does less and less effective over time).<br /> <br /> 3) While I don't want to come over as overly crass here, that's a lot of people that might not have realized it, but voted for this. People voted against controlled burns in their neighborhoods because they didn't want the smoke and air quality bad days, because fires started in other places so why should they deal with it (because it still meant lots of fuel was in their neighborhoods and fire doesn't give a shit about city lines). People voted against ordinances to reduce or remove certain ornamental plants that look nice but also explode during intense fires spreading the fire even faster. Etc. etc. etc. <br /> <br /> And that gets us to the problem: we needed <i>generations</i> of southern Californian residents to be doing their part to keep the area resistant to fires (because fires have been happening there for thousands of years, and people have been living there for thousands of years, so it's not like we don't understand how to live there). Nobody alive today could have done enough to undo all the damage of generations of neglect of problems that could have been addressed before they got this bad. They could have started the process, they could have done some to make the damage less intense, but this was going to be a bad fire for reasons beyond any living individuals' control.<br /> <br /> IMO, people looking for heads to roll are wasting their time. Trying to pin the blame on a small group of individuals and seeing them lose their jobs doesn't fix all of the issues that will make the next round of bad fire so bad. Those issues are still going to be there, waiting for the right winds, and humidity, and increased winter heat levels, and improperly managed brush overgrowth, and so on until people focus on fixing all of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T12:02:53-08:00","id":1547698,"title":"","content":"The winds were 100mph; you can't fight a fire with winds at that speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T01:40:05-08:00","id":1547710,"title":"","content":"It'll sound cold, but I just don't care anymore. The people screaming and whining for someone's head to roll after this latest batch of wildfires will eventually get themselves burned right out of the population, and we really will not miss them. Just like the ones who complain about any earthquakes, but move to an earthquake prone state. Or those who cry about floods washing their homes and lives away, but move to a flood plain. When they finally complain away anyone who could do anything about the problem, they'll be left with the problem itself wiping them out and nobody to give a damn. Hearing that they voted/legislated away any possible preemptive countermeasures just removes the last shred of sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T11:45:06-08:00","id":1547716,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that the vast majority of people living in the path of natural disasters do not have the kind of agency you're ascribing. I get caring is hard, but there's no magical place on the planet to just move to where there's work, affordable living, and no natural disasters to worry about. People are also interconnected, that's why caring matters. That's why we need some level of government to let communities manage the infrastructure necessary to make living somewhere comfortable; it's not a job that can be done on an individual basis.<br /> <br /> You bring up earthquakes... but that's a perfect example of what happens when people keep caring and aim their efforts in the right way: In the past 25 years ten people have died in earthquakes in California. The last major earthquake before that killed 57 people in one quake. California's fault lines are still active, powerful quakes that do lots of damage happen regularly... but we don't hear about them because after a bunch of bad ones in the 90s, California majorly revamped building codes and that's lead to more and more quake resiliency over time. California buildings are now more like crumple zones in cars: there's still plenty of damaged structure to clean up and repair after a big quake, but people are protected. Being worried about earthquakes in California (as long as nobody does something stupid like lessen the building code restrictions because earthquakes don't kill as many people as they used to) is kinda silly because as far as natural disasters go... things are pretty well in hand.<br /> <br /> Fires are harder, because there's less of a &quot;one-size-fits-all&quot; solution. You need lots of people, doing different things, in different places, to not just protect themselves, but also make sure fires are more easily contained so that they don't jump to other places. Breaks in that chain negatively impact everyone, not just the people failing to do their part. Your town can do all the fire prep, and do it right, and strong enough Santa Ana winds will make it all pointless if the next town over didn't. The people that didn't most certainly need to shut up and sit down when discussions of accountability and rebuilding with better infrastructure take place, but they're not a majority of people impacted by all this either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T05:56:19-08:00","id":1547734,"title":"","content":"I feel like venting about people with a pseudo-worldweary affect who express views verging on eugenics as a response to bad things happening in the world, in a way that only really ends up revealing that they don't know what they're talking about but feel inordinately clever for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T10:00:09-08:00","id":1547911,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking about the US executive order concerning gender identity, the implications it has for trans and NB people I know personally and those people I know by reputation and millions of them whom I don't know but whose basic stories are easily picked up on, and I just want to scream.<br /> <br /> It's just such a horrifying thing to happen to people whom you know deserve better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T04:45:55-08:00","id":1547928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1547911#post1547911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep thinking about the US executive order concerning gender identity, the implications it has for trans and NB people I know personally and those people I know by reputation and millions of them whom I don't know but whose basic stories are easily picked up on, and I just want to scream.<br /> <br /> It's just such a horrifying thing to happen to people whom you know deserve better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ain't happy about that executive order either, but I'm going to do my best to keep living my life as best I can. I don't like that any government documents will now have to refer to me by my birth name and my biological sex, but I'll do my best to manage. I have a good support system, a will that will ensure that when I die (and I hope that is many years from now) that I will be buried and honored as the man I truly am, and both my husband and my Dad have my back and respect my gender identity, and I am thankful for those blessings in my life.<br /> <br /> I do feel very bad for a lot of my trans brothers and sisters who don't have any good support system at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T16:20:10-08:00","id":1548040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1547928#post1547928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ain't happy about that executive order either, but I'm going to do my best to keep living my life as best I can. I don't like that any government documents will now have to refer to me by my birth name and my biological sex, but I'll do my best to manage. I have a good support system, a will that will ensure that when I die (and I hope that is many years from now) that I will be buried and honored as the man I truly am, and both my husband and my Dad have my back and respect my gender identity, and I am thankful for those blessings in my life.<br /> <br /> I do feel very bad for a lot of my trans brothers and sisters who don't have any good support system at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty pissed about it too. I have several trans friends and I'm so upset for them. All I can do right is try my best to support them in any way I can, but this whole thing is crazy and it's very upsetting that this is happening.<br /> <br /> Hell, every day it seems I hear about another awful executive order... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T12:35:40-08:00","id":1548114,"title":"","content":"Not looking forward to going out in -30 weather for the next few days or the upcoming tarrifs that will be happening today and seeing prices go up and or possible job losses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-03-2025, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T18:49:17-08:00","id":1548125,"title":"","content":"The whole tariff thing that frustrates me so much is I haven't seen a single serious case for how they'll help... anybody. The global economy is in a messy place. Fixing it is going to have costs. Someone, somewhere, it going to shoulder the burdens of those costs.<br /> <br /> I could stomach tariffs even if I have my issues with them if, despite short term pain, there was some idea of how it helps in the long run. Even the most pro-tariff serious economists seem to think what's already been put in place is bad, and the whole idea of a broad tariff strategy is high risk/high reward in the best of circumstances... and we're not going in with the best of circumstances as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T18:55:01-08:00","id":1548126,"title":"","content":"The cynic in me says that the tariffs will benefit the very wealthy, but it won't help working people like you and me as it's hard to make ends meet at the best of times and this is another burden that will hurt us","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T00:06:40-08:00","id":1548133,"title":"","content":"It doesn't even help the wealthy. It might in the short term, and we know how much current economics has corporations obsessed with the quarterly bottom-line no matter what the long term consequences; since they can easily shift the costs onto other people. The whole reason tariffs and excise taxes went from the backbone of international commerce to a tool of diplomatic coercion is because when there's an economic collapse (and there's always going to be another one under basic capitalism) even the wealthy can't avoid it.<br /> <br /> The rich can only escape the eventual bust of a tariff scheme if the tariffs are targeted more specifically: the more practical domestic production is, the easier it is for them to push off the costs.<br /> <br /> For example, a 20% tariff on coffee imports would pretty much bankrupt huge swathes of the service industry. The US consumes 300 times more coffee that we're capable of producing (since the only state that can grow coffee at scale is Hawaii there isn't much room for expansion). Coffee would get prohibitively expensive for average folk, and there's no &quot;bail out&quot; that's possible because there simply isn't the domestic supply. Billions in the markets would vanish, and companies wouldn't even have the money to pay out the golden parachutes to their C-suite idiots. <br /> <br /> Across the board tariffs means you can't even contain it to specific industries either. Even industries that would remain viable without lots of imports ballooning costs suffer because the investor class will skew shit and screw it all up. A rush on corn futures as investors dump import reliant items like my coffee example isn't sustainable either.<br /> <br /> Like... we know what happens with this. The Smoot-Hawley Act with tried to use tariffs to end the Great Depression only made it so much worse. It didn't equalize things or anything that drastic, but huge amounts of the wealthy class's worth were wiped out in just a few years once the retaliatory tariffs started kicking in. There's history that shows what happens in response to this stuff. It's just bad for everyone.<br /> <br /> The only possible benefit this has is to someone with power over tariffs and a desire to be perceived as &quot;strong&quot; by being a geopolitical economic bully. And even trying to make yourself feel good by bullying people around isn't exactly some perpetual happiness machine either.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T08:18:41-08:00","id":1548143,"title":"","content":"It's honestly not complicated. Trump just likes tariffs, it's that simple. He doesn't need to go ask Congress for anything. He doesn't need to get anyone's permission. He doesn't need to wait for people to do investigations. He doesn't need to work with anyone. He can just wake up and say, &quot;25% tariffs on Lichtenstein!&quot; and that's that. Tariffs are something that he has full and absolute power over and there's no check or balance on it. That's why they're his favorite tool in the Presidential toolbox. Does he care if tariffs work or if they hurt people? No, it doesn't matter. He likes using them and believes using them makes him look strong and powerful, that's it. There's no economic foundation at all, and it's kind of a waste of time looking for one. When it comes to Trump's tariffs, it's just pure ego.<br /> <br /> What people should really be worried about is Trump deciding to take military action against Canada or Greenland. People in his peripheral circle (who are friends with the people he talk with) are saying that Trump's talk about wanting Canada/Greenland and being willing to use military force should absolutely be taken at face value. Apparently he's been talking with Putin, and believes that territorial acquisition is necessary to cement his place in history alongside Washington and Lincoln. If he can take territory peacefully, he'll do it. But if he needs the military, that's definitely on the table. I seriously won't be surprised if everyone wakes up some morning and have see troops occupying Greenland, or Canada or both.<br /> <br /> This also plays into the Project 2025 playbook - have some major issue come up that causing people to protest, then declare martial law, suspend civil rights, suspend further elections and maintain power perpetually. We've seen the exact same scenario play out in other countries that fell from being democracies into dictatorships I'm betting that's how some people are planning for them to play out here.<br /> <br /> I hope everyone has a their own personal Rubicon, where when it gets crossed, they'll do what they can to take power back. As we've seen numerous times throughout history, if people aren't willing to fight for their political power, they're not going to keep it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T13:24:14-08:00","id":1548152,"title":"","content":"I hope that we can end the tarrifs as it doesn't help anyone in the long run, but I don't think that it will happen during the Trump presidency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T14:27:01-08:00","id":1548155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1548143#post1548143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope everyone has a their own personal Rubicon, where when it gets crossed, they'll do what they can to take power back. As we've seen numerous times throughout history, if people aren't willing to fight for their political power, they're not going to keep it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, we're approaching a second &quot;Rubicon&quot; decision point where people need to decide if they even want to be in North America until everything has played out. Something that's a lot more work that people are going to realize until it's too late if it gets to that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T10:45:34-08:00","id":1548191,"title":"","content":"Does anyone really want to leave the United States at all Heavy Arms? I hear it said many times but nothing really comes of it despite the issues of whatever leadership is in power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T11:13:43-08:00","id":1548193,"title":"","content":"I know multiple people (including family members) that have either moved to other countries either as ex-pats or on the path to full naturalization. So yeah, it happens.<br /> <br /> The problem is most people that want to leave don't have options. It's expensive and emotionally taxing to uproot yourself and possibly family even to move to a much lower cost of living country. Most countries have very strict immigration laws as well. One of my in-laws lived abroad for two years hoping to get accepted for a naturalization program but in the end was rejected and had to come back to the US ... basically leaving her dead broke and relying on family support for years getting back on her feet here.<br /> <br /> That's the thing with a lot of people just talking big about it online. They, broadly, have not done their research. They don't have their papers in order. They don't know which countries are actively seeking immigrants and (crucially) in what fields. Unless things get so bad that other countries start accepting US citizens as refugees, it takes months or even years just to have everything in order to even try to go somewhere else. Hence most online chatter about it as all talk. It's people that think moving to Canada is the same as moving from New Jersey to New York. <br /> <br /> I have the dubious privilege of being from a family of all refugees. All of my grandparents (either as adults or as children) fled conflicts - sometimes enduring some severe hardships - to get to the US. I've heard all of their stories about what it took. Since I was eighteen I've been sure to have what I need to get out of the US just in case. If I finally decide it's time to pull out one of those plans, something else I know is that means I'm not announcing it online before I do. I'll talk about it after my long term residency is validated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T11:30:10-08:00","id":1548194,"title":"","content":"The online people can be the worst when they meltdowns when things don't go their way. They act like children who have adult bodies and it's embarrassing to say the least.<br /> <br /> Just getting a passport to visit the United States was hard and making sure I had enough money and how long I wanted to stay and all the red tape to cut through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-04-2025, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T22:49:00-08:00","id":1548248,"title":"","content":"At least the Tarrifs are being kicked down the road for another month, but it still likely to happen and already we are pulling out American beer \ud83c\udf7a out the liquor stores in Canada.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T10:20:22-08:00","id":1548336,"title":"","content":"Sylvester Stallone allegedly made a statement that he wouldn't be able to make Rambo today as it might be seen as problematic. It's been some time since I seen the first film but for the life of me I can't see what issues that this generation would have.<br /> <br /> Can someone please help me out here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T14:51:02-08:00","id":1548341,"title":"","content":"Stallone's using &quot;can't make X today,&quot; as a thought terminating cliche as far as I can tell. He made a Rambo movie in 2019. It was garbage. Without even taking inflation into account First Blood (the 1982 movie) made more at the box office, and cost less to make, than Rambo: Last Blood (the 2019 movie) did.<br /> <br /> Realistically speaking:<br /> <br /> 1) The Rambo franchise has been one-upping shitting on its own legacy since the first sequel. Each film has grown more and more detached from the deep and insightful commentary of the first film that turned it into a massive sleeper hit, and further into jingoistic violence-fests where Rambo has accepted that he's nothing more than a killing machine so he'll keep murdering whoever the most convenient &quot;bad people&quot; are until he finally dies. They also keep adding women into Rambo's life only for them to die because the man hadn't been through enough trauma apparently.<br /> <br /> 2) Vietnam is history. The war might still be part of living memory, but most people alive today were born after it ended (since that was 50 years ago and all). First Blood was hugely influential in opening up audiences and Hollywood to cinema that was far more critical of how American society treats veterans returning from war. It's not a big genre for understandable reasons, but it stays relevant by today's movies discussing more recent conflicts. People make movies about the US wars in Afghanistan and Iraq now.<br /> <br /> 3) One of the best reasons First Blood wouldn't have the same impact now? People listened to the movie! It's no longer taboo to discuss PTSD, veteran homelessness, or suicide rates. We haven't solved these issues, but we're still massively farther along towards making sure vets get the help they need coming back from war than we were 50 years ago. A film who's legacy involves sparking a national conversation in the 80s about the silence suffering of people returning from war doesn't have the same point in the 2020s after that conversation led to most people agreeing that &quot;Yeah, that's bullshit, we should take care of these people properly.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's really simple. Compare the Rocky franchise to the Rambo franchise. The Rocky movies are now the Creed movies as Rocky helps Adonis Creed through his rise in the boxing world. New stories, with new characters, but still feeling like part of a continuation of the original thematically; not just because Stallone came back as Rocky. The Rambo movies are still the Rambo movies. John Rambo is 77 years old, and still a one-man army mowing down countless mooks while managing to shrug off injuries that should give healthy 20 year olds permanent disabilities. Rambo III is literally a movie about Rambo helping the Afghanis fight against the Russians, but the 2008 and 2019 films just ignore that going on completely (I don't know about most people, but if you wanted Rambo to be relevant now, the futility of war from his perspective seeing US military causalities from the War on Terror rack up seemed like a pretty obvious narrative to explore).<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> As an ethical matter rather than an artistic (or corporate financial one), Stallone also just shouldn't be making any movies until he steps down from the position he's accepted from the current administration. As someone that's accepted a political appointment with the stated goal of advocating for the White House's cultural priorities to become the focus on Hollywood output, any film he works on since taking the position should be inherently tainted as propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T18:10:07-08:00","id":1548346,"title":"","content":"Possibly my favorite, albeit equally most disappointing, example of &quot;Can't Make X is Nonsense&quot; is Mel Brooks bought into and spouted the hype that he couldn't make a movie today....and then proceeded to make History of the World Part 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T19:51:38-08:00","id":1548350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1548346#post1548346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly my favorite, albeit equally most disappointing, example of &quot;Can't Make X is Nonsense&quot; is Mel Brooks bought into and spouted the hype that he couldn't make a movie today....and then proceeded to make History of the World Part 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did he end up saying that? I recall an interview where he said he could probably make some movies, like Young Frankenstein, but that he wouldn't be able to make Blazing Saddles today and would have been canceled if he'd tried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T21:57:17-08:00","id":1548351,"title":"","content":"Blazing Saddles would probably offend people today as it is very politically incorrect by today's standards.<br /> <br /> On a side note it's does get little sad when you see action heroes you loved back in the day and are old enough to collect pensions still trying to pretend that they can still do things that they could do when they were younger. Stallone got hurt trying to do some of his own stunts in the first Expendables movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-10-2025, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T06:05:23-08:00","id":1548357,"title":"","content":"Blazing Saddles almost always comes up on this, and for some reason people (apparently even Mel Brooks?) forget that the original barely got made in the first place. They had to get the <i>president of Warner Bros.</i> at the time to step in just to let them show the movie in three theaters as a premiere before the studio execs would sign off on a full release. While wildly successful, it was also extremely controversial back in the 70s too. People seem to forget that Mel Brooks was considered to be a provocateur that made transgressive comedy that was meant to be boundary pushing and offensive.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, comedy, like all art, provides successful artists with two choices: keep doing the same thing that made you successful until you're pandering to a stale shrinking crowd that's paying you for nostalgia instead of being creative, or you need to come up with new material that adapts with the times so you connect to audiences as their tastes and expectations change. A rare few can juggle both for awhile, but most end up chasing one or the other eventually.<br /> <br /> Also... Mel Brooks is in his late 90s... even if he made something so bad he got cancelled... he finally fully retires in time to see 100? What's there to be scared of when it comes to potentially career ending risks when you've outlived most people anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T08:58:18-08:00","id":1548361,"title":"","content":"I remember some of the trouble Mel Brooks had with making Blazing Saddles as they couldn't get his humor and he wanted to cast some people in the film and he couldn't.<br /> <br /> He wanted the late Richard Pryor to play the lead but the studio said no because of how bad the comedian drug and alcohol problems were becoming and I think he wanted John Wayne be in it. However the Duke turned it down saying that he did not think his fans would buy him in a comedic film at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T09:01:39-08:00","id":1548362,"title":"","content":"I remember watching the later Rambo films and how it did move away from a struggling vet trying to reconnect with society to a one man army that could take on anyone without taking any real injuries. The eighties action films were a fun but strange time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T09:16:36-08:00","id":1548364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1548351#post1548351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blazing Saddles would probably offend people today as it is very politically incorrect by today's standards.</div> </div> </div> </div>People do, in fact, still make fun of racists.<br /> <br /> Like, people always say this as though they somehow misremember Blazing Saddles as a movie that has an unflattering depiction of black people, when arguably its framing of them and direction of the acting (including the depiction of how somebody might try to utilise prejudicial attitudes towards them for their own ends, often for their safety) is a lot more nuanced and sophisticated than many other films of its day. Other films would play straight what Bart very explicitly is using as a means to harness white people's prejudices about him against them.<br /> <br /> Unless it's also some comment of &quot;you couldn't make a film where people are constantly dropping racial slurs&quot;, which is somewhere between &quot;no&quot; and &quot;errr... good?&quot;<br /> <br /> It gets folded into a whole narrative of &quot;progressives are so jumpy and sensitive that they have no critical thinking and want everything to be sanitized&quot;, which is not inaccurate to some people but is mostly just deployed to be reductive of and caricature the whole thing to discredit any sense of critical evaluation at all. A great many, if not most such people, can process authentic depictions of terrible people in artistic contexts that condemn them.<br /> <br /> (And every now and then you get somebody where it's hard not to think that their experience of Blazing Saddles is finding it funny for racists to go around fully mask off, that kind of humour that is like &quot;outrageous... it do be like that, though&quot;.) <br /> <br /> I'd be a bit disappointed in Mel Brooks were it not for the fact that the younger version of him comes off a lot more as though he'd actually get it, because Blazing Saddles is a film he actually made with a great deal of care and sensitivity for not trying to make jokes about things that would actually be over the line (like outright lynching).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T12:05:17-08:00","id":1548372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1548351#post1548351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blazing Saddles would probably offend people today as it is very politically incorrect by today's standards.</div> </div> </div> </div>People have been saying this enough, in volume, in my lifetime that it becomes laughable on it's face, even if movies like Django: Unchained, BlacKKKlansman, Jojo Rabbit, Sorry to Bother You, and more didn't prove it false on it's face.<br /> <br /> Also, most of the people saying it tend to be the people who think being able to get away with saying the n-word is the main joke, as opposed to the actual main joke being that the people saying the n-word are morons, but that's a little off-topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-10-2025, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T15:57:48-08:00","id":1548377,"title":"","content":"Like, the whole thing of &quot;you couldn't make Blazing Saddles today, people would be offended&quot;...<br /> <br /> Are people under the impression that the word was inoffensive in the 70s? Like, even to actual racists, it was the kind of thing that would have been considered crass to use in a lot of contexts and media, to be open and explicit about it. That's why you never have anybody using it in Westerns (wildly popular in the preceding decades), despite those depicting a time period in which it actually would have been a fairly common and casual thing to use in everyday conversation about black people.<br /> <br /> <i>Which is what the film is lampooning!!! It's making fun of the fact that Westerns present a sanitized version of the past for the benefit of people who otherwise have such racism as a basic part of their lives and draw a sense of heritage from the places and periods depicted! It intended to offend the audience that would be uncomfortable with being frankly confronted with that part of their own worldview and history!</i><br /> <br /> You wouldn't make Blazing Saddles today because a lot of the context has changed, so you'd need to find a new milieu along which to hold that kind of mirror up to society.<br /> <br /> (And then that film would not get made not because mean progressives would excoriate it, but because the way film studios have consolidated under late capitalism express a kind of bland uniformity in the films they're generally willing to put out.)<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about all of this, and I really need to see if I can get myself DVDs of A Black Lady Sketch Show or something. Everything I manage to get about that show from Youtube makes it clear that it's so good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T16:22:18-08:00","id":1548379,"title":"","content":"I loved many of the movies you mentioned and I remembered how funny it was that Sheriff Bart in Blazing Saddles outwitted the townsfolk who wanted to shoot him by pulling a gun on himself and took himself hostage and couldn't believe that it worked.<br /> <br /> Mel Brooks was mocking their intelligence and the villian in the film Hedley Lamar wasn't even racist bin general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T19:39:12-08:00","id":1548417,"title":"","content":"Politics; I'm tried of everyone talkin' about politics around me and they don't shut up about it; they just go on and on. Can't they go back to ranting on how horrible Disney's Star Wars shows are? At least I like Star Wars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T22:22:13-08:00","id":1548421,"title":"","content":"I get slightly annoyed by the idea that popular culture villians are misunderstood heroes and forgot why these people are not heroes.<br /> <br /> Ie Magneto is not to a hero at all, he has understandable and sympathetic reasons for his actions, but in the end he is still a bad guy who serves as a cautionary tale about what happens when one fights monsters and becomes one himself.<br /> <br /> Or Dr. Doom despite having a code of honor and a sense of nobel obligation to his subjects is driven by petty jealousy against the fact that Reed Richards is slightly smarter and caught the error in Victor Von Doom's calculations and Dr. Doom would love to show the world that he is smarter and let's not forget that life under Doom wouldn't be pleasant as we would have no real rights and would sacrifice everything for God like powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T01:01:10-08:00","id":1548423,"title":"","content":"The problem is that fictional characters are whatever the authors want them to be. Long running characters are especially prone to seeing big shifts in their narrative roles as stories progress.<br /> <br /> Also, hero and villain are concepts extremely tied to who's perspective you're seeing events from. The people of Latveria are generally presented as seeing Dr. Doom as a hero because, to them, despite some character flaws, he overthrew an utter tyrant and is a reasonable and generous ruler for an absolute monarch. That's to Doom's personal power his tiny poor country has a quality of life (save for personal liberties like privacy) that rival most advanced nations. From the perspective of a Latverian trying to claim the Reed Richards is a hero despite his own extensive character flaws isn't an easy sell. Has Richards used his amazing intellect to do anything but stroke his own ego and play hero when it suits him? Mr. Fantastic isn't exactly proving that the freedoms of liberal democracy are so great compared to the whims of a dictator when Richards can't invent his way into free zero pollution energy for the masses, end homelessness, come up with cheap and easy ways to repair aging infrastructure, etc. And he can team up with Tony Stark, Hank Pym, and a slew of other hero geniuses to solve all those problems but... doesn't.<br /> <br /> Doom is the villain though, because we're on the other side.<br /> <br /> Magneto is even more complicated because the allegory of the X-Men as a stand in for the struggle of minorities to be accepted means it needs to reflect the reality of the lives of minorities. Lots of minorities are looking around and saying, &quot;Magneto was right.&quot; Which is to say, people like Malcolm X were right: the ballot or the bullet. If the oppressors in our society refuse to all people as equals in reality not just aspirations (&quot;the ballot&quot;), then then only moral choice for the oppressed is resistance (&quot;the bullet&quot;). It's the oppressors' choice. And Magneto said all along, that the oppressors are never willingly going to share the ballot. Hard to make a case he was wrong right now.<br /> <br /> When you look at real people, real complicated, conflicted people, nobody's really a &quot;hero&quot; or a &quot;villain.&quot; There's people doing the best they can, and people doing the worst they can, and a lot of people somewhere in the middle. When George III made it clear he wasn't going to give the ballot to the American colonists, the took him up on the bullet. There was a violent revolution. The colonists won. And the story of history calls them heroes for a number of reasons. You can look across the world to other revolutionary movements fighting their governments who's labels aren't going to be heroes for lots of reasons that has nothing to do with the righteousness of their cause, or even the ethics of how they fought it.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, &quot;Magneto was right&quot; didn't come from fans. It came from the comics first. No matter how hard Charles and his students fought to prove coexistence was possible, some anti-mutant movement pushed back even harder and with far less effort swayed public opinion their way. It came about because the history of the Marvel universe proved him right; which forces a reexamination of his methods and how justified they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T15:20:27-08:00","id":1548452,"title":"","content":"To be fair Igazu. There's always been some level of politics in entertainment, but I go with the notion that previous writers had a good amount of life experiences to draw upon and how nothing is simple and that people don't like the hard sell approach that some of today's writers like to use.<br /> <br /> In regards to Disney Star Wars, outside of Rogue One it has been very lackluster with bad storytelling, one dimensional characters and in some cases really bad fight scenes.<br /> <br /> The Force Awakens was a poor retread of New Hope and the only character with any potential was Finn and we saw him become a sidekick in the later films and Kylo Ren started off okay but quickly we saw in the Force Awakens that he comes across as child with temper tantrums.<br /> <br /> If you're going to follow in the foot steps of Darth Vader, you better learn some self control as I don't think anyone really feared or respected him that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T15:31:58-08:00","id":1548454,"title":"","content":"I'd rather talk about politics in entertainment, than have to hear hours of political rants. <br /> <br /> Oh, and Blazing Saddles, um, my grandfather, who was in the navy in WW2, walked out of the theater within ten-minutes. I, however, think it's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T20:37:58-08:00","id":1548458,"title":"","content":"I think one way to put it might be that there's a difference between having a reasonable discussion about the politics espoused in a creative work (identifying what they are, do they fit the narrative, are they really supported by the story, etc.) than people using creative works as a springboard to talk about someone's personal political pet peeves (&quot;Here's a two hour video essay on how five minutes of movie X proves me right about all of my political stances&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T20:38:52-08:00","id":1548459,"title":"","content":"I hope that this is just an honest editing mistake from a DCU fan website where when a picture of the many people who played Superman at the most recent con and actor Dean Cain seemed to have his image cut out and social media personalities like Ryan Kinel, Clownfish TV and others were framing this as politically motivated as Mr. Cain is a outspoken conservative.<br /> <br /> I'm just hoping that it was an website user that is inexperienced at uploading photos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T20:40:11-08:00","id":1548460,"title":"","content":"That is a fair statement Heavy Arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T11:56:54-08:00","id":1548916,"title":"","content":"Please save us from the armchair conspiracy theorists. When there is breaking news that is happening in real time, there is always going to be mistakes made that will be corrected in later editions.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"