plan could be to put tariffs up, crash the market, rich people buy up stock, then reverse the tariffs so prices go back up. It's just a rug pull on a massive scale. But then again seeing Canada and Mexico start slapping tariffs on US products may piss him off and make him keep tightening tariffs. You can't really predict what Trump will do, in fact I don't think Trump usually knows what he's going to do from one day to the next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-05T10:49:54-08:00","id":1548985,"title":"","content":"I saw that AnubisXy and that provides some hope. On a different track, we had the distinct &quot;pleasure&quot; of a white supremacy group protests outside of my local Tim Hortons and a government office that helps new Canadians settle in our country/community.<br /> <br /> A small group of people wearing masks holding signs saying white lives matter and deport them all. What a local disgrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T15:58:19-08:00","id":1549058,"title":"","content":"We at least got an update on happened to Gene Hackman and his wife Besty sudden tragic deaths. Nothing nefarious as some social media trolls like to claim. Sounds like Besty had been very ill with a disease and died from it. With his primary caregiver dead Gene Hackman passed away as he was quite frail and in poor health.<br /> <br /> But sadly we will still get the conspiracy theorists coming up with alternative &quot;facts&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-08T05:01:49-08:00","id":1549073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1549058#post1549058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We at least got an update on happened to Gene Hackman and his wife Besty sudden tragic deaths. Nothing nefarious as some social media trolls like to claim. Sounds like Besty had been very ill with a disease and died from it. With his primary caregiver dead Gene Hackman passed away as he was quite frail and in poor health.<br /> <br /> But sadly we will still get the conspiracy theorists coming up with alternative &quot;facts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard about that yesterday. It's really scary and sad... He probably had no idea what was even happening. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yea, the conspiracy theorists just don't know when to stop.. ugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-10T17:00:35-07:00","id":1549141,"title":"","content":"Yes there was talk that Gene Hackman was suffering from dementia, but I don't know if this was confirmed as I recall his one daughter said that the last time they talked that he was still mentally sharp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-10T17:38:44-07:00","id":1549144,"title":"","content":"Hopefully it's just grief talking and it'll be resolved calmly soon, but the ME said Hackman had clinical signs of Alzheimer's, but the daughter was adamant that wasn't the case. It's a very emotional thing to have publicized to the world, so I can appreciate the family not liking that just being revealed; even if it explains a lot in the chain of events that seems to have happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T11:05:19-07:00","id":1549194,"title":"","content":"I certainly can understand that the Hackman family didn't want the possibility of Gene Hackman having dementia being released in such a manner. I believe that the late Sean Connery also suffered from it in his later years and we only knew about it because the family disclosed it after his passing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T22:30:22-07:00","id":1549226,"title":"","content":"Feeling somewhat dismayed by how angry or unhinged some social media personalities can be and I recently saw some comic book reviewer called something Vengeance and I wonder if he is really a happy person at all and is jealous of professionals who have lived their dreams and he is stuck at being a loud mouth on YouTube.<br /> <br /> For instance said YouTubers went on a rant about Alan Moore and how he doesn't like like the man's politics, and I'm thinking Alan Moore has always injected his politics into his stories in one form or another and and the end of the day is still going to be remembered as a good storyteller and you won't be remembered at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T11:34:55-07:00","id":1549246,"title":"","content":"I can't believe that writer Peter David is very ill and needs medical help. He was one of my favorite writers growing up in the 1990's. I remembered his run on The Incredible Hulk and Spider Man 2099 and his Star Trek novels and amusingly enough he had a science fiction series called PSI-Man that he wrote under the name of David Peters that was my first introduction to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-13-2025, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T12:17:43-07:00","id":1549252,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it sucks to hear that PAD is ill again, though given his first major stroke that also required community support to raise funds for happened in 2012, I guess I feel a bit less shock at his declining health now (as it seems like he's had multiple strokes in the past few months on top of other issues). I don't want to turn this into a bigger discussion of medical access, but he endured his life savings being completely destroyed by his first stroke (he couldn't see properly or use one of his arms for months, though he did regain most of his faculties and he eventually got back to creating), and now he's facing that shit show all over again is a travesty beyond the personal hardship for him and is family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T13:05:50-07:00","id":1549255,"title":"","content":"My home having been without a kitchen and floors coming up on two weeks now is starting to grate on me a bit. It's not just about how the microwaved food is often of lower quality, it's the loss of the whole compelling experience of cooking, and having a little spot to be active in.<br /> <br /> At least the new kitchen is coming sooner rather than later, and should prove to provide all of the old benefits and more.<br /> <br /> Not sure when the fact that the water supply has been cut off somehow will be so resolved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T15:57:25-07:00","id":1549272,"title":"","content":"That is what makes it worse that Peter David is in such dire straits because of medical costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T16:12:47-07:00","id":1549273,"title":"","content":"Found out the near-vacant lot I was thinking of buying, well, the only standing structure left, the garage, didn't have a shower or bathroom in it like most houses in the area. I could have lived out of it if it did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-19T11:28:06-07:00","id":1549445,"title":"","content":"It is so fucking weird sometimes seeing the way the intersection between accessibility to prominent people's opinions through social media and fandom defensiveness can make people fixated on really incidental things.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm just after watching a video by a Youtuber who produces recaps and reviews of horror video games concerned with the original Silent Hill. And the comment section has quite a lot of people who are unaccountably salty over the fact that she said she didn't want to do a video about the remake of Silent Hill 2.<br /> <br /> People liking the game is fine, but I cannot imagine why folks would be such aggressive evangelists for it.<br /> <br /> I find the most bizarre when they're like &quot;oh, you're just cynically exploiting the fact that it ended up being a big success&quot;. And like... the mental convolutions to not understand how something like that can make the Silent Hill franchise topical enough to be an opportune time to bring it up (such as, say, for an audience of people whose interest in it is brought back up or the newly introduced who want to learn more about its past).<br /> <br /> It's bizarre at times to see how so many people can be so hostile towards something as mild as benign disinterest.<br /> <br /> I know somebody who once said over people liking a movie without being mindful of its flaws (and hostile towards people pointing them out) that it doesn't mean they love the movie better, just that they love it sadder. I wonder what the evaluation should be of people who love a thing and become aggressive towards people saying they're not interested in it.<br /> <br /> (I say this while reflecting on times in my own past when my behaviour has been similar, if not outright the same)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T20:03:40-07:00","id":1549763,"title":"","content":"So, I know this is pushing the lines on politics given why it's happening... but the ridiculousness of it hopefully transcends concerns about that:<br /> <br /> The US government is officially putting tariffs on penguins. No on buying and selling penguins. On multiple populations of penguins that my government claims are ripping us off in regards to international trade; as they are the only permanent terrestrial residents of a number of island &quot;countries&quot; (they're territories claimed by Australia but aren't just being hit with the Australian tariffs) which made the list of countries getting hit with the new economic policy.<br /> <br /> If this was from yesterday, it could have been one hell of an April Fool's joke but... no... this is from today and appears to be 100% real. <br /> <br /> I'm also going to point out that the last time a human government went to war with terrestrial birds in Australian territory, the birds won.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T20:46:39-07:00","id":1549765,"title":"","content":"I'm almost feeling sorry for Disney as they seem to either have flops or getting sued, but then I remembered that much of it is self inflicted and they were told that getting very political would be harmful to the bottom line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T12:10:21-07:00","id":1549780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1549765#post1549765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm almost feeling sorry for Disney as they seem to either have flops or getting sued, but then I remembered that much of it is self inflicted and they were told that getting very political would be harmful to the bottom line.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've been very political before. Hell, they've even made US propoganda before. It's worked well for them prior, and of course this is disregarding the fact that everything is political.<br /> <br /> The main problem of Disney's live action* remakes (I assume that's what this is about) is, in a nutshell, it's blatantly hollow. THe movies themselves have no purpose beyond using nostalgia to make money, which is already a uphill battle because adapting a cartoon to live-action tends to mean you have to work extra hard to match what the original is doing, and quite frequently it can't. The &quot;critical self-reflection&quot; they engage in, this &quot;progressive relook&quot; at their properties is about all they can do to warrant the existence of their remakes. It doesn't work, though, because it very frequently tries to brand safe in it's progressiveness and therefore cannot really take it's own properties to task, so either they address problems with all the strength of wet spaghetti, or they address problems that weren't actually problems to begin-and in both cases, their lack of investment in their progressive attempts means that they tend to resolve their &quot;issues&quot; with non-sequitors that ultimately have nothing to do with the movie, or even really the issues. The results are movies that aren't as animated in their presentation and is directionless with their story and characters.<br /> <br /> So the progressives in the audience aren't going to lap it up, and otherwise stack that on the list of reasons Disney is a gigantic banal evil, and of course there are going to be people who hate it just because it looks progressive(even if it isn't). The only audience left are the wine moms who want to feel secure that, in pursuing an obsession that ensures they will go to DIsney World as often as possible until they die, they have staked their childhood nostalgia in something that is actually a-okay to enjoy, which is like a third of their normal audience.<br /> <br /> So, yes, they've brought it on themselves, but let's not pretend Disney is a company that didn't make Der Fueher's Face or Mulan.<br /> <br /> *Obligatory &quot;live-action&quot; because someone's going to say something boring about the Lion Kings and I might as well head that off in the vain hope I won't actually have to hear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T13:36:49-07:00","id":1549781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1549763#post1549763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I know this is pushing the lines on politics given why it's happening... but the ridiculousness of it hopefully transcends concerns about that:<br /> <br /> The US government is officially putting tariffs on penguins. No on buying and selling penguins. On multiple populations of penguins that my government claims are ripping us off in regards to international trade; as they are the only permanent terrestrial residents of a number of island &quot;countries&quot; (they're territories claimed by Australia but aren't just being hit with the Australian tariffs) which made the list of countries getting hit with the new economic policy.<br /> <br /> If this was from yesterday, it could have been one hell of an April Fool's joke but... no... this is from today and appears to be 100% real.<br /> <br /> I'm also going to point out that the last time a human government went to war with terrestrial birds in Australian territory, the birds won.</div> </div> </div> </div>In all fairness, these allegedly uninhabited islands export $1.4 million in machinery and electronics to the U.S. per year, according to World Bank data (a presumably unbiased source). Not that much, but not a negligible amount. So while I don\u2019t agree with the tariffs in general, these particular tariffs are not completely ridiculous either.<br /> <br /> I Googled \u201ctariffs penguins\u201d and found an article in the Guardian (another unbiased source) discussing this issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T15:25:53-07:00","id":1549782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1549781#post1549781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all fairness, these allegedly uninhabited islands export $1.4 million in machinery and electronics to the U.S. per year, according to World Bank data (a presumably unbiased source). Not that much, but not a negligible amount. So while I don\u2019t agree with the tariffs in general, these particular tariffs are not completely ridiculous either.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK... so we're going to be serious on this instead of just enjoying the silly side of this stupidity...<br /> <br /> 1) These are not &quot;allegedly uninhabited&quot; islands. They are uninhabited. Humans go to (some) of them for a mixture of reasons, but no humans actually reside on them.<br /> <br /> 2) These are not countries, despite being labeled as such by the current US government. It is ridiculous to place a tariff on an uninhabited island claimed as territory of another country. There's already tariffs being put on Australia so there's no reason to not treat any exports from these islands as Australian goods for tariffs.<br /> <br /> 3) $1.4 million is categorically negligible in this context. The US gross imports in 2024 were $4.11 <u>trillion</u>. That means we're talking ~0.000035% of US imports. How can we call that a meaningful trade issue? Also 10% tariffs means the US wants to pocket $140,000.00 out of this trade (there's no permanent residents, there's nobody to make &quot;deals&quot; will for these tariffs to be leverage)... something that could be achieved and orders of magnitudes more in any number of revenue streams.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's completely ridiculous. Tariffs on Australia are questionable but broad tariffs is what the administration wants to do. Separate tariffs for these islands? Pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T17:55:42-07:00","id":1549786,"title":"","content":"Speaking of funny is that a film called Working Man that is a typical Jason Stratham movie is beating out the live action version of Snow White with a fraction of the budget. A decade or so ago this film would be direct to video product or just be a mid film before that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T18:38:18-07:00","id":1549794,"title":"","content":"I don't have anything, that's worth venting about (Should I vent about that?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T18:52:00-07:00","id":1549798,"title":"","content":"Eh... that's a fairly skewed look.<br /> <br /> First, Snow White has been out longer (movies always drop in the box office sales over time) so another movie coming up and starting to compete with it isn't exactly special. A Working Man has only had a better daily domestic box office half of the days its been out, and only one of those days ways on a weekend. Again, no shock there, an action movie aimed at adult audiences is going to do better with the after-work folks with free time on weekdays than a family orient film, which does better on Saturday and Sunday when it's easier to wrangle the kids to an activity and so on. Yes, Snow White speedy domestic decline is an embarrassment for Disney, but Snow White - despite all the negative criticism about if from pretty much all sides of American life - had a far better opening weekend.<br /> <br /> Second... maybe something to consider around &quot;does Disney know what they're doing?&quot; is to look at the international numbers. Snow White is still going to be a financial dud considering how much they spent on it, but when you look at the global box office instead of the domestic one... it's an entirely different set of numbers. The US is not the only country that buys movie tickets... and a lot of other countries don't have the same cultural norms around remakes (esp. the level of automatic nostalgia for the &quot;original*&quot; films that you tend to see in US audiences). It doesn't look like the international audiences are flocking to see it, but there also doesn't seem to be a serious impact from the America-centric controversy it's had. Meanwhile A Working Man isn't even in international distribution.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, hard data is that Snow White was mishandled. But at the same time, it's not nearly as bad as some random anecdote like comparing it to a US-only action movie makes it look either (also a decade ago we were still in the era of things like the Taken franchise where these sorts of action movies were making huge numbers at the box office and were not direct to video mid stuff). Disney has probably long since crunched the numbers to know how to offset a big domestic backlash with international sales in case the movie doesn't do well broadly.<br /> <br /> And, of course, never lose sight of the fact that those most responsible for the decisions that ensured Snow White was going to land with a thud (since Disney keeps plowing through with these &quot;live action&quot; remakes and they keep doing worse instead of audiences coming around to them), are rich and protected from the backlash, while lots of working folks trying to make ends meet are the ones that shoulder the burden of working on a box office bomb.<br /> <br /> * - Lets remember that Disney built a huge amount of its animated catalogue on public domain stories, including Snow White, it's not something the company created from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T19:51:59-07:00","id":1549800,"title":"","content":"I like public domain characters and stories and in a decade or so both Batman and Superman will enter the public domain and that will be strange that Warner Bros won't own them anymore. Unless they get some sort of legal ruling that prevents that from happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T04:09:51-07:00","id":1549811,"title":"","content":"I feel really depressed. Hope you guys are doing better than I am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T05:09:37-07:00","id":1549812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1549765#post1549765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they were told that getting very political would be harmful to the bottom line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm sure Disney executives devote a lot of their time to trawling through Critical Drinker videos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T11:09:33-07:00","id":1549818,"title":"","content":"Disney executives are to concerned about being investigated by the FCC illegal hiring practices then social media personalities like Clownfish TV, Ryan Kinel and the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T15:45:29-07:00","id":1549828,"title":"","content":"Huh, coulda sworn I did a whole little rant about the difficulties of when long running characters enter the public domain and how messy it is based on existing examples of long running media going from partially in the public domain to fully in the public domain.<br /> <br /> Anyway....<br /> <br /> If Disney is worried about the FCC investigating them for illegal hiring practices we have a lot bigger problems in our country than Disney being shitty megacorp... as the FCC has no legal authority to investigate hiring practices and the FCC is one of the better constructed federal agency to maintain its independence from the whims of changing administrations (the FCC is run by a board and the board members can't be legally fired just because a new president doesn't like them, presidents get to nominate new board members as vacancies open up). Them being co-opted/pressured into exceeding their statutory powers successfully and in a fashion that actually worries a corp like Disney would be really bad because of much larger issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-05T00:06:17-07:00","id":1549842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1549818#post1549818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disney executives are to concerned about being investigated by the FCC illegal hiring practices</div> </div> </div> </div>So, when you say &quot;they were told that getting very political would hurt their bottom line&quot;, you weren't talking about the online perspective that media featuring non-white or non-straight people wouldn't have a sufficient audience, but governments threatening to persecute them over exercising First Amendment rights?<br /> <br /> And you don't feel sorry for that because it is &quot;self inflicted&quot;?<br /> <br /> I find that an odd statement of perspective to make. Like if somebody said &quot;I would feel sorry for this journalist being imprisoned for openly reporting on endemic corruption, but hey, they were warned to keep their mouth shut and went ahead anyway, so they really did it to themselves&quot;.<br /> <br /> What of the spouse or parent who says &quot;look what you made me do&quot;?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T15:34:43-07:00","id":1549925,"title":"","content":"Is science fiction becoming a dying genre right now? I noticed at my local Chapters that the science fiction section is getting smaller and romantic fantasy is getting bigger. Is the same thing happening where your at or is it a isolated thing. Either way I can usually get my fix of the genre in the second hand stores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T15:57:55-07:00","id":1549930,"title":"","content":"It's not exactly an easy question to answer more broadly? Sure, looking at a few metrics, science fiction has dipped a bit from last year at this time but... lots of science fiction is still being published (from your phrasing I'm assuming we're talking about fiction books, not more broad media forms), so &quot;dying&quot; is clearly not happening either. Genres are naturally going to ebb and flow in popularity - both locally and on larger scales - so any short term trend is a very small thing to try to use for reading tea leaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T16:02:58-07:00","id":1549931,"title":"","content":"Yes I'm talking about the books themselves and I noticed that it's section was getting smaller in Chapters just like Westerns and horror books.<br /> <br /> Though with Westerns I'm not overly surprised as it seemed a more niche genre and you would see larger selections of that genre in second hand stores then in Chapters or similar big box book stores.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-07-2025, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T13:38:12-07:00","id":1549977,"title":"","content":"Geneticists successfully isolating and reviving small bits of traits from extinct animals is no the same as returning said animals to nature. It is most certainly not a replacement for conserving endangered and threatened species that are still capable of being saved because some tech bros are promising we'll have the tech to bring them all back in a decade or two (probably)... because they say so no matter what the science actually says.<br /> <br /> The potential for humanity to undo the massive damage to biodiversity we've caused over the last few hundred years is great. It's not an excuse to make it worse in the meantime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T21:56:36-07:00","id":1549993,"title":"","content":"I see why you wanted to put more of your response in the vent thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T22:30:29-07:00","id":1549996,"title":"","content":"Yea. This didn't &quot;de-extinct&quot; anything, it just made a heavily transgenic line of timber wolves that have a few genes that never flowed that way in real life. And on that note, I'll be really surprised if Colossal actually publishes the data they claim to have that supports the promo's story about wolves being most closely related to dire wolves out of extant modern canids (a paper from 2021 places non-Golden jackals, African wild dogs, and dholes as closer, in descending order).<br /> <br /> Edit: Apparently no one and nothing is closely related to dire wolves. Colossal, however, is still in error to say that <i>Canis lupus</i> is the closest living relative (because a non-golden jackal, African wild dog or a dhole is as equally good or bad a choice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 04-11-2025, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T07:14:12-07:00","id":1550037,"title":"","content":"Boy, I sure do love that the current American government was the type of thing to put a cartoon character in charge of public health, so that he can escalate language of contempt towards autistic people and how much their increasingly apparent existence is some kind of problem to be solved, and use that as a consequence to weaken vaccination in one of the biggest populations of the world.<br /> <br /> Seems like a pretty odd side effect of people voting with their wallets. Still, I can't fully bring myself to decry that motivation, given the outcome. You cannot deny, those wallets have never looked so slim and sexy. Those are some wallets that are going to be ready for swimsuit season given how much weight they're shedding, I can tell you that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"ran