div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/J4zZCuNAGRo?si=L9yEB9dCy3wdatDR\" data-code=\"J4zZCuNAGRo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/J4zZCuNAGRo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T23:54:11-07:00","id":1550257,"title":"","content":"David Faustino is a name I haven't heard in a long time. Though I do remember he did a spot on Robot Chicken and they both talked about how people would mix them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T00:01:24-07:00","id":1550259,"title":"","content":"Funny enough it was Master Ninja that introduced me to Lee Van Cliff in the first place then I saw his work in the old spaghetti westerns he did when he was younger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T12:55:12-07:00","id":1550320,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it's even possible for a good Fantastic 4 movie to be made? Judging from the trailers I saw thus far it doesn't seem promising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T14:45:04-07:00","id":1550323,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I didn't see anything in the trailer that strikes me as a bad sign. Everything worrying about the film is, well, stuff outside of the movie: Marvel saying this is not the MCU continuity but that the same cast will be showing up in the MCU in the next Avengers movie, people feeling that Pedro Pascal is over-exposed right now and that John Krasinski's casting in Dr. Strange 2 was wasted, etc.<br /> <br /> It looks like they're actually respecting the comics (helped by setting the story in the 60s so they can keep it retro in aesthetic instead of updated for 2025 tastes), Galactus looks like Galactus, we're not getting hit with yet another origin story for characters that have had their origin story done to death already, the Fantastic Four don't have secret identities and are famous people like they should be...<br /> <br /> I have no idea how it will be on release, nor do I know how people are going to like it in 2025, but if this was the trailer we got in 2015 instead of that dumpster fire, people would have been hyped as hell for a version that looked way more faithful to the comics than the 2005 one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T17:22:16-07:00","id":1550325,"title":"","content":"It seems Pedro Pascal is everything Dusney related","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T02:01:17-07:00","id":1550331,"title":"","content":"And a lot of is good? Even the stuff that isn't great doesn't really seem to be his fault. Wonder Woman 1984 was probably his worst project in recent years (and wasn't Disney!), but he did better than most actors could with what he had. Like I said, I get why people feel that he's over-exposed right now, but that's a pretty minimal thing to claim is a sign the movie is going to be bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-26T05:23:59-07:00","id":1550395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1550320#post1550320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it's even possible for a good Fantastic 4 movie to be made? Judging from the trailers I saw thus far it doesn't seem promising.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that new trailer looked pretty good!<br /> <br /> I'm hoping this will better than the last few Marvel movies. I mean, they weren't bad (I've seen waaay worse), but they weren't as good as they could be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1550323#post1550323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I didn't see anything in the trailer that strikes me as a bad sign. Everything worrying about the film is, well, stuff outside of the movie: Marvel saying this is not the MCU continuity but that the same cast will be showing up in the MCU in the next Avengers movie, people feeling that Pedro Pascal is over-exposed right now and that John Krasinski's casting in Dr. Strange 2 was wasted, etc.<br /> <br /> It looks like they're actually respecting the comics (helped by setting the story in the 60s so they can keep it retro in aesthetic instead of updated for 2025 tastes), Galactus looks like Galactus, we're not getting hit with yet another origin story for characters that have had their origin story done to death already, the Fantastic Four don't have secret identities and are famous people like they should be...<br /> <br /> I have no idea how it will be on release, nor do I know how people are going to like it in 2025, but if this was the trailer we got in 2015 instead of that dumpster fire, people would have been hyped as hell for a version that looked way more faithful to the comics than the 2005 one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you! I've often thought if they wanted to make a good F4 movie they need to stop trying to start in the present and it needs to be in the 60's. You have them time travel to the present or something as part of the story, but it needs to start in the 60's. And from the looks of the new trailer it looks like that's what they're doing. I'm excited to see it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-26T12:46:44-07:00","id":1550400,"title":"","content":"Esp. since, while WW 1984 proves its no panacea for the superhero genre, going into the past has been really successful for both Marvel and DC films already there's no reason to fear audiences are going to reject the idea the same way the studios were nervous about Captain America 1 and Wonder Woman 1 when it was more of an unknown of how well period pieces would mix with modern superheros.<br /> <br /> I've seen a lot of fan speculation about FF and the more plausible idea for how Marvel will move the team from the upcoming stand alone film into the main MCU... they're fairly reasonable based on what we know, and Marvel's general direction as a studio. But I also worry that fandoms have grown over analytical and wrapped up in trying to predict things that it's only making it harder to make a fun movie in a big franchise. I get the fun of trying to be right about what a story is going to do by pouring over all the hints and what not... but then the goal of that is to enjoy the vindication or the surprise if the studio managed to pull off something else. When you put studios in a place where movies get dragged online for either being too predictable (in an era where people will spend hours scouring each frame of a trailer for hints...), or fans get upset when their pet speculations turn out wrong... fans are just telling the studios they'll never be happy and the studios are just incentivized to make whatever puts general audience butts in seats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T03:50:16-07:00","id":1550434,"title":"","content":"(Post deleted)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 04-28-2025, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T05:52:01-07:00","id":1550438,"title":"","content":"Boats. They live on boats. Boats that do long haul shipping, fishing, and salvage operations and can be in those waters for months on end. When a salvage crew brings up a ship that's close enough to one of those islands, it gets counted as being exported from that island to wherever the valuable bits are sold.<br /> <br /> Given some of those islands are nature preserves it would be illegal to build your own house there, let alone a manufacturing facility.<br /> <br /> I made no specific characterizations of the people responsible. Please do not put such words in my mouth.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why it's sticking in your craw so much that I tried to vent about the tariffs with a bit of levity attached, but that's all that was going on until you decided to return to this, again. Especially in a thread that has generously allowed some skirting around its &quot;no politics&quot; clause but does have one in place, I don't know what you seem dead set on turning this into a discussion that gets deeply political.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T07:30:28-07:00","id":1550439,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>This thread has specifically called out &quot;no politics&quot; in the rules, and I have issued warnings on it before. Refrain or be removed. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T13:52:49-07:00","id":1550463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1550400#post1550400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Esp. since, while WW 1984 proves its no panacea for the superhero genre, going into the past has been really successful for both Marvel and DC films already there's no reason to fear audiences are going to reject the idea the same way the studios were nervous about Captain America 1 and Wonder Woman 1 when it was more of an unknown of how well period pieces would mix with modern superheros.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you! And you're spot on with Wonder Woman and Captain America. Those were perfect period pieces and fit those heroes well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1550400#post1550400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen a lot of fan speculation about FF and the more plausible idea for how Marvel will move the team from the upcoming stand alone film into the main MCU... they're fairly reasonable based on what we know, and Marvel's general direction as a studio. But I also worry that fandoms have grown over analytical and wrapped up in trying to predict things that it's only making it harder to make a fun movie in a big franchise. I get the fun of trying to be right about what a story is going to do by pouring over all the hints and what not... but then the goal of that is to enjoy the vindication or the surprise if the studio managed to pull off something else. When you put studios in a place where movies get dragged online for either being too predictable (in an era where people will spend hours scouring each frame of a trailer for hints...), or fans get upset when their pet speculations turn out wrong... fans are just telling the studios they'll never be happy and the studios are just incentivized to make whatever puts general audience butts in seats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I'm pretty sure they'll move the F4 over into the main MCU timeline...if not at the end of this movie, then soon, probably in one of the crossover movies. And I think that makes sense, start them in a 60's like world, then get them interacting with the main universe.<br /> <br /> You're right about some people being over critical of every little detail. It does kind of feel like a lot of the newer movies are a lot of cameos and setup for other movies, where the older MCU movies were just trying to tell a good story first and didn't worry so much about all the setup. If that makes sense..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T15:06:55-07:00","id":1550466,"title":"","content":"It's 100% a valid criticism that the MCU has declined significantly in the balance of each film standing on its own merits and fitting into the larger MCU, which is a large driving factor in the burnout on the MCU.<br /> <br /> It's basically why I eventually stopped collecting mainstream US comics back in the 90s: too many crossovers, too many things happening to my main characters in other series that I would have to buy other comics to know what was going on, and then even more to have the context of those series current events too. Marvel and DC (and even Image and Dark Horse did it to some extent) kept pushing for megafans that bought everything at the cost of fans that only followed specific characters being able to do so.<br /> <br /> Marvel and DC also have extremely long histories of repeating mistakes so... I'm not really shocked it's bleeding into the movies that they aren't looking at previous negative trends in superhero stories sales and trying to not do the same things.<br /> <br /> I was thinking a bit beyond the MCU though, and more towards the general culture of &quot;pre-dissecting&quot; films before they even come out because it's apparently good content on social media platforms. Maybe it's my old man nostalgia goggles getting to me, but going to movies just isn't as fun as it used to be because it feels like I'm surrounded by a bunch of movie critics there to confirm their biases about the films instead of fans (either of the specific subject/artists, or just general cinephiles) there to have fun. While I don't want someone bringing a chicken to the theater, I kinda want to go to see the Minecraft movie just because people are going to see it in droves to have fun and not care if the movie isn't deep, or original, or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T00:58:53-07:00","id":1550565,"title":"","content":"I get amused by the statement when it comes to comicbook movie shills that it happened in the comics and not ask was the source material that good to begin with?<br /> <br /> I'm a fan of Iron Man but I don't want to see a live action version of The Crossing where he gets manipulated by Kang/Immortus into becoming a villian and getting replaced by a 18 year old version of himself.<br /> <br /> Or I don't think Spider Man fans want the Clone Saga or One More Day as a film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T01:42:47-07:00","id":1550566,"title":"","content":"The adaptations can redeem some plots. The old (well, not the oldest) Spider-man Animated series did the Clone Saga and it was (low bar) leaps and bounds better than the comics version. I think MCU's Civil War was way better than the comics as well.<br /> <br /> I guess it can help that adaptations don't have nearly as massive of a backlog of continuity to manage.<br /> <br /> That said... they can also screw them up (The Killing Joke animated movie was almost perfect which made one very infamous addition all that much harder to stomach). But IMO we've seen more good examples of bad comic story-lines being redeemed than whatever the opposite is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T02:47:23-07:00","id":1550569,"title":"","content":"I was surprised that they did a adaptation of Batman The Killing Joke as it's a pretty dark story by Alan Moore and maybe be left alone. But that is just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T04:02:48-07:00","id":1550574,"title":"","content":"Yeah but, and I get this is a big if, if you got rid of the Barbara Gordon romance side plot they added in, wouldn't it have been a really solid adaptation of the story? The DC animated stuff has been pretty good. They also handled the Dark Knight Returns really well by not messing with the core story elements and they didn't shy away from keeping the darker elements from that either.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'd trust the DCAU stuff as much in the future with WB's leadership changes being an utter shit show for handling longstanding franchise well, but there's decades of solid demonstrations they did already of the ability to translate comic to screen successfully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T22:04:54-07:00","id":1550616,"title":"","content":"It sucks that storytelling quality has declined so quickly for comic book movies. Maybe a few years down the road it might change, but right now they have had more flops then success.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T05:30:02-07:00","id":1550621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1550466#post1550466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's 100% a valid criticism that the MCU has declined significantly in the balance of each film standing on its own merits and fitting into the larger MCU, which is a large driving factor in the burnout on the MCU.<br /> <br /> It's basically why I eventually stopped collecting mainstream US comics back in the 90s: too many crossovers, too many things happening to my main characters in other series that I would have to buy other comics to know what was going on, and then even more to have the context of those series current events too. Marvel and DC (and even Image and Dark Horse did it to some extent) kept pushing for megafans that bought everything at the cost of fans that only followed specific characters being able to do so.<br /> <br /> Marvel and DC also have extremely long histories of repeating mistakes so... I'm not really shocked it's bleeding into the movies that they aren't looking at previous negative trends in superhero stories sales and trying to not do the same things.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I got out of collecting comics for the exact same reason! It seemed like every year there was a company wide crossover and I just couldn't keep up with it all. A crossover every now and then between books is fine, it's a connected world, but it shouldn't happen all the time...<br /> <br /> And I don't mind the movies and tv shows crossing over with, but it's just starting to be a lot to deal with...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1550466#post1550466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking a bit beyond the MCU though, and more towards the general culture of &quot;pre-dissecting&quot; films before they even come out because it's apparently good content on social media platforms. Maybe it's my old man nostalgia goggles getting to me, but going to movies just isn't as fun as it used to be because it feels like I'm surrounded by a bunch of movie critics there to confirm their biases about the films instead of fans (either of the specific subject/artists, or just general cinephiles) there to have fun. While I don't want someone bringing a chicken to the theater, I kinda want to go to see the Minecraft movie just because people are going to see it in droves to have fun and not care if the movie isn't deep, or original, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I hear ya. People see a trailer and pour every tiny detail and form this solid opinion about something before they even see it. Or just out right hate it because they hate every thing. Hell, look at a lot of Star Wars YouTubers who just hate everything... it's crazy.<br /> <br /> As for movie theaters, I just stopped going. I used to love going to the theater, but there isn't one super close to me anymore, and etiquette in the theaters is at rock bottom at the moment. So, it's easier for me to just wait and watch things at home...seems like a better viewing experience.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T07:17:31-07:00","id":1550624,"title":"","content":"I'm with you Mr. Gone when it comes to going to theatres and I mentioned about it in this forum. Comic's in the 1990s were bad for mega part company wide crossovers with the tag line that nothing would be the same.<br /> <br /> Several of my friends who were fans of Peter David first run on the Incredible Hulk would groan when it was crossover time as they the Hulk would be screwed and for me it was just a question of why do you think that you need this big of a crossover and does having so and so is needed?<br /> <br /> As with YouTubers, I usually just follow Chris Mcfreely for his Transformers lore, Space Ice as he loves to roast bad or praise good over the top action films, Multiversial Wisdom that has Batman coming up with plans or reacting to things that catch his eye. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-03-2025, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T14:53:21-07:00","id":1550641,"title":"","content":"My going to theaters has dropped for a lot of reasons... one of which is that the locally independently owned one (and that's hella rare to have instead of a chain theater and I gladly supported them over driving a bit farther for cheap franchise theaters) managed to show up in a Jordan Klepper segment (which is the downside of independent businesses... sometimes they decide to make the owner's politics really obvious, and don't care how off putting it is to a lot of people to have to think about that when they just want to see a movie). COVID wasn't taken seriously around here so... that was a big risk I wasn't going to take. And the current economy isn't helping either.<br /> <br /> Say what you will about the Star Wars franchise, but I remember going to the Episode I premier locally and it was what people love about being a fan: a giant gathering of folks with a shared interest being awesome to each other as we get to experience a rare cultural event. You could kinda tell Phantom Menace wasn't going to go down with a great reputation in history later, but we all were too caught up in the moment to realize the stuff we completely gave a pass because HOLY SHIT THE DUEL OF FATES WAS EVERYTHING WE HOPED. Hell the theatrical re-release of the original trilogy with the not-so-popular Lucas edits wasn't as hype because the edits were seen skeptically pretty fast, but it was still some great nights of fun with fellow fans.<br /> <br /> At Endgame, when Cap finally got to say &quot;Avengers Assemble!&quot; most people where cheering, but my theater had a enough people noticeably being snide about people being &quot;manipulated&quot; so easily. It's not manipulation, it's what fans actually wanted to see on screen. It seems like it keeps getting worse. Even outside of big franchises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T15:16:50-07:00","id":1550645,"title":"","content":"I remember the long line ups when the prequels were being shown and how everyone was so excited and the only criticism at the time were from activists who accused George Lucas of racial stereotyping. The fans didn't care about that nonsense.<br /> <br /> For me it was seeing the first Batman film by Tim Burton and seeing a more gothic looking Dark Knight then the camp from the Adam West era. I wasn't upset that Batman used a grappling gun or that they gave the Joker a name and meshed his origin with Joe Chill. We got to see a good comic book movie and the response was positive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T15:40:21-07:00","id":1550651,"title":"","content":"Batman was kinda different because nobody really knew what to expect out of Burton and Keaton. It's a classic now, but at the time most people were skeptical until they actually saw it. So seeing it in theaters was different than a lot of other movies because you had this major cultural iconic character and... a movie that nobody really knew what to think about it based on who made it and who was in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T16:49:05-07:00","id":1550652,"title":"","content":"I remember watching Icons Unearthed Batman and how much of a battle it was to get the film made and how Warner Bros had it doubts that it would be a success. When I went to see it at age 12 or 13 and it was packed with people and everyone enjoyed it. But I do remember from some interviews and articles that they thought it wouldn't be good because of the casting of Michael Keaton and Burton helming it and he was known for more his quirky offbeat stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T22:42:08-07:00","id":1550653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1550645#post1550645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember the long line ups when the prequels were being shown and how everyone was so excited and the only criticism at the time were from activists who accused George Lucas of racial stereotyping. The fans didn't care about that nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think Star Wars has any Jewish fans who might have had issues with the prominent character presented as being a greedy, sleazy, cheating trader with a Yiddish accent and large nose when they first saw it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T00:35:28-07:00","id":1550655,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but realistically he's a bit more of a broadly offensive caricature of Middle Eastern peoples more broadly. Lots of Arabs were just as offended as Jews.<br /> <br /> That said, the backlash about how lazy Lucas was in that regard goes well beyond that one character. And unfortunately the fans did not do a good job of keeping their displeasure aimed in the right direction. Ahmed Best (the guy that played Jar-Jar) reported being suicidal due to the hatred aimed at him via Jar-Jar; as Ahmed (who is very much black) actually suggested a lot of Jar-Jar's stuff as something that was part of humorous persona Ahmed had used in comedy before.<br /> <br /> So, no, I don't think it's right to blame a &quot;few activists&quot; because the prequel trilogy 100% deserves it's reputation for relying on cheap ethnic stereotypes to define new aliens species introduced; esp. using a ton of CGI that obscured the actors who might have softened it a bit. But it did get out of hand in how widely aimed said criticism got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T12:00:22-07:00","id":1550667,"title":"","content":"It's unfortunate that Ahmed Best got so much unwarranted attacks by people who didn't know his acts and made his life miserable. But wasn't more of the media personalities that led the charge instead of fans? I just thought Jar Jar Binks was just annoying and took the place of 3-PO as the character that got caught up in events that he was ill prepared for. I didn't dislike the character and saw it as something meant for a younger audience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T15:50:21-07:00","id":1550674,"title":"","content":"No. Over 30 fan websites were made (just in English!) dedicated to hating on Jar Jar.<br /> <br /> TVTropes has an entry called &quot;The Scrappy&quot; named after Scrappy-Doo from the Scooby-Doo franchise. Some languages where people don't get the older American reference renamed it &quot;The Jar Jar&quot; instead... because that many people hated the character he's a synonym for a type of bad characters in multiple languages.<br /> <br /> That's not a few celebrities or activists doing. That's the fandom rising up and say, &quot;Lucas, wtf dude?&quot; The &quot;activists&quot; (I don't really consider that a legitimate title for people no advocating any real solutions) largely took the aggregate negative reactions to Watto, Nute Gunray, and Jar Jar, expanded it to even more characters (the really tenuous attempt to say that one of the pod-racers looking like a Scottish terrier and drinking a lot was aimed at the Scots) to justify a wider brush to paint with.<br /> <br /> The reality is simple: Lucas drew heavily from old school space operas that came before Star Wars which frequently used racist stereotypes (Ming the Merciless being the obvious example), and in the prequels Lucas was free to do things without the same amount of oversight that the original trilogy saw (Lucas's original treatment for A New Hope is out there, we are very lucky it got a rewrite by professional script doctors). That sort of freedom can lead to a lot of unintentional inclusions by not thinking about how something from the 1930s might need alteration for the late 1990s to be seen as acceptable. Lucas is also no Kurosawa, and copying Kurosawa's take on comedic side characters makes it clear that Lucas made an inferior copy instead of putting a new spin inspired by a master film maker.<br /> <br /> It's also really painfully obvious how much Lucas needed a good editor and more creative voices in his works when you look at things like the Clone Wars show and expanded animated series actually giving Jar Jar a bit of redemption (even getting Ahmed to play Jar Jar again): the animated shows reframe Jar Jar as an animal empath (possibly mildly Force sensitive, possibly just a thing some Gungans can do). He struggles with social norms, reacts to things extremely, and so on in Phantom Menace because he's not really aware of his connections to wildlife skewing how he sees things. After the events of the prequel trilogy and interacting with the Jedi, he learns it's an actual power he can control, is much calmer and clear headed, and can actually call Naboo wildlife to his aide after getting a better handle on his powers. That's not something Lucas came up with, but it's such a small tweak to the character that makes him so much less grating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T03:40:32-07:00","id":1550680,"title":"","content":"Fifty-years ago, Lucas had innovative ideas on special-effects, produced a movie based on that, then, people would be criticizing his story-telling capacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T05:31:47-07:00","id":1550683,"title":"","content":"1) John Dykstra had innovative ideas on special effects, George Lucas had ambitions to make something people had never seen before and was put in touch with Dykstra through mutual acquaintances.<br /> <br /> 2) Lucas was a director, primary credited screenwriter, credited with multiple story credits (as in he came up with the core story and someone else flushed it out into a final product), and did some uncredited storytelling work as well. Reducing him just the producer - esp. when talking Star Wars - is very strange. Oh, and he also wrote multiple novels too.<br /> <br /> 3) If you work in a storytelling medium like films as part of the creative storytelling process (esp. if you take on multiple major roles like director and primary screenwriter), people are going to judge you on your storycraft. Lucas wrote, directed, and produced (and was an uncredited main editor of) all three of the prequel movies. If there are creative problems with the prequel trilogy, there is litterally only one person to blame them on. So film critics are going to judge that work and if it's lackluster, they're going to blame the guy that opted to do all of the high level decision making himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T11:15:28-07:00","id":1550698,"title":"","content":"Icons Unearthed Star Wars talks alot what went on in the making of the original Star Wars films and much of a toll it took on George Lucas and how it fueled his desire to control everything in the IP. It shows why having different people involved in a production can be a good thing when they need to tell what needs to be said and not what you want to hear","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-09-2025, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T12:42:48-07:00","id":1550702,"title":"","content":"And just to make something clear, I don't think Lucas is some sort of overrated talentless hack or some BS like that. He's just not a strong storyteller. He's smart, he stuck to genres like pulp action and space opera where deep storytelling chops aren't necessarily what audiences want; sure they're not bad if you have them, but it's not the main draw. He's never shied away from how derivative his stuff is, he unabashedly knew to market to kids despite people what a bunch of corporate suits (who made Lucas rich by letting him have the merchandising rights to all those trading cards and toys Star Wars kids bought in droves) thought, and so many other things. He's on the pretty sort list of billionaires that can point to their careers and say, &quot;yeah, I actually earned that,&quot; not matter how much he stood on the shoulders of giants.<br /> <br /> He just belongs in a class of business people like Thomas Edison and Steve Jobs (both also notoriously controlling) who have a mythology due to being the face of a brand/company that isn't reality, but the truth (mostly that 90% of their success was being really good at finding the right people to make their ideas happen) doesn't actually diminish what their vision, ambition, and skills produced. It also doesn't excuse that it's a type of personality that a lot of people don't really like in-person because controlling perfectionists are... not pleasant to be around when things aren't going their way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T22:13:55-07:00","id":1550721,"title":"","content":"I agree that dialogue or solid storytelling isn't George Lucas strong suit as it was shown in the prequels, but I gave him props for creating a fun series of movies with the original trilogy and we saw how having the right people working with him and refining his ideas and how his ex wife was a master in the editing room. It seems like when he got total control of everything Star Wars he got mostly yes men and women and it showed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T12:27:52-07:00","id":1550911,"title":"","content":"I wonder if we complain about lore changes for the sake of it and not the reasons why?<br /> <br /> For example in GI Joe it would make sense that most of them wouldn't be Vietnam veterans as they are all collecting pensions and making them serve in the Middle East would make better storytelling sense and as it sticks to the core concepts of the characters it shouldn't be an issue.<br /> <br /> Sometimes change can be a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T16:52:00-07:00","id":1550924,"title":"","content":"Confirmation bias is definitely a problem for fandoms. It's natural to how humans think. It's unavoidable that when we get attached to a piece of media, that we are going to have an instinctive negative reaction to changes to it. There are things people making media can do to soften that reaction, and there's things we can do to not let knee-jerk reactions be our only ones, but it's always going to happen on some level.<br /> <br /> The problem is when the knee-jerk negativity towards changes in things we like is where the conversation ends. As you said, change can be good. The social media era has only exacerbated things by rewarding fast negative responses and not really rewarding long thoughtful considerations of things. Clickbait works because enough people click the bait. Social media also adds another layer of difficulty in communications by siloing people into bubbles. If 90% of the criticism you see of a change to a franchise is designed to piss you off by being the kind of criticism you hate, you think that most criticism is coming from a bad place (and social media companies know that means you're more likely to engage).<br /> <br /> I think the best thing for modern major franchises would be to look at things like where my handle/avatar come from, or even Batman as a media franchise: change things so much that change is part of the brand. Part of being a Gundam fan is enjoying that the Gundam franchise is constantly doing need continuities with new characters and new creative teams. Yes, the corpos in charge love it, because it means a whole new pile of merch to sell each time (and like GI Joe, Gundam is about selling toys in the end), but the fans don't feel &quot;used&quot; because the don't have to justify selling you the 10th version of Char's Zaku, when they can sell you 10 different Mobile suits that are all pink/red to evoke the Char clone stock character type in the franchise.<br /> <br /> If a fan didn't jive with Gundam Seed? Well, they wait four years and a completely new Gundam story is going to happen.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if you're a Batman fan, there's always different takes of Batman for you to get into. If you thought Nolan's Batman didn't really have the staying power for a trilogy? Well, we have Matt Reeve's The Batman now. Thought Batfleck was kinda interesting but the live-action Synder version of things was doomed to fail at a high level? There's plenty of animated Batman stories that have similar themes and explorations of the character where he's been at it for a long time and is starting to question his crusade's worth. Batman fans can debate any given story, but the Batman franchise can shift gears and the worst that happens is a dud that people were already prepared to ignore and look forward to a different thing soon enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T11:38:49-07:00","id":1550967,"title":"","content":"The only live action version of Batman I didn't like was the Joel Schumacher ones and felt it was to light on story and to much on visuals. Sort of your typical Michael Bay film where he used special effects and stunts to hide weakness in the story. <br /> <br /> As for Ben Affleck, I didn't see him as Batman and I always felt he was a better behind the camera then infront of it. Though I felt he was good in The Town and The Accountant and I can't discern why he was good there and bad in other roles.<br /> <br /> I haven't watched the Matt Reeves version yet and it might be a long time before I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T05:19:38-07:00","id":1551119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1550924#post1550924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, if you're a Batman fan, there's always different takes of Batman for you to get into. If you thought Nolan's Batman didn't really have the staying power for a trilogy? Well, we have Matt Reeve's The Batman now. Thought Batfleck was kinda interesting but the live-action Synder version of things was doomed to fail at a high level? There's plenty of animated Batman stories that have similar themes and explorations of the character where he's been at it for a long time and is starting to question his crusade's worth. Batman fans can debate any given story, but the Batman franchise can shift gears and the worst that happens is a dud that people were already prepared to ignore and look forward to a different thing soon enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the best things about Batman, is that there can be a lot of different versions and it still basically feels like the same character. So if you didn't like one version there are still some others to choose from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1550967#post1550967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't watched the Matt Reeves version yet and it might be a long time before I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hearing some rumors that Matt Reeves might be out as director of the new Batman. Not sure if that means they'll be moving on from Robert Pattinson or what...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T09:57:24-07:00","id":1551127,"title":"","content":"To give some appropriate credit, my Batman point is largely inspired by Hardy LeBel (a former level and multiplayer map designer for Bungie).<br /> <br /> He gave an interview to HiddenXperia (if you ever want to learn every last detail about Halo lore, he's one of the best folks out there doing that kind of content) discussing why he thinks the fans of Halo don't really understand why the franchise has struggled so much since Bungie left it, and his feelings on what Microsoft and (now) Halo Studios should do moving forward in order to not only get the franchise to recover, but also make it easier for it to endure. The Batman movies were a big part of his argument for this sort of constant rebooting approach (mostly because it's simple and accessible to most people compare to many examples he could pull from decades of working in video games).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T23:49:55-07:00","id":1551178,"title":"","content":"I heard that Matt Reeves is suffering from health issues and that it's preventing him from making the sequel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T04:28:32-07:00","id":1551184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1551178#post1551178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard that Matt Reeves is suffering from health issues and that it's preventing him from making the sequel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, dang. I'm sorry to hear that. Hopefully he can beat whatever he's dealing with it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T10:46:15-07:00","id":1551198,"title":"","content":"The Matt Reeves situation reminds me of what was happening with Kurt Busiek when he got sick and couldn't do his series Astro City for a time. That title was his pride and joy and he couldn't get into the proper mind set for it when he got ill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T21:17:28-07:00","id":1551210,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why people are starting to knock Tim Burton's version of Batman now on social media. If it wasn't for the success of his film there would be no Batman Animated Series or future films of the character down the road. Whatever you think of Tim Burton as a person as a director he is extremely good and knows how to craft a good story and as a Batman fan I always gave him props for his Batman work.<br /> <br /> It should be noted according to Unearthed Batman it was a struggle to get the film green lite as Warner Bros had little faith that a live screen film would work at all.<br /> <br /> I just don't get some of the posts from YouTubers who weren't even alive when it came out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-22T17:32:42-07:00","id":1551215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1551210#post1551210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why people are starting to knock Tim Burton's version of Batman now on social media. If it wasn't for the success of his film there would be no Batman Animated Series or future films of the character down the road. Whatever you think of Tim Burton as a person as a director he is extremely good and knows how to craft a good story and as a Batman fan I always gave him props for his Batman work.<br /> <br /> It should be noted according to Unearthed Batman it was a struggle to get the film green lite as Warner Bros had little faith that a live screen film would work at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does any of that put it beyond critical evaluation?<br /> <br /> I, for one, was alive when that movie came out (probably), and absolutely adored it when I was young for reasons including how it resonated with the animated series that was my obsession, and certainly came back to it as an adult and found a perspective of &quot;even setting aside questions of this as an adaptation of Batman, this isn't the most tightly plotted piece of cinema&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't get some of the posts from YouTubers who weren't even alive when it came out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly some of them had to analyse Shakespeare in school and thought &quot;hey, taking a look at and giving an opinion on a thing that happened before I was born is completely uncontroversial&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-22T21:38:48-07:00","id":1551220,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about what's so infuriating about people criticizing Burton's Batman. Can you link some of those videos <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a>?<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned, while I do think it is the best Batman movie I saw, it isn't above criticism. And it's really weird to complain about the critic's age. People can still watch the movie today and have an opinion. But I really want to understand what this criticism is to see if there's something bad about it (bad criticism, as in criticism badly done, is a thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-22T23:36:23-07:00","id":1551222,"title":"","content":"Well, as someone that saw both of the Batman movies in the theaters? I think in hindsight there's a lot I think didn't age well that a younger me ignored because I was watching a great adaptation. Batman Returns aged worse than the first movie did, but both show early signs of the limits of Tim Burton's directorial style. Burton is very dependent on a lot of aesthetic to paper over weak plotting and pacing of his stories. You can overlook a lot of it in things like Batman because comics aren't exactly the most logically coherent genre, and films like Beetlejuice where the style is kinda the point.<br /> <br /> Having watched most of Burton's films... I feel like Batman and Batman Returns benefit a lot from being very early in his career; before a lot of his lesser tendencies grew more and more clear after repetition from film to film. The constant attempts to juxtapose &quot;normal&quot; vs. dark whimsical visuals despite the needs of the story makes each rewatching his films less fun because you realize you're watching someone with a handful of tricks and doesn't seem to care about learning more.<br /> <br /> Burton has also said some things on the public record in the meantime that haven't helped anything. I admit it's not the most charitable reading of his statements (but I don't feel very charitable considering the context), however he very much feels that other people's stories exist for him to slap his coat of paint on and then their his stories and the originals don't need to be thought about or acknowledged. Trying to justify completely stripping the context of WWII, Nazism, and a Jewish protagonist from Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children, and then looking at many of his older creative choices in adapting existing materials can make many of them feel less &quot;creative liberty that adds to the larger canon of the character,&quot; and more &quot;Burton being self-indulgent.&quot; How the Penguin's entire plot in Batman Returns is very much an example of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-23T10:05:16-07:00","id":1551236,"title":"","content":"I get what you say, but I think he was what Batman needed for a movie. Not in the sense of being overly competent for the job, but that his style was exactly what a Batman movie needs.<br /> <br /> Take that with a lot of my personal taste, though. I very much dislike versions of Batman with military-grade tech, for example, and some other aspects of the character that have been very popular in the last decade. Which doesn't make them less Batman, just not my cup of tea Batman.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Burton's take is quite repetitive. I couldn't bear to watch his rendition of Sweeney Todd, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-23T13:31:06-07:00","id":1551242,"title":"","content":"I mean, I'd argue that Bruce Timm is exactly what a Batman movie needs, he just only works in animation (and is a huge reason why DC fans consider the 90s and later DCAU some of the best stuff ever made for the franchise). I appreciate that it'd be hard to argue that <i>Mask of the Phantasm</i> would have been released in theaters without the success of the Burton films, but I'll stand by it being superior to them in every artistic merit. I'd also argue that Matt Reeves is the only live-action Batman movie director since the Adam West years to actually remember that Batman is supposed to be a world class detective (you know, DC, Detective Comics), even if Reeves purposefully chose to do an early Batman who's still figuring out what being Batman truly means so we don't get into the Batcomputer solving most of the mystery for us.<br /> <br /> Burton, Schumacher, Nolan, and Synder all completely skip having any sort of mystery for Batman to solve; or at least put in some nod to the idea before the mystery essentially solves itself. Even the 1966 movie has Batman and Robin needing to investigate Underworld United and untangle some plot before it gets on with highly stylized violence. It might be campy as all get out, but it never forgets that all the Batgear is to facilitate telling the story in a reasonable amount of time, not to skip past Batman collaborating with Robin, Alfred, and Commissioner Gordon is what needs to break the case. It's not to say the movies those guys made are unwatchable or something, but I don't think you can hold up a given director's work with the character as what Batman &quot;needs&quot; and skip one of his most defining features. It might be what Warner Bros. needed, but that's a different consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-24T17:36:54-07:00","id":1551266,"title":"","content":"Batman Begins at least makes him a bit more of a detective in the somewhat more realistic sense of acquiring evidence that could be used to build a case against somebody for a conviction.<br /> <br /> It's just a bit unfortunate that even that element gets largely rendered irrelevant when Falcone becomes sidelined as a target and the replacement is somebody dealt with by a crashing train rather than the courts.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T00:03:13-07:00","id":1551267,"title":"","content":"I admit it might be a bit of a semantic nitpick, but I feel there's a difference between &quot;crime fighter&quot; and &quot;detective&quot; as a narrative role. In Batman Begins, we know who the bad guys are, and they frankly aren't even shy about stating their goals on screen. There's no mystery to unravel. The tension in the story is not, &quot;will Batman figure out the bad guy's plot, and at what cost?&quot; but rather, &quot;what will Batman need to do to take the bad guys down despite Gotham's corruption.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, to go all the way back to 1966, even with a lot of campy and a very thin mystery, there's tension in that movie because Batman is up against multiple rogues that are purposefully mixing their signature calling cards to throw Batman off. Yeah, we know what their goal is, but their methods are purposefully obscured to put us in Batman's shoes as he tries to figure out who's doing what with who's toys<br /> <br /> Another comparison could be to Thomas Jane's Punisher... who does a lot of investigating of his enemies. But the goal is more militaristic recon so he can effectively attack them at their weakest. Even with all the &quot;detective&quot; work, we don't see the Punisher as a detective, just a man on a destructive mission of complete vengeance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T06:29:26-07:00","id":1551269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1551267#post1551267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit it might be a bit of a semantic nitpick, but I feel there's a difference between &quot;crime fighter&quot; and &quot;detective&quot; as a narrative role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but there <i>are</i> narratives about detectives pursuing people who are known criminals, but not in a manner that can yet be proven in a court of law. I'm just saying that there's valid space for a depiction of Batman concerned with aiding the police in building their case as well as perpetrators whose identities and activities are totally unknown at the outset.<br /> <br /> I mean, would we be saying that he's not a detective in Batman Year One?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T14:17:58-07:00","id":1551273,"title":"","content":"Like I said, I was meaning this as a narrative role. Yes, there's definitely room for Batman stories that don't focus on him as a detective in that sense, but it becomes a problem when that's increasingly absent from his live action depictions.<br /> <br /> And... which Year One? Year One has been retread a lot (Batman Begins, Mask of the Phantasm, a direct animated adaptation called Batman Year One, and The Batman, all take direct inspiration from the original comic arc). The original comic? It's a mix, but that's part of the point. Bruce/Batman are trying to figure out who and what they need to be. Sometimes he's being a narrative detective (working with Dent and Gordon to get Skeevers to go on the record against both Falcone and the corrupt cops on the mob's take), sometimes he's not (when he crashes a party with multiple politicians, upper tier police officers, and crime bosses, to tell them that the Batman is here to clean up their mess), which is fine for the idea of a fresh and uncertain Batman struggling with how to pursue his overarching goals. The end of Year One is with Batman accepting his role as a detective - more than a symbol of fear via vigilante justice, but someone that can go places and find information Gotham's corruption hamstrings the few good cops from getting - when he accepts the Joker case from Gordon. <br /> <br /> Batman Begins cutting Skeevers out (which I can understand, it would be a lot to add to the story unless they dropped Ras as the big bad for a later movie) and reducing it to Batman handing Rachel a pile of things that are more blackmail material against corrupt officials than useful evidence for convictions, is cutting a lot of the narrative detective aspects of Batman out of the story IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T15:46:40-07:00"