 the narrative detective aspects of Batman out of the story IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-26T14:16:34-07:00","id":1551300,"title":"","content":"Sad news in the comic world as Peter David passed away at age 68 from long standing health issues and his wife needed to get a go fund me page to help with costs. It's a shame as I really enjoyed his work on Incredible Hulk, Spider Man 2099 and a wide variety of science fiction novels for Star Trek and Babylon 5.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-26T14:18:37-07:00","id":1551301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1551220#post1551220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about what's so infuriating about people criticizing Burton's Batman. Can you link some of those videos <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a>?<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned, while I do think it is the best Batman movie I saw, it isn't above criticism. And it's really weird to complain about the critic's age. People can still watch the movie today and have an opinion. But I really want to understand what this criticism is to see if there's something bad about it (bad criticism, as in criticism badly done, is a thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>It just mostly youtubers like Ranting for Vengence who is clueless about the many versions of the Dark Knight and even James Gunn took pot shots at the film saying it wasn't that great because of how the costume moved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-26T14:23:20-07:00","id":1551303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1551276#post1551276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So im at my folks house watching tv and have noticed the reason tv is in decline. And i realised tv is fucking shit now, intitially i thought it was nostalgia but i have a good memory and i recall it being objectivly less shit like 5 years ago. Its embarrising how bad the scifi and history channel are<br /> <br /> between this and the enshitification of the net and gaming being overpriced im giving serious thoughts to going back to drugs, specifically acid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what you mean about finding shows that are appealing to me anymore and I find myself watching older shows and movies then what is current right now, but I do like National Geographic and stuff like My Lottery Dream Home. Currently that only movie I'm really stoked for is Mission Impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-26T16:05:44-07:00","id":1551305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1551301#post1551301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It just mostly youtubers like Ranting for Vengence who is clueless about the many versions of the Dark Knight and even James Gunn took pot shots at the film saying it wasn't that great because of how the costume moved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe... don't care what a 15 year old YouTuber says - at best as an act to get clicks if not just because he really believes the racist shit he says - about stuff that came out when his dad was a kid?<br /> <br /> People don't make inflammatory click-bait videos because everyone agrees with them... because if everyone agreed with them it wouldn't get clicks. They're saying shit other people aren't saying because it's a way to stand out in a very large crowd; even if they say objectively horrible things instead of anything insightful.<br /> <br /> As for James Gunn... that's not really a hot take there. The Burton/Schumacher style Batsuits were notoriously hard on the actors because they were extremely restricting, which then caused lots of problems for everyone else because whole scenes had to be reworked to account for how poorly the rubber cowl idea works on film. Burton has said there are shots that weren't as good as he wanted because the suit got in the way of Keaton's ability to act in it. Keaton said the suit's restrictive movement and isolating nature (it limited visibility and hearing) was so intense that after the first day of shooting he wasn't sure they were going to be able to maintain the shooting schedule because he wasn't sure he was going to be able to do his scenes in it; they had to constantly struggle with it the whole time. Props to Keaton though for both (1) working through it anyway and (2) actually using it by turning the isolation and pain into inspiration for how Bruce feels and acts<br /> <br /> Even Nolan included a joke about it in his trilogy while Bruce and Lucius Fox were discussing suit design and making the cowl easier to move in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T22:48:57-07:00","id":1551361,"title":"","content":"Kinda of disheartening to keep on hearing that Marvel and DC Comics are bad from bad actors. I mean pick your decade and you will always find terrible comics and ideas that outnumber the good work from other talents.<br /> <br /> Though maybe making them more affordable and being seen on newstands might help the industry somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-06T02:25:52-07:00","id":1551499,"title":"","content":"If you fall on baits, the algorithm will give you more baits. Unfortunately it's on us to avoid bad actors on YouTube and TikTok.<br /> <br /> Search actively by channels that you find to be better. I'm personally following Cinematerapy for movies (and some others, but they're Brazilian channels, like Super8).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-06T11:56:24-07:00","id":1551502,"title":"","content":"I have been enjoying watching Space Ice who roasts bad movies, music videos from Ghost, Chris Mcfreely Transformers lore and Warhammer 40 K lore from Weshammer and Lutein.<br /> <br /> That said it's sometimes amusing to watch people have meltdowns and make a video in their car and show people how not to act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-06-2025, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T22:07:30-07:00","id":1552026,"title":"","content":"More sad news from the world of comics. Jim Shooter who started writing comics at the unbelievable age of 14 passed away from Esophageal cancer at age 73. I remember from his Secret Wars mini series and the Valiant Comic line.<br /> <br /> Whatever you think of him personally, he left a big mark on the business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T21:46:52-07:00","id":1552066,"title":"","content":"Sad news about the passing of actor Michael Madsen the other day. He was great playing bad guys in Quentin Tarantino film's and his dance scene in Reservoir Dogs was chilling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://