on b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1552599#post1552599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That really sucks...</div> </div> </div> </div>Black sabbath are a major shaping factor in my life in terms of culture, friends and aesthetics. Its like a respected political or religious figure has died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T11:31:47-07:00","id":1552671,"title":"","content":"It sucks that people that I watched or listened as a child are dying. First Val Kilmer, Michael Madsen, Julian McMahon, Malcom Jamal Warner, Ozzy Osborne and now Hulk Hogan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T11:43:21-07:00","id":1552672,"title":"","content":"It sucks that Hulk Hogan passed away at age 71 due to cardiac arrest, whatever you thought of Terry Boliea the man behind the persona. You can not deny that he helped make wrestling a mainstream success along with Vince McMahon during the eighties and paved the way for future stars like Shawn Michael's, Steve Austin, The Rock and many others down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T14:05:16-07:00","id":1552673,"title":"","content":"It's not a matter of &quot;denying&quot; the success of the WWF/WWE. It's that the costs incurred socially and morally in all of the pain and suffering those two caused along the way. How many non-white wrestlers quitting before they got a chance due to Terry's racist harassment is worth it? How many women is Vince allowed to use his power to coerce for what we got?<br /> <br /> That's why I don't really care about separating the person from the persona. The person is who made the social good of entertainment worse than it could have been because they could use the persona as a shield. Hulk Hogan wasn't just a character Terry Boliea played for the audience. Hulk Hogan was a curtain so we couldn't see all of the shit Terry was doing that made wrestling promotions less safe physically and mentally. And all the while gatekeeping the fuck out of the industry, not helping new talent come up in the world.<br /> <br /> Hulk Hogan and Vince McMahon didn't &quot;pave the way&quot; for most of the wrestlers in the WWE. Vince just bought the smaller promotions and the talent with it and became a billionaire of their work and investment. The Anoa'i Family? They paved the way for The Rock (and a lot of other big names), and they had to fight against McMahon and stooges like Hogan that only wanted to give them ethnic stereotype gimmicks while ensuring the championships always go back to white wrestlers (something that lasted way too long in the industry...); giving the credit to the racists in the organization is downright ugly instead of acknowledging the generational dynasties that actually train up the greatest talents we get to see perform. <br /> <br /> The past is the past. What happened happened. Terry was who he was. The importance of not sugar-coating his legacy is so that the future can do better. We don't need jabronis to have nice things, no matter how many people try to convince us they'll give us a pittance of their extorted profits if we let them be part of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T07:01:28-07:00","id":1552801,"title":"","content":"My car battery died this morning. Sucks. Luckily I got Triple A to start it back up, so now I\u2019m happy again and ready to go about my day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T02:05:15-07:00","id":1552827,"title":"","content":"The the Online Safety Act age verification is a complete joke on a number of levels, creepy authoritarian aspects aside it's laughably easy to circumvent and I'm fairly confident there's going to be a massive date breach further down the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T04:25:34-07:00","id":1552880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1552827#post1552827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The the Online Safety Act age verification is a complete joke on a number of levels, creepy authoritarian aspects aside it's laughably easy to circumvent and I'm fairly confident there's going to be a massive date breach further down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! I've been hearing some of the news about it and it is crazy! I can't (well, I can sadly) believe they're trying to do this. There is most definitely going to be a HUGE data breach!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T13:46:41-07:00","id":1552889,"title":"","content":"I decided to go and read some things by the defenders of the OSA to even see if there were some points. I actually found an op-ed by someone that work(ed?) for one of the UK agencies that did a lot of the drafting of it, and he did manage to make at least some points that are worth considering. Not enough to change my mind about the OSA (and in many ways his overall arguments made my opinion of it worse), but he at least did make a good case on the balancing act of giving the government flexibility to address problems as the Internet changes (something lots of people have been complaining about for decades is how far behind our governments constantly are regarding digital regulations) with protecting personal liberties.<br /> <br /> For me, the biggest problem with the OSA is that it basically treats everyone on the Internet as an international megacorp with billions sitting around waiting to be paid to executives that could easily absorb the impact of increased regulations. The law has zero considerations for non-profits and small businesses that simply cannot afford to pay third party verification systems; even more so if they want to pay for quality ones that have decent security of people's data unlike the big tech companies that have no motives to use anything but the cheapest vendor that's good enough. What about a 18 year old university student that relies on a school provided computer? That computer is technically the institution's property, which means all the data to verify the student's age is now suddenly also the school's property... or the student is barred from legally protected activities by a law that doesn't provide any outs.<br /> <br /> I really don't think much thought was given into how this is just going to consolidate power over the Internet even more into the hands of the companies that already have too much power over something that is ever increasingly a necessity of life in many countries; not just a perk for those that can afford it. You can make as much of a case as you want about how you're going to make the companies take responsibility for moderating content.... but if your legal schema kills off all of their competitors over time, they can just come back and lobby to deregulate the Internet, or there isn't going to be an Internet for countries that don't comply.<br /> <br /> Data breaches suck... but that's already a constant problem. The influence Jeff Bezos already has over the Internet via AWS is already a problem too, but it's going to get even worse if he can force even more smaller companies to tie themselves into Amazon's ecosystem by making it the only affordable user-verification platform around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T16:25:21-07:00","id":1552891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1552801#post1552801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My car battery died this morning. Sucks. Luckily I got Triple A to start it back up, so now I\u2019m happy again and ready to go about my day.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least you got help with your battery and hopefully you got it replaced on that day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T17:02:10-07:00","id":1552893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.the