ave a good system to rapidly communicate that to websites and apps) way of providing that service.<br /> <br /> In the US car insurance is scammy has hell, because you have to have car insurance to legally drive anywhere, and the US is built around making people drive to get what they need. There is no public car insurance option, so you're at the mercy of whatever company you can afford. That's obviously bad.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile you also need a license to drive... which you get from the government. And it might not be a perfect system but getting and maintaining a driver's license is very straight forward and you don't have scumbags trying to sell you cheap licenses that are for real legit because... only the government issues legit ones.<br /> <br /> It really shouldn't be hard to get a &quot;digital license&quot; where you take some existing government ID to a government office, and they can give you a ID card that doesn't contain all your sensitive data, but counts as proof of age for websites. So many potential problems vanish quickly..</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. got sidetracked and didn't get to reply earlier. But well said! I'm with you on all of this. We'll see how everything plays out, but it's really starting to seem like we have some even darker days ahead of us.. ugh..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-09T05:50:41-07:00","id":1553025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1552994#post1552994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sad news if you were a fan of the show WKRP back in the day. Loni Anderson who played the lovely Jennifer Marlow passed away last week or so. I remember her from the show and some movies and I remember if I recall correctly that on a show that was set in the same universe as Golden Girls and Empty Nest. Getting old can suck for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard about that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yea, getting old suuuuucks...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T17:13:40-07:00","id":1553047,"title":"","content":"Not to get too overly focused on the OSA, but I recently heard another two points about how bad the law is:<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly, VPN searches (and from anecdotal evidence of Internet usages in other nearby countries it seems like people are using VPNs more already) have skyrocketed because it's a simple way around the law.<br /> <br /> 1) Less important to me, but something you'd think might matter to legislators, the way the modern Internet ad-revenue economy works is based on gathering data to target ads. If everyone in the UK under the age of 40 is using a VPN... then every UK company trying to advertise to UK customers is basically shit out of luck.<br /> <br /> 2) More importantly, children (the people the law is supposed to protect) are far less likely to use paid VPNs (who by virtue of being paid for their services are usually better for protecting your data) vs. all the free VPNs out there (which have countless instances of being scams to gather and sell data). So not only are adults feeling forced to pay for VPNs just to do legal Internet stuff without letting their data be sucked up by companies with horrible histories of data breaches, children are going to be giving their data to scammers... kinda the opposite of making them safer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T18:09:50-07:00","id":1553050,"title":"","content":"One thing I never really got in spoken English: after all, how do you pronounce Men and Women, to distinguish from Man and Woman!? There's a theoretical difference, but is there a <b>real</b> one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T20:11:27-07:00","id":1553054,"title":"","content":"IME local accent/dialect really matters. In some the difference is notable enough to pick up on, and in others it can be hard even on native English speakers to pick up on. English dialectical looseness when it comes to stresses and vowels is one of the reasons it can be such a hard language to learn to full fluency. I know the way I say the four words sounds fairly distinct to me, but still confuses non-English speakers because it makes zero phonetic sense (esp. Women vs. Woman and the way I was taught to pronounce the Os differently).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T11:07:05-07:00","id":1553069,"title":"","content":"INME there's lots of coworkers I had who thought I was from Atlantic Canada because of how I said certain words and I'm not from that part of Canada but I worked with many people from that region and picked up the vocal inflection. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T18:23:49-07:00","id":1553077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553069#post1553069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">INME</div> </div> </div> </div>Inland Northwest Mathematics Experience?<br /> Institute for Numerical Methods in Engineering?<br /> <br /> I really tried to find what INME stands for, but couldn't, and that's bugging me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, and other American English speakers, I've found this video on the pronunciation of Man vs Men. Is it accurate?<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AkRg0-trHtc&amp;t=1s\" data-code=\"AkRg0-trHtc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/AkRg0-trHtc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T03:43:07-07:00","id":1553084,"title":"","content":"I'd say that's broadly accurate, but it's worth remembering that America is big and there's a lot of variations within a country of 330+ million people.<br /> <br /> IME most guides like that oriented around the &quot;newscaster&quot; accents. These are accents largely associated with newscasters/presenters/hosts to maximize clarity and reduce the speakers normal accent; though a lot of people that engage with public speaker or address (like actors) will likely have some coaching in it for the same reason. But they're still somewhat regional, so there's a few that means throwing on the local news means you'll probably have a vague idea of what cost you're on (including the Great Lakes or the Gulf of Mexico).<br /> <br /> A lot of the faster accents make it much harder to hear that vowel shift in &quot;man&quot; much less prominent, while a lot of the accents prone to drawls can make the more direct eh in &quot;men&quot; harder to distinguish because of the tendency to elongate vowels broadly.<br /> <br /> It's also usually a subtle sign that someone grew up in a mixed language family when they do a different vowel shift that makes a bit more sense with their linguistic background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T04:51:11-07:00","id":1553086,"title":"","content":"Broadly accurate will have to be good enough, it's a starting point and as didactic as it gets. Even countries with far smaller populations or area can have an astounding amount of variation, I would have to say the same for Brazilian Portuguese, or Japanese, and so on. But with an entry point it's easier to notice and understand those variations.<br /> <br /> It was like that when I learned how the TH is pronounced. Before having an entry point, it was just T's and D's switching randomly to me, and without an actual explanation of the phoneme I would still be stuck there decades later. That's what happens when a sound simply doesn't exist in your language. Even the fact that speakers of other languages may hear it as an S sound was wild to me. After learning it in a similar fashion, I could exercise to the point of it becoming very clear to me when it's used.<br /> <br /> People learning Portuguese usually have this problem with the \u00c3O sound, just to be clear that this isn't an &quot;English&quot; thing, but rather every language will have this kind of &quot;barrier&quot; for every other language, if not always the same barriers for any given language.<br /> <br /> Newscaster accents are usually a good entry point. In fact most language courses focus on this kind of accent or a slightly more didactic version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T11:01:43-07:00","id":1553102,"title":"","content":"I know a few professors that moved to the US and really struggled when they realized that the US lacks even a de facto didactic accent that they could learn for teaching and academic discussions first, and then pick up local flavor as time went on. I practically half-taught one of my classes because I was the only student with lots of experience with talking with Chinese immigrants so I already internalized a lot of the words/phonemes that tend to be barriers.<br /> <br /> I also grew up studying enough Hebrew to deal with the fact that it has a few consonants that don't exist in English (or do, but only in borrow words and in phoneme structures that can be difficult to generalize out from).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T11:33:08-07:00","id":1553106,"title":"","content":"I meant In My Experience Monteparnas. I was using Internet shorthand slang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T19:54:45-07:00","id":1553153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553106#post1553106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant In My Experience Monteparnas. I was using Internet shorthand slang.</div> </div> </div> </div>The N got me by surprise, sorry. I thought it could be that, but when I tried to look out in the internet for INME it only returned other things, and my Autistic mind really stuck with the idea that you were talking about something else I wasn't understanding.<br /> <br /> On another note, while I saw it a week ago, I want to share this video, which in a sense is a vent, and one directly about our hobby:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5BRLn2Ii4Rc\" data-code=\"5BRLn2Ii4Rc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5BRLn2Ii4Rc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T20:56:19-07:00","id":1553158,"title":"","content":"Not just about our hobby... Eddy Webb is a cited source in the video and he makes games that have their own forums here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T04:28:29-07:00","id":1553322,"title":"","content":"Really worried about my cat. He\u2019s twenty years old and in poor health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T13:51:42-07:00","id":1553347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553322#post1553322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really worried about my cat. He\u2019s twenty years old and in poor health.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really feel for you.<br /> <br /> One of my cats is 11 and I already worry about when things will start to go down (they didn't, yet).<br /> <br /> But 20 is quite an age for a cat so... congrats on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T17:47:44-07:00","id":1553356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553347#post1553347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really feel for you.<br /> <br /> One of my cats is 11 and I already worry about when things will start to go down (they didn't, yet).<br /> <br /> But 20 is quite an age for a cat so... congrats on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I really appreciate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T21:46:52-07:00","id":1553362,"title":"","content":"I recently finished watching a documentary on the Wrestling family The Von Erich's who hailed from Texas and it's heartbreaking to see how much tradegy one family can go through. <br /> <br /> Kevin Von Erich went from having 6 brothers to being the only one left and still grieving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T11:24:00-07:00","id":1553543,"title":"","content":"I'll have to hold on all my games for a time for a horrible reason.<br /> <br /> One of my players, and DM of the game I play in, got Guillain\u2013Barr\u00e9 syndrome. What a luck.<br /> <br /> He fortunately got help (and the correct diagnosis) sooner rather than later, so it may be that he gets better in less than 6 months. I can only pray for his health by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-30T09:00:22-07:00","id":1553554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553543#post1553543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to hold on all my games for a time for a horrible reason.<br /> <br /> One of my players, and DM of the game I play in, got Guillain\u2013Barr\u00e9 syndrome. What a luck.<br /> <br /> He fortunately got help (and the correct diagnosis) sooner rather than later, so it may be that he gets better in less than 6 months. I can only pray for his health by now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh whoa, that's a little scary! Glad they got some help early... hopefully everything goes ok for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-31T06:00:35-07:00","id":1553563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553554#post1553554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh whoa, that's a little scary! Glad they got some help early... hopefully everything goes ok for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been at his house last night with the rest of the group, to commemorate his birthday with a barbecue (a Brazilian one, just to be clear). He's recovering already, so good signs for now. But even if everything goes well it's expected that his recovery will plateau in the next days and get slower, as is normal for the syndrome. With luck he'll by then be good enough to go back to our games (he really needs it more than me), so he'll have his RPG fix while waiting for full recovery.<br /> <br /> But if things don't go so well, then it may be several months before we can go back to our schedule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T13:30:12-07:00","id":1553592,"title":"","content":"Rabies cases are up in the US... and the only data supported suspect is vaccine &quot;skepticism&quot; for... canine vaccines. Enough people are worried about potential vaccine side effects in dogs... that a virus that is nearly universally fatal is getting worse...<br /> <br /> I just... what the fuck.... if your dog lives 15 years to see a side effect congrats! Your dog is geriatric by canine standards and didn't die from one of the most painful and horrific endemic mammalian viruses in North America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T13:57:41-07:00","id":1553593,"title":"","content":"It's amazing that viruses that we didn't have to deal with because of vaccines that were invented in our parents time is coming back because antivaxers believed of a discredited study twenty some odd years ago with Jenny McCarthy being the spokesperson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T18:17:09-07:00","id":1553597,"title":"","content":"Measles, Polio, Rabies, Mumps, Pertussis, Chicken Pox, Rubella, Diphtheria, those are all on the rise or risking a comeback in the US.<br /> <br /> I'd like to say that's why vaccines should be both obligatory and given freely by the state, and in fact I do think it should, but you can't easily make up for popular support. We're seeing this problem here, too, as the political polarization absorbed vaccination stances.<br /> <br /> Brazil isn't yet in as bad a situation on the vaccination front as the US, but it's getting close, and the future seems bleak if this trend doesn't reverts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T20:57:34-07:00","id":1553598,"title":"","content":"It's good that your friend is recovering from Gillian- Barre Monteparnas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T21:34:37-07:00","id":1553600,"title":"","content":"I think the thing that gets under my skin the most with rabies vs. the general threat to public health that the anti-vaxx movement has led to, is that vaccines are currently our only defense against it. There's no drugs to take once you're infected that will fight it off, no treatment regimen to endure the symptoms while your body fights the disease, or anything like that. Once you're infected, you've entered the absolute worst lottery ever because you need to hit a perfect jackpot just to survive; and survival means horrific pain and suffering with likely life-long impairments.<br /> <br /> We also can't ever just get rid of rabies; even if we get better medicines in the future. The ease at which it spreads between mammals means anything short of wiping out our entire ecosystem will leave rabies viruses around to reinfect wildlife and that will eventually get back to us. <br /> <br /> Strong vaccine programs are the best thing to do for so many diseases no human alive today should have to struggle with, but at least we have alternatives. We can save lives and reduce suffering in less efficient and less economic ways if we have to. Rabies? It's vaccination or nothing... and we don't even vaccinate most humans because the primary vector for transmission to humans are pets. I don't mean to be callous, I love my pets as family, and I make sure they get their shots because I believe the risk-reward is a no-brainer for their health and happiness. But as I said before, most potential vaccine complications are just medically less risk because most pets don't live that long compared to humans. If you have pets like some birds or tortoises that can match (or beat) humans for longevity, yes, it changes your math on how to measure risk... but that's not what's driving this nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T21:56:19-07:00","id":1553601,"title":"","content":"It's just crazy that in barely 25 years we are seeing people not giving themselves and their families vaccines because of a loud minority who peddle ridiculous conspiracy theories or point to rising stats for autism because of said vaccination and don't ask how the numbers came to be.<br /> <br /> I learned that the rise of austim was that some neurological disorders were reclassified because it fit under the general diagnosis. But you won't hear that as it would ruin the narrative that they are trying to spin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-03-2025, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T18:41:33-07:00","id":1553616,"title":"","content":"Overall the rise of Autism statistics come from Autism becoming easier to diagnose, plus some changes in how we diagnose it, yes. There's no indicator whatsoever that the actual frequency is changing significantly.<br /> <br /> And I don't think it fair to reduce the entire anti-vaxx movement to this single argument, it's important to understand this isn't about Autism. While this bogus study answered for the biggest swell in their numbers in recent decades (but not the current one), the bigger picture is something else entirely, and the arguments behind it are far more varied.<br /> <br /> Historically anti-vaxxers are as old as variolation, which means they're older than actual vaccines. And the arguments vary wildly, but ultimately mostly fit in three general types: confusion, distrust and politically induced bias.<br /> <br /> Confusion is pretty common. Doctors aren't the only ones telling people what to believe. And when you have two people you trust telling you conflicting things, choosing what to follow isn't that simple, especially when your health is at risk. The result is people trying to make what they think are the best decisions they can under a barrage of conflicting data. And Doctors aren't completely in the right, either. For example, vaccines have problems, they have risks of all kinds and limitations. Now, <b>I know</b> the benefits far outweigh the risks, but doctors frequently minimize or deny the actual risks out of fear that people will avoid vaccines if they misunderstand the message, which isn't an unfounded fear either. But when people find out that there are actual data for the risks those doctors are denying, believing the doctors themselves becomes quite harder.<br /> <br /> Distrust can have a lot of sources. Many people distrust authority figures by default. Many distrust anything that come from outside their communities and isn't supported by their leaders. Others distrust anything they can't (think they) completely understand and fit in their theory of the world. People distrust new things, things they can't see, complicated things, numbers, there's a lot people can distrust. This has been one of the hardest barriers for vaccine acceptance ever. Take Afghanistan, where vaccination dropped after Bin-Laden was captured, because it became known that his capture came by US agents infiltrating vaccination programs to secretly take DNA samples from children related to him. Think about all the people around that distrust their government and their intentions. Or about the people that are used to law enforcement in their area being more of an enemy than safety.<br /> <br /> We had a situation here in Brazil, 120 years ago, when tensions escalated to the point of open violence in the streets, a week-long riot that included even a coup d'\u00e9tat attempt, because of a law for mandatory vaccination, an event known as the Revolta da Vacina (Vaccine Revolt). It's frequently told with comic undertones as to make fun of &quot;the ignorance of that people&quot;, but this hugely misinterprets the general state of the relationship between the common Rio de Janeiro population and their authorities, and how much mistrust was building due to mistreatment and mishandling of social concerns. When officials come to raze your house before your eyes and remove your family from the premises, without much explanation besides &quot;sanitary reforms&quot;, it doesn't sound so farfetched that the government would poison you for its own interests.<br /> <br /> But the big villain today is politically induced bias. Unfortunately, around the world political parties embraced vaccination or its negation as political stances. That just can't go well.<br /> <br /> I do understand <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> special problem with Rabies, though. It's another level entirely. Almost 60k people die each year of Rabies around the world, plus unreported cases (estimated around 15k). It's one of the most certain causes of death known to humanity. Symptoms can begin anything between a week and several months after infection, and when they do, you're a goner. The single treatment available has been around since 2004 and saved a whopping number of 5 people. 5, total, in 21 years. Even then the process was royally painful, they stayed in hospital for years and carry severe aftereffects for life. Without this treatment your chances of survival are above 0% only in the strict sense that it is technically impossible to affirm, it may be that you can survive Rabies, we just never saw a single case even in legend through the whole human history. So that's it, we have vaccines, the Milwaukee Protocol, and a statistical imperative as options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T14:45:01-07:00","id":1553625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553563#post1553563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been at his house last night with the rest of the group, to commemorate his birthday with a barbecue (a Brazilian one, just to be clear). He's recovering already, so good signs for now. But even if everything goes well it's expected that his recovery will plateau in the next days and get slower, as is normal for the syndrome. With luck he'll by then be good enough to go back to our games (he really needs it more than me), so he'll have his RPG fix while waiting for full recovery.<br /> <br /> But if things don't go so well, then it may be several months before we can go back to our schedule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh nice!! Glad to hear he recovering ok!<br /> <br /> Hopefully everything can get back to normal soon..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553592#post1553592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rabies cases are up in the US... and the only data supported suspect is vaccine &quot;skepticism&quot; for... canine vaccines. Enough people are worried about potential vaccine side effects in dogs... that a virus that is nearly universally fatal is getting worse...<br /> <br /> I just... what the fuck.... if your dog lives 15 years to see a side effect congrats! Your dog is geriatric by canine standards and didn't die from one of the most painful and horrific endemic mammalian viruses in North America.</div> </div> </div> </div>It boggles my mind how stupid some people can be. I do not get all this antivax rhetoric, it's so crazy to me.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553600#post1553600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the thing that gets under my skin the most with rabies vs. the general threat to public health that the anti-vaxx movement has led to, is that vaccines are currently our only defense against it. There's no drugs to take once you're infected that will fight it off, no treatment regimen to endure the symptoms while your body fights the disease, or anything like that. Once you're infected, you've entered the absolute worst lottery ever because you need to hit a perfect jackpot just to survive; and survival means horrific pain and suffering with likely life-long impairments.<br /> <br /> We also can't ever just get rid of rabies; even if we get better medicines in the future. The ease at which it spreads between mammals means anything short of wiping out our entire ecosystem will leave rabies viruses around to reinfect wildlife and that will eventually get back to us.<br /> <br /> Strong vaccine programs are the best thing to do for so many diseases no human alive today should have to struggle with, but at least we have alternatives. We can save lives and reduce suffering in less efficient and less economic ways if we have to. Rabies? It's vaccination or nothing... and we don't even vaccinate most humans because the primary vector for transmission to humans are pets. I don't mean to be callous, I love my pets as family, and I make sure they get their shots because I believe the risk-reward is a no-brainer for their health and happiness. But as I said before, most potential vaccine complications are just medically less risk because most pets don't live that long compared to humans. If you have pets like some birds or tortoises that can match (or beat) humans for longevity, yes, it changes your math on how to measure risk... but that's not what's driving this nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well said. And I'm totally with you. Vaccines are some of the best things we have to fight all these diseases, so I just don't understand why people wouldn't want that! It's crazy!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T22:23:09-07:00","id":1553635,"title":"","content":"Oh I agree that the discredited study from 25 years ago wasn't the sole cause for anti vaccine activists, but it certainly helped paved the way for what we saw in recent years with the political warfare when Covid happened and we had a vaccine created and these people spread falsehoods and I admit that I have a personal dislike for them as my parents got sick with the delta strain of Covid because they wouldn't get vaccinated or practice social distancing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T01:00:14-07:00","id":1553636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553635#post1553635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I agree that the discredited study from 25 years ago wasn't the sole cause for anti vaccine activists, but it certainly helped paved the way for what we saw in recent years with the political warfare when Covid happened</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't think it played a major role.<br /> <br /> What happened during Covid (and it happened all around the world) was that social distancing and other actual measures that could be taken would impact economic policies in course, and a lot of politicians didn't want that to happen. They denied the gravity of the situation at first just to justify not doing stuff that would compromise their political positions. Those politicians were almost always right-wing, but that's not really the point.<br /> <br /> From that their opposition jumped to the opportunity to make them look as &quot;anti-science&quot; and make &quot;good science&quot; a political stance, hopping to capitalize on it. I personally blame the Left for doing it, even being left-wing myself, because that was what really stoked the fires of this lunacy, turning health science (vaccines just came along) into a part of political polarization. Only then anti-vaxx nut-jobs got to be accepted in the halls of power.<br /> <br /> And for a lot of them, especially the most dangerous ones, the supposed risk of autism is just one more in a long list of ludicrous accusations. It wasn't the first, the last or particularly important. It was just the most visible theory at the time outside of the Conspiracy Theory circuit. If anything the biggest problem is the idea that it's the delivery system for the Mark of the Beast, in number of people affected, followed by any variant of &quot;the government will spy on us through it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T04:02:05-07:00","id":1553637,"title":"","content":"While trying to tiptoe around the rules of the thread, I'd just point out that science got politicized a long time ago. This might be a bit of an US bias, but in every country science costs capital in some form or another. Who gets the resources and how has been a political football on all sorts of topics for my entire life.<br /> <br /> I feel like COVID was far more a catalyst for deepening political divides and tribalism that were festering but hadn't dominated governing completely. There used to be more issues where you could get some people from one side, and some people from the other side, to agree that on this issue they agreed and then you could get some traction on that issue at least.<br /> <br /> A good example was the in the US was that the very weird US gun culture associated with the right used to ally a lot with the environmental activists associated with the left: gun culture used to be oriented a lot more around hunting - and hunting requires big protected natural spaces - and more protections for old growth forests is good in environmentalist books. But that overlap in interests can't compete with the polarization that's occurred. <br /> <br /> I think you're right about how COVID pushed the anti-vaxx movement from what used to be a fringe left-associated phenomena to a mainstream right-associated one, but I'm not sure history really supports the idea that the politicization of science really started a few years ago. It seems far more likely that existing social fractures just got worse than something truly new occurred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T06:36:29-07:00","id":1553640,"title":"","content":"I was focusing on how it happened in the specific context of COVID/Anti-vaxx, in part because it made a stark divide where science is almost completely in one side and pseudoscience almost completely in the other, especially health sciences. Note that I'm not talking <i>scientists</i>, good and bad ones can be at either side for whatever reasons, although at least some <b>are</b> facing this weird pressure to side with political views they wouldn't otherwise, to defend their scientific stance.<br /> <br /> Science has been politicized since it exists. While the effort to disentangle itself from politics is part and parcel for the scientific method, the method isn't the whole of the law and politics both use and influence science in myriad ways.<br /> <br /> But that's usually limited in scope and specific to each situation. Politicians capitalizing on fear raised by either kind of science is common. They ultimately define where a lot of financing goes, both as in to which research topics as in to which specific hypotheses. Even without pseudoscience or actual politicians in the way, politics may affect which studies get more attention and which policies derive from a study (there's an interesting, longstanding story about the screening of women in their 40s for breast cancer). Science is affected all the time, and there <b>is</b> politics in Academia, both as a reflection of larger politics and internal politics.<br /> <br /> And unfortunately I don't think that's US bias on your part. Specifics vary as always, but overall this is an everywhere problem with science. What COVID brought, though, was a remarkable and strong association in most of the world between anti-vaxx and mainstream right-wing, to the point of actual conspiracy theorists becoming health officials without any credentials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T11:23:39-07:00","id":1553643,"title":"","content":"I love conspiracy theories in general Monteparnas. They are so exciting to read and listen to and see the flaws in the argument. I mean such grand cabals have a degree of control and skill that is impossible to work in the real world or that it's all unfounded rumors.<br /> <br /> For instance the Covid vaccine idea of being used to keep track of your actions. I don't think that would be a problem with a cellphone glued to your ear or having credit and debit cards and being online gives more than enough information about you.<br /> <br /> I remember some of the 9/11 craziness with how it was inside job. Sorry the steel in the buildings didn't melt and noone in authority claimed it, but when you have two aircrafts coming at high speeds crashing into the world towers and damaging the support structures and add in the fires of the crash and what it's typically in a office building. That's more than enough to further weaken the structure holding it up <br /> <br /> I remember telling some people that Conspiracy theories are almost like a religion for some folks and many agreed it was a fair assessment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-05-2025, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T13:07:25-07:00","id":1553645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553637#post1553637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While trying to tiptoe around the rules of the thread, I'd just point out that science got politicized a long time ago. This might be a bit of an US bias, but in every country science costs capital in some form or another. Who gets the resources and how has been a political football on all sorts of topics for my entire life.<br /> <br /> I feel like COVID was far more a catalyst for deepening political divides and tribalism that were festering but hadn't dominated governing completely. There used to be more issues where you could get some people from one side, and some people from the other side, to agree that on this issue they agreed and then you could get some traction on that issue at least.<br /> <br /> A good example was the in the US was that the very weird US gun culture associated with the right used to ally a lot with the environmental activists associated with the left: gun culture used to be oriented a lot more around hunting - and hunting requires big protected natural spaces - and more protections for old growth forests is good in environmentalist books. But that overlap in interests can't compete with the polarization that's occurred.<br /> <br /> I think you're right about how COVID pushed the anti-vaxx movement from what used to be a fringe left-associated phenomena to a mainstream right-associated one, but I'm not sure history really supports the idea that the politicization of science really started a few years ago. It seems far more likely that existing social fractures just got worse than something truly new occurred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you (again)! Seems my whole life science has been politicized... but, for a long time at least it seem most people trusted science (for the most part)! It's only been in recent years where there seems to be this huge anti-science sentiment, even among our elected officials. It's crazy!<br /> <br /> And yea, it's so strange to me how the whole anit-vax movement sprang up and then got co-oped by right wing grifters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553640#post1553640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was focusing on how it happened in the specific context of COVID/Anti-vaxx, in part because it made a stark divide where science is almost completely in one side and pseudoscience almost completely in the other, especially health sciences. Note that I'm not talking <i>scientists</i>, good and bad ones can be at either side for whatever reasons, although at least some <b>are</b> facing this weird pressure to side with political views they wouldn't otherwise, to defend their scientific stance.<br /> <br /> Science has been politicized since it exists. While the effort to disentangle itself from politics is part and parcel for the scientific method, the method isn't the whole of the law and politics both use and influence science in myriad ways.<br /> <br /> But that's usually limited in scope and specific to each situation. Politicians capitalizing on fear raised by either kind of science is common. They ultimately define where a lot of financing goes, both as in to which research topics as in to which specific hypotheses. Even without pseudoscience or actual politicians in the way, politics may affect which studies get more attention and which policies derive from a study (there's an interesting, longstanding story about the screening of women in their 40s for breast cancer). Science is affected all the time, and there <b>is</b> politics in Academia, both as a reflection of larger politics and internal politics.<br /> <br /> And unfortunately I don't think that's US bias on your part. Specifics vary as always, but overall this is an everywhere problem with science. What COVID brought, though, was a remarkable and strong association in most of the world between anti-vaxx and mainstream right-wing, to the point of actual conspiracy theorists becoming health officials without any credentials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I have much to add, but I did want to say that during the start of Covid people got to see Science in action, and for some reason they completely misunderstood it. There is a scientific method, and I don''t think most people actually see that, so it got mistaken for scientists &quot;not knowing what they're doing&quot;. But, that probably plays more into the education system (or lack thereof) more than anything.<br /> <br /> Hell, you have people like RFK Jr. telling people they shouldn't trust the experts. What the hell!?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553643#post1553643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love conspiracy theories in general Monteparnas. They are so exciting to read and listen to and see the flaws in the argument. I mean such grand cabals have a degree of control and skill that is impossible to work in the real world or that it's all unfounded rumors.<br /> <br /> For instance the Covid vaccine idea of being used to keep track of your actions. I don't think that would be a problem with a cellphone glued to your ear or having credit and debit cards and being online gives more than enough information about you.<br /> <br /> I remember some of the 9/11 craziness with how it was inside job. Sorry the steel in the buildings didn't melt and noone in authority claimed it, but when you have two aircrafts coming at high speeds crashing into the world towers and damaging the support structures and add in the fires of the crash and what it's typically in a office building. That's more than enough to further weaken the structure holding it up<br /> <br /> I remember telling some people that Conspiracy theories are almost like a religion for some folks and many agreed it was a fair assessment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conspiracy theories can be fun to read, so long is it's understood that it's basically fiction. Sometimes people get a little too into them though, and that's when the problems start.<br /> <br /> But who doesn't love a good conspiracy theory sometimes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, this reminds me. Yeeears ago I was super into all the JFK assassination conspiracies. Not that I really believed them, but there was a lot of weirdness, so it seemed like something was up. But then, I saw a documentary that explained the &quot;magic bullet&quot; and pointed out the actual orientation of the seats in the limo, and then it all made sense how a single bullet can do it... no magic or alternate shooters needed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T13:10:40-07:00","id":1553646,"title":"","content":"I think the core appeal of conspiracy theories is that the grant a sense of control in a world where very little is under our direct control; which is where I think the overlap with religious psychology lives. Even if you can't change things, you can at least know The Truth and expose it as an act of assertion to push back against the pessimism reality can crush people with.<br /> <br /> The fact that the vast majority of conspiracy theories seem to always circle back around to anti-Semitic tropes makes them far less amusing for me though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T13:20:48-07:00","id":1553647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553643#post1553643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember telling some people that Conspiracy theories are almost like a religion for some folks and many agreed it was a fair assessment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conspiracy Theories are a complex phenomenon that I find fascinating as a Psychologist and from the perspectives of social sciences. They're also obviously a horrible social problem. And yes, it is actually really close to religion as a psychological phenomenon. It fosters community, a sense of profound understanding, it stirs and feeds emotions, has rites of sorts, there are indeed a lot of connections. Unfortunately not just with &quot;regular&quot; religion, but also with the worse definition of a &quot;cult&quot;, there's pressure, isolation, exhaustion, it keeps the person in constant activity within the &quot;cult&quot; and ever more segregated from the outside world.<br /> <br /> It has also a lot of similar people in leadership, although this is far less visible in CT. But believe, they're there, feeding the process and guiding the victims.<br /> <br /> What makes Conspiracy Theories hard to fight, though, is that conspiracies are real. Conspiracies are a thing that happen IRL, even if not at such terrible scale. And sometimes it's big nonetheless, like the Phoebus Cartel that imposed a hard limit on lamp's lifespans through the whole of Europe and North America (and by controlling those factories, most of the world, period) for 14 years, and whose policies mostly remained in effect after that for more than six decades (until incandescent bulbs got mostly phased out). Apple was accused of not simply making the iPhone less durable, but actively sabotage it to destroy the battery after 1 year, and <u><b>it ended up being true</b></u>. They got caught and were forbidden from doing that, but only in 2017 and the question was still being fought in the justice in some countries at least until 2020, while they were doing that since who-know's-when, probably the beginning, which would mean a 10-year long conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Those things happen. Most elaborate crimes are conspiracies. Many simple crimes are still conspiracies. There are theories about conspiracies that are actually well though, even if sometimes hard to believe, and sometimes actually true. Heck, systemic racism is the direct result of a conspiracy and fuels a lot of conspiracies, and that isn't really all that uncommon. Antisemitism fuels conspiracies, ironically justified on ludicrous Conspiracy Theories\u2122.<br /> <br /> But what makes a Conspiracy Theory\u2122 &quot;special&quot; is not just the scope of it, but how it justifies any weak spot with more complex claims (generally, but not always, outlandish), how it makes bold claims about social groups and fields of work the theorist has no real connection with (be it &quot;Muslims&quot; or &quot;Doctors&quot; or &quot;Physicists&quot;), and usually how many and varied people it claims to be &quot;in the know&quot;, as if it were possible to make any worldwide group of people united by something as flimsy as &quot;going to college&quot; (<i><b>any</b></i> college) to be so united in thought that 99% of them know a secret and keep it secret. Not to say they're impossibly efficient.<br /> <br /> More important, though, what makes the Conspiracy Theory\u2122 is the Conspiracy <u><b>Theorist</b></u>, the person under the cult sway, and how this person explains, justifies and builds upon the Theory, with selective data, huge amounts of logical fallacies (small amounts of logical fallacies are normal, everyone does that naturally, we have to policy ourselves), arbitrary selection of sources, and a lot, a huge fucking lot of <b>PASSION</b>.<br /> <br /> Real conspiracies take effort to identify and analyze, and you have to be always careful with the data you get and to read what it really says, not what you want it to say, even if it means getting you to completely unexpected conclusions or just the conclusion that there was no conspiracy. And even when there are, they're far less intricate and efficient than Conspiracies\u2122. By the way, if you look into any of the real conspiracies I cited, while they're impressive in their own right, the details are actually quite mundane, even pedestrian, and a lot of their effectiveness come from outside forces or tendencies rather than any extraordinary organization job.<br /> <br /> Yes, I think I can say I love Conspiracies, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T14:19:29-07:00","id":1553648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553645#post1553645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">during the start of Covid people got to see Science in action, and for some reason they completely misunderstood it. There is a scientific method, and I don''t think most people actually see that, so it got mistaken for scientists &quot;not knowing what they're doing&quot;. But, that probably plays more into the education system (or lack thereof) more than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>People misunderstand the Scientific Method with scientists &quot;not knowing what they're doing&quot; since always, that's unfortunately normal, and still not something we have an easy fix for, even education isn't that guaranteed. It helps, certainly, and the US doesn't have the best system around (not that Brazil does), but far from a guarantee. Actually, how to turn education into &quot;scientific literacy&quot; is still a huge challenge in education (you know, besides all the political and financial challenges, and that's all so depressing).<br /> <br /> Authority figures actually have a huge, and I mean a <b>huge</b> impact. Public servants, politicians, religious figures, community leaders, those are actually the people that must either be scientifically literate, or at the very least well informed, because their confidence in the work of scientists is what really spreads this confidence over their communities. This is so, so important, and it's sad that scientists frequently dismiss exactly those people in their communication efforts because they're focused on trying to feed people with hard-to-understand data.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553645#post1553645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But who doesn't love a good conspiracy theory sometimes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I frequently go back to Moon Landing Denial. Most of them don't really make a lot of sense, but the core idea is so realistic. Because the Space Race was overall an astounding failure for the US until that point, and the Space Program was such a drainage of money. The Soviets did absolutely everything before the US up until that point. So even if the technology was available, the whole plan feasible, even then it would make sense to fake an earlier landing for propaganda reasons.<br /> <br /> Of course, it simply isn't true. Not only do we have all the proof for the landing, enacting a good enough forgery would be actually orders of magnitude harder to make at the time given the scrutiny around it. And the reasons didn't all existed, either. The Moon Landing was glorified over all other achievements just because it was the one who was ahead of the Soviets, it was pure propaganda, but the idea that it was more important than any other point of the Race was completely made up, it's an arbitrary goal set after the fact, so it wouldn't make any sense to go to this length just then, nor did it end the Space Race.<br /> <br /> The Space Race at first was about strategic exploration of space technology. It was about gathering data, learning to make use of space for communications and several other things, and while it soon became clear that it wouldn't be a lot about weapons, of course it was about weapons. With time the propaganda aspect grew, until it surpassed the strategic aspect, and after the Landing it faded again behind strategy. Faking the Moon Landing is a tricky propaganda move when you have an active enemy seeking ways to prove you're a fraud, and mostly useless from a technological/strategic standpoint. And finally there was science, that didn't care about television shows either, but really for the governments it was a means to an end, even if for the actual scientists and engineers in both space agencies the science was the whole point.<br /> <br /> And the race would go on for a few more years, the Apollo program alone would have 6 more missions (plus 3 scrapped missions, I think) ending in 1972. Only after that would the funding for NASA begin to decline. Usually the end of the Space Race is roughly marked at 1975 with the Apollo-Soyuz mission, a joint effort between the US and the USSR, but it's hard to say it really ceased. In a lot of ways it remained for the rest of the Cold War, and reignited with Putin's ascension and the return of Russia to its position as a global powerhouse. It's pretty alive today, I'd say.<br /> <br /> My, I really have a problem being succinct...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T15:12:51-07:00","id":1553649,"title":"","content":"Fair point Heavy Arms about the antisemitic themes showing up in conspiracy theories such as 9/11 where they claim that no people of Jewish ancestry died and were told to stay away. Strange that they could never find the people who &quot;survived&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T15:16:33-07:00","id":1553650,"title":"","content":"I love the We didn't land on the Moon theory and it was a Hollywood production. They could never explain how it could be kept secret at all in any strong detail.<br /> <br /> It's easy to fake it, but how would you keep everyone quiet? We as a species are really bad at keeping things secret and we are not as smart and skilled as we think we are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T15:34:14-07:00","id":1553652,"title":"","content":"I remember how Penn and Teller did a report on JFK and how the magic bullet wasn't magical and it was how the people in the motorcade were seated Mr. Gone.<br /> <br /> One of my personal favorites is the Clinton Kill Count Conspiracy. Essentially anyone who has a tenous connection to Bill and Hillary that have passed away over the years were really murdered in a way that wouldn't draw suspicion. Most of the people they spotlightted in their stories were shown that they did die from what was the official cause of death.<br /> <br /> Never do they explain how Ann Coulter, Kenneth Start, Newt Gingrich and the late Rush Limbaugh were spared from what was cleverly disguised assassinations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T20:24:33-07:00","id":1553657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553650#post1553650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's easy to fake it, but how would you keep everyone quiet? We as a species are really bad at keeping things secret and we are not as smart and skilled as we think we are.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't even that easy to fake it, not in context. It's easy to make a realistic footage that fool's the average viewer, but this footage has to fool actual specialists all across the world, including legions of eager scientists, interested filmmakers, <b>and a fucking enemy super-potency with state-of-the-art technology</b>, just ready to take on any opportunity to morally beat the US to the ground.<br /> <br /> So faking it <i>well enough</i> wasn't easy at all. The know-how and resources to bust it wasn't just plentiful, the scrutiny was out of this world and precisely by the people with the know-how, resources and invested interest in finding out what's really going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T20:54:04-07:00","id":1553659,"title":"","content":"That was brought up also Monteparnas and seriously it wouldn't be feasible as there would be enough experts and talented amateurs astronomers that would see through it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T06:02:07-07:00","id":1553666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553646#post1553646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the core appeal of conspiracy theories is that the grant a sense of control in a world where very little is under our direct control; which is where I think the overlap with religious psychology lives. Even if you can't change things, you can at least know The Truth and expose it as an act of assertion to push back against the pessimism reality can crush people with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I hear ya! It does seem to give people a sense of control by having &quot;knowledge&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553646#post1553646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the vast majority of conspiracy theories seem to always circle back around to anti-Semitic tropes makes them far less amusing for me though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ugh. Don't even get me started... it's messed up!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553648#post1553648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People misunderstand the Scientific Method with scientists &quot;not knowing what they're doing&quot; since always, that's unfortunately normal, and still not something we have an easy fix for, even education isn't that guaranteed. It helps, certainly, and the US doesn't have the best system around (not that Brazil does), but far from a guarantee. Actually, how to turn education into &quot;scientific literacy&quot; is still a huge challenge in education (you know, besides all the political and financial challenges, and that's all so depressing).<br /> <br /> Authority figures actually have a huge, and I mean a <b>huge</b> impact. Public servants, politicians, religious figures, community leaders, those are actually the people that must either be scientifically literate, or at the very least well informed, because their confidence in the work of scientists is what really spreads this confidence over their communities. This is so, so important, and it's sad that scientists frequently dismiss exactly those people in their communication efforts because they're focused on trying to feed people with hard-to-understand data.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I hear. People have always misunderstood it, but for whatever reason it seemed worse to me during 2020 where more people saw it in action and were totally confounded by it. It's crazy..<br /> <br /> But yes, we could do with some better education...and some better authority figures who understand science and can help communicate it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553648#post1553648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I frequently go back to Moon Landing Denial. Most of them don't really make a lot of sense, but the core idea is so realistic. Because the Space Race was overall an astounding failure for the US until that point, and the Space Program was such a drainage of money. The Soviets did absolutely everything before the US up until that point. So even if the technology was available, the whole plan feasible, even then it would make sense to fake an earlier landing for propaganda reasons.<br /> <br /> Of course, it simply isn't true. Not only do we have all the proof for the landing, enacting a good enough forgery would be actually orders of magnitude harder to make at the time given the scrutiny around it. And the reasons didn't all existed, either. The Moon Landing was glorified over all other achievements just because it was the one who was ahead of the Soviets, it was pure propaganda, but the idea that it was more important than any other point of the Race was completely made up, it's an arbitrary goal set after the fact, so it wouldn't make any sense to go to this length just then, nor did it end the Space Race.<br /> <br /> The Space Race at first was about strategic exploration of space technology. It was about gathering data, learning to make use of space for communications and several other things, and while it soon became clear that it wouldn't be a lot about weapons, of course it was about weapons. With time the propaganda aspect grew, until it surpassed the strategic aspect, and after the Landing it faded again behind strategy. Faking the Moon Landing is a tricky propaganda move when you have an active enemy seeking ways to prove you're a fraud, and mostly useless from a technological/strategic standpoint. And finally there was science, that didn't care about television shows either, but really for the governments it was a means to an end, even if for the actual scientists and engineers in both space agencies the science was the whole point.<br /> <br /> And the race would go on for a few more years, the Apollo program alone would have 6 more missions (plus 3 scrapped missions, I think) ending in 1972. Only after that would the funding for NASA begin to decline. Usually the end of the Space Race is roughly marked at 1975 with the Apollo-Soyuz mission, a joint effort between the US and the USSR, but it's hard to say it really ceased. In a lot of ways it remained for the rest of the Cold War, and reignited with Putin's ascension and the return of Russia to its position as a global powerhouse. It's pretty alive today, I'd say.<br /> <br /> My, I really have a problem being succinct...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I know I use the word a lot, but all the moon landing conspiracy theories are so crazy to me! LOL. How anything could think a conspiracy that big wouldn't crack under it's own weight is beyond me.<br /> <br /> And just to say, I think it's really sad we cut the NASA budget so badly that we stopped going to the moon. I get that it's super challenging, but if we'd keep up the missions and research who knows where we'd be right now...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553650#post1553650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the We didn't land on the Moon theory and it was a Hollywood production. They could never explain how it could be kept secret at all in any strong detail.<br /> <br /> It's easy to fake it, but how would you keep everyone quiet? We as a species are really bad at keeping things secret and we are not as smart and skilled as we think we are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get this! I knew a guy who thought we faked the initial moon landing, but then thought we did eventually go to the moon when it looked like other countries might go so we could plant all the evidence of the initial faked landing. LOL!<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553652#post1553652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember how Penn and Teller did a report on JFK and how the magic bullet wasn't magical and it was how the people in the motorcade were seated Mr. Gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool Penn and Teller did an episode on it. I saw it in a documentary series, and once they laid it all out, it made perfect sense! If you're interested, I'll see if I can track it down..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553652#post1553652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my personal favorites is the Clinton Kill Count Conspiracy. Essentially anyone who has a tenous connection to Bill and Hillary that have passed away over the years were really murdered in a way that wouldn't draw suspicion. Most of the people they spotlightted in their stories were shown that they did die from what was the official cause of death.<br /> <br /> Never do they explain how Ann Coulter, Kenneth Start, Newt Gingrich and the late Rush Limbaugh were spared from what was cleverly disguised assassinations?</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL! I hadn't heard that one before...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T10:50:06-07:00","id":1553673,"title":"","content":"It's a lesser known Conspiracy Theory Mr. Gone about the Clinton's and what you told me about the man who told you their take on the Moon landing hoax is funny.<br /> <br /> Of course there is even funny rumors in entertainment that made me chuckle and cringe sometimes.<br /> <br /> For example there was a rumor in professional wrestling that Jim &quot;Ultimate Warrior&quot; Hellwig died in the late 1980's-early 1990's and the late Kerry Von Erich pretended to be him. <br /> <br /> How did this start? Hellwig after an absence from WWF/WWE returned with shorter hair and a slimmer build and that was enough to start this rumor and it was clearly still the same guy. <br /> <br /> That was the funny rumor. The more cringe one involved the late Randy Savage and Stephenie MacMahon. This rumor implied that he had sex with the bosses daughter who was underaged at the time.<br /> <br /> This has never been proven and most people involved in wrestling don't believe it and it was apparently traced to a website that was in business of spreading rumors. If it was true I'm pretty sure Randy Savage would have been found dead in ditch somewhere with his genitals gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-06-2025, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T14:11:19-07:00","id":1553675,"title":"","content":"While it's a bit of a small bugbear when it comes to the topic of scientific literacy, I find something very emblematic of the larger cultural problem:<br /> <br /> Low stakes science is treated as a joke by mainstream culture.<br /> <br /> For most people that aren't part of a scientific field, the entire concept of &quot;low stakes&quot; science is not something they even consider; despite something everyone intuitively understands the moment you bring it up. You don't trust someone that just finished a pre-med Bachelor's degree with heart surgery. Likewise, you don't trust someone with a Bachelor's degree in a medical research field to run a multi-million dollar facility dedicated to working on cancer treatments. Everyone needs low stakes practical experience to hone their skills and prove to the rest of the world that they should be given serious responsibilities. People in trade jobs need apprenticeships. If you want to be a manager in a retail setting, you have to start in sales. Etc.<br /> <br /> But most people just do not link that to all the studies that get a passing media snicker and a &quot;what about curing cancer?&quot; punchline. Even people with public perceptions as being very pro science, science literacy, and so on still fall into this. Stephen Colbert is an excellent example of someone that's not a scientist, but loves science, and still can't resist the low hanging fruit on mocking some very niche study that - if nothing else came of it - is still a vital tool for training in the science profession.<br /> <br /> A lot of people are also still very caught up in the Great Man Theory of history when it comes to science. Despite science being an inherently collaborative field where anything that actually matters requires lots of and lots of people to do the theoretical work, the practical work, and then the reproduction work, for it to go from an idea to a fact, we think of science in terms of the giants of the field. And even then, a lot of the engineers that turn science into functional technology get a lot of the spotlight as well (not to put them down, but the conflation of the science that shows what we can do, and the people that figure out how to make it work doesn't help people understand what science is really about).<br /> <br /> If we talk about evolution... most people can name Darwin. Maybe they might remember Lamarck if reminded. Do they know about Russel (who's graciousness towards letting Darwin publish first led to Russel getting dubbed the &quot;Darwin of the East&quot; despite him figuring out evolution by natural selection first, proving it fast, and proving it far more conclusively)? Do they know how much Thomas Huxley did to earn the title of &quot;Darwin's Bulldog&quot; in his staunch defense of Darwin's work against social critics and stubborn academics? And that's not even getting into the names of folks like the crew of the Beagle that made Darwin's voyage possible. That's not getting into the almost two centuries of evolutionary scientists that have done immensely important work with the field Darwin broke open.<br /> <br /> Everyone cares about Edison and Tesla... nobody cares about the crew of people that did the work of figuring out the best light bulb filaments. Nobody considers the material science &quot;sexy&quot; or &quot;ground breaking&quot; even though it lit up our world. The men that sat around testing the applications of electricity to animal hairs are a forgotten footnote, and the scientists doing just as vital work today know they're going to end up just as forgotten... and likely far less likely to be respected than the Menlo Park folks were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T16:20:12-07:00","id":1553678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553666#post1553666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have always misunderstood it, but for whatever reason it seemed worse to me during 2020 where more people saw it in action and were totally confounded by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that the political interest meant we had important authority figures actively seeding mistrust and sabotaging scientific dissemination.<br /> <br /> For someone who trusted the right sources and followed the news it was easy to follow the science being done. But for a lot of people the amount of noise was unbearable, and they had figures they trusted telling conflicting interpretations of what was going on.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that there are scientists and scientists. A lot of specialists are still bad-faith actors perfectly willing to sabotage science for personal gains, a lot of pseudoscience is lead by people with actual credentials the general public isn't prepared to evaluate. There was no shortage of actual doctors putting their weight behind politicians siding with science denial and giving a veneer of actual good science to it. When the figure you trust start to have actual professionals with them, what are you expected to believe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553666#post1553666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And just to say, I think it's really sad we cut the NASA budget so badly that we stopped going to the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if going to the moon was all that important. It would probably have stopped anyway, or at least slowed down significantly, even if their budget actually increased.<br /> <br /> But it was surely more interesting for society than redirecting this money back to the already hyper-financed military. A lot more projects could have been conducted, we could know so much more by now. We could have more practical experiences with space tech, leading to even more technological developments in many fields. NASA could have brought international participation in its projects sooner and more intensely, which not only means benefiting the international community, it means more diversity of ideas and interpretations that can greatly haste development.<br /> <br /> We could already have more identified planets in the outskirts of the Solar System, more directly explored objects inside it, more unmanned exploration missions landing in the many planets and moons that are still untouched, and even maybe a few manned missions to a few other places than the moon (maybe even Mars, although I'm skeptical at that as the challenges have only proved ever greater than previously thought).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553666#post1553666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew a guy who thought we faked the initial moon landing, but then thought we did eventually go to the moon when it looked like other countries might go so we could plant all the evidence of the initial faked landing.</div> </div> </div> </div>To his benefit, no other nation ever put an actual person on the moon.<br /> <br /> But that's because this is a lot more trouble than it's worth and unmanned missions do the work better, they're just less exciting. The Soviets actually planted the first flag on the moon all the way back in 1959, so 10 years before the American flag (and in the 21st century India and China followed suit, Israel is planning their own flag mission, too).<br /> <br /> Other countries got to see the evidence of the landing as soon as it happened, actually. It was tracked by several independent observers as it happened, as NASA had fully released the whole schedule of the mission (this was the whole point, for this to be as public as possible). The Soviets abandoned plans for crewed missions precisely because they knew it was real. Heck, by 1972 even schoolchildren with amateur radio systems could track the Apolo-17 mission. The samples brought from the moon are plenty of evidence and they're also available for study by international research institutions (as close to &quot;public&quot; as you can go with sensitive materials). Since the late 2000's direct evidence has only built up, by people that could perfectly verify if it matches dates and stuff to know if it was planted. But those people know nothing, who really know how to analyze this data are Bill from Chicago and Bart from Nashville.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553673#post1553673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example there was a rumor in professional wrestling that Jim &quot;Ultimate Warrior&quot; Hellwig died in the late 1980's-early 1990's and the late Kerry Von Erich pretended to be him.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;They died, this is a pretender!&quot; is an old classic that never fades. Everyone who's anyone will at some point be either the faked or the faker (when the faker is even named), from politicians to youtubers. If you search for &quot;celebrity replacement conspiracy theories&quot; you'll find dozens of them just in the US, and they happen all around the world. Presidents are common targets.<br /> <br /> And of course, it only gets better when you find out that look-a-likes are an actually very common thing. Someone somewhere looks just like you. Probably more than one person. When you're an anonymous person your chances of finding them are small, but even then not by that much, and many people find their &quot;doppelgangers&quot; every year, sometimes befriend them, etc. Sometimes your doppelganger isn't even the same gender and biological sex as you, but you're still almost indistinguishable. When you're famous your look-a-likes may even find their way into low-key fame or make a buck out of it through perfectly legitimate means.<br /> <br /> So, does that has anything to do with the conspiracy theories? Not directly, but it gives &quot;evidence&quot; for the theories as photos of &quot;you&quot; may crop up anywhere at any time.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553675#post1553675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's a bit of a small bugbear when it comes to the topic of scientific literacy, I find something very emblematic of the larger cultural problem:<br /> <br /> Low stakes science is treated as a joke by mainstream culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's so true and so harmful. Not only does it make for a low-hanging fruit for jokes, which is already a problem, it impacts financing, and in many cases furthers bad habits within the very academic community as some departments and researchers feel the pressure to decide on which research to make based on how outlandish they can dress their claims instead of how much it can really produce in terms of actually relevant data (just look at how much news we get about &quot;this research will change everything we know about &lt;topic&gt;&quot; all the time).<br /> <br /> I frequently watch the videos of Sabine Hossenfelder complaining in particular of how this trend completely overtook Particle Physics, with so much expensive research being made that won't really advance anything as meaningfully as it could with a fraction of the budget, making wildly unfounded claims at how impactful it is, just because the researchers fear loosing budget and even their jobs if their public isn't excited enough.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T18:42:23-07:00","id":1553679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553673#post1553673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was the funny rumor. The more cringe one involved the late Randy Savage and Stephenie MacMahon. This rumor implied that he had sex with the bosses daughter who was underaged at the time.<br /> <br /> This has never been proven and most people involved in wrestling don't believe it and it was apparently traced to a website that was in business of spreading rumors. If it was true I'm pretty sure Randy Savage would have been found dead in ditch somewhere with his genitals gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rumor emerged because Macho Man was the one major &quot;Golden Era&quot; WWF star who went to WCW in the 90's and never came back in any way once WCW folded.<br /> <br /> Hulk Hogan, Jimmy Hart, Rowdy Roddy Piper, Mean Gene Okerlund, Scott Hall, Kevin Nash, and the like all returned eventually. For fuck's sake, even <i>Bret Hart</i> eventually agreed to come back to WWE and appear on TV (even if it was just to prevent his legacy from getting the &quot;Self-Destruction of The Ultimate Warrior&quot; treatment)<br /> <br /> But Macho Man never did return, and was barely even mentioned at all until his death in 2011. And anyone who worked at WWF/WWE in the 90's and 2000's always said McMahon always got eerily quiet and refused to talk about it whenever anyone asked him about Macho Man and this knowledge got circulated through various shoot interviews and dirt sheets.<br /> <br /> As such, a lot of people were speculating wildly about what happened. This eventually led to those awful rumors about him and Stephanie.<br /> <br /> Occam's Razor indicates something much less fucked up and more mundane.<br /> <br /> Vince was upset that Savage ran to WCW shortly after Hogan did, and unlike Hogan, who was already on the outs with Vince after the steroid trials and hadn't been in any contract with WWF for over a year at that point, Savage jumped ship and took all that Slim Jim money with him.<br /> <br /> Vince McMahon is infamous for holding petty grudges over things that ultimately didn't amount to much in the long run (his enmity with Jeff Jarrett lasted for damn near twenty years all because of a pay dispute that was much less than the money made from Macho Man's Slim Jim contract)<br /> <br /> When WCW went under in 2001, Macho Man still had his AOL Time Warner contract AND had the royalties from Slim Jim. Even after he stopped being in the commercials himself, he got royalties from the &quot;SNAP INTO A SLIM JIM!&quot; audio clip alone (which still plays in damn near every Slim Jim commercial to this day)<br /> <br /> He didn't return to WWF/WWE because he simply didn't need to. He was old, his body wasn't in the best shape, and money wasn't an issue for him and neither was fame.<br /> <br /> Hulk Hogan was a diva who still wanted to be in the spotlight as long as possible, Ric Flair was and still is notoriously profligate with his money. Rowdy Roddy Piper was frugal but kept working and doing Legends appearances every now and then to ensure he could provide for his wife, kids, and grandkids. Macho Man had plenty of money from Slim Jim royalty payments, wasn't bad with his money like Ric Flair was, didn't desperately cling to the spotlight like Hogan did, and didn't have a large family full of kids like Piper. Taking bumps and touring on the road all the time wasn't worth it for him by the time WCW fell.<br /> <br /> All he needed to do was collect them royalty checks from Slim Jim, do the occasional appearances at conventions, and have cameos in movies and TV every so often, and he was set for life. He didn't need McMahon or the WWE and would only appear if they agreed to induct his brother Lanny with him into the Hall of Fame.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 09-06-2025, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-07T08:31:09-07:00","id":1553682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553673#post1553673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a lesser known Conspiracy Theory Mr. Gone about the Clinton's and what you told me about the man who told you their take on the Moon landing hoax is funny.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you might like that one! It always cracked me up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553673#post1553673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course there is even funny rumors in entertainment that made me chuckle and cringe sometimes.<br /> <br /> For example there was a rumor in professional wrestling that Jim &quot;Ultimate Warrior&quot; Hellwig died in the late 1980's-early 1990's and the late Kerry Von Erich pretended to be him.<br /> <br /> How did this start? Hellwig after an absence from WWF/WWE returned with shorter hair and a slimmer build and that was enough to start this rumor and it was clearly still the same guy.<br /> <br /> That was the funny rumor. The more cringe one involved the late Randy Savage and Stephenie MacMahon. This rumor implied that he had sex with the bosses daughter who was underaged at the time.<br /> <br /> This has never been proven and most people involved in wrestling don't believe it and it was apparently traced to a website that was in business of spreading rumors. If it was true I'm pretty sure Randy Savage would have been found dead in ditch somewhere with his genitals gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I'd heard either of those before! Crazy...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553675#post1553675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's a bit of a small bugbear when it comes to the topic of scientific literacy, I find something very emblematic of the larger cultural problem:<br /> <br /> Low stakes science is treated as a joke by mainstream culture.<br /> <br /> For most people that aren't part of a scientific field, the entire concept of &quot;low stakes&quot; science is not something they even consider; despite something everyone intuitively understands the moment you bring it up. You don't trust someone that just finished a pre-med Bachelor's degree with heart surgery. Likewise, you don't trust someone with a Bachelor's degree in a medical research field to run a multi-million dollar facility dedicated to working on cancer treatments. Everyone needs low stakes practical experience to hone their skills and prove to the rest of the world that they should be given serious responsibilities. People in trade jobs need apprenticeships. If you want to be a manager in a retail setting, you have to start in sales. Etc.<br /> <br /> But most people just do not link that to all the studies that get a passing media snicker and a &quot;what about curing cancer?&quot; punchline. Even people with public perceptions as being very pro science, science literacy, and so on still fall into this. Stephen Colbert is an excellent example of someone that's not a scientist, but loves science, and still can't resist the low hanging fruit on mocking some very niche study that - if nothing else came of it - is still a vital tool for training in the science profession.<br /> <br /> A lot of people are also still very caught up in the Great Man Theory of history when it comes to science. Despite science being an inherently collaborative field where anything that actually matters requires lots of and lots of people to do the theoretical work, the practical work, and then the reproduction work, for it to go from an idea to a fact, we think of science in terms of the giants of the field. And even then, a lot of the engineers that turn science into functional technology get a lot of the spotlight as well (not to put them down, but the conflation of the science that shows what we can do, and the people that figure out how to make it work doesn't help people understand what science is really about).<br /> <br /> If we talk about evolution... most people can name Darwin. Maybe they might remember Lamarck if reminded. Do they know about Russel (who's graciousness towards letting Darwin publish first led to Russel getting dubbed the &quot;Darwin of the East&quot; despite him figuring out evolution by natural selection first, proving it fast, and proving it far more conclusively)? Do they know how much Thomas Huxley did to earn the title of &quot;Darwin's Bulldog&quot; in his staunch defense of Darwin's work against social critics and stubborn academics? And that's not even getting into the names of folks like the crew of the Beagle that made Darwin's voyage possible. That's not getting into the almost two centuries of evolutionary scientists that have done immensely important work with the field Darwin broke open.<br /> <br /> Everyone cares about Edison and Tesla... nobody cares about the crew of people that did the work of figuring out the best light bulb filaments. Nobody considers the material science &quot;sexy&quot; or &quot;ground breaking&quot; even though it lit up our world. The men that sat around testing the applications of electricity to animal hairs are a forgotten footnote, and the scientists doing just as vital work today know they're going to end up just as forgotten... and likely far less likely to be respected than the Menlo Park folks were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I hear ya! Low Stakes Science is super important! I get it doesn't always make for huge headlines, but it's still very important. So yea, it kinda sucks it just treated like a punchline a lot of times..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553678#post1553678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that the political interest meant we had important authority figures actively seeding mistrust and sabotaging scientific dissemination.<br /> <br /> For someone who trusted the right sources and followed the news it was easy to follow the science being done. But for a lot of people the amount of noise was unbearable, and they had figures they trusted telling conflicting interpretations of what was going on.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that there are scientists and scientists. A lot of specialists are still bad-faith actors perfectly willing to sabotage science for personal gains, a lot of pseudoscience is lead by people with actual credentials the general public isn't prepared to evaluate. There was no shortage of actual doctors putting their weight behind politicians siding with science denial and giving a veneer of actual good science to it. When the figure you trust start to have actual professionals with them, what are you expected to believe?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with ya. And it's crazy to me that you sometimes even have scientist who work against their best interests. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553678#post1553678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if going to the moon was all that important. It would probably have stopped anyway, or at least slowed down significantly, even if their budget actually increased.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, sadly, it was more done because the US didn't want some other country to do it first. Kind of sad. But, at least we went...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553678#post1553678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it was surely more interesting for society than redirecting this money back to the already hyper-financed military. A lot more projects could have been conducted, we could know so much more by now. We could have more practical experiences with space tech, leading to even more technological developments in many fields. NASA could have brought international participation in its projects sooner and more intensely, which not only means benefiting the international community, it means more diversity of ideas and interpretations that can greatly haste development.<br /> <br /> We could already have more identified planets in the outskirts of the Solar System, more directly explored objects inside it, more unmanned exploration missions landing in the many planets and moons that are still untouched, and even maybe a few manned missions to a few other places than the moon (maybe even Mars, although I'm skeptical at that as the challenges have only proved ever greater than previously thought).</div> </div> </div> </div>I know! There is so much more we could have done had we kept up those missions. We could maybe even had a moon base! I know, that's a little far retched, but I can dream! And year, some proper manned missions to Mars would be awesome too! Super hard to pull off, but I think the research would be worth it! Maybe someday if the US can ever get it's act together again..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553678#post1553678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To his benefit, no other nation ever put an actual person on the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Good point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553678#post1553678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's because this is a lot more trouble than it's worth and unmanned missions do the work better, they're just less exciting. The Soviets actually planted the first flag on the moon all the way back in 1959, so 10 years before the American flag (and in the 21st century India and China followed suit, Israel is planning their own flag mission, too).<br /> <br /> Other countries got to see the evidence of the landing as soon as it happened, actually. It was tracked by several independent observers as it happened, as NASA had fully released the whole schedule of the mission (this was the whole point, for this to be as public as possible). The Soviets abandoned plans for crewed missions precisely because they knew it was real. Heck, by 1972 even schoolchildren with amateur radio systems could track the Apolo-17 mission. The samples brought from the moon are plenty of evidence and they're also available for study by international research institutions (as close to &quot;public&quot; as you can go with sensitive materials). Since the late 2000's direct evidence has only built up, by people that could perfectly verify if it matches dates and stuff to know if it was planted. But those people know nothing, who really know how to analyze this data are Bill from Chicago and Bart from Nashville.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yea! I mean, there is an almost overwhelming amount of evidence that we did actually go. How people can just dismiss it is beyond me... it's so easy to verify. But I know, when has facts and evidence ever meant anything. LOL.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your 