n actor and he admitted to the fact that doing mic work is something he isn't good at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-08-2025, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-07T12:16:53-07:00","id":1553685,"title":"","content":"I should make something clear. My parents are not antivaxxers at all and took the medical advice seriously and still got sick because some of their friends didn't believe in COVID prevention tactics or the vaccines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-07T14:54:11-07:00","id":1553686,"title":"","content":"Early in the pandemic a coworker of mine got everyone sick at the office because he proudly went to church events designed to be against every health guidance of the time. Those events were even forbidden in my city at the time, it was like an underground movement to spread the disease.<br /> <br /> Fortunately I escaped then due to being on sick leave for unrelated issues, but even after vaccination I eventually got COVID at least twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-08T04:32:16-07:00","id":1553692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553684#post1553684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was always a big Randy Savage fan and his promos were entertaining. In fact I recently read a autobiography on Randy Savage that covered his life and career in and out of the ring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I thought he was pretty fun too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553684#post1553684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Mr. Gone here's another ridiculous rumor from wrestling. The infamous Montreal Screwjob was a work and that Bret Hart was sent to WCW to sabatoge them.<br /> <br /> It's ignored the fact that Vincent wasn't sure if his company could survive in its current state and be able to pay Bret Hart his salary. People forget that WCW was still winning the ratings war at the time but cracks were starting to show. Not to mention that Shawn Michaels and Bret Hart had real life issues and then they bring up that Hart tenure was lackluster and fuel the rumor of a work.<br /> <br /> The same WCW that had great talent that was misused and went to other promotions for better chances like Chris Jericho, Mick Foley, Steve Austin and Mark Calloway?<br /> <br /> They never answer the question of why they would continue denying it as a genuine betrayal by Vincent MacMahon and what's the point of continuing the charade and we all agree that Bret Hart isn't that good of an actor and he admitted to the fact that doing much work is something he isn't good at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Yea, Bret Hart was cool and all... but he wasn't a great actor. He was fine, but not great. So yea, I don't think he could have pulled that off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's interesting though, thanks for sharing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-08T17:17:48-07:00","id":1553696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553684#post1553684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was always a big Randy Savage fan and his promos were entertaining. In fact I recently read a autobiography on Randy Savage that covered his life and career in and out of the ring.<br /> <br /> At Mr. Gone here's another ridiculous rumor from wrestling. The infamous Montreal Screwjob was a work and that Bret Hart was sent to WCW to sabatoge them.<br /> <br /> It's ignored the fact that Vincent wasn't sure if his company could survive in its current state and be able to pay Bret Hart his salary. People forget that WCW was still winning the ratings war at the time but cracks were starting to show. Not to mention that Shawn Michaels and Bret Hart had real life issues and then they bring up that Hart tenure was lackluster and fuel the rumor of a work.<br /> <br /> The same WCW that had great talent that was misused and went to other promotions for better chances like Chris Jericho, Mick Foley, Steve Austin and Mark Calloway?<br /> <br /> They never answer the question of why they would continue denying it as a genuine betrayal by Vincent MacMahon and what's the point of continuing the charade and we all agree that Bret Hart isn't that good of an actor and he admitted to the fact that doing mic work is something he isn't good at.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard that theory regarding Bret Hart in WCW, though I have heard it applied to Scott Hall and Kevin Nash as well as Vince Russo.<br /> <br /> The rumor about Hall and Nash is bullshit given that the nWo was so white hot at first that it helped fuel WCW's infamous 83-week winning streak that almost put WWF out of business and the nWo only started to become an obvious detriment to WCW around 1999 or so (the cracks begin to show after Starrcade 1997's infamously botched finish but the effects of Starrcade '97 and the nWo's continued over-exposure in 1998 on WCW's downfall are only really visible in retrospect)<br /> <br /> Now, Vince Russo on the other hand....that's probably the one wrestling conspiracy theory that I could actually believe as true. <br /> <br /> Russo was tired and felt overworked at WWF and McMahon let Russo go to WCW in mid-1999 at the height of the Monday Night Wars with minimum fuss and Russo was even briefly let back into WWF/WWE's writing room in 2001-2002 during the whole back-to-back debacles that were The InVasion and the failed nWo revival. Bear in mind that while WWF was winning the Monday Night Wars by 1999, WCW was still doing well enough thanks to Goldberg's popularity and that while their decline became way more noticeable in Summer 1999, it wasn't seen as an obviously doomed company barreling towards self-destruction like it was in 2000.<br /> <br /> McMahon knew better than anyone that Vince Russo wasn't the real architect of the Attitude Era (if anyone deserves that title, it's Paul Heyman) and the good ideas that Russo did have were because he was kept reined in and his ideas were refined and filtered by McMahon, Bruce Pritchard, Jim Cornette, and the other writers and bookers at WWF. For every good idea like &quot;Crash TV&quot;, Val Venis, The Brood, Mike Tyson at WM, or The Ministry of Darkness, Russo had a shitton of other far worse ideas that slipped through the cracks like Beaver Cleavage, Owen Hart's Blue Blazer gimmick, and Brawl For All.<br /> <br /> Letting him run down to Atlanta and run WCW's booking and writing without any filters or sense of checks and balances would be a perfect way to sabotage the competition.<br /> <br /> Russo joins WCW in late 1999 and the company goes full &quot;WCW 2000&quot; and even after bringing back Eric Bischoff and Kevin Sullivan to rein in Russo, it's still not enough and by the time he's out, the damage is done.<br /> <br /> So, the whole conspiracy theory about Vince McMahon letting Vince Russo leave WWF for WCW amicably with the intent of sabotaging the competition does make sense and would be in-character for a Machiavellian sociopath like him, it still seems a bit too over-the-top.<br /> <br /> Heck, for all his faults, Russo did properly point out how badly WCW misused younger talent and tried his best to dismantle the &quot;glass ceiling&quot; within the company, which makes me think that McMahon didn't send in Russo as a saboteur (or if he did, then Russo sure as hell wasn't in on it)<br /> <br /> Plus Jamie Kellner wanted to end WCW on Turner networks no matter what it took. He even was willing to keep the old AOL Time Warner contracts going so long as it kept wrestling off his channels. Had Eric Bischoff had a little more time to negotiate a deal with Fox after USA blew him off, there's a good chance WCW would've limped away and survived to fight another day after March 26th, 2001 and would've probably endured by filling the same spot that TNA Impact Wrestling (and later AEW) would later hold in the 21st Century pro wrestling landscape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-10T21:43:53-07:00","id":1553743,"title":"","content":"I feel sorry for the family of the late Charlie Kirk who was shot and killed today in Utah. Even if you disagreed with what he said in general, it doesn't make it ok to murder him or possibly have people who are going to celebrate his passing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T01:34:53-07:00","id":1553747,"title":"","content":"If you live your life in a fashion where lots of people would volunteer that they'd celebrate your death, it's probably worth reconsidering your methods if not a lot more.<br /> <br /> The fact that people feel the need to lament the murder of a man, and the suffering of his family, because he got famous for being a vile blowhard... and thus ignore all the people dead, injured, or emotionally damaged by gun violence that nobody is talking about in the news because they were normal decent people that didn't advocate that we should proudly accept gun deaths to patriotically protected a law and thus the media doesn't care about them.<br /> <br /> It's far more indicting of our society that people feel the need to publicly opine on the inappropriateness of how to discuss the murder of a famous person, while ignoring everyone else suffering from the consequences of the US's policies without a platform to advocate from; both domestically and abroad since US guns aren't being used just to kill people here.<br /> <br /> There was literally another school shooting in Colorado that happened around the same time... and that's not the gun violence that gets top billing of the day. School kids being shot? Old news, nobody cares. Famous asshole gets shot? Round the clock coverage and instantly SEOed for all the news clicks. That's what our media thinks we want, and I struggle to blame them for thinking it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T11:30:32-07:00","id":1553752,"title":"","content":"In my part of Alberta, the big scandal was the fact that a Edmonton Public school library was trying to ban books including the Hand Maids Tale by Margaret Atwood. Our Premier Danelle Smith got called out for it and quickly had to backtrack saying that some books got included in by mistake.<br /> <br /> Either way banning books is never a good thing in general and tells people that you are scared of different viewpoints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-11-2025, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T13:03:02-07:00","id":1553754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553743#post1553743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel sorry for the family of the late Charlie Kirk who was shot and killed today in Utah. Even if you disagreed with what he said in general, it doesn't make it ok to murder him or possibly have people who are going to celebrate his passing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is a deeper problem with the current state of US problems that it has gotten to a point where a person can have been such a dedicated advocate for policies that harm a lot of traditionally marginalized people and their families that the ethics of how to respond to his being murdered feel confused.<br /> <br /> But I also think <i>that</i> he contributed to such harm makes the matter of how to assess people celebrating his murder also more complicated.<br /> <br /> (For my part, I think it is short-sighted to do so, because this is not a time to lend credence to narratives of &quot;liberals are the dangerous savages, actually, and will probably get around to their own turn at insurrection to overturn an election any day now&quot; and galvanize policies that might respond to that narrative.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T13:44:36-07:00","id":1553755,"title":"","content":"Let's not beat around the bush here. Kirk advocated for <b>the murder </b>of some minorities. He wasn't arguing about economic policies, or how to fix various systems we all agree are broken, or any of that. He regularly argued for outright no-process death sentences for people that aren't like him.<br /> <br /> I don't anyone that's confused about this. Murder is wrong so - while advocating for murder doesn't justify murdering the advocate - advocating for murder is wrong. Being happy that a murder advocate was killed isn't confusing because it isn't really complicated. This is the world Kirk was fighting for; he was the confused one about how one-sided that harm can be.<br /> <br /> The ethics or how to respond aren't what's complicated or confusing for people of significant public profile either; non-ethical considerations like optics and profits are what's complicating matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T16:09:43-07:00","id":1553758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553754#post1553754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is a deeper problem with the current state of US problems that it has gotten to a point where a person can have been such a dedicated advocate for policies that harm a lot of traditionally marginalized people and their families that the ethics of how to respond to his being murdered feel confused.<br /> <br /> But I also think <i>that</i> he contributed to such harm makes the matter of how to assess people celebrating his murder also more complicated.<br /> <br /> (For my part, I think it is short-sighted to do so, because this is not a time to lend credence to narratives of &quot;liberals are the dangerous savages, actually, and will probably get around to their own turn at insurrection to overturn an election any day now&quot; and galvanize policies that might respond to that narrative.)</div> </div> </div> </div>They already think that, so why bother caring about them? These are people who actively engaged in an insurrection because they didn't like the outcome like spoiled children, and have been single-mindedly trying to ignore the truth of what they did this whole time because it paints them as backwards idiots. You can't reason with fanatics, especially when they write some inane script to follow instead of reality. Who the hell CARES what they think now? Ethics? What's that? This country hasn't seen ethics for over a decade now and hasn't stopped plodding along sniffing out profits to bother looking for any. <br /> <br /> There were three incidents of democratic personages being attacked in their home in the last few years, one of them was even killed, and the media didn't dwell on that for more than a week before they moved right on. They barely gave it a passing commentary after it happened. But one, odious, right-wing trashfire gets what was coming to him and suddenly it's &quot;<i>oh no! the sky is falling!</i>&quot; I'll bet they keep this garbage circulating for a whole month while they wring as much pathos and tug-jobs from right-wing media moguls as they can.<br /> <br /> The alarmist bastards calling this an assassination are giving it too much credit. Poetic justice like this is too perfect to be the result of a plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T18:39:38-07:00","id":1553761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553752#post1553752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my part of Alberta, the big scandal was the fact that a Edmonton Public school library was trying to ban books</div> </div> </div> </div>How sweet.<br /> <br /> I can't say I much care about Kirk because I have more important shit happening here, and good news for a change (Bolsonaro's condemnation).<br /> <br /> But for what I can say, the ass-hole getting murdered doesn't change he being an ass-hole, or make his demise more relevant than literally more than 100k others just in the same day around the world.<br /> <br /> And who am I to blame people for being happy about this? Of course his death isn't justified (if it even was because of his ideas), so what? What do we stand to gain by bashing people for their feelings? As if other public figures wouldn't face the same.<br /> <br /> Not to say we're talking the death of someone who publicly celebrated the deaths of others and wouldn't stop talking shit about victims of murder, and did so with his family publicly by his side, so I am not moved by their plight. If they don't deserve the pain of loss, they're not in a position to complain, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T19:40:38-07:00","id":1553763,"title":"","content":"I do have pity for his kids, because they're too young to have had a say in anything that matters to the rest of us. His wife? Yeah, she knew what she was a part of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T20:33:28-07:00","id":1553786,"title":"","content":"Is everyone getting this regular request to verify if you're human by CloudFlare?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Mispelled the source 09-13-2025, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T20:55:52-07:00","id":1553788,"title":"","content":"No more than usual, but I tend to get a lot for reasons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T23:17:50-07:00","id":1553791,"title":"","content":"I didn't used to get it on these forums, now I have to do it every hour or so around here. It's kinda annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T10:26:02-07:00","id":1553798,"title":"","content":"All these anti-AI checks are simply the latest example of letting these tech idiots solve a problem THEY caused by instituting more and more invasive &amp;/or draconian measures in the name of &quot;security&quot;. A &quot;security&quot; they threatened in the 1st place with their greed, hubris, and stupidity. Already this desperate push to spread AI like a disease is screwing up normal internet use. It's only a matter of time now before some bigger problem results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T10:40:41-07:00","id":1553800,"title":"","content":"&quot;We've got this great idea! It's basically autocomplete, but it takes up orders of more magnitude in power to make function and offers nothing over it! It's the future, I swear!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T11:57:28-07:00","id":1553840,"title":"","content":"Things I want to see in a movie that mocks tropes.<br /> <br /> Ie the private eye that get's a late night phone call from a colleague about something that they don't want to share over the phone and wants to meet you at such and such place.<br /> <br /> My response would be. &quot; I'm not getting out of my warm bed and traveling across town to find you dead and figuring out what you wanted to tell me. So let's not waste time and just tell me what you learned.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T10:30:18-07:00","id":1553903,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how I feel about Jimmy Kimmel possibly not having a show because he doesn't like the current President. I was never a fan of Kimmel to begin as I remember him from Win Ben Stein's Money and the Man Show and thought he was pretty low brow for my tastes.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it's a good idea that he and Colbert lost their respective shows because of political pressure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T11:00:07-07:00","id":1553906,"title":"","content":"Just remember, in both cases the host of the show is pretense. What that said and about who was not why they got fired/suspended (even if that's why them in particular), it's because both parent companies had major business deals pending that require governmental stamps of approval, and the government used that to pressure them to show that they'd comply for money's sake instead of not complying for integrity's sake.<br /> <br /> And that should scare everyone because the US government is huge and what it does ripples around the world. When it's openly abusing regulatory powers to chill speech, it's bad for more than just those of us living here.<br /> <br /> And even so, it's fine to feel bad about this more broadly. A big swath of people in the US are getting fired over quoting Charlie Kirk or posting videos of Charlie Kirk because it's not &quot;respectful enough&quot; of Kirk's legacy to... point out what he said. Which is in stark contrasts to his least controversial position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T13:10:58-07:00","id":1553909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553903#post1553903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how I feel about Jimmy Kimmel</div> </div> </div> </div>If you like his work or not is inconsequential.<br /> <br /> First, someone did. Those people deserve their entertainment.<br /> <br /> Second, it's what he does (or did) for a living. Going for someone's job for petty reasons is a horribly messed up thing to do.<br /> <br /> Third and more important, that's a message. This is Trump saying he can and will use his power to shut down dissent in the industry whenever he wants, with poorly made up justification, and get away with it.<br /> <br /> As someone from a country that actually went through this more than once in the past, and watch those things happening abroad, I'm sorry to say that, but...<br /> <br /> Donald Trump doesn't want to become a Dictator. <b>He is. </b>This boat sailed months ago, and the people with any power to stop him already lost their timing. Things won't get better for democracy in the US.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T18:00:23-07:00","id":1553913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553906#post1553906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What that said and about who was not why they got fired/suspended (even if that's why them in particular), it's because both parent companies had major business deals pending that require governmental stamps of approval, and the government used that to pressure them to show that they'd comply for money's sake instead of not complying for integrity's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, even with the most cynical viewpoint of corporations, acting in the name of integrity should be not be strictly necessary. The most mercenary attitude of a media conglomerate should still have the perspective of &quot;hey, the government making these kinds of interventions based on political interests and ideological divides should be kind of illegal, and even actually unconstitutional&quot;.<br /> <br /> And, you know... companies fight the US government all the time. They even fight it during the times when the government is actually in the legal right on the matter. Choosing to not fight here is possibly somewhere between &quot;huh, for some unaccountable reason, we can't find the motivation to fight this particular brand of intervention&quot; and &quot;oh shit, a government with a pretty flimsy respect for the rule of law and all the implications that has for the future of fighting being regulated in courts, best switch gears to capitulation in the names of operating business&quot;. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T05:41:56-07:00","id":1553920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553909#post1553909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you like his work or not is inconsequential.<br /> <br /> First, someone did. Those people deserve their entertainment.<br /> <br /> Second, it's what he does (or did) for a living. Going for someone's job for petty reasons is a horribly messed up thing to do.<br /> <br /> Third and more important, that's a message. This is Trump saying he can and will use his power to shut down dissent in the industry whenever he wants, with poorly made up justification, and get away with it.<br /> <br /> As someone from a country that actually went through this more than once in the past, and watch those things happening abroad, I'm sorry to say that, but...<br /> <br /> Donald Trump doesn't want to become a Dictator. <b>He is. </b>This boat sailed months ago, and the people with any power to stop him already lost their timing. Things won't get better for democracy in the US.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was away in Scotland for a week, and didn't have great phone reception, so when I finally saw that all this happened I couldn't believe it! It's getting really scary now and I do like what this says about things to come...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T05:46:45-07:00","id":1553921,"title":"","content":"Sorry to vent about something that seems like nothing compared to the current political climate in the US (which is so scary to me)... but my wife and I went to Scotland last Wednesday for a week and while we arrived in Edinburgh, our luggage did not. It made it to the airport just as our tour left the hotel, and it basically never left the airport. For whatever reason they could not seem to get it to us. One day it seemed like they would, and we watched via the airtags as our luggage was driven all over Edinburgh, and then went back to the airport. It was crazy! We had to buy new luggage and a new suitcase. We were able to pick it up at the airport when we flew home, and luckily it did make it back home with us.<br /> <br /> We filed a delayed baggage reimbursement claim, and they are sending us a check for the new clothes and luggage, but it was a bit of a pain to deal with. We didn't let it spoil our trip though... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T13:47:23-07:00","id":1553926,"title":"","content":"The subject of lost luggage is something I'm of two minds on.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, the possibility of some of my possessions (especially clothes) being misplaced or even lost for good like that is terrifying to me. My great sense of attachment to my things is where that starts, but also the horrible sense of exposure it would entail. Buying clothes while abroad is something I don't want to do under the best of circumstances, let alone just to have anything to wear at all.<br /> <br /> On the other, it would be really funny to have an excuse to in-real-life quote Robot Chicken Emperor Palpatine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T14:54:55-07:00","id":1553927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553926#post1553926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The subject of lost luggage is something I'm of two minds on.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, the possibility of some of my possessions (especially clothes) being misplaced or even lost for good like that is terrifying to me. My great sense of attachment to my things is where that starts, but also the horrible sense of exposure it would entail. Buying clothes while abroad is something I don't want to do under the best of circumstances, let alone just to have anything to wear at all.<br /> <br /> On the other, it would be really funny to have an excuse to in-real-life quote Robot Chicken Emperor Palpatine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was pretty crazy I will admit! We had all the important stuff (meds and the like) with us, so it was just clothes. But still, it was a bit of a pain having to buy new clothes and a suitcase in a place we'd never been before.<br /> <br /> I tried not to let it spoil the trip though and I just rolled with it. I think if we hadn't been with a tour group and we'd been on our own I might have panicked a lot more..LOL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T15:36:23-07:00","id":1553928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553921#post1553921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to vent about something that seems like nothing</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be sorry about that, this' still the main point of the thread.<br /> <br /> I just got two sick days. Couldn't sleep well for some nights, and when this happens my body plays a number on me, every time. Stomach burn, nausea and headache. Not a funny day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T16:23:31-07:00","id":1553929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553928#post1553928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't be sorry about that, this' still the main point of the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! And true, but you know, after recent events it seems a little trivial..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553928#post1553928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got two sick days. Couldn't sleep well for some nights, and when this happens my body plays a number on me, every time. Stomach burn, nausea and headache. Not a funny day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awww, sorry about that. I had some issues sleeping over in Scotland, I assume because of the time difference. But I sometimes deal with a little insomnia as I've gotten older too. And I don't well with little sleep.<br /> <br /> Sorry you were sick though. Hopefully you're starting to feel a bit better.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T17:01:39-07:00","id":1553930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553929#post1553929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry you were sick though. Hopefully you're starting to feel a bit better.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am, fortunately, and thanks!<br /> <br /> You should try Melatonin when traveling abroad, it helps with adaptation (it isn't useful for everyday use, though, unless you have actual reduced Melatonin production, as I have).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T05:27:42-07:00","id":1553936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553930#post1553930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am, fortunately, and thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear it!!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553930#post1553930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should try Melatonin when traveling abroad, it helps with adaptation (it isn't useful for everyday use, though, unless you have actual reduced Melatonin production, as I have).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! I hadn't thought of that! I don't usually take Melatonin, so I guess I hadn't considered it. I'll have to remember that for next time, because I have to admit it was a little rough dealing with that time change. lol.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T11:41:30-07:00","id":1553941,"title":"","content":"My vent now probably won't be very popular with the US members of the forums, but I have to do it.<br /> <br /> Of course as a Brazilian I'm biased towards Santos Dumont instead of the Wright brothers as the forefather of aviation, but studying the history of aviation only made this bias into a full rage against how the brothers are treated as heroes by many.<br /> <br /> The history of aviation is mostly a history of people collectively working on the dream of flight. Since the 19th century several people were working on techniques and improvements for flying with all kinds of contraptions. Ideas big and small that were then taken by the next one, everyone sharing their works and discoveries. Even Santos Dumont was just a piece in the great work of getting to the skies, <b>and he knew it</b>. His designs were made publicly available, and his <i>Demoiselle</i> went on to be not only the first series production aircraft (and one with zero fatal accidents to this day), but one of the main influences on future aircraft greatly because Santos Dumont licensed it for free to everyone, all versions he made.<br /> <br /> But the Wright brothers were first and foremost selfish and narcissistic assholes. Their work was done in secret and the first thing they did was to not only patent everything they did, but make the patents in such a way as to cover for things they <u>didn't</u> create and to be as generic as possible and so cover any other possible innovation that even vaguely resembled their tech. They had the guts to write their patent in such a way that they could even claim patent over the aileron, a popular (and eventually vital) piece for airplanes that not only existed before, <i>they didn't actually made or used it</i>.<br /> <br /> For years airplane makers were forced to either pay them or fight them fiercely in court for the right to make something, <i>anything at all</i>, as the US got engulfed in the <i>Wright Brothers' Patent Wars</i>. Things were easier outside the US, but still not ok, as they fought for their patents everywhere to try to force everyone to pay them. This was their actual public declarations, by the way, that they would make the world recognize their vital role in modern aviation and pay what they were owned, all the while ignoring how their work was also <b>heavily</b> based on contributions even by the very people they were suing, and how half their patent claims were bullshit (including the aileron that went to be the main piece of tech they made money with).<br /> <br /> It got so bad that by the Great War the US aircraft industry was lagging heavily behind Europe and the US military had to simply buy airplanes for the war because nothing worth even trying was available domestically. Pressed by the military, the US government was forced to create the Manufacturers Aircraft Association to pool patents and finally unblock aircraft development and production. Several historians still argue that their Patent wars not only stalled the US aircraft industry, but in fact jeopardized (not impeded, but greatly slowed) the evolution of aeronautics for a decade.<br /> <br /> What really makes Santos Dumont the father of aviation in my opinion isn't the <i>14-bis</i> (the first airplane to fly publicly in a presentation widely recognized), but Airship N\u00ba 6, then the <i>Demoiselle</i>, and more importantly his many contributions in this process that went on to be freely available for everyone to build upon and create the future of human flight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T16:28:06-07:00","id":1553943,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Most US forum members are probably learning about Santos-Dumont from your post. The pro-Wright Brothers propaganda in US history classes basically treats the development of heavier-than-air powered flight as a bunch of ridiculous inventors building silly machines that crash instantly or fall apart before even getting up to speed; and then &quot;blam&quot; the Wrights just got it. The idea that this was a serious area of international organized engineering research is very absent from our history books.<br /> <br /> And US history tends to spin a lot of our inventor &quot;heroes&quot; with very positive alternate terms (Henry Ford and Thomas Edison also get the same treatment despite their very scummy behaviors) rather than being willing to treat historical figures as the flawed humans they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T19:57:30-07:00","id":1553949,"title":"","content":"Very true indeed.<br /> <br /> I didn't expected many people to know Santos Dumont*. He's famous in Brazil and France, and I think that's about it unless you're seriously into aviation history. My beef is with the Wright Brothers and how they actually harmed aviation far more than helped it due to their greed. I wouldn't be as pissed-off if people just thought aviation was a collective endeavor without any particular hero, or praised one of the other names that could claim the first &quot;valid&quot; flight, like Traian Vuia, Cl\u00e9ment Ader, or even Karl Jatho.<br /> <br /> To be honest, the &quot;first airplane&quot; thing is mostly a marketing stunt. A lot of people did a lot of &quot;flights&quot; that both contributed something to the field, yet weren't really practical airplanes, and both the <i>14-Bis</i> and the <i>Wright Flyer</i> were exactly that. Nice shows and good proofs of concept, but nothing else. The very concept of an aviation institution was actually older, the A\u00e9ro-Club de France was organizing regular events since 1898. Actual, viable airplanes for something other than stunts would only appear in 1909, by a bunch of people (including Dumont and the Wright Brothers, but with newer models).<br /> <br /> Romanticizing science heroes is, unfortunately, a common thing. I just find it harder to swallow for a few cases than others, and the Wright Brothers are in this camp (together with Edison) because of how they actually harmed the field instead of improving it. That's my problem right there. They made the thing, but also made it into a personal mission to jeopardize development as much as they could, in many ways pioneering corporate takes on IP.<br /> <br /> * For whatever it's worth, the - (hyphen) doesn't exist in Dumont's name in Portuguese. It's present in his name in some languages, including English, Japanese and French, it isn't in many others, I have no idea where it came from. But in Portuguese you don't hyphenate composite surnames, having more than one surname is normal for us as we get both paternal and maternal surnames, so having two surnames is a standard in most Portuguese-speaking countries, and we can have up to six surnames before it becomes really weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T20:33:42-07:00","id":1553950,"title":"","content":"I thought Dumont started to use the hyphen when he was doing his work in France because it was easier in various forms as the composite surnames aren't as much of a thing in continental culture. Basically he had to register a lot of his craft as the &quot;Santos-Dumont [No. X]&quot; and originally didn't use it when just signing his name, but then started adding it to avoid confusion. I think most US aviation history enthusiasts see it with the hyphen because we read a lot of stuff in translation from French.<br /> <br /> In the US itself more broadly, a hyphen or not is very dependent on cultural/ethnic background and how much you're willing to put up with slow-to-be updated government systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-21T05:42:36-07:00","id":1553953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553943#post1553943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Most US forum members are probably learning about Santos-Dumont from your post. The pro-Wright Brothers propaganda in US history classes basically treats the development of heavier-than-air powered flight as a bunch of ridiculous inventors building silly machines that crash instantly or fall apart before even getting up to speed; and then &quot;blam&quot; the Wrights just got it. The idea that this was a serious area of international organized engineering research is very absent from our history books.<br /> <br /> And US history tends to spin a lot of our inventor &quot;heroes&quot; with very positive alternate terms (Henry Ford and Thomas Edison also get the same treatment despite their very scummy behaviors) rather than being willing to treat historical figures as the flawed humans they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I gotta admit, I didn't know much if anything about Santos-Dumont... that's crazy how I'm just learning this now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-21T13:10:43-07:00","id":1553959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553950#post1553950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Dumont started to use the hyphen when he was doing his work in France because it was easier in various forms as the composite surnames aren't as much of a thing in continental culture. Basically he had to register a lot of his craft as the &quot;Santos-Dumont [No. X]&quot; and originally didn't use it when just signing his name, but then started adding it to avoid confusion. I think most US aviation history enthusiasts see it with the hyphen because we read a lot of stuff in translation from French.</div> </div> </div> </div>I initially thought the same, but it seems he's not hyphenated in Germany and Spain, but is in Italy and the Netherlands. We can guess it has to do with having more contact with his letters or his patents, but without much more to work with it seems to be mostly random. That the hyphen started in France is almost certain. I can't say for sure how strong those trends are in their respective countries, either, because I have a very limited source to work with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553953#post1553953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I gotta admit, I didn't know much if anything about Santos-Dumont... that's crazy how I'm just learning this now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, the not-knowing-Dumont part is actually pretty expected. Most Brazilians never heard of the Wright Brothers, either. My particular problem with their reputation is because of the harm their did to the field.<br /> <br /> If you want to research on him, though, it's a very interesting figure, one who really contrasted to the Wrights because he was &quot;obscenely nice&quot;. But the early history of aviation is really full of curious people and experiments, to the point that the <i>Wright Flyer</i> and the <i>14-Bis</i> are straight-up boring in comparison to many other things being done. A lot of important design innovations that went in their wings, for example, had been developed for Daedalus-style gliders mimicking bats, pigeons, what-have-you, by people that actually mustered the courage to jump from high places on those contraptions.<br /> <br /> Oh, and it's also important for the history of clocks, specifically because of wristwatches! The first wristwatch was from 1810, but it was a unique piece of jewelry for a queen, and for almost 100 years those time pieces were just novelty jewels without practical purpose. Santos Dumont asked Louis Cartier for a watch that were more practical, because pocket watches were a pain in the ass during a flight, so in 1904 Cartier made for him the first modern wristwatch, practical and meant for men (which was important back then), a model called Cartier Santos Wristwatch. Cartier still produces this line. The reason wristwatches got traction was basically because they took the aviation community by storm, and then the military, specially by the start of the Great War.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the history of aviation is crazy.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-22T04:26:00-07:00","id":1553965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1553959#post1553959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, the not-knowing-Dumont part is actually pretty expected. Most Brazilians never heard of the Wright Brothers, either. My particular problem with their reputation is because of the harm their did to the field.<br /> <br /> If you want to research on him, though, it's a very interesting figure, one who really contrasted to the Wrights because he was &quot;obscenely nice&quot;. But the early history of aviation is really full of curious people and experiments, to the point that the <i>Wright Flyer</i> and the <i>14-Bis</i> are straight-up boring in comparison to many other things being done. A lot of important design innovations that went in their wings, for example, had been developed for Daedalus-style gliders mimicking bats, pigeons, what-have-you, by people that actually mustered the courage to jump from high places on those contraptions.<br /> <br /> Oh, and it's also important for the history of clocks, specifically because of wristwatches! The first wristwatch was from 1810, but it was a unique piece of jewelry for a queen, and for almost 100 years those time pieces were just novelty jewels without practical purpose. Santos Dumont asked Louis Cartier for a watch that were more practical, because pocket watches were a pain in the ass during a flight, so in 1904 Cartier made for him the first modern wristwatch, practical and meant for men (which was important back then), a model called Cartier Santos Wristwatch. Cartier still produces this line. The reason wristwatches got traction was basically because they took the aviation community by storm, and then the military, specially by the start of the Great War.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the history of aviation is crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa! I didn't know that about wristwatches either! That's pretty interesting. I'll have to look into all that a little more! Thanks for the quick history lesson!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T19:35:10-07:00","id":1554116,"title":"","content":"I sometimes wonder if having the internet and social media causes more harm then benefits? Some of the loud and vocal minority make things seem worse than it really is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T03:54:04-07:00","id":1554121,"title":"","content":"If one looks to the history of innovations in mass communication? Probably not. People lamented TV, cinema, radio, newsprint, and even printed books on the same grounds.<br /> <br /> The Internet is just technology. It doesn't cause harm or benefit on its own. It's how we use it that determines that.<br /> <br /> For me, there are two big questions the Internet poses:<br /> <br /> First, is if the Internet represents a technology that we can't fully adapt to the new reality of. Past technologies came with an inherent limitation that meant we had a lot of time for societies to adapt to new things and transition more smoothly (though rarely perfectly: planting kids in front of the TV to keep them busy was certainly an issue). The Internet has grown incredibly quickly and is still changing on a rapid basis. Laws meant to regulate the Internet to combat this are usually out of date before they're written, and they're usually written by people that don't really understand what the second and higher level impacts are going to be. In fifty years, I highly doubt history will judge the Internet are harmful technology, but most likely our struggles to adapt to it aren't going to be taken seriously and the blame will be on us for not seeing the obvious ways to do it &quot;right&quot; that later generations will consider common sense and normal.<br /> <br /> Second is the ephemeral nature of digital information. The Internet understandably wants digital information, but digital information has a very short shelf life. With so much cultural expression happening in the digital world, we're already at the point where one disaster could cause a loss of information not seen ever in human history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T11:09:21-07:00","id":1554124,"title":"","content":"It's also worth mentioning that a lot of the problems ascribed to the internet existed way before it. And while we have some evidence of things getting worse, we also have the problem that the internet, by its own nature, makes the problem more public, so this very evidence is biased to some degree. Are we seeing more problems because there are more problems, or because the internet makes the problems more visible?<br /> <br /> Most people nowadays think, for example, that child kidnapping is on the rise, as we have more news than ever of such kidnappings. But the fact is that precisely because it became far less common, it also turned into relevant news. When I was young, posters of lost children were ubiquitous, they were everywhere, and in places like police departments there were huge murals with photographs of lost/kidnapped children. <b>From the previous month alone, and all local</b>. Simply put, no newspaper would waste time with a child kidnapping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T15:49:06-07:00","id":1554148,"title":"","content":"Just a minor vent. I hate it that I create a NPC or character in a game or story and they don't fit in at all and you wonder if they can ever be used. Has that happened to you and did you ever find a use for them in later attempts? attpt<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T06:08:37-07:00","id":1554156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1554148#post1554148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a minor vent. I hate it that I create a NPC or character in a game or story and they don't fit in at all and you wonder if they can ever be used. Has that happened to you and did you ever find a use for them in later attempts? attpt</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I've come up with ideas for NPCs for a game, but then didn't end up using them for whatever reason. Sometimes they get reused in a different game, and sometimes not..<br /> <br /> So you're not alone..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T16:12:04-07:00","id":1554181,"title":"","content":"I am trying to grasp on how people can get a driver's licence and be ignorant traffic rules. Today I saw a driver go down the wrong way of a high traffic area to make a turn down another lane. Good thing it was a slow part of the day when this happened and we would have a major traffic flow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-16T10:25:16-07:00","id":1554390,"title":"","content":"We lost Tomonobu Itagaki, one of my favorite game developers of all time.<br /> <br /> The dude was legendary and he will be missed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T15:07:09-07:00","id":1554611,"title":"","content":"Ace Frehley the oriiginal guitarist and founding member of KISS passed away at age 73. I know that he had issues with substance abuse that got him kicked out the band and I hoped that in his later years he got over it, but he was a big part of the original band's success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T17:31:14-07:00","id":1554623,"title":"","content":"Ace Frehley was legendary and I'm definitely gonna miss him","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T14:53:22-07:00","id":1554796,"title":"","content":"I'm disappointed in some reporters when some of them have nothing better to do then make a article that is commenting on the looks of so and so.<br /> <br /> In this case it was about Pamela Anderson who has decided to stop wearing make up now and we have this clown saying it makes her look old and not mentioning the fact is that she is 58 years old and she is going to look way different then she was when she was at age 28 or 38 years of age. She still looks good for her age and is probably in better health and happier then these people who do these articles.<br /> <br /> Of course I remember these same people who were shocked that at the time a 67 year old Arnold Schwenzger couldn't make himself look he did when he was he was 37 when he did the first Terminator film and was returning to the role in Terminator Genysis , these are people who don't understand how unpredictable the aging process can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-02-2025, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T17:29:27-08:00","id":1555038,"title":"","content":"I like to thank that there's no such thing as bad story ideas, but only but awful execution of a story idea. Does anyone on this forum feel the same way in this notion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T18:41:45-08:00","id":1555042,"title":"","content":"I do, at least. Character concepts, too.<br /> <br /> But there <b>is</b> a difference in how hard it is to do a good job with a given idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T19:01:45-08:00","id":1555045,"title":"","content":"I think it's a statement that relies too much on the vagueness of things like what &quot;bad&quot; means, and when a &quot;story idea&quot; becomes a &quot;story&quot; via execution. <br /> <br /> Philosophers have been debating the fundamental aspects of applying moral conditionals (&quot;bad&quot; &quot;awful&quot;) to actions for thousands of years. That's basically the entire field of ethics.<br /> <br /> For example, even if I were to broadly agree to the premise of there being no inherently bad story ideas in an ideal sense, I could still make the case that there are story ideas that are bad in reality/a practical sense because they're beyond human ability to execute in a non-negative fashion. &quot;Idea&quot; and &quot;execution&quot; are not something simple to classify as easily divisible in human creativity. There's also a whole level of debate of when does executing an idea in a different fashion result in just executing a different idea?<br /> <br /> Since we're on the Onyx Path forums and all, there's a pretty good case to be made for the opening fiction of the 2e Infernals book to include story ideas that are simply beyond being executed well. Whether that means in an ideal form those ideas are bad or not, and whether you could rewrite the text to something less awful without just swapping the ideas for ones that can be executed better, have a lot of assumptions behind them to make a firm position on. In the end though, you're going to struggle to find anyone that's going to defend the choice for Exalted 3e to just drop that mess and overtly retcon for something else.<br /> <br /> While by no means perfect, I think a better base premise would be something like: &quot;I think there are no story ideas that should be beyond artistic consideration.&quot; I think it largely gets to the same goal as a way of thinking about artistic expression, while being a lot easier for people to intuitively grasp the implications. It also centers that agency of artists without obliging them towards some sort of moral imperative. If there are good story ideas that have simply been let down by artists failing to execute properly, the moral burden is on artists to try; otherwise a good thing is being denied to humanity. By leaving good, bad, etc. out of the equation, you're letting artists simply consider a concept and decide whether or not they want to tackle it further. It doesn't matter if someone else thinks an idea is &quot;good&quot; and should be made by the &quot;right&quot; artist, it matters if the artist thinks they want to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T04:22:56-08:00","id":1555052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1555038#post1555038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to thank that there's no such thing as bad story ideas, but only but awful execution of a story idea. Does anyone on this forum feel the same way in this notion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you in general Lysander.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T13:04:09-08:00","id":1555170,"title":"","content":"Kinda political and religious but people why try &quot;i used to be like you.&quot; As a prelude to explaining how im wrong irritates me<br /> <br /> 1) dont presume, you have no idea what im &quot;like&quot;<br /> 2) i didnt blink<br /> 3) im not clear how mildly deviating would make you do a 180 and find the idea insulting that you're implying id do the same<br /> 4) you're probably lying anyway so fuck off.","signature":"","edite