ss=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-13-2025, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T18:11:54-08:00","id":1555652,"title":"","content":"I have something today that I must vent, despite not being anything wrong or whatever:<br /> <br /> Food fetishes and foot fetishes gross me out, royally. Hate 'em, and hate when I bump into them in any media, anywhere.<br /> <br /> Since I was a child I have problems with feet, kinda like Timmy Turner in a certain episode of <i>Fairy Godparents</i>. Their place is on the floor or ground and not near any other part of me or where I eat, much less near my face or near food. And any and all sensual activity including feet will get me cold instantly and wanting to puke.<br /> <br /> And food and sex together for me is taking two of the things I love the most and ruin them both. I can only think of sticky skin and sweat tasting food (or worse). Bleh. It grosses me less than feet, but still makes me sad and disappointed.<br /> <br /> There are other fetishes I don't like, and surely some that causes me moral revulsion, but nothing that causes the gut reaction of those two abominations. And believe me, I've been places, I've seen some shit, sometimes literally (which sure, is the next worst thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T18:51:49-08:00","id":1555654,"title":"","content":"I HATE JURY DELIBERATIONS! I have to listen to my fellow jurors, and their complete lack of understanding of the US Constitution. <br /> <br /> &quot;The defense never said he didn't say that&quot;. Me: Um, the Defense is not required to; he can remain silent and its up to the State to prove it. <br /> &quot;Well, the Prosecutor said. . .&quot; Me: That's not evidence, I don't care what the Prosecutor said or the Defense-attorney said; I only care about what the witnesses, the video, and the judge's instructions. <br /> There's no audio to the video; we have no idea what was said; for felony, criminal-threats, it has to be oral; and it's not proven beyond a reasonable-doubt.<br /> &quot;The witness is evidence&quot;. Me: No, I don't believe him; he's full of ****. <br /> &quot;But, look how he jumps&quot;. Me: I don't care. We don't know what was said; at all. For all we know the Defendant made a sexual-pass at him; I'd jump too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T20:02:56-08:00","id":1555658,"title":"","content":"Witness testimony is evidence, even if weak evidence. Unfortunately... yeah... 12 Angry Men is fiction and deliberations aren't going to simply course-correct into rational analysis over time. Fortunately, most jury systems require unanimous votes for convictions... so it might suck but you can be the check jury systems require: someone that holds the prosecution to the appropriate standards. If you feel that a hung jury is the best result you can get after talking to your fellow jurors... take it. You get to live knowing you did the right thing. It's possible the prosecutor opts to take another stab at it and the next jury doesn't have a you in it... but we can't help it. There's also appeals if the admissible evidence and the verdict seem wildly out of sync to judges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T22:34:05-08:00","id":1555667,"title":"","content":"Eyewitness accounts are always unreliable<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T22:53:47-08:00","id":1555670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1555654#post1555654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I HATE JURY DELIBERATIONS!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why most of the world doesn't use lay juries to the extent the US does. Well, because of your reasons, I mean, not because you specifically hate them. Even the UK, who was the model for the system, has backed down a lot compared to how the US handles it. It's specially bad when the local population has a bias the body of jurors isn't made to compensate in some way, and the US system overall has very little guards against that problem.<br /> <br /> Not that trained judges make everything ok. They have actual understanding of the law, but when they do have bias they also have very little to check them, as you can see in the US Supreme Court. So we're dealing with a problem that, while I think the US system is especially bad in how it handles this, isn't by any degree easy to deal with or anything anyone really knows how to solve.<br /> <br /> But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Heavy Arms</a> said, as limited as they are the system does have some checks and you're in a position to apply them, even if others don't listen to reason. People are emotional and biased and that can't be helped, but you can prevent a conviction if nothing else. And at least it's a trial, most of the criminal convictions in the US never even get to this stage because prosecutors are sly assholes. From every 20 criminal convictions in the US, only 1 ever went to trial, all the others are plea bargains under threat of worse punishment, regardless of guilt.<br /> <br /> In Brazil we have juries only for murder-like cases, which includes inducing suicide and forced abortion (when abortion with the consent of the pregnant woman is a crime, it doesn't go to a jury). All other cases are by single judges. Also our system for selecting jurors is less random, which is slightly better if only because when authorities are sensible they can nudge things. Overall I think it's a better system, but I can tell you we still have a helluva lot of problems with biased judges, especially misogynistic assholes, and our juries are just slightly better than randomness. Other countries have other solutions and other problems.<br /> <br /> We also don't give prosecutors the power to doom someone's life so thoroughly, but the price is a very morose judicial system. So pick your poison, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1555667#post1555667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eyewitness accounts are always unreliable</div> </div> </div> </div>Most evidence is to some degree.<br /> <br /> Frequently eyewitnesses are the <i>only</i> relevant evidence for whatever happened, and ways to compensate their problems also exist.<br /> <br /> IRL trials aren't like in the movies, and while it doesn't means that problems don't happen, the idea that eyewitness are always problematic and shouldn't ever be used, or that they can say whatever and that'll pass, is mostly fiction.<br /> <br /> Sure, it's not <i>completely</i> fiction. But it's mostly fiction. In cases where the witnesses are really full of shit and yet they sway the jury, you can bet the jury most likely was biased to begin with and the witness isn't by far the bigger problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T12:06:58-08:00","id":1556098,"title":"","content":"I'm curious but do YouTubers like Critical Drinker, Jesterbell, Ryan Kinnel and G&amp;G follow the same script as they seem to have the same compliants about movies or games they don't like and seem to paint very broad strokes. <br /> <br /> It makes me wonder if Terminator 2, Aliens, Blade or even Kill Bill and or Predator 2 came out today and would they praise it for being good entertainment or call it slop with Dei and girlbosses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T13:10:04-08:00","id":1556102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1556098#post1556098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious but do YouTubers like Critical Drinker, Jesterbell, Ryan Kinnel and G&amp;G follow the same script as they seem to have the same compliants about movies or games they don't like and seem to paint very broad strokes.<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder if Terminator 2, Aliens, Blade or even Kill Bill and or Predator 2 came out today and would they praise it for being good entertainment or call it slop with Dei and girlbosses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't say for sure because I don't watch them, but first you have to define what you mean by following the same script.<br /> <br /> Is it that they have very similar opinions about movies? Is it that they make similar criticism? Or is it that something in the actual structure of the video is to like each other, or yet that they use the same words?<br /> <br /> A lot of things may explain any of those. Anti-Woke communities in the internet, for example, tend to have very similar criticism and very similar words to name them, words that only make real, complete sense to community members. Other criticisms are very common among some circles, or even in general, and some ways to describe them are just common jargon. Some video structures are easy to copy, others are copied from famous content creators, and some are just common sense because they work too well and became standards in some niches.<br /> <br /> Fame and influence is also a complex thing because content creators aren't just members of a circle/clique, they're also a clique of their own, and some creators are more famous and influential among equals than for the general audience (this is true in the arts in general, many of the most influential artists in every medium have very little actual following besides their enormous influence among artists).<br /> <br /> My two cents based on the few information given is that this seems to be a lot of the first type, but I would really need more to say. Sometimes, though, there's just not much youtubers from a given niche can say differently (science content creators, for example, will only disagree strongly in many subjects if at least one of them is a farce, because they'll agree with consensus whenever there's one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T21:48:05-08:00","id":1556111,"title":"","content":"Yes Monteparnas is that these channels use the same lingu and talking points with little deviation and they will use click baiting images of people that they target and alter them to look unappealing.. I can see how the term echo chamber is a valid statement.<br /> <br /> But I'm am seeing that people are starting to realize that these folks are just plain angry folks who will work on people's fears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T00:32:13-08:00","id":1556116,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, it will likely to continue to work because it makes YouTube/Google/Alphabet money for it to be this way. Negativity and confirmation bias fuels more views than other options, and corporations are fine with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T03:41:00-08:00","id":1556120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1556111#post1556111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes Monteparnas is that these channels use the same lingu and talking points with little deviation and they will use click baiting images of people that they target and alter them to look unappealing.. I can see how the term echo chamber is a valid statement.<br /> <br /> But I'm am seeing that people are starting to realize that these folks are just plain angry folks who will work on people's fears.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should stop watching toxic channels to begin with, instead of hopping for them to get better.<br /> <br /> On top of the money they make for Alphabet, this is a social phenomenon that extends far beyond them. They have a steady supply of viewers, first because a lot of people simply agree with them and like to see their ideas confirmed time and again in as many channels as possible, second because people realizing means nothing, there is always new people coming, it's a revolving door.<br /> <br /> They have no reason to change, and the only thing that matters in the end is the views. Stop giving them yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T06:30:18-08:00","id":1556123,"title":"","content":"I actually have Monteparnas, I just watch Codex Unknown, Space Ice, Chris Mcfreely and music videos from my favorite artists. I curtailed my viewing habits when I saw that they were tourist's when they were shocked about alternate timelines and multiverses are a thing in science fiction and fantasy genres..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T11:30:12-08:00","id":1556128,"title":"","content":"Something that bugs me somewhat.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think that I speak for everyone of a certain fandom, that this is awful or great!&quot; <br /> <br /> You can only speak for yourself of what you like or don't like as art is subjective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T15:03:20-08:00","id":1556139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1556128#post1556128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that bugs me somewhat.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think that I speak for everyone of a certain fandom, that this is awful or great!&quot;<br /> <br /> You can only speak for yourself of what you like or don't like as art is subjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! &quot;I think I speak for everyone...&quot; has always bugged me too! People can like or dislike something and not everyone has to like or dislike the same things..<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T19:08:37-08:00","id":1556214,"title":"","content":"Do you think that Media Literacy skills are becoming more rare? It's been something I've been thinking about as I realized that I need to better explain why I like or dislike a novel, movie or tv show other than broad strokes I've fallen into the habit into unless it's something like Transformers or something I have a passion for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T19:42:34-08:00","id":1556216,"title":"","content":"That implies a high level of media literacy skills being common in the population at some point... for most of history the vast majority of humans haven't had the resources to consume media on that level.<br /> <br /> Media literacy in the global north is dipping by most metrics, and everyone wants to point the blame somewhere, but it's a messy thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T20:19:43-08:00","id":1556218,"title":"","content":"I'm going to try anyway Heavy Arms and keep a better account when I want to talk about something I like or have problems with in regards to media.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T22:53:47-08:00","id":1556228,"title":"","content":"It's also worth to mention that this dip isn't as intense as many like to believe, because there's in general a strong and pervasive tendency to romanticize how widespread this kind of thing have been in the past. Especially people greatly overestimate how much their contemporaries were critical of the media they consumed and underestimate how much current generations are, and this is a constant trend. We have the added problem that scientists are people and frequently research end up not being immune to this trend, either.<br /> <br /> So in general it's been lowering, especially in the Global North, but it's not by far a straightforward thing or a terrible dip. It has never been as great to begin with and isn't just disappearing, especially as people notice and react to this trying to find their way. I don't personally think we're in a terrible spot compared to any other moment in history, although I do think it healthy to do what you can and be more aware of what you consume and what it means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T02:23:02-08:00","id":1556230,"title":"","content":"A big part of the problem in analyzing what's going on, is that we're in a point of history with massive and rapid changes in media consumption coupled with multiple innovations in new kinds of media. There isn't really history we can look back on and try to extrapolate things like &quot;is this a temporary dip that will bounce back in a decade or two once innovation slows,&quot; or, &quot;have we finally innovated beyond the ability for humans to fully adapt and the dip will be difficult to impossible to fully recover from.&quot; And that's before we get into the issues of social pressures because a lot of people don't consider media literacy a good thing (or at least are quite selective about it). It is to the benefit of many powerful people for the common folk to not have strong media literacy skills since that would make them harder to control; as has been the case for thousands of years. Also... a lot of the time it's good to not think too hard about our entertainment... if the goal is to provide happy easy times for our weary minds, engaging our minds on critical interpretations is kinda self defeating; and that's a whole academic debate on if the debate is truly reduced skills or less use of the skills due to other stressors increasing a desire for more escapist engagement styles.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, broadly, I do believe it's good to think about what media you consume, why, and know the pitfalls and dangers of said media (esp. before recommending it to others) as a matter of self-reflection and thus more productive discussions. But it's also good to make sure that's what other people want to talk about before you get too deep into it (or at least if you're willing to break some social norms by going there anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T02:13:19-08:00","id":1556599,"title":"","content":"Some guy-[states idea]<br /> <br /> me-[your idea is incorrect and here's why]<br /> <br /> Some guy-[I disagree but won't back it up in any context, lets just agree to disagree]<br /> <br /> No fuck off, you said your piece so back it up. You want to agree to disagree, don't say your dumb idea's in the first place and waste my time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T18:00:25-08:00","id":1556974,"title":"","content":"I hate &quot;agree to disagree&quot; unless it becomes too clear that we have irreconcilable differences on basic premises.<br /> <br /> But now I have to vent a little about something a lot of people gush: I really don't like Cameron's Avatar movies, or at least how some people praise their plots.<br /> <br /> They're basic and uninspired. Even the first is just a mash-up of decades of white-meets-natives movies, a lot of the story's structure is just Disney's Pocahontas.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, they're <i>gorgeous</i>. If you take them as an excuse to explore visuals, that's good entertainment. And if they're your first contact with this kind of movie, they're sufficiently well done to deserve being a game-changer for you. But they're not objectively good plots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T00:51:30-08:00","id":1557204,"title":"","content":"It's disappointing to see what sort of books are on the banned list at one the local bookstores because of what is happening in the States. I saw at the table of banned books The Diary of Anne Frank, Hunger Games by Suzanne Collins, Twilight by Stephanie Meyer, Percy Jackson by Rick Riordan, Wicked by Gregory McGuire, The Hand Maid's Tale by Margaret Atwood, Throne of Glass by Sarah J Mas and George Martin book and a few other authors that I'm not overly familiar with.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking at the book store I help out at that we should have a section of banned books and the reasons for why they are banned to show the how foolish it is to censor a book because you don't like the subject matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  More things that I remembered later. 01-02-2026, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T08:20:09-08:00","id":1557256,"title":"","content":"It only took barely 24 hours before media grifters went after Supergirl and using the buzzwords woke and the usual outrage farming.<br /> <br /> The new twist is that they are calling it a James Gunn film even though it's written by Ana Nogueira and is directed by Craig Gillespie. I know that James Gunn is in charge of the Detective Comics Cinematic Universe but that means he has lots of administrative work to do on a daily basis and won't be making as much movies as he would like.<br /> <br /> One thing is that interesting is that some of &quot;critics&quot; are displaying there lack of knowledge of Supergirl backstory and that brings back memories of school of when you're going to be for or against something is that you needed to research the topic.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T19:28:02-08:00","id":1557294,"title":"","content":"Considering people got upset that the most recent Superman movie leans into the idea that literal immigrant Kal-El is an immigrant, there is a point where you can just ignore a lot of the shallow online nonsense.<br /> <br /> It's also a long standing practice in movies (and even other media when they can manage it) to highlight a specific person that might not be that active in a given film when there's a reputational matter. As long as most viewers associate James Gunn with good superhero movies/etc., WBD (or whatever they become in the future) is going to want him to put his name on things publicly as an assurance of quality even if he has to delegate a lot of the work to others. It's a standard enough move in studio history I'm really not sure there's much to glean about it other than self-awareness that the previous DC movies weren't well liked as a whole.<br /> <br /> And of course, when it comes to comic book characters most characters that have been around long enough that they have 10+ back stories that an adaptation can pull from. A character that's been around since 1958 doesn't have &quot;a&quot; backstory to get critical about; they have multiples and new takes are going to pick and chose from elements of those for what works for stories that aren't bound to the current comic canon timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T22:11:07-08:00","id":1557297,"title":"","content":"It was stuff like this that made me decide to improve my media literacy skills and try to be better at explaining what I enjoyed or didn't enjoy in a film, novel, tv show or games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T00:45:52-08:00","id":1557331,"title":"","content":"I'll possibly get a lot of bad rep here for what I have to say, but...<br /> <br /> Really, I'm starting to hate the &quot;no AI art&quot; stance overall.<br /> <br /> That's not that I don't see the problems associated with &quot;AI art&quot;. I do. But I think most of the criticism is severely misplaced, and this misplacement hurts common people on both sides of this debacle without really addressing the very real problems behind it.<br /> <br /> What I see is that virtually every problem associated with AI art is actually just a new iteration of older problems that have been harming artists for a very long time, and blaming AI shifts attention from the real causes, real solutions, and maybe more important, real problems that were already there and will stay unsolved. AI doesn't steal art, companies do, and have been doing for more than three centuries. AI doesn't fire people from their jobs to hire at worse, more exploitative conditions, companies do and most artists work under a very oppressive system. AI doesn't flood social media and the internet, users do, and platforms don't curate <i><b>because they don't want to</b></i>. AI doesn't refuses regulations, companies do, and politicians abide.<br /> <br /> AI is a tool. It doesn't do art, but this doesn't change that people can do art with it. A camera doesn't do art either, the image being a precise, soulless record done through light and physics, yet a photographer or filmmaker <b>is</b> an artist by planning and executing how the camera will be used, and the results curated. Doing slop with AI is certainly easy and fast, but this kind of uninspired and unskilled mass production of media is hardly a new phenomenon. There is such a thing as good art with AI, but it takes time, work and skill like any other art, because you has to plan and curate, you have to learn and iterate complex prompts, and you have to know how composition works to produce anything worthy.<br /> <br /> Seriously, those problems have been pointed out by people in the industry at least for several decades <i>in their current form</i>. Companies force most artists to relinquish rights on their creations and pay pennies for their valuable work. We need serious legal reforms that stop the exploitation system, not to blame a technology that, seriously, won't go away like that. AI even has the best advantage to solve common problems that people blame on it, but existed before: it can infuse metadata on the output that identifies it was AI made, and it can index its own training database for easy audit. More than any other technology around, AI can make it easier for everyone to know where something came from and what was used as &quot;inspiration&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lets demand AI companies be required to audit their training datasets and remove unlicensed material. Lets reform copyright laws to guarantee creators their rights against companies that control the market and can simply gate-keep you from work if you don't sell the IP. Lets demand AI companies to implement a simple standard that lets any program to identify quickly if something was made by AI. Lets demand platforms to curate or forbid AI content (there's a lot of difference between AI for content creation and AI for personal use). Lets demand real solutions to real problems by real, deliberate offenders that will otherwise just find other ways to exploit us as they always did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T04:12:36-08:00","id":1557342,"title":"","content":"I think there's some strong points that come from trying to remind people that all computer programs are just tools and how they're used is what really matters.\\<br /> <br /> That said, &quot;just being a tool,&quot; doesn't mean the potential for good in a given technology can ever overcome the risks of the bad. For example, I've read lots of essays trying to convince people otherwise, but I cannot hold any position on nuclear weapons besides, &quot;nobody should have these, everyone that already has them should be pressured to the maximum possible extent to disarm from that particular technology, and everyone trying to make more should face maximal pressure to stop.&quot; Mutual assured destruction is a demonstrably failed geopolitical stance, and to this days vast sums of human resources are wasted maintaining arsenals to make sure we can end civilizations (if not humanity completely) if the wrong people get into a hot war. Nukes are also just tools, and while I think in the hindsight of history their first use is growingly seen as far less justified than it was presented that is debatable at least. In the now? There's no good reason for any country to be making more of them, and doing anything with their olds ones besides destroying them as safely as our current technology allows.<br /> <br /> While I don't think generative algorithms are as potentially destructive as nukes are, I think a much stronger case has to be made for their good than is currently being made. Passing laws and those laws being followed on an global level is not exactly something humanity has a good track record on.<br /> <br /> Another problem is money. Multiple major companies in this sector have said that the regulations that you're proposing would simply cause them to pull their products because it would render them impossible. The people that make the biggest models have, even if that's not their spin on it, admitted there is no non-exploitative form of these models that can operate at the scale necessary for commercial use. They have made it clear our options are &quot;No AI art,&quot; or, &quot;human made art's primary role in society is to be stolen for model consumption.&quot; That is the stance of the companies responsible for the most popular models.<br /> <br /> From that perspective, the public has no real power unless we rally around &quot;No AI Art.&quot; Either that is a bluff by these companies, and they do have ways to monetize their product in an ethical fashion if faced with losing a vast sum of money already invested in these things happening, or they don't and morally we have no choice because ethical use doesn't really exist at scale. This gets back to my nukes analogy. Either, at least at commercial scale, these programs are in the same moral category as nukes, and thus we need to be opposed to them for the sake of stopping massive damage to human flourishing, or we need to be opposed to them as if they're nukes until the people in charge of these companies start rolling out the normal TNT version that has clear ethical use cases that can be adequately covered by regulations.<br /> <br /> If &quot;AI Art&quot; (also the AI label is a gigantic problem of its own) is just a tool like any other, it also needs to compete with existing tools like any other on a fair ground. Nobody on the planet is making &quot;good&quot; &quot;art&quot; with these tools on a fair playing field with other creative endeavors in the same style of media. They are all being subsidized by companies out to prove their product has positive use cases. How many &quot;AI artists&quot; would there be if you had to pay $100 US per prompt you run? How much would they have to charge for a final product? Can that really be competitive to more traditional methods? At some point the free prompts for quality tools era has to end. Data center capacity costs resources, research and model improvements cost resources, complying with regulations for ethical use are going to cost resources. Right now, all of that is coming from rich people investing in other rich people. But they didn't get that rich giving their money away. They want returns on their investments. That system doesn't work in an ethical non-exploitative economic model.<br /> <br /> I assure you that exceedingly few people that hold a &quot;No AI art,&quot; don't also agree that we need to find a way to fix late stage capitalism. There's too many problems in the world to try to treat any of them in isolation, but that's part of the fuel for unnuanced rallying cries. Like all protest slogans isn't generally necessary to take a far stronger stance than the more nuanced positions people would actually accept. I'm sure you'd find most &quot;No AI Art&quot; advocates are more receptive if you treated the slogan as just being short for, &quot;Pause AI art until we fix late stage capitalism and then we'll been in a place to give AI a fair shake to see it the technology is a net positive.&quot;<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> That all said, I do want to highlight one thing I think that really hurts your position: &quot;There is such a thing as good art with AI, but it takes time, work and skill like any other art, because you has to plan and curate, you have to learn and iterate complex prompts, and you have to know how composition works to produce anything worthy.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't learn composition from LLM/etcs. This is a fundamental weakness in the argument for the current level of technology actually being able to produce &quot;good&quot; outputs. You essentially have to study composition in an essentially traditional fashion so you can filter outputs. This means that all &quot;good&quot; outputs are just a traditionally trained artistic eye spotting when the model lucked into something worth refining.<br /> <br /> It's a largely self-defeating position. &quot;Learn how to do artistic photography to the point where you could be a professional photographer so you can understand photographic composition well enough, but then stop working in photography and move to working in prompts as a whole secondary skillset to develop so the computer can generate the images and you have to spend lots of time refining outputs until you finally have something good.&quot; That really isn't that great of an argument over just.... being a digital photographer. Art is an extremely weak area to argue for these models because if you assume all the ethical issues get solved, you're fundamentally left with adding steps to do what people are already doing. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T17:15:35-08:00","id":1557356,"title":"","content":"My experience has been mostly one of being unable to have a healthy talk about AI because the people that usually have a balanced stance on things, at least in my circles, are currently so against AI that no argument for doing research or anything else is possible, despite me agreeing with fighting all the same problems. It's not that I want to defend all the bad things being done, but I can't have a decent conversation about any aspect of the technology at all.<br /> <br /> I agree that if the tech ends up being ethically indefensible, that's it. Although I'm unsure if GenAI/LLMs would compare more to nukes or to fission technology in general. One of the reasons I think we should demand they follow copyright laws and have their own power sources is precisely because if this really makes them unsustainable, they'll break and that's that, good riddance. And it isn't as if they were really profitable to begin with. I'm for the &quot;No AI Art&quot; slogan as a slogan. I just don't think being radically against it for real will do much good in the long run.<br /> <br /> About AI as a tool for art, it can do some things other tools can't as easily. I'm by no means thinking AI replaces them for making good art, I don't think any tool ever managed that, but I do think it has uses the same way every other tool has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T21:12:49-08:00","id":1557361,"title":"","content":"The question I have to ask for AI is if the benefits outweigh the drawbacks? Regardless this technology is going to happen and we better be smart on how we handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T21:53:39-08:00","id":1557362,"title":"","content":"I think there is a lot of justified emotion around it that's hard to push aside for a healthy conversation. People are losing jobs/work over a technology that isn't actually proven to do what it's proponents say it might be able to do. It's not a technology that's been given time to germinate naturally. It went from a potential innovative concept to something that was suddenly being treated as the future as a fait accompli; not just by enthusiasts and a few tech bros, but 1/3 of the US investment system is basically bound up in the bet that it will all payout.<br /> <br /> Effectively, nobody was really given a choice. Nobody was given time to a form a fully considered stance. Before a single large model has come close to even finding a path to profitability, the companies pushing the tech are effectively holding the entire global economy hostage so that everyone is going to have to adopt the tech to avoid one of the largest economic disasters ever - even if that means we have to do accept every unethical thing being done as a necessity - or let the system shatter when the vast majority of people are already in economic hardship.<br /> <br /> We're not talking about regulating a technology because it has obvious implications that need to be addressed before it gets too far, we're talking about needing to legislate our way out of a cesspool of unethical behavior by a gaggle of the richest people on Earth in control of some of the richest companies on Earth that we've already been tossed into.<br /> <br /> You can say that you're not sure being radically against it will do much good... but what is being nuanced going to do at this stage? Unethical actors have already pushed everyone else into a place where we're trying to navigate a giant series of iffy choices because we don't know what's going to happen. It's simple to criticize people that are taking a hard stance when you think it's too hard... but you're just as open to being criticized as having too soft a stance if you don't have a better solution people can actually do something towards. &quot;No AI Art&quot; is simple to do something about<b></b>: don't buy it, and encourage others to join you.<br /> <br /> A healthy conversation is a two-way street. If you approach it as something the other people need to move on, but you're already in one of the acceptable positions... how's that going to go?<br /> <br /> As for the art part... I haven't seen an real examples myself yet. I've heard talk. I've seen tools that aren't about creating more easily but aiding in other things. And that's still discounting the whole &quot;these tools are built on a mountain of unethical actions,&quot; issue. Humans will have art one way or the other. If AI art has to wait a decade or two... human creativity will survive. Whatever new tools we could get will still be possible. I know a bunch of digital artists. They've been enjoying a decade of consistent development of great &quot;non-AI&quot; tools that have made their art form more and more expressive in various ways. Zero of them would say, &quot;i need this tool now, regardless of the social costs,&quot; no matter how much they love those tools after getting them. They could do their art before, they could endure doing it the older way for good tools made with good methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T22:03:26-08:00","id":1557363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1557361#post1557361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless this technology is going to happen and we better be smart on how we handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much dislike this particular line of thinking.<br /> <br /> Lots of technologies get made and then fade into history as trivia, factoids, and so on. Trends that people look back on and wonder what people could have every thought was so inevitable about them.<br /> <br /> Baby boomer were told the future would bring us all flying cars. And someone actually built a flying car. And it sucked. It's a silly novelty. No technology is inevitable. Every tool has to actually be useful or it'll get tossed into the trash for better options. We have been here before, recently no less, and seen &quot;the future&quot; arrive and then everyone passed on it. AR glasses? Crypto? NFTs? All of those were &quot;going to happen and we better be smart on how we handle it.&quot; And the smartest thing was to ignore everyone hyping them up. My entire life we've constantly been on the verge of VR tech that will radically change entertainment and... dozens of attempts in and we're still just at headsets that are comfortable enough you can play some niche games on.<br /> <br /> This technology is going to be made, because it's already been made. That doesn't mean it's going to &quot;happen&quot; in some larger social sense because that's the only possible outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T01:15:06-08:00","id":1557582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1557361#post1557361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question I have to ask for AI is if the benefits outweigh the drawbacks? Regardless this technology is going to happen and we better be smart on how we handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this framing (as far as real discussion/understanding goes) is that it greatly misrepresent the role of the decision-makers and social systems involved, and how they can guarantee or impede anything about anything.<br /> <br /> &quot;No AI Art&quot; slogans and demands work because they threaten the bottom line of the people who are misusing the tech, and that's a real fight worth of fighting. But &quot;benefits and drawbacks&quot; do not exist in a vacuum and aren't solely dependent on the technology in question.<br /> <br /> Implementation is also a very complex thing. As Heavy Arms said, technologies <i><b>can and do fail at social relevance</b></i>. Virtual Reality as we know it, motion sensors and all, exists since 1968 (with primitive versions as old as 1956), yet it's just a fad that comes and goes with ambitious pretensions never delivered to this day. Commercially available biometric sensors exist since 1974, yet only in the past two decades did it gained real trust for development outside edge cases and spy movies. And flying cars suck.<br /> <br /> AI as we speak of today, that is, specifically Generative Neural Networks (particularly GAN-type ones), has a lot of intricacies and complex problems that are still far from a given on what they'll do to their use. LLMs in particular are intense resource consumers (as are Crypto Farms that no one gives a serious thought about, but should), and even media generators can get pretty hungry at scale. Their need for training material is also very far from a settled matter, nowhere is it written that AI companies will get away with stealing IP material forever, especially given that on top of heavy public distrust being levied, that also creates a lot of issues with large companies that are also heavily IP dependent, not to say how slop is making platforms rich right now, but is also compounding problems that may become an intense headache for them in the near future.<br /> <br /> My position is that we should talk seriously about the tech and how we can use it ethically and positively <i>to the degree it's possible to begin with</i>, but a lot of things about it are far from settled, and questioning if it should be implemented to begin with is definitely still on the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1557362#post1557362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is a lot of justified emotion around it that's hard to push aside for a healthy conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right on this, and that's why in my last post I tried to re-frame my position as less one of disagreement and more one of personal frustration. I'm doing research on the area and liking this work a lot, yet I can't talk to my usual circles about it and that's emotionally draining.<br /> <br /> But this whole situation has a lot more to it. For example, until now the numbers don't match the overall perception that AI destroys jobs/work. It's hard to say for sure because a lot is happening at the same time and no one has the whole picture yet, but very few cuts in the job market can be traced to AI at all, far below the baseline growth. AI still requires a lot of work, by a lot of people, and a lot of skill. It <b>IS</b> touted by many companies as the reason for their layoffs, but just as with ending Home Office, a lot of it is layoffs the companies were expected to do anyway, the AI is just a nice tale to tell to shareholders.<br /> <br /> Overall I think a more nuanced conversation is more likely to give us actionable answers to some of the many problems those unethical actors caused. And by any means it doesn't mean not being firmly against everything being effectively done. I won't personally pay for anything AI made or AI related that hasn't been painstakingly proven to be ethical (and I know how limiting that is) if I can avoid it in any way - and I'll be very vocal against any situation where I'm not given a choice.<br /> <br /> Definitely I don't want to make this yearning for decent discussion in any way a negation of the very real need to fight against everything that's happening, and that is exactly how you said: a huge, sweeping <i><b>financial </b></i>dependence led by unethical actors faster than anyone could reasonably react, and now we have a helluva mess to deal with.<br /> <br /> What I can give a modicum of credit to the &quot;will come anyway&quot; argument is that there's a lot of high-level political and military interest in keeping this tech going. Generative AI, and particularly LLMs, are in the strange position of being technologies that need test data to such a degree that having &quot;everyone&quot; using it isn't a seller's dream, it's an R&amp;D necessity. One that would make any tech unfeasible were it not for the strategic relevance it has for the only people who really have enough power and resources to bypass the problem: governments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T12:18:42-08:00","id":1558081,"title":"","content":"I'm actually starting to feel sorry for folks like Critical Drinker, Ryan Kinnel, Geeks &amp; Gamers and there like. They have to be really unhappy people judging by all the videos they make about what they hate about &quot;modern&quot; cinema and wax nostalgic about previous decades.<br /> <br /> There was plenty of bad movies, games, shows, music and books that were made. Now some of them are becoming bitter as society has changed and we are being more mindful of that the good old days were not always good for everyone.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T17:29:33-08:00","id":1558170,"title":"","content":"It doesn't take much for media grifters to froth at the mouth over unconfirmed rumors about whom is being cast in a film.<br /> <br /> In this case it's the rumor of actress Lupita Nygonio as Helen of Troy in Christopher Nolan Odyssey film and we the usual suspects griping about it.<br /> <br /> First off it hasn't been confirmed what role that Keyan/ Mexican actress Lupita Nygonio has been cast as and there's a few cast members on the film that we don't know what.character they are playing.<br /> <br /> Also Lupita looks very attractive and I don't see the issue as Helen was never really described by Homor in the story and was more of a minor character in the tale and we don't know for sure if Helen ever did exist. But who knows we might find out one day that Helen of Troy was based on a real person just like we learned that the city of Troy did exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T17:38:52-08:00","id":1558171,"title":"","content":"To paraphrase many people on the Internet:<br /> <br /> If you have a complaint about casting a dark-skinned woman as Helen of Troy based on anything like &quot;realism&quot; or &quot;historical accuracy,&quot; you have to address the story of her conception and birth before your complaint will be taken seriously.<br /> <br /> Also... the same people are not going to complain about how pale the cast is compared to the whole rather tan/olive/etc. complexions normal to the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T18:45:55-08:00","id":1558174,"title":"","content":"Oh I know Heavy Arms about the absurd nature of the attacks. Almost the entire cast isn't from Greece and this isn't a historical fiction as we have Gods and Goddesses, Siren's, Cyclops and a visit to the Underworld. They are getting bent out shape over a rumor.<br /> <br /> The same people who freaked out about the rumor of Denzel Washington being cast as Magneto or even further back when there was talk about Idris Elba being considered for James Bond. It was just rumor and we didn't know who serious the consideration was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-10T18:06:27-08:00","id":1558222,"title":"","content":"I'm mad about Discord. Their new policy will require that people send them a picture of an ID confirming that they're an adult. Supposedly Discord will delete the ID immediately after confirmation, but I don't trust them with my ID at all. Not to mention they just had a big data breech a couple of months ago. So now my friends and I have to look around for a new chat app to roleplay on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-11T18:41:56-08:00","id":1558248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558222#post1558222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mad about Discord. Their new policy will require that people send them a picture of an ID confirming that they're an adult. Supposedly Discord will delete the ID immediately after confirmation, but I don't trust them with my ID at all. Not to mention they just had a big data breech a couple of months ago. So now my friends and I have to look around for a new chat app to roleplay on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crud; I have a Discord-account, but, I don't use it; I only got it because I heard it was the last place any forum out there about Cyberpunk: 2020; then, all I found was stuff about Cyberpunk's video-game. Sigh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T16:31:38-08:00","id":1558268,"title":"","content":"We had a mass shooting at a school in the town of Tumbler Ridge in British Columbia with at least 9 confirmed dead and 25 injured with the most recent report thus far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T16:28:16-08:00","id":1558401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558268#post1558268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had a mass shooting at a school in the town of Tumbler Ridge in British Columbia with at least 9 confirmed dead and 25 injured with the most recent report thus far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, that's awful. Sorry to hear that...<br /> <br /> Well, it makes the thing I was gonna complain about seem pretty trivial now... I've just been dealing with a cold for almost two weeks now. Ugh. I did take some covid tests and luckily it's not that. But this crud just will not clear....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T06:38:39-08:00","id":1558445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558222#post1558222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mad about Discord. Their new policy will require that people send them a picture of an ID confirming that they're an adult. Supposedly Discord will delete the ID immediately after confirmation, but I don't trust them with my ID at all. Not to mention they just had a big data breech a couple of months ago. So now my friends and I have to look around for a new chat app to roleplay on.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes me also mad is that the conversation always seems to start around the question of &quot;protecting children from getting exposed to bad stuff on social media&quot;. And then you barely get a discussion about whether removing anonymity on the internet really is the only valid solution to this issue and what it means to give these platforms (or third parties that work together with the platform) more of your personal information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T10:11:29-08:00","id":1558451,"title":"","content":"An additional issue? Grok recently doxxed someone; and the only obvious way Grok could have gotten her info is because Twitter forces you to send a copy of your ID as part of the process for getting imitator accounts taken down. Even if the age verification teams delete your stuff ASAP, it takes a microsecond for a scrapper on their computer to take it anyway.<br /> <br /> There are lots of ways to do this responsibly. The problem is that it requires governments to listen to actual people, not the rich that will lose a bit of revenue in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-28T11:36:17-08:00","id":1558560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558222#post1558222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mad about Discord. Their new policy will require that people send them a picture of an ID confirming that they're an adult. Supposedly Discord will delete the ID immediately after confirmation, but I don't trust them with my ID at all. Not to mention they just had a big data breech a couple of months ago. So now my friends and I have to look around for a new chat app to roleplay on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The increasingly intrusive of online id is proving frustrating, I've started opting out of a lot of online stuff or at least working around it for example I've started alternative methods for music, to the point were I bought a cd player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T08:33:04-08:00","id":1558569,"title":"","content":"Yea.... the world (and internet) is getting pretty crazy these days. With all the age verification craziness and the AI nonsense, the internet seems to be getting worse and worse. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And then there is everything happening in the real world these days... it's all so bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558560#post1558560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The increasingly intrusive of online id is proving frustrating, I've started opting out of a lot of online stuff or at least working around it for example I've started alternative methods for music, to the point were I bought a cd player.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still download a lot of MP3s, but I also also have a stereo system with a turn table and a cd player, so I have a lot of vinyl records and cds! I have a TON of dvds and blu-rays too. Physical media is definitely the way to go these days!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T09:16:49-08:00","id":1558570,"title":"","content":"The hard thing with physical media is that a lot of things don't have readers commonly available anymore. Things like working VHS players are going to be very valuable unless there's a massive shift that will allow them to go back into production.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T12:09:43-08:00","id":1558572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558569#post1558569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still download a lot of MP3s, but I also also have a stereo system with a turn table and a cd player, so I have a lot of vinyl records and cds! I have a TON of dvds and blu-rays too. Physical media is definitely the way to go these days!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> my local tesco does communal drop off. I picked up jeepers creepers 2 which has certain sentimental value. Im gonna drink beer and watch it tonight.<br /> <br /> Ive also re-installed winamp and burnt all my cds onto my pc. As well as onto my phone. Thinking about buying a modern ipod equivelant. The object is my conveniance not luddism.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T14:05:16-08:00","id":1558575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558570#post1558570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hard thing with physical media is that a lot of things don't have readers commonly available anymore. Things like working VHS players are going to be very valuable unless there's a massive shift that will allow them to go back into production.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's a good point! Yea, I don't think there are any new model VHS players (though some new movies have been released on VHS fairly recently).<br /> <br /> But yea, with older media it does get harder to find equipment to play them on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558572#post1558572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my local tesco does communal drop off. I picked up jeepers creepers 2 which has certain sentimental value. Im gonna drink beer and watch it tonight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's cool! Glad they have some good ones! Hope you enjoy the movie again! That one is pretty fun (horrible creator aside). Been a while since I've seen it...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558572#post1558572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ive also re-installed winamp and burnt all my cds onto my pc. As well as onto my phone. Thinking about buying a modern ipod equivelant. The object is my conveniance not luddism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice!! I still have my iPod classic 120GB, and I have the last model iPod touch. I definitely listen to it to more than anything, but I load it up with all the stuff in my actual library. So I'm with you on convenience there. But, there is something fun about playing vinyl records, so I like to listen to music that way when I can.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T14:10:42-08:00","id":1558576,"title":"","content":"The last mass manufacturer of VHS players closed a decade ago. So pretty much everything since has been back-stock or refurbished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T00:01:15-08:00","id":1558582,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that trans people won't be villified because it's seems that the shooter at Tumbler Ridge was a trans woman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T04:21:12-08:00","id":1558583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558576#post1558576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last mass manufacturer of VHS players closed a decade ago. So pretty much everything since has been back-stock or refurbished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Dang. I figured it'd been a while. With the resurgence of old media, I wonder if someone will make a new VCR before too long? I mean cassette tapes are making a come back (for some reason) so it's not out of the realm of possibility..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558582#post1558582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that trans people won't be villified because it's seems that the shooter at Tumbler Ridge was a trans woman.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;They&quot; have been trying to vilify trans women for a quite while now, so if that's the case it'll just be one more thing sadly....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T14:45:46-08:00","id":1558597,"title":"","content":"The problem with VCRs vs. an audio cassette is the output issue. Making a VCR that can output to most modern screens adds a lot of costs to manufacturing that cassettes don't have to deal with since audio jacks basically haven't changed in decades. It's not a technical dilemma in the sense of nobody knows how, it's just an expensive enough fix that you either need people willing to spend a lot of money on it, or a huge boom that can counter the costs with scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T16:21:02-08:00","id":1558599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558597#post1558597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with VCRs vs. an audio cassette is the output issue. Making a VCR that can output to most modern screens adds a lot of costs to manufacturing that cassettes don't have to deal with since audio jacks basically haven't changed in decades. It's not a technical dilemma in the sense of nobody knows how, it's just an expensive enough fix that you either need people willing to spend a lot of money on it, or a huge boom that can counter the costs with scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doh! I didn't even think about that! Yea, a lot of modern tvs just don't have the old inputs a VCR would need. I know you can get converters, but still, not everyone is tech savvy enough to know what to get.<br /> <br /> What makes it kinda sad too is I'm sure there are still lots of a movies and shows on vhs that never got the dvd treatment... hopefully there are people out there digitizing those, but I'm sure there is a lot that'll be lost to time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T22:52:33-08:00","id":1558697,"title":"","content":"It's always strange to hear crazy theories about celebrities when they look or act differently from appearance to public appearance. In this case Jim Carrey has been replaced by a clone because he looks so different from last year.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that he is looking like someone who is 60 years old who has been battling depression for a long time and the medication he is taking is having side effects and he might have had some work done on his face.<br /> <br /> I don't think it was to much work as he wouldn't want to alter his face extensively as it helped shaped his career as a comedic actor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-07-2026, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T13:01:17-07:00","id":1558828,"title":"","content":"Met up with an old friend today who proposed her goth phase was silly and she moved on to better things. (Some modelling in the late 00's)<br /> <br /> As a gothy metal head who still dress' like one a couple of things occured..<br /> <br /> 1) i make more money than her and have a more important job than her.<br /> <br /> 2) shes divorced and her sons a noted fuck up.<br /> <br /> 3) she really doesnt suit blonde and tanned, especially in our mid 40's<br /> <br /> 4) shes somehow got dumber in the last 10 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> This sort of stuff is why i tend to get cold to people who view counter culture a phase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-12-2026, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T05:36:31-07:00","id":1558833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1557361#post1557361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question I have to ask for AI is if the benefits outweigh the drawbacks? Regardless this technology is going to happen and we better be smart on how we handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They absolutely do NOT outweigh them.<br /> <br /> Ram prices have sky rocketed, because the corporations bought up all the ram sticks for their new programs, leaving the general public fighting for scraps.<br /> <br /> Companies like Nvidia want to charge people a subscription service to play video games, and it's not unlimited play time either. That's right, the video game companies want to put a limit on how long gamers are allowed to play their game library within a designated time window.<br /> <br /> And even though it is far from perfect in its current state, we are already seeing various politically motivated groups from around the world trying to use AI generated images and videos for the purpose of spreading propaganda around the internet.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> AI is still in its infancy state, and we're already starting to abuse its power. What do you think's gonna happen when we start upgrading it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T02:43:11-07:00","id":1558848,"title":"","content":"from my outlook, it's not so much the technology as mankind's fallibility, I've already clocked some practical uses for it at my job and when done it works well, I also know a trans person who worked through her self-actualization by creating images of the &quot;real me&quot; which is interesting. Ai is grossly misused so it's clear we're &quot;not ready&quot; for it for want of a better word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T12:40:11-07:00","id":1558854,"title":"","content":"That is sort of the problem though. The bad actors in the technology space purposefully want to lower the bar of use for the cases you're talking about to normalize the technology and its usage.<br /> <br /> But it's not practical. They're running those services at a loss in the hope of capturing economic niches until no humans go into them and we have to us their algorithms if we want anything at all. Then they can start charging the real costs they need to turn a profit, and it will most likely turn out that maintaining humans with the skills would have been cheaper than automating in the end; or trying to recover skills after destroying entry level work for a decade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T13:51:40-07:00","id":1558855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558854#post1558854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is sort of the problem though. The bad actors in the technology space purposefully want to lower the bar of use for the cases you're talking about to normalize the technology and its usage.<br /> <br /> But it's not practical. They're running those services at a loss in the hope of capturing economic niches until no humans go into them and we have to us their algorithms if we want anything at all. Then they can start charging the real costs they need to turn a profit, and it will most likely turn out that maintaining humans with the skills would have been cheaper than automating in the end; or trying to recover skills after destroying entry level work for a decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if politicians, dictators, and activists have already begun to exploit the technology for their own narrative, it's proof that we are not ready for this kind of technology.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the people who using it for that kind of propaganda have proven to be just as lazy as AI artists. Because a closer inspection on these videos often reveals comically massive errors.<br /> <br /> For example, videos of starving children taking a bite of falafel, and then the food remains mysteriously intact.<br /> <br /> Or a vehicle having the ability to phase through a water fountain to escape a drone attack, which somehow leaves the front lawn perfectly unscathed after shooting it with a missile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 03-14-2026, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T14:40:59-07:00","id":1558856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558854#post1558854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is sort of the problem though. The bad actors in the technology space purposefully want to lower the bar of use for the cases you're talking about to normalize the technology and its usage.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, thats more or less my point. The technology will not be used correctly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T15:52:14-07:00","id":1558857,"title":"","content":"And my point is more that the technology is already being misused on a massive scale, and even seemingly harmless or positive use cases are most likely feeding into the problem. Very few people have the knowledge, skills, resources, and time to take advantage of this technology and not end up making the bad situation it's already in worse. That's why the next words after your quote stopped are, &quot;But it's not practical.&quot; Even the &quot;good&quot; uses are still tied to strongly to the past, current, and future misuses to escape the longer term issues at hand. It's not just a human fallibility problem, or a problem with some people using the technology incorrectly. It's acting exactly as certain people want it to, and that includes trying to maximize tying innocuous uses into detrimental ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T16:13:14-07:00","id":1558858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558857#post1558857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And my point is more that the technology is already being misused on a massive scale, and even seemingly harmless or positive use cases are most likely feeding into the problem. Very few people have the knowledge, skills, resources, and time to take advantage of this technology and not end up making the bad situation it's already in worse. That's why the next words after your quote stopped are, &quot;But it's not practical.&quot; Even the &quot;good&quot; uses are still tied to strongly to the past, current, and future misuses to escape the longer term issues at hand. It's not just a human fallibility problem, or a problem with some people using the technology incorrectly. It's acting exactly as certain people want it to, and that includes trying to maximize tying innocuous uses into detrimental ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, we get awesome shit like the Epstein vs Diddy video.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, I definitely do not trust the society we currently live in right now to use this technology responsibly.<br /> <br /> Maybe we'll be more mature in another 20 years. But as it stands right now, shit has gotten way too chaotic for us to be investing resources in this kind of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T14:30:22-07:00","id":1558900,"title":"","content":"Something ive notived wod players do a lot<br /> <br /> <br /> some guy-&quot;im looking for advice on how to [blank]<br /> <br /> 60-90% of the replies-&quot;you shouldnt [blank]<br /> <br /> <br /> Just dont reply if you're not going to be useful. This is a tabletop game, not spelunking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T15:57:13-07:00","id":1558902,"title":"","content":"While I try to avoid posting when I'm staunchly against something like that... I do feel like sometimes, &quot;this is a bad idea, at least as presented,&quot; is a useful response too.<br /> <br /> For example, I regularly respond to, &quot;I'm making my first mage for Mage the Ascension, so I'm going to start with Arete 1 so I can learn the game,&quot; with &quot;you shouldn't do that, because it makes the game harder to learn.&quot; And I try to explain it fully so people can see why I feel that way, but it certainly can come off as slapping people down for &quot;playing wrong.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-27T06:01:47-07:00","id":1559041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1558902#post1558902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I try to avoid posting when I'm staunchly against something like that... I do feel like sometimes, &quot;this is a bad idea, at least as presented,&quot; is a useful response too.<br /> <br /> For example, I regularly respond to, &quot;I'm making my first mage for Mage the Ascension, so I'm going to start with Arete 1 so I can learn the game,&quot; with &quot;you shouldn't do that, because it makes the game harder to learn.&quot; And I try to explain it fully so people can see why I feel that way, but it certainly can come off as slapping people down for &quot;playing wrong.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, and I commend you for doing that.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately a lot of the &quot;True Art Personal Horror&quot; snobs have poisoned the well so thoroughly that it causes a knee-jerk reaction in some people whenever people try to explain things, and even more unfortunately, the inmates are running the asylum when it comes to Personal Horror hyper-purism and have been for quite some time, even before Parawolf came about. That whole &quot;No badwrongfun allowed!&quot; BS.<br /> <br /> V5 and pretty much all the Parawolf stuff is the epitome of that mindset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","valu