er b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559145#post1559145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's always interesting to see folks weaponized nostalgia and overlook that each generation had its challenges and it wasn't the good old days that they wax on about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear ya. I grew up in the 80's and 90's, and while there is some good stuff from those decades, it wasn't all great...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-01T23:24:45-07:00","id":1559177,"title":"","content":"It's amazing how people can be openly racist, homophobic, transphobic and sexist on social media and there channels don't get taken down even when it violates guidelines.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> I saw a reaction channel about Nerdrotic who did a ai generated rap music video about Papa being the new Snape in the upcoming Harry Potter series and has the actor on a broom doing drive bys with a handgun.<br /> <br /> Nerdrotic and his buddy Critical Drinker get upset when they get called out for their bigotry by most sensible people and act like the victims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-02-2026, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-01T23:48:58-07:00","id":1559178,"title":"","content":"As Stephanie Sterling recently said in a video about how the latest Jimquisition video got demonetized for &quot;promoting gambling,&quot; in a critique of how gambling strategies are coming back in video games along side the normalization of online gambling broadly: &quot;YouTube doesn't have rules, it has Community Guidelines.&quot; While YouTube/Google/Alphabet are hardly unique in all of that, the whole point is to shirk responsibility as hosting services for content to moderate said content, and put the blame on the users for not adequately using the impotent tools provided to flag bad actors as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-02T00:30:43-07:00","id":1559179,"title":"","content":"Not to long ago I watched a scientist who talks about social interaction and how Social Media can have a harmful effect on people in general when they are given a diet of outrage and how big tech companies are not your friend and will create tools to worsen the trend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-02T03:55:57-07:00","id":1559180,"title":"","content":"Fundamentally the problem is one of scale. The best and worst parts of social media are driven by the ability to become part of social interactions you never would have otherwise. You can get beyond all the limitations of time, distance, needing extant social connections, etc. This, however, requires scale and discoverability. You need a lot of people on the platform for someone to take a risk and engage with someone they don't have a preexisting social connection with, and a way to communicate some basis for why someone might be worth messaging. The bigger things get, the harder moderation gets, and the overall costs go up broadly. Eventually you need money, and the easiest ways to monetize social media are ads and data collection/sale.<br /> <br /> That profit incentive is where the companies become the problem (corporations are never our friends, even if small ones can let the humans within them overcome that). If you make your money on ads and demographic data on users to sell... then you want to maximize engagement. And promoting negative engagement does that more efficiently than promoting positive engagement.<br /> <br /> The only real hope is that as more people grow up in a world where social media is the norm, there's a expectation change towards desiring positive social interactions that overrides things like fearing losing your community by migrating platforms. If enough users want positive interactions, and can leave for a different platform with low barriers, the incentives change. You can't sell ads and collect data if your users all go because your platform is too ugly. Adequate moderation becomes a necessity for profitability, and overall we'd have a better outcome. But... we're not there yet, and it's not clear if we're even moving in that direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-02T13:02:52-07:00","id":1559187,"title":"","content":"I do hope so Heavy Arms, the big channels like them are seeing a drop in the number of views per video despite having over a million subscribers. The cost of living takes more precendance over a race or gender swapped character from a IP or how we see to be inching closer to WW 3 or how a federal agency is acting with no oversight.<br /> <br /> Talk about not reading the room so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-02T13:04:29-07:00","id":1559188,"title":"","content":"In regards to Harry Potter, I was never super into it as I wasn't the target audience and just knew that it was a popular series of books. But to go after people who are cast in a live action version because they didn't match some preconceived notion is bs. The same with people who cosplay and they have a different skin color then you and etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-02-2026, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-03T17:12:40-07:00","id":1559207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559188#post1559188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to Harry Potter, I was never super into it as I wasn't the target audience and just knew that it was a popular series of books. But to go after people who are cast in a live action version because they didn't match some preconceived notion is bs. The same with people who cosplay and they have a different skin color then you and etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea... I think it's pretty stupid when people get mad about race swapped characters... it's like who cares?<br /> <br /> That said, the creator of Harry Potter is absolute garbage, so I'm definitely not watching this new series...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-03T20:06:05-07:00","id":1559208,"title":"","content":"While I'm also broadly in the camp of not being fussed about race-swapping, there are times where it's a bad choice.<br /> <br /> For Snape in particular there's a few issues with making Snape non-Caucasian. First, he voluntarily joined the racist and fascist bad guys in his youth. Having a black man play a character that decided to join a &quot;pureblood&quot; supremacist organization in a setting where non-European magic is seen as inherently inferior by said group is a whole mess of extra work to do with the character. It's hardly an impossible feat to do, but it's a lot to address for an adaptation of an existing work (and a second adaptation at that). It's also going to make doing the scenes of Snape, Lily, and James as children take on an entirely different tone without a lot more work. Without serious revisions, James will came off as a racist jerkass, Snape an even bigger hypocrite, and Lily either stupid or malicious for not making her feelings for Snape clearer and letting Snape pursue her despite a socially frowned on relationship she wasn't actually interested in anyway. And we're supposed to sympathize with all three of them by the end of the story.<br /> <br /> To keep to Alan Rickman characters...<br /> <br /> If you wanted to remake Die Hard (please, nobody remake Die Hard), you could race swap lots of characters with zero impact on the story. But if you race swap Hans Grubber into an explicitly Palestinian character.. I think everyone would understand that's a bad idea even if you ignore people that are objecting for less than thoughtful reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-04T07:01:15-07:00","id":1559214,"title":"","content":"I'm just waiting for the usual suspects have a fit about British actor Idris Elba playing Man At Arms in the upcoming He-man film. They already fuming at a scene where Adam is at a desk with a name plate with pronouns.<br /> <br /> I find it interesting as I recall that it was religious conservatives went after Masters of The Universe for promoting same sex attractions and occultism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-04T12:29:00-07:00","id":1559218,"title":"","content":"The usual suspects don't really care. I think that's important to remember in all of this. What they're complaining about isn't the &quot;real&quot; issue. It's just a thing to direct their feelings towards. What they are angry about are other things, but for any number of (possible even sympathetic if ruined sympathy by their life choices) reasons they're not actually going to publicly talk about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-04T15:14:29-07:00","id":1559220,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that it's fear that is driving the usual suspects as the world is changing beyond their recognition and can't handle it. I wouldn't put it past it some of them don't believe the stuff they peddle but like the money they make off farming outrage.<br /> <br /> Though some like Ryan Kinnel, Ranting For Vengeance are racist in general. Critical Drinker I don't know for sure if he started out as one, but got indocinatred into such exetrism later or was always one but has let the mask slip?<br /> <br /> On a side note I find it interesting that when they claim that they don't hate strong female characters, they bring up only Sarah Connor and Ellen Ripley. What no love for Dana Scully, Buffy Summers, Xena Warrior Princess or Ziva Divid or some other notable female characters from the same time period?<br /> <br /> It's as if they don't want to acknowledge how limited their knowledge of popular culture really is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-05T00:01:30-07:00","id":1559225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559220#post1559220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a side note I find it interesting that when they claim that they don't hate strong female characters, they bring up only Sarah Connor and Ellen Ripley. What no love for Dana Scully, Buffy Summers, Xena Warrior Princess or Ziva Divid or some other notable female characters from the same time period?<br /> <br /> It's as if they don't want to acknowledge how limited their knowledge of popular culture really is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know damn well people are going to get up and arms about Xena being overly sexualized if people say they want more of her.<br /> <br /> Though before we got a home computer, my whole family used to tune in to watch Buffy, Xena and Hercules together; those were great shows back in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-05T00:11:48-07:00","id":1559226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559177#post1559177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's amazing how people can be openly racist, homophobic, transphobic and sexist on social media and there channels don't get taken down even when it violates guidelines.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> I saw a reaction channel about Nerdrotic who did a ai generated rap music video about Papa being the new Snape in the upcoming Harry Potter series and has the actor on a broom doing drive bys with a handgun.<br /> <br /> Nerdrotic and his buddy Critical Drinker get upset when they get called out for their bigotry by most sensible people and act like the victims.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how the Death Eaters used the killing curse so frequently, people started asking why they don't just carry guns, that actually sounds funny.\u200b<br /> <br /> Also, it's not a preconceive notion. Hermione and Snape are explicitly described in detail as being white in the books. So for the author to turn around and say that they've always been black, and that she just forgot to mention it is a retcon that is blatantly meant to pander to a wider audience. As if to say that the black community can't possibly enjoy the series without some form of representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-05T03:55:45-07:00","id":1559229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559226#post1559226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering how the Death Eaters used the killing curse so frequently, people started asking why they don't just carry guns, that actually sounds funny.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not a preconceive notion. Hermione and Snape are explicitly described in detail as being white in the books. So for the author to turn around and say that they've always been black, and that she just forgot to mention it is a retcon that is blatantly meant to pander to a wider audience. As if to say that the black community can't possibly enjoy the series without some form of representation.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we're on the subject, I think it's a fun fact to point out that Ron is actually smarter in the books than he was in the movies.<br /> <br /> For one example, it's supposed to be Ron who explains to the gang what a &quot;mudblood&quot; is, instead of Hermione. Which makes sense, because Ron is a member of one of the 'sacred 28' families of pure blood wizards, while both of Hermione's parents are muggles.<br /> <br /> How and why does she know wizard slurs!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T04:10:15-07:00","id":1559240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559208#post1559208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm also broadly in the camp of not being fussed about race-swapping, there are times where it's a bad choice.<br /> <br /> For Snape in particular there's a few issues with making Snape non-Caucasian. First, he voluntarily joined the racist and fascist bad guys in his youth. Having a black man play a character that decided to join a &quot;pureblood&quot; supremacist organization in a setting where non-European magic is seen as inherently inferior by said group is a whole mess of extra work to do with the character. It's hardly an impossible feat to do, but it's a lot to address for an adaptation of an existing work (and a second adaptation at that). It's also going to make doing the scenes of Snape, Lily, and James as children take on an entirely different tone without a lot more work. Without serious revisions, James will came off as a racist jerkass, Snape an even bigger hypocrite, and Lily either stupid or malicious for not making her feelings for Snape clearer and letting Snape pursue her despite a socially frowned on relationship she wasn't actually interested in anyway. And we're supposed to sympathize with all three of them by the end of the story.<br /> <br /> To keep to Alan Rickman characters...<br /> <br /> If you wanted to remake Die Hard (please, nobody remake Die Hard), you could race swap lots of characters with zero impact on the story. But if you race swap Hans Grubber into an explicitly Palestinian character.. I think everyone would understand that's a bad idea even if you ignore people that are objecting for less than thoughtful reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeaa... I was thinking about saying something similar about Snape, but I wasn't sure how much Harry Potter I wanted to bring up. But I'm with you... that is on character that seems a little messed up to race swap, because the backstory of the character doesn't jell with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T06:54:21-07:00","id":1559244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559208#post1559208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm also broadly in the camp of not being fussed about race-swapping, there are times where it's a bad choice.<br /> <br /> For Snape in particular there's a few issues with making Snape non-Caucasian. First, he voluntarily joined the racist and fascist bad guys in his youth. Having a black man play a character that decided to join a &quot;pureblood&quot; supremacist organization in a setting where non-European magic is seen as inherently inferior by said group is a whole mess of extra work to do with the character. It's hardly an impossible feat to do, but it's a lot to address for an adaptation of an existing work (and a second adaptation at that). It's also going to make doing the scenes of Snape, Lily, and James as children take on an entirely different tone without a lot more work. Without serious revisions, James will came off as a racist jerkass, Snape an even bigger hypocrite, and Lily either stupid or malicious for not making her feelings for Snape clearer and letting Snape pursue her despite a socially frowned on relationship she wasn't actually interested in anyway. And we're supposed to sympathize with all three of them by the end of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is it stated that they view different forms of magic as being inferior? Hogwarts may be the primary school of focus, but it's located in Scotland. If I remember correctly, there are about 6 other schools around the world, including one located in Africa that has a reputation for students becoming animagi at remarkably young ages. They also practice magic without wands, learning to cast spells with their bare hands.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then there were the students from the French and Russian schools that appeared in the Tri-Wizard tournament, that received a very warm welcome at Hogwarts.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> Voldemort and his Death Eaters were supremacists in the sense that they mistakenly believed your upward magical potential was linked back to blood purity. Those who came from unbroken, magical bloodlines were inherently superior wizards to those who mingled with muggles. That's the entire premise behind the &quot;Sacred 28&quot; families, in that they are all pureblood lineages.<br /> <br /> <br /> However, it turns out that the ability to use magic is a genetic trait. Either you have the ability to use magic, or you don't. Your pedigree has nothing to do with how strong your potential is, which Voldemort ironically proved by having the wizard Nazi's absolutely terrified of him, despite being a halfblood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T09:58:04-07:00","id":1559248,"title":"","content":"I really don't feel like having some sort of deep dive conversation about the political narratives of the Potter franchise. The reference I made was in supplemental material written after the main books when they wanted to world build more of the setting (which is also where 99% of the information on the non-European schools is officially written).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T11:38:03-07:00","id":1559250,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that it might go against the rules of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T11:46:28-07:00","id":1559279,"title":"","content":"I guess what struck me about Nerdrotic ai generated video of Papa Esudo flying around on a broom stick and shooting up the place is how is that Snape is a wizard and wouldn't need such tools to mess up your day.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that Gary from Nerdrotic is employing American stereotypes of black people to an English actor and that the country of Great Britain has very tough gun control laws.<br /> <br /> I shouldn't be shocked as he more or less admits that he sells outrage and doesn't care about whom he hurts in the process be it Brie Larson, Daisy Ridley, Rachel Zeigler and now Milly Alcock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-11-2026, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T14:54:54-07:00","id":1559281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559279#post1559279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that Gary from Nerdrotic is employing American stereotypes of black people to an English actor and that the country of Great Britain has very tough gun control laws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems pretty easy to get a knife though. I've been seeing a lot of satire recently about how frequently people get stabbed in England.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T18:23:20-07:00","id":1559282,"title":"","content":"It's pretty easy to get a knife pretty much anywhere humans life full time. They're kinda super-useful tools that have been around for thousands of years for a reason.<br /> <br /> Knife crimes in the UK are also about 10% of the per capita rate as the US despite all of the US's guns... it's almost like violent crime is more complicated or something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-08T03:19:02-07:00","id":1559286,"title":"","content":"People will always find ways to make weapons out of anything and if I remember correctly there is three types of crimes.<br /> <br /> Crimes of passion, crimes of profit and crimes of compulsion .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-08T15:00:08-07:00","id":1559294,"title":"","content":"People will get creative with weapons... but lets not lose perspective of effectiveness and realistic dangers posed by different options.<br /> <br /> As for types of crime? There isn't any sort of objective thing there. Any classification of crimes is arbitrary and there are lots of schemes depending on what you're basing the classifications on (motive, possible punishment, impact of the crime, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T00:36:31-07:00","id":1559340,"title":"","content":"It is interesting that we hold women in the entertainment industry to a different standard then their male counterparts.<br /> <br /> You know that we grade women more on their attractiveness factor then how good they are in playing a role be it a superhero, horror or action film.<br /> <br /> I can't think of to many men who were subjected to the same type of scrutiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T11:04:02-07:00","id":1559485,"title":"","content":"This isn't really a vent per say, I'm just disappointed that the Buffy the Vampire Slayer revival isn't going to happen and I was curious to see a older and wiser Buffy Summers and what happened to her and her friends after the end of season 7 and if they would use any material from the Dark Horse comics line.<br /> <br /> So was anyone else looking forward to the revival when it was announced and disappointed that it's not going to happen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T15:54:16-07:00","id":1559491,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit disappointed, but my expectations went down when we saw both Buffy and Firefly revivals both getting announced around the same time. Considering that both are so linked to Joss Whedon, but the revivals include people that clearly hate working with him, it just hit my doubt button pretty hard that everything was as lined up as necessary to make sure things are going to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T23:16:54-07:00","id":1559498,"title":"","content":"I understand what you mean Heavy Arms in regards to how Joss Whedon is viewed now in light of the Justice League movie and how he treated the actor who played Cyborg and that on the set of Buffy that he wasn't allowed to be near the late Michelle Trachtenberg without someone close by and Charisma Carpenter certainly had her issues with him.<br /> <br /> Even if Joss Whedon didn't have these troubles I had my doubts that he could capture lighting in a bottle twice as that show came at the right time and place and would all the cast be willing to reprise their roles?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T14:17:13-07:00","id":1559508,"title":"","content":"Yeah, though I think the reason Firefly is probably still going to end up with something is that they decided to go animated (and there's a lot more space in the Firefly setting to do things as there was just the one season and the movie for people that didn't read the novels and comics). Doing animated means it's a lot easier to work around the schedules of different cast members (and possibly avoid any IRL person conflicts). The Buffy revival seemed more to be the more ambitious of the two, and a lot of speculation seems to point to Hulu just pulling the plug as it became clear the situation was more complicated than they realized (somehow).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-19T04:29:21-07:00","id":1559517,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this qualifies as political but I got banned from reddit for noting that the LGB alliance seems mostly to be old women. Under promoting identity-based hate or attacks. You can't make this shit up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T01:01:18-07:00","id":1559578,"title":"","content":"I vehemently despise the pronunciation of &quot;<i>Camaria&quot;</i> that seems to have taken root in V5.<br /> <br /> I don't give a damn if it's supposed to be phonetically correct. The mere sound of it is physically offensive to my ears. Every time I hear it, I can't help but mentally cringe / wince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T04:22:29-07:00","id":1559581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559578#post1559578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vehemently despise the pronunciation of &quot;<i>Camaria&quot;</i> that seems to have taken root in V5.<br /> <br /> I don't give a damn if it's supposed to be phonetically correct. The mere sound of it is physically offensive to my ears. Every time I hear it, I can't help but mentally cringe / wince.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea... I'm kind of with you. I know that's probably correct, but I've said it with 'rilla' for so long, that just sounds right.<br /> <br /> Same to me with the Sabbat. Years ago my group always pronounced it like Sabbath (of course drop the h), so when I hear Sa-bot, it just sounds weird...lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T11:31:58-07:00","id":1559585,"title":"","content":"I honestly wish more TTRPG settings would vary these sorts of terms. Why would Spanish speaking vampires, English speaking vampires, Chinese speaking vampires, and Swahili speaking vampires all say a word the same way? That's not how reality works in the slightest. Hell, the US and the UK have English words that are said completely differently. Trying to force one &quot;right&quot; way of saying a word on the setting just makes it feel faker in practice.<br /> <br /> Though this also comes from someone that is reminded on a very frequent basis that trying to &quot;correct&quot; people is pointless. You get used to a way of saying something the way you get used to it, and that's right for you. How other people do it is right for them. That's just culture and language in action. Though I would ask to maybe be careful in express things. These words are not things the WoD authors made up. They come from real world cultures. Telling someone that grew up with a word as part of their culture that you only know because of a game that hearing it the way native speakers would say it is actively offensive to you? That's pretty messed up if you stop to think about. You can express you preferences without that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> I mean, how does Sabbat make any sense English language? It's Shabbath or Shabbat in Hebrew, and Sabbaton in Greek... why did you not just go with one of the two instead of mixing them up even more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T13:27:36-07:00","id":1559587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559585#post1559585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Telling someone that grew up with a word as part of their culture that you only know because of a game that hearing it the way native speakers would say it is actively offensive to you? That's pretty messed up if you stop to think about. You can express you preferences without that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not as simple as just <i>&quot;I prefer this specific pronunciation method.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> As I said, &quot;Camaria&quot; makes me <b>physically uncomfortable</b> when I hear it.<br /> <br /> It doesn't just sound wrong, it also feels wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though in the case of Sabbat, I don't care either way. They're both fine for me.<br /> <br /> Edit: If a pack of vampires told me I was now drafted into the Sabbaton, I'd probably be excited. They make learning history awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 04-23-2026, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T17:07:15-07:00","id":1559588,"title":"","content":"People aren't born with some sort of allergy to word pronunciation. Developing the kind of dislike you're describing isn't necessarily purposeful, but it's not something you can blame on other people either. &quot;Camaria&quot; is the original way to say the word, it's the way over 600 million people on Earth are going to say it because that's still how you'd say it in Spanish at least. You're calling that physically offensive, and shirking the fact that it could only get that way because you walked down the path of encoding a preference too firmly. Nobody can just force you to have that reaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T17:51:19-07:00","id":1559589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559588#post1559588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People aren't born with some sort of allergy to word pronunciation. Developing the kind of dislike you're describing isn't necessarily purposeful, but it's not something you can blame on other people either. &quot;Camaria&quot; is the original way to say the word, it's the way over 600 million people on Earth are going to say it because that's still how you'd say it in Spanish at least. You're calling that physically offensive, and shirking the fact that it could only get that way because you walked down the path of encoding a preference too firmly. Nobody can just force you to have that reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're making baseless speculations.<br /> <br /> Usually, when I don't like how something is pronounced, it's because it was originally introduced to me in a different way, and my mind just got accustomed to hearing it pronounced that way. Even if there are other pronunciation methods, I'm just used to the first version and prefer to use it as my default.<br /> <br /> The many different ways of pronouncing Sabbat, for instance. I personally prefer to go with Sabbat, but don't care if somebody decides to use Sabbath instead.<br /> <br /> Yet when it comes to Camarilla, removing the L's becomes irritating to listen to.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, most of the characters in Bloodlines 2 decided to use Camarilla, with the only exception I can think of being the Lasombra mentor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T19:22:37-07:00","id":1559590,"title":"","content":"What baseless speculation did I make exactly?<br /> <br /> Camarilla, is a Spanish word that means, &quot;little room,&quot; (camera is the Latin based root for room, -illa is a diminutive). It gained the meaning of a secret group of private advisors to a powerful individual through various cultural linguistic means just like the idiom of &quot;back room deals&quot; in English came about to imply secret meetings away from a small group of elite people. So, &quot;camaria&quot; being the original and Spanish way to pronounce it isn't baseless or speculative. The number of Spanish speakers is something I just looked up quickly because the exact number according to any specific authority didn't seem important enough to bother with to get past baseless.<br /> <br /> Humans don't have intrinsic physical reactions to normal vocal range sounds; not sure what's baseless or speculative about that. You called my post baseless why basically agreeing that it's a learned reaction not a born one. I highly doubt the words tortilla or quesadilla cause the same reaction in you; but that would at least be speculation. Any auditory processing issues would also hit far more than one word and wouldn't be linked to first exposure bias as is this case but an individual's existing processing difficulties across the board.<br /> <br /> And yeah, you're dodging that it's not something forced on you. It's a habit and a preference to you own admission. You're the only explanation for how it went from &quot;different from my preference&quot; to &quot;causes physical discomfort.&quot; Even if you didn't do that on purpose, it's still you in the end that did it. It's not baseless since there's no mechanism to sit down and force someone to learn to experience pain from a single specific word being said one way over another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T22:10:32-07:00","id":1559591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559590#post1559590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What baseless speculation did I make exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>The part where you insinuate that I was trained or conditioned to find the word offensive. As if I would actively choose to develop an audio tick for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> That is most certainly not the case. V5 was the first time I came across the phrase, and it immediately did not sit right with me.<br /> <br /> Camaria sounds wrong, it feels wrong, and I don't like that it's becoming increasingly more common as of late.<br /> <br /> As for humans having a physical reaction to vocal range, you'd be surprised. When I was much younger, I could taste smells. Not sure how that works, but it did. I could also tell if a TV was turned on 3 rooms away, by sensing the output of static electricity from the screen.<br /> <br /> Sadly, these heightened senses faded over time as I got older. But they were cool super powers while they lasted.<br /> <br /> ------------------<br /> <br /> I was told Camarilla meant &quot;The Backscratchers.&quot; As in <i>&quot;you scratch my back, I scratch yours.&quot;</i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T01:37:40-07:00","id":1559594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559591#post1559591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part where you insinuate that I was trained or conditioned to find the word offensive. As if I would actively choose to develop an audio tick for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're just ignoring my wording or worse. Gotcha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5 was the first time I came across the phrase, and it immediately did not sit right with me. </div> </div> </div>The idea that you are seriously claiming it is actually causing you physical discomfort instead of that being hyperbole doesn't mesh with human anatomy or language acquisition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Camaria sounds wrong, it feels wrong, and I don't like that it's becoming increasingly more common as of late. </div> </div> </div>Pronouncing it as &quot;camaria&quot; is a centuries old thing. That you keep ignoring that this is a real word with a real history that you're disrespecting because of your preferences is what I was calling out. Treating it as off puttingly new because it's new to you doesn't make it &quot;wrong.&quot; I don't care if you use the &quot;L&quot; version in your games, non-Spanish speakers have been saying it that way for 200 years too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for humans having a physical reaction to vocal range, you'd be surprised. </div> </div> </div>Doubtful, and certainly not by your examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I was much younger, I could taste smells. Not sure how that works, but it did. </div> </div> </div>Everyone does this to some degree. The vast majority of what people perceive as &quot;taste&quot; or &quot;flavor&quot; is actually aroma stimuli not something coming from the taste buds in the mouth. Smells we associate with specific taste-experiences help prime the body for the assumed type of interaction. Your brain making you experience the sensation of eating your favorite cookie when you smell it stimulates increase salivation to increase the amount of enzymes in your body that break down the simple carbohydrates in sugars and simple starches. Your brain triggering a similar response when exposed to high sulfur odors (whatever nasty food that gets linked to, rotten eggs frequently) primes the gag reflex because many harmful bacteria you don't want to eat give off sulfur gases even if sulfur itself is generally harmless to ingest.<br /> <br /> Children that are very sensitive to this tend to grow out of it as their palates expand and they eat more diverse foods as that forces the brain to assume less based on initial scent impressions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could also tell if a TV was turned on 3 rooms away, by sensing the output of static electricity from the screen. </div> </div> </div>This is a reasonably common phenomenon as well. Children hear more of the higher register, meaning they can pick up on electric whines adults don't. We literally grow out of this as our skulls mature and our ear canals change shape until that range goes away for the vast majority of people that experience this for a significant part of their childhood.<br /> <br /> I never lost this, which actually sucks because that's directly linked to ear and sinus infections as the passages in my head are narrower than they should be and thus get clogged up more easily. It was also a lot less fun when TVs weren't flat screens because powering up a CRT is something you can hear from other people's houses compared to the static discharging off of any of the flat screens most people use these days.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was told Camarilla meant &quot;The Backscratchers.&quot; As in <i>&quot;you scratch my back, I scratch yours.&quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>Given the spread of the word throughout Europe in the 1800s I'm sure in some languages and cultures it has that meaning because loan words vary in implication like that, but you have the Internet, you can just look up the basic definition if you think I'm misrepresenting it. Most definitions though stick with the idea of a camarilla as an established - if likely informal - group not just people that broadly like to trade in favors. It's a meaning that came from royal courtly politics... so horse-trading and scheming are usually baked into the concept in some fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T06:48:56-07:00","id":1559600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559594#post1559594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the spread of the word throughout Europe in the 1800s I'm sure in some languages and cultures it has that meaning because loan words vary in implication like that, but you have the Internet, you can just look up the basic definition if you think I'm misrepresenting it. Most definitions though stick with the idea of a camarilla as an established - if likely informal - group not just people that broadly like to trade in favors. It's a meaning that came from royal courtly politics... so horse-trading and scheming are usually baked into the concept in some fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can attest it does.<br /> <br /> I also think that meaning and &quot;little room&quot; meaning are symbolicaly related. In spanish at least, words that define &quot;closed areas where people meet&quot; are often words used to define groups of close association, usually with connotations of groups that do scheme and do secret things.<br /> <br /> Like with &quot;conclave&quot; (ethimology of that word it's &quot;with key&quot;, as in a room closed with a key) , &quot;circle&quot; (inner circle, red circle), conciliabulo or conventiculo (words for places that held assambly, but that ended becoming related more with illegal reunions than any sort of formal reunions).<br /> <br /> So, historically, calling an elite of scheemers &quot;the small room&quot; seems on board to me<br /> <br /> For the reccord, not all Spanish speakes pronounce the same way. On Argentina &quot;-illa&quot; and &quot;-ia&quot; are pronounced very different, and &quot;-illa&quot; isn't a common diminutive (I'm not sure if I've ever tougth of the Camarilla as &quot;small room&quot; 'til it came on this thread - tho it's easy to see how it checks out), we use &quot;-ita&quot; instead, but since that diminutive on Argentina has a meaning of <i>affection </i>(small versions of things are often cute) I'm sort of glad that the vampire conspiration ain't called the &quot;Camarita&quot;, or it would be impossible to take it seriously :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":".  clarification 04-24-2026, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T09:50:12-07:00","id":1559604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559594#post1559594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea that you are seriously claiming it is actually causing you physical discomfort instead of that being hyperbole doesn't mesh with human anatomy or language acquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know my body better than you, dude.<br /> <br /> If I say it's causing me problems, then it's causing me problems. Regardless of what you believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T10:00:03-07:00","id":1559605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559594#post1559594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pronouncing it as &quot;camaria&quot; is a centuries old thing. That you keep ignoring that this is a real word with a real history that you're disrespecting because of your preferences is what I was calling out. Treating it as off puttingly new because it's new to you doesn't make it &quot;wrong.&quot; I don't care if you use the &quot;L&quot; version in your games, non-Spanish speakers have been saying it that way for 200 years too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not the word is real and has history behind it is completely irrelevant to the subject. It does absolutely nothing to change the fact that the word makes me uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> I have also stressed the point that it is this specific word that is the cause of the issue. As none of the other iterations in the WoD lexicon have had the same effect on me. At least none at the time of me writing this reply.<br /> <br /> This thread was supposed to be a place for us to vent our frustrations, not be subjected to a lecture about how we're guilty of 'wrong think.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 04-24-2026, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-29T19:11:09-07:00","id":1559667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not the word is real and has history behind it is completely irrelevant to the subject. It does absolutely nothing to change the fact that the word makes me uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually and hilariously, it does a lot to change the fact the word makes you uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Namely, it makes it clear that the discomfort is self-inflicted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-29T19:12:50-07:00","id":1559668,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Please drop this and let's discuss something else. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-29T19:17:09-07:00","id":1559669,"title":"","content":"Can do!<br /> <br /> One of the ways I can tell I'm getting older is just how much road trips are starting to weigh on me. I used to be able to do a 10-hour trip and immediately move into loading up a moving truck, now apparently I need to wait for the next day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-29T23:16:19-07:00","id":1559672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559667#post1559667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually and hilariously, it does a lot to change the fact the word makes you uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Namely, it makes it clear that the discomfort is self-inflicted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fuck off.<br /> <br /> I'll remember this the next time you mention any particular words you have a problem with.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------<br /> <br /> Anyways, why did Hotpockets decide to remove the protective holders from their packages?<br /> <br /> The box tells me that they did it to improve quality and taste, but I have no idea how the hell that works.<br /> <br /> All it did was force me to pick up a freshly cooked, scalding Hotpocket with my bare hands!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-30T03:36:37-07:00","id":1559677,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>I wasn't kidding. Take the day off. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-01T04:52:12-07:00","id":1559687,"title":"","content":"I got pissed at some people giving me shit for mourning the death of David Allan Coe the other day, calling him a racist and getting on their moral high horse towards both him and his fans, and accusing him of being someone more in the vein of Johnny Rebel, which is untrue.<br /> <br /> First off, I'm Black so miss me with all that shit.<br /> <br /> Secondly, their main bits of evidence were that some of his songs (namely &quot;If That Ain't Country&quot; and &quot;She Said Someday, I'll Understand&quot;) contained a certain slur that I'm not going to say here because I ain't opening that can of worms, but they tend to ignore the context in those songs.<br /> <br /> &quot;If That Ain't Country&quot; says it once as part of a very antiquated simile (and there's a radio edit that changes it to &quot;Working like a slave&quot;, for crying out loud)<br /> <br /> &quot;She Said Someday, I'll Understand&quot; is a song written for the purposes of shock humor and ironic satire and IIRC, was written by a Black man originally with the intent of a White guy singing it to make the joke work better (the song's about a guy whose wife leaves him for a Black guy) and that song's on one of his &quot;X-Rated&quot; albums that also has songs about banging Linda Lovelace or songs with lyrics such as &quot;I was into whips and things and she was into pain&quot;, so it's not meant to be taken that seriously. It's shock jock humor.<br /> <br /> The difference between David Allan Coe and Johnny Rebel is that David Allan Coe was an outlaw who had a &quot;nothing sacred&quot; attitude and was even pro-LGBTQ at a time where that was not the norm, and he was willing to go for the low blows for the sake of shock, while Johnny Rebel's music only existed to serve as literal propaganda for the KKK.<br /> <br /> IMHO, there's a massive gulf of difference between saying a slur in an ironic shock jock context and saying a slur as part of a propaganda effort for actual violent hate groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-02T16:26:58-07:00","id":1559706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559669#post1559669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can do!<br /> <br /> One of the ways I can tell I'm getting older is just how much road trips are starting to weigh on me. I used to be able to do a 10-hour trip and immediately move into loading up a moving truck, now apparently I need to wait for the next day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me about it! I take a 2 hour car trip and my freaking back and legs hurt! Getting old suuuuckks..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-02T22:44:14-07:00","id":1559710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559687#post1559687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got pissed at some people giving me shit for mourning the death of David Allan Coe the other day,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I haven't heard that name in decades!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-04T02:29:45-07:00","id":1559754,"title":"","content":"Getting old does suck Me. Gone when you see how young your co workers are getting and you have no idea where the time went.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-04T15:04:51-07:00","id":1559774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559754#post1559754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting old does suck Me. Gone when you see how young your co workers are getting and you have no idea where the time went.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all about perception; when I go to college-campuses to read at their libraries, I feel out of place, even though, I can still pass as a student; they often ask me, when I'm looking for a particular book, &quot;Just use your school-card and you can access the database&quot;. Me, &quot;um, I lost that, like, decades ago&quot;. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-04T15:49:13-07:00","id":1559778,"title":"","content":"That sucks that you got heat for mourning the death of David Allen Coe. All by the same type of people who went after Ozzy Osbourne for being a &quot;devil&quot; worshipper because of a few songs and not knowing about how rumors are not facts Matt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T15:01:52-07:00","id":1559794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559778#post1559778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sucks that you got heat for mourning the death of David Allen Coe. All by the same type of people who went after Ozzy Osbourne for being a &quot;devil&quot; worshipper because of a few songs and not knowing about how rumors are not facts Matt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to joke that we could synthesize a cure for Covid out of Ozzy's blood, referring to the time he bit the head off a bat.<br /> <br /> It sucks that legends like Ozzy and Dio are gone now, but at least their music will continue to live on. Far longer, I think, than the crap being produced today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T21:44:38-07:00","id":1559798,"title":"","content":"It's amazing how Ozzy Osbourne lived as long as he did considering all the drugs and alcohol he ingested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T23:46:13-07:00","id":1559800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1559798#post1559798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arro