posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560239#post1560239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure im arguing with someone using chatgt ai for their arguements on vtm reddit. Whats disapointing is how high the rating is. Its also frustrating im not 100%</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh.. sorry about that. I'm getting real tired of all this AI BS. But lately, at least for me, if I suspect it's AI then it usually is. But I'm with you, I do hate sometimes that's it getting harder to tell...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-28T06:14:09-07:00","id":1560243,"title":"","content":"I have recently discovered that you can circumvent Youtube's ads by watching the videos through Bing.<br /> <br /> It's inconvenient; but if it means that I don't have to watch that disgusting baby commercial anymore, I'll tolerate it!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-29T01:49:50-07:00","id":1560252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560243#post1560243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have recently discovered that you can circumvent Youtube's ads by watching the videos through Bing.<br /> <br /> It's inconvenient; but if it means that I don't have to watch that disgusting baby commercial anymore, I'll tolerate it!</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to use brave browser which youtube cannot detect. The sheer scale of adverts and amount of slop content means they dont deserve my time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T09:28:42-07:00","id":1560409,"title":"","content":"For thread rules I'm going to be a bit vague... but I really despise how much gambling apps hiding as &quot;trading&quot; apps as somehow becoming part of US news sources. People are literally treating odds shifting strongly in favor of one result over the other as the same as what's going on in reality. The odds heavily going in the favor of one sports team over another doesn't mean the game is a blowout, it just means nobody expects a last minute turn around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T10:41:42-07:00","id":1560411,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that I never got the gambling craving as I knew the odds are not in your favor.<br /> <br /> Not really a rant, but Hasbro has some Transformers toys coming up and I don't know what I know what I should buy with my \ud83d\udcb8\ud83d\udcb0 as it's expensive. I'll probably get Swindle for sure and the new version of Armada Megatron.<br /> <br /> To many choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T19:13:17-07:00","id":1560417,"title":"","content":"An actual rant. YouTube is proving once again how their enforcement of terms of services is a joke is going after Multiversal Wisdom with demonization because they didn't like his green Batcave background and despite his efforts of changing it. It wasn't enough and he has to take down a year's worth of videos and redo them.<br /> <br /> He is not a drama channel and is a fan of the Dark Knight who does a series of videos where he comes up with rehabilitation, contingency plans and his thoughts on other heroes and characters from other places. Lately he used Lex Luthor in a couple of videos and had Batman talking to Wolverine or Deadpool in a pub about what is happening in their work lives so to speak.<br /> <br /> It's a good channel and doesn't deserve this behaviour from YouTube when you have channels that clearly spout homophobic, transphobic, antisemitic and racist remarks in their video titles and go on tirades and nothing happens.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T20:57:51-07:00","id":1560421,"title":"","content":"I really want to try getting into Mage the Ascension, as its free form approach to spell casting sounds both fascinating and entertaining.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, most of the Mystic Traditions are grounded in cultural identities that I know fuck all about, and haven't the time or patience to do more in depth research.<br /> <br /> At best, I might be able to pull off a Celestial Chorister. But that would require me to lean heavily into the Christianity angel, and I've already renounced the faith twice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How does spell casting look in terms of Mage: the Awakening? Is it still as free form as Ascension? One video I watched about it said they reduced the system to &quot;D&amp;D spell casting,&quot; but I'm not sure what they meant by that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-07T01:10:19-07:00","id":1560423,"title":"","content":"While a full comparison of Ascension and Awakening should probably go somewhere else, Awakening is mechanically very similar to Ascension, but metaphysically very different.<br /> <br /> Awakening is more mechanically cohesive and has far, far more examples (and ones that actually follow the rules clearly) in 2e alone than Ascension does over four editions combined. But it's still a broad set of magical &quot;traits&quot; that cover wide domains of reality, where your rating in each dictates what level of control you have and beyond that you can try to do whatever spells you want (though realistically just because you can come up with the idea doesn't mean you'll have the stats and situational bonuses necessary to actually do it).<br /> <br /> To achieve this though - and it neatly addresses a specific concern mentioned - by stripping the major factions of specific real world cultural identities. This means there's no need to understand the dance of Paradigms and Practices that define the factions of Ascension in Ascension's metaphysical framework and then balancing portraying identities hooked into those belief systems on top of it. Awakening's factions are based on how the groups of mages view magic and what to do with it beyond strong roots in specific non-Mage philosophies (there are some roots so they're not completely divorced). There's plenty of taste that's going to go into how people feel about this side of it that tends to dictate how the application in the actual rules &quot;feels.&quot; For example the &quot;D&amp;D spell casting&quot; comparison has nothing to do with the actual spell casting rules. It has to do with the amount of spells in the Awakening core books (enough that many players will rarely need to invent their own), and how they're presented without the flavor or flair that comes from examples rooted in a specific faction's cultural identity. So instead of Ascension core books with less example spells but ones with lots more flavor to them that invites players into the tone and inventiveness of free form magic, you get a long list of blander spells that have labels and keywords to help clearly show how they derive from the base improvised casting rules.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the biggest difference in all of this is that Ascension front loads a lot of things when you're making a character, where Awakening takes a more opt in approach. In Ascension you have to make a mage with a whole magical philosophy that ties into their cultural identity so they have some way to comprehend the power they possess. In Awakening you can start as a bland fantasy wizard that just casts the spells they've been taught, follow all the steps to be safe from backlashes, and so on... but you're giving up an insane amount of power to do so. Awakening mages that build up a magical persona that embodies their ideals and beliefs - and a persona that can mesh with at least their cabal-mates - through cultural expressions gains a lot of power for taking that root; but there's always risk as it can be used against you too. This also goes for spell casting in general as Awakening puts more risk in how strong your effect is than if it's overtly magic in the eyes of normies or not. If you want to spam kinetic blasts that are basically on par with a decent gun, your magic is unlikely to ever bite you in the ass... but if you want to push that into an artillery shot that can level a building in a single blast... well you just have to be willing to take the risks of exerting that kind of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-07T02:57:31-07:00","id":1560425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560423#post1560423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a full comparison of Ascension and Awakening should probably go somewhere else, Awakening is mechanically very similar to Ascension, but metaphysically very different.<br /> <br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the lengthy explanation. In hindsight, probably should have asked this in one of the Mage threads.<br /> <br /> So, it sounds like Awakening is more stream lined and newbie friendly compared to its predecessor.<br /> <br /> I've also heard that 2nd edition made Paradox backlash significantly easier to deal with, by giving players the option to shunt its effects onto the people around you.<br /> <br /> Which sounds like a very good way for a mage to succumb to hubris and find themselves surrounded by pissed off rivals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-07T03:50:40-07:00","id":1560428,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say streamlined. Some parts are (esp. Awakening 2e over 1e), but other parts aren't. What it is, is more mechanically rigorous. That means there's more charts to consult and variables to figure out, to make up for a lot less of the ST just picking a number based on their best interpretation of the game. Some newbies are going to be OK with the extra steps and math involved, others are going to find it abstract and hard to turn the numbers into characters compared to Ascension's approach. There's a lot of preference and taste involved in how people feel about these sorts of priority shifts. The CofD in general also tends to rely on systems that work best when the players are actively pushing for their use. Some players are very into player-facing systems and others do better with ones that leave more in the hands of the ST. Awakening is pretty friendly for people that are already familiar with TTRPG play, but I'm not sure I'd recommend it for a brand new player or even someone that's dipped their toes into D&amp;D and is looking to try something else.<br /> <br /> Both editions of Awakening allow for mages to either contain Paradox (generally that means eating damage) or letting the backlash happen as it will. Releasing a backlash doesn't mean you get ot point at someone else and they get to deal with your problem. It means handing the ST a suite of options to make your character's life &quot;interesting&quot; that you have no further say in what the outcome will look like; which will also earn you enemies even if a mix of directly (like summoning Abyssal entities) or indirectly (like having the Guardians up your ass because they really hate people that feed the Abyss frequently). But yes, it is on purpose designed to reward the players for engaging with the obsessions and hubris of mages by making it mechanically fun (and usually some sort of reward) to let cool but bad things happen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-07T04:50:27-07:00","id":1560429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560428#post1560428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, it is on purpose designed to reward the players for engaging with the obsessions and hubris of mages by making it mechanically fun (and usually some sort of reward) to let cool but bad things happen</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Losing is FUN!&quot;</i> - Rogue-like players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-07T14:07:58-07:00","id":1560438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560421#post1560421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want to try getting into Mage the Ascension, as its free form approach to spell casting sounds both fascinating and entertaining.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, most of the Mystic Traditions are grounded in cultural identities that I know fuck all about, and haven't the time or patience to do more in depth research.<br /> <br /> At best, I might be able to pull off a Celestial Chorister. But that would require me to lean heavily into the Christianity angel, and I've already renounced the faith twice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just play a Hollow One and make up your own pseudo-tradition.<br /> <br /> Problem solved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-07T22:44:30-07:00","id":1560446,"title":"","content":"Not a vent, but sad news in the Buffy The Vampire Slayer fandom with the passing of Anthony Head whom played Rubert Giles in the series as well the Nabob coffee series of commericals where I first saw of him..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T00:13:45-07:00","id":1560651,"title":"","content":"Just a bit of a rant.<br /> <br /> I'm annoyed at how badly Disney has mishandled Star Wars. We just had the first Star Wars movie in almost a decade, it barely entered the cultural consciousness and it has the worst box office performance of any Star Wars movie to date. You'd think after nearly a decade people might be a bit more excited to see Star Wars on the big screen. Being part of a series that only people with Disney+ can watch definitely affected how many people wanted to go see the movie. If you hadn't watched the Mandalorian, why would you want to watch Mandalorian and Grogu? <br /> <br /> I think Disney royally screwed up with the sequel movies. Nobody really cares that much about that era, not even the people working for the company. So everything they've spent the last 10 years on has been fiddling around in the pre-sequel era. The problem is, the people who liked the sequel movies and didn't care about the stuff before it don't really care about the pre-sequel stuff. And the people who didn't like the sequel stuff, it's hard to get invested in all of the stuff leading up the sequels knowing that, for example, Luke's Jedi Academy will get wiped out, Coruscant gets destroyed, the New Republic collapses, etc. <br /> <br /> Next year, finally, exactly 10 years after Rise of Skywalker, we're getting Jedi Starfighter which will be the first major piece of media set in the post-sequel setting, but I doubt it's going to do very well either. For most people their main interest in Star Wars is the Jedi and their cool lightsabers.<br /> <br /> Really, I think Disney needs to just step up and start moving the franchise into the post-sequel setting. If building directly out of the sequels is too difficult, then just do a time skip. The next movie could take place 60 years after Rise of Skywalker. Rey's old or retired, but her Jedi Academy is has been doing well. Then Disney can start fresh in a new Star Wars era and a new setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T16:19:03-07:00","id":1560686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560651#post1560651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Disney royally screwed up with the sequel movies. Nobody really cares that much about that era, not even the people working for the company. So everything they've spent the last 10 years on has been fiddling around in the pre-sequel era. The problem is, the people who liked the sequel movies and didn't care about the stuff before it don't really care about the pre-sequel stuff. And the people who didn't like the sequel stuff, it's hard to get invested in all of the stuff leading up the sequels knowing that, for example, Luke's Jedi Academy will get wiped out, Coruscant gets destroyed, the New Republic collapses, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>People cared a great deal about the sequel era, and waited 20 years for the chance to see it.<br /> <br /> The problem, however, is that Disney decided to turn the sequels into a reimagining of the original trilogy, instead of continuing forward with a new story.<br /> <br /> Anybody who claims that Rey was hated just for being a woman is dangerously close to OD'ing on copium. People don't have a problem with female Jedi. Heck, they've wanted to see Princess Leia wielding the yellow saber for a long time now. The problem is that Rey was presented as a mary sue that never had to work for any of her victories.<br /> <br /> One of the big villains that comes along after the fall of the empire is a red Twi'lek lady, who manages to scare even Luke with her whip saber, because he didn't know how to fight against it at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T20:35:43-07:00","id":1560687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560686#post1560686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People cared a great deal about the sequel era, and waited 20 years for the chance to see it.<br /> <br /> The problem, however, is that Disney decided to turn the sequels into a reimagining of the original trilogy, instead of continuing forward with a new story.<br /> <br /> Anybody who claims that Rey was hated just for being a woman is dangerously close to OD'ing on copium. People don't have a problem with female Jedi. Heck, they've wanted to see Princess Leia wielding the yellow saber for a long time now. The problem is that Rey was presented as a mary sue that never had to work for any of her victories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shit take. Luke was despised as a whiny farmboy for years, and had about as much fall into his lap as Rey did. The main difference is that Rey's parental figures came pre-killed. It didn't happen on camera, either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T22:05:48-07:00","id":1560689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560687#post1560687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shit take. Luke was despised as a whiny farmboy for years, and had about as much fall into his lap as Rey did. The main difference is that Rey's parental figures came pre-killed. It didn't happen on camera, either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rey awakens to the force and starts achieving in a matter of weeks what took Luke years to achieve. The first time he tries to rush off and tackle Vader, he got the shit kicked out of him and had to go back for additional training. Even after that, he still couldn't defeat Vader without drawing upon the power of the dark side, and still would have been effortlessly killed by Palpatine, had his father not intervened at the last second.<br /> <br /> I know that Palpatine is the most powerful Sith who ever lived during his reign, and that Rey is his grandaughter. But Luke and Leia are the children of bio-engineered Force Jesus, and they still had to work their asses off to become Jedi masters.<br /> <br /> Rey was a terrible addition to the franchise, who's only purpose was to shit on the fandom, and preach Cathleen's idiotic agenda. Which she openly confessed to when she said she didn't care about Star Wars and only wanted to <i>&quot;spread the message.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T00:12:17-07:00","id":1560692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560687#post1560687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shit take. Luke was despised as a whiny farmboy for years, and had about as much fall into his lap as Rey did. The main difference is that Rey's parental figures came pre-killed. It didn't happen on camera, either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I never really saw that. Most people seemed to have liked the character growth Luke underwent between movies 4 and 6. By Episode 6, Luke is anything but a whiney farmboy. I think if Rey had undergone similar growth throughout the sequel trilogy, it would have helped her reception. But in Episode 9, she largely still felt the same as she had been in Episode 7. Unfortunately her growth was more in terms of power levels than character development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T01:30:17-07:00","id":1560697,"title":"","content":"Luke was redeemed in the eyes of the hardcore Star Wars fanbase by the novels that made up most of the material for the franchise for a long time. Even with Luke getting better writing than Rey did, he was still a bland protagonist following the Hero's Journey to a T. A giant complaint after RotJ was the Luke's &quot;growth&quot; was completely off screen. He ends ESB at his lowest point, physically and emotionally devastated and... RotJ starts up with him having already come to grips with everything and finishing his training with Yoda so he can just Jedi badass his way to the finale where there's at least some showing instead of telling of his character development.<br /> <br /> I will standby a simple basic issue with the sequel trilogy that's not only a fundamental reason why it both was a giant financial success, but also something with zero legs in culture, and also something that bled into the rest of the Disney era: there's no core creative vision for the franchise.<br /> <br /> The original trilogy is beloved because Lucas's vision was there the whole time, and especially the second two movies put far better filmmakers in charge of executing it but they didn't try to do something other than what Lucas wanted; but well.<br /> <br /> The prequel trilogy has a mixed legacy because it was all Lucas: all of his creative vision and lack of talent as a director and self-editor. But what's giving it reevaluation and nostalgia is that at least it's still a single vision over the films and a strong enough vision a ton of good material was built off of the foundations it made (esp. the Clone Wars show).<br /> <br /> The sequel trilogy and the further Disney era really doesn't have a vision you can point to. Individual creators put their stamps on individual parts without someone being the foundation of it all. Individual films and shows ping pong between great and horrible; and as long as enough money is made the higher ups don't really care. It's also how the MCU lost its way as nobody really knew what to do with it after long enough. It's why the DC movies couldn't build into a franchise that people actually liked; and are only finally seeming to manage after they installed Gunn to be the creative vision keeper for that franchise.<br /> <br /> The Star Wars films have never been the height of great movie making. They've always been blockbuster popcorn entertainment. That's why the sequels put buts in seats no matter how much fans were complaining and no matter how much vision-by-committee justified those complaints. Most people don't watch Star Wars for deep plots and well crafted characters. Those things just need to be good enough that you can shut off your brain and enjoy the space-wizard fights and space combat. It's what happens after the movies leave the theaters that gets bad when the visioon isn't there, so the foundations for more material isn't there, and the fan interest isn't there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T04:31:41-07:00","id":1560706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560697#post1560697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luke was redeemed in the eyes of the hardcore Star Wars fanbase by the novels that made up most of the material for the franchise for a long time. Even with Luke getting better writing than Rey did, he was still a bland protagonist following the Hero's Journey to a T. A giant complaint after RotJ was the Luke's &quot;growth&quot; was completely off screen. He ends ESB at his lowest point, physically and emotionally devastated and... RotJ starts up with him having already come to grips with everything and finishing his training with Yoda so he can just Jedi badass his way to the finale where there's at least some showing instead of telling of his character development.<br /> <br /> I will standby a simple basic issue with the sequel trilogy that's not only a fundamental reason why it both was a giant financial success, but also something with zero legs in culture, and also something that bled into the rest of the Disney era: there's no core creative vision for the franchise.<br /> <br /> The original trilogy is beloved because Lucas's vision was there the whole time, and especially the second two movies put far better filmmakers in charge of executing it but they didn't try to do something other than what Lucas wanted; but well.<br /> <br /> The prequel trilogy has a mixed legacy because it was all Lucas: all of his creative vision and lack of talent as a director and self-editor. But what's giving it reevaluation and nostalgia is that at least it's still a single vision over the films and a strong enough vision a ton of good material was built off of the foundations it made (esp. the Clone Wars show).<br /> <br /> The sequel trilogy and the further Disney era really doesn't have a vision you can point to. Individual creators put their stamps on individual parts without someone being the foundation of it all. Individual films and shows ping pong between great and horrible; and as long as enough money is made the higher ups don't really care. It's also how the MCU lost its way as nobody really knew what to do with it after long enough. It's why the DC movies couldn't build into a franchise that people actually liked; and are only finally seeming to manage after they installed Gunn to be the creative vision keeper for that franchise.<br /> <br /> The Star Wars films have never been the height of great movie making. They've always been blockbuster popcorn entertainment. That's why the sequels put buts in seats no matter how much fans were complaining and no matter how much vision-by-committee justified those complaints. Most people don't watch Star Wars for deep plots and well crafted characters. Those things just need to be good enough that you can shut off your brain and enjoy the space-wizard fights and space combat. It's what happens after the movies leave the theaters that gets bad when the visioon isn't there, so the foundations for more material isn't there, and the fan interest isn't there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The films also had the problem of not being able to portray the same level of information or detail as the books.<br /> <br /> For example, by Mace Windu's own admission through internal dialogue, he and Palpatine were exactly equal in terms of combat performance. Mace utilizing his Vaapad style lightsaber form, and Palpatine having access to the infinite power of the dark side. If Palpatine had been taking the fight seriously, the two of them would have been locked in an eternal stalemate, with neither opponent managing to defeat the other.<br /> <br /> Palpatine threw the match, because it was part of his plan to turn Anakin.<br /> <br /> <br /> Additionally, Palpatine is considered to be <b>the most</b> powerful Sith lord in all of galactic history. Allegedly having mastered every technique from all his predecessors. His command of Force Lightning was so great, he could destroy whole planets by conjuring an apocalyptic storm on their surface.<br /> <br /> Then he gets into a fight with Yoda, the most powerful Jedi at the time, and all they do is throw a bunch of chairs at each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's also in the books that we get an explanation for how Palpatine was able to successfully come back from death. He both mastered the technique of essence transference, and he cracked the code on how to successfully make clones with force sensitivity. A feat that was previously believed to be impossible, due to how the midichlorians actively resisted attempts to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T04:45:50-07:00","id":1560708,"title":"","content":"For clarification (sorry for the nerding out) - creating a Force sensitive clone is extremely difficult, because the midichlorians will naturally reject the clone body, thus failing to bond with it.<br /> <br /> Palpatine discovered a unique species of lizard who are surrounded by a personalized bubble of anti-Force aura which disrupts the midichlorian's ability to communicate with each other.<br /> <br /> He found that by placing these lizards within close proximity to a cloning tank, it would prevent the rejection process and force the midichlorians to accept the clone as their new host.<br /> <br /> Voila, that's how you create a clone with Force sensitivity! Once he figured that out, he merely had to use essence transference to take over the body of his own clone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T13:24:17-07:00","id":1560717,"title":"","content":"Novels don't have more information or details than films, they just wildly differ in what kinds of things they communicate effectively.<br /> <br /> You don't put the details of how a character's plan works in regards to dozens of other setting details in a blockbuster action adventure film... because people don't go to action adventure films to get a huge chunk of time in the movie having deep setting lore explained to them. Novels are far better for world building and adding lots of details the fans will pour over because novels have more time to be character studies since you're never going to have a duel in print that is as spectacular as it looks on screen; and thus there's more time to drop details as characters are doing things.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why heist films and who-do-its have some very standard storytelling techniques to help do exposition to explain the schemes in a fashion that doesn't put the audience to sleep. The top crook narrates the plan over the action of it actually taking place. The detective narrates the true events as you see a replay of events but in a new light. These convey tons of information, but how they do it is very different from novels in the same genre because of the pros and cons of medium choice.<br /> <br /> That said, novels still have to employ their own methods well. We had Palpatine resurrect himself as a clone back in the Legacy era without any need to do deep dives into the melding of science and the Force. He just did it via hording cloning tech for himself, clones of Force users tended to result in Force user clones as something that was already established, and hand-wave Dark Side power to allow his Force ghost to take over a clone body. The newer novels only need to explain so much because Lucas added a bunch of extraneous details that made it harder to suspend disbelief when the sequel movies opted to copy the resurrection storyline. One fan's deep lore enjoyment is another fan's convoluted mess that takes them out of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T17:57:26-07:00","id":1560734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560689#post1560689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rey awakens to the force and starts achieving in a matter of weeks what took Luke years to achieve. The first time he tries to rush off and tackle Vader, he got the shit kicked out of him and had to go back for additional training. Even after that, he still couldn't defeat Vader without drawing upon the power of the dark side, and still would have been effortlessly killed by Palpatine, had his father not intervened at the last second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither Kylo nor Snoke seemed all that impressive. The former threw temper tantrums without having the menace of his grandfather, and the latter was just kind of there, without any actual gravitas or hint that he was anywhere near Palp's level. So, yeah, not buying it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that Palpatine is the most powerful Sith who ever lived during his reign, and that Rey is his grandaughter. But Luke and Leia are the children of bio-engineered Force Jesus, and they still had to work their asses off to become Jedi masters. </div> </div> </div>They're all the product of someone who really wanted to make Buck Rogers but couldn't get the rights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rey was a terrible addition to the franchise, who's only purpose was to shit on the fandom, and preach Cathleen's idiotic agenda. Which she openly confessed to when she said she didn't care about Star Wars and only wanted to <i>&quot;spread the message.&quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>Pffft. A CEO's agenda? What, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mhRjGpKfhA8\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I want to make even more money to be even richer!&quot;</a>?<br /> <br /> Well, she did, probably. The movies made a lot of money because people who are terminally attached to SW went to go see them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I never really saw that. Most people seemed to have liked the character growth Luke underwent between movies 4 and 6. By Episode 6, Luke is anything but a whiney farmboy. I think if Rey had undergone similar growth throughout the sequel trilogy, it would have helped her reception. But in Episode 9, she largely still felt the same as she had been in Episode 7. Unfortunately her growth was more in terms of power levels than character development.</div> </div> </div> </div>During the 90s, no one thought that highly of Luke. This was the time of TIE Fighter making it bigger than X-Wing on PCs and edgy empire fanboys. I had the displeasure of being dragged into the fandom that way. It was awfully suspicious, too, that Luke started getting accolades when Rey made her appearance. While the prequels might have had some influence there, the catalyst was absolutely Rey Hate. All the energy of &quot;Aww, but Uncle Owen!&quot; was forgotten because someone else had the spotlight.<br /> <br /> Not to say that the new trilogy were good movies, of course. &quot;Somehow, Palpatine returned&quot; was an instant meme for a reason. But, again, nostalgia baited 4.4B USD out of audiences because they can't NOT watch a Star Wars film. The stranglehold SW has over pop culture is even greater than D&amp;D's influence over the ttrpg crowd. But Rey is a distraction from the actual problems: the writing, the corporate executive control over movie production, the super commercialization of creative works.<br /> <br /> But sure. Go ahead and keep arguing that Rey doesn't make sense in a franchise that stops making sense as a whole if you start thinking about it for more than five minutes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(I think I should perhaps thank my GM for the WEG rpg. Pulling an alien abduction-style storyline with heads getting taken off and put back on, good as new, cured me of any attachments to the franchise, cold turkey.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T18:49:59-07:00","id":1560735,"title":"","content":"Star Wars has also always been about the commercialization. George Lucas is a billionaire because he convinced Fox to give him the merchandise rights that they thought were going to be worthless as they assumed the money would be in box office and then the film would be forgotten as a fad. The Ewoks existed as much to sell new toys to kids as any cartoon that was basically a 30 minute commercial for the toys of whatever you were watching.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean SW is bad, but just like the franchise my forum avatar comes from, the height of the fandom came from having merch to buy and Lucas never shied away from doing what he could to keep putting out stuff to make a buck off of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T19:00:18-07:00","id":1560736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560734#post1560734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither Kylo nor Snoke seemed all that impressive. The former threw temper tantrums without having the menace of his grandfather, and the latter was just kind of there, without any actual gravitas or hint that he was anywhere near Palp's level. So, yeah, not buying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>He had enough gravitas to wipe out the newly formed Jedi Order and put the new Republic on the back foot. Granted it was offscreen, but still.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560734#post1560734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Pffft. A CEO's agenda? What, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mhRjGpKfhA8\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I want to make even more money to be even richer!&quot;</a>?<br /> <br /> Well, she did, probably. The movies made a lot of money because people who are terminally attached to SW went to go see them.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the agenda of <i>&quot;The Force is Female&quot;</i> - Men suck, and if you disagree, you're a sexist bigot. Check your privilege!<br /> <br /> Blah, blah, blah - shut the fuck up, lady.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 06-18-2026, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T21:04:44-07:00","id":1560738,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Force is Female,&quot; was an advertising campaign by <b>Nike</b> the shoe company that sponsored multiple events including one for increasing female representation in high level positions in the film industry... and obvious event for Kathleen Kennedy to attend and support. She got a free shirt, and a bunch of idiots on the Internet turned it into a misogynist conspiracy theory. Do better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T21:31:17-07:00","id":1560739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560738#post1560738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do better.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>NO.</b><br /> <br /> Like I said, dangerously close to ODing on copium.<br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> Now, to get the focus on something other than how badly Disney has fucked the franchise of Star Wars...<br /> <br /> I'm worried that the new announcement reveals for Xenoverse 3 may be suggesting we're forced to play a Saiyan who simply uses trans-spheres (soul spheres, whatever they're called) to simply shapeshift into the other playable races.<br /> <br /> A fear which is supported by news that The Breakers was originally planned to be Xenoverse 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 06-19-2026, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T21:42:10-07:00","id":1560741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560739#post1560739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>NO.</b><br /> <br /> Like I said, dangerously close to ODing on copium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.<br /> <br /> This is a strange comment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T22:16:13-07:00","id":1560744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560741#post1560741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm.<br /> <br /> This is a strange comment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me I'm wrong, though? Pretty much every male character got the shaft in some way or another.<br /> <br /> <b>Luke</b>, who was a champion of caring about his friends and resisting impossible odds gave into depression to become an isolated hermit living on a rock that believed the Jedi deserved to fail. Okay, that may be true, but the New Order didn't just stop at the Jedi. They went after the new Republic too!<br /> <br /> <b>Kylo</b> was portrayed as being even more of a whiny emo than pre-surgery Anakin. Something I didn't even know was possible. Also, the boy who was raised from birth as a member of the Skywalker bloodline and presumably trained in the ways of the Force, can't take down a farm girl, who only just recently picked up a lightsaber for the first time.<br /> <br /> Not gonna criticize Han's death, because I'm reasonably certain he also died like that in the original expanded universe. If I'm wrong, somebody feel free to correct me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Snoke</b>... the physical avatar of disappointment and wasted potential.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Finn</b> - Yeah, sorry pal, but you're not the main character anymore. China doesn't like dark skinned heroes, which is why your image was removed from the foreground and shrunk on the international posters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T05:02:35-07:00","id":1560752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next year, finally, exactly 10 years after Rise of Skywalker, we're getting Jedi Starfighter which will be the first major piece of media set in the post-sequel setting, but I doubt it's going to do very well either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really want get too drawn into the Star Wars hate (I thought the new Disney made Star Wars Movie were good, especially The Last Jedi! Rise of Skywalker was probably my least favorite of the new ones, but it had it some ok moments). But, just to nitpick/clarify, the new movie coming out is just called 'Starfighter'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T11:24:19-07:00","id":1560788,"title":"","content":"The Star Wars novels were filled with good stories with great writers, but the rules were that it couldn't contradict the movies. While I didn't care for the sequals myself I'm not going to insult people who do and the cast did the best with what they were given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T13:06:12-07:00","id":1560792,"title":"","content":"There were some serious stinkers in the Legacy EU books. The &quot;can't contradict the movies&quot; rule came from Lucas to help put some quality controls on people writing back when he didn't have the time or interest to actually read every book to maintain the SW brand. He wanted to license to as many novelists (and comic artists, and etc.) as possible because money, but he realized things were getting crazy with zero oversight. So he created a set of rules to keep what is and isn't &quot;canon&quot; and that was enough of a limit to get a most consistent identity to the franchise.... until he blew a lot of it out of the water with the prequels anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T13:58:08-07:00","id":1560793,"title":"","content":"I personally enjoyed the Timothy Zahn the most. As far the Disney Star Wars movies I enjoyed Rogue One the best and I can't comment on the other TV stuff because I only watched a few episodes and couldn't get into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-20-2026, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T09:49:51-07:00","id":1560865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560792#post1560792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were some serious stinkers in the Legacy EU books. The &quot;can't contradict the movies&quot; rule came from Lucas to help put some quality controls on people writing back when he didn't have the time or interest to actually read every book to maintain the SW brand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boba Fett dueled Vader to a draw in lightsaber combat.<br /> <br /> Bobba Fett, a guy who didn't even have Force sensitivity, and was therefor limited to normal human capabilities.<br /> <br /> Vader, established to be the greatest Jedi killer who ever lived. Yes, even more so than Clone Wars Grievous.<br /> <br /> Also, since Rey is Palpatine's granddaughter, I'm going with the belief that her father was Triclops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T11:32:20-07:00","id":1560980,"title":"","content":"To further expand on Heavy Arms point on how media grifters twisted the narrative when it comes to women in media.<br /> <br /> They did the same to Brie Larson, Rachel Zeggler and now Milly Alcock.<br /> <br /> With Larson they made her sound like that she had a problem with middle aged white males doing movie reviews and left out the bit where she said she want more women and other visible minorities having a voice.<br /> <br /> With Rachel Zeggler they went after her because she mentioned that the Snow White cartoon was very much a product of its time and the live action movie was going to reflect the changes in society since then.<br /> <br /> It was strange to see them crash out over a movie that they weren't the target audience. Then when she did Shazam 2 and said she took the role because she needed to work they made it sound like she was insulting fans and left out that she was a new actress and needed experience and enjoyed her time on the set.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly was that West Side Story hadn't come out yet and we had COVID lockdowns and nobody was working. Not to mention she wasn't the lead in the Shazam flick and admitted that acting is a job to make money.<br /> <br /> Strange that they don't have the same level of critism when any male actor said the same thing.<br /> <br /> Now Milly Alcock made the truthful statement of how certain elements of society are very comfortable of objectiving women bodies and how hot they are and we saw the grifters get mad when a truthful statement was made.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact the man who hosts Friday Night Tights admitted to the grift when he made the statement of how they take one little thing and twist it around and build a narrative around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-25-2026, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T20:24:00-07:00","id":1561017,"title":"","content":"GreatHorned Ratkin are you referring to the Star Wars story where Boba Fett was tasked to get a package from some criminal and it contained the living head of a seer that Vader and Papaltine wanted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T11:01:34-07:00","id":1561031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1560980#post1560980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Rachel Zeggler they went after her because she mentioned that the Snow White cartoon was very much a product of its time and the live action movie was going to reflect the changes in society since then.</div> </div> </div> </div>She also made dumb shit comments, like calling the prince a 'creepy stalker' when I'm pretty sure the guy only shows up at the very end of the movie to break the spell and take Snow White back to her own castle.<br /> <br /> <br /> And she was so insufferable to work with, that the actress who played the evil queen couldn't stand to be in the same room with her when they were off set. Oh, she also voiced her open hatred of the IDF, which said actress was previously a member of, because <b>enlistment is mandatory</b> and not something she had a choice in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly, she went to an empty theater to watch her own movie, bringing along her own bouquet of flowers, and then proceeded to hoot, holler, and cheer at the top of her lungs after the credits rolled, like a fucking maniac!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 06-26-2026, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T15:28:52-07:00","id":1561040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561031#post1561031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She also made dumb shit comments, like calling the prince a 'creepy stalker' when I'm pretty sure the guy only shows up at the very end of the movie to break the spell and take Snow White back to her own castle.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the old Disney cartoon, the prince shows up once while Snow White is in the woods singing, sings a song with her, &quot;falls in love&quot; and then spends the rest of the movie off screen (largely to save animation time), before finding her in a glass coffin and decides to kiss what he is told is her corpse with no idea that it would heal her. It's not exactly a solid romance story even if &quot;creepy stalker&quot; is a bit much... kissing the dead body of a girl (and Snow White is a girl, not a woman) you've met once is pretty iffy.<br /> <br /> And the Disney version drastically tones down how creepy the original fairy tales are... like Snow White being a child (as in 7-8 years old) when the adult prince kisses her as an act of romantic love.<br /> <br /> Snow White, the story, doesn't do the prince any real favors as making him normal regarding romance and love.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And she was so insufferable to work with, that the actress who played the evil queen couldn't stand to be in the same room with her when they were off set. </div> </div> </div>Gal Gadot has repeatedly stated that they had a fun and positive work experience even despite differing opinions on Israel's actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, she also voiced her open hatred of the IDF, which said actress was previously a member of, because <b>enlistment is mandatory</b> and not something she had a choice in. </div> </div> </div>Israel provides plenty of legal ways out of military service from basic conscientious objection, to specific higher education programs. Gal Gadot also has a long post-service history of defending IDF actions, and has worked with the current Israeli government in a pro-Israel PR campaign. She's not someone that did her service 20 years ago and then moved on with her life. She's a major celebrity and she's chosen to lend her voice to causes she feels strongly about publicly. Painting her as a passive victim of public sentiment is not a fair assessment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, she went to an empty theater to watch her own movie, bringing along her own bouquet of flowers, and then proceeded to hoot, holler, and cheer at the top of her lungs after the credits rolled, like a fucking maniac! </div> </div> </div>If this is your bar for being a &quot;fucking maniac&quot; every celebrity is a fucking maniac because this is pretty much nothing compared to what many have done. Renting a movie theater for a private screening is not hard to do. I've organized a private screening as part of a birthday party for a college friend; and we were not there to be serious film nerds... we were having a party. Our own theater, concessions, our pick of movie, and all of that totaled ~$250. I'm sure it's way more expensive in LA or wherever Zeggler did it, but it's not some crazy extravagance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T16:08:38-07:00","id":1561043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561040#post1561040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the old Disney cartoon, the prince shows up once while Snow White is in the woods singing, sings a song with her, &quot;falls in love&quot; and then spends the rest of the movie off screen (largely to save animation time), before finding her in a glass coffin and decides to kiss what he is told is her corpse with no idea that it would heal her. It's not exactly a solid romance story even if &quot;creepy stalker&quot; is a bit much... kissing the dead body of a girl (and Snow White is a girl, not a woman) you've met once is pretty iffy.<br /> <br /> And the Disney version drastically tones down how creepy the original fairy tales are... like Snow White being a child (as in 7-8 years old) when the adult prince kisses her as an act of romantic love.<br /> <br /> Snow White, the story, doesn't do the prince any real favors as making him normal regarding romance and love.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been decades since I watched the movie, but the only scene of a prince happening upon a singing princess that I remember is from Sleeping Beauty when the fairies were tugging on his cape. And yes, I'm aware the original story was way creepier (European folk tales, how fun!).<br /> <br /> But that's not the version we got. We got the Disney version. Also, while I'm aware that Snow White is supposed to be 14 in the Disney version, she always looked much older. Probably because the height of the dwarves gave off the illusion she was taller than she actually is.<br /> <br /> Although, I will give them credit for getting one thing accurate about the original. The movie destroyed the careers of both Snow White's actresses!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T21:58:30-07:00","id":1561046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561040#post1561040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the old Disney cartoon, the prince shows up once while Snow White is in the woods singing, sings a song with her, &quot;falls in love&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically speaking, it's not in the woods, but while she's doing her scullery maid work at the start of the film.<br /> <br /> And he introduces himself by popping in behind her and joining in her song, and visibly catching her off guard.<br /> <br /> And then when she keeps backing away from him, at the very least flustered if not actually frightened, he keeps approaching her and talking about how he wants to get to know her (or something to that effect).<br /> <br /> Now granted, the scene progresses to a point of him singing up to her balcony and her being won over by that, because movie. Still, it's not hard to see how the preamble would very closely resemble the lived and shared experiences of women who had to deal with goes who imposed upon them and wouldn't take a hint. Hell, even the positive response can be framed through ways in which women are socialised to try and deescalate such scenarios by playing along until they can extricate themselves.<br /> <br /> All it takes is being familiar with how women talk about this kind of stuff and not being invested in a perspective of despising them for being outspoken in general, and about feminism in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-27-2026, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T22:17:17-07:00","id":1561047,"title":"","content":"Fair, it's been awhile and I hadn't recalled all the details, I was just pretty sure they had a song at the start; not that he just showed up at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T22:31:40-07:00","id":1561048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561047#post1561047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair, it's been awhile and I hadn't recalled all the details, I was just pretty sure they had a song at the start; not that he just showed up at the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, I'm not playing the &quot;um actually&quot; game in this particular instance. That's just setting the stage for the fact that the details actually do correspond particularly well with those kinds of red flags.<br /> <br /> Although I think the distinction that he is technically intruding upon her in her home does contribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T02:20:44-07:00","id":1561051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561046#post1561046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically speaking, it's not in the woods, but while she's doing her scullery maid work at the start of the film.<br /> <br /> And he introduces himself by popping in behind her and joining in her song, and visibly catching her off guard.<br /> <br /> And then when she keeps backing away from him, at the very least flustered if not actually frightened, he keeps approaching her and talking about how he wants to get to know her (or something to that effect).<br /> <br /> Now granted, the scene progresses to a point of him singing up to her balcony and her being won over by that, because movie. Still, it's not hard to see how the preamble would very closely resemble the lived and shared experiences of women who had to deal with goes who imposed upon them and wouldn't take a hint. Hell, even the positive response can be framed through ways in which women are socialised to try and deescalate such scenarios by playing along until they can extricate themselves.<br /> <br /> All it takes is being familiar with how women talk about this kind of stuff and not being invested in a perspective of despising them for being outspoken in general, and about feminism in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was she actually a princess in the original version, or just a super beautiful servant? Because I'm pretty sure that if the royal princess didn't want to be bothered, she could just summon the guards. It might offend the prince diplomatically, but I'm pretty sure the prince wouldn't risk starting a war by harassing the princess in her own castle.<br /> <br /> That's the funny thing about all these stories where the main protagonist is the prince / princess of a kingdom or some such. They seemingly forget they have an entire nation's resources at their disposal, and instead get the idea that they must venture out to stop a great evil with nothing more than a ragtag bunch of travel companions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T03:16:46-07:00","id":1561052,"title":"","content":"Snow White (depending on version) is sent away from or flees her life as royalty because the queen is trying to kill her. She has no access to protection because she's in hiding and that doesn't really work if you have a detachment of the royal guard around... also the person after her controls the nation in question. It's not really forgotten as much directly contrary to the plot to have her be able to solve her problems by exerting her royal status. Also keep in mind that as a princess who's the only current child of the last king, who she marries would be of national importance to her country... meaning even as a child she would have been raised to assume she'd be married off to a suitable match instead of finding love.<br /> <br /> The Disney versions, also to get away from how young she was originally, downplay how much the original stories paint her as intensely naive. She might know how to run a household for the dwarfs because running a household would be things she'd learn as a princess, but she only survives the first few attempts on her life because the dwarfs are constantly saving her from herself; often when she directly ignores their instructions on how to deal with normal people. And even in the Disney version that's still how the plot basically functions: despite being in hiding with a royal trying to assassinate her, she just trusts people with exceedingly little second thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T07:39:01-07:00","id":1561053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561051#post1561051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was she actually a princess in the original version, or just a super beautiful servant?</div> </div> </div> </div>The queen forces her to do menial labour with the expectation that will make her less beautiful.<br /> <br /> I'm not otherwise inclined to get into the weeds of the worldbuilding or verisimilitude of that film, or any perceptions of fantasy fiction or history that might be reductive of either or both. The important thing is that, for a feminist critique of one work while setting up the context of another, there's an apparent vibe.<br /> <br /> Like, it's not even about whether somebody is literally calling the prince a creep in the text or subtext of the film, not least because he's hardly in it. It can be enough to make a point of how what is there doesn't exactly age well towards an idea of trying to put in something more contemporary.<br /> <br /> I just happened to be watching the film a few months ago, and I know that was an element that jumped out at me. Just for being a brief spot that is kind of &quot;yikes&quot;. <br /> <br /> (To be clear, I regard the new Snow White movie as extremely mid at best. Just with a point that I regard extremely mid as neither exceptional with regards to these live-action remakes, nor something that warrants the level of mobilised vitriol that movie got. It's possible to both say &quot;there's a legitimate feminist critique of the original work&quot; and &quot;feminist updates attempted in a modern movie fall short because they're likely coming mostly from a place of corporate sanitisation rather than a genuine voice&quot;. In any event, not really failings that can be attributed to the people in the film, beyond anybody's observations that the kind of menace and bombast that might be expected of the Evil Queen aren't really within Gal Gadot's range.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T04:32:46-07:00","id":1561075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561017#post1561017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GreatHorned Ratkin are you referring to the Star Wars story where Boba Fett was tasked to get a package from some criminal and it contained the living head of a seer that Vader and Papaltine wanted?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know, I personally didn't read the story. But I have seen the artwork for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T23:06:04-07:00","id":1561182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561075#post1561075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know, I personally didn't read the story. But I have seen the artwork for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the artwork is subpar then it's the story I'm recalling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T23:10:59-07:00","id":1561183,"title":"","content":"Who said that Rachel Zeggler is insufferable? The same media grifters who edited her statements to make her look and sound terrible DarkKing?<br /> <br /> Folks like Critical Drinker, Geeks and Gamers, Ryan Kinel and Nerdrotic don't have much creditability anymore as they have been caught making stuff up on numerous people they don't like such as Rian Johnson or James Gunn<br /> <br /> Now they are doing thumbnails of making Milly Alcock look ugly by making her look ape-like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-02-2026, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T11:34:05-07:00","id":1561196,"title":"","content":"I should add that they want Christopher Nolan's Odsesey to fail so they can blame it on having Lupita Noyonga playing Helen and Elliott Page playing Achilles. <br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T14:28:36-07:00","id":1561200,"title":"","content":"While I understand why grifters go after the targets they do... Helen and Achilles are very minor characters in the Odyssey since the crux of the story is what happens after the Trojan War, not during it.<br /> <br /> And while the movie industry has gotten completely hard to predict how things will do... Nolan's track record of getting people into theaters remains high, and they've already broken records for IMAX presales in the US. Even if it's not some major smash hit, it seems unlikely that it will under perform. Of course, the rage-bait types will probably try to paint, &quot;only met expectations&quot; as a &quot;bomb&quot; considering their track records.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T15:17:16-07:00","id":1561205,"title":"","content":"Oh I know Heavy Arms about how minor of a role Helen and Achilles play in the Odyssey as unlike the grifters. I have read both the Illad and the Odyssey and know that Christopher Nolan is a good film maker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-02-2026, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T19:20:12-07:00","id":1561212,"title":"","content":"On the plus side more and more people are not falling for their rhetoric as it's buzzword bingo and they use the same wording with little variance. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T21:26:07-07:00","id":1561217,"title":"","content":"In other gripes:<br /> <br /> Sony's announcement of phasing out physical media is a horrifying glimpse of a completely self-inflicted digital Dark Age. PSN customers had 550 movies erased from their consoles because Sony didn't want to pay to keep the licensing for those films and thus everyone that paid to &quot;rent&quot; them lost their money completely and without warning. The PS3 and PS Vita stores went off-line with almost no warning so a huge number of games just became inaccessible to anyone that can't find a physical copy. If Sony is serious about basically killing BluRay on top of the PS6 not having the option of an disc drives (not even as an additional extra) and you can only buy store codes in stores... we can only hope that something happens to change this mess.<br /> <br /> Customers already prefer digital media for convenience, cloud use, and so on. But why are people going to spend $70-$80 for games that can get deleted on a whim? Lots of people aren't buying discs... but there's the reassurance that they could if they wanted to so they can have movies, TV shows, and games without worried about delistings and deletions (or at least archivists could preserve them) that buoyed that relaxation around digital products. Do they really think this is the way to save the already floundering video-game industry? Are they just counting on bots buying bot made games or something?<br /> <br /> I really hope that the EU's upcoming meetings around digital product ownership and consumer rights changes tone from their last report with this happening and game preservation advocate's concerns getting even more real than they already were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T08:33:02-07:00","id":1561240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561217#post1561217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other gripes:<br /> <br /> Sony's announcement of phasing out physical media is a horrifying glimpse of a completely self-inflicted digital Dark Age. PSN customers had 550 movies erased from their consoles because Sony didn't want to pay to keep the licensing for those films and thus everyone that paid to &quot;rent&quot; them lost their money completely and without warning. The PS3 and PS Vita stores went off-line with almost no warning so a huge number of games just became inaccessible to anyone that can't find a physical copy. If Sony is serious about basically killing BluRay on top of the PS6 not having the option of an disc drives (not even as an additional extra) and you can only buy store codes in stores... we can only hope that something happens to change this mess.<br /> <br /> Customers already prefer digital media for convenience, cloud use, and so on. But why are people going to spend $70-$80 for games that can get deleted on a whim? Lots of people aren't buying discs... but there's the reassurance that they could if they wanted to so they can have movies, TV shows, and games without worried about delistings and deletions (or at least archivists could preserve them) that buoyed that relaxation around digital products. Do they really think this is the way to save the already floundering video-game industry? Are they just counting on bots buying bot made games or something?<br /> <br /> I really hope that the EU's upcoming meetings around digital product ownership and consumer rights changes tone from their last report with this happening and game preservation advocate's concerns getting even more real than they already were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heard about this! It's so crazy to me! If there are no physical discs, what the point of a console then? Makes zero sense to me. Might as well have just have a gaming PC with Steam at that point. I mean, the whole point of a console was to make it easier to buy, own and play a game. If there are no physical disc drives, then the PS6 is just a gaming rig locked to a single storefront. A storefront that can decide on a whim to remove whatever games it wants from your library. It's crazy..<br /> <br /> This of course makes me worry a bit about physical media as whole... because I'm not sure what the down stream effects on movies and such will be. Hopefully there are places that still plan on making physical blu-ray (and 4k) discs...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T10:39:16-07:00","id":1561242,"title":"","content":"I saw that on Tom Christie satire on the PS5 of where is the disc drive for the consule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T11:51:58-07:00","id":1561245,"title":"","content":"Yesterday was a sad day with the death of Hikaru Kurosaki.<br /> <br /> While the Metal Hero pseudo-franchise started in Japan a few years earlier with Gavan and the Uchuu Keiji Trilogy, it reached Brazil with the fourth production, Kyojuu Tokusou Juspion (MegaBeast Investigator Juspion), known here as &quot;O Fant\u00e1stico Jaspion&quot; (it's a cognate, I don't think it requires translation).<br /> <br /> In Brazil this was one of the biggest television phenomena in history, by comparison it would be like He-Man and Transformers combined. It was the start of our relationship with Japanese media, which was a phenomenon in Brazil more than 10 years before reaching a similar status in the US (and at the time by dubs that actually tried to stay true to the original instead of heavily editing to blend into local standards).<br /> <br /> Kurosaki was the main actor. His death weighs heavily here, more than in Japan proper. Age 64, relatively young, the cause wasn't publicly disclosed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T12:15:53-07:00","id":1561247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561240#post1561240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there are no physical discs, what the point of a console then? Makes zero sense to me. Might as well have just have a gaming PC with Steam at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, the driving factor of console sales for ~15 years has been exclusives rather than hardware. While not just the PS3 specifically, the PS3 came out at the tipping point where price, convenience , and playing in person with friends became less important to sales than exclusive video games that you can only get by being in the right console ecosystem. Console prices have steadily been getting closer to PCs, PCs are ubiquitous enough that it's not hard to get a decent gaming PC and set it up as fast as you can setup a console, and multiplayer has largely moved online.<br /> <br /> By most analyses somewhere around 80% of sales of games that are released in both physical and digital formats are purchased digitally only. So that would be a higher number of digital only sales if digital only games were included (like most indies have to be these days).<br /> <br /> Consoles are going to get more expensive, so cutting out parts lets them be cheaper and most customers already by digital only. Do the numbers add up? Well Sony thinks so. So there's logic there even if it's &quot;short term gains for long term chaos,&quot; thinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This of course makes me worry a bit about physical media as whole... because I'm not sure what the down stream effects on movies and such will be. Hopefully there are places that still plan on making physical blu-ray (and 4k) discs... </div> </div> </div>The only silver lining is that Blu-Ray is licensed by the Blu-Ray Association; which is a consortium of a ton of major industry companies from manufactures to software to film makers.<br /> <br /> One of the things people don't think about when we compared the Blu-Ray vs HD-DVD situation as a &quot;war&quot; is that it included a &quot;peace treaty.&quot; Blu-Ray won, but to make sure a small number of companies couldn't hold the new standard hostage against everyone else the BRA was formed so every company could use Blu-Ray tech, software, and branding on fair footing.<br /> <br /> So, Sony can't blow up Blu-Ray media on their own. The question is what everyone else in the industry decides to do. Is Sony the leader, or going rogue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T12:16:45-07:00","id":1561248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561217#post1561217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other gripes:<br /> <br /> Sony's announcement of phasing out physical media is a horrifying glimpse of a completely self-inflicted digital Dark Age. PSN customers had 550 movies erased from their consoles because Sony didn't want to pay to keep the licensing for those films and thus everyone that paid to &quot;rent&quot; them lost their money completely and without warning. The PS3 and PS Vita stores went off-line with almost no warning so a huge number of games just became inaccessible to anyone that can't find a physical copy. If Sony is serious about basically killing BluRay on top of the PS6 not having the option of an disc drives (not even as an additional extra) and you can only buy store codes in stores... we can only hope that something happens to change this mess.<br /> <br /> Customers already prefer digital media for convenience, cloud use, and so on. But why are people going to spend $70-$80 for games that can get deleted on a whim? Lots of people aren't buying discs... but there's the reassurance that they could if they wanted to so they can have movies, TV shows, and games without worried about delistings and deletions (or at least archivists could preserve them) that buoyed that relaxation around digital products. Do they really think this is the way to save the already floundering video-game industry? Are they just counting on bots buying bot made games or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't surprise me, unfortunately. Executives love hype, and it they can manufacture and program hype, they'll have their ideal loop! Sure, it's fake, but then, technically so is the value of money...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T16:08:54-07:00","id":1561258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561247#post1561247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, the driving factor of console sales for ~15 years has been exclusives rather than hardware. While not just the PS3 specifically, the PS3 came out at the tipping point where price, convenience , and playing in person with friends became less important to sales than exclusive video games that you can only get by being in the right console ecosystem. Console prices have steadily been getting closer to PCs, PCs are ubiquitous enough that it's not hard to get a decent gaming PC and set it up as fast as you can setup a console, and multiplayer has largely moved online.<br /> <br /> By most analyses somewhere around 80% of sales of games that are released in both physical and digital formats are purchased digitally only. So that would be a higher number of digital only sales if digital only games were included (like most indies have to be these days).<br /> <br /> Consoles are going to get more expensive, so cutting out parts lets them be cheaper and most customers already by digital only. Do the numbers add up? Well Sony thinks so. So there's logic there even if it's &quot;short term gains for long term chaos,&quot; thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I get what you're saying... even if I do find it pretty crazy. Exclusives were never really a factor for me, but I know people only had certain consoles specifically for exclusives..<br /> <br /> And I think a lot of people who purchased games digitally assumed that once purchased they'd have access to them forever, but I think that'd proving not to be the case. I always had a feeling it might go that way though unfortunately.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561247#post1561247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only silver lining is that Blu-Ray is licensed by the Blu-Ray Association; which is a consortium of a ton of major industry companies from manufactures to software to film makers.<br /> <br /> One of the things people don't think about when we compared the Blu-Ray vs HD-DVD situation as a &quot;war&quot; is that it included a &quot;peace treaty.&quot; Blu-Ray won, but to make sure a small number of companies couldn't hold the new standard hostage against everyone else the BRA was formed so every company could use Blu-Ray tech, software, and branding on fair footing.<br /> <br /> So, Sony can't blow up Blu-Ray media on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yea! I almost forgot that's what came out of the format war. So, that's at least something!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561247#post1561247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is what everyone else in the industry decides to do. Is Sony the leader, or going rogue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, that is a good question. I'd like to hope a lot of companies see the value in physical media... but who knows these days.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T20:56:21-07:00","id":1561268,"title":"","content":"It looks like Microsoft/XBox is going to at least keep physical for a now. It's good PR for them since they're trying to recover after years of bad management decisions, and Sony/PS put the nail in the coffin of the XBox One by attacking it for trying to go all digital while the PS3 and PS4 would remain physical + digital. So XBox being committed to physical for at least one more console is likely if only to take advantage of Sony being really stupid. It doesn't hurt that digital only consumers can already treat their PCs as a XBox through GamePass; less demand on consoles means you can reduce supply and thus reduce costs. Esp. if securing a stable supply of GPUs is what's driving all console prices through the roof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T21:43:12-07:00","id":1561272,"title":"","content":"It always suck when someone from a popular Franchise passes away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T05:39:39-07:00","id":1561291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561268#post1561268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like Microsoft/XBox is going to at least keep physical for a now. It's good PR for them since they're trying to recover after years of bad management decisions, and Sony/PS put the nail in the coffin of the XBox One by attacking it for trying to go all digital while the PS3 and PS4 would remain physical + digital. So XBox being committed to physical for at least one more console is likely if only to take advantage of Sony being really stupid. It doesn't hurt that digital only consumers can already treat their PCs as a XBox through GamePass; less demand on consoles means you can reduce supply and thus reduce costs. Esp. if securing a stable supply of GPUs is what's driving all console prices through the roof.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good at least. For now anyway... who knows what they'll do in the future, but for now that's good.<br /> <br /> Hopefully Nintendo will continue with actual cartridges too. I know for a bit they were doing like digital keys or some nonsense, but hopefully they'll keep doing physical too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561272#post1561272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always suck when someone from a popular Franchise passes away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it does... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T10:47:49-07:00","id":1561301,"title":"","content":"Some sad news if you are a wrestling fan. The wrestler Konnan recently had to undergo a double leg amputation in addition to other health issues he has had over the years. Also sometime before that Marcus&quot;Buff&quot; Bagwell had to undergo a leg amputation himself.<br /> <br /> Something of a wake-up call when you remember what physical abuse they put themselves through to entertain the fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-04-2026, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:36:11-07:00","id":1561308,"title":"","content":"And... XBox gave up on it's chance to one-up Playstation... but at least they actually gave a reason for it that Sony should have 100% started with: their games are getting too big for Blu-Ray, as Blu-Ray was really designed for non-interactive media first. Most Blu-Ray discs cap out at 50 GB... which was huge when the format was introduced, but I'm pretty sure most of us recognize that's not really practical anymore. Hell. most games you buy on physical media these days still require a bunch of downloading to use precisely to add in stuff so you don't have to go back to the old days of swapping discs.<br /> <br /> I don't get why companies don't start with reasonable practical issues that inform unpopular decisions. There would be so much less upset at all of this if Sony started their narrative with, &quot;current disc tech can't keep up with increased game file sizes, so we're prioritizing digital,&quot; would have not been liked, but would have been accepted as necessary until someone makes a better disc. Or, hell, maybe even try going back to multi-disc games if physical media already has a large nostalgia factor anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T16:35:18-07:00","id":1561324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561308#post1561308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... XBox gave up on it's chance to one-up Playstation... but at least they actually gave a reason for it that Sony should have 100% started with: their games are getting too big for Blu-Ray, as Blu-Ray was really designed for non-interactive media first. Most Blu-Ray discs cap out at 50 GB... which was huge when the format was introduced, but I'm pretty sure most of us recognize that's not really practical anymore. Hell. most games you buy on physical media these days still require a bunch of downloading to use precisely to add in stuff so you don't have to go back to the old days of swapping discs.<br /> <br /> I don't get why companies don't start with reasonable practical issues that inform unpopular decisions. There would be so much less upset at all of this if Sony started their narrative with, &quot;current disc tech can't keep up with increased game file sizes, so we're prioritizing digital,&quot; would have not been liked, but would have been accepted as necessary until someone makes a better disc. Or, hell, maybe even try going back to multi-disc games if physical media already has a large nostalgia factor anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea! Totally with ya! If they'd started with that, then it'd be something. Of course, they could use multiple discs, or try to come up with some new discs that can handle the additional data. I want to say that 4K blu-rays are close to 100GB, so why not switch to those? Though, I know in a lot of case the games are still bigger than those... but still.<br /> <br /> But yea, there is definitely a conversation to be had about new storage technology... so why they didn't start by saying that is beyond me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 07-05-2026, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T11:46:35-07:00","id":1561351,"title":"","content":"This is why I still prefer to buy DVD and Blu-ray discs of my favorite TV shows or movies as I don't have to worry that a streaming service might drop content that they view as troubling or it aged badly. My defense is that we need the unvarnished truth to show what people in the past believed in and try to do better.<br /> <br /> You can't truly learn from history if you hide it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T13:09:15-07:00","id":1561353,"title":"","content":"On a different track. It's maddening to be a collector and seeing how expensive the hobby is becoming and you may have to give up certain items because you don't have the funds for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T04:27:01-07:00","id":1561462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561351#post1561351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I still prefer to buy DVD and Blu-ray discs of my favorite TV shows or movies as I don't have to worry that a streaming service might drop content that they view as troubling or it aged badly. My defense is that we need the unvarnished truth to show what people in the past believed in and try to do better.<br /> <br /> You can't truly learn from history if you hide it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! I'm a big proponent of physical media! I want to curate my own collection, not be subject to the whims of some big corporation who can decide to remove things whenever..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561353#post1561353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different track. It's maddening to be a collector and seeing how expensive the hobby is becoming and you may have to give up certain items because you don't have the funds for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I totally know how that goes. It's rough getting priced out of things. Kind of the reason I got out of collecting comics. It just got a little too expensive and there was just too much to keep track of...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T04:40:38-07:00","id":1561464,"title":"","content":"I'm not really one for physical collections, but I decidedly am of having the file/software in my own machine. Physical is too fragile to my taste, and thanks to my horrible brother I got too used to have my things broken.<br /> <br /> For me, two or three physical machines with my software and at least two other cloud services is the way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T13:30:39-07:00","id":1561478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561464#post1561464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really one for physical collections, but I decidedly am of having the file/software in my own machine. Physical is too fragile to my taste, and thanks to my horrible brother I got too used to have my things broken.<br /> <br /> For me, two or three physical machines with my software and at least two other cloud services is the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that. I do keep a lot of digital files (and a backup of those files), so I totally know how it goes.<br /> <br /> I do like to keep physical copies when I can, but there are days when I look at all the space it takes up and wonder why I collect so much. LOL.<br /> <br /> Hopefully some day when I'm gone my kid can sell some of this and make a little money. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T14:19:44-07:00","id":1561480,"title":"","content":"For me it really depends on how I experience the media itself.<br /> <br /> When it's things like books, I always want to have a physical copy if I can even if I use a digital copy 99% of the time when I'm just looking something up when it comes to my TTRPG collection. I find reading a physical book more enjoyable when I want to actually sit down and spend some time getting into it. I'm much more likely to find tasty ideas when physically reading that I tend to skip when it's digital (most people here are very familiar with some of my more common typos... I have a friend that didn't even know this account was me but figured it out from those alone, and that comes from a bit of a mental disconnect I have with digital text where I don't process it as thoroughly as I do printed or written text).<br /> <br /> For things like music, TV, and films, I used to be more physically inclined, but I've largely shifting to digital. These days I only worry about physical media for these if either I know it's something I want to be able to experience with a group (my home TV is basically a mini-theater for when friends come over and we want to watch a movie together at this point), or it's explicitly a choose to support specific artists/creatives by upgrading my purchase.<br /> <br /> For video games, I've moved rather strongly towards digital. I mean, it's already a digital media in the first place, the physical media only started as a simple way to get a digital file from the distributor to our homes. While we mentioned the storage issues of optical discs earlier... SSDs keep growing to pace. You can get a 4 TB thumb drive, while the current largest game on the market if you include all of the add-ons and DLC hits ~500 GB. Though SSDs can't replace physical media for storage (files generally degrade within a year if not plugged in, and most SSDs will start to crap out in about a decade outside of highly optimized conditions), if your collection is growing and you're keeping up with storage needs you're highly unlikely to lose data permanently unless something happens that's a much bigger problem than archiving your collection.<br /> <br /> That all said, I really wish there was more energy towards digital archiving. Way too much is being handled by enthusiasts and not large scale organizations. Which means there's minimal R&amp;D going into better forms of digital storage meant for archival purposes. The fact the the sun could just fart out a CME that happens to be big enough and gets close enough to Earth and boom... decades of human creativity gets erased... seems to not be a concern to nearly enough people. I know governments and businesses aren't run on altruism, but they all use extensive databases that aren't backed up in a fashion that can withstand a sudden high energy EMP (whether natural or something humanity ends up inflicting on itself). These are institutions that need records, and more and more those records are getting too big to back up on paper alone. Not funding solutions to long term digital storage is incredibly silly... but warning them hasn't worked for decades... so I don't have a lot of hope it'll change before something bad happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T15:00:06-07:00","id":1561483,"title":"","content":"I'm running into car \ud83d\ude97 problems with my engine and with my vehicle being 16 years old if it's worth the money \ud83d\udcb2\ud83d\udcb0 to replace the engine and having to spend 2500-10,000 on it.<br /> <br /> Especially with some of the repair work I had to get in the last year and a half.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T16:29:56-07:00","id":1561492,"title":"","content":"My grandfather had a very good rule of thumb for such things:<br /> <br /> If the cost of fixing something is more than 1/3 the value after it's fixed, it's not worth fixing anymore.<br /> <br /> While that can't resolve things like not being in a position to get a new (or new to you) car at the moment, sometimes you've got to fix a problem even if you're going to replace it soon anyway, it been a good way for me to make sure I'm not sinking money into things when I should be planning for a replacement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T19:22:54-07:00","id":1561497,"title":"","content":"I do think that physical media must continue, even if not for me. I just think it's a lesser concern when it comes to new products...<br /> <br /> IF they keep being ours and start to be archived, rather than kept as temporary services without a backup, because ownership by the company is more important, even if the result is loss.<br /> <br /> So I thoroughly agree we need way more effort into developing archival-quality media and record our cultural artifacts.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately that's not the logic of the market, and to be honest I don't see this logic changing as long as we have the current IP model.<br /> <br /> Not saying it would be simple to replace, even if the will to do it existed. But the core problem is a model that rewards hoarding of ideas at the expense of everything else, because denying access outside your limited system is more lucrative than letting go of past production. Not to say that stifling innovation by others through knowledge retention is more profitable than investing in innovation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T20:12:30-07:00","id":1561499,"title":"","content":"I'm probably going to have exchange vehicles, but I want to check with another shop that I have dealt with and doesn't pad the bill with unneeded charges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T07:32:41-07:00","id":1561514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561499#post1561499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably going to have exchange vehicles, but I want to check with another shop that I have dealt with and doesn't pad the bill with unneeded charges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone who owns a vehicle must study how it works internally because of those damned charges.<br /> <br /> I think in the ideal world this should be a requirement anyway, but that's because in the ideal world people don't feel the need to have a car.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T11:29:23-07:00","id":1561527,"title":"","content":"From what I have seen by the estimate, the cost to fix the engine is worth more money than the car is currently worth. So while I trust the crew that I'm going to get a second opinion on the engine issues. I think that they will say it's not worth the money as your car is reaching the end of its lifespan with over 250,000 km on it .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T11:45:14-07:00","id":1561528,"title":"","content":"On a more entertaining note. I did enjoy Space Ice roasting another Stephen Seagal movie and Mr. Seagal has taken mumbling his dialogue to a new level where you need subtitles to understand what he is saying.<br /> <br /> But at least he wasn't using a audio double this time and he used the stairs this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T19:08:16-07:00","id":1561546,"title":"","content":"In a ideal world Montparnasse, all vehicles would be built for long term reliability with no corners cut in making of automobiles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T21:07:52-07:00","id":1561551,"title":"","content":"While I think we're currently living in an era with a lot of perverse incentives when it comes to how manufacturers can maximize profits that leads to consistently negative consumer outcomes, there's a point where it stops being cutting corners and just becomes accepting that reality doesn't do perfection. There's always going to be a tipping point where the diminishing returns of more quality assurance ends up increasing prices higher than people could afford anyway. It's always going to be some level of balancing act.<br /> <br /> That's why it's better for everyone if we go in the direction monteparnas pointed: get as many people off of reliance on single modes of transportation. If it's viable to cycle/e-bike, drive, take a bus, or take light rail to do all of your regular travel, not only do you have choices so your normal method suites your lifestyle, you have backups if something goes wrong and you're not stuck without any options until you address whatever happened. Redundancy is generally the most efficient counter to inevitable breaks in the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T23:35:08-07:00","id":1561555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561546#post1561546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a ideal world Montparnasse, all vehicles would be built for long term reliability with no corners cut in making of automobiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of reasons why modern cars are built how they are, not all of them about cutting corners. Actually there's a bunch of brands that don't.<br /> <br /> In part, modern cars are <i><u>made</u></i> to break easily for a very serious reason: that makes accidents more survivable. I lived in the time when cars were made of durable materials.<br /> <br /> Between the greater energy transfer to the passengers and the survivors getting stuck in a distorted mass of steel, even with lower speed car crashes were way more lethal.<br /> <br /> Cars are still lethal. On top of the things Heavy Arms said, how it's important to have options, especially low cost, public options, I simply find the very notion of car as a personal right an absurd.<br /> <br /> We're talking a heavy machine that's intensely resource-heavy at every point of its lifetime: a lot of resources to make, a lot of resources on fuel, a lot more on maintenance, then road maintenance, garages, because cars don't just consume a lot, they require infrastructure that isn't a joke. And with power to transport five people plus heavy baggage at considerable speeds.<br /> <br /> All so people could feel free and each have one to drive alone, leave unused most of the day, conducting without much care because it is so ubiquitous and necessary it is unfeasible to actually demand from every one the level of caution it actually demands? At no point this was sustainable, and no one thought it would be when the automobile revolution was planned and executed.<br /> <br /> Problem is, none of those problems is solvable, because they are a direct result of the proposal of this machine: It will always be big and fast, so it'll always be more resource-heavy and dangerous than the alternatives.<br /> <br /> Same reason we don't have flying cars: we do, actually, had for a very long time. They're called helicopters and are hugely expensive, harder to pilot, harder to park and way noisier. That's not failure. That's the price of flying. The more we improve the tech, the more both get better, so the difference isn't really going anywhere.<br /> <br /> Now we live in a world where the problems of too many cars compounded to an extreme. It's reaching the topping point or already went over it. Fortunately younger generations are starting to see how ridiculous the cost is and seeking other options more readily.<br /> <br /> Of course it's hard for generations who grew up hearing that cars are freedom, rite of passage, basic adult right and absolute necessity to wrap the head around all those things being false. But they are... Except for one: thanks to a lot of work done on planning cities around cars and some countries like the US dilapidating the public transport system to appease lobbyists, it is indeed a necessity for many who have no choice. And a very real disability for others that can't afford one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T04:30:58-07:00","id":1561565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561480#post1561480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it really depends on how I experience the media itself.<br /> <br /> When it's things like books, I always want to have a physical copy if I can even if I use a digital copy 99% of the time when I'm just looking something up when it comes to my TTRPG collection. I find reading a physical book more enjoyable when I want to actually sit down and spend some time getting into it. I'm much more likely to find tasty ideas when physically reading that I tend to skip when it's digital (most people here are very familiar with some of my more common typos... I have a friend that didn't even know this account was me but figured it out from those alone, and that comes from a bit of a mental disconnect I have with digital text where I don't process it as thoroughly as I do printed or written text).<br /> <br /> For things like music, TV, and films, I used to be more physically inclined, but I've largely shifting to digital. These days I only worry about physical media for these if either I know it's something I want to be able to experience with a group (my home TV is basically a mini-theater for when friends come over and we want to watch a movie together at this point), or it's explicitly a choose to support specific artists/creatives by upgrading my purchase.<br /> <br /> For video games, I've moved rather strongly towards digital. I mean, it's already a digital media in the first place, the physical media only started as a simple way to get a digital file from the distributor to our homes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend towards physical for most things, books, movies, music... but I do like having digital sometimes, I mean I have a HUGE MP3 collection. But, I like digital so long as I can actually control the files. Meaning I can keep copies downloaded and access them whenever. <br /> <br /> But in the case of video games on a console, it seems like while you keep a download on your console, the company can decide to remove it from their storefront and then it sounds like even though you downloaded it, you can no longer access that game. It's possible I'm wrong in that, but it seems that way.<br /> <br /> And in the case of a lot of movies and games people have paid for, they've lost access to those when the company decided to remove them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561480#post1561480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we mentioned the storage issues of optical discs earlier... SSDs keep growing to pace. You can get a 4 TB thumb drive, while the current largest game on the market if you include all of the add-ons and DLC hits ~500 GB. Though SSDs can't replace physical media for storage (files generally degrade within a year if not plugged in, and most SSDs will start to crap out in about a decade outside of highly optimized conditions), if your collection is growing and you're keeping up with storage needs you're highly unlikely to lose data permanently unless something happens that's a much bigger problem than archiving your collection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've gone though a lot of different storage types in my day, floppy discs, zip discs, cd's, dvds, now hard drives. I currently have an 8TB external hard drive for all my stuff and then I have an exact duplicate of it I keep in a fireproof box. I just want to make sure I keep everything for as long as I'm able.<br /> <br /> I wish we could make SSDs a bit better. The fact the data degrades if not plugged in regularly is kinda worrisome...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561480#post1561480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all said, I really wish there was more energy towards digital archiving. Way too much is being handled by enthusiasts and not large scale organizations. Which means there's minimal R&amp;D going into better forms of digital storage meant for archival purposes. The fact the the sun could just fart out a CME that happens to be big enough and gets close enough to Earth and boom... decades of human creativity gets erased... seems to not be a concern to nearly enough people. I know governments and businesses aren't run on altruism, but they all use extensive databases that aren't backed up in a fashion that can withstand a sudden high energy EMP (whether natural or something humanity ends up inflicting on itself). These are institutions that need records, and more and more those records are getting too big to back up on paper alone. Not funding solutions to long term digital storage is incredibly silly... but warning them hasn't worked for decades... so I don't have a lot of hope it'll change before something bad happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally with you on this! There needs to be a lot more thought put into digital archiving. You think with all the money being wasted on stupid AI data centers we could use a fraction of that money on better digital archiving... ugh.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561499#post1561499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably going to have exchange vehicles, but I want to check with another shop that I have dealt with and doesn't pad the bill with unneeded charges.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Oh no! Sorry about that. Always a pain to have to get a new car...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561528#post1561528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more entertaining note. I did enjoy Space Ice roasting another Stephen Seagal movie and Mr. Seagal has taken mumbling his dialogue to a new level where you need subtitles to understand what he is saying.<br /> <br /> But at least he wasn't using a audio double this time and he used the stairs this time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, Stephen Seagal. For a hot minute he had it all...but he is certainly something else now. LOL!<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T04:57:07-07:00","id":1561567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561565#post1561565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in the case of video games on a console, it seems like while you keep a download on your console, the company can decide to remove it from their storefront and then it sounds like even though you downloaded it, you can no longer access that game. It's possible I'm wrong in that, but it seems that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not always, but sometimes is.<br /> <br /> Most games you can play offline still are full in your console. While the videogame will hardly have space for a huge collection, if you can get it you're ok.<br /> <br /> Some aren't like that. There are tests here and there with games that require regular validation to stay playable, once a week or once a month, and others you can only play online just so you have to validate the software.<br /> <br /> Those don't necessarily need to be in the store, but need a backend structure anyway. It won't become unplayable just because isn't there, but if the server goes down (as eventually will go), your game is useless.<br /> <br /> You can still recover many, though not through official channels. Usually the game you have is still complete, just not validating, so disabling the validation is possible, and legal. Unless it is under a leasing contract, a new move they're trying, then it's not only illegal, they can even make the game self-erase.<br /> <br /> But the real problem for most players today is the multiplayer, not the game working.<br /> <br /> Currently, games rely ever more on massive or at least several players. But they removed the option of configurable Ethernet and make the number of players too big for it to be feasible to gather so many people in a house.<br /> <br /> It's a life service strategy. You have the game, but they keep the structure to play with others. Without them you're alone, and eventually they will leave.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the only part of the market trying to keep archives and protect history for you is also the part that's trying to bring the whole market down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T08:49:48-07:00","id":1561571,"title":"","content":"There's a funny story but probably untrue story about Stephen Seagal Mr. Gone.<br /> <br /> According to the story it was a bet by a couple of Hollywood executives that they could make someone with no real acting talent and make him a famous star..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T16:06:58-07:00","id":1561576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561567#post1561567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not always, but sometimes is.<br /> <br /> Most games you can play offline still are full in your console. While the videogame will hardly have space for a huge collection, if you can get it you're ok.<br /> <br /> Some aren't like that. There are tests here and there with games that require regular validation to stay playable, once a week or once a month, and others you can only play online just so you have to validate the software.<br /> <br /> Those don't necessarily need to be in the store, but need a backend structure anyway. It won't become unplayable just because isn't there, but if the server goes down (as eventually will go), your game is useless.<br /> <br /> You can still recover many, though not through official channels. Usually the game you have is still complete, just not validating, so disabling the validation is possible, and legal. Unless it is under a leasing contract, a new move they're trying, then it's not only illegal, they can even make the game self-erase.<br /> <br /> But the real problem for most players today is the multiplayer, not the game working.<br /> <br /> Currently, games rely ever more on massive or at least several players. But they removed the option of configurable Ethernet and make the number of players too big for it to be feasible to gather so many people in a house.<br /> <br /> It's a life service strategy. You have the game, but they keep the structure to play with others. Without them you're alone, and eventually they will leave.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the only part of the market trying to keep archives and protect history for you is also the part that's trying to bring the whole market down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh dang! I wasn't sure on of that, so thanks for the extra info. Sounds like it can be a little crazy figuring out which work easily and which don't. But, glad to hear at least some digital ones still on the console will work so long as the files are still there..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561571#post1561571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a funny story but probably untrue story about Stephen Seagal Mr. Gone.<br /> <br /> According to the story it was a bet by a couple of Hollywood executives that they could make someone with no real acting talent and make him a famous star..</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL! You know, I wouldn't be shocked at all if that were true. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T16:29:08-07:00","id":1561577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561576#post1561576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh dang! I wasn't sure on of that, so thanks for the extra info. Sounds like it can be a little crazy figuring out which work easily and which don't. But, glad to hear at least some digital ones still on the console will work so long as the files are still there..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> LOL! You know, I wouldn't be shocked at all if that were true. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sure that there's some kernel of truth there Mr. Gone as the industry in the past has tried to push certain people to the forefront.<br /> <br /> I can see that they would cast a actor who didn't look like an action star who were popular and had the chiseled muscular build with a good head of hair. You had Seagal who wasn't super muscular and had a receding hairline and looked more like a typical person on the street.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately they inflicted upon the world a very self centered man with thin skin who couldn't take criticism and be allowed to struggle in a fight scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T05:29:39-07:00","id":1561625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561577#post1561577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure that there's some kernel of truth there Mr. Gone as the industry in the past has tried to push certain people to the forefront.<br /> <br /> I can see that they would cast a actor who didn't look like an action star who were popular and had the chiseled muscular build with a good head of hair. You had Seagal who wasn't super muscular and had a receding hairline and looked more like a typical person on the street.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately they inflicted upon the world a very self centered man with thin skin who couldn't take criticism and be allowed to struggle in a fight scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it's kinda crazy how self centered that dude is! He seemed ok for the first few movies maybe, but after a while he got super full of himself.<br /> <br /> And I guess they weren't totally wrong to want kind of a normal looking guy as an action star, look at Bruce Willis in the first Die Hard. Later on he get all muscled up, but in that first movie he looks pretty much like a regular dude.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T10:47:45-07:00","id":1561627,"title":"","content":"It's a shame on what happened to Bruce Willis with his Asphasia and steady decline. Whatever your personal feelings are on him, nobody should have to suffer neurological decline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T11:49:57-07:00","id":1561657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561627#post1561627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a shame on what happened to Bruce Willis with his Asphasia and steady decline. Whatever your personal feelings are on him, nobody should have to suffer neurological decline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I felt bad for him. That's rough to deal with. And it does explain a few things about him in his later years before we all knew... doesn't excuse all of that behavior, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T13:31:28-07:00","id":1561658,"title":"","content":"Lots of people in the entertainment business who were jerks don't deserve some of the health problems they get.<br /> <br /> Unless it's Steven Seagal and then it's hard to muster any empathy for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-13-2026, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T14:53:55-07:00","id":1561660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561658#post1561658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of people in the entertainment business who were jerks don't deserve some of the health problems they get.<br /> <br /> Unless it's Steven Seagal and then it's hard to muster any empathy for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know if it's his case, but no one deserves Alzheimer's Disease, Dementia, or other that wipes memory and/or fundamental cognition.<br /> <br /> It destroy your very capacity of being yourself, and that isn't just terrifying: it also means the person who'll face the worst of it isn't the same who lived that life before.<br /> <br /> Whatever crimes your enemies committed, the disease won't punish them, but replace them for an innocent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T16:43:17-07:00","id":1561665,"title":"","content":"With Bruce Willis it was Asphasia that gradually robbed him of his ability to communicate and as an actor that would be a terrible fate as he spent a good chunk of his adult life in a profession that he enjoyed and be forced to give it up.<br /> <br /> There's talk that he is suffering from other cognitive issues but since it's from tabloid sources I'd would take it with a grain of salt \ud83e\uddc2.<br /> <br /> And from personal experience it's very tragic to see a loved one suffer from Vascular Dementia and see more and more bad days outnumber the good days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T14:47:04-07:00","id":1561739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561658#post1561658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of people in the entertainment business who were jerks don't deserve some of the health problems they get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree... serious health issues are no joke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561658#post1561658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it's Steven Seagal and then it's hard to muster any empathy for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeeaaa... that's a good point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561660#post1561660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know if it's his case, but no one deserves Alzheimer's Disease, Dementia, or other that wipes memory and/or fundamental cognition.<br /> <br /> It destroy your very capacity of being yourself, and that isn't just terrifying: it also means the person who'll face the worst of it isn't the same who lived that life before.<br /> <br /> Whatever crimes your enemies committed, the disease won't punish them, but replace them for an innocent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I'm definitely with you on that. It's horrible that people have to deal with that... and like you said, then in the case of someone who has done something horrible, you're left with a person who can't remember any bad they did. It's sad...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T11:09:00-07:00","id":1561775,"title":"","content":"I like working in retail, but I wish some people would read the fine print. Some items are not carried in the store and must be ordered online through a 3rd party vendor that we have a contract with. Or it's here but we're still unloading the truck or said truck hasn't arrived yet.<br /> <br /> Most people are cool with the fact but there's always someone who is not so understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T11:41:46-07:00","id":1561778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561775#post1561775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like working in retail, but I wish some people would read the fine print. Some items are not carried in the store and must be ordered online through a 3rd party vendor that we have a contract with. Or it's here but we're still unloading the truck or said truck hasn't arrived yet.<br /> <br /> Most people are cool with the fact but there's always someone who is not so understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's dealing with people. As a bank clerk I've seen all sorts of problematic and even crazy customers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T14:01:24-07:00","id":1561781,"title":"","content":"I used to have a job in a business-to-business environment rather than normal retail and we still had people like that. There's something surreal about listening to someone complain about unreasonable customers that don't understand that shipping takes time... and then have that person yell at you because their shipment hasn't unloaded 30 minutes before schedule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T16:23:07-07:00","id":1561789,"title":"","content":"A different (though technically a call back) grumble:<br /> <br /> I was prepared for a lot of stupid takes regarding the Odyssey with it releasing tomorrow... but someone that went to the early premiere complaining that it was in American English just... boggles my mind. There isn't a correct English accent for an ancient Greek poem adaptation.<br /> <br /> I could understand a desire for the film to use different accents to help sort the different groups presented in the narrative... but it's not like Homer wrote it that way or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T16:50:02-07:00","id":1561791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561789#post1561789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but someone that went to the early premiere complaining that it was in American English just... boggles my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure...<br /> <br /> I mean, if the casting had been trained/selected to display a range of Greek and Turkish accents, that would have been cool and all. Also quite impressive.<br /> <br /> Because. You know. Would be quite unexpected.<br /> <br /> Or if they talked in Koin\u00e8 and the movie was subtitled for all audiences, that would be very nice to see.<br /> <br /> You know, nothing like hiring people from across the British Islands, India and Australia to represent with fidelity all the accents Homer painstakingly describes in detail in the poem he recited from memory...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T17:16:50-07:00","id":1561793,"title":"","content":"Was the person that was complaining Heavy Arms a major social media personality with a proven track record of horrible takes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T17:38:30-07:00","id":1561796,"title":"","content":"I didn't recognize them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T18:17:28-07:00","id":1561799,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of smaller and less polished media grifters like Yellow flash, Ranting For Vengeance, Ryan Kinel and Overlord DVD who seem to get everything from Reddit and their source is &quot;Just Trust Me People.&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T21:45:23-07:00","id":1561804,"title":"","content":"To be fair it wasn't a big surprise that the media grifters would be going after Christopher Nolan Odsesey when it was announced that Trans actor Elliot Page and Lupita Nyongo were cast in the film and could keep their channels running and were still doing hit jobs on Disney Star Wars, Star Trek, MCU, DCU, Brie Larson and Rachel Zeggler.<br /> <br /> Strange that they didn't have a problem with the principal cast not looking like they were from that part of the world or held political views that they the grifters would call &quot;woke&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T01:00:22-07:00","id":1561811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1561804#post1561804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange that they didn't have a problem with the principal cast not looking like they were from that part of the world</div> </div> </div> </div>For them that's not a thing. It's Ancient Greece, ergo, it's white.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me how much I find the term &quot;Western World/Civilization&quot; distasteful.<br /> <br /> It is intended to mean a portion of the world that share a strong common cultural background, and defines this part of the world by their inheritance of Greek and Roman cultures.<br /> <br /> But it's actually only applied to white people for the sake of being white and even then, most of the time that it does is take the view of six of the richest countries in the world, maybe adding the opinions of a few convenient actors, and pretend it represents the whole of Europe.<br /> <br /> Reality: Romans and Greeks didn't had an European identity. For them, the World\u2122 was the Mediterranean, and even then with focus on the Eastern Mediterranean. While they each saw themselves as a superior civilization, they saw as still worthy of the title the peoples of the old Levant: Iranians, Akkadians, Canaanites including Hebrew, Egyptians, going as far east as Mesopotamia at least, and as far south as Nubia. Not equals or anything like that, but for sure people you can talk with.<br /> <br /> They thought of Europe in varying degrees of violent, dimwitted barbarian. When the Empire fell, the works of Greek philosophers was lost to Europe. They would have been irretrievably lost if not for the brave efforts of Muslim scholars. Muslims who later occupied Al-Andaluz, in southern Spain, and turned it into a center of learning that slowly reintroduced that philosophy and much more to Europe.<br /> <br /> Came the Spanish Reconquista, and with the cultural spoils of Andaluzia the kingdoms of the Iberian Peninsula became the superpowers that started the Navigations, carrying a culture of Romance language, the Roman Christianity and the recovered Greek wisdom enhanced by the Muslims. Aside everything horrible they did in this continent, they achieved the goal of mostly imposing their culture, and they did it completely. It's not without reason that we're called Latin America, inheritors for good and ill of the language of the Italian Lacio.<br /> <br /> Let me be clear: Greeks and Romans were xenophobic assholes. Arabs weren't saints. Some changes the Germanic peoples brought to Roman institutions were definitely improvements. And the loss of so much indigenous culture in America is horrific beyond measure. But for all the gods, seeing a bunch of mainly Germanic assholes claiming both the cardinal direction (poor Celts) and the cultural &quot;origin&quot; that had little to do with them all along, while pushing to the margins literally everyone with some actual legitimacy to it, that's infuriating.<br /> <br /> Also false, since the views of the &quot;Western World&quot; is frequently the West minus Celts, a lot of other ethnic minorities in Western Europe, and almost the entirety of Eastern Europe. Any similarity is a happy coincidence, England and Spain didn't invent imperialism, colonialism, genocide and cultural erasure when they went to the sea, they had plenty of time practicing in their backyards and never stopped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T11:39:40-07:00","id":1561834,"title":"","content":"It reminds me of what the late Lemmy K from Motorhead said about of how he couldn't wrap his head around racism and how judging an entire group of people on the actions of a few bad apples was stupid and I remember a response he gave to you a young black teenager to enjoy whatever music you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-17-2026, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T23:04:38-07:00","id":1561959,"title":"","content":"Another old grumble. When people call women who reach a certain age and say they hit a wall \ud83e\uddf1. I don't know but when said people don't look all that good themselves shouldn't cast stones and your proving what actor Doug Bradley of Hellraiser fame that the entertainment industry is harsh on women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T13:57:55-07:00","id":1562009,"title":"","content":"Speaking of entertainment industry, I don't like when popular series get cancelled because they <i>&quot;didn't hit the right target demographic.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Mother fucker, who cares about the target demographic!? If your show is popular, it's still making money!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T18:09:03-07:00","id":1562017,"title":"","content":"There's got to be more than that DarkKing. A network cancelling a popular Franchise because it didn't reach the target audience seems self defeating and they are in the business of making money \ud83d\udcb0 of any IP's they have rights to","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T19:03:06-07:00","id":1562022,"title":"","content":"It's not complicated: target demographics are tied to advertising and merch sales.<br /> <br /> Popularity only matters if you sell something directly to consumers. A box-office sales don't care about target demographics because it doesn't matter who buys a ticket as long as tickets get sold.<br /> <br /> If you make your real money on ads and sales of additional items, then you can't just be popular, you have to be popular with people that are going to spend money based on that. A show that's targeted towards kids is going to attract advertisers shilling kids stuff (mostly so the kids pester parents into buying stuff), and and tie-in products you have in the works have to work for kids. If your show isn't popular with kids, but rather popular with 30 somethings with kids that are enjoying the nostalgia kick but don't have a lot of disposable income, you're going to have to completely swap your ads which is going to be a financial hit for awhile, and you might make a fraction of the merch sales you were expecting to.<br /> <br /> That's how popularity doesn't turn a profit because of demographics. It sucks, but it's just something that's gotten worse despite having been the way things have been done for longer than most of the posters here's parents have been alive. Ads have been part of entertainment back when radio was a fancy new technology, and maximizing ad returns by targeting ads has been part of the equation the whole time. It was just back in the early radio days, they could only target on very broad grounds because there were only a few core groups being catered to. Now we've been data-mined to hell and back so we can be microtargeted; which forces creators to play the algorithm game (even if they're on streaming giants like Netflix or whatever) or risk not getting money even with plenty of views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T21:43:57-07:00","id":1562023,"title":"","content":"I forgot that IP makes a great deal of money from merchandise such as toys, video games and tie in novels and many more that I haven't brought up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T06:03:11-07:00","id":1562042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562022#post1562022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not complicated: target demographics are tied to advertising and merch sales.<br /> <br /> Popularity only matters if you sell something directly to consumers. A box-office sales don't care about target demographics because it doesn't matter who buys a ticket as long as tickets get sold.<br /> <br /> If you make your real money on ads and sales of additional items, then you can't just be popular, you have to be popular with people that are going to spend money based on that. A show that's targeted towards kids is going to attract advertisers shilling kids stuff (mostly so the kids pester parents into buying stuff), and and tie-in products you have in the works have to work for kids. If your show isn't popular with kids, but rather popular with 30 somethings with kids that are enjoying the nostalgia kick but don't have a lot of disposable income, you're going to have to completely swap your ads which is going to be a financial hit for awhile, and you might make a fraction of the merch sales you were expecting to.<br /> <br /> That's how popularity doesn't turn a profit because of demographics. It sucks, but it's just something that's gotten worse despite having been the way things have been done for longer than most of the posters here's parents have been alive. Ads have been part of entertainment back when radio was a fancy new technology, and maximizing ad returns by targeting ads has been part of the equation the whole time. It was just back in the early radio days, they could only target on very broad grounds because there were only a few core groups being catered to. Now we've been data-mined to hell and back so we can be microtargeted; which forces creators to play the algorithm game (even if they're on streaming giants like Netflix or whatever) or risk not getting money even with plenty of views.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did 'collectors' all collectively die out when I wasn't looking?<br /> <br /> Why do people even have basement cellars, if they aren't using them as a trophy room for their limited edition action figures? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T08:05:36-07:00","id":1562045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562042#post1562042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did 'collectors' all collectively die out when I wasn't looking?<br /> <br /> Why do people even have basement cellars, if they aren't using them as a trophy room for their limited edition action figures? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Collectors aren't that big a demographic, despite growth. For franchises like Star Wars collectors can respond for up to 35% of the market in spending, rarely more.<br /> <br /> That's the absolutely very best scenario: a SW show that hits whatever audience will make a lot of money because collectors will buy anything from the show and it's well established among them. Even then, if they get prepared to sell mostly light saber toys for 5-10 yo boys and the show doesn't hit this demographic, that means two thirds of expected revenue is lost.<br /> <br /> For a new IP collectors are not an established demographic. They'll be maybe 10%, even less of the viewers. Collector culture around a new show takes time to form. If a new cartoon faces the very same situation, they may see more than 9/10 toys getting dust despite success.<br /> <br /> It's not a small thing: merch requires a lot of design, prep, logistics to get to stores. Even just changing production rates with the factory can be a nightmare.<br /> <br /> We have a clear contrast of how it works with Disney's <i>Encanto</i>: the movie was a far greater success than expected, but still Disney made the wrong bet. The character Isabela has the iconic Princess appeal despite not being the main one, is a standard pretty girl, and before her development arc is the flowery type. Disney heavily invested in her merch, with huge variety of options and high volumes. The least investment was on Luisa, the muscled strong sister, who got three or four simple toys total.<br /> <br /> By the end of 2024, 3 years after release, they hadn't managed to match the merch enough to the actual demand. Isabela's merch tanked hard as even those who wanted her didn't want her flowery design, while Luisa is still today the hardest to find and by then still had considerable waiting lines. For Disney this was not a small hiccup: it was a disaster. Even if for them it didn't mean to &quot;cancel&quot; Encanto, it was a big financial failure.<br /> <br /> A series has It even worse with sponsorship and advertising. Those are the things that keep most shows going, and also depend on target audience. Sometimes you can change them with some ease, but there's always a challenge involved as several factors affect who'll benefit from buying the spot, if they want the association, if the time is good for them and if they can match the price you want... Or need.<br /> <br /> Sometimes those are all workable problems. But other times the cost of changing course can be genuinely prohibitive, or still so fraught with market uncertainty that ditching the whole thing for a safer bet is cheaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T11:06:33-07:00","id":1562052,"title":"","content":"Collecting is an expensive hobby DarkKing and not everyone can afford to do it. As adults we collect because of a love a particular franchise. But it's not likely we are going to play with them and most toys and such are geared towards kids to play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T12:01:55-07:00","id":1562054,"title":"","content":"It's also important to remember that contemporary collector culture is directly impacted from C-suite boardrooms down to individual customer choices by the rise of microtransactions and digital &quot;collectibles.&quot;<br /> <br /> The cost and barrier of entry to, say, getting a fomo skin colab in Fortnight is an insanely more profitable enterprise for businesses and feels less onerous to consumers in the moment (and is if you're only paying microtransactions very selectively, but that whole environment is designed to get you to be as spend-happy as possible). No factories, no shipping, no storage... just a file that can copied infinitely and given an arbitrary price designed to feel inexpensive but still make tons of money in aggregate.<br /> <br /> This is kinda good for physical collectors because collectibles are actually rare and therefore special again. We're not in the false-scarcity hype bubble that nuked comic books when it burst and made Beanie Babies a thing people were buying as &quot;investments.&quot; Physical merch has to actually be kinda special and something desirable to just own and put on display/used instead of being locked away to ensure mint-in-box status. But that also comes with, well, higher prices on top of the economy being shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T14:49:16-07:00","id":1562058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562052#post1562052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Collecting is an expensive hobby DarkKing and not everyone can afford to do it. As adults we collect because of a love a particular franchise. But it's not likely we are going to play with them and most toys and such are geared towards kids to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had sooooo many Ninja Turtles and G.I Joes as a kid.<br /> <br /> Then came the short lived Beanie Baby craze. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T15:54:32-07:00","id":1562062,"title":"","content":"The Beanie Baby callback is the perfect example of Heavy Arms' point. That whole craze was manufactured scarcity dressed up as investing, and it collapsed the second people realized the tags didn't mean anything. What Fortnite skins did was move that same dopamine hit into something with zero storage costs and infinite supply, so the studios win either way. Kind of grimly funny that it took digital microtransactions to make physical collecting feel meaningful again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29129-daria22","name":"daria22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T22:45:23-07:00","id":1562073,"title":"","content":"It was Transformers and GI-Joe myself that I spent considerable time getting as a child. Now when I have time and I see a great Transformers figure that was from F1 or Beast Wars. I have to caution myself not to go overboard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T23:17:18-07:00","id":1562075,"title":"","content":"Just an old grumble. I wish people who are fanboys or fangirls of Batman need to understand that his contingency plans doesn't guarantee victory and it only gives the Dark Knight a fighting chance of survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T04:04:13-07:00","id":1562078,"title":"","content":"Even then, said contingency plans only work on the assumption that the former ally is still holding back in that fight.<br /> <br /> No amount of kryptonite in the universe is going to save you, if Superman decides to fly into low orbit and just snipe you with telescopic heat vision. And don't tell me he can't, because there's a comic panel that shows him scorching half a planet with a more wide dispersal version of this very technique.<br /> <br /> <br /> Where as The Flash is so fast, he can travel across the entire universe faster than instantaneous teleportation. Batman wouldn't even have the opportunity to activate his contingency plan, before he would be dead where he stood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T06:37:23-07:00","id":1562080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562075#post1562075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just an old grumble. I wish people who are fanboys or fangirls of Batman need to understand that his contingency plans doesn't guarantee victory and it only gives the Dark Knight a fighting chance of survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the sentiment, but I think it has a few problematic assumptions.<br /> <br /> The first is the dismissive language that treats the fandom as a unified thing. &quot;Fanboy/girl&quot; carries a connotations you know to not be neutral, of someone who's by definition intense to unreasonable levels.<br /> <br /> Are everyone who buy the trope of &quot;perfect planner&quot; actually intense about the character? Are all those who are intense buying the trope? Are all intense fans unreasonable?<br /> <br /> The &quot;should&quot; part is similarly questionable. Why should? A story can abide to &quot;absurd&quot; rules for a number of reasons. Some Batman stories are satire on the superhero aspect, others are just it played straight: why's a solar-powered affront to physics or a &quot;force of infinite momentum&quot; more realistic than the guy who's just &quot;that good&quot;? Or are they just distinct concepts that catter to distinct audiences?<br /> <br /> Sure, if you're in a particular discussion, with particular assumptions, there may be a number of ways how people assuming this trope as a trump over others can be disruptive, but I think analyzing the specifics is more interesting than lumping a whole fandom in a crude simplification.<br /> <br /> On arguing about how a plan would fail if the opposition stepped out of character, I think that is missing the whole point of what a plan is, royally. Plans work because people behave in a consistent manner, that's the whole point of a plan and of having personality. If Superman or Flash decide to act out of character, they're not Superman or Flash. What's the point by then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T09:07:46-07:00","id":1562085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562080#post1562080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On arguing about how a plan would fail if the opposition stepped out of character, I think that is missing the whole point of what a plan is, royally. Plans work because people behave in a consistent manner, that's the whole point of a plan and of having personality. If Superman or Flash decide to act out of character, they're not Superman or Flash. What's the point by then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman's contingency plans are precisely designed for out of character situations. He made them for situations where Superman, the Flash, Wonder Woman, or any other super hero turns against the people of earth, and needs to be taken down.<br /> <br /> Take the existence of Red Kryptonite, for example. Instead of killing Kryptonians, it inverts their personality for 24 hours. Which means that when Superman is exposed to it, he temporarily becomes an evil tyrant, instead of the blue boyscout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T09:42:45-07:00","id":1562086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562085#post1562085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman's contingency plans are precisely designed for out of character situations. He made them for situations where Superman, the Flash, Wonder Woman, or any other super hero turns against the people of earth, and needs to be taken down.<br /> <br /> Take the existence of Red Kryptonite, for example. Instead of killing Kryptonians, it inverts their personality for 24 hours. Which means that when Superman is exposed to it, he temporarily becomes an evil tyrant, instead of the blue boyscout.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still they're not completely random, not to say it's perfectly reasonable to consider that:<br /> <br /> 1. We don't see all plans, only the ones that get leaked, compromised or used. It's reasonable to imagine he would have different plans for different situations;<br /> <br /> 2. It's also reasonable that he doesn't have plans for literally anything, first because the authors didn't thought about it, second because some scenarios may, indeed, be unwinnable.<br /> <br /> All in all, it's a waste of time to keep comparing a given plan in a piece of fiction to any number of scenarios that didn't happen in said fiction. You're not comparing powers or something, you're essentially comparing plot-dependent details by proposing the plot wasn't there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T10:38:52-07:00","id":1562088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562086#post1562086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All in all, it's a waste of time to keep comparing a given plan in a piece of fiction to any number of scenarios that didn't happen in said fiction. You're not comparing powers or something, you're essentially comparing plot-dependent details by proposing the plot wasn't there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose. I just wanted to highlight the fact that Batman being the legendary strategist and master of 20 different fighting styles is nowhere near as much of an advantage as his fandom would like to believe.<br /> <br /> If any of the Justice League's core members truly did go evil, and stopped restraining themselves, they could destroy Batman with very little effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T11:23:15-07:00","id":1562090,"title":"","content":"Admittedly I was general in my statement Montparnasse about fanboys and fangirls. But in my experience is that they have very little knowledge of other characters in the universe that there favorite wouldn't be able to do much against and think Batman, Wolverine, and Thanos are infallible/unbeatable.<br /> <br /> I'm a big Batman fan and I roll my eyes when I encounter this mindset. As smart and capable as the Dark Knight is and he needs it in a world where we have Amazon's, Green Lanterns, Speedsters and God like superhumans to have an edge. <br /> <br /> He can't account for everything and people can counter your plans in ways you didn't expect.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T14:33:58-07:00","id":1562094,"title":"","content":"I don't understand the whole Noire genre, or its appeal.<br /> <br /> Every single Noire story I've ever seen has followed the same exact formula.<br /> <br /> 1 - It's depicted in black and white<br /> <br /> 2 - It's told from the perspective of a private detective.<br /> <br /> 3 - They spend nearly the entire story monologuing about how much of a shit hole society has become.<br /> <br /> 4 - Very likely dies at some point in the story.<br /> <br /> Like, I could get it if this was a one off case. Maybe a couple movies. But an entire genre of story telling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T15:25:20-07:00","id":1562095,"title":"","content":"Like any media genre part of the problem is that the definitions are going to be fuzzy. If you only watch &quot;classic&quot; noir... of course they're all in black and white. If you include later &quot;neo-noir&quot; films you're going to get color films. That's just when the movies where made and what the available technology (or at least budgets) was.<br /> <br /> So, by point:<br /> <br /> 1 - the main period of noir films was still during the black and white era of film making. While color film existed, it was extremely expensive and the costs didn't come down until after the initial genre heyday. Modern noir films (or whatever sub-noir label you want to apply) may or may not keep to their aesthetic. Nolan's <i>Memento</i> is kind of the perfect example of a neo-noir as it is half black and white, and half color.<br /> <br /> 2 - The minority of film noirs are actually PI lead stories. Undercover/plain clothes police and overt criminals are more common protagonists in the genre. Femme fatales are common protagonists during a period where female lead movies were not common. The PI lead is more present in modern references to specific genre hits being icons for the genre rather than being what the genre was actually like. Imagine in 60 years people treating the first Iron Man movie as the prototypical superhero movie, and thus all references to superhero films are about rich geniuses in power armor despite how obvious it is to us now that's really not what the genre is like.<br /> <br /> 3 - Monologues are definitely part of the genre because it's meant to highlight the isolation and alienation experienced by people on the edges of society. The whole point is that these are people with nobody to talk to that would understand them and the hard life they've been pushed into. Like any genre it's something that can be done well, or not. If you hate jump scares you're not going to like the horror genre much, but that doesn't mean it's hard to grasp the role of the technique and how it appeals to people that do.<br /> <br /> 4 - Lots of noir protagonists don't die... not really sure where that's coming from. But the name &quot;noir&quot; comes from the idea that these are films with dark themes and gritty plots. It's a genre that mixed the hopeless of people that didn't recover well from the Great Depression with an influx of German creatives fleeing from the rise of Nazism. So, yeah, it's not a genre where heros win or even survive as a default.<br /> <br /> Like, if you don't like the genre, that's cool, there's plenty of them, but it doesn't sound like you've gotten access to the variety within it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T16:05:33-07:00","id":1562096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562095#post1562095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 - Lots of noir protagonists don't die... not really sure where that's coming from. But the name &quot;noir&quot; comes from the idea that these are films with dark themes and gritty plots. It's a genre that mixed the hopeless of people that didn't recover well from the Great Depression with an influx of German creatives fleeing from the rise of Nazism. So, yeah, it's not a genre where heros win or even survive as a default.<br /> <br /> Like, if you don't like the genre, that's cool, there's plenty of them, but it doesn't sound like you've gotten access to the variety within it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My dad's been watching the Sin City show lately, where it currently seems like the detective who was the main focus of the story up to this point has killed himself.<br /> <br /> There's also Rotshreck from The Watchmen, who ends up begging Dr. Manhatten to kill him near the end of the movie.<br /> <br /> And then we have Fabien from Bloodlines 2, who is already dead at the beginning of the story and hitching a ride in our body.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Anyways, thanks for the analytical breakdown. It's just not my thing, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T16:26:04-07:00","id":1562097,"title":"","content":"Social Media grifters are scraping the bottom of the barrel for content to vent about. There shocked that The Odyssey is very successful and are trying to claim it's still a flop.<br /> <br /> But now some of them are upset in the upcoming Avengers Doomsday movie that Rebecca Romijn who is returning as Mystique is opting to use CGI to make her skin look blue with only her face, neck and arms having protethecs instead of the full body makeup she would spend several hours having in the makeup chair.<br /> <br /> I can see why she wouldn't be want to go through that again. But some are complaining about it and it's very sad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T17:00:56-07:00","id":1562099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562094#post1562094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the whole Noire genre, or its appeal.<br /> <br /> People love gritty crime stories and there's a audience for every genre.<br /> <br /> Every single Noire story I've ever seen has followed the same exact formula.<br /> <br /> Name a genre that doesn't follow common themes?<br /> <br /> So that is strange statement.<br /> <br /> 1 - It's depicted in black and white<br /> <br /> The earliest films were shot in black and white for cost issues and also it helps sell the settings better. Not to mention to hide flaws in set design.<br /> <br /> 2 - It's told from the perspective of a private detective.<br /> <br /> They are the main protagonist of the story and it works for that reason.<br /> <br /> 3 - They spend nearly the entire story monologuing about how much of a shit hole society has become.<br /> <br /> So does Cyberpunk and other genres and it about how nothing is simple and problems are not solved cleanly or neatly.<br /> <br /> 4 - Very likely dies at some point in the story.<br /> <br /> Not always as I remember Mike Hammer and others who don't die. When the character does die it usually for good reasons and not for shock value.<br /> <br /> Like, I could get it if this was a one off case. Maybe a couple movies. But an entire genre of story telling?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to watch more noir films.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-24-2026, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T17:25:23-07:00","id":1562100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562096#post1562096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, thanks for the analytical breakdown. It's just not my thing, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't want to harp on this... maybe watch some actual noir films before deciding that? Sin City is the only thing you listed that even kinda qualifies as noir and it's extremely hyperbolic in how it uses noir tropes (given the creator, judging noir by Sin City is like judging historical epics by 300), with the other two being noir themed characters in non-noir pieces.<br /> <br /> I completely get not wanting to spend time on older films like <i>The Maltese Falcon</i> to see what the height of the original genre was like because watching older movies is always its own barrier... but there's a lot of more recent stuff that's much more representative of the noir genre even if it gets classed as neo-noir, tech noir, or whatever.<br /> <br /> There's no guarantee you'll like it, but I think it's not hard to agree that watching some actual noir stories would be a better way to go than stuff with some noir-ish flavor sprinkled on it if you want to really know how you feel about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T18:28:54-07:00","id":1562101,"title":"","content":"Sin City is more pulp thriller, hard-boiled crime and neo -noir then classic noir adventure. As it has cast of rotating characters that takes place in a corrupt city ruled by ruthless mob families and the Roarkes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T22:20:04-07:00","id":1562102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562088#post1562088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose. I just wanted to highlight the fact that Batman being the legendary strategist and master of 20 different fighting styles is nowhere near as much of an advantage as his fandom would like to believe.<br /> <br /> If any of the Justice League's core members truly did go evil, and stopped restraining themselves, they could destroy Batman with very little effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this all he's supposed to be in their analysis?<br /> <br /> Is being a that good character trope really not that much? In which context?<br /> <br /> What being like that means in their fictional universe? What resources they give access to?<br /> <br /> What &quot;going evil&quot; even means outside a specific plot?<br /> <br /> Is it a &quot;this character now exists only to defeat Batman&quot; thing?<br /> <br /> I personally think a version of any League member made only to defeat Batman will be a proof of his success, not failure, as you have to go this far.<br /> <br /> By the way, a version of any of them made only to prove they can destroy one specific other member would succeed at doing so regardless.<br /> <br /> Going back to what I originally pointed, which &quot;fandom&quot; are you referring to? There are fans of Batman that don't like his participation in the League. Who don't like perfect plans, but prefer other versions/aspects of the character. There are plenty of fans that know the character is a powerhouse only within a specific depiction and are fine with this.<br /> <br /> You're not highlighting anything about the character. You're highlighting that you don't like the fact some people are annoying fans and you prefer to bash the whole work and fandom rather than engage meaningfully with the question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562090#post1562090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly I was general in my statement Montparnasse about fanboys and fangirls. But in my experience is that they have very little knowledge of other characters </div> </div> </div> </div>This is a universal problem. The most vocal fans of anything are usually young, ignorant and loudly disparaging over things they don't know, because protecting perceived superiority is their thing.<br /> <br /> Some works and characters get more or less than normal of this, but just look at the morons who shout around about Goku, Naruto, Boruto, the Emperor of Mankind, Thanos, Iron Man, Wolverine and so on.<br /> <br /> Are they the fandom? I'm a fan of some of those and know both the fandom and a lot of others within that find such loudmouths just as annoying as anyone else thinks.<br /> <br /> Batman being a super strategist that can defeat anyone is a valid depiction, it's a genre of its own. Not my cup of tea, but for each their own. Most fans of this depiction understand that it isn't a clearcut fact in a neutral comparison with other characters.<br /> <br /> Many fans appreciate limitation, I like Batman in Gotham, taking care of detective work and scarying criminals with party tricks, while being mindful of how his costumed activities are far from the solution and that he's just punching poor people while the real cause is of Gotham's problems is systemic inequality and the high society that finances violence, a system Bruce Wayne is a part of and needs far more ingenuity to even scratch.<br /> <br /> In fact I'm personally annoyed even with Lucius Fox and the whole hyper tech, military grade version of the character that's all the rage these days. But all those are Batman, my fave version isn't truer or better intrinsically, it's just what I like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562094#post1562094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the whole Noire genre, or its appeal.<br /> <br /> Every single Noire story I've ever seen has followed the same exact formula.<br /> <br /> 1 - It's depicted in black and white<br /> <br /> 2 - It's told from the perspective of a private detective.<br /> <br /> 3 - They spend nearly the entire story monologuing about how much of a shit hole society has become.<br /> <br /> 4 - Very likely dies at some point in the story.<br /> <br /> Like, I could get it if this was a one off case. Maybe a couple movies. But an entire genre of story telling?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like Noir either and I know this is not their thing.<br /> <br /> Noir is a gritty social examination marked by pessimism and using a lot of chiaroscuro. It's a big influence on WoD, by the way. I don't like because gritty and pessimism aren't my thing, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Also it's a genre, not a character trope. Being Noir-coded isn't being Noir. Next you'll say that Spider Man Noir is a Serious expression of the genre.<br /> <br /> By the way, I like many parodies and satires on Noir, but the best ones are by people that get, like and respect the genre rather than just bashing it mindlessly the way The Boys bash superheros.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562097#post1562097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social Media grifters are scraping the bottom of the barrel for content to vent about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always did, I still don't know why you keep watching their stuff. Just stop feeding the trolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T23:17:49-07:00","id":1562104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562102#post1562102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this all he's supposed to be in their analysis?<br /> <br /> Is being a that good character trope really not that much? In which context?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, that's all that Batman is <b>supposed to</b> be, because Batman is also <b>supposed to</b> be a normal human. While the feats that he is capable of performing may seem extraordinary, it is theoretically possible for other people to achieve the same feats, if they worked for it.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the writers sometimes like to wank Batman off, by having him demonstrate pseudo-magical feats that he learned from Tibetan Monks. Or having his reflexes be elevated to such an absurd degree, he's able to catch machine gun fire with his hands.<br /> <br /> For reference, Myth Busters proved that the stories of martial artists catching arrows out of mid flight is just Hollywood showmanship. Even after building a machine that was capable of moving at 10X the world speed record, it was still too slow to catch a flying arrow.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a result, Batman's whole character concept has a bad habit of contradicting itself. He's supposed to be a normal human, but the feats he has demonstrated far exceed even the greatest of human capabilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562102#post1562102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What &quot;going evil&quot; even means outside a specific plot?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean in the context of the character turning against the people of earth, and abandoning their moral principles.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of arguments which will defend Superman, claiming that the reason why he struggles in so many fights, is because he is holding back his power. Out of fear of accidentally hurting somebody. So it stands to reason that if Superman, or some other hero were to shed that mentality and truly go all out with their powers, not even a fully prepped Batman would be able to stop them.<br /> <br /> <br /> And that's another thing that should be brought up. Virtually every argument I see regarding if Batman could defeat somebody includes some variation of <i>&quot;with prep time&quot; </i>added as a condition to the fight.<br /> <br /> Well, what if there was no prep time? What if the opponent was fully aware of who Batman was (some of his villains actually are), and decided instead of fooling around, they were just going to go straight for the throat and attack him before Batman had the chance to set everything up?<br /> <br /> Or, what if the villain didn't fall for Batman's trap, and instead attacked him from a different angle? Like that one episode where Lex tries to lure Superman into a reinforced panic room that's lined with red solar energy generators. Instead of walking inside and getting his ass kicked, Supes decided to close the door with Luthor inside, and then used his super strength to rip the entire chamber out of his foundations and fly away with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562102#post1562102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it a &quot;this character now exists only to defeat Batman&quot; thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Discussing plot armor is irrelevant, because then it becomes a situation of the winner being down to the writer's bias. Whoever the writer wants to win is going to win, regardless of how ridiculous it seems.<br /> <br /> I'm basing my argument on a more realistic outcome, based on previously demonstrated character feats.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T00:18:44-07:00","id":1562108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562104#post1562104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm basing my argument on a more realistic outcome, based on previously demonstrated character feats.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're basing your arguments on whatever you want to justify diminishing others.<br /> <br /> Batman is only supposed to be a character in a story. &quot;Human&quot; characters whose abilities are actually beyond reasonable are an old thing. It is a story. It's not supposed to be real.<br /> <br /> And I'll say real, because the very concept of realism is not what most people think it is. It's about being convincing, appearing feasible in reality, which actually relies on expectation. A lot of &quot;realistic&quot; fiction is just a ludicrous bunch of bullshit that matches people's expectations. Similarly there are &quot;unrealistic&quot; depictions that are actually closer to reality.<br /> <br /> So unless the Myth Busters found out that it's possible to deflect bullets with magic bracers and accelerate from 0 to Mach 10 without the body being turned to mulch, Batman is not required to follow real physics or to have them approve his antics. He's what a top human is in the DC universe, where he's far from the only ridiculously effective at that.<br /> <br /> Your answer to what going evil means also just evades what I said. More words, and still says nothing of what the character would actually wants. Prep time is relative, technically already he had time to prep against everyone he knows about. He's the ultimate planner in a universe where this goes to bizarre extremes, so what?<br /> <br /> The writer doesn't have bias. They're an author. Anyone they want wins because everything in the fiction is defined by them. There's no hero without a writer in the Justice League. And the story isn't about being &quot;realistic&quot;, it's about being enjoyable.<br /> <br /> We just go back to the start: you're not being realistic or smart or mature or anything of the sort. You're just building justification to pretend superiority at people for liking something you disapprove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T00:19:06-07:00","id":1562109,"title":"","content":"I don't watch them anymore Montparnasse, but I do like when other channels are calling them out. Also I do like the drama when their predictions completely fall apart such as Odyssey being a big success so far.<br /> <br /> They don't want to take a loss at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-24-2026, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T00:35:47-07:00","id":1562110,"title":"","content":"I'd hardly call Batman a normal person DarkKing when he is in a universe with gods, aliens, superhumans, magic, psionic and other strange things. I don't mind him with the JLA but I prefer him operating in Gotham city as a dark mysterious figure as I like that element of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T00:47:10-07:00","id":1562112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562108#post1562108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We just go back to the start: you're not being realistic or smart or mature or anything of the sort. You're just building justification to pretend superiority at people for liking something you disapprove.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the hell are you talking about?<br /> <br /> I was responding to comments from previous posters about how the character's fandom likes to over exaggerate said character's chances of victory. I was not pretending superiority over anyone.<br /> <br /> As for all that other stuff you were saying, it came across as a bunch of random nonsense to me.<br /> <br /> Yes, I'm fully aware the characters are fictional, and subject to the writer's creativity. That is NOT what we were discussing. We were discussing whether or not Batman's contingency plans would prove effective in practice.<br /> <br /> To which I was trying to point out that said plans only work if the person he's trying to bring down is restraining themselves. Because a fully unrestrained opponent is a far different challenge he has to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 07-24-2026, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T00:53:23-07:00","id":1562113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562110#post1562110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd hardly call Batman a normal person DarkKing when he is in a universe with gods, aliens, superhumans, magic, psionic and other strange things. I don't mind him with the JLA but I prefer him operating in Gotham city as a dark mysterious figure as I like that element of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>His super power is being rich!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T02:04:24-07:00","id":1562114,"title":"","content":"DarkKing, the problem with your whole thing on Batman is that you can't analyze Batman's contingency plans &quot;realistically,&quot; because Batman isn't realistically possible. While it's true that he's not supposed to have overt superpowers, it's also undeniable that he's supposed to be beyond human in how much he can be good at at the same time. Nobody in reality could do everything Batman does. Even if they had the physical and mental potential combined with the access to obscene wealth... there's literally not enough time in the day. He might not be beyond human in an specific endeavor, but he's far, far beyond human in the number of things he's reached and maintains the pinnacle of human aptitude at.<br /> <br /> So how can you fairly state what the appropriate level of planning he's capable of? What's too extreme for a man that can balance being a CEO, a physical workout routine that would require ~15 hrs a day to maintain, a vigilante, a tutor to younger vigilantes, a member of a superhero team, and keep himself up to date on dozens of scientific fields related to forensics and psychology? <br /> <br /> He's also canonically stated that the Justice League is his primary contingency plan against both himself and any other hero that goes bad. He doesn't plan on soloing Superman as plans A to T or so (though he has managed to solo Supes at least once...), his initial plans are for the entire rest of the league to help him. Again, official stories have made it explicit that a lot of his plans are meant fail if the Justice League works together because Bruce is just as worried about going bad and wants to lose if that happens as the Justice League is unified against him.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's some fans overstating things... but it's hard to say they're any significant group when Batman having extremely complex planning skills is canonically part of his skill set; and we've seen him pull of some seemingly absolutely insane plans in the official material successfully. If fans are just taking a version of Batman that can pull the kinds of plans they're talking about, at worst their cherry picking which Batman they like... but so is anyone that picks a Batman that's not that good at planning and nobody is actually right or wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T03:39:59-07:00","id":1562117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562113#post1562113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His super power is being rich!</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to check out Absolute Batman as he comes from a blue collar background in this alternate universe that is infused with Darkseid's evil. Also in this alternate universe his mother survived and his future rogues gallery are childhood friends of his with the exception of the Joker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-24-2026, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T03:59:40-07:00","id":1562118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562117#post1562117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need to check out Absolute Batman as he comes from a blue collar background in this alternate universe that is infused with Darkseid evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolute is quite interesting, although it's also a very different take on everything and everyone.<br /> <br /> For wealth as superpower, that's literally Catman, who's been both villain and hero and is little known outside some obscure comics. His whole thing is being what Wayne and Queen are accused of, played straight to show what it is like.<br /> <br /> Batman in the Justice League is a superlative planner because of course he is. What else would he do there if he weren't? The whole point is to have all the most popular DC heroes, so having Batman is nonnegotiable, and having him just to be useless wouldn't do much for an entertaining story. He has to be able to deceive Dark Seid, so he will be.<br /> <br /> Want to read less over-the-top Batman? Most of the time his own series go in this direction, give or take crossover shenanigans. Still quite super, but there organized crime is supposed to be a challenge and criminals with powers are unbeatable in direct confrontation. Lately I'm really enjoying Wayne Family Adventures, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T07:47:17-07:00","id":1562125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562117#post1562117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need to check out Absolute Batman as he comes from a blue collar background in this alternate universe that is infused with Darkseid's evil. Also in this alternate universe his mother survived and his future rogues gallery are childhood friends of his with the exception of the Joker.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's also built like a Space Marine, and wields a giant battle axe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T08:21:09-07:00","id":1562127,"title":"","content":"FUCK!<br /> <br /> Paizo has decided to terminate their official partnership with Archives of Nethys.<br /> <br /> I don't know how this is going to affect their website, but I'm very worried about the potential of losing access to a free, easy guide to gameplay mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T10:38:39-07:00","id":1562129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562125#post1562125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> He's also built like a Space Marine, and wields a giant battle axe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That size didn't help him at the building site when the Joker physically manhandled pretty easily. But then the Joker is something beyond human in 