;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T04:14:51-07:00","id":1562340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562310#post1562310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm somewhat disappointed that when Space Ice did his They Live esipode that the antisemitic people came onto the message boards. I hope that Space Ice will delete those posts soon or it will be tough to watch future roasts from him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'm not familiar with Space Ice. I'll have to look into em..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T11:42:00-07:00","id":1562344,"title":"","content":"The thing is that Space Ice is a roast channel and not a political one. So I shouldn't be surprised that when he did They Live the other day that antisemitic people would show up in the posts and say what people that aliens represent.<br /> <br /> They don't care that John Carpenter was explicit that the film was a critic on mindless consumerism, Reaganomics and yuppies and that the aliens were meant to embody them.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that Space Ice will delete those posts, but he might be busy working on his next show to roast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T17:13:21-07:00","id":1562359,"title":"","content":"I know that going in that Christopher Nolan Odsesey would be subjected to bad takes. But now some folks are complaining about Ulysses is showing signs of PTSD in the film.<br /> <br /> Imagine being upset about acknowledging about how soliders or survivors of disasters being traumatized by such things.<br /> <br /> I can definitely see after a decade of warfare at Troy that Ulysses not being the same person he was at the start seeing friends and colleagues dying or suffering brutal injuries and wondering afterwards if this was worth it.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that we are seeing greater awareness about PTSD in popular media. <br /> <br /> We saw it Made Max Fury Road where Max is mentally worse then he was after what ever events happened since Thunderdome.<br /> <br /> In the original Michael Bay Transformers film we see that Prime is more troubled after countless eons of warfare and in fact in IDW they had the Autobots and Decepticons enter a tense ceasefire and how both sides have trouble going back to their old lives and we see it now that Image comics is following that story beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T22:38:05-07:00","id":1562404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562359#post1562359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the original Michael Bay Transformers film we see that Prime is more troubled after countless eons of warfare and in fact in IDW they had the Autobots and Decepticons enter a tense ceasefire and how both sides have trouble going back to their old lives and we see it now that Image comics is following that story beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've been fighting each other for 10's of millions of years. Do they even have old lives to go back to anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T22:47:35-07:00","id":1562407,"title":"","content":"That's the thing DarkKing was that members of both sides lament of what the conflict turned them into and how they missed there old lives and feared what kind of future lives they could make at the end of the war with so much bad blood between both sides.<br /> <br /> The writers were conveying of how nobody in war never really wins. Even Megatron at this point has seen how far he had fallen from what his original goals were and felt shame.<br /> <br /> I should stress this was when IDW held the publishing rights to Transformers and wanted to move the story forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-01-2026, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T01:00:11-07:00","id":1562421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562407#post1562407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing DarkKing was that members of both sides lament of what the conflict turned them into and how they missed there old lives and feared what kind of future lives they could make at the end of the war with so much bad blood between both sides.<br /> <br /> The writers were conveying of how nobody in war never really wins. Even Megatron at this point has seen how far he had fallen from what his original goals were and felt shame.<br /> <br /> I should stress this was when IDW held the publishing rights to Transformers and wanted to move the story forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their old lives were a caste system, where your form dictated your function. It's kind of the whole reason for why Megatron and the other Decepticons rebelled in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> Megatron and Soundwave were forced to compete in gladiator matches for the entertainment of Cybertron's nobility. They have literally never known a life that did not revolve around combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Shockwave had his emotions surgically removed, so that he could approach the world through pure, cold, scientific logic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Optimus was just a lowly clerk / scribe, not the great leader of Cybertron we know him as today.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T08:49:28-07:00","id":1562428,"title":"","content":"That's not a matter of justification, and war is not the same as any combat.<br /> <br /> However you feel about the rightness of a cause won't change how traumatic war is, and the toll it takes from the participants.<br /> <br /> And for what it's worth, irl gladiators didn't fight to the death or anything like that through most of history, only when they were criminals slated for execution.<br /> <br /> War is horrific. It can be more or less horrific, but it always is. Most combatants in it are scarred for life, PTSD being the most common consequence (others are possible).<br /> <br /> So the thought of the past as a desirable state is common, even if this past isn't good. It's not necessarily wanting to go back to the previous state of affairs, but to your previous, healthier self. It has nothing to do with regret, either, but with emotional longing.<br /> <br /> Frequently combatants feel their role not as a fight for betterment of one's own state, but as a sacrifice. What they lost to the war is bigger than what they stand to gain for themselves, if anything they feel justified by future benefits to others. Again not universal, but extremely common.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is only a layer and things are far more complex in reality, but point in case this is both a valid aspect to explore in a story and a realistic one for lots of people who went to war or lived it at home.<br /> <br /> If the Transformers had a previous life you find worth of living, if what they long for is even real or romanticized memories, and if this is true to the original Odyssey, those are utterly irrelevant questions. Don't like it, don't watch it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T11:04:00-07:00","id":1562434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562428#post1562428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for what it's worth, irl gladiators didn't fight to the death or anything like that through most of history, only when they were criminals slated for execution.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>According to the show &quot;Adam Ruins Everything&quot; actual gladiator matches were more like sporting events. This is because training, outfitting and healing a gladiator was expensive, and if they were constantly killing each other, you'd just be wasting money.<br /> <br /> <b>Slightly related fun fact:</b> Soundwave was the only gladiator who actually came close to defeating Megatron in the arena. Which is probably why he's also the only Decepticon that Megatron treats like an equal, instead of a subordinate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T14:10:25-07:00","id":1562441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562434#post1562434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the show &quot;Adam Ruins Everything&quot; actual gladiator matches were more like sporting events. This is because training, outfitting and healing a gladiator was expensive, and if they were constantly killing each other, you'd just be wasting money.</div> </div> </div> </div>A little more complicated, but in essence, yes.<br /> <br /> The games started as a ritual to the god of death during the early Roman Kingdom. Once a year, only a few matches, and the participants were untrained sacrifices, preferably criminals.<br /> <br /> With time the games gained certain popularity and evolved into the sport. I think saying it was just because they were expensive a bit unfair, Romans weren't really into killing people for the lulz, even slaves.<br /> <br /> But they gained more and more safety as time passed and that was certainly because trainers wanted to preserve the investment. Fighters in the arena would also make a lot of money from fans, so despite being socially despised there was a number of free men who joined.<br /> <br /> Overall was as safe as a fighting sport could be at the time, most would live to retire (but retire young and hurt, that's for sure) and the famous judgment by the Emperor thing was about a prize, not condemning anyone. It still existed as an execution and ritual, though, so battles to the death existed.<br /> <br /> Not everything was nice all the time, and the rebellion of Spartacus was real (though not like depicted in media), but for most of the existence of the Roman Empire they were the second most popular athletes, all things considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T09:05:26-07:00","id":1562491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562233#post1562233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't believe that Sargon of Akkad is still around on YouTube and making bad takes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fucking Carlgon is still around in real life as well. He recently crawled out of his hole to become a regional organiser for Restore Britain, the party for people too right-wing to be happy in Reform.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T12:18:46-07:00","id":1562499,"title":"","content":"I heard that Istar and that it didn't work out well for him. Who would have guessed that being a bigot would hurt your chances in politics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-03-2026, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T14:31:30-07:00","id":1562504,"title":"","content":"Eh, hope that stays true, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Reform UK and Restore Britain are growing. The far right keeps solidifying positions across most of the world, and their voters actually like bigotry.<br /> <br /> The old guard of the left is really not going well overall, the new guard has little financing, and the more centrist parties are increasingly failing the current challenges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T15:34:22-07:00","id":1562512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562504#post1562504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, hope that stays true, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Reform UK and Restore Britain are growing. The far right keeps solidifying positions across most of the world, and their voters actually like bigotry.<br /> <br /> The old guard of the left is really not going well overall, the new guard has little financing, and the more centrist parties are increasingly failing the current challenges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they don't like being stabbed and raped in broad daylight, or having police show up on their doorstep within the hour of posting something the government doesn't like on the internet?<br /> <br /> The UK is turning into a lawless hellscape, where criminals go unpunished, and people are being stripped of their right to speak out.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> There's even videos posted by UK tourists who came to America and are utterly bewildered at how safe and trusting our society is compared to their home countries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T17:39:36-07:00","id":1562522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562512#post1562512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The UK is turning into a lawless hellscape, where criminals go unpunished, and people are being stripped of their right to speak out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure...<br /> <br /> But just to be clear: there's no right to speak out in the UK. It never existed there. Ever. It's one of the reasons why your flimsy constitution has a right to Free Speech among the first batch of amendments, as a reaction to England's control over speech.<br /> <br /> They don't have a constitution and they don't have any law where free speech is in any way, shape or form even partially protected.<br /> <br /> Its protection, when it exists, is exclusively through common sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T20:51:08-07:00","id":1562526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562512#post1562512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The UK is turning into a lawless hellscape, where criminals go unpunished, and people are being stripped of their right to speak out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um.. based on what? Every attempt to study this has show that, on average the UK has seen a steady decline in all forms of crimes over the past 40 years. They might not punish individual criminals as harshly as the US... but the US is a huge outlier in how punishing our punishment systems are, and how little we invest in rehabilitation and reintegration post punishments to help keep recidivism rates low. The UK's approach to these things is extremely normal by peer-nation standards.<br /> <br /> Here's a very simple thing to consider on whether or not this is a matter of reality or perception:<br /> <br /> The majority of Western European countries, and the USA all simultaneous think crime is on the rise in their countries (despite there not being evidence to back that up), and also think it's just them and other countries are safer.<br /> <br /> This doesn't make any sense. Someone from the UK that takes a holiday to France says France is much safer than the UK... while the French are saying that crimes the worst its been in years, and the data says both countries are basically on par with each other while both are all trending down in crime rates.<br /> <br /> If everyone was having a spike in crime, people that travel wouldn't be constantly amazed at how safe other places.<br /> <br /> The most likely explanation is that you get flooded with negative information about where you live because most people aren't closely following what's happening in other countries. However you get your news and whatnot, it's going to focus on topics that most affect you and that means local stuff. The media also tends to have a negativity bias because bad news generates more interested than good news.<br /> <br /> A more neutral example than violent crimes: The UK is having a big discourse about how &quot;ebikes&quot; are actually a bad thing somehow. One of the biggest problems? The major news outlets call everything with two wheels and a battery an ebike. That means a normal bicycle with a small electric motor to help with local commuting is being lumped in with battery powered motorcycles. It doesn't matter that UK law has clear demarcations between different types of vehicles and most of the problems are electric motorcycles being driven like they're bicycles despite that already being illegal... all battery powered bikes are getting bad press.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's even videos posted by UK tourists who came to America and are utterly bewildered at how safe and trusting our society is compared to their home countries. </div> </div> </div>And the vast majority of it is grifter-influencer nonsense. Countries (not just the US) have tourism sectors. Companies want tourists to come to their country. They sponsor influencers (and the countries themselves frequently chip in too) to make positive content about the country or a specific area without directly talking about the hotel brand or whatever. This is painfully obvious when you can find Instagram or TikTok accounts where people basically do the exact same, &quot;Wow, X country/city is so much better than they tell you in the news,&quot; every 3ish years and don't even feel the need to scrub their old videos that show them reacting as if it was all new to them the last few times they did it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562522#post1562522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But just to be clear: there's no right to speak out in the UK. <br /> ...<br /> Its protection, when it exists, is exclusively through common sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't true. The UK speech protections are a matter of statue instead of constitutional right, but that doesn't mean those protections don't exist and the government there gets to treat them as &quot;guidelines&quot; or some such. The UK government certainly has more power than the US government to censor speech because of how the acts establishing the right are framed, but the US courts have also managed to find ways to create exceptions to the 1st Amendment to the point where they're practically the same core balance of freedom of expression and public interest in people not actually being able to say whatever they want, whenever they want, however they want, without legal repercussions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T21:26:06-07:00","id":1562527,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I'm confused, are you trying to insult the USA, or praise it?<br /> <br /> Because, you called our constitution <i>&quot;flimsy&quot;</i> but then went on a rant about how other countries don't have one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562526#post1562526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um.. based on what? Every attempt to study this has show that, on average the UK has seen a steady decline in all forms of crimes over the past 40 years. They might not punish individual criminals as harshly as the US... but the US is a huge outlier in how punishing our punishment systems are, and how little we invest in rehabilitation and reintegration post punishments to help keep recidivism rates low. The UK's approach to these things is extremely normal by peer-nation standards.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Based on crime analytics, and how there has been reports that a shockingly high number of repeat offenders are just being released onto the streets. Despite having a rap sheet that by all rights deserves at least a life sentence, if not the death penalty.<br /> <br /> So maybe you'd be so kind as to tell me why there is a meme going around, claiming that the traditional greeting in London involves multiple stab wounds?<br /> <br /> <br /> Or how a man in the UK died, after being stabbed by an immigrant; and when the cops arrived on scene, they did not believe that the attacker was the aggressor in the situation, because his victim was white. Straight up telling the man as he was bleeding out, that they didn't believe his story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------<br /> <br /> As for those grifters, the pay out must be quite hefty indeed, for them to fly all the way to another country and record themselves on the internet talking about how bad their homeland is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T23:17:34-07:00","id":1562529,"title":"","content":"It doesn't have to be money for social media grifters DarKing as they sell outrage, hate and fear and use cherry picked narratives to back their claims and even in the past mainstream media would be very selective in how they reported stories to push a narrative.<br /> <br /> Ranting For Vengeance hates black people with a passion and he is from Ireland and the total number of black people who live there make up a grand total of 1% of the total population and I strongly doubt he has ever seen one in person and gets his stuff from far right news and white nationalist groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T23:32:02-07:00","id":1562531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562527#post1562527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, you called our constitution <i>&quot;flimsy&quot;</i> but then went on a rant about how other countries don't have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to answer for someone else, but you are aware that you can be critical of two different systems because both are seriously flawed, just in different ways?<br /> <br /> The US constitution is pretty damned flimsy because what it actually says doesn't matter, what 5+/9 unelected lifetime appointees with no oversight say it says is what the law actually is.<br /> <br /> Countries without constitutions, or their constitutions serve a very different purpose than the US one does, can have all sorts of issues because rights can be stripped as easily as they can be granted without a robust system to prevent capricious government actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Based on crime analytics, and how there has been reports that a shockingly high number of repeat offenders are just being released onto the streets. </div> </div> </div>Have you looked into the issues around this at all?<br /> <br /> First, as I mentioned with the ebikes thing? The UK popular discourse has been pushed away from the difference between repeat offenders (that is people that serve their time, and then once free of restrictions go back to committing crime) and recalled offenders (which is the UK version of having your parole revoked).<br /> <br /> Second, the UK tried to get tough on crime... and now their prisons are full... and unlike the US they take the laws around prison facilities seriously so they don't just pack dozens of people into rooms designed for five. They started over-policing because the public felt (again, not really backed up by data) like certain crimes were on the rise, and that filled the prisons with minor offenders, and thus a strain on the system resulting in trying to get as many people out of prison as fast as possible.<br /> <br /> Third, the UK legal standards around life sentences and capital punishment are much higher bars than the US, which means most criminals will eventually get out... and reintegration services are always something that gets slashed what budgets get tight because spending money on those ex-convicts is &quot;dirty&quot; despite that money being the best way to keep them from going back to crime (public services getting cut also tends to be popular and... also leads to more crime for predictable reasons). Even so, recidivism rates in the UK are still half of what they are in the US.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite having a rap sheet that by all rights deserves at least a life sentence, if not the death penalty. </div> </div> </div>According to who? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So maybe you'd be so kind as to tell me why there is a meme going around, claiming that the traditional greeting in London involves multiple stab wounds? </div> </div> </div>Racism and classism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or how a man in the UK died, after being stabbed by an immigrant; and when the cops arrived on scene, they did not believe that the attacker was the aggressor in the situation, because his victim was white. Straight up telling the man as he was bleeding out, that they didn't believe his story. </div> </div> </div>If you're talking about Henry Nowak.. that's a hell of a lot of believing biased spin in the phrasing there. His killer wasn't an immigrant, the police never referenced people's races even if they clearly didn't believe Nowak at first, and the police started to provide first aid over the killer's objection to Nowak saying he'd been stabbed and it was clear then that the wounds were fatal even if they'd rushed him too surgery ASAP. But yeah, the police aren't your friends, and they screw up even when they don't have malicious intent. They guy that killed him got a life sentence (and his mother picked up a charge for trying to hide the knife) and multiple police officers on the scene have faced some level of repercussions even if none of them criminal. <br /> <br /> Of course, this doesn't actually change anything in the broader picture. Like most fear mongering people in power pick a single event and try to turn it into a wave of bad things happening; even if hordes of evidence points to a very different truth. One provocative case gets people upset, while reams of data mean nothing to them. Hence my above comment about racism and classism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for those grifters, the pay out must be quite hefty indeed, for them to fly all the way to another country and record themselves on the internet talking about how bad their homeland is. </div> </div> </div>The payout might not be life changing, but it's good enough a lot of people make good money off it. And who doesn't have bad shit to say about their country? If I could get $4K to go on a vacation, record it, get VIP/backstage passes/etc. perks, and all I have to do is talk shit about the US? Sign me up. I talk shit bout my country all the time because there's plenty about it to talk shit about... getting paid for it would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T00:12:15-07:00","id":1562535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562526#post1562526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't true. The UK speech protections are a matter of statue instead of constitutional right, but that doesn't mean those protections don't exist and the government there gets to treat them as &quot;guidelines&quot; or some such. The UK government certainly has more power than the US government to censor speech because of how the acts establishing the right are framed, but the US courts have also managed to find ways to create exceptions to the 1st Amendment to the point where they're practically the same core balance of freedom of expression and public interest in people not actually being able to say whatever they want, whenever they want, however they want, without legal repercussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad in overstating it, I forgot the 1998 Human Rights Act.<br /> <br /> But still not everything you said is strictly true. There are a few key differences that matter a lot, and the limitations are not as balanced, even if their relevance kinda is, but also nuanced.<br /> <br /> First difference is that while frequently used interchangeably, Freedom of Speech (protected in the US) and Freedom of Expression (as stated in the Universal Declaration of Human Rights) have two key distinctions. One in that Expression covers all forms of communication, but the other that it protects the idea itself, not the specific words used, while Speech refers more directly to the words.<br /> <br /> This is important because that's the origin of the US idea that you can say anything, and how hard it is to pass legislation or rulings limiting it in several situations. I know this is not really a legal problem, but is an actual political problem.<br /> <br /> But other things differ. The Human Rights Act of 1998 in the UK has Freedom of Expression defined in article 10 with far more clear space for limitations than the US 1st amendment. The UK further passed several laws to define limits to it that are generally more clear, and as such more actionable, than in the US.<br /> <br /> And finally you have the system of Common Law that's the whole of it in the UK, where not only can laws be more freely reinterpreted, but also customs and practices have legal weight without need for formalization.<br /> <br /> So all together it's a way weaker protection than in the US when it comes to speech itself, and that specially hurts people trying to emulate the US far right (a thing that's happening the world around). Most in the UK weren't ever primed to the notion of &quot;right to say whatever&quot; as happened in the US, so UK citizens are naturally more careful with how they say things.<br /> <br /> Yeah, though, I really got carried and said very much bullshit when I said &quot;no way, shape or form&quot;. But still I stand that calling what they have Freedom of Speech is too imprecise to be considered correct.<br /> <br /> Oh, and about tourists: it's also likely that most have the impression of being safer because the areas where tourists usually travel are safer than average for the city, partially because a lot of people work to make them so, and criminals of more serious type avoid them, it's bad business.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562527#post1562527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I'm confused, are you trying to insult the USA, or praise it?<br /> <br /> Because, you called our constitution <i>&quot;flimsy&quot;</i> but then went on a rant about how other countries don't have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither, I was stating three facts that you didn't understood.<br /> <br /> 1. The US constitution is weak. <i>Extremely</i> so. This is not about the country in general, its people or its history. It kinda is about its government but in a very complicated manner.<br /> <br /> I don't deny the historical importance of the US constitution. It was one of the first (first or second depends on how you count those things), and extraordinary for its time and the circumstances. The document everyone built upon in the following centuries.<br /> <br /> But the problem of being a pioneer is that, well, everyone built upon. For the last centuries almost all other nations developed constitutions, most more than once. Ideas got to circle around, new structures and systems tried and tested, exchange was constant since constitutions are public documents. It became an art and a science that was repeatedly improved upon.<br /> <br /> So today the US has what's arguably the weakest constitution in the world. Not the weakest government or legal system, but the weakest constitution. It's enormously outdated. It belongs in a museum, especially for being so historically important, but not in a court of law or as a guide for legislation.<br /> <br /> 2. I tried to show a historical link. The reason the US constitution, which was built by former UK nationals who rebelled against the crown and faced the full force of the UK legal system because of that, has Free Speech as the First Amendment is a reaction to having their ideas persecuted by the UK with full legal support.<br /> <br /> My main point was the lack of legal support for free speech in the UK, which isn't new, so they aren't really losing all that.<br /> <br /> 3. The other fact is that the UK has no constitution. As in, you were talking about the UK, remember? You said they're losing their right to free speech, remember? I'm saying they never had one the way you think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562527#post1562527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on crime analytics, and how there has been reports that a shockingly high number of repeat offenders are just being released onto the streets. Despite having a rap sheet that by all rights deserves at least a life sentence, if not the death penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just went through the UK crime rate statistics for the last 13 years and there's no significant increase in crime rates.<br /> <br /> Also no news of their rules for release changing. The UK releases people from prison when their term is due, like everyone else.<br /> <br /> No sign of any of those having &quot;a rap sheet that by all rights deserves at least a life sentence&quot;. Also, the UK doesn't have death penalty, so saying that is bizarre.<br /> <br /> They also have lower recidivism than the US and the lowest is among those who receive community service style sentences rather than prison.<br /> <br /> So I'll ask you to show your sources and cases, so we can examine properly, since you're the one making bold claims and I couldn't find any confirmation myself. Otherwise I'll have to conclude you're severely misguided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562527#post1562527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So maybe you'd be so kind as to tell me why there is a meme going around, claiming that the traditional greeting in London involves multiple stab wounds?</div> </div> </div> </div>First because it's a meme, memes aren't proof of violence trends, they're proof that someone thinks something and others find it fun. By the way, most such memes are created and spread by US citizens, not British.<br /> <br /> Second because in a safe country any violent crime gets extra attention, and when gun crimes are almost unheard of you don't have a lot of other options.<br /> <br /> Third, and this is really a problem they're facing, there's currently an uptick in knife violence among British minors related to gang fights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562527#post1562527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or how a man in the UK died, after being stabbed by an immigrant; and when the cops arrived on scene, they did not believe that the attacker was the aggressor in the situation, because his victim was white. Straight up telling the man as he was bleeding out, that they didn't believe his story.</div> </div> </div> </div>The murder of Henry Nowak by Vickrum Singh Digwa. Tell me about anecdotal evidence.<br /> <br /> So, this was one case. Not a trend. One. Not one that year. One.<br /> <br /> Protests ensued and a lot was done, the officers faced repercussions, revisions were called on the police system, and Digwa got life sentence, with minimum 21 years before being able to ask for parole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562527#post1562527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for those grifters, the pay out must be quite hefty indeed, for them to fly all the way to another country and record themselves on the internet talking about how bad their homeland is.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Do you seriously don't know how tourism marketing works?<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, they're well paid. Not sure if a hefty sum, but enough to be worthy their time.<br /> <br /> Also... Most people see this as an opportunity to travel, not a terrible chore for having to do it.<br /> <br /> There's always people who'll happily talk bad about their homeland for any pay, it's not like the ones paying are looking to convert staunch nationalists or anything. And that talking lies, if the bad things are real? I'm with Heavy Arms, I'll talk happily about the problems in Brazil for free, imagine being paid.<br /> <br /> Seriously, what do you think they're losing for accepting to make a few days, one week tops trip? That they'll still use to produce high value content? Because anywhere in the world a local traveling abroad is high value content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 08-03-2026, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T01:23:28-07:00","id":1562538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562531#post1562531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Countries without constitutions, or their constitutions serve a very different purpose than the US one does, can have all sorts of issues because rights can be stripped as easily as they can be granted without a robust system to prevent capricious government actions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Speaking of which:</b> back during the cold war era, the government passed a law that allows them to revoke the citizenship and deport anyone in the country who is confirmed to have become a communist within 5 years of immigrating to the US.<br /> <br /> And this law was never overturned. It still exists to this day, but people just forgot about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562531#post1562531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second, the UK tried to get tough on crime... and now their prisons are full...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that doesn't mean let them out; it means the country has an over abundance of crime it needs to deal with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562531#post1562531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Third, the UK legal standards around life sentences and capital punishment are much higher bars than the US, which means most criminals will eventually get out... and reintegration services are always something that gets slashed what budgets get tight because spending money on those ex-convicts is &quot;dirty&quot; despite that money being the best way to keep them from going back to crime (public services getting cut also tends to be popular and... also leads to more crime for predictable reasons). Even so, recidivism rates in the UK are still half of what they are in the US.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, believe me, I'm aware that our 'rehabilitation' system is practically designed to fail.<br /> <br /> I don't remember which black comedian it was, but they addressed this point by telling a story about how even after serving time, the outside world still treated them like a constant threat. They then asked the question of <i>&quot;If you're going to keep punishing me, then what was the point of me going to prison?&quot;</i>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T01:27:41-07:00","id":1562539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562529#post1562529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't have to be money for social media grifters DarKing as they sell outrage, hate and fear and use cherry picked narratives to back their claims and even in the past mainstream media would be very selective in how they reported stories to push a narrative.<br /> <br /> Ranting For Vengeance hates black people with a passion and he is from Ireland and the total number of black people who live there make up a grand total of 1% of the total population and I strongly doubt he has ever seen one in person and gets his stuff from far right news and white nationalist groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never even heard of the guy.<br /> <br /> But now you've put the mental imagery of black people speaking with an Irish accent in my mind, and this amuses me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T03:17:19-07:00","id":1562544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562538#post1562538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this law was never overturned. It still exists to this day, but people just forgot about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were a number of laws of this nature passed. Multiples were ruled unconstitutional by the federal courts (including a few Supreme Court cases). While yes, some of them have never been formally overturned, that's only because the US legal system allows for zombie laws that are clearly unconstitutional and would be overturned if a case ever got in front of a judge, but nobody gets charged under them and the Congress has no incentive to spend time on getting rid of them... and that's all of the methods of getting rid of them.<br /> <br /> Sure they're forgotten if people even learned about them in the first place, but that's because they're irrelevant to actual policy enforcement. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, that doesn't mean let them out; it means the country has an over abundance of crime it needs to deal with. </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't indicate an uptick in crime, it means sentences got longer (or crimes without prison time were upgraded to having some) and they didn't have the infrastructure to keep up with the resulting increased population of incarcerated people. The math here is not hard. If you increase how long people spend in prison signficantly, the amount of crime stays the same - or even goes down slightly, and don't build more prison beds... you run out of space.<br /> <br /> Why are you insisting there's some increase of crime in the UK? Do you have any specific dataset to point to on this? Everything you're bringing up has completely different reasons than what you're asserting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, believe me, I'm aware that our 'rehabilitation' system is practically designed to fail. </div> </div> </div>Then why are you struggling with the idea that the UK has dipped its toe into going in the same direction and it's not going well for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avata