orts? You know. Credible sources. Not some social media clout ladder climber that only wants to post provocative material for clicks.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you're never going to provide enough proof I should watch anything Nux did, because nobody should give him a single click. That doesn't mean you can't try real sources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Please stop</i> pestering me with this, because I have neither the interest, nor the energy to get into a political argument with a brick wall. </div> </div> </div>Apologize for promoting a sexual predator as a credible source and I'll consider it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>MOVING. ON. TO. NEW. TOPIC.</b> </div> </div> </div>Didn't work last time, not going to work this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T15:36:07-07:00","id":1562586,"title":"","content":"I knew that name sounded familiar and I remember him just being a troll who likes to manipulate content to make things look worse and I question criminal stats as numbers can be manipulated and how many of those cases got dropped from lack of proof or overturned by bad investigating.<br /> <br /> You need to take what social media channels with a grain of salt as many have been caught making things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-04-2026, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T15:40:42-07:00","id":1562587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562578#post1562578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's not enough proof for you, then nothing I can provide for you will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proof for you is a single guy making videos where he has total control over edition, no links to the sources, just because he shows stuff?<br /> <br /> Have you ever tried to see people with other opinion to compare, so you can have a reference?<br /> <br /> By what Heavy Arms said he actually knows who the Vtuber in question is, so... He seems to know your &quot;evidence&quot; and not be convinced.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, you're right. If this is the best evidence you can provide, against all the other data sources publicly available and the reports of actual British people actually living in the UK, I guess you indeed can't provide anything that could convince someone who doesn't already agree with you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562578#post1562578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>MOVING. ON. TO. NEW. TOPIC.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>No, no.<br /> <br /> You're the one making claims and stuff. It's on you to show your sources, and even if they're a really bad thing you can be way clearer about them, like giving more than once single name.<br /> <br /> We have a right to ask for that. We also have a right to remain in topic anyway.<br /> <br /> I am really curious to know about your sources, really am. I like to know new stuff and I like to learn the influences that get people to think what they think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T16:18:13-07:00","id":1562591,"title":"","content":"Among my hobbies, I like drawing, and am trying to get better at painting. Regrettably, at present, that's also complicated because, as you'll discover if you scroll back through this thread, my Kamvas is currently bricked because the hardware business can't just be about serving up hardware; it also has to be about making money off of people, such as by putting in a useless USB hub on top of a tablet monitor that's hooked up to my tower PC (which has more USB slots than I know what to do with) so that it causes an eventual circuit problem that bricks the tablet's pen.<br /> <br /> DarkKing, the people you're listening to in the chud-o-sphere of Vtubers are about the same, only with less utility, because at least this less than optimum Huion product managed to last as a tablet for four years and still works as a monitor. Whatever rush you get from watching them, it's like a really skeevy wrestling circuit where they encourage people to play off of kayfabe at every waking hour. Instead of just sharing creative or other pursuits with people, they're getting money off of the outrage that they're stirring up in you, and they've managed to set up a positive feedback loop so that you'll keep digging in and going further in on this. All the hatred and doomposting they do is entirely to get them clicks; it has no connection to reality, any more than the most ridiculous and shocking claims in less virtual conservative spheres, like when Candace Owens did tranvestigation BS against the first lady of France (and any transvestigation shit to begin with, just to be clear).<br /> <br /> So consider dropping some of the media you're consuming and taking on a slower-paced hobby. I'd obviously endorse drawing and inking or, say, going through a novel series. Download Blender and sculpt minis with it. Get those spoons back and put them into a different pursuit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T20:29:05-07:00","id":1562609,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> I don't understand how people are able to make such great art with an electronic tablet. I can scarcely write a digital signature, without it coming out all squiggly.<br /> <br /> Tell me the secrets of your witchcraft!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T21:55:30-07:00","id":1562611,"title":"","content":"Candace Owens is still a thing? I thought after her departure from Daily Wire that she would lapse into obscurity like all the people who work there and left. Of course the Daily Wire I heard isn't doing to well either like the other outrage channels on social media.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T22:42:52-07:00","id":1562615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562611#post1562611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Candace Owens is still a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The transvestigation on France's first lady at least went big a few years ago.<br /> <br /> It's interesting that every time the right goes on one of those investigation they inevitably find out that their target was a cis woman all along.<br /> <br /> Almost as if trans people are honest and don't actually try to commit identity fraud pretending to be cisgender, ain't it?<br /> <br /> DarkKing, what your sources have to say about it? You can take the opportunity to disclose them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T23:00:11-07:00","id":1562617,"title":"","content":"That is really scraping the bottom of the barrel for content Montparnasse and even worse when such folks tried to claim that Michelle Obama was originally a man with no proof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T05:14:47-07:00","id":1562627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562617#post1562617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is really scraping the bottom of the barrel for content Montparnasse and even worse when such folks tried to claim that Michelle Obama was originally a man with no proof.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was a trend.<br /> <br /> Not so much scrapping the barrel, but trying to prove their thesis that trans people are actually a conspiracy that explain people who don't fit their gender beliefs and are trying to fraud the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T07:25:38-07:00","id":1562639,"title":"","content":"As with so many in-vogue conservative trends, it also started eating itself as transvestigators got J.K Rowling in their sights. And the people probably still won't re-think their assumptions, even though their standards will leave them forever doubting anyone that isn't ridiculously hyperfeminine or hypermasculine. Often, even people who are might get accused; this is a thing that knows neither reason nor evidentiary standards. They just babble about Baphomet and continue spinning out ridiculous &quot;occult&quot; nonsense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562609#post1562609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> I don't understand how people are able to make such great art with an electronic tablet. I can scarcely write a digital signature, without it coming out all squiggly.<br /> <br /> Tell me the secrets of your witchcraft!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as with signing my name, I started on paper with a pencil and got a few years of practice. Well, technically I got back into drawing via a Bamboo and then switched back when my new (at the time, RIP 17.1&quot; MSI) laptop decided not to play well with said Bamboo, but actually drawing things out so that you can see where your hand is veering off from your thoughts is necessary, and often requires a lot of drawings to veer off before you get the hang of it; there's a notable quote about everyone having about ten thousand bad drawings in them. No worries about the concepts; you can always revisit them. An Andrew Loomis book can also help to unravel some of this, and is back in print (if out of stock sometimes).<br /> <br /> (I also took a class on anatomy and physiology when I was an undergrad. Though, most of my study drawings there were for organs, muscles, bones and what have you, uncovered by skin and tissue bundles... which is an entire other genre of art when divorced from this context.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T08:07:10-07:00","id":1562643,"title":"","content":"Heh, &quot;people being stripped of their right to speak&quot;.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is, recent politics in the UK have actually undermined free speech in the form of their persecution of groups that advocate for Palestine and organise in protest to that effect. And these things are actually an outrage to foundational principles of an otherwise liberal democracy.<br /> <br /> But most of the people who phrase it like that are probably talking about recent laws and their enforcement that are trying to integrate justice with modern social media by making it an offence to post hate speech that promotes violent action.<br /> <br /> And the thing is, sometimes the people who get arrested or even charged with that as a crime are ultimately exonerated.<br /> <br /> Which is a thing that happens with criminal charges all the time. To a serious minded person, there's actually a legitimate point that the new legislation has kinks to work out.<br /> <br /> But the people most loudly and reductively critical of it aren't interested in approaching the subject in terms of analysis of how to effectively legislate ways to combat modern communications technology being used to create pervasive hostile environments to vulnerable demographics. They just want to promote an outrage machine of reactionary politics, the narrative that conservative and bigoted people are unduly persecuted. <br /> <br /> Hell, even in its current form it isn't legislation that would be strong enough to criminalise something like promoting an idea that certain demographics or liberal policymakers constitute an existential threat into an audience that will statistically include a percentage of socially destabilised people with low media literacy that is liable to both take it at face value and emotionally process it in a manner somewhere between contributing to harassment campaigns and going on spree murders or partaking in targeted riots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T08:25:05-07:00","id":1562644,"title":"","content":"Really, the funniest thing to me about accusations of being in an echo chamber is that reactionaries don't seem to understand how much the fact that people arguing against them know their talking points and their dog whistles means that they actually <i>are</i> going to the places where they speak to one another and observing it in detail.<br /> <br /> They start from a position of &quot;nobody who knows this information would be unconvinced by it&quot; and so double think themselves into either believing that opponents don't know the information despite all evidence to the contrary or that it's axiomatic that their opposition does not engage in good faith.<br /> <br /> Like seeing somebody say with a straight face that a compilation of Charlie Kirk saying racist and misogynistic shit constituted cherry picking without regards to the fact that the sheer number of clips must have constituted a person going through a <i>lot</i> of Charlie Kirk content without finding any of it convincing and the fact that there was a lot of stuff to find. You're not cherry picking a person if you're able to find them saying something thirty or forty times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T08:54:07-07:00","id":1562649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562556#post1562556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to explain to you where I'm getting the data for this, but I'm pretty sure that might trip some fire alarm in the moderator department.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I personally recommend <b>Nuxtaku</b>, if you have the patience to sit through his hour long videos. He actually posts clips and screencaps of evidence to support what he's talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I actually went on to at least know something about this &quot;source&quot; you recommended and even watched something from him through a view-denial app.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised. I thought he would be bad, but he is even worse than I thought. I mean, even if you set aside his grooming of at least two minors, the 16+ channel with porn and poor control for age, the early videos sharing the very things he claims to be against and the time he made a porn channel for a 14yo for money and let it run publicly for a year, his normal videos are already plenty of reason to kick him from YouTube.<br /> <br /> Click baits galore. False information all the time and it isn't even the hard to find out kind. His &quot;evidence&quot; can be traced back to context with a search and never hit any confirmation, he essentially took pieces out of context and made up a narrative dissociated from reality to an absurd degree.<br /> <br /> Oh, also doxxing other creators and then blaming &quot;mysterious impersonators&quot; is the kind of dick move I think YouTube should take seriously. And the time he interfered with an investigation potentially helping the criminal to escape, I'm surprised it isn't a crime in the US.<br /> <br /> All in all, far from something moderation here should worry about, but I agree with Heavy Arms: you should apologize for presenting this predator as a credible source. He's at every level a horrible person who's either a criminal or a regular at brushing with the bad limits of the law. But at least the sexual predator part seems quite likely to be true.<br /> <br /> What about your other sources? I'm still curious as I think they can at least be more entertaining to watch and read about. Nux Taku (I think I know where he takes the name from, and if I'm right this is offensive to that porn site) was just a big disappointment. And if any of your sources has anything positive to be said about, I will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562643#post1562643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh, &quot;people being stripped of their right to speak&quot;.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> But most of the people who phrase it like that are probably talking about recent laws and their enforcement that are trying to integrate justice with modern social media by making it an offence to post hate speech that promotes violent action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here in Brazil we did such a law several years ago. Basically two things are against the law in this regard, to promote violence or discrimination, and to humiliate or harass people through hate speech.<br /> <br /> Imitating a monkey in the stadium to refer to and humiliate a black player is, as a number of foreigners found out recently, worth jail time. It isn't much time and there are several ways to get out fast, but the lesson is usually taught, and all I have to say is that it serves them right. But to be clear, this is the far end of the law. Most people who got jailed did it in similarly disgustingly public, persistent and aggressive manner, usually disturbing the peace and all the nine yards around them.<br /> <br /> As we say, &quot;racista filho da puta aqui n\u00e3o se cria&quot;.<br /> <br /> What I hate right now its that the conservatives in our low chamber, the C\u00e2mara dos Deputados, are trying to revoke this law despite it being actually quite popular, but the crowd of &quot;free speech is my right to offend you&quot; is getting strong.<br /> <br /> Oh, I also hate how they use Free Speech as an argument to block others from arguing against them because &quot;this is curbing their rights&quot;. And we don't even have &quot;free speech&quot; here, we have Freedom of Expression enshrined in our constitution, which is the reason the above is a crime: when you call someone a racial slur you are not expressing an idea, you're just using words as a means to do harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T09:08:34-07:00","id":1562650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562644#post1562644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, the funniest thing to me about accusations of being in an echo chamber is that reactionaries don't seem to understand how much the fact that people arguing against them know their talking points and their dog whistles means that they actually <i>are</i> going to the places where they speak to one another and observing it in detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hilarious. You correctly identify the person or thing they're talking about, show you already know the whole &quot;secret&quot; they have, add a lot of information they didn't knew, give the sources for where you learned that, and they say you're &quot;deafened by ...&quot; and &quot;refuse to take a glance because ...&quot;, when you just shown that you did look, did listen and did understood, but you have other sources.<br /> <br /> By the way: &quot;you're in an echo chamber&quot;<br /> &quot;I actually saw your evidence, but also saw this, this and this, so I disagree&quot;<br /> &quot;I never saw those, but you would agree if you opened your eyes to diverse sources&quot;<br /> ... Wait, what?<br /> <br /> And as they say, I don't think Charlie Kirk should have died. But Charlie Kirk thought Charlie Kirk should have died.<br /> <br /> It's a price we pay for the right of having guns, ain't it? Or is it only true when children are killed? Asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T09:45:56-07:00","id":1562654,"title":"","content":"So they think that a woman that doesn't follow typical &quot;female&quot; interests are really trans? Why do I get the feeling that these people are terminally online and never interact with people.<br /> <br /> I learned something new everyday Montparnasse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T10:02:37-07:00","id":1562657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562654#post1562654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they think that a woman that doesn't follow typical &quot;female&quot; interests are really trans? Why do I get the feeling that these people are terminally online and never interact with people.<br /> <br /> I learned something new everyday Montparnasse.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they think woman that don't try to look like a doll are trans.<br /> <br /> First target in the trend was an athlete that was to muscular, strong and kinda square, and they wanted proof that trans women are taking cis women place in sports.<br /> <br /> Said athlete had to come publicly to explain she has a birth condition that increases testosterone production. Unnecessary exposure, since athletes are physically examined and the associations know if they're trans or not, but the representatives saying it wasn't enough.<br /> <br /> By the way: high performance athletes are all genetic anomalies to some degree. All of them, that's why they're the best and goes for both sexes.<br /> <br /> Every target was chosen by appearance in an increasing spiral of lunacy. Brigitte Macron got their attention after Trump went gloating about having a more beautiful wife. They looked at her and thought she was too ugly, tanned and rough looking to be a real woman, would be their jackpot to both get a trans infiltrator and prove Emmanuel Macron is gay.<br /> <br /> And found out she looks like a French woman at her 70s with artificial tan, probably because she's a French woman at her 70s with artificial tan, though a way less weird one than Trump's.<br /> <br /> Rinse and repeat, it's essentially that. They're otherwise ok with women having &quot;male&quot; interests as this os their basis to say those women are being victimized by trans women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T10:24:43-07:00","id":1562658,"title":"","content":"I remember when Joan &quot;Chyna&quot; Lauer first came out and people thought she was trans but steroids and a accident made her look less feminine. But she was a biological female.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T10:42:27-07:00","id":1562661,"title":"","content":"I can not put into words how infuriating and <i>exhausting</i> the increasing unwillingness of people to make a distinction between a trusted and a verifiable source is, or why that distinction matters.<br /> <br /> And everything is set up to amplify that behavior. Verifying anything gets harder and harder. Video and images are about to become completely worthless, and everything written is put behind the blurry walls of a machine that has no cognition but is made to string words together that look like an answer.<br /> <br /> You don't get news, you get vibes for clicks. You don't get source code, you get vibe code. You don't get search results, you get vibes around a keyword. If you click on one such result, you don't get an answer but vibe text that is made by a vibe machine to please the vibe search into giving it a higher vibe rank. If the vibe result actually provides a source, it doesn't exist or is vibe generated itself.<br /> <br /> At work I have to regularly defend the well over twenty years of expertise in my field against the vibes of someone who prompted an LLM and somehow feels more inclined to trust the judgement of an unconscious machine because its language is better at licking boots. They could look up and see how these things work, but it's easier to just trust the vibes of the market.<br /> <br /> I know ranting about LLMs is uncool and done to death, but I'm seriously starting to burn out on the acceleration of ignorance these things produce. And I'm not even opposed to using neural net or token transformation tech for applications where it makes sense. However, the increased effort of verification is absolute poison for people who won't even bother to verify a first level source.<br /> <br /> Ok, rant over.<br /> <br /> \u0414\u043e\u0432\u0435\u0440\u044f\u0439, \u043d\u043e \u043f\u0440\u043e\u0432\u0435\u0440\u044f\u0439","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T11:22:39-07:00","id":1562668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562661#post1562661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can not put into words how infuriating and <i>exhausting</i> the increasing unwillingness of people to make a distinction between a trusted and a verifiable source is, or why that distinction matters.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I know ranting about LLMs is uncool and done to death, but I'm seriously starting to burn out on the acceleration of ignorance these things produce. And I'm not even opposed to using neural net or token transformation tech for applications where it makes sense. However, the increased effort of verification is absolute poison for people who won't even bother to verify a first level source.<br /> <br /> Ok, rant over.<br /> <br /> \u0414\u043e\u0432\u0435\u0440\u044f\u0439, \u043d\u043e \u043f\u0440\u043e\u0432\u0435\u0440\u044f\u0439</div> </div> </div> </div>I get your frustration, though I disagree on one fundamental point:<br /> <br /> This is not new. They're just repeating an old trend of clinging to a chosen source rather than making searches.<br /> <br /> Have you never been or seen the person everyone goes for answers? And have you noticed that regardless of how much this person knows, they just accept their word and happily ignore any recommendation on making your own research?<br /> <br /> At work we have a search engine at hand just for the company normative. It's gigantic, and since we're a Brazilian bank they're not guidelines, they're serious law covering every procedure. Reading it is important, disobeying can have heavy consequences, and they are regularly changing.<br /> <br /> 95% of workers rely on others to know what to do instead of reading, go by memory until the procedure they remember outright fails before asking if it changed, and get really angry when someone tells them to read the normative, even if this person tells exactly what to look for.<br /> <br /> I've seen people be fired as consequence and even then nothing changed.<br /> <br /> LLMs are worsening this due to easy access, but the problem is actually way older. They are content with any answer, regardless if it is correct, and will frequently set up their brains to not only believe, but fiercely defend anything they heard as undeniable truth. And the cause: this is instinct to save energy, because thinking about it is literally harder.<br /> <br /> And yeah, bootlicking also helps a lot, which is sad, but just look in the corporate world how much sycophants always have it easier. Even when it's just their nature, I'm not even cynical enough to say they're always doing it in bad faith or are always incompetent. But the effect is depressingly effective.<br /> <br /> But I also disagree that verifying is getting harder, I find it actually easier. We have more sources, and if you know how to reign in their stupidity LLMs are excellent to accelerate the search and curation of sources.<br /> <br /> It just keeps not being automatic. You have to know how to verify and put the effort, and that's what most people won't do. Also the internet multiplied non curated sources, which means you don't have at least a baseline for where people get most of their disinformation. TV gave us a common ground, but also a hard to verify source that could and did, nonetheless, lie. The internet made the source of their lie harder to pinpoint, and AI is empowering people to lie to themselves more effectively than ever.<br /> <br /> Still I think human made lies have a tendency to be more dangerous.<br /> <br /> Videos haven't been trustworthy ever. Taking things out of context or manipulating them is as old as the record technologies themselves. And without a decent legal framework to crack down on fake news and their production process, I'd say we're already too saturated by them to say AI is making much of a difference.<br /> <br /> I'd say even the opposite: if we pass law making invisible watermarks and similar mandatory, AI would make way easier to track fake news to the source. Sure, it would still be possible to bypass, but it would require enough effort to get us back to Photoshop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T11:51:28-07:00","id":1562674,"title":"","content":"Just a minor vent. I feel sorry for YouTube channels where the Creator wrote a great script and used AI to make the mini story and they get lumped into others who use the same tools to make low content trash \ud83d\uddd1\ufe0f.<br /> <br /> Such people who have great writing talents and they've use AI to enhance their channel by creating a mini espoide shouldn't be tarred with the same brush \ud83e\udea5 \ud83d\udd8c\ufe0f.<br /> <br /> On a different note using Nux as a source is like using Jeremy Hambly as a source as he has a history of harrassing women at cons and was banned from any Magic The Gathering events because of what he did to cosplayer Sprinkle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-04-2026, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T13:47:31-07:00","id":1562687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562674#post1562674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such people who have great writing talents and they've use AI to enhance their channel by creating a mini espoide shouldn't be tarred with the same brush \ud83e\udea5 \ud83d\udd8c\ufe0f.</div> </div> </div> </div>They should.<br /> <br /> YouTube monetizes. This is not personal, is commercial use.<br /> <br /> Hire a fucking artist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T16:33:44-07:00","id":1562701,"title":"","content":"Belated vent - I found out yesterday that Michael Poe, of the webcomics Exploitation Now, Errant Story, and Does Not Play Well With Others, died back in March. I knew he hadn't exactly been doing well for quite some time, to say the least (kidney cancer and a general compromise to renal function requiring dialysis), but the confirmation of dreaded outcomes and the fact that a neighbor of mine that I talked to regularly about art (he was an animator and storyboard artist back in the 90s) died about the same time last year is making it hit extra-hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T19:59:43-07:00","id":1562707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562687#post1562687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They should.<br /> <br /> YouTube monetizes. This is not personal, is commercial use.<br /> <br /> Hire a fucking artist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> It always starts with making small concessions. But it can eventually snowball, if left unchecked.<br /> <br /> I do not want this AI bullshit being incorporated into my every day life. Between the fucked up user interface, and the even more fucked up AI generated ads it chooses to play on every video, I wish somebody would find out where they're housing all these AI data centers and toss a handful of industrial strength magnets into it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T21:05:28-07:00","id":1562708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562707#post1562707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> It always starts with making small concessions. But it can eventually snowball, if left unchecked.<br /> <br /> I do not want this AI bullshit being incorporated into my every day life. Between the fucked up user interface, and the even more fucked up AI generated ads it chooses to play on every video, I wish somebody would find out where they're housing all these AI data centers and toss a handful of industrial strength magnets into it!</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no small concessions. They're big.<br /> <br /> We already have the technical side of tracking and identifying AI content figured out enough to start. This is enough, for example, to have YouTube sort out AI generated content and filter it for you. We can make the AI itself have a built in public database of the works used in its training, so anyone can verify if protected work was used, and if it used work not licensed specifically for it. Wanna upload a work and ask the AI if it was used? Doable, even if none of them do that. It's not perfect, but we can reign in this madness.<br /> <br /> So you know what we can do today if they want to? Crack down every commercial AI trained with protected works, restrict those trained with open content to personal use, allow only those trained with specific licenses to be used for commercial purposes, channeling money back to the actual people who owns the works, and still make every browser, smart TV, phone or video platform automatically identify AI content so the user can either search for it or filter it out easily.<br /> <br /> And the reason we don't? Lobby plus customer deceiving workflows. Most commercial AI image or video generators make the bulk of their money out of business accounts. Those business accounts are focused on using AI to make ads, as you've seen. But due to public outcry, being caught doing it is bad business. So they only work with generators that won't be easy to identify, making it possible to deny, or at least never confess, it was done with AI.<br /> <br /> By proxy the AI companies divert the attention of public and lawmakers elsewhere while lobbying to remain unregulated in this area so they aren't forced to implement and improve real safety measures.<br /> <br /> Currently their greatest ally is the public outcry against Deep Fake, Porn and CSAM coupled with being viewd as similar to social platforms, which they aren't. That way they can implement shitty moderation layers that curb people's free use of the tool for perfectly legal generations, but are irrelevant for their actual money source, and pretend to be doing their part. And it stays impossible to find the sources of any illegal content that gets out, the damage being done without any control.<br /> <br /> Destroying datacenters won't do much, either. Running the AI locally isn't hard, so you'd have to destroy every computar capable of running them for a big company, which is impossible. What we need is proper regulation, put actual checks on it so criminals can be identified and apprehended, artist paid and worker wages protected from using AI as excuse for reduction.<br /> <br /> On another note, I still want your news sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T23:18:19-07:00","id":1562715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562708#post1562708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Destroying datacenters won't do much, either. Running the AI locally isn't hard, so you'd have to destroy every computar capable of running them for a big company, which is impossible. What we need is proper regulation, put actual checks on it so criminals can be identified and apprehended, artist paid and worker wages protected from using AI as excuse for reduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know they can just rebuild the AI somewhere else. But that's going to take time, money, and who knows how many months worth of training, if you wipe out the backups.<br /> <br /> We may not be able to stop the advent of AI, but we can certainly make it as irritating for those responsible as they make it for us.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562708#post1562708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On another note, I still want your news sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not getting them. I already told you people twice now I'm moving on to a new subject. Also, check the front page. The OP (who is an admin, by the way) even told us not to bring politics into this.<br /> <br /> So drop it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T23:32:26-07:00","id":1562717,"title":"","content":"Sources for evaluating the crime rates in a country aren't politics; it's literally looking for sources for basic facts and truth on a real thing that will exist regardless of ideologies, policies, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T08:14:51-07:00","id":1562728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562715#post1562715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know they can just rebuild the AI somewhere else. But that's going to take time, money, and who knows how many months worth of training, if you wipe out the backups.<br /> <br /> We may not be able to stop the advent of AI, but we can certainly make it as irritating for those responsible as they make it for us.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're not getting them. I already told you people twice now I'm moving on to a new subject. Also, check the front page. The OP (who is an admin, by the way) even told us not to bring politics into this.<br /> <br /> So drop it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not going to take time.<br /> <br /> The AI itself is small and has several backups, it's the process that's resource-heavy and even then not that much for most uses, the giant costly servers we see have to serve millions to a few hundreds of millions users each.<br /> <br /> Image and video generators are 8 to 10 times lighter than an LLM. The most heavy Backup scenario for a company's LLM would require 60 Tb in hard disk, which is doable, if heavy, for a home computer. For an LLM is 12 Tb worst case scenario, each full backup being about 2 Tb. This is literally each director having a full backup in their phones.<br /> <br /> Restoration time for the marketing companies making the ads you hate and the slop everyone and their dog hates, would be up to 2 hours for the video AIs.<br /> <br /> Even for an LLM, where size and training requirements also impact other things down the road, worse case scenario is 60-70 days, but likely 1-3 weeks.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately a complete obliteration of data centers that run AI, only, would put YouTube down longer than the slop makers.<br /> <br /> And that's for the most professional setups. A simpler local AI is so small that I can backup a library of image generators on my phone and take a day to restore one for use in a PC without any training. And believe me, people do that, those things have backups everywhere.<br /> <br /> Without destroying far more tech infrastructure than just AI data centers, you'd barely stop the flow for a morning. A lot of things in local host wouldn't even flinch.<br /> <br /> The lost data centers would impact everything else far more, expect an economic crisis, some serious problems with interrupted services of all kinds, and a new mega hit on the GPU market (gamers will hate you forevah).<br /> <br /> Even then, if only the data centers are hit you can expect basic AI services to be online in less than 24 hours. Some are back in 4h, with total recovery taking 2 months. The economic crisis will be less than a trillion dollars worldwide, but still impact for more than 1 or 2 years.<br /> <br /> If you go full hate and destroy everything the main AI companies have, then the crises can hit 4 trillion dollars, AI take weeks to go back online and a year to total recovery, and we'd have a longer time to climb out of recession and luckily stop relying so much on critically vulnerable systems.<br /> <br /> Full hate scenario: the world takes 10 years to recover from recession, the AI systems take 1 year to resume normal operations, AI slop is back before noon.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms said, sources aren't politics. In fact, claiming things without backup is closer to it. Giving your sources when asked is just proper behavior in a discussion or forum. We'll happily link ours if you ask, most posters here will, I think, and you don't need to link, just to say it.<br /> <br /> Making serious claims, accusing others of being blind and uninformed, saying they have to get &quot;better information&quot;, but never share your sources is actually pretty impolite. We're not pissed because you're impolite, but because the claims are offensive to a lot of people, but it's impolite still, and being offensive claims only worsen it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T09:07:04-07:00","id":1562733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562728#post1562728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Making serious claims, accusing others of being blind and uninformed, saying they have to get &quot;better information&quot;, but never share your sources is actually pretty impolite. We're not pissed because you're impolite, but because the claims are offensive to a lot of people, but it's impolite still, and being offensive claims only worsen it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do not want my sources. Because I gave them and was immediately met with counter arguments that the guy was a groomer, and that all his evidence could have easily been faked.<br /> <br /> No, what you want is to keep pressuring me on this issue, until I get so frustrated, I end up violating a community rule and get hit with disciplinary action.<br /> <br /> I'm not falling for it, and the next person who tries to force the issue with me again is getting reported for harassment.<br /> <br /> I have already asked you people repeatedly to stop. I was even polite with the second time and said 'please.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T11:18:54-07:00","id":1562739,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to grasp the concept of how someone can come to work in the receiving area and not be bothered to wear steel toed shoes. That is mandatory PPE when unloading trucks or moving skids and it's been made clear on the first day of orientation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T12:58:39-07:00","id":1562743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562733#post1562733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not want my sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really care at this point because if you had <b>sources</b> we wouldn't be here because you could discard one bad source for the rest.<br /> <br /> monteparnas is much more serious about wanting to see where you're getting your information because she's much kinder in her rhetorical charity than I am.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because I gave them and was immediately met with counter arguments that the guy was a groomer, and that all his evidence could have easily been faked. </div> </div> </div>No, you have given a single source with the claim that source has sources.<br /> <br /> You don't get to transfer a source's sources to yourself. If you cite a well researched piece with lots of primary and secondary sourcing, you are citing a single tertiary source, not all the tertiary source's sources. We have source-hierarchies because there are long held and reasonably good assumptions about reliability that are position-dependent. That is, how we judge primary source biases is very different from how we judge secondary source bias, and so on. Historical performance is a huge factor in analysis of tertiary sources because as an inherently compilation tier of sourcing, tertiary source methodology and consistency is make or break for their usefulness. <br /> <br /> A good tertiary piece - even one written by a bad source - should be something where you can reconstruct the argument yourself based on the sources they used so you can upgrade yourself to a tertiary source. That's at least something with good methodology because good methodology is replicable. If you can't replicate a tertiary source's argument for yourself using their sources, then that source is extremely weak for your rhetorical goals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, what you want is to keep pressuring me on this issue, until I get so frustrated, I end up violating a community rule and get hit with disciplinary action. </div> </div> </div>monteparnas and I have both said that an apology is what we think is an appropriate resolution to this tangent. Apologizing isn't a violation of the community rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not falling for it, and the next person who tries to force the issue with me again is getting reported for harassment. </div> </div> </div>Fair warning if you go through with it, the mods have repeatedly taken disciplinary action against users that try to use them as a threat against other users in the past.<br /> <br /> It's been explained why people feel is justified to stick on instead of just letting go, that reasoning is not &quot;because we want to harass you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have already asked you people repeatedly to stop. I was even polite with the second time and said 'please.' </div> </div> </div>No. You <b>told</b> us to stop. Words aren't magic. Adding &quot;please&quot; to an otherwise rude gesture doesn't transfigure it into a polite one.<br /> <br /> You also can't bluff once you've already shown your cards. If you say you're done with a topic but re-engage when people respond anyway? You're not done with it, you're not out of energy about it, etc. If you really were, you'd leave our posts hanging in the wind unanswered already.<br /> <br /> It doesn't feel like you're actually done with this topic, it feels like you don't want to have a discussion on it with people that can seriously challenge your position on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T13:00:33-07:00","id":1562744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562739#post1562739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to grasp the concept of how someone can come to work in the receiving area and not be bothered to wear steel toed shoes. That is mandatory PPE when unloading trucks or moving skids and it's been made clear on the first day of orientation.</div> </div> </div> </div>If use is not properly enforced, and most companies don't, people won't use PPEs. Few will.<br /> <br /> PPEs are uncomfortable, get in the way and in day to day activities you don't see accidents enough to grasp the risk, even if told they're there. And for most people it's lived experience what matters for real.<br /> <br /> So no, being told everything there's to know about it, including being mandatory, does nothing. This last part is relevant only if there's real report and punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T13:13:24-07:00","id":1562745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562733#post1562733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do not want my sources. Because I gave them and was immediately met with counter arguments that the guy was a groomer, and that all his evidence could have easily been faked.<br /> <br /> No, what you want is to keep pressuring me on this issue, until I get so frustrated, I end up violating a community rule and get hit with disciplinary action.<br /> <br /> I'm not falling for it, and the next person who tries to force the issue with me again is getting reported for harassment.<br /> <br /> I have already asked you people repeatedly to stop. I was even polite with the second time and said 'please.'</div> </div> </div> </div>You gave one, that's not them. It's one, who happened to be bad.<br /> <br /> I want your sources legitimately because of two reasons, the first being to give you the opportunity despite my expectations on what they'll be, the second being to better understand you. I'm a psychologist, I like to understand people.<br /> <br /> Asking for sources isn't special and the only one making it so is you. As Heavy Arms said we're going to leave you alone, or at least reduce this drastically if you make the sensible decision of apologizing for what was legitimately a problem. Not because you believing the guy and not knowing how shitty he is was a problem, but because doubling down after being informed definitely was.<br /> <br /> Offering your sources is also a valid decision, sensible if less so. We'll proceed to analyze them, still demand the apology and all that, but it will at least move things forward and reduce pressure.<br /> <br /> Having you break down is not in our intentions in any way. You don't know how posters who do that behave. I'm actually quite surprised by your resistance, not expecting to press it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T13:39:39-07:00","id":1562746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562739#post1562739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to grasp the concept of how someone can come to work in the receiving area and not be bothered to wear steel toed shoes. That is mandatory PPE when unloading trucks or moving skids and it's been made clear on the first day of orientation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember the last time I saw steel toed shoes. Or if I did, then they must have it built inside the shoe lining now, instead of the outside.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> generally speaking, if somebody asks you 3 times to leave them alone, and you continue to aggravate them, that's a sign that you actually want to get a reaction out of them.<br /> <br /> I am no longer engaging in this line of discourse. Any and all future posts relating to this particular topic will go ignored by me. Now stop wasting both our times, and pick something else to vent about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T14:30:05-07:00","id":1562753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562746#post1562746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> generally speaking, if somebody asks you 3 times to leave them alone, and you continue to aggravate them, that's a sign that you actually want to get a reaction out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if by a reaction you mean &quot;get them to do something, in general or in particular, including things you're on your right to ask or demand&quot;. Which is very different from wanting specifically a break down or something.<br /> <br /> I've been direct, clear and honest about what I want and, given the events, I'm entitled to it, be it the apology, or the sources then the apology. I'm not aware if you understood the situation, but defending a sex offender as a trustworthy source is pretty grave. Especially when you declare not that you don't believe he's a sex offender, but that you don't think he being a sex offender is a problem, and you did that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T14:48:14-07:00","id":1562756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562744#post1562744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If use is not properly enforced, and most companies don't, people won't use PPEs. Few will.<br /> <br /> PPEs are uncomfortable, get in the way and in day to day activities you don't see accidents enough to grasp the risk, even if told they're there. And for most people it's lived experience what matters for real.<br /> <br /> So no, being told everything there's to know about it, including being mandatory, does nothing. This last part is relevant only if there's real report and punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>The guy got reported to management and the safety team last night when we learned about it last night. I know that you think you are invincible when you are teen but that is a serious lapse in judgement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T14:52:15-07:00","id":1562757,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=DarkKing;n1562746]<br /> <br /> I can't remember the last time I saw steel toed shoes. Or if I did, then they must have it built inside the shoe lining now, instead of the outside.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the steel toed shoes I've seen have it inside the shoe lining and when you work in a warehouse or the receiving area of places like Walmart, Target and grocery stores it is required that you wear it along with other items such as safety glasses if you are making a cardboard combo bale and you are using wire strapping.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T12:34:57-07:00","id":1562785,"title":"","content":"It's really strange to see people upset that characters in comics, movies and games get updated looks. This is just a minor pet peeve as looks should get updated as technology improves or what might work in the past wouldn't fly today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T20:03:06-07:00","id":1562812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562785#post1562785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really strange to see people upset that characters in comics, movies and games get updated looks. This is just a minor pet peeve as looks should get updated as technology improves or what might work in the past wouldn't fly today.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much technology, but culture and art styles. But haters gonna hate and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T10:48:06-07:00","id":1562838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562785#post1562785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really strange to see people upset that characters in comics, movies and games get updated looks. This is just a minor pet peeve as looks should get updated as technology improves or what might work in the past wouldn't fly today.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more irritating that they keep rebooting the comics every 10 years or so.<br /> <br /> Especially when they make it a very clear plot point that rebooting the franchise is not supposed to happen again in the future.<br /> <br /> *ahem* DC Comics...<br /> <br /> The whole point of the Crisis on Infinite Earths storyline was to get rid of the multiverse by compressing all the major stories down into a single continuity. But then they gradually rebuilt a new multiverse.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Blackest Night / Brightest Day storyline explicitly stated that death was going to be permanent from now on. Only for us to get the story of The Hands, who reboot the comics once again.<br /> <br /> <br /> They keep telling us that changes are going to have a lasting impact, only for the to backpedal on that decision so they can launch a new line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T10:59:29-07:00","id":1562839,"title":"","content":"I strongly dislike company wide crossovers and DC doing reboots every few years. But they are not the only comic company that does it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T03:48:57-07:00","id":1562870,"title":"","content":"If Pokemon put as much effort into producing a good quality game again as they do for <i>trying to</i> crush Palworld, then maybe Palworld wouldn't have been created in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T18:33:55-07:00","id":1562911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562870#post1562870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Pokemon put as much effort into producing a good quality game again as they do for <i>trying to</i> crush Palworld, then maybe Palworld wouldn't have been created in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since their budgets for the main games for all those years leaked, I seriously agree.<br /> <br /> Their thing this whole time wasn't make games with quality, was to protect niche hard enough to profit on releasing minimum investment gold mines one after another.<br /> <br /> Now they'll have to start putting some money in it, cause Palworld is here to stay and likely won't be the only one for long.<br /> <br /> I wonder if they'll ever apologize for this level of bad faith. Or if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29009_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29009\" data-vbnamecard=\"29009\">DarkKing</a> will ever apologize for defending a groomer as source, or at least reveal other sources that may or may not make up for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T22:10:36-07:00","id":1562918,"title":"","content":"From what I have seen of bad faith criticism by Social Media in general is that they double down on the retoric and come out with even more bizarre excuses why they are not wrong at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T22:45:37-07:00","id":1562920,"title":"","content":"In all fairness, that's something that long predates social media. Like most things, social media just amplifies rather than creates problems. If you look at the history of fad diets... the same exact tactics of scare mongering about food safety and modern food innovations secretly leading to unhealthy results combined with selling books, pills, meal kits, and so on has basically remained unchanged in over 60 years. Social media just makes it easier to pump into everyone's feeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T23:06:19-07:00","id":1562921,"title":"","content":"That is true that technology has been a boon for conspiracy theories, bad science, bad faith criticism, and amping up the worst elements of society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T23:19:42-07:00","id":1562924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562911#post1562911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since their budgets for the main games for all those years leaked, I seriously agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pokemon is the largest intellectual property in the world. Anybody who tried to defend them by saying they lacked the budget is out of their minds.<br /> <br /> Also, it's easy to say you're the undisputed king of the arena, when nobody is trying to challenge you.<br /> <br /> Well, a challenger has entered the ring, and it's time for Pokemon to show the world that they can actually defend their title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T02:48:55-07:00","id":1562932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562921#post1562921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true that technology has been a boon for conspiracy theories, bad science, bad faith criticism, and amping up the worst elements of society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has it, though?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it isn't a problem that has to be addressed, but as Heavy Arms said those are fairly old problems. And I'm not sure if social media really makes as big a difference as it seems at first.<br /> <br /> Truth is, a lot of those have always circled around quietly, but quietly doesn't mean weakly at all. Search about what kind of things people believed 30, 50, 70 years ago, and how spread the crazier shit was, and you'll see our past isn't any pristine era of enlightenment and accuracy.<br /> <br /> Mass media had similar problems with another spin. Sure, overall they curated things and left a lot of heavy shit out of reach, but they also had their own lies and semi truths to spread, and no one could compete with their attention to try and set the record straight.<br /> <br /> Social media sped up the life cycle of rumors and corrections, and laid it bare for everyone to see, but didn't create and it's hard to measure how better or worse it was when more subtle. In the end ignorance has always been widespread, it was just hidden before.<br /> <br /> Personally I think we should demand more political action in this regard. Modern tech can propagate problems, but also solutions. What it won't do by itself is force the companies that control it to work for a better society. We can't keep going relying on corps to limit damage out of the goodness of their hearts.<br /> <br /> On Nintendo: what the leaks revealed is that Pokemon was getting less than 10% of the budget you'd expect from a franchise of its size. While there are no hard numbers, games AAA usually cost hundreds of millions to make, sometimes past half a billion, just to keep up with expected quality. Yet Pok\u00e9mon has drawn suspicion and criticism for slow improvement for quite sometime.<br /> <br /> Now we have the hard numbers. Scarlet/Violet, the most recent entry in the franchise that sold over 28 million copies, had a budget around 20 million dollars, less than a dollar per copy. This isn't a crime, but is an eye opener on how much they rely on brand and why they're so bullish with even remotely perceived competition.<br /> <br /> Well, with Switch 2 being officially leasing rather than sold, anyway, I'm out of this train for good one way or another, but it's a shame this got this far and I hope for whoever sticks to the next gen that it will be worth the indignity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T03:27:34-07:00","id":1562934,"title":"","content":"Oh I agree that the past wasn't a example of enlightened viewpoints. I remember Mom showing me her school books and how shockingly racist and sexist it was. I remember seeing news articles that had artwork that depicted boxer Joe Lewis looking like an animal or spreading the slur that black people are lazy.<br /> <br /> Or barely a century ago there was still strong anti Irish and Italian sentiment and were seen as undesirable to America.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T05:46:26-07:00","id":1562948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562920#post1562920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all fairness, that's something that long predates social media. Like most things, social media just amplifies rather than creates problems. If you look at the history of fad diets... the same exact tactics of scare mongering about food safety and modern food innovations secretly leading to unhealthy results combined with selling books, pills, meal kits, and so on has basically remained unchanged in over 60 years. Social media just makes it easier to pump into everyone's feeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, you could take it back to 19th century clean living movements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T09:25:48-07:00","id":1562963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562948#post1562948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, you could take it back to 19th century clean living movements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some papyri from Egyptian Middle Kingdom already hint to quackery being practiced over the gullible.<br /> <br /> Among their magical healing rituals and prays, Egyptian physicians did knew a lot of remedies that could really help, and a lot of things that seemed to, but didn't or even were poisonous. So, yes, there was already formal training and actual medical knowledge to be passed, and a number of assholes without either taking advantage of others and putting them in risk.<br /> <br /> Did it include diets and lifestyle fearmongering? Extremely probable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T12:40:12-07:00","id":1562971,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but then I don't get to say, &quot;exact&quot; tactics and have to be less absolute with &quot;similar&quot; as the tactics did change in the eras pre-mass media a bit. The human inclination clearly goes back thousands of years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T15:06:37-07:00","id":1562979,"title":"","content":"You know that you are getting old when you're happy that the kids are going back to school and not in stores being disruptive and being rude to fellow customers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T15:13:48-07:00","id":1562981,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Did it include diets and lifestyle fearmongering? Extremely probable.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Id say yes as people who go on diets or exercising expect quick fixes and that it doesn't work that way. I'm old enough to remember the glee of religious folks who said AIDS was divine punishment against Homosexual and Lesbian society or freaking out about disgraced tv personality Ellen DeGeneres coming out as lesbian and they were calling her names.<br /> <br /> More recently Elliot Page who only crime is existing as a Trans-man and some people can't handle it and they act like that he came to their house to abuse there kids and pets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T15:28:34-07:00","id":1562982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562971#post1562971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but then I don't get to say, &quot;exact&quot; tactics and have to be less absolute with &quot;similar&quot; as the tactics did change in the eras pre-mass media a bit. The human inclination clearly goes back thousands of years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, the fad diets and lifestyle part I have the impression that may have been really close to today, already. From what I've seen in some Greek and Roman sources, I think maybe they only difference was selling books.<br /> <br /> Children in stores are a problem because this is not the place for a child to be. That's boring, I totally understand the child being unquiet. The fact parents can't leave the children in a better place is a bigger annoyance to everyone<br /> <br /> Otherwise modern parenting is a rabbit hole of problems, a matrioshka of no-win decisions and paradoxical pressures. A devilish Catch-22 that's greatly weighing down society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T15:32:09-07:00","id":1562983,"title":"","content":"Many of the disruptive children are by themselves with no adult supervision and that is disappointing. I know with the cost of living requires both parents to work to make ends meet. But surely one of them would be home?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T16:14:14-07:00","id":1562987,"title":"","content":"To be fair I think retcons in comics sometimes get painted with a broad brush. Some of them work as they better explain weakness in a storyline by fleshing it out. I like the idea that you never truly face Darkseid as you are dealing with a avatar that is meant to interact on our plane of existence and he embodies a cosmic concept and single person.<br /> <br /> Or that according to Supergirl that her cousin never truly faced Brainiac but his drones.and it worked in Superman Brainiac.<br /> <br /> Others of course don't work because it was meant as shock value such Iron Man The Crossing or Ben Reilly being the original Spider Man and the one people who married Mary Jane and followed for years was a clone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T18:01:51-07:00","id":1562995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562983#post1562983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many of the disruptive children are by themselves with no adult supervision and that is disappointing. I know with the cost of living requires both parents to work to make ends meet. But surely one of them would be home?</div> </div> </div> </div>How would one be home if they both have to work?<br /> <br /> It doesn't work like that. Parents are given a shitty hand because they're tasked with taking care of the future generation, but at the same time told to take the brunt of it without complaining.<br /> <br /> What do you want? Working to improve life is a fallacy, if financial conditions are a requisite you curb reproductive rights royally. While the current system refuses to take material responsibility over the children, it can't survive without a growing population, either.<br /> <br /> Parents are required under great pressure to have kids, then told it's their choice and their weight to carry, despite it being literally too big, it's the caretake of a new member of society. They have to educate by themselves, to feed by themselves, to protect and all sorts of highly specialized tasks, 24/7.<br /> <br /> Seriously, they're setup for failure and that's normalized. It shouldn't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T19:22:49-07:00","id":1562998,"title":"","content":"I've seen parents that both work, but make sure one of them is home looking after the children. A few families I know had one parent work the morning shift and another would work evenings. They found a way to make sure that one person was always home even if both had to work. It's difficult, but not impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T11:36:34-07:00","id":1563014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1562998#post1562998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen parents that both work, but make sure one of them is home looking after the children. A few families I know had one parent work the morning shift and another would work evenings. They found a way to make sure that one person was always home even if both had to work. It's difficult, but not impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's conditional. There are people who can isn't the same as everyone can.<br /> <br /> To begin with, because for most people there's no &quot;choosing shifts&quot;. You get the job you can, you start to ask for specific hours when your job allows it.<br /> <br /> One of the most common fallacies in US culture is the idea that people have a choice on where to work and with what, when reality is that circumstances dictate a lot of what really is feasible.<br /> <br /> You're assuming a model of familiar structure without noticing, and however common it may be, lots of families won't fit. Are there two parents? What qualification they have? Do their area has suitable jobs? Is their current job one of those? What's the costs and risks of change? What are the options if something fail?<br /> <br /> Do you really think any answer to those can be made universal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T07:54:59-07:00","id":1563028,"title":"","content":"I'm not American but your point stands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T11:36:25-07:00","id":1563103,"title":"","content":"How many people are starting to really hate click baiting titles or images?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T23:04:49-07:00","id":1563115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1563103#post1563103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many people are starting to really hate click baiting titles or images?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot? Everyone?<br /> <br /> I really don't know many people that don't hate click bait.<br /> <br /> But it isn't really new and probly not going away anytime soon. Remember those variety TV shows where they'd announce the juiciest part saying it will be soon and hyping it, just to end with it being the very last thing to happen, if at all? And usually a far cry of the promises.<br /> <br /> Reminds me a lot of DarkKing talking about their mysterious ground shaking sources we never get to see because apparently disliking a groomer and recurring liar means we want to incite a fight rather than, you know, want an apology for publicly defending a groomer and recurring liar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 08-15-2026, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T02:16:57-07:00","id":1563116,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure most of the sources were of the same level of creditability like Nux. Such as Yellow Flash, Overlord DVD, Andrew Tate and The Quartering. <br /> <br /> Anyway I didn't even give the channel with the click baiting title my time of day even though I'm a sucker for behind the scenes stories of how movies are made and nice little tidbit when a director mentioned that a scene was improvised and they kept it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T12:27:14-07:00","id":1563147,"title":"","content":"I really dislike Alberta separatists as it's all about emotion and not reality. Sure as much I have issues with Ontario and Quebec and it's huge concentration of political power I still like being part of Canada and that my home province shouldn't leave.<br /> <br /> We would have to create our own currency, police force, military, economy, social services and countless others that I have not considered.<br /> <br /> Not to mention would we be recognized as a nation by the rest of the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T20:10:17-07:00","id":1563153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1563147#post1563147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dislike Alberta separatists as it's all about emotion and not reality. Sure as much I have issues with Ontario and Quebec and it's huge concentration of political power I still like being part of Canada and that my home province shouldn't leave.<br /> <br /> We would have to create our own currency, police force, military, economy, social services and countless others that I have not considered.<br /> <br /> Not to mention would we be recognized as a nation by the rest of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans are emotional. You're right on spotting the problem (not that it is a bad idea, just that being overly emotional leads to badly made decisions), but you'll find sooner or later that a lot of seemingly rational people are all emotion too, and then that we all are, we just learn to recognize and try to police ourselves rather than ever stop that.<br /> <br /> Or, put in another way: be a little patient. Not lenient with bullshit, but patient. They're just people that found something they really care about, and that won't always result in the best expression.<br /> <br /> Unless they're supremacist scum, then hate them with a vengeance to your heart's content. Disclaimer: that's a joke, but by the &quot;not lenient&quot; you're free to be mean to them in public anyway, it's about survival and decency.<br /> <br /> The recognition part is the hard one, though not the most important. First is state presence, you have to build an administrative system that can run then place in practice. Second is local recognition, the people must see your system as more legitimate than the alternative. Third is resistance, you have to keep the other part out of your business. Only fourth will international recognition be relevant.<br /> <br /> Also none of those are binaries, they're all way too fluid and nuanced, even because functional isn't the same as liked or efficient or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T21:59:34-07:00","id":1563158,"title":"","content":"Just like with Quebec when they tried to do the separation vote, they found out many of their citizens didn't want to leave and the indigenous communities wanted to stay and they controlled a region the size of British Columbia. Many Albertans and indigenous communities are for staying in Canada.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T22:08:53-07:00","id":1563159,"title":"","content":"Sad news for fans of the show Heroes. Hayden Panettiere passed away today at age 36 with no official cause of death yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T11:36:16-07:00","id":1563255,"title":"","content":"I wish the people writing for Onyx Paths would find somewhere else to fit their narrative sections into the books. It frustrates me that when digging through DriveThruRPG, I can't tell what material I'm getting, because they decided to start off with 5 pages worth of fluff material, and we run out of preview pages before we even get to the table of contents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T11:45:04-07:00","id":1563257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1563255#post1563255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish the people writing for Onyx Paths would find somewhere else to fit their narrative sections into the books. It frustrates me that when digging through DriveThruRPG, I can't tell what material I'm getting, because they decided to start off with 5 pages worth of fluff material, and we run out of preview pages before we even get to the table of contents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more of a DriveThru problem, but I have to agree that having the Table of Contents early in the book would be nice for a change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T11:53:38-07:00","id":1563259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1563257#post1563257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's more of a DriveThru problem, but I have to agree that having the Table of Contents early in the book would be nice for a change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would certainly make it easier to figure out which books you want to buy, instead of trying to hunt them down via links on Wikipedia.<br /> <br /> Even videos that review the releases of their books only seem to keep to the bare bones explanation and skim through the contents without giving a clear picture of what you're purchasing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T04:14:50-07:00","id":1563276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1563159#post1563159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sad news for fans of the show Heroes. Hayden Panettiere passed away today at age 36 with no official cause of death yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard about that! It's so sad... she was really young too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T11:08:05-07:00","id":1563287,"title":"","content":"Why's so hard for some people to simply accept the pain of others?<br /> <br /> Today I had to take the most painful decision a pet parent may have to. Banguela was with us for 12 years, I loved him dearly even if I knew he wouldn't last much more than this.<br /> <br /> It hurts on me and my wife. He was a member of the family, and an important emotional bond so what's the fucking problem?<br /> <br /> Now I have to call a doctor to get a medical report, as I'm in no condition to work. But I also have to make up a reason to be in a depressive episode, as while having diagnosed chronic depression validates almost any crisis, for a lot of doctor it simply isn't a thing if the reason is a lost pet.<br /> <br /> Having a pet has nothing to do with deciding to have children or not, caring for the animal has no bearing on one's capacity to care for humans, and feeling awful when you lose anything you love is just natural, but I'm here stuck without much anyone to talk with about this because of all those bizarre conclusions.<br /> <br /> Even worse if it's a cat, because a lot of people aren't satisfied in not liking a species, they lose the ability to form basic theory of mind if your affection goes towards a cat, even if they could accept your affection for almost anything else they don't care about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T15:14:56-07:00","id":1563292,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just like with Quebec when they tried to do the separation vote, they found out many of their citizens didn't want to leave and the indigenous communities wanted to stay and they controlled a region the size of British Columbia. Many Albertans and indigenous communities are for staying in Canada.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to intervene here and please ask you not to lump Qu\u00e9bec separatism, which is rooted in historical oppression, with Alberta separatism seems to be almost purely fuelled by oil industry lobbyists and economic frustrations. I personally find the comparison quite offensive.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not fully convinced by Qu\u00e9bec separation, but I swear my whenever I read my fellow Canadians online, they always manage to push me further by the constant criticism, always there to remind us that we\u2019ll always be outcasts. We aren\u2019t without issue but it gets grating. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure you probably feel similar sometimes as Alberta is often represented as \u2018\u2019US-Lite\u2019\u2019 in online spaces. Which is also not helping national unity.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, visiting the Maritimes last year reminded me that my fellow canadians in real life space are actually pretty nice.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure you\u2019re a cool person, no hard feeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why's so hard for some people to simply accept the pain of others?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most certainly a lack of empathy and consideration for animal lives.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Sorry for your loss.</span> <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\u2639</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T18:17:18-07:00","id":1563293,"title":"","content":"No hard feelings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T22:51:11-07:00","id":1563297,"title":"","content":"Lack of empathy is dangerous thing to see or experience. Especially when you see it on social media and it gives a very distorted view of how we should treat others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T11:30:42-07:00","id":1563423,"title":"","content":"I really wish that media grifters would stop using the 2.5 times what a movie needs to make to break even or make a profit based on the budget.<br /> <br /> It doesn't include how much money tie in media also brings in a significant amount of money or that most studios will use tax breaks and incentives to lower the cost of making the movie and possibly increase the potential profit or that now most studios will give films shorter theatrical runs now before it goes to streaming or Blu Ray and DVD.<br /> <br /> There still thinking that things haven't changed in the last decade or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T17:35:16-07:00","id":1563438,"title":"","content":"That's a market staple, not the grifters being in bad faith, even if they're beings in bad faith anyway.<br /> <br /> A movie is an investment. Investors need this data because it tells how much the movie will pay back in a short to medium horizon. This is called ROI, Return Of Investment.<br /> <br /> ROI is complex, but to help financial decisions each industry has a few rules of thumb to get a measure of how much something is a safe bet or not, how reliable/consistent a business is, above all how sustainable its baseline return is.<br /> <br /> In this last point, for cinema movies have this 2,5 times budget as Box Office target because that's what you need to cover everything, then get enough to keep the studio going and the cut for the investors that'll keep them investing.<br /> <br /> Less than that doesn't mean the studio won't ever get a decent return, but it does mean that movie was a financial risk whose return may take too long to come, which can jeopardize the studio's future works and scare investors away.<br /> <br /> What has to be questioned isn't if this number is solid. It is as solid as it gets for what it tells. You have to question if they understand what this number really means and if they're reading the right data for what they're talking. Box Office is a particular data point with a particular meaning that may be relevant or completely out of place depending on the conversation.<br /> <br /> But I don't get it, if you hate those grifters so much, why are you always looking at what they talk about? You already know they're just shit posting at everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T18:01:42-07:00","id":1563440,"title":"","content":"I don't watch them anymore, but people at work will bring up their talking points and I try to debunk the grifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T18:03:04-07:00","id":1563441,"title":"","content":"I know mostly watch Chris Mcfreely, Commdin Cam, Space Ice, cat videos and the odd music Video.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T19:17:29-07:00","id":1563445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1563440#post1563440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't watch them anymore, but people at work will bring up their talking points and I try to debunk the grifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, got it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's gritting when you hear coworkers talking stupid bullshit not knowing it's stupid bullshit. I feel you.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, the 2,5 thing is mostly something to bring up when the discussion point is if the movie in question gave enough return. That's usually relevant if the studio has been having problems or if it is the first of a franchise and you wanna know if they're likely to make the next in the line.<br /> <br /> Let's say a Marvel movie, I wouldn't bother as it is a successful franchise already, so a hiccup here or three is unlikely to make them stop. But the first Disney Star Wars that was relevant, as if for some reason that movie had flopped, that could change their strategy for the franchise.<br /> <br /> Overall that's it, you wanna know if the studio is entering or leaving a crisis, or if an experiment is a financial success likely to be repeated. If a conversation isn't drifting to this perspective it probably isn't worth your time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T19:39:25-07:00","id":1563447,"title":"","content":"The End of Oak Street is a new IP and because it came out competing against Spider Man Brand New Day and the Odyssey it's underperforming and many of the people who I have talked to have greatly enjoyed it. But you know that some people will use to spin a false narrative.<br /> <br /> I enjoy watching behind the scenes stories of movies and TV shows or seeing what the cast is doing now. But I saw a thumbnail of the cast of The Fifth Element which came out nearly 30 years ago and the channel chose to make 50 year old Mila Jovovich look quite elderly and I didn't bother clicking it. If you have to resort to that then clearly you are not worth watching.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T20:03:44-07:00","id":1563450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1563447#post1563447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The End of Oak Street is a new IP and because it came out competing against Spider Man Brand New Day and the Odyssey it's underperforming and many of the people who I have talked to have greatly enjoyed it. But you know that some people will use to spin a false narrative.<br /> <br /> I enjoy watching behind the scenes stories of movies and TV shows or seeing what the cast is doing now. But I saw a thumbnail of the cast of The Fifth Element which came out nearly 30 years ago and the channel chose to make 50 year old Mila Jovovich look quite elderly and I didn't bother clicking it. If you have to resort to that then clearly you are not worth watching.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You got it right. That's a moment when talking Box Office is worth it, but can still be done wrong.<br /> <br /> Competing with much waited movies is hard. I hope this IP do get their share under the sun after they forget the bitter taste of not having a chance. It's sad when good movies lose their momentum because they got the unlucky of being released side by side with a blockbuster.<br /> <br /> Hope your coworkers are listening and giving it a try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T11:29:16-07:00","id":1563473,"title":"","content":"I also like to point out that just because a movie did very well at the box office doesn't always mean it was successful in terms of storytelling or that many films that are well regarded now didn't light it up at the box office because of tough competition.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head Montparnasse I can list Blade Runner, John Carpenter The Thing, Highlander, Shawshank Redemption and others that didn't do well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-25-2026, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":""