2026-08-26T11:11:40-07:00","id":1563502,"title":"","content":"More sad news is that Tim Curry from Clue, Legend, Rocky Horror Show, Scary Movie 2 Loaded Weapon and countless others has passed away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T11:46:17-07:00","id":1563541,"title":"","content":"Even more sad news is the passing of voice actor Peter Cullen who voiced Optimus Prime, Ironhide, Eyeore, and the vocal sounds for the original Predator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T14:24:52-07:00","id":1563546,"title":"","content":"My gf burst into tears about cullen. She was brittle after tim curry and losing eyore pushed her over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zryfjSaxXLo?is=FnfaCLVi30QsWEIn\" data-code=\"zryfjSaxXLo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zryfjSaxXLo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T17:52:20-07:00","id":1563550,"title":"","content":"I hope that she feels better Ragged Robin and yes this month has seen the loss of Hayden Panettiere, Dolly Parton, Tim Curry and now Peter Cullen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T17:59:52-07:00","id":1563551,"title":"","content":"On a different track i would like to see the term girlboss retired as it's been used as a blanket term for any female character in media that doesn't fit the damsel in distress or love interest by a vocal minority who don't like that they are not being catered to.<br /> <br /> Also it's quite infantile to view grown adult women as girls when they are not clearly children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T20:32:21-07:00","id":1563554,"title":"","content":"I don't know, nowadays using &quot;girl&quot; and &quot;boy&quot; to refer to grown people has been kinda standard, at least as far as I could see. Seems to be less infantilization and more the language changing as man/woman are being more associated with either formal language or conservative &quot;real sexes&quot; discourse.<br /> <br /> Note that my view is quite limited, though, as I read/hear English in a limited set of contexts. I do have that impression, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T20:52:44-07:00","id":1563555,"title":"","content":"Very seldomly do you hear grown men referred as boys as they would find it disrespectful and not to mention the racist connection it was used to males who were from african ancestry.<br /> <br /> I personally find it insulting to call an adult woman a girl when she clearly isn't a child or under the age of 18.<br /> <br /> For girlboss it was a reference to a type of woman who excelled in the corporate world using many of the same tactics that their male counterparts would employ.<br /> <br /> Now so many activists have devauled the term by using it as an insult if a woman is confident, driven and successful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-28-2026, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T21:48:47-07:00","id":1563556,"title":"","content":"Interesting to know.<br /> <br /> Here we don't have such connection between calling with any of the words for a young or child male and racial connotations, at least not that I'm aware, and it is pretty common to use &quot;menino(s)&quot; in mixed gender groups, at least.<br /> <br /> Outside those depends on context, but I'd say you risk more being seen as childish than as infantilizing others if you use in an inadequate context. It's pretty weird to see someone here feeling disrespected by being called that, but I can picture someone being pissed at language like that being used with them to refer to anyone else. Even then, very uncommon today, I see it used even in the office.<br /> <br /> Language also has nuance. It's beyond doubt that infantilizing women feels disrespectful, but the words &quot;menina&quot; and &quot;garota&quot; here don't necessarily convey this intention, and I can say that many like to be referred with such words that avoid referring to age. We use them with each other all the time.<br /> <br /> Not that I expect the same to hold true in other languages and countries. Rather, what gave me the impression that this was happening in English is the contact I have with the internet and movies and series. I'd ask if you're sure the standards you know are broadly applicable too, but that's just because I'm used to people here assuming something is widely understood one way, just to find out it's a regionalism.<br /> <br /> Girlboss I know what is and how it has accrued a demeaning connotation. I also know how bad things are within the corporate world, where sexism is masked but extremely dominant still, and women are judged constantly for doing the things their actual jobs, position and career goals demand. No few will use either praise as veiled insult or similar derogatory terms to try to demean or slander a woman for being what she should as a professional.<br /> <br /> Many don't actually think women should be at all professionals, they think women in an office are there to do menial tasks and take care of the place as a house, regardless of job titles, and they get pissed when a woman refuses to clean or make coffee to, you know, work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T1