ound the <b>Kanto</b> region like horses!<br /> <br /> Even the smallest among them still measure at a hefty size of 5'03 in height, and 237 pounds in weight.<br /> <br /> So, why are they so commonly depicted in fan art as being around the size of normal dogs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-12T22:57:39-07:00","id":1564000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1563867#post1563867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I am certain that these AI generated ads are just being thrown onto the internet, without any human oversight now!<br /> <br /> While scrolling through youtube shorts, one ad that keeps popping up, is a Lego animation telling me that the world is being controlled by Jewish vampires!<br /> <br /> Does anybody have a copy of the Berenstain Bears laying around?<br /> <br /> Can you please check to make sure we haven't crossed into another parallel dimension without noticing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just finally saw what you were talking about and it's quite disgusting and with YouTube not bothering to enforce the terms of services agreement. We are seeing more content creators becoming more willing to air there bigotry as they know nothing will be done to them<br /> <br /> Examples of this include Deranged Doomer, Ryan Kinel, Ranting For Vengeance, Critical Drinker and Nerdrotic just to name a few.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-13-2026, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T00:04:02-07:00","id":1564002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1563999#post1563999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When standing on all fours, <b>Arcanine</b> is supposed to clock in at being somewhere between 6 to just under 8 feet tall, and weighs between 370 to 533 pounds. During the first Pokemon intro, we can see that <b>Officer Jennies</b> ride them around the <b>Kanto</b> region like horses!<br /> <br /> Even the smallest among them still measure at a hefty size of 5'03 in height, and 237 pounds in weight.<br /> <br /> So, why are they so commonly depicted in fan art as being around the size of normal dogs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say I got any of those numbers, but just don't put much stock on fanart.<br /> <br /> Short answer is, a lot of them just want to draw their dogs as Arcanine. And it isn't as if official materials were that much better when looked closely.<br /> <br /> Do you know how much weight Ash used to carry? That Pikachu of his is 15Kg minimum. He carried a Larvitar, which is close to solid rock, as if it weren't heavier than a rabbit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T00:56:13-07:00","id":1564003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564000#post1564000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I just finally saw what you were talking about and it's quite disgusting and with YouTube not bothering to enforce the terms of services agreement. We are seeing more content creators becoming more willing to air there bigotry as they nothing will be done to them<br /> <br /> Examples of this include Deranged Doomer, Ryan Kinel, Ranting For Vengeance, Critical Drinker and Nerdrotic just to name a few.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Critical Drinker did satirical movie reviews?<br /> <br /> At least, that's the content I'm familiar with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I got the measurements off Serebii, which is a site that's pretty much dedicated to recording all the games in the pokemon franchise. Even has the complete stats from the Pokedex entries.<br /> <br /> Pokedex says Pikachu is only about 13 pounds. But Larvitar is 158!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 09-13-2026, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T01:56:52-07:00","id":1564004,"title":"","content":"Critical Drinker went full into doing outrage content and became more bigoted in general. If he is not a racist IRL then he is a great actor as he pulls it off effortlessly. Critical Drinker is blatantly msyigonist as he doesn't seem to respect or even women as human.<br /> <br /> The moment a woman is on the screen and isn't a love interest or damsel in distress, our Will Jordan labels them a girlboss and won't use their characters name or even the name of the actress in question and if they are dark skinned then it's worse.<br /> <br /> Examples of this include is that he uses AI to create thumbnails to make persons of color look worse or crying. Or focus on them in a cast picture ie when he posted a picture of the cast of Minecraft and put the actress Danielle Brooks front and center and asked what is wrong with this picture.<br /> <br /> Another was the recent Spider-man animated movie and Critical Drinker showed his msyigony when he called Peter Parker daughter May &quot;it&quot;.<br /> <br /> So Critical Drinker doesn't do movie criticism anymore and just spews hatred and let the mask slip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-19-2026, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T04:08:05-07:00","id":1564008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564003#post1564003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I got the measurements off Serebii, which is a site that's pretty much dedicated to recording all the games in the pokemon franchise. Even has the complete stats from the Pokedex entries.<br /> <br /> Pokedex says Pikachu is only about 13 pounds. But Larvitar is 158!</div> </div> </div> </div>I know Serebii, though I've seen it err a few times, I much prefer Bulbapedia, but I said I didn't get it as in I didn't had the patience to run so many values on conversion to readable SI standard.<br /> <br /> My mistake on pikachu aside, picture a fat rat in your head doing everything it does with this weight. My neck wouldn't handle 6 Kg dancing around pulling and pushing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T11:56:59-07:00","id":1564020,"title":"","content":"On a brighter note is that many of these media grifters channels are not getting the same type of views they got a couple of years ago. People are wising up to them as nothing more than outrage merchants and are starting to learn that most people don't care about what they say or even know who they are when they go to entertainment conventions.<br /> <br /> Nerdrotic got a huge blow to his ego when most of the Star Trek cast that he went after didn't even know who he was. He and Drinker have over a 1 million subscribers but in the grand scheme they are tiny and most of the entertainment industry are unaware of them<br /> <br /> These channels can only say Marvel, DC comics, Hollywood and the gaming industry is dying so many times before people see that they don't know how the business works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-14-2026, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T19:07:03-07:00","id":1564030,"title":"","content":"I really appreciate how we name things in Brazil. It's easy to not notice in the day to day life, especially without reference of what others do, but I recently heard someone comment about how chocolate candy bar names in English are uninspired, and looking at some lists now I have to agree.<br /> <br /> The following are among maybe the 30 most sold in the country, not by any margin a local thing. It's not that everything is like that, but, well...<br /> <br /> Here we have:<br /> <br /> 1. Diamante Negro (Black Diamond)<br /> <br /> 2. Sonho de Valsa (Dream of Waltz)<br /> <br /> 3. Prest\u00edgio (Prestige)<br /> <br /> 4. Bis<br /> <br /> 5. Sensa\u00e7\u00e3o (Sensation)<br /> <br /> 6. Serenata de Amor (Serenade of Love)<br /> <br /> 7. Alpino<br /> <br /> 8. Caribe<br /> <br /> 9. Talento (Talent)<br /> <br /> 10. Mundy<br /> <br /> 11. Opereta<br /> <br /> 12. Ouro Branco (White Gold)<br /> <br /> 13. Tortuguita (Portunhol for Little Tortoise)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T16:14:12-07:00","id":1564060,"title":"","content":"Sad news if you are a fan of actor Bruce Campbell as he has admitted that he is battling an inoperable type of cancer and has maybe 5 years at most before he succumbs to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T02:19:03-07:00","id":1564075,"title":"","content":"not sure if this is vent but more a musing on edgy humour-<br /> Edgy humour is tricky because you're always going to attract that guy who only really gets the crudity of the joke. I'm a big fan of 'edgy humour' but what a lot of people miss is the edge which is part of the challenge, you have to be very whitty to make the joke transient while still being funny and not just a prick.<br /> <br /> If you look at doug stanhope who jokes about child abuse and stealing from his dead mother and you can see how it works vs sneako who it doesn\u2019t get it or say nick fuentez who just uses it as cover for malign views. Like any form of humour it relies on being funny and competant but the stakes are higher because of the edge.<br /> <br /> It feels weird to say &quot;you're enjoying the joke wrong.&quot; but here we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T19:44:28-07:00","id":1564109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564060#post1564060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sad news if you are a fan of actor Bruce Campbell as he has admitted that he is battling an inoperable type of cancer and has maybe 5 years at most before he succumbs to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We also lost robot Jesus (Peter Cullen) not too long ago. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T22:13:52-07:00","id":1564112,"title":"","content":"Yes losing Peter Cullen was a blow as a segment of our childhood is now gone forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T18:15:43-07:00","id":1564147,"title":"","content":"Election Day can't come soon enough. I am so sick of seeing the exact same fucking Jon Ossoff campaign advertisement on every single video I click.<br /> <br /> Even worse, the ad is unskippable!<br /> <br /> Which is another point I want to vent about<b></b>: <i>Staggering the advertisement skip times.</i><br /> <br /> Some ads load up their skip bar super fast, so you can ignore them after a few seconds.<br /> <br /> While in the case of others, the bar loads much, much slower. To the point where the entire ad plays from start to finish, before you can get on with watching your video.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T22:53:58-07:00","id":1564158,"title":"","content":"That's weird.<br /> <br /> Campaign advertising here is severely regulated. That would be a fast ticket to being removed from the election entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T23:43:55-07:00","id":1564159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564158#post1564158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's weird.<br /> <br /> Campaign advertising here is severely regulated. That would be a fast ticket to being removed from the election entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here in America, you practically can't escape it. When the election season rolls around, commercials will be flooded with ads where the rival parties talk about how great they are, and how terrible the other is.<br /> <br /> Under normal circumstances, I would find it mildly amusing. But this season is particularly irritating.<br /> <br /> It's the exact same ad every time. Talking about how Jon Ossoff exposed the abuse of foster kids, then passed a federal law to prevent it.<br /> <br /> I would have thought human trafficking was already illegal, but okay.<br /> <br /> <b>Alternatively:</b> I will get an advertisement featuring a woman complaining that her husband has to work 2 jobs to support the family, while Jon is trying to increase taxes.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is, these two advertisements will often play back to back with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 09-18-2026, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T07:21:30-07:00","id":1564167,"title":"","content":"And of course when election season ends, it is back to the incessant drug commercials, which are even more unethical.<br /> <br /> There was a claim going around last year that the major news networks (CNN, FoxNews, etc) get so much of their money from pharma ads that they would likely go under if those ads were ever restricted. I don't know how true the claim is, but if it is valid that's yet another good reason to curtail drug commercials. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately I mostly see pharma commercials on streaming services, and stopping them on tv wouldn't actually stop them elsewhere. That said, I doubt the corporations would sink nearly as much money into making them if they couldn't put them on tv.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T12:32:58-07:00","id":1564169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564167#post1564167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course when election season ends, it is back to the incessant drug commercials, which are even more unethical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and those tend to stir up my anxiety, since I'm not exactly in the healthiest condition!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T07:22:56-07:00","id":1564191,"title":"","content":"Big corpos like to spread the rumors that they can go under if whatever because loosing them is a real anxiety for many. But I seriously doubt they'll suffer that much if/when pharma gets regulated.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but I can't really think about the US as anything other than one of the weakest legal systems and democracies in America, kept afloat in practice due to economic reasons, not any merit of its outdated system.<br /> <br /> That goes a long way, but is hitting hard limits.<br /> <br /> Pharma ads here are heavily regulated and usually short. Bad faith companies seek other ways of advertising because formal ads aren't an option for their model. And I still think we have a growing problem, imagine with almost no rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T10:49:25-07:00","id":1564244,"title":"","content":"I can believe that there's a strong kernel of truth that the major media corporations get lots of money from pharma ads, but it's not the only source as they have sponsorship deals with numerous companies to run ads. It's how they make much of the money at any given time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T13:27:37-07:00","id":1564277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564191#post1564191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big corpos like to spread the rumors that they can go under if whatever because loosing them is a real anxiety for many. But I seriously doubt they'll suffer that much if/when pharma gets regulated.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but I can't really think about the US as anything other than one of the weakest legal systems and democracies in America, kept afloat in practice due to economic reasons, not any merit of its outdated system.<br /> <br /> That goes a long way, but is hitting hard limits.<br /> <br /> Pharma ads here are heavily regulated and usually short. Bad faith companies seek other ways of advertising because formal ads aren't an option for their model. And I still think we have a growing problem, imagine with almost no rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fake pharma&quot;, as in the unregulated &quot;dietary supplements&quot; and other &quot;alternative&quot; material, should not go unmentioned. It makes even more cash than actual pharma, even as prevalent as that is. Several times as much, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T16:20:51-07:00","id":1564283,"title":"","content":"I know, but fake pharma is also a bigger problem because it is not a legit business being empowered by lack of regulation, it is a scam deliberately existing within regulatory failure points. Related and disproportionately big in the US, too, but still a different and more widespread beast.<br /> <br /> One of the problems I see here: there are some &quot;wellness&quot; companies that follow the law strict on their official materials, but they let vendors create unofficial ones with the bogus info that spread like wildfire, but can't be tracked back to the company.<br /> <br /> But yeah. The wellness industry and its fake pharma branch are a plague upon society that requires removal with prejudice. And I stand by the conviction that pseudoscience is never harmless and should be given no quarter, ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T08:40:19-07:00","id":1564301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564277#post1564277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Fake pharma&quot;, as in the unregulated &quot;dietary supplements&quot; and other &quot;alternative&quot; material, should not go unmentioned. It makes even more cash than actual pharma, even as prevalent as that is. Several times as much, in fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>My dad and I went into a &quot;holistic&quot; medical shop one time, and they had these tiny glass bottles that were stuffed with dirt, herbs, and bits of colored paper.<br /> <br /> I shit you not, they were selling them for <b>60$</b> a piece, and marketed them as <i>&quot;healing charms.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T13:55:26-07:00","id":1564310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564301#post1564301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I shit you not, they were selling them for <b>60$</b> a piece, and marketed them as <i>&quot;healing charms.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a problem.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: whatever you or I think of this kind of thing, whomever buys a charm knows exactly what they're buying, what it is based on, that it doesn't have a lick of science to it, they believe in it because they believe in magic.<br /> <br /> And there's nothing wrong in selling magic to people who believe in magic. No one's being deceived.<br /> <br /> But the wellness industry sell pseudoscience: stuff that has no scientific basis, but pretend to it. Things that use technical explanations, sell a performance of rigorous study, but has none.<br /> <br /> What matters isn't if it is real, but how it answer to three questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Does it pretends to an authority it doesn't have to make baseless claims?<br /> <br /> 2. Are sellers discouraging people from seeking actual professional help they need first?<br /> <br /> 3. Is it dangerous? Consuming it can have real harmful effects depending on circumstances?<br /> <br /> Rarely do the selling of charms and magic stuff runs afoul of those. The people involved only claim the authority they in fact have (none or as occult believers), are either silent on the matter or inform their things do not substitute for actual professional help, and the trinkets and rituals are harmless. No one is telling people to eat the charms.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the fake pharma frequently check all those boxes: a fake professional that either claims to be something they're not, let it implicit, or argue to have a corpus of evidence they don't; they imply or directly state that normal medicine is bogus and harmful, you shouldn't just use their product, you should divert resources from other treatments to it; and they're messing with nutrition, medication and exercises that can have real effects, just not the effects they claim.<br /> <br /> Hospitals have been dealing regularly with the outcomes of those bastards. People are dying for real in some cases. I lost a friend a couple years ago that way, I couldn't make her see the harm before it was too late, and it still haunts me. In the disabled community horror stories about fake pharma are popping up all the time, there's always a new victim of MMS and other stuff.<br /> <br /> Let mystics be mystics. The real problem are people pretending to be professionals (or worse, some actual unethical professionals) to milk money while inflicting serious consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T21:06:03-07:00","id":1564317,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry to hear that you lost a friend to bogus Science Montparnasse <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-24T00:38:53-07:00","id":1564318,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I apologize, but I fail to see the distinction. You say that selling people a tiny bottle filled with dirt and crumbled paper for 60 dollars is okay, because people believe in its power to improve their physical and mental health.<br /> <br /> But by that same logic, Big Pharma has likewise convinced people that their pseudo science can help improve their lives.<br /> <br /> So what makes it okay for one side to do it, but not the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-24T11:14:26-07:00","id":1564327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564318#post1564318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what makes it okay for one side to do it, but not the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>This:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564310#post1564310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What matters isn't if it is real, but how it answer to three questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Does it pretends to an authority it doesn't have to make baseless claims?<br /> <br /> 2. Are sellers discouraging people from seeking actual professional help they need first?<br /> <br /> 3. Is it dangerous? Consuming it can have real harmful effects depending on circumstances?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fake pharma does all 3, consistently, sometimes to extremes. Magic thingamajigs usually don't.<br /> <br /> Read my post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T09:41:12-07:00","id":1564359,"title":"","content":"I am becoming increasingly convinced that these Juro Spiders will fuck anything with a pulse, because it seems like every single day I find new ones appearing on my property.<br /> <br /> Also, they share communal webs with each other. Something which I've never seen any other spider species do in my life time.<br /> <br /> I tried spraying them with poison, but they came right back after a day or two. So now I just smack the hell out of them with a broom, and it seems to drive them further away from the house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T10:20:51-07:00","id":1564360,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, I'm jealous because we don't have any Nephilinae where I live. From what I read they don't impact pollinator populations, and even act as pest control. Their venom isn't harmful to humans, and they're pretty - subjective, I know, but consider just destroying their webs to get them to move instead of smacking them.<br /> <br /> Communality in spiders isn't as rare as it's made out to be tbh. Some usually solitary species can and will tolerate each other when there's enough food around.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">This post was brought to you by the Ministry Of Spider Public Relations.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T11:45:28-07:00","id":1564364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564360#post1564360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, I'm jealous because we don't have any Nephilinae where I live. From what I read they don't impact pollinator populations, and even act as pest control. Their venom isn't harmful to humans, and they're pretty - subjective, I know, but consider just destroying their webs to get them to move instead of smacking them.<br /> <br /> Communality in spiders isn't as rare as it's made out to be tbh. Some usually solitary species can and will tolerate each other when there's enough food around.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">This post was brought to you by the Ministry Of Spider Public Relations.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The Juro Spiders have recently invaded the Smokey Mountains, which is the area I live around.<br /> <br /> Physically, they're harmless to humans, as well as being extremely timid. But they'll eat virtually anything that gets caught in their webs, including pollinators.<br /> <br /> They're also orb weavers, meaning that their webs are just a giant mass of silk, instead of the more typical design we're familiar with.<br /> <br /> Our hired mower wouldn't go down around to get the back yard, because doing so would require him to drive his lawn mower straight through a giant nest of the things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T12:24:51-07:00","id":1564367,"title":"","content":"Trichonephilinae, they changed classification of the jor\u014d.<br /> <br /> Orb weavers make a mess, but isn't as bad as it looks, around here most spiders are orb weavers. Just clean it up with a broom, preferably one you use just for that (because getting the silk out of the broom will be tedious).<br /> <br /> Spiders in general are harmless for humans. Our natural fear is actually a biology mystery, because all primates share the same system: a specialized, super-fast pattern recognition for araneiforms that identifies a spiderlike thing faster than you can recognize your eye is working, that tends to activate anxiety systems.<br /> <br /> But almost no spider is dangerous to primates at all, much less humans.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: Brazil is one of the countries with the greatest number of potentially lethal spider species.<br /> <br /> Funnier fact: that's a whopping total of 3. From more than 4k species in the country, the life threatening ones are 3. And the most dangerous has a killing rate of 2,6% if the bite does occur and goes untreated.<br /> <br /> Even funnier fact: in the US, a study in California IIRC found out that from every 20 patients that go to the hospital because of a spider bite, 1 was, in fact, bitten by a spider.<br /> <br /> Anyway, just clean their webs, it's usually faster than it seems because they look way denser than they actually are. And it's not as if you had much of a choice. Otherwise I hope against hope that doesn't become an ecological calamity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T12:29:02-07:00","id":1564368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564364#post1564364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they'll eat virtually anything that gets caught in their webs, including pollinators.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that's the point. The may catch some pollinators, and even a small bird once in a while. What I meant is that in the states they were introduced to earlier haven't noticed any negative impact on the environment so far - they're invasive, but not necessarily harmful. Food chains change, but not every invasive species presents a problem.<br /> <br /> For Joros, it's still too early to tell what their introduction means, especially with very recent introductions like in Appalachia. If you want to help figure that out, I encourage you to log observations on iNaturalist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564364#post1564364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're also orb weavers, meaning that their webs are just a giant mass of silk, instead of the more typical design we're familiar with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their silk is so cool. I personally would love to see one in my garden, but the closest thing we have are Argiope/Wasp Spiders.<br /> <br /> You would be in Widow range, right? I'm surprised a harmless orb weaver is somehow more concerning/annoying than an actual medically significant species. Is it the size?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T12:44:10-07:00","id":1564369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564367#post1564367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact: Brazil is one of the countries with the greatest number of potentially lethal spider species.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is legit paranoia here in central Europe that a Brazilian Wandering Spider gets imported with a bunch of bananas. I think it happened once, but most of the time it's just a Huntsman.Tabloids absolutely<i> love</i> to drum up spider paranoia though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T12:44:45-07:00","id":1564370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564368#post1564368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You would be in Widow range, right? I'm surprised a harmless orb weaver is somehow more concerning/annoying than an actual medically significant species. Is it the size?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they set up near our windows.<br /> <br /> It's not ONE spider that's concerning. These things breed at a shockingly fast rate. Just a few weeks ago, I counted no less than 7 of them all sharing a single web. And there were about 4-5 additional webs within 20 feet of each other.<br /> <br /> They also gradually expand their webs every day. At first it was just off to the side of the porch, but they gradually continued to get wider and wider, until they were blocking the walkway up to the house. I was forced to tear it down so we could actually get out to the driveway.<br /> <br /> If it was just one or maybe two of them setting up where it didn't interfere with anything, I'd have no real problem with them. But they're blocking main pathways around my house, such as the driveway, the garbage cans, and the garden hose. Also, they are breeding faster than we can keep track of; I wasn't speaking hyperbole when I said I discover new ones every day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T12:49:45-07:00","id":1564371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564367#post1564367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, just clean their webs, it's usually faster than it seems because they look way denser than they actually are. And it's not as if you had much of a choice. Otherwise I hope against hope that doesn't become an ecological calamity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Introducing a foreign species to the local ecosystem has never worked out in humanity's favor.<br /> <br /> That said, researchers are asking people to help them collect these things instead of killing them, so that they can study their webs. Juro spider silk is stronger than normal webbing, and is unique for having a bright, golden color when the light reflects off it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T14:44:18-07:00","id":1564372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564368#post1564368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would be in Widow range, right? I'm surprised a harmless orb weaver is somehow more concerning/annoying than an actual medically significant species. Is it the size?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know what it really takes to get bitten by a Widow?<br /> <br /> It's actually nearly impossible. Most cases of Widow envenoment aren't really bites, but the person pressing or slapping the spider and accidentally hitting the fangs. I'm not aware of a single case where the widow attacked.<br /> <br /> Wandering Spiders are one of the few species around the globe that actively attacks humans, but still far less than their reputation suggests. And fear of spiders is higher where dangerous species are rarer/non existent. Again, it's just baffling as we don't know of a single spider ever that could have justified evolutionary fear.<br /> <br /> Here where I live it's common, as it isn't a region with many Brown or Wanderings. I know a number of people with arachnophobia that can't stand the sight of the tiniest jumping spider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564371#post1564371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Introducing a foreign species to the local ecosystem has never worked out in humanity's favor.<br /> <br /> That said, researchers are asking people to help them collect these things instead of killing them, so that they can study their webs. Juro spider silk is stronger than normal webbing, and is unique for having a bright, golden color when the light reflects off it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it works once in a while, just doesn't get attention, but is a dangerous gamble indeed.<br /> <br /> I did thought I was recognizing the species, now I confirmed. We have some Jor\u014d Spiders here. I don't know why they fill a given space and not others, but they didn't spread nearly as much.<br /> <br /> But you may not be witnessing reproduction. Those spiders may be migrating. Jor\u014d only lay eggs once a year and are born in spring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T16:19:01-07:00","id":1564373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564372#post1564372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know what it really takes to get bitten by a Widow?<br /> <br /> It's actually nearly impossible. Most cases of Widow envenoment aren't really bites, but the person pressing or slapping the spider and accidentally hitting the fangs. I'm not aware of a single case where the widow attacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know bites are 99% defensive, but accidental squishes can happen especially with combfoots who like to hang out in dark nooks. What I meant was that Widows at least warrant a bit of attention.<br /> <br /> ... or you are a really annoying youtuber who insists on handling a Red Widow individual that very obviously isn't in the mood for it. That will get you a bite, too.<br /> <br /> But anyway, I can also see <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29027_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29027\" data-vbnamecard=\"29027\">GreatHornedRatkin</a>'s point of not wanting their house cocooned. I second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> broom advice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T17:51:40-07:00","id":1564374,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> <br /> <br /> Oh, you said 'widow!'<br /> <br /> Sorry, I misread it as 'window' - which is apparently a place that they like to set up around. I don't know why exactly, but given the fact that most of them have been in front of glass surfaces, it seems to check out.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, I don't want my house completely encased in webs. Just stay in the garden, or up in the corner; not the main walkways I use to get around.<br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> From what studies have been conducted so far, it is actually very difficult to startle a Juro into biting you. They're far less aggressive than other species, and they have the longest 'freeze up' period of any species we've studied so far.<br /> <br /> Most spiders when they get spooked will freeze for a few minutes before moving again. Where as the Juros have frozen for upwards of 40 to 60 minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T21:35:53-07:00","id":1564377,"title":"","content":"Yeah, tried to find out some local suggestion on dealing with golden webs, but nothing. They're unlikely to make such a mess around here, so pest control guides don't even bother.<br /> <br /> Overall not much to do. Broom or sticks to remove them, a vacuum cleaner if you feel like it, but has to empty it ASAP right after, and that's it. Most advice actually ends at &quot;clean the backyard, don't attract them&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are poisons that affect them, but not the regular ones, so maybe calling a professional is the best option if going physical don't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-27T05:20:47-07:00","id":1564379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564374#post1564374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I misread it as 'window' - which is apparently a place that they like to set up around. I don't know why exactly, but given the fact that most of them have been in front of glass surfaces, it seems to check out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just a general orb weaver thing. Reflections of the sun during day or lights from inside during the night will attract flying insects, so windows and any lights are favorite spots for them. Windows also provide a nice frame structure for their webs, making them prime real estate.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-27T08:34:14-07:00","id":1564380,"title":"","content":"Well, my cat just fucking died on me, and in a rather horrifying fashion too. I couldn't tell if she had rabies, or was a fucking skinwalker.<br /> <br /> My brother said she spent the night sleeping in the cat box; and just moments ago, she flopped on the ground and started having extremely labored breathing, along with what I suspect were seizures. She kept staring out with a blank, soulless expression and making weird yowling sounds. Her breathing became gradually slower until she eventually went limp and became totally unresponsive.<br /> <br /> At one point, she did the creepiest stretch I've ever seen from a cat. Totally soundless, without blinking, and just slowly contorting herself backwards while stretching out her legs and staring directly at me.<br /> <br /> I noticed she had a wound on her stomach which looked like some wet cat litter may have gotten inside of it, but couldn't inspect it closer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 09-27-2026, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-27T10:43:42-07:00","id":1564381,"title":"","content":"I'm really sorry.<br /> <br /> This was not rabies. May have been FELV, this kind of sudden crisis is typical for it. But that's besides the point now.<br /> <br /> Anything you must talk about, we're here. Not much, but I at least understand the pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-27T11:22:42-07:00","id":1564382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564381#post1564381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really sorry.<br /> <br /> This was not rabies. May have been FELV, this kind of sudden crisis is typical for it. But that's besides the point now.<br /> <br /> Anything you must talk about, we're here. Not much, but I at least understand the pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, she'd taken to sleeping in the litter box for a while now. Not sure what caused it, but my best guess would probably be anxiety.<br /> <br /> After a few weeks, the ammonia in the cat urine caused her to develop sores, and I guess one of them finally got infected.<br /> <br /> I don't know, this is just my best guess. She died right before we were about to take her to an animal hospital, which would have been at least an hour's drive away.<br /> <br /> <br /> Her name was <i>'Squeaker'</i> because she was the most vocal kitten out of her litter. Even as an adult, she would constantly meow for attention whenever you pet her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-27T12:18:01-07:00","id":1564383,"title":"","content":"It's always hard to lose pets as they are big part of the family growing up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-28T18:05:32-07:00","id":1564400,"title":"","content":"Just a minor vent about people thinking that professional wrestling is totally fake. Yes the matches are scripted but the physical toll that there job does on the performers are quite serious and real.<br /> <br /> I have to admit that I did like the video where adult film actress Mia Khalifa went into the ring to see what it is like after bad mouthing them was quite pleasing. She found out that the rings don't have much give or the ropes don't provide much protection and I'm sure that the chop she was given by the wrestler was hit with more force then what is usually given.<br /> <br /> Now if only Bill Maher would step in and see how hard physically that wrestlers push themselves to entertain us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-28T22:10:55-07:00","id":1564406,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing, it IS totally fake. The point is actually that the fakeness isn't relevant.<br /> <br /> Stage magic and theater are also totally fake. It is besides the point. People watch those things for entertainment that comes from the artistry of the show.<br /> <br /> What people must reckon with is that artistry isn't easy, and entertaining is hard work. That goes on different ways to every entertainer. It includes a lot of brain power and, yes, physical toll, that in professional wrestling is quite harsh<br /> <br /> I think you didn't even gave it proper credit yet, because that goes beyond the physical stress of the fight you see. An actual fighter faces a lot more, but only once in a while. A wrestler is not only training techniques, but rehearsing the choreography, practicing with colleagues to get the timing and position, and frequently making their moves way more taxing than they need to be because they have to be impressive, not effective, and impressive is hard.<br /> <br /> All that aside learning stage position, character, all sorts of stuff any actor has to learn. If most are not excellent actors (though some are), you have there a highly specialized actor that must keep the show going on during intense workout and stress.<br /> <br /> But I think only that we could avoid calling Mia a porn actress. She has been out of this stage for a long time, it gave her a lot of problems and she has been trying for many years to leave that behind. I don't think it should be something to be ashamed of, but is not what she wants to be known for today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"m