t":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T18:26:28-07:00","id":1564656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502169-feel-free-to-vent?p=1564639#post1564639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have just recently become aware that youtube actually has an option to block specific ads. However, it's so hard to locate, that I would have missed it completely, if it weren't for searching Reddit.<br /> <br /> During the ad play, if you check the bottom left corner, there is an extremely tiny 'I' mark that brings up the option to report / block / like the ad.<br /> <br /> Why am I venting about this?<br /> <br /> Well, because I've blocked a certain ad 4-5 times, and yet it still keeps showing up. Reddit commenters suggest this is because they are circumventing the ad by using spam accounts. Which violates the terms of service.<br /> <br /> So next time it happens, I'm clicking to report the ad, instead of block it!</div> </div> </div> </div>If you use Opera browser and or, install Adblock, it blocks all the ads from Youtube.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to l